1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Guthrie DNA Project: Inferred Status Only
2 CONT Descendants of James Guthrie (merchant) and Christian Scott
2 CONT Y-DNA Verified to match Guthrie Family Group 1A
2 CONT Haplogroup: R-M269 / / R-FT13875
2 CONT Require Y-DNA matches traceable to earlier generations for verification of historical paper trail.
2 CONT ______________________________________________________________
2 CONT Alexander Guthrie 2nd Baron Guthrie 3rd Kincaldrum
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 14 Jul 1460 • Guthrie, Angus, Scotland
2 CONT "Sir Alexander was son and heir of Sir David Guthrie of Guthrie chief of his name by Janet daughter of Sir Archibald Dundas of Dundas Knight."
2 CONT
2 CONT Succession to Baronies of Guthrie, Kincaldrum and Lour (Age = 14)
2 CONT 23 Aug 1474 • Scotland
2 CONT Instrument of Sasine in favour of Alexander Guthre as son and heir of deceased David Guthre of Guthre, kt., of lands of Guthrie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charges by Lords of Council and Session
2 CONT 1478 • Scotland
2 CONT Sir Alexander Guthrie of Kincaldrum was charged before the Lords of Council and Session, by the Abbot and Convent of Cupar about a mill built on Kincaldrum, and withholding the multures of the corn of the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT Succession to Guthrie Titles and Properties
2 CONT 1513
2 CONT Either before or at the time of his death the titles and properties owned by the Guthrie family were split between the 4 sons: David Guthrie died with his father at Flodden Field, so David's son Andrew inherited Guthrie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 09 Sep 1513 • Flodden Field, Scotland
2 CONT Burke&Burke:"Sir Alexander, surrounded by friends and vassals, attended his sovereign to the fatal field of Flodden, and there fell, with his eldest son David, his three brothers-in-law, David, William and George Lyon, and his nep
2 CONC hew, Sir Thomas Maule.
2 CONT
2 CONT Succession to Guthrie Titles and Properties
2 CONT Alexander's 3 other sons inherited the remaining titles and property: Alexander 4th of Kincaldrum; George of Kincreich; John 1st of Hiltoun.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Guthrie '''Clan Guthrie'''] From Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of the clan<br/>
2 CONT The family of Guthrie took their name from the lands of the same name in the county of Angus and their name is one of the oldest in that county.[3] The origin of the name Guthrie is not known, although there is a tradition that th
2 CONC e lands were named Guthrie by an early king of Scots, after a fisherman gut three fish to serve his hungry monarch.[3]........ 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16th century and clan conflicts<br/>
2 CONT David's son, '''Sir Alexander Guthrie''', was killed at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden '''Battle of Flodden'''] in 1513.[3] In 1567 the Guthries signed a bond upholding the authority of the infant James VI of
2 CONC  Scotland against that of his mother, Mary, Queen of Scots.[3] Around the same time the Clan Guthrie were feuding with their neighbours, the Clan Gardyne.[3] Alexander Guthrie had been assassinated at Inverpeffer and the Guthries 
2 CONC retaliated.[3] The feud lasted until 1618,[4] when the Guthries were saved from their actions by a royal pardon.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I30953&tree=CC
