1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Descendants of Alexander Guthrie
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/u/t/Steven-P-Guthrie/GENE1-0005.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. III LAIRD OF GUTHRIE ANDREW5 GUTHRIE (DAVID4, ALEXANDER3, DAVID2, ALEXANDER1) He married CHRISTIAN GAIRDEN, daughter of LAIRD OF GAIRDEN PATRICK GAIRDEN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for III LAIRD OF GUTHRIE ANDREW GUTHRIE: III LAIRD OF GUTHRIE: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Guthrie of Guthrie, who was infeft upon a precept from chancery, as heir served and restored to Sir Alexander Guthrie, of that Ilk, his good sire in the lands and barony of Guthrie, and the lands of Balnabriech. The sasine 
2 CONC is dated, 15th May, 1514. He subsequently obtained a charter from King James V of the said lands and barony, with the tower, fortalice, manor place, mills, &c. and right of partronage of the provostry of Guthrie, prebendary, and o
2 CONC ther kirks and Chaplanrys there, containing a novodamus and new erection of the whole, into a barony, for his faithful services, dated, 9th March, 1538-9, and was infeft therein by sasine, dated, 31st March,1539. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Guthrie of Guthrie resigned the lands and barony of Guthrie to his son Alexander, with the commonty in the muir of Montrathmont, reserving his own life rent, upon which settlement the said Alexander obtained a charter, unde
2 CONC r the great seal, from Queen Mary, dated,13th March, 1543-4, and being infeft thereon, 2nd May, 1544. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of ANDREW GUTHRIE and CHRISTIAN GAIRDEN is: 
2 CONT *1. 13.	i.	 	ALEXANDER6 GUTHRIE, d. October 1587.
