1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis==
2 CONT
2 CONT =Forfarshire became the administrative district of Angus in 1928.=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis (1402 – 21 March 1459) P.C. was a Scottish nobleman, created Lord Glamis on 28 June 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was the son''' of Sir John Lyon of Glamis (c.1377–c.1435) and Elizabeth Graham, daughter of Sir Patrick Graham of Dundaff and Kincardine and Euphemia Stewart, Countess of Strathearn. Sir John was the son of Sir John Lyon (d.
2 CONC  1382) and Princess Joanna Stewart, daughter of Robert II of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lyon was hostage in England for King James I from 1424 until 9 November 1427 when he was exchanged for another hostage. He was one of the Lords Auditors (1450–1451) and Master of the King's Household (1450–1452) to King
2 CONC  James II. He was Ambassador to England (1451) and again (1455). He was Keeper of the Castles of Kildrummy, Kindrocht and Balveny (1456–1459).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Late in 1427 or soon thereafter he married Isabel, daughter''' of Sir Walter Ogilvie of Lintrethan, Treasurer of Scotland. '''They had at least four children:
2 CONT *Alexander Lyon, 2nd Lord Glamis
2 CONT *John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis
2 CONT *William of Peetanya
2 CONT *Elizabeth, the wife of Alexander Robertson of Strowane
2 CONT
2 CONT The late Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother, Lady Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon, was a descendant of Lord Glamis.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Lyon,_1st_Lord_Glamis
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________
2 CONT *'''Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis, Lord of Kinghorn1,2,3
2 CONT *'''M, #37595, d. 21 March 1459
2 CONT *Father	Sir John Lyon, Lord of Kinghorn, Chamberlain of Scotland2 b. c 1378, d. 1435
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth Graham2 d. b 1417
2 CONT *'''     Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis, Lord of Kinghorn was born at of Glamis, Forfarshire, Scotland. He married Isabel Ogilvy''', daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy, Lord High Treasurer and Isabel Glen, '''circa 1427; Her 1st marriag
2 CONC e.4,3 Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis, Lord of Kinghorn died on 21 March 1459 at Belhelvies, Aberdeenshire, Scotland.3
2 CONT *'''Family     Isabel Ogilvy d. 1484
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis+ d. 1 Apr 1497
2 CONT **Elizabeth Lyon+
2 CONT **Alexander Lyon, 2nd Lord Glamis d. 1486
