1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Elizabeth Lyon1
2 CONT *F, #37796
2 CONT *Father	Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis, Lord of Kinghorn d. 21 Mar 1459
2 CONT *Mother	Isabel Ogilvy d. 1484
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Lyon married Alexander Robertson after 1 April 1440.
2 CONT *'''Family     Alexander Robertson d. c 1506
2 CONT *Children	
2 CONT **Robert Robertson+2
2 CONT **Duncan Robertson2 d. b 1506
2 CONT **Andrew Robertson2
2 CONT **James Robertson2
2 CONT **Mary Robertson+2
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S11561] Unknown author, Burke's Landed Gentry, p. 1926.
2 CONT *[S11570] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Landed Gentry, by Sir Bernard Burke, p. 1926.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1259.htm#i37796 __________________________
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth Lyon
2 CONT *F, #9903
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 Nov 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.16%
2 CONT *'''     Elizabeth Lyon was the daughter''' of Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis and Isabel Ogilvy. '''She married Alexander Robertson, 9th of Glenerochie''', son of Robert Robertson and Lady Margaret Stewart, on 1 April 1440.1
2 CONT *'''      From 1 April 1440, her married name became Robertson.
2 CONT *'''Children of Elizabeth Lyon and Alexander Robertson, 9th of Glenerochie
2 CONT **Duncan Robertson2 d. b 1506
2 CONT **Robert Robertson+2 d. b 1506
2 CONT **Andrew Robertson2
2 CONT **James Robertson2
2 CONT **Mary Robertson2
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 3363. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p991.htm#i9903 ________________________
2 CONT *Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis (1402 – 21 March 1459) P.C. was a Scottish nobleman, created Lord Glamis on 28 June 1445.
2 CONT *He was the son of Sir John Lyon of Glamis (c.1377–c.1435) and Elizabeth Graham, daughter of Sir Patrick Graham of Dundaff and Kincardine and Euphemia Stewart, Countess of Strathearn. Sir John was the son of Sir John Lyon (d. 1382
2 CONC ) and Princess Joanna Stewart, daughter of Robert II of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT *Patrick Lyon was hostage in England for King James I from 1424 until 9 November 1427 when he was exchanged for another hostage. He was one of the Lords Auditors (1450–1451) and Master of the King's Household (1450–1452) to King J
2 CONC ames II. He was Ambassador to England (1451) and again (1455). He was Keeper of the Castles of Kildrummy, Kindrocht and Balveny (1456–1459).
2 CONT *Late in 1427 or soon thereafter he married Isabel, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvie of Lintrethan, Treasurer of Scotland. They had at least four children:
2 CONT **Alexander Lyon, 2nd Lord Glamis
2 CONT **John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis
2 CONT **William of Peetanya
2 CONT **'''Elizabeth, the wife of Alexander Robertson of Strowane
2 CONT *The late Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother, Lady Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon, was a descendant of Lord Glamis.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Lyon,_1st_Lord_Glamis ___________
2 CONT *'''A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain & Ireland Vol. 2    by Burke, Bernard ....
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera02inburk
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera02inburk#page/1719/mode/1up
2 CONT *   From their ancestor DUNCAN DE ATHOLIA, Earl of Athol, they are known among the highlanders of Scotland as "Clandonachy," or descendants of Duncan. He m. 1st, a dau. of Malcolm, Earl of Lennox, and had a son, ROBERT DE ATHOLIA,
2 CONC  ancestor of the STRUAN family. Duncan, by his 2nd wife (presumed to have been a dau. of Angus Moer, Lord of the Isles), had a son, PATRICK DE ATHOLIA, who received from his father the Barony of Lude, ancestor of the great Scottis
2 CONC h family of ROBERTSON of Lude, represented by Col. JAMES ALEXANDER ROBERTSON, of the 82nd Regt., son and heir of Lieut.-Gen. William Robertson, of Lude, by Margaret his wife, eldest dau. of George Haldane, Esq. of Gleneagles, co. 
2 CONC Perth. A younger branch of the Lude family were the ROBERTSONS of Tulliebelton, co. Perth, 
2 CONT *   ROBERT DE ATHOLIA (the eldest son of Duncan de Atholia) had, by his 1st wife, dau. and co-heir of Sir John Stirling, of Glenesk, a dau. Jean, to. Alexander Menzies, of Fothergill. By his 2nd wife he had a son, 
2 CONT *   DUNCAN DE ATHOLIA, mentioned in the Rotuli Scotiæ under the name of "Duncanus de Atholia, dominus de Ranagh." He was s. by his son, 
2 CONT *   ROBERT DE ATHOLIA (Reoch), one of the most noted chiefs of his day. He arrested the murderers of JAMES I., and for this good service received a Crown charter, erecting his whole lands into a free barony, dated 1451, and also a
2 CONC n honourable augmentation to his arms. He m. the Lady Margaret Stewart, by whom he had three sons, 
2 CONT **'''	ALEXANDER, his heir. 
2 CONT **	Robert, of Dalcabon, ancestor of SIR ALEXANDER ROBERTSON, who assumed the surname of COLYEAR, and was created a baronet, 1677. His son and successor, SIR DAVID COLYEAR, Bart., a military officer of reputation, was elevated to t
2 CONC he Scottish Peerage as EARL OF PORTMORE, a dignity which remained with his descendants until the death s. p. of the late Earl of Portmore. 
2 CONT **	Patrick. 
2 CONT *He d. temp. JAMES II., and was s. by his son, 
2 CONT *'''   ALEXANDER ROBERTSON, or son of Robert, which from this date, became the designation of the family. He m. 1st, Elizabeth, dau. of Patrick, Lord Glammis, by whom he had 
2 CONT **	DUNCAN, who d. v. p. 
2 CONT **	Robert, m. Isabell, dau. of John, Earl of Athol, and d. v. p., leaving a son, 
2 CONT ***		WILLIAM, s. his grandfather. 
2 CONT **	Andrew, ancestor to the ROBERTSONS of Ladykirk, Edradynet, &c. 
2 CONT **	James, ancestor of the ROBERTSONS of Kindrochit, Achlichs, &c. 
2 CONT **	Mary, m. Andrew Moray, of Ogilvie and Abercairney. 
2 CONT *He m. 2ndly, Elizabeth, dau. of John, Earl of Athol, by whom he had 
2 CONT **	Alexander, ancestor of the ROBERTSONS of Faskally. 
2 CONT **	John, of Muirton, ancestor of ROBERTSON-WILLIAMSON, of Lawers. 
2 CONT **	Margaret, m. George, 7th Earl of Errol, and had issue. 
2 CONT *He d. about 1506 or 1507, and was s. by his grandson, 
2 CONT *   WILLIAM ROBERTSON, of Struan, who was killed in a feud with the Earl of Athol. He was s. by his son, 
2 CONT * .... etc. _______________
2 CONT *	'Robertson01' 
2 CONT *Duncan de Atholl, 5th of Glenerochie, 1st Chief (a 1346) 
2 CONT *Duncan is generally accepted as the first Chief of the Clan Donnachaidh which took its name from him. In the early 15th century when (for the first time) many families chose lasting family names, the head of the family was Robert
2 CONC  (4th Chief) and members of the senior family in the Clan took Robertson as their family name. In support of their chief, many of their kinsmen took that name also although others preferred names such as Duncanson or MacDonachie. 
2 CONT *   m. dau of Malcolm, 5th Earl of Lennox 
2 CONT **     1. Robert de Atholl, 6th of Glenerochie 
2 CONT **        m1. Jean Stirling (dau of Sir John de Striveling of Glenesk) 
2 CONT ***          A. Jean de Atholl 
2 CONT ***             m. Alexander Menzies of Fotheringill 
2 CONT **        m2. heiress of Fordill 
2 CONT ***          B. Duncan de Atholl, 7th of Glenerochie 
2 CONT ****               i. Robert 'Ruadh', 8th of Glenerochie, 4th Chief (d c08.1460) 
2 CONT ****               Robert had most of his lands, including Glenerochie, pulled together into one Barony of Struan. 
2 CONT *****'''                    a. Alexander Robertson, 9th of Glenerochie/Struan (d c1506) 
2 CONT *****'''                       m1. (01.04.1440) Elizabeth Lyon (dau of Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord of Glamis) 
2 CONT ******                         (1) Duncan Robertson (dvp) 
2 CONT ******                         (2) Robert Robertson (dvp) 
2 CONT ******                            m. Margaret Stewart (dau of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl) 
2 CONT *******                              (A) William Robertson, 10th of Struan (d 1532) 
2 CONT ********                                   (i) Robert Robertson, 11th of Struan, 7th Chief 
2 CONT ********                                      m. (09.02.1544/5) Mariota MacIan (dau of Ian MacIan of Ardnamurchan) 
2 CONT ********                                   (ii) Isabel Robertson 
2 CONT ********                                      m. David Moncreiffe in Kirkwall (d c1625) 
2 CONT ******                         (3) Andrew Robertson ancestor of Robertsons of Killichangy, Ladykirk, Eastertyre and Edradynate
2 CONT ******                         (4) James Robertson of Calvine
2 CONT ******                         (5) Mary Robertson
2 CONT ******                            m. Andrew Moray, 5th of Abercairney (d Flodden 09.09.1513)
2 CONT *****                       m2. (before 24.04.1504) Elizabeth or Isabel Stewart (dau of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl)
2 CONT ******                         (6) Alexander Robertson, 1st of Faskally (d by 03.1557)
2 CONT ******                            m. (by 01.05.1543) Elizabeth or Isobel Hay
2 CONT ******                         (7) John Robertson of Muirton ancestor of Robertson-Williamsons of Lawers
2 CONT ******                         (8) Margaret Robertson
2 CONT ******                            m1. Thomas Innes of Elrick (d before 1528)
2 CONT ******                            m2. (c1528) George Hay, 7th Earl of Erroll (d 30.01.1573-4)
2 CONT *****                    b. Robert Robertson of Dalcabon
2 CONT *****                    c. .... etc. 
