3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Fraser-5th-of-Lovat/6000000011747849930?through=6000000002225026281 & https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Dunbar/6000000011748053429?through=6000000002225026281
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugh Lovat''' (born c. 1436 - died c. 1500/1501) was summoned to Parliament as '''Lord Fraser of Lovat''' sometime between 1456 and 1464.  According to James Balfour Paul, Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat died before 14 October 1501
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugh_Fraser,_1st_Lord_Lovat Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat] at  Wikipedia 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to James Balfour Paul's 1908 volume 5 of ''The Scots Peerage'', Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat was the son of Thomas Fraser of Lovat but it is not known who Thomas's wife was. Hugh succeeded his father before May 1455 and a
2 CONC s a minor was put under the care of Archibald Douglas, Earl of Moray (d. 1455).[1]  
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard Burke, in his 1869 ''A Genealogical And Heraldic Dictionary of The Peerage And Baronetage of The British Empire'', designates the same Hugh Fraser as the “3rd Lord Lovat” and says that he was the son of Hugh Fraser, 2nd Lo
2 CONC rd Lovat and his wife who was a sister of David Wemyss "Of that Ilk", and the grandson of Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat (died 1440) and his wife Janet who was a sister of William Fenton "Of that Ilk".[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family tree published by the modern ''Clan Fraser of Lovat organization'' agrees with James Balfour Paul in designating him as '''Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat''' and that he was the son of Thomas Fraser of Lovat.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke stated that he married Lady Margaret, daughter of the Earl of Glamis and was succeeded by his son, Thomas Fraser, 4th of Lovat.[2] However, according to James Balfour Paul, Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat married Violetta, daugh
2 CONC ter of Patrick Lyon, 1st Lord Glamis (d. 1459) and they had the following children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas Fraser, 2nd Lord Lovat (heir and successor).
2 CONT # Margaret Fraser, married Hector de Kilmalew and had a son, Alexander.
2 CONT # Egidia Fraser, who married Ferquhard Mackintosh, 12th of Mackintosh.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The modern Clan Fraser of Lovat organization states that Hugh Fraser, 1st Lord Lovat also had a son called Hugh Fraser from who descend the cadet branches, the Frasers of Fairfield, Merkinch, Aberchalder, Foyers, Kinmonarie, and D
2 CONC unchea.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
