3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU gg-gd/o James I, King of Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Lambe/4999403641320055080
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Elizabeth Gray (c. 1464 – bef. 19 January 1529/1530)==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Overview===
2 CONT Elizabeth Gray was a noblewoman belonging to the Scottish Clan Gray. Born around 1464, her life spanned the late 15th and early 16th centuries, defined by high-profile aristocratic marriages that linked her to several prominent Sc
2 CONC ottish peerage families. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family and Lineage===
2 CONT Elizabeth was the daughter of '''Andrew Gray, 2nd Lord Gray''' (c. 1446–1514)—a prominent political figure, Privy Councillor, and Justiciary—and his first wife, '''Janet Keith''' (daughter of Sir Robert de Keith). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriages and Engagements===
2 CONT As documented in *The Scots Peerage* and contemporary records, Elizabeth's marital and betrothal history includes:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''John Lyon, 4th Lord Glamis'''
2 CONT #* '''Married:''' Circa 18 May 1487.
2 CONT #* '''Details:''' Through this union, she became Lady Glamis. John Lyon passed away around 1500, leaving Elizabeth a widow. 
2 CONT #* '''Notable Issue:''' 
2 CONT #** George Lyon, 5th Lord Glamis (died c. 1505)
2 CONT #** John Lyon, 6th Lord Glamis (born c. 1491, died 1528)
2 CONT #** Alexander Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Walter Drummond, Master of Drummond (Engagement / Contract)'''
2 CONT #* '''Contract Date:''' January 1502.
2 CONT #* '''Details:''' As a wealthy and prominent widow (following the death of Lord Glamis), a formal marriage contract was drawn up between Elizabeth Gray and Walter Drummond (born c. 1492). However, this union never culminated in a 
2 CONC wedding. Walter ultimately went on to marry '''Elizabeth Graham''' in February 1514, while Elizabeth Gray pursued other matches.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly'''
2 CONT #* '''Married:''' After 27 July 1511 (confirmed via a royal charter on that date granting her, as the widow/Lady Glamis, lands in Banff and Strathbogie).
2 CONT #* '''Details:''' Following this marriage, she was styled as the Countess of Huntly. Alexander Gordon died in 1524.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes'''
2 CONT #* '''Married:''' Before June 1525 (anchored by a charter detailing the lands and barony of Ballinbreich).
2 CONT #* '''Details:''' Her final marriage made her the Countess of Rothes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT Elizabeth died prior to '''19 January 1529/30'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT While Rothesay on Bute Island is a prominent historic location with deep ties to Scottish nobility, contemporary authoritative records (such as *The Scots Peerage*) do not explicitly document Rothesay as Elizabeth Gray's actual de
2 CONC ath place. Her death is formally anchored by administrative and estate records prior to 19 January 1529/1530, making any specific geographic location of death speculative.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Confusion and Misattribution===
2 CONT In various online family trees and legacy genealogical records, Elizabeth Gray is sometimes egregiously misidentified as the wife of '''John Lamb''' of Trimley in Suffolk (who died in 1495), occasionally appearing under speculativ
2 CONC e composite names like "Mary" or "Elizabeth May Gray Lamb" with overlapping dates. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This is a severe and completely unfounded historical mix-up. As a high-ranking Scottish peeress whose life, vast estates, and successive marriages to Lord Glamis, the Earl of Huntly, and the Earl of Rothes are meticulously verifie
2 CONC d through contemporary Scottish charters, legal records, and *The Scots Peerage*, Elizabeth Gray of Scottish nobility had zero connection to a Suffolk yeoman or merchant like John Lamb. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lamb's actual wife remains unknown in contemporary documentation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===This is wrong:
2 CONT
2 CONT from:  https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/137277981/elizabeth-may-lambe
2 CONT
2 CONT "Elizabeth May Gray Lambe BIRTH:	1456 Huntly, Aberdeenshire, Scotland DEATH:	19 Jan 1529 (aged 72–73) Scotland BURIAL:	Unknown, Specifically: Unknown MEMORIAL ID:	137277981 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth May Gray Lambe (1456 Huntly, Aberdeenshire, Scotland-1/19/1529 Scotland) was born the daughter of Andrew Gray and Janet Keith Gray.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her known siblings were: Patrick Gray and Isobel Gray.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Lyon Lambe (1451-1495). She was said to have married twice after that.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their possible children were: George Lambe, John Lambe born (abt 1488-), Alexander Lambe and in some trees; Richard Lambe (1490-1495), (my line) (sp. Agnes Ford (1494-)), Cecylle Lambe (abt 1492-) and Alys (1494-) Lambe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to the many Lamb sites and my Lamb relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members: Spouse: John Lambe 1451–1495.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Richard Thomas Lambe 1490–1580."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # http://www.fkrug.com/PhpGedView/individual.php?pid=I7368&ged=Krug-Eckermann.ged&tab=0&PHPSESSID=5b928429b8efb987b0276e086de351c8
2 CONT # https://www.patrickspeople.scot/ourfamily/2941.htm cites 
2 CONT ## 1 e-books, The Scots Peerage ed. Sir James Balfour Paul vol. 8 (1911).
2 CONT ## 2 e-books, The Scots Peerage ed. Sir James Balfour Paul vol. 4 (1907).
2 CONT ## 3 e-books, Historical Records of the Family of Leslie 1067-1869 vol. 2 by Col. Leslie of Balquhain (1869).
