2 CONT 13. ALEXANDER6 GUTHRIE (ANDREW5, DAVID4, ALEXANDER3, DAVID2, ALEXANDER1) died October 1587. He married ISOBEL WOOD, daughter of WILLIAM WOOD. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ALEXANDER GUTHRIE:
2 CONT
2 CONT This laird is one of the subscribing barons to the articles agreed upon in the general assembly of the kirk, in July, 1567, and also one of those, to the bond or association, for supporting the king and his government, after Queen
2 CONC  Mary's resignation. He was assassinated at his house of Inverpeffer, where he was residing, by his cousin, Patrick Gairden of Gairden, in consequence of a feud that had arisen between the two families. He was a leading Presbyteri
2 CONC an. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for ISOBEL WOOD: OF BONNYTON 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of ALEXANDER GUTHRIE and ISOBEL WOOD are: 
2 CONT *1. 16.	i.	 	V LAIRD OF GUTHRIE ALEXANDER7 GUTHRIE.
2 CONT *2. 17.	ii.	 	WILLIAM GUTHRIE, d. 1622.
2 CONT *3. 	iii.	 	GABRIEL GUTHRIE. Provost of the collegiate church, of Guthrie who was living 15 November, 1583. . 
