1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "JAMES SCRIMGEOUR, son and heir-apparent of Sir John Scrimgeour, had a royal charter of the lands of Glastre, or Glassary, co. Argyll, and Inverkeithing, co. Fife, 27 January 1459-60.11 He had succeeded his father before 13 August
2 CONC  1463, when he appended his seal as Constable of Dundee to a charter of William Maxwell of Teling."
2 CONT
2 CONT from The Scots Peerage
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Scrymgeour of Dudhope1 
2 CONT M, #16965, d. 1478 
2 CONT Last Edited=14 Jan 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Scrymgeour of Dudhope was the son of Sir John Scrymgeour and Isabel Oliphant.2 
2 CONT He married Margaret Maitland.2 He died in 1478.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Constable of Dundee.3 He lived at Dudhope, Angus, Scotland.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir James Scrymgeour of Dudhope
2 CONT
2 CONT #    Egidia Scrymgeour+3
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir James Scrymgeour of Dudhope and Margaret Maitland
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Mariot Scrymgeour+4 d. 1518
2 CONT #     Sir James Scrymgeour+2 d. 1504
2 CONT #     Elizabeth Scrymgeour+2
2 CONT #     John Scrymgeour+2 d. Oct 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Scrymgeour-7
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said that James married twice some saying firstly Janet Lyon and secondly to Margaret Maitland who was identified as mother to his younger son and perhaps other younger family,
2 CONT
2 CONT James had issue although the order is not known but probably by first marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Matilda who married to Robert Graham of Fintry about 1479 and was mother to John Graham of Balargus..
2 CONT # Jane who about 1475 married Walter Ogston of that Ilk and had daughters
2 CONT # . Elizabeth who appears to have married John Sandilands of Calder
2 CONT # James his heir
2 CONT # Mariota who married Robert Arbuthnott of that Ilk contract 10 Sep 1475.
2 CONT
2 CONT and by his second wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT #John designed after 1490 as Master John Scrymgeour of Glassary.
2 CONT #Katherine married Dougal Campbell of Auchinbreck contract 26 Apr 1490
2 CONT
2 CONT But note: Per Vol. 1 of Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition (2003), James' mother is Isabella Oliphant, and the mother of his children is Margaret Maitland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Maitland-7
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Maitland was born about 1440. She married as second wife to James Scrymgeour, Constable of Dundee about 1465 and was mother to his younger children.
2 CONT
2 CONT She survived the Constbable who died about 1478.
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow, Margaret married about 1480 as second wife to David Hering of Lethendy.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT At Lethendy on 8 October 1490, when David Hering granted his son and heir James Hering of Cluny the lands of Lethendy and others in Fife and Berwickshire, he reserved a terce for Margaret Maitland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
