1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAVID SCRYMGEOUR OF SONAHARD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Wedderburn Book, David Scrymgeour of Sonahard, here treated, is a younger son of Sir John Scryrngeour, constable of Dundee. He is noticed in the witness list of a document issued by his father on 11 March 1458.
2 CONC  [https://archive.org/details/wedderburnbookv100wedd/page/169/mode/1up Wedderburn Book I: 169]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 August 1461: Letters of reversion by Adam Cant, burgess of Edinburgh, in favour of James Scrimgeour, son and heir of John Scrimgeour of Dudwp, constable of Dundee, in respect of an annualrent from lands of Bordlande in barony
2 CONC  of Inverkething. Witnesses: David Scrimgeour of Sonharde; David Maxwell; James Erewyn; James Matlande; David Scrymgeour; Herbert Chattow; Thomas of Fentoun; Thomas Laing, notary public; Robert Marschel, clerk. Seal on tag. [https
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f28%2f32&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+scrimgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of 
2 CONC Dalhousie, Additional Dalhousie Papers, reference GD45/28/32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
