1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Mary Stewart married Sir William Abernathy, 6th of Saltoun
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps36/ps36_451.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT NameLady Mary STEWART Of Albany , F Birth Dateabt 1366 Birth PlaceDoune Castle, Stirlingshire, Scotland FatherDuke Robert STEWART 1st Of Albany, Regent Of Scotland , M (1339-1420) MotherCountess Margaret GRAHAM Of Menteith , F (~1
2 CONC 334-1380)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses
2 CONT
2 CONT 1Sir William ABERNETHY 6th Of Saltoun , M Birth Dateabt 1365 Birth PlaceSaltoun, East Lothian, Scotland Death Date1420
2 CONT
2 CONT Death PlaceSaltoun, East Lothian, Scotland Marr Dateabt 1385 Marr PlaceSaltoun, East Lothian, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT William , M (~1386-1411)
2 CONT
2 CONT  James , M (~1388->1446)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Patrick , M (~1390-)
2 CONT
2 CONT  John , M (~1392-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for William (Spouse 1) William de Abernethy, sixth of Saltoun, must have succeeded his father about the end of the fourteenth century. He was probably born not later than 1365, if he is the person who witnessed a charter gra
2 CONC nted by Sir James de Douglas, Lord of Dalkeith in 1388. He also witnessed, in 1397, a grant by George, Earl of Angus to James Sandilands of the wardshhip of his son and heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of ‘le Quhew,’ probably influenze, in 1420,
2 CONT
2 CONT having married a daughter of Robert, Duke of Albany. If he had only one wife, her name was Maria, as in 1404, he got a charter from King Robert III to himself as ‘dilectus confederatus noster,’ and Mary, his wife, of certain lands
2 CONC  in the barony of Rethy and Kingaltuy on his own resignation. But, as the lady is not designed niece of the King, this seems rather to indicate that she was a second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir William, killed at the battle of Harlaw, 24 July 1411 … 2. James. There is a charter, 26 July 1393, by Archibald, Earl of Douglas, to James de Abernethy … 3. Patrick, witness to a charter by the Regent Albany … 4. John. The
2 CONC re is some ground for believing that the John Abernethy who received from Sir William Abernethy …
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE SCOTS PEERAGE, ed. by Sir James Balfour Paul, Vol VII, Edinburgh, 1906, pp. 405-06.
