2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stirnet's "Lyon01" page (which is based on ''[http://www.stirnet.com/sources-and-acknowledgements/#TSP The Scots Peerage]'' and ''[http://www.stirnet.com/sources-and-acknowledgements/#BP A Genealogical and Heraldic History of t
2 CONC he Peerage and Baronetage]'' (AKA ''Burke's Peerage''), 1934 edition; see link below) and The Peerage's record for this John (which is based on based on ''[http://www.stirnet.com/sources-and-acknowledgements/#TCP The Complete Peer
2 CONC age of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant], new ed.'' and ''[http://www.stirnet.com/sources-and-acknowledgements/#BP A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage and 
2 CONC Baronetage]'' (AKA ''Burke's Peerage''), 2003 edition; see link below) do not mention this John having any kind of marital or sexual union with anyone other than Jean/Janet Keith (daughter of Robert Keith by Elizabeth Douglas).  F
2 CONC urthermore, they do not mention any use of the surname [https://www.geni.com/surnames/holmes Holmes] by this John, or the existence of any issue of this John that had or used that surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT The Life Summary of Sir John When Sir John Lyon 7th Lord Glamis was born about October 1515, in Forfar, Angus, Scotland, United Kingdom, his father, John Lyon, was 24 and his mother, Janet Douglas, was 20. He married Janet Keith o
2 CONC n 5 February 1544, in Glamis, Forfarshire, Scotland. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 2 daughters. He died on 3 October 1592, in Middlesex, England, United Kingdom, at the age of 77, and was buried in Scotland, United 
2 CONC Kingdom.
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lyon, 7th Lord Glamis is the son of John Lyon, 6th Lord Glamis and Janet Douglas. He married Janet Keith, daughter of Robert Keith, Master of Marischal and Lady Elizabeth Douglas, on 6 February 1542/43.2 He died before 18 Sep
2 CONC tember 1559.
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Lyon, 7th Lord Glamis gained the title of 7th Lord Glamis.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT      He was imprisoned and sentenced to be executed, but was respited until he should attain majority, in the interim, he was orderd to be closely confined and his estates declared forfeited. On the death of King James V, he was r
2 CONC eleased and restored to his estates and honours by Parliament, 15 March 1542/3.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Lyon, 7th Lord Glamis and Janet Keith
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Sir Thomas Lyon, Master of Glamis
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Margaret Lyon+1 d. Dec 1625
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.John Lyon, 8th Lord Glamis+ b. c 1544, d. 17 Mar 1578
2 CONT
