1 NAME Elizabeth Ruthven, Countess of Erroll
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY ELIZABETH RUTHVEN Countess of Erroll ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Elizabeth Ruthven, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Ruthven-1st-Lord-Ruthven/5464458449390117010?through=6000000002187985208 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Forbes/600
2 CONC 0000002187985186?through=6000000002187985208. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Elizabeth Ruthven, here treated married William, fifth Earl of Erroll
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Elizabeth Ruthven, here treated, married (contract 9 December 1523) Ninian, Lord Ross of Hawkhead and Melville. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/259/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 259]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 December 1523: Charter by which Ninian, Lord Ross and Melville, confirms that he has given certain lands to Elizabeth Ruthven, Countess of Errol. The lands in question were to be held by Elizabeth and the male heirs procreate
2 CONC d between her and Ninian. Lord Ross and Melville. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 12 December 1523. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/55/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 24
2 CONC 4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 October 1523: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms possession of the lands of Argarth, in the barony of Erroll and sheriffdom of Perth, to William, Earl of Erroll. The lands in q
2 CONC uestion had previously been resigned in favour of the Earl's deceased father, also William, Earl of Erroll, by John Duke of Albany. The late Earl and his wife Elizabeth Ruthven held Argarth in conjunct fee and liferent. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/212/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 972]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitlan
2 CONC d Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility
2 CONC  of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume IV. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1907), 597 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/qr/ruthven2.php Stirnet: Ruthven 2]'''
