1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Jean Stewart===
2 CONT * Birth: 1350, Scotland
2 CONT * Death: 	1404, Scotland Also known as Johanna
2 CONT
2 CONT Tenth and youngest child, sixth daughter of Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland and his first wife, Elizbeth Mure. Lady Jean was the granddaughter of Sir Walter Stewart and Margory de Brus, Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan and Janet Mure
2 CONC , daughter of Ronald Mure of Pokellie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jean was the wife of Sir John Keith, the son of sir William Keith and Margaret Fraser. They were married 17 Jan 1374 and had a son:
2 CONT # Robert Keith, Lord of Strathkyn d 1401
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Keith died 18 Mar or 27 Dec 1375.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, Lady Jean was the wife of Sir John Lyon of Glamis, King's secretary, Chamberlain of Scotland and Keeper of the Privy Seal. They were married between June and October of 1376 and had
2 CONT
2 CONT # one son, Sir John Lyon who married Elizabeth Graham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John the father died 04 Nov 1382, killed during an argument in Menmuir, Scotland by Sir James Lindsay of Crawford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thirdly, Lady Jean was the wife of Sir James Sandilands of Calder, son of sir James and his wife, Eleanor. They were married about Nov 1384 and had 
2 CONT
2 CONT # one son, Sir James Sandilands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James and his son were assassinated Dec of 1426.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jean was buried at the Abbey Church of Scone with her second husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Johanna. She married John Lyon between 27 Jun 1376–02 Oct 1377. She married James Sunderlands Sandilands about 1384. She married John De Keith on about 17 January I373.
2 CONT
