2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Lady Eupheme Graham:
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10810.htm#i108095
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Eupheme Graham [1]
2 CONT *F, #108095, 
2 CONT *d. between 1 August 1468 and 1 November 1468
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.8%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Eupheme Graham and Robert Stewart, Master of Fife were engaged on 4 May 1414 but the marriage did not take place.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She and Sir Walter Stewart were engaged on 5 September 1415 but the marriage did not take place.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas, son of Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Lady of Galloway, between 24 February 1423 and 26 April 1425.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton, son of Sir James Hamilton, 5th of Cadzow and Janet Livingston, after 25 February 1440/41.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died between 1 August 1468 and 1 November 1468.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Patrick Graham, Earl of Strathearn and Eupheme Stewart, Countess of Caithness.[2] 
2 CONT *She gained the title of Countess of Strathern. 
2 CONT *As a result of her marriage, Lady Eupheme Graham was styled as Countess of Douglas on 17 August 1424. 
2 CONT *As a result of her marriage, Lady Eupheme Graham was styled as Lady Hamilton on 28 June 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Eupheme Graham and Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas
2 CONT *1. Margaret Douglas+[5] d. bt Jan 1473 - 1475
2 CONT *2. William Douglas, 6th Earl of Douglas [6] b. c 1424, d. 24 Nov 1440
2 CONT *3. David Douglas [7] b. b 1439, d. 24 Nov 1440
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Eupheme Graham and James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Hamilton+[8] b. bt 1442 - 1443, d. a Mar 1517
2 CONT
