2 DATE 24 JUL 1411
2 PLAC just north of 
2 ADDR
3 CITY Inverurie
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Sheriff of Angus
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "...The gallant sheriff's eldest son, Sir Alexander Ovilvy of Auchterhouse, was "the gracious gud Lord Ogilvey" of the Ballad of Harlaw:
2 CONT >For faith and magnanimity
2 CONT >He had few fellows in the field, 
2 CONT >Yet fell by fatal destiny,
2 CONT >For he nae ways wad grant to yield.
2 CONT "In that tremendous conflict north of Aberdeen against Donald of the Isles in 1411, Sir Alexander and his eldest son, George Ogilvy, were among the slain."
2 CONT '''Source:''' [https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Highland_Clans_of_Scotland_Their_His/pmgZAAAAIAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=Sir+Alexander+Ogilvy+Auchterhouse+1411&pg=PA453-IA4&printsec=frontcover ''The Highland Clans of Scotland: an
2 CONC d Traditions''; "Clan Ogilvy"], Volume 2.
2 CONT ///////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT >Name: Sir Alexander OGILVY of Auchterhouse, M 
2 CONT >Birth Date: abt 1366 
2 CONT >Birth Place: Auchterhouse, Forfarshire, Scotland
2 CONT >Death Date: 7/24/1411
2 CONT >Death Memo: Killed at the battle of Harlaw 
2 CONT >Father: Sir Knight Walter OGILVY Auchterhouse, M (~1345-1392) 
2 CONT >Mother: Heiress Isabel RAMSEY of Auchterhouse, F (~1355-)
2 CONT >>Spouse: Lady Auchterhouse, F 
2 CONT >>Birth Date: abt 1380 
2 CONT >>Married Date: abt 1395 
2 CONT >>'''Children:''' 
2 CONT >>George, M (~1395-1411)
2 CONT >>Patrick, M (~1397-1429)
2 CONT >>Andrew, M (~1395-)
2 CONT >>David, M (-<1440)
2 CONT >>Marjory, F (~1403->1476) Notes for Sir Alexander OGILVY Of Auchterhouse ... his [Walter’s] marriage with >>Isabel Ramsay, daughter and heiress of Sir Malcolm Ramsay, Lord of Auchterhouse
2 CONT
2 CONT He had issue:
2 CONT 1. Sir Alexander Ogilvy of Auchterhouse, Sheriff of Angus ...
2 CONT 2. Walter, ancestor of the Airlie family. 3. John of Ogilvy, ancestory of the family of Ogilvy of Innerquharity. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''' THE SCOTS PEERAGE, ed. by Sir James Balfour Paul, Vol I, Edinburgh, 1906, p. 108-11.
2 CONT /////////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT Sir Alexander Ogilvey of Auchterhouse, Sheriff of Angus.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was present at the battle of Harlaw, received many charters from King Robert III between 1398 and 1404, and as a reward for his service received from that king an annualrent out of the customs of Dundee.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died after 24 July 1411, at the Battle of Harlaw.  He had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. George also had been killed at Harlaw. He had issue. 2. Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Grandon and Auchterhouse ... 3. Sir Andrew Ogilvy of Inchmartin ... 4. David Ogilvy of Balmuto ... 5. Marjory, married to David, third Earl of Crawfo
2 CONC rd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE SCOTS PEERAGE, ed. by Sir James Balfour Paul, Vol I, Edinburgh, 1906, p. 109-10
2 CONT ///////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT SIR ALEXANDER OGILVIE of Auchterhouse, whose grandson, another Sir Alexander, had only one daughter, Margaret, his sole heiress, who conveyed the estate and dignity of Sheriff to James Stewart, Earl of Buchan, her husband, who was
2 CONC  Lord High-chamberlain of Scotland, anno 1471. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The male line of Sir Alexander, eldest son of Sir Walter of Auchterhouse, thus ending, the representation devolved upon the next heir-male descended of his brother, Sir Walter, of Lintrethan ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE PEERAGE OF GREAT BRITAIN AND IRELAND, by Robert Pollard, vol. 1, p. 123.
