2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/17/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 17]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 September 1472: nstrument of resignation by Agnes Johnstoun [Johnston], wife of Alexander Abircromy [Abercromby], laird of Ley, in hands of Thomas, bishop of Aberdeen, of lands of Ditouch and Braco, in lordship of Galcholis,
2 CONC  sheriffdom of Banff, for new infeftment in favour of herself and her said spouse, and of Alexander Abircromy [Abercromby], their son, and Jonet Ogilvy, daughter of James Ogilvy of Deskfurde [Deskford], his [future] spouse. Notary
2 CONC : Robert Leis [Lees], priest, Aberdeen diocese. Procurator: Walter Ogilvy of Auchlevin.
2 CONT Witnesses; Thomas [Spens]. bishop of Aberdeen, sirs and masters Duncan Lichtoun [Lichton], chancellor, Robert Stewart, archdeacon, Andrew Liel [Lyell], treasurer, Thomas Waus [Vaus] and John Myrtoun [Myrton], canons of Aberdeen. [
2 CONC https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of For
2 CONC glen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/1/1]''''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 November 1484: Obligation (in Scots) by Sir James Ogilvy of Deskfurd knight to William earl of Eroll lord Hay and constable of Scotland his heirs, executors and assignees. The earl having sold to Sir James his lands of Knokd
2 CONC urne, in the forest of Boyne and sheriffdom of Banff, redeemable by payment of 17 score and 10 merks Scots before Martinmas next, and it being provided that if the lands were not then redeemed, Sir James should pay to the earl 210
2 CONC  merks Scots for the "utir waill" of the lands; therefore Sir James obliged himself in that event to pay the said 210 merks, in full payment of 28 score merks for the lands, at Yule next. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrson
2 CONC linecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH1%2f6%2f114&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland, Photocopies of Erroll Charters, reference RH1/6/114]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 January 1492: Instrument of Protest by Christina Lesly [Leslie], relict of William of St. Clair [Sinclair], Master of Caithness,and Lord of the barony of Newburgh, cited before the Official of Aberdeen at the instance of Sir
2 CONC  James Ogilvy [Ogilvie] of Desfurde [Deskford] and Patrick Gordon of Methlic [Methlick]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD33%2f65%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland, Marquess of Aberdeen and Temair, reference GD33/65/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 January 1493-94: Bond of manrent by Andrew Dun of Rate to Sir James Ogilvy of Deskfurd and James Ogilvy of Dunnaketh, his son and heir. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD248%2f3
2 CONC 431%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), reference GD248/3431/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1499: Reversion, by Thomas Annande to Sir James Ogilvy of Deskfuyrde. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f421%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=152
2 CONC 0&di=y National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous small collections of family, business and other papers, reference GD1/421/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 April 1504: Instrument narrating decreet arbitral, 19 March 1503-04, made by William, bishop of Aberdeen, James Ogilvy of Deskfurd and Walter Ogilvy of the Boyne, kts., and Andrew Elphinstone of Scheves, arbiters in action be
2 CONC tween William Meldrum of Five and Elizabeth Barclay, his spouse, on one part, and George Meldrum of Petkerry, his son and apparent heir, on other part, relative to disputes over lands of Jakistoun and others in barony of Formertin
2 CONC , sheriffdom of Aberdeen. Seal gone. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD248%2f397%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland
2 CONC , Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), reference GD248/397/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
