1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN MAXWELL OF NETHER POLLOCK===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1371-1372 Robert of Maxwell lord of Mernes granted to his kinsman Sir John of Maxwell knight, lord of Nether Pollok, and the lady Isabel his wife, the whole lands of Dryppis in the barony of Kilbrydeshire in the sheriffdom o
2 CONC f Lanark, reserving to himself and his heirs the moothill (mons) nearest to the town of Dryppis, on the top of which a stone was erected, for holding his courts there so often as he should happen to hold pleas on the people of the
2 CONC  said lands for wrong done to himself or his heirs only. [https://archive.org/details/originesparochia01bann/page/508/mode/1up Origines Parochiales Scotiae I: p. 508]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://thepeerage.com/p244.htm#i2433 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Maxwell of Pollok was the son of Sir John Maxwell of Pollok.2 He married, firstly, Elizabeth de Lindsay, daughter of Sir James de Lindsay of Crawford and Egidia Stewart.2 He married, secondly, Elizabeth de Saint Michel.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir John Maxwell of Pollok and Elizabeth de Lindsay
2 CONT # Egidia Maxwell+4
2 CONT # Sir John Maxwell of Pollok+4
