1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From ODNB:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Kennedy's successor, Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure (d. 1408x29), who had been a hostage in England for King David's ransom in 1357, appears to have been twice married, first to Marion Sandilands of Calder and then to Agnes Ma
2 CONC xwell of Pollok, but Sir James Kennedy (d. 1408), the eldest son of the second rather than the first marriage, was during his father's lifetime designated as heir to the family's lands and titles, possibly following his marriage t
2 CONC o Mary Stewart, a daughter of King Robert III. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA376&lpg=PA381&dq=Duncan+Kennedy+of+dalgabre&id=X6xRAAAAMAAJ&ots=xGiQwWFjkm&output=text Seldens of Virginia] and Allied Families, Volume 1.  By Mary Selden Kennedy.  Page 378
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife, Agnes, daughter '''(sic: sister)'''of Sir Robert Maxwell of Calderwood, he had three sons, John, Thomas, and David, who was one of the retinue of knights and esquires who attended Margaret of Scotland into France on h
2 CONC er marriage to the Dauphin, Louis, Anno Domini 1436.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://digital.nls.uk/histories-of-scottish-families/archive/95363711?mode=transcription
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, eldest son of John Kennedy, married, first, Marion, daughter of Sir James Sandilands of Calder, by whom he had three sons, Gilbert, John, and Roland ; and secondly, Agnes Maxwell, daughter of Sir Joh
2 CONC n Maxwell of Pollok, by his wife, Isabel Lindsay, daughter of Sir James Lindsay of Crawford, by the Princess Egidia, sister of Robert II. The eldest son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy and Agnes Max- well was James, who married the Princes
2 CONC s Mary, daughter of Robert III., in 1403, and by her had six sons. James was killed by his brother GILBERT, in consequence of the preference shown to the second family (they having been disinherited to make way for James).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps33/ps33_438.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # James , M (~1384-<1408)
2 CONT # Alexander , M (~1386->1415)
2 CONT # Hugh “Come With The Penny” , M (~1388-)
2 CONT # John , M (~1390-<1473)
2 CONT # Thomas , M (~1392-)
2 CONT # David , M (~1394-)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps33/ps33_438.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Maxwell married before 1384 Gilbert Kennedy, Knt., of Dunure, Ayrshire, son and heir of John Kennedy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT # James
2 CONT # Alexander
2 CONT # Hugh (of Ardstynchar)
2 CONT # John, Knt. (of blairquhan),
2 CONT # Thomas (of Kirkoswald and Bargany), and
2 CONT # David.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Agnes, was living 2 November 1404. Sir Gilbert Kennedy was living in November 1408
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Agnes, wife of Gilbert Kennedy, styled “kings Kinswoman” by King Robert II in 1404.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: MAGNA CARTA ANCESTRY, by Douglas Richardson, ed. by Kimball G. Everingham, Salt Lake City, Utah, pp. 536-7.
2 CONT
2 CONT ================
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p244.htm#i2431
2 CONT * Agnes Maxwell1 
2 CONT * F, #2432, b. before 1358
2 CONT * Last Edited=27 May 2003
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Maxwell was born before 1358.1 She was the daughter of Sir John Maxwell and Isabel de Lindsay.1 She married Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, son of John Kennedy of Dunure.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Kennedy.1  [ Not buying that - MARRIED NAMES IN 14th century ? !!! ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Agnes Maxwell and Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure+ d. a 8 Nov 14081 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 40. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 
2 CONC 106th edition. 
2 CONT
