1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM MAXWELL OF AIKENHEAD===
2 CONT
2 CONT William Maxwell of Aikenhead is the son of Sir John Maxwell of Pollock and his first wife Isabella Lindsay. [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/15/mode/1up/search/akinhead Memoirs of the Maxwell of Pollock, i, 
2 CONC p. 15]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 February 1423:  John Maxwell of Calderwood gave the lands of Kilcadroblaw in the barony of Maldisle to his uncle William Maxwell of Aikenhead. For greater security William Maxwell of Aikenhead obtained a charter of confirmation 
2 CONC under the Great Seal of Scotland on 26 July 1424. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/2/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1424-1513, charter number 9 on p. 2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 May 1421: William Maxwell of Aikenhead witnessed two charters issued at the Castle of Cumnock on 6 May 1421 and 31 May 1423 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/12/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotla
2 CONC nd, A. D. 1424-1513, charter numbers65 and 66  pp. 12-12] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/n6/mode/1up William Fraser, Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock, Vol. I. Memoirs & Charters (Edinburgh 1863), 497 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev200fras#page/n6/mode/1up William Fraser, Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock, Vol. II. Correspondence (Edinburgh 1863), 453 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/495/mode/1up/search/akinhead Pedigree of Maxwell of Aikenhead]
