1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ROBERT MAXWELL OF CALDERWOOD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Maxwell of Calderwood is the second the son of Sir John Maxwell of Nether Pollock and his wife Isabella Lindsay. [https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/462/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock
2 CONC  I: 462] His father gave him the lands of Calderwood and his possession of the same was ratified by the feudal superior, James Stewart, Lord of the Barony of Kilbride, by a charter of confirmation dated 21 October 1400. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/138/mode/1up?view=theater Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock I: 138-9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death and Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Maxwell of Calderwood, here treated, travelled to France in 1420 in aid of Charles VII. He was mortally wounded soon after landing there, He made his will at Chinon, there, on the 7 September 1420, and it was ratifie
2 CONC d on the 3 April 1421, before which date he was in all probability dead. He was certainly dead before 6 May 1421, when his son John witnessed a charter, in which he is designated Dominus de Calderwood. Sir Robert was buried in the
2 CONC  church of the Friars Minors in the city of Angers in France. [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/463/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs I: 463]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Child of First Marriage ==
2 CONT
