1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAVID EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK AND EDNAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000020816007489?through=6000000008248653864 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Isab
2 CONC ella-Stewart/6000000002174773680?through=6000000008248653864 [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa01bann/page/n69/mode/1up Inchaffrey Registrum: Appendix 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, is the cousin of https://www.geni.com/people/Euphemia-Stewart-Countess-of-Strathearn/6000000002166210799 Identified as such, on 18 March 1414 she confirmed the grant of Tull
2 CONC yallan previously made to David's father. [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa01bann/page/n69/mode/1up Inchaffrey Registrum: Appendix 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, died before 22 September 1426.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/10/mode/1up RMS, 1324-1513: charter number 61]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Maitland/6000000008248653868?through=6000000008248653864 [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/edmonstone1.php Stirnet: Ed
2 CONC monstone 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176654013849?through=6000000008248653864
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from The Douglas Book===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 April 1420: Witnessed by Johanne de Edmonstone, fratre germano Dauid de Edmonstone domini eiusdem, and others. [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/53/mode/1up The Douglas Book. Volume III, p. 54]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Register of Inchaffray Abbey===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 March 1414: Confirmation by Eufemia Countess Palatine of Stratherne in her viduity (with the consent of Walter Earl of Athol and Caithness her uncle and governor) to her cousin David of Edmonstone, of former grants to his fa
2 CONC ther Sir John of Edmonstone, of the lands of Tullyallan. At Perth 18th March 1414. [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa01bann/page/n69/mode/1up Inchaffrey Registrum: Appendix 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 August 1418: Charter by Archibald of Douglas, the son and heir of Archibald Earl of Douglas, confirming the grants of the lands of Tullyallan by the said Earl, and by Patrick Earl Palatine and Eufemia Countess Palatine of St
2 CONC ratherne, his wife, and cousin of the said Archibald Douglas, in favour of the said Sir John and David of Edmonstone. At Edinburgh, 10th August 1418. [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa01bann/page/n69/mode/1up Inchaffrey
2 CONC  Registrum: Appendix 37]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 January 1411-12: Charter by John Stewart, Earl of Buchan and king's chamberlain in favour of David Wintoun of the lands of Andoyt (Andat), in the earldom of Buchan and sheriffdom of Aberdeen, following his resignation; lands 
2 CONC to be held to him and his spouse, Janet Keith, the longer liver of them and their heirs male, whom failing to Ingram Wintoun, David's cousin, and his heirs male, whom failing to David's male heirs whatsoever bearing the surname Wi
2 CONC ntoun and their arms. Witneses: Malcolm Fleming, lord of Biggar; Alexander Seton, lord of Gordon; and DAVID EDMONDSTON, our cousins. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f3%2f1%2f1&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Gordon Family, Earls of Aberdeen, reference GD255/3/1/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 November 1416: CHARTER by Robert, duke of Albanie [Albany], earl of Fyfe [Fife] and of Mentech [Menteith], and governor of Scotland, confirming grant by John de Anand [Annan] de Milis [Miles] to Alexander de Strathachin [Stra
2 CONC chan], of his lands of the barony of Kynnetlis [Kinnettles], in the sheriffdom of Forfare [Forfar]; to be held of the crown for services used and wont. Witnesses, Gilbert, bishop of Aberdeen, chancellor; David de Edmondstound [Edm
2 CONC ondston] and Patrick de Abernethi [Abernethy], grandsons of said duke; Andrew de Hawic [Hawick], rector of Listoun [Liston], the duke's secretary; Walter de Curry, James de Arnut [Arnott] and William Berclai [Barclay], esquires. D
2 CONC ated at Doune in Menteith. (Not in R.M.S.) [Fragment of the Governor's Seal remains]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD68%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df
2 CONC =&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Murray of Lintrose, reference GD68/1/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 September 1426: REX constituit JOHANNEM DE EDMONDSTOUN tutorem dativum administratorem omnium terrarum, etc. Jacobi de Edmondston, filii et heredis Dav. de E. de Edname, infra regnum Scotie usque ad legitimam etatem dicti Ja
2 CONC cobi. ii. 42. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/10/mode/1up RMS, 1324-1513: charter number 61]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 September 1426: REX confirmavit literas Johannis de Edmonstoun, tutoris dativi Jacobi de E. filii et heredis quond. David de E. dom. de Ednam, — [qua concessit ROBERTO DE HERYOT, capellano regis,— Hospitale beate Laurencii d
2 CONC e Ednam, vic. de Roxburgh — vacans per mortem Magistri Alex, de Crychtoun — pro toto tempore vito ejus, cum omnibus terris, redditibus, &c., ad diet. Hospitale spectantibus: — Test. Jon. electo confirmato eccl. Glasguen., D. Jac. 
2 CONC de Douglas dom. de Dalketh, D. Walt, de Ogilvy dom. de Ballician, D. Tho. de Kyrkpatrik dom. de Kilosbarn, militibu.s, et Henrico de Lewynstoun dom. de Manerstoun, scutifero:— Apud Edinburgh, Sep. 25, 1426: Test, ut in carta confi
2 CONC rmata. ii. 58. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/11/mode/1up RMS, 1324-1513: charter number 62]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Register of Dunfermline Abbey===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 April 1554: Jacobus dei gra Rex Scottoru Abbati & quetuj mo'asterij de Dunfmlyn falute • Quia p inq'sicoem de madato nro p vicecomite nrm de Edinburgh fcam & ad capellam n'ram retornata comptu eft q quod Dauid de Edniondston 
2 CONC de eode pater Jacobi de Edmondston lator' pntiu obijt vltio vestit' & sasit vt de feodo ad pace & fide nram de tris de Halys estir & Westir cu pt' jacen infa vicecoitatu de Edinburgh & q diftus Jacobus e legitim' & ppinquior heres
2 CONC  eiusde quod Dauid pris fui de dict tris cii pt' et eft legitie etat' & q dce terre cu pt' de vobis tenet' in capite  vobis pcipim' & madamus qats cum jde Jacobz vobis fecit p dcis tris cu pt' quod de jure facere tenet' sibi vel s
2 CONC uo certo attora latori pntiu sasina dcaru t'aru cu pt' juste hre saciat' & sine dilacoe saluo jure cuiuslibet & hoc nullo modo omittat' Tefte meipo apud Streuelyn vicefio die mefis Aprilis Anno regni nri tricesimo. [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/details/registrumdedunfe00bann/page/284/mode/1up Dunfermline Registrum: 405]'''
2 CONT
