2 CONT From thePeerage.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT      Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany was born in 1362. He was the son of Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany and Margaret Graham, Countess of Menteith. He married, firstly, Joan Douglas before 1389. He married, secondly, Isabel
2 CONC  of Lennox, Countess of Lennox, daughter of Duncan, 8th Earl of Lennox and Helen Campbell, between 17 February 1392 and 8 November 1392. He died on 24 May 1425 at Castle Hill, Stirling, Stirlingshire, Scotland, beheaded. He was bu
2 CONC ried at Church of the Black Friars, Stirling, Stirlingshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany held the office of Justiciar North of the Forth on 2 April 1389.1 Between September 1402 and 1415 he was held prisoner by the English, when he was finally exchanged for the Earl of Northumb
2 CONC erland. He fought in the Battle of Homildon Hill on 14 September 1402 at Homildon Hill, Scotland, where he was taken prisoner. He held the office of Regent of Scotland between 1420 and 1424. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Duke o
2 CONC f Albany [S., 1398] on 3 September 1420. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Fife on 3 September 1420. He succeeded to the title of Earl of Monteith on 3 September 1420. On 25 March 1425 he was attainted and forfeited all of 
2 CONC his honours.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany
