2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Borthwick, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/William-Abernethy-of-Saltoun/6000000003484306877?through=6000000046925102299, who was killed in action at the Battle of Harlaw on 24 July 1411.[http://archiv
2 CONC e.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/96/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 96]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Borthwick, here treated, married her sister's step-son https://www.geni.com/people/William-Douglas/6000000026907315783?through=6000000046925102299, following upon a papal dispensation dated 9 December 1421. [http://arc
2 CONC hive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/96/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Borthwick is the daughter of Sir William Borthwick, 1st of Borthwick.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Borthwick married, firstly, Sir William Abernethy, 7th of Saltoun[1], son of Sir William Abernathy, 6th of Saltoun and Lady Mary Stewart. Her married name became Abernethy in 1413.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #William Abernethy d. 1428
2 CONT #Laurence Abernethy, 1st Lord Saltoun of Abernethy b. c 1400, d. b 13 Mar 1460/61
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, she and William Douglas obtained a marriage license on 9 December 1420. From 9 December 1420, her married name became Douglas. No children are known for that marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT *Robert Douglas, The peerage of Scotland : containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom, from their origin to the present generation, (Edinburgh: R Fleming, 1764), p. 76, digital images, https:
2 CONC //archive.org/details/peerageofscotlan00doug/page/76
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00046213&tree=LEO
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Borthwick-7
