1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALLAN MACDONALD (aka ALLAN MACRUARI) fourth of Moydart===
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 15th century the 4th chief, Allan, wielded power on the west coast. Alan fought in the battle of Harlaw in 1411 when the Highland forces led by the Lord of the Isles defeated those of the Scottish Crown. Charles MacDonald d
2 CONC escribed him in his book "Moidart, Among the Clanranalds" as having "consecrated his life to plunder and rapine". He imprisoned the Macintosh chief and others in the castle dungeon. He was eventually imprisoned by James I and exec
2 CONC uted in 1509.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/bub_gb_CxYXAAAAYAAJ#page/n3/mode/1up The Macdonalds of Clanranald by Alexander Mackenzie, FSA. Scot (A. & W. Mackenzie, Inverness, MDCCCLXXXI), 108 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/historyofmacdlor00mack#page/n8/mode/1up History of the Macdonalds and Lords of the Isles; with Genealogies of the Principal Families of the Name, by Alexander Mackenzie, FSA, Scot., (A. & W. Mackenzie
2 CONC , nverness, MDCCCLXXXI), 534 pp. For Macdonald of Clanranald see pp. 367-437]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mac/macdonald01.php Stirnet: Macdonald 01]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mac/macdonald02.php Stirnet: Macdonald 02]
