1 NOTE {geni:about_me}      Jean Lyon's Profile Family Tree & Genealogy Tools 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Lyon Born July 25, 1556 in Angus, Scotlandmap Daughter of John Lyon and Elizabeth (Abernathy) Lyon Sister of Joan Lyon, Elizabeth (Lyon) Kerr and Patrick Lyon	 Wife of Archibald Douglas — married [date unknown] [location unkn
2 CONC own] Wife of Robert Douglas — married [date unknown] [location unknown] Wife of Alexander Lindsay — married May 31, 1590 in Scotlandmap Mother of Anne Lindsay, William (Douglas) Seventh Earl of Morton, Margaret Lindsay, Elizabeth 
2 CONC Douglas, Margaret Douglas, John Lindsay, Anna Lindsay and Alexander Lindsay	 Died March 1610 in Scotlandmap Profile managers: Andy Askey private message [send private message] and Robert Graham private message [send private messag
2 CONC e] Last modified 26 February 2015. This page has been accessed 181 times. Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jean Lyon was the daughter of John Lyon, 8th Lord Glamis and Elizabeth Abernethy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     She married by contract, firstly, Robert Douglas, Master of Morton, son of William Douglas, 6th Earl of Morton and Lady Agnes Leslie, on 19 March 1582/83. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     She married by contract, secondly, Archibald Douglas, 8th Earl of Angus, son of David Douglas, 7th Earl of Angus and Margaret Hamilton, on 29 July 1587. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     She married, thirdly, Sir Alexander Lindsay, 1st Lord Spynie, son of David Lindsay, 10th Earl of Crawford and Margaret Bethune, on 31 May 1590. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     She died from 7 August 1607 to March 1610. 
2 CONT
2 CONT     From 19 March 1582/83, her married name became Douglas. As a result of her marriage, Jean Lyon was styled as Countess of Angus after 29 July 1587. From 31 May 1590, her married name became Lindsay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Jean Lyon and Archibald Douglas, 8th Earl of Angus
