1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.kristensen.au/OurFamily/ps23/ps23_454.html Our Family History]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT David was born about 1495 son to David Ogilvy grandson to David Ogilvy of Inchmartine.
2 CONT He may have been reared in the household of David Barclay of Collairnie as the latter had attempted to support the claim of David Ogilvy the grandson of David Ogilvy of Inchmartine for infeftment in the lands and barony of Inchmar
2 CONC tine.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 January 1510/11, David was described as "eldest son of the deceased David Ogilvy nepos of the laird of Ynchmarten" when he was principal witness to the Instrument of Sasine given by John Murray sheriff of Fife recording infe
2 CONC ftment of David Barclay in the lands of Collairnie.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://www.kristensen.au/OurFamily/ps23/ps23_453.html cites 
2 CONT ## Barclay of Collairnie Charters No.14 dated 15 Jan 1510/11. see [1]
