2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/u/t/Steven-P-Guthrie/GENE1-0007.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 7TH LAIRD OF GUTHRIE WILLIAM GUTHRIE.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for VII LAIRD OF GUTHRIE WILLIAM GUTHRIE: VII LAIRD OF GUTHRIE: 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Laird of Memys and the Laird of Kincreich. Was served and retoured heir to his brother, and had a precept from chancery, for infefting him in the lands and barony of Guthrie, dated 20th June, 1616, upon which he got sas
2 CONC ine and infeftment, the 27th September, following. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The laird having no male issue, he first wadsett a part of the barony of Guthrie to David Guthrie, of Kincaldrum, great grandson of Alexander, second son of Sir Alexander Guthrie, the third baron, redeemable for payment of 22,000 
2 CONC merks, (1222pounds. 4s. 5 3/4 d. sterling) by contract, dated, the 19th and 23rd April, 1621. Upon this contract David obtained a charter of the wadsett lands, of the date of the contract to be held of the disponer; and thereafter
2 CONC , with consent of Isabella Fenton, his spouse, a daughter of the family of Easterogill, he disponed irredeemably to the said David, the whole lands and barony of Guthrie, and temple lands of Kincreich, making over in warrandice, t
2 CONC he lands of Memis, by contract of alienation, dated, 10th September, 1623; and there being charters granted in terms of this contract, David was infeft in these lands, on the 12th of that month, and subsequently obtaining a charte
2 CONC r of confirmation, under the great seal, of date, 24th July, 1630, he became David Guthrie of Guthrie. 
