1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===John de Lyons 
2 CONT *Born 1320 Warkworth Northamptonshire England
2 CONT *Married Margaret St John
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1336 Sir John de Lyons donated a carucate of land [the area a plough team of eight oxen could till in a single annual season] to St Leonard’s Hospital near Banbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1376 Sir John de Lyons granted further possessions to Robert, the chaplain of the hospital
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1385 without issue Estate passed to his sister Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://clanlyon.wordpress.com/2012/05/20/de-lyons-of-warkworth-castle/
2 CONT
2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT '''Do not confuse this John with https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Lyon-III-lV-Baron-of-Fortevlot-Forgandenney-Drumgawknames-Chambe/6000000003345404573.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==family==
2 CONT died without issue
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
