2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Life Summary of Sir John When Sir John de Lyon was born from 9 January 1314 to 8 January 1315, in Glamis, Forfarshire, Scotland, his father, John de Lyons II Baron of Warkworth, was 26 and his mother, Baroness Alice de Saint L
2 CONC iz, was 15. He married Margery Saint John about 1340, in Warkworth, Northumberland, England, United Kingdom. They were the parents of at least 1 son. He died on 4 November 1382, in Forfarshire, Scotland, at the age of 68.
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Lyons  Born 1320 Warkworth Northamptonshire England Married Margaret St John In 1336 Sir John de Lyons donated a carucate of land [the area a plough team of eight oxen could till in a single annual season] to St Leonard’s 
2 CONC Hospital near Banbury. In 1376 Sir John de Lyons granted further possessions to Robert, the chaplain of the hospital Died 1385 without issue Estate passed to his sister Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This John is not the so-named son of Sir John de Lyons of Warkworth by Alice St. Lise; that John is https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Lyons/6000000039792942896.  Do not confuse them.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * http://dgmweb.net/FGS/Lyon/LyonJohn-JeanStuart.html
2 CONT
