1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT II, KING OF SCOTS (formerly JOHN STEWART, HEREDITARY STEWARD OF SCOTLAND) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart, Earl of Carrick, who succeeded to the throne of Scotland as Robert II, King of Scots, gave the lands of Torranys, together with the Parc of Clounqwarn, Knocglas, Clonskeache Clayanysse, and Ardachryge,  all in the
2 CONC  barony of Kilbride and Sheriffdom of Lanark, to John Semple (aka Johanni Sympille), son and heir of Thomas Semple (aka Thome Sympille). [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112105151130&view=1up&seq=207 Registrum Magni S
2 CONC igilli Regum Scotorum. Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1306-1424. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, LL.D. (Scotland’s National Archives Reprinted by the Scottish Record Society in Conjunction with Clark Constable, Edin
2 CONC burgh, 1984), charter number 490 on page 177]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert II, also remembered as Robert the Steward, was the King of Scots who ruled from 1371 to his death. He was the only child of Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland and his first wife Marjorie Bruce, daughter of Robert
2 CONC  the Bruce and Isabella of Mar. On the death of his father in 1326, he became the hereditary steward of Scotland. In 1318, Robert II was named heir to King Robert I, his maternal grandfather. Although he lost his position after Ki
2 CONC ng Robert’s son David was born, he was made heir apparent to David. Robert II was then made a guardian of the kingdom in 1334 when David escaped to France. He succeeded the throne after David’s death in 1371. During his reign as t
2 CONC he king, he took no active part in the renewed war for independence. He married Elizabeth Mure in 1336; he had four sons and five daughters with her. A superior claim to the throne was asserted on behalf of the king’s two daughter
2 CONC s and two sons by his second wife, Euphemia Ross. From 1384, the kingdom was reigned over by Robert’s oldest son with Mure, John, Earl of Carrick aka King Robert III, and later by another son, Robert, Earl of Fife. Robert II died 
2 CONC in 1390 in Dundonald Castle in Ayrshire."
2 CONT [https://www.thefamouspeople.com/profiles/robert-ii-of-scotland-38177.php]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00006037&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert II, The Steward, King of Scots''' was born 2 March 1316. He died 19 April 1390  in Dundonald Castle in 1390 and lies buried at Scone Abbey.  He was also known as  Robert, High Steward of Scots and by his Gaelic Name, Roi
2 CONC bert II Stiùbhairt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coronation: 26 Mar 1371
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruled:  22 February 1371 to 19 April 1390
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceded by:  David II  (Dàibhidh Bruis)  Ruled  7 June 1329 - 22 Febuary 1371
2 CONT
2 CONT Succeeded by  Robert III   Ruled  19 April 1390 - 4 April 1406
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Stewart, born in 1316, was the only child of Walter Stewart, High Steward of Scotland. He had the upbringing of a Gaelic noble on the Stewart lands in Bute, Clydeside, and in Renfrew. [Wiki]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Basics==
2 CONT Son of: Walter Steward 1293 - 9 Apr 1326  and   Marjorie Bruce  December 1296 - 2 March 1316  (Daughter of Robert  I)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Mure   c.1348
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Stewart, Earl of Carrick
2 CONT # Walter Stewart, Lord of Fife  (d. 1362)
2 CONT # Robert Stewart, Duke of Albany, Earl of Fife and Monteith
2 CONT # Alexander Stewart, Earl of Buchan, Lord of Badenoch and Ross 
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart
2 CONT # Marjory Stewart
2 CONT # Isabella Stewart 
2 CONT # Katherine Stewart
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stewart, the elder 
2 CONT # Jean Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT 2.   Euphemia de Ross  1355 
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT # David Stewart, 1st Earl of Caithness, Earl of Strathearn
2 CONT # Walter Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stewart, the younger
2 CONT # Egidia Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate  children of with Mariota de Cardney
2 CONT # Alexander Stewart of Innerlunan
2 CONT # Sir John Stewart of Cardney
2 CONT #  James Stewart of Abernethy & Kinfaun
2 CONT # Walter Stewart
2 CONT # Possible Unknown Daughter(s)
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate  children with Moira Leitch
2 CONT # Sir John Stewart of Bute
2 CONT # Possible Unknown Daughter(s)
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate  children with  Unknown
2 CONT # Sir John Stewart of Dundonald
2 CONT # Thomas Stewart, Bishop of St Andrews
2 CONT # Alexander Stewart, Canon of Glasgow
2 CONT # James Stewart, Canon of Glasgow 
2 CONT # Possible Unknown Daughter(s)
