1 OCCU Princess Margaret Stuart, daughter of Robert II, King of Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} daughter of Eobart (Robert) II, King of Scotland, Princess of Scotland, daughter of King Eobert (Robert) II, note: 2nd wife of John,Lord of the Isles
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Stewart''', Princess of Scotland was born Abt 1342, Dundonald Castle, Irvine, Ayrshire, Scotland.  (Alternate birth date of abt 1330)  She died Abt 1410 (ALT: Abt 1387) in Scotland (580, 1970, 9910, 9912).
2 CONT
2 CONT about Dundonald Castle: [http://www.historic-scotland.gov.uk/propertyresults/propertyoverview.htm?PropID=PL_105]
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Robert II Stewart, King of Scots (1315-1390) and Elizabeth Mure, Queen of Scotland (1317-1355)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # on 14 Jun 1350 to '''Eoin MacAngus Mac Donnell''', 7th Lord of the Isles (1330-87), son of Angus Óg MacDonald, 6th Lord of the Isles and Agnes O'Cahan. He was born in 1326 in Finlaggan Castle, Island of Islay, Scotland 9911 and 
2 CONC died in 1387 in Ardtornish Castle, Lochaline, Argyllshire, Scotland (580,1970, 9910, 9911.) (fn1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eoin Mac Donnell and Margaret Stewart:
2 CONT # Donald MacDonald, 8th Lord of the Isles
2 CONT # Agnes D'Isles
2 CONT # Alisdair Carrach "Mangy" MacDonald
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Footnotes==
2 CONT
2 CONT # 5. Lady MARGARET Stewart  .  Robert II King of Scotland granted "insulam de Colowsay" to "Johanni del Yle…et…filis nostre Margarete sponse sue" by charter dated Jul 1376[1179].  m (dispensation 14 Jun 1350) as his second wife, J
2 CONC OHN MacDonald Lord of the Isles, son of ANGUS Og Lord of the Isles & his wife --- (-1387). (Crawley, Medlands)
2 CONT
