2 CONT
2 CONT …. m firstly (1336, dispensation 22 Nov 1347) ELIZABETH Mure, daughter of Sir ADAM Mure of Rowallan, Ayrshire & his [first wife Joan Cunningham or his second wife Janet Mure] (-before 1355). John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Contin
2 CONC uator) records that "Robertum regem, secundum" married "de facto unam de filiabus Adæ de More militis", by whom he had "filios et filias extra matrimonium", but that they married in 1349 after papal dispensation[1073]. The Liber P
2 CONC luscardensisnames "Elizabeth filia domini Adam de Mure" as first wife of "dominus Robertus rex secundus"[1074]. The Papal dispensation for the marriage of "Robertus dni de Stratgnf militis…David Regi Scotie…nepos" and "Elizabeth M
2 CONC ox", issued by Pope Clement VI, is dated 22 Nov "pontificatus nostri anno sexto" (1347)[1075].
