1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===EUPHEMIA STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Euphemia Stewart, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Euphemia-Stewart-Countess-of-Strathearn/6000000002166210799 who is her putative daughter-in-law '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Euphemia Stewart is the daughter of Sir John Stewart of Ralilston  the half brother of Robet II, King of Scots. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/214 The Scots Peerage VI: 214] She is identified as Egidia
2 CONC  Stewart in the Scots Peerage account of the Scottish Kings. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/14 The Scots Peerage I: p. 14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Euphemia Stewart married Sir Patrick Graham of Kinardine and Dunduff. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/14 The Scots Peerage I: p. 14] See also [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page
2 CONC /214 The Scots Peerage VI: 214] '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Egidia Stewart==
2 CONT * Father: John Stewart, of Ralston 
2 CONT * Mother:	Alicia Mure 
2 CONT * Married: Patrick Graham, of Kincardine and Dundaff   Also known as Euphemia
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT * 1. Patrick Graham, of Dundaff and Kilpont, Earl of Strathearn
2 CONT * 2. Robert Graham, of Kilpont
2 CONT * 3. David Graham
2 CONT * 4. Alexander Graham
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Graham of Kincardine, Lord of Dundaff; married (1) Matilda; married (2) about 1384 to Euphemia/Egidia, daughter of Sir John Stewart of Ralston. Patrick died before 1404.
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick was a Knight-Banneret. He was one of the hostages for the release of King David II. He was one of the commissioners who conducted negotiations with the English in 1394.
2 CONT
2 CONT His two eldest sons by his second marriage met particularly violent ends. Sir Patrick Graham of Dundaff and Kilpont (see below) was murdered by his brother-in-law Sir John Drummond of Concraig in 1413. The next son, Sir Robert Gra
2 CONC ham of Kilpont, was one of the group which assassinated King James I at Perth on 21 February 1437, and he was executed at Stirling Castle later that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------- 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/214/mode/1up The Scots peerage] founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Published 1904 by D. Douglas in Edinburgh .  Vol Vl page 214.  "Of the second marriage, there were born four sons: Patrick, Sir Robert, David, Alexander ..."	
2 CONT # [S280] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Graham01 (Reliability: 3)
2 CONT # [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#Walter6Stewartdied1326B Medlands] "2.         JOHN Stewart of Ralston .  m ---.  The name of John's wife is not known.  John & his wife had four children: ...."
2 CONT # [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#Walter6Stewartdied1326B MedLands] c)         EGIDIA Stewart .  m ([1384]) as his second wife, PATRICK de Graham of Kincardine and Dundaff, son of DAVID [VI] de Graham & his wife --- 
2 CONC (-after 6 May 1400). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3891&tree=CC
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-6424 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT The name "Gille Stewart" is seen on http://www.thepeerage.com/p516.htm#i5151, but http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#Walter6Stewartdied1326B does not support this.  There was a daughter Eupheme or Egidia who married Patr
2 CONC ick Graham about 1384. Accordingly, this profile has been merged into Euphemia (Egidia) Stewart.
