1 NAME Eupheme /Lindsay of Glenesk/
2 GIVN Eupheme
2 SURN Lindsay of Glenesk
2 _MARNM Lindsay of Glenesk
2 NICK Euphemia
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1360
2 ADDR
3 CITY Glenesk
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 13 NOV 1413
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==(Eupheme?) Lindsay== 
2 CONT * Father	Sir Alexander Lindsay, Laird of Glenesk ,   d. Oct 1381, Candia, Crete  
2 CONT * Mother	Catherine Stirling, Heiress of Glenesk ,   d. Bef 19 Oct 1378
2 CONT * died before 13 NOV 1413 when her 2nd husband remarried 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # David Stewart, Earl of Strathearn, Earl of Caithness ,   b. Est 1356,   d. Bef 15 Mar 1390  (Age ~ 34 years) 
2 CONT # Sir William Graham, of Kincardine,   d. 1424 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of 1st husband
2 CONT #  Euphemia Stewart, Countess Palatine of Strathearn, Cts. of Caithness ,   b. Bef 1375,   d. Abt 1434  (Age ~ 59 years)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of 2nd husband include 
2 CONT # Alexander Graham,   d. Abt 1421/1422
2 CONT # John Graham
2 CONT # Elizabeth Graham
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=john_d_newport&id=I17219
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Sir William Graham of Kincardine; possibly married (1) after 1390 to a daughter of Sir Alexander Lindsay of Glenesk and Catherine Stirling; married (2) before 1404 to Mariota, daughter of Sir John Oliphant of Aberdalgie; marri
2 CONC ed (3) about 13 November 1413 to Mary, daughter of Robert III, King of Scots and Annabella Drummond (died after 1458). William died in 1424.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife (if the marriage took place) was widow of David Stewart, Earl of Caithness and Strathearn, a younger son of King Robert II. The only child of this earlier marriage, Euphemia Stewart, married William's half-brother S
2 CONC ir Patrick Graham of Dundaff and Kilpont, and they were the parents of Malise Graham, Earl of Menteith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Discussion 
2 CONT * [http://listsearches.rootsweb.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/2006-05/1147320597  SP Correction: Sir William Douglas and his Lindsay wife] 2006 ... In 2 parts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/216/mode/2up The Scots peerage] founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Published 1904 by D. Douglas in Edinburgh .  Vol Vl.  Page 217-218.  "Graham, Duke of Montrose."  "He married first, in his father's lifetime, a lady whose name is not certainly known."
2 CONT # https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n28/mode/1up Links
2 CONT * http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00116924&tree=LEO
2 CONT * sister to http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Lindsay,_1st_Earl_of_Crawford
