0 @I6000000002188101804@ INDI
1 NAME James /Ogilvy/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Ogilvy
2 _MARNM Ogilvy
1 NAME James Ogilvy, 1st Lord Ogilvy of Airlie
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 25 SEP 1504
1 OCCU 1st Lord Ogilvy of  Arlie, 1st Lord Ogilvu of Airlie
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES OGILVY, EARL OF AIRLIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''formerly Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Bamff Charters ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1483: Instrument of sasine which confirms possession of the lands of Mawis and Peddrey to Gilbert Ramsay and his wife Margaret Ogilvy. Gilbert Ramsay is identified as the son and apparent heir Alexander Ramsay, who is id
2 CONC entified as the son and heir of Finlay Ramsay. Margaret Ogilvy is identified as the daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie. Her brother Thomas Ogilvy acted as bailie and gave sasine to Gilbert and Margaret,  and her brothers Archi
2 CONC bald Ogilvy and John Ogilvy were the witnesses present. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/34/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.thepeerage.com/p12.htm#i112 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie, 1st Lord Ogilvy of Airlie was born circa 1430.2 He was the son of Sir John Ogilvy of Lintrathen and Margaret Seton.2,3 He died before 25 September 1504.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He married,
2 CONT #  firstly, Elizabeth Kennedy circa 1450.2 
2 CONT # secondly, Elene Douglas, daughter of William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus and Margaret Hay, before May 1478.2,4
2 CONT #  thirdly, Jean Lyle before 1504.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Lord Ogilvy of Airlie [Scotland] on 28 April 1491.2 He held the office of Ambassador to Denmark on 18 May 1492.2 He lived at Lintrathen, Angus, Scotland.2 He lived at Airlie, Angus, Scotland.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p12.htm#i112
