1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Walter Ogilvy, of Wester Powrie and Auchterhouse; Hereditary Sheriff of Forfar; inherited both Auchterhouse and the office of Sheriff on the death of his uncle Sir Malcolm Ramsay c 1365. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Sir Walter Ogilvy of
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p292.htm#i2916
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Ogilvy of Wester Powry and Auchterhouse [1]
2 CONT *M, #2916, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1330
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Ogilvy of Wester Powry and Auchterhouse was born circa 1330.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Wester Powrie.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Wester Powrie and Marjory Ramsay.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Hereditary Sheriff of Forfar circa 1365, inherited from his uncle, Sir Malcolm Ramsay.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Walter Ogilvy of Wester Powry and Auchterhouse
