1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Auchterhouse:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p3042.htm#i30417
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Auchterhouse [1]
2 CONT *M, #30417, 
2 CONT *d. 1429
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 Jan 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Auchterhouse married Christian Keith, daughter of Sir Alexander Keith of Grandon, before 1413.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1429, drowned at sea on the way from France to Scotland.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir Alexander Ogilvy of Auchterhouse.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Sheriff of Angus[2] 
2 CONT *He lived at Auchterhouse, Angus, Scotland.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Justiciar of Scotland north of the Forth in 1427.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Patrick Ogilvy of Auchterhouse and Christian Keith
