1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ANDREW OGILVY OF INCHMARTINE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Sir Andrew Ogilvy of Inchmartine, here treated. He was alive on 16 April 1461, [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/44/mode/1up Melville and Leslie Chart
2 CONC ers: charter number 47] and may still have been alive on 31 July 1461, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f998&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1465&d
2 CONC i=n NRS: GD26/3/998] but he probably died before 18 May 1462, when his eldest son and heir is noticed as David Ogilvy of Inchmartine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f999&st
2 CONC =1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1465&di=n NRS: GD26/3/999] He certainly died before 30 April 1492. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/613/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2886]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Charter Chest at Wemyss Castle ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 August 1418: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/19/mode/1up The Melvilles, Earls of Melville, and the Leslies, Earls of Leven. Volume Third - Charters: charter number 27]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 July 1427: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/20/mode/1up charter number 28]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1441: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/26/mode/1up charter number 34]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 October 1444: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/27/mode/1up Charter number 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1445-46: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/28/mode/1up charter number 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 April 1449: Transumpt made 21 April 1449, of Indenture between Sir Andrew of Ogilvy of Inchmartin, and John of Wemyss of that ilk, for exchange of lands. 31 August 1445.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/melvillesearlsv300fras/page/29/mode/1up charter number 37]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1461: Transumpt of Obligation and Bond of Manrent by Walter of Tulch to Sir Andrew Ogilvie of Inchmartin, 16 April 1461. Transumpt dated 28 June 1461.
