2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1431: Charter by Andrew de Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Inchmartyne [Inchmartine] in favour of his eldest son, David de Ogilby [Ogilvie], of lands in GD26/3/971. [Tag, seal gone.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlin
2 CONC ecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f972&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartyne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/972]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1439: Charter by which Sir Andrew Ogilvy of Inchmartine and his wife Marjorie confirm that they have given the lands of Balmulto in the sheriffdom of Fife to David Bosvile of Craigincat in exchange for David's lands
2 CONC  of Wester Drone in the same sheriffdom. James II, King of Scots confirmed this charter under the Great Seal of Scotland on 24 February 1439. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/52/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: char
2 CONC ter number 217]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 February 1439: Charter by which David Bosvile of Craigincat confirms that he has given the lands of Wester Drone in the sheriffdom of Fife to Sir Andrew Ogilvy of Inchmartine, and his wife Marjorie, in exchange for Sir Andre
2 CONC w's lands of Balmulto in the same sheriffdom. Wester Drone was to be held by Sir Andrew and Marjorie and their lawful male heirs, whom failing by Alexander Ogilvy son and heir of David Ogilvy and their male heirs, whom failing by 
2 CONC Sir Andrew's nearest lawful heirs. James II, King of Scots confirmed this charter under the Great Seal of Scotland on 24 February 1439. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/52/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter nu
2 CONC mber 218]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 August 1449: Charter by John de Skierlyn [?Skirling ?Skilling; see GD26/3/970 and GD26/3/975] in favour of Sir Andrew de Ogilvy [Ogilvie] of Inchemartyn [Inchmartine], kt., of lands of the Tempil [Temple] of St. John [Knights
2 CONC  Templars] in lordship of Inchemartyn. Witnesses: David de Ogiluy [Ogilvie], eldest son of said Sir Andrew, Patrick de Ogiluy [Ogilvie], son of said David, sir Thomas de Cruam [Cramb] and sir James Nefe [Neave], chaplains. [Seal a
2 CONC ppended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f982&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family
2 CONC , Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/982]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 August 1451: Instrument of Sasine (2 copies) in favour of Sir Andrew de Ogilyy [Ogilvie] of Inchemartyne [Inchmartine], kt., of half of lordship of Inchmartyne formerly belonging to John de Wemys [Wemyss], following on prece
2 CONC pt, dated 15 August 1451, by Sir John de Ruthven, kt., sheriff of Perth. Witnesses: William Scot [Scott] of Balwery [Balwearie], Patrick de Ogiluy [Ogilvie], son of said Sir Andrew, Alexander Scot [Scott], esquires, sir Thomas de 
2 CONC Corss [Corse - Cross], priest, and John Dikysone [Dickson]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f986&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/986]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1461: Instrument of Sasine in favour of David de Ogilby [Ogilvie], son and apparent heir of Sir Andrew Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Inchmartyne [Inchmartine], kt., of 4 oxgangs of lands of Inchmartyne following on precept by And
2 CONC rew, Lord Gray. Witnesses: Thomas Oliphant of Dromie [Dron], sir John Symons [Simmonds] and sir Thomas de Murray, chaplains, James Kynman [Kinman - ?Kininmonth], John Murdac [Murdoch], James Haldastoun [Hiddleston], John Constabil
2 CONC l [Constable], Robert Noroway [Norway], Alexander Smyth [Smith], Martin Gardenar [Gardner], John Dicsoun [Dickson] and John Clerk [Clark]. [Seal appended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD26%2f3%2f998&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1465&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/998]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1462: Bond by Alexander de Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Duntrone [Duntrune] to David de Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Inchmartyne [Inchmartine] not to sell or wadset said Alexander's parts of lands of Inchmartyne without consent of said Da
2 CONC vid. [Seal appended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f999&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1465&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the L
2 CONC eslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/999]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1492: Charter by which David Ogilvy of Inchmartine salutes the souls of his father and mother, "Andree  O. patris sui, Mariote 0. matris sue" and, with the consent of his wife Mariote Hay, confirms that he has given an
2 CONC  annualrent of 12 merks from his lands of Petmedill and Inchmartyn to the Convent of the Friars Minor of Dundee. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/613/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2886]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
