2 CONT '''6 July 1501: David Ogilby of Inchmartin. "Comperit, Andro, Lord Gray, and Maister James Henresone as procuratouris for David Ogilby of Ynchmartin, and protestit that becaus Thomas Berclay, son and executour till umquhile David 
2 CONC Berclay of Cullernye, and David Ogilby, nevo til the sade David Ogilby of Ynchmartin, gert summonf [him] for the wrangus postponyng and deferring til infeft the sade David Ogibly yongar, his nevo, heretably  be charter and saising
2 CONC  in dew forme in al and sindry his landis and baronry of Ynchmartin, with the pertinence, liand in the schirefdome of Perth, and certane utheris punctis contenit in the copy of the summondis, and wald nocht compere til folow him, 
2 CONC that thairfore thai suld refound the costis and expensis sustenit be him herethrow and that he suld nocht ansuere thairto quhill  he war new summond." [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarro
2 CONC w&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    36
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 February 1503: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 249]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    37
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 February 1503: "The prior of Perth. In the acc[i]one and caus persewit be the prior and freris predicatouris of Perrth aganis David Ogilby of Ynchmartin for the wrangus withhalding fra thaimof five bollis of quhete and ane h
2 CONC alf, aucht til furth of the landis of mannis of Ynchmartin," the said prior being personally present and the said David compearing by James Ogilby, his son and procurator, the lords, in presence of the king, and with consent of sa
2 CONC id James, as procurator, decern that David shall pay to the prior and convent a half chalder of wheat and a half chalder of bear, "of the great met that is now", that is now to be delivered immediately, as victuals owed to them of
2 CONC  the said lands of all times past. They also decern, with the same consent, that David shall pay to the prior and convent yearly in time to come a half chalder of wheat and a half chalder of bear, of King William's measure, for th
2 CONC is year to start as between this date and Whitsunday next, thereafter to be delivered between Martinmas and Pasche, and they [ordain] letters for distraint. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Baln
2 CONC agarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 268]'''
2 CONT
