1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER OGILVY OF DUNTRUNE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Ogilvy of Duntrune, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Glen/6000000026866295352?through=6000000026866166409 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/176/mode/1up RMS 1424
2 CONC -1513: charter number 821] It seems quite likely, therefore, probable even, that he is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/David-Ogilvy-of-Balmuto/6000000026866398362?through=6000000026866166409 The lands of Kinneff appear to h
2 CONC ave been in his possession on the day that he died, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1002&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD26/3/1002] and, 
2 CONC consequently, he may occasionally have been noticed as Alexander Ogilvy of Kinneff. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/oo/ogilvy01.php Stirnet: Ogilvy 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Alexander Ogilvy of Duntrune, here treated. He was alive on 11 June 1475, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f3047&st=
2 CONC 1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=duntrune&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD45/16/3047] but it would appear that he died unmarried and without lawful issue before 18 March 1476, when David Ogilvy of Inchmartine is noticed as his heir of
2 CONC  entail. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1002&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD26/3/1002]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                   1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1462: Bond by Alexander de Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Duntrone [Duntrune] to David de Ogilby [Ogilvie] of Inchmartyne [Inchmartine] not to sell or wadset said Alexander's parts of lands of Inchmartyne without consent of said Da
2 CONC vid. [Seal appended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f999&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=duntrune&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Les
2 CONC lie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/999]'''
