1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == EDWARD DE BRUCE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Documentary evidence for the life of Edward de Bruce has not been found. It would appear that his existence may depend entirely upon a pedigree which was produced by the late Mary Elizabeth Cumming Bruce. She identified him as 
2 CONC the husband of Agnes de Airth in her publication 'Family Records of the Bruces and Cumyns' and said that he and his wife were mentioned in a charter dated 24 April 1417 by which Robert Duke of Albany confirmed possession of the la
2 CONC nds of Erth Chaumerlain to Sir William of Craufurde of Manuel. This is wrong. Edward and his putative wife are not mentioned in this charter. Moreover, she did not identify any other evidence for him. [https://archive.org/details/
2 CONC familyrecordsofb1870bruc/page/318/mode/1up Family Records: p. 318] The charter cited by Mary Elizabeth Cumming Bruce was printed in full by the late Major William Bruce Armstrong, in his account of the family of Bruce of Airth. [h
2 CONC ttps://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n36/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth: pp. 9-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/familyrecordsofb1870bruc/page/n4/mode/1up Family Records of the Bruces and Cumyns. With an Historical Introduction and Appendix from Authentic Public and Private Documents. By M. E. Cumming Bruce.
2 CONC  (William Blackwood and Sons, Edinburgh and London, MDCCCLXX), 692 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n6/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth and their Cadets. By Major William Bruce Armstrong. (Printed for Private Circulation, Edinburgh, MDCCCXCII), 137 pp. plus drop-linr pedi
2 CONC gree charts and Appendices]'''
