1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''''Red Book of Scotland''''' Vol. 2 Bot-Car [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/62525/images/redbookofscotlandvolume2bot-carpdf-00099?pId=6968 p. 186-187]:—
2 CONT >SIR DAVID BRUCE, 4th OF CLACKMANNAN, to whom the fee of the lands of Clackmannan was assigned in his and his father joint charter for those lands on 24 October 1393 and which he succeeded to on his father's death in 1405. He made
2 CONC  a renunciation of the tithes of the mills of Clackmannan to the Canons Regular of Cambuskenneth on 6 October 1406 [C2/4/26] and d. before 8 July 1449. He m. Jean, daughter of Sir John Stewart of Innermeath and Lorne, and was fath
2 CONC er of:
2 CONT ># John Bruce, 5" of Clackmannan, (see below).
2 CONT ># Patrick Bruce, had a charter from Alan Kinnaird of that Ilk for the lands of Huyl, in the barony of Kinnaird, in which he is styled son of the deceased Sir David Bruce of Clackmannan on 8 July 1449. [C2/4/26]
2 CONT ># Robert Bruce, who was executed on 19 January 1450, for involvement with the Livingston faction in their crimes against the King. [Auchinleck Chronicle.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://www.clackmannanshire.scot/index.php/history/barony-of-clackmannan The Barony of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1403 – 1405''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-3rd-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000001806551174?through=6000000168873893042 Sir Robert Bruce - 3rd Baron of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Bruce inherited the Barony of Clackmannan and its lands at the death of his father. He received the charter of the Lands of Rait from King Robert III in 1393. Died around 1405.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barony passed from father to son
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1405 – 1428''' [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-4th-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000168874433890?through=303632326640007080 Sir David Bruce - 4th Baron of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Bruce renounced the rights to the mills of Clackmannan from the Canons of Cambuskenneth on October 6th, 1406. Died around 1428.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Barony passed from father to son
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1428 – 1473''' [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-5th-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000001806579012 Sir John Bruce - 5th Baron of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in a charter decree between himself and Luke Stirling of Ratherns in April 1435. In 1456 had Sasine for the lands of Rait in Perthshire.
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT a1 https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-2nd-Baron-Clackmannan-Rate-proprietor-of-lands-of-Kennet/303632884430002646?through=6000000001806551174 & https://www.geni.com/people/Isobell-Stewart/6000000003615927768?through=60000000
2 CONC 01806551174
2 CONT >a1b1 https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-3rd-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000001806551174?through=6000000168873893042 <1389 - d<1406
2 CONT >x NN mistress
2 CONT >>a1b1c1 https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Bruce-of-Wester-Kennet/6000000168873893042?through=6000000001806551174
2 CONT >xx https://www.geni.com/people/Annabelle-Scrymgeour/303632326640007080?through=6000000001806551174
2 CONT >>'''a1b1c2 https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000168874433890?through=303632326640007080, who succeeded.'''
2 CONT >>a1b1c3 Alexander of Stanehous and Airth
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://archive.org/stream/collectionstowar1868clac/collectionstowar1868clac_djvu.txt From the Charters of Clackmannen]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 May 1389''' Thomas obtains Kennet from his father .— Charter of Robert de Bruys of Clackmannan and Rate to and in favour of Thomas de Bruys, his son, where- by " for good services" he grants the said Thomas the lands of Weste
2 CONC r Kennet and others for payment to his said father of a silver penny yearly. In the history of Noble British Families, part 3, p. 15, it is stated that Robert de Bruce died about this period, and the next Charters of resignation w
2 CONC ere probably made by the possessor of the estate on succeeding thereto. [WHY, THO?]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4th Oct., 1393''' — Crown Charter of Resignation by King Robert III., proceeding on the Procuratory of Resignation of Robert de Bruys, whereby the King new grants the lands and Barony of Clackmannan, and all the pertinents, to 
2 CONC Robert de Bruys, whom failing, to '''David Bruys, his eldest son, and the heirs male, procreated or to be procreated, of his body,''' whom failing, to Thomas Bruys, also his son, and the heirs male of his body, to be held of the K
2 CONC ing and his successors in fee and heritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT By this Charter, Robert deBruys had gone through the ceremony of resigning or giving them back to the King during his life, and the King then made a new grant of them to him, and his two sons, and their heirs male.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10th June, 1393''' — Charter by Robert de Bruys, Lord of Rate and Clackmannan, to his " beloved son, Thomas de Bruys," and his heirs, and assigns of an annualent of ten merks, payable furth off his lands of Tullygarth, lying in
2 CONC  the county of Clackmannan, and that in con- sideration of a certain sum of money paid to him, the said Robert de Bruys, in his urgent necessity. To be holden of the said Robert de Bruys and his heirs redeemable on payment of the 
2 CONC sum of 25 merks.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18th February, 1399''' — Crown Charter of Resignation and Confirmation by King Robert III., ratifying and confirming the Char- ter No. 9, granted by Robert de Bruys to his son, Thomas, of the lands of Wester Kennet, Pitfoulden,
2 CONC  and the Cruikitland, all lying in the county of Clackmannan. From this time the estate of Kennet con- tinued separate from that of Clackmannan, and although the families continued on the most intimate terms, and the heiress of Ke
2 CONC nnet, in 1568, married one of the cadets of Clackmannan, the estates have never been united.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24th Sept 1428''' Instrument of Sasine in favour of Peter or Patrick de Bruys, in the lands of Wester Kennet, in the Barony of Graysmenstone and county of Clackmannan, proceeding on the precept contained in No. 13, to which Pet
2 CONC er Bruys had acquired right as heir to his father, sasine given by John de Bruce, Lord of Clackmannan, in presence of Sir David Stuart of Durrisdeer, knight, Robert Merce.. Etc The Sir David Stewart of Durrisdeer,who appears as a 
2 CONC witness, appears to have been of the Rossyth family, and was closely related to the Bruces.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8th July, 1449'''— Charter by Allan  de Kinnaird of that Ilk to Patrick Bruce, son of the deceased David Bruce of Clackmannan, knight, of the lands of Hayle, in the Barony of Kinnaird and county of Perth, and that in considerat
2 CONC ion of a certain sum of money paid to  him by the said Patrick Bruce. To be holden of the said Allan de Kinnaird in fee and heritage for payment of a silver penny at the feast of Pentecost, yearly, in name of Blench form, if asked
2 CONC  only. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/collectionstowar1868clac/collectionstowar1868clac_djvu.txt
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT '''BRUCE,  EARLS  OF  ELGIN  AND AILESBURY''' [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/466/mode/1up?view=theater Balfour Paul, James, ed. (1906). The Scots Peerage, Vol. III. Edinburgh: David Douglas. pp. 467–468. 
2 CONC ISBN 0-9711966-2-1.]
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000168874433890 Sir  David  Bruce],  the  elder  son,  succeeded  his  father about  1406.  As  David  Bruce  dominus  de  Clacmanan,  miles, he  made  a  renunciat
2 CONC ion  of  the  tithes  of  the  mills  of  Clack- mannan, on  6  October  1406,  to  the  canons  regular  of Oambuskenneth.  He  married  [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Stewart/6000000003146136856?through=6000000168874433890 Je
2 CONC an],  daughter  of  Sir  John Stewart  of  Innermeath  and  Lorn,  and  by  her  had  issue three  sons,  viz. : —
2 CONT 1.  John,  succeeded  in  Clackmannan.
2 CONT 2.  Patrick  had  a  charter  from  Alan  de  Kynnarde  of  the lands  of  Hill,  8  July  1449,  confirmed  16  May  1450.
2 CONT 3.  James,  mentioned  1449.
2 CONT
