1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >====Medlands: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#JamesLindsayMMargaretKeith Scotland: Untitled Nobility]
2 CONT >a) '''JAMES Lindsay (-1397).''' 
2 CONT >'''Burnett records''' payments to his mother “as widow of Sir James Lindsay”, noting that in “1379-80, 1380-1, 1381-2 and 1382-3 her son Sir James Lindsay appears as recipient of the whole annuity” (full source citations)[1292]. 
2 CONC
2 CONT >'''Burnett records''' that accounts in May 1397 indicate that “both mother and son had died within the previous year” (full source citations)[1293].  
2 CONT >'''m MARGARET Keith''', daughter of WILLIAM Keith Marshal of Scotland & his wife Margaret Fraser (-after 1397). 
2 CONT >'''James & his wife had two children:''' 
2 CONT >'''i)''' MARGARET Lindsay.  m THOMAS Colville, son of ROBERT Colville of Oxenham & his wife --- (-1411). 
2 CONT >'''ii)''' EUFEMIA Lindsay.  m JOHN Herries of Terregles, son of ---.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul, J. B. (ed.) (1906) The Scots Peerage: Founded on Wood’s Ed. of Sir Robert Douglas’s Peerage of Scotland; Containing an Historical and Genealogical Account of the Nobility of that Kingdom. Edinburgh, Scotland, UK: David Dougl
2 CONC as. Available at: '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/11/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.org]''', pp. 11-12. '''Note:''' ''Medlands refers to this source for further information.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Lindsay of Crawford''' is reported to be the son of Sir James Lindsay of Crawford, and his wife, Egidia Stewart. He is said to have married Margaret Keith, and to have had two daughters, Margaret and Eufemia. He is re
2 CONC ported to have died in 1397. – [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2116.htm#i21160 The Peerage, Database Online].
2 CONT
2 CONT Lindsay, A. C. et al. (1858) ''Lives of the Lindsays or, A Memoir of the Houses of Crawford and Balcarres; to which are added, Extracts from the Official Correspondence of Alexander Sixth Earl of Balcarres, during the Maroon War''
2 CONC . 2nd ed. London, England, UK: John Murray. Available at Google Books RE: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Lives_of_the_Lindsays/bGZfAAAAcAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Sir%20James,%20the%20second%22 Sir James, the Second], '''''and
2 CONC ''''' [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Lives_of_the_Lindsays/bGZfAAAAcAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22No.%20VIII.—Page%2073.%22 Appendix: No. VIII].
