1 OCCU Lord or Dunure, 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dead: 11/8/1408	, 1450 or 1386
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lelandva/kenne007.htm#id3888
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Sir Gilbert7 Kennedy of Dunure (John6, Gilbert5de Carrick, Gilbert4, Roland3, Nicol,2, Duncan1) married Marion Sandilands of Calder, daughter of Sir James Sandilands of Calder and Elenora (--?--) Countess of Carrick, after 1354
2 CONC .11 He married Agnes Maxwell after 1380.12 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a hostage for David II, in 1354; had a grant from Sir John his father, a charter from Robert III of lands of Cassillis in 1404. Sir Gilbert married twice according to the Peerage and McDowall,  and they agree that the first
2 CONC  wife was Marion, daughter of Sir James Sandilands of Calder by Elnora, Countess of Carrick; but McDowall claims James, the son who married the King's daughter, was by the second marriage but that because of his royal wife he was 
2 CONC put before the older brother, Gilbert, and became heir.13 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Gilbert7 Kennedy of Dunure and Marion Sandilands of Calder were as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i. Gilbert8; b. after 1360.  He was disinherited by his father and died in French dervice and had no issue; he killed his brother James.14
2 CONT *ii. Alexander of Ardstychar; b. after 1360. 
2 CONT *8. iii. Sir James of Dunure, b. circa 1380; m. Princess Mary (--?--). 
2 CONT
2 CONT CORRECTION: 1) Gilbert 2) John 3) Roland 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Gilbert7 Kennedy of Dunure and Agnes Maxwell were as follows: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *i. Sir Hugh8 of Ardstincher; b. after 1380.15  *He is the ancestor of the Kennedys of Bargany.16
2 CONT *ii. John; b. after 1390.17 
2 CONT *iii. Thomas; b. after 1390.*Pitcairn says Bargany family descend from him.19
2 CONT *iv. David; b. after 1390.20 
2 CONT
2 CONT CORRECTION: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # James , M (~1384-<1408)
2 CONT #  Alexander , M (~1386->1415)
2 CONT #  Hugh “Come With The Penny” , M (~1388-)
2 CONT #  John , M (~1390-<1473)
2 CONT #  Thomas , M (~1392-)
2 CONT #  David , M (~1394-)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps33/ps33_438.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Records of the family of Cassels and connexions”
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, eldest son of John Kennedy, married, first, Marion, daughter of Sir James Sandilands of Calder, by whom he had three sons, Gilbert, John, and Roland ; and, secondly, Agnes Maxwell, daughter of Sir Jo
2 CONC hn Maxwell of Pollok, by his wife, Isabel Lindsay, daughter of Sir James Lindsay of Crawford, by the Princess Egidia, sister of Robert II. The eldest son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy and Agnes Max- well was James, who married the Prince
2 CONC ss Mary, daughter of Robert III., in 1403, and by her had six sons. James was killed by his brother GILBERT, in consequence of the preference shown to the second family (they having been disinherited to make way for James).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2448.htm#i24475
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure 
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #24475, d. after 8 November 1408
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=22 Jun 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT      Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure was the son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure and Agnes Maxwell.1 He died after 8 November 1408.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger+ d. b 8 Nov 1408 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 40. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 10
2 CONC 6th edition. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lelandva/kenne005.htm#id3886
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Sir Gilbert5 de Carrick (Gilbert4, Roland3, Nicol,2, Duncan1) obtained a charter to several estates; among these was Dunure and the Castle of Lochdown, still held by the Family. From this time on the Family dropped the name Car
2 CONC rick and assumed Kennedy before 1309.9 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Gilbert5 de Carrick and an unknown spouse were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. i. Sir John6 of Dunure
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Dead: 11/8/1408 , 1450 or 1386
