1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===THOMAS MAXWELL OF POLLOK===
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John</strong>, who got a charter under the great seal from king James IV. <em>Johanni Maxwell de Nether Pollock</em>, of the lands of Henrystoun, &c. &c. dated 8th July 1495...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He had the honour of knighthood conferred upon him by king James IV. and married a daughter of the family of Houston of that ilk, by whom he had only one daughter, Elizabeth, his sole heiress...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died in the end of the reign of king James V. and was succeeded by his only child."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~battle/baronage/page451.html The Baronage of Scotland], Robert Douglas, 1798, page 421
2 CONT
2 CONT ==pedigree==
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=9aU0AAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA9&ots=QeiONJQ7Sn&dq=Sir%20Robert%20Maxwell%20of%20Maxwell%2C%20Caerlaverock%2C%20Mearns%20and%20Pencaitland&pg=PA7#v=onepage&q&f=true "Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollok"]
2 CONT
2 CONT IV- 3. Sir Aymer de Maccuswell, second of Caerlaverock. Married Mary of Mearns and acquired the Barony of Mearns. 1195-1266. He had
2 CONT *V- 3. Sir John Maxwell, ancestor of the Maxwells of Pollok. 1270-1306. Had
2 CONT **VI- 1. Sir Robert Maxwell, second of Pollok. 1306-1330. Had
2 CONT ***VIM. Sir John Maxwell, third of Pollok. 1330-1360. Had
2 CONT ****VIII- 1. Sir John Maxwell, fourth of Pollok. Married first Isabella Lindsay, and second, Elizabeth St. Michael. 1360-1405
2 CONT *****IX-1. Sir John Maxwell, fifth of Pollok. 1405-1429.
2 CONT ******X. Thomas Maxwell, sixth of Pollok. 1429-1450.
2 CONT
