1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == PATRICK MAXWELL OF STANLEY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Maxwell of Stanley, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Robert-Maxwell-of-Calderwood/6000000002187771918?through=6000000225715475824 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Danielstoun
2 CONC /6000000002188035021?through=6000000225715475824. He received a Crown charter of the one half of the lands of Stanley, part of the Dennistoun estates of his mother, on the resignation of Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood, dated 16th 
2 CONC of August 1473, and on the 15th November following, witnessed a charter, in which he is styled brother-german of Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood. [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/463/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs
2 CONC  I: 463]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Maxwell is reported to have died without issue. [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/463/mode/1up Maxwell Memoirs I: 463-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 August 1473: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirms that '''Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood''' has given one half of the lands of Stanele, adjacent to Thornle on the east, to Patrick Maxwell and his la
2 CONC wful male heirs, whom failing to return to Sir John and his heirs. Sir John reserved his own liferent of the property, and the liferent of his wife Margaret. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/232/mode/1up Reg
2 CONC ister of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 1137 on p. 232]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 November 1473-74: Charter issued by Alexander Cunninham of Achinbowy. Witnessed by Joh. Maxwell de Caldoewod militie, Pat. Maxwell fratre germano dicti Joh. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/235/mode/1u
2 CONC p Register of the Great Seal of Scotland,  A.D.1424-1513, charter number 1151 on p. 235]'''
2 CONT
