2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 June1493: Certified copy of Charter dated 15th June 1493, confirming a Charter dated 10th June 1493 by Sir Alexander Scrymgeour Chaplain Laird of Sonahard with advice and consent propinquiorum amicorum meorum to James Scrymg
2 CONC eour, eldest son of David Scrymgeour his brother and his heirs and successors of the Lands of Sonahard, to which Charter James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee, John Scrymgeour of Glastre, and James Scrymgeour Burgess of Dundee and 
2 CONC others are witnesses. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f816&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=David+Scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the
2 CONC  Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/816]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1500: Instrument of Sasine of the said lands of Kirktoun of Earlstradighty in terms of the said Charter propriis manibus of the said James Scrymgeour, Constable in favor of the said James Scrymgeour the son of the decea
2 CONC sed David Scrymgeour, brother of the said Alexander Scrymgeour. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f774&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=David+Scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/774]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 May 1506: Instrument of Sasine of the third part with the pertinents of the said warrandice lands of Wallace Craigie in security and warrandice of Ten Merks of annualrent annually issuing from the lands of Kirktoun proprijs 
2 CONC manibus of the said Mr. John Scrymgeour of Glastre tutor foresaid in favor of James Scrymgeour of Kirktoun of Earlstradighty ad mandatum brevis regis, bearing date the 28 May 1506. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f781&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour+of+kirktoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dunde
2 CONC e, reference GD137/781]'''
