2 CONT '''Elizabeth Edmonstone of Tulliallan, here treated, is the daughter of Janet Napier, otherwise Janet, lady of Edmonstone. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD15%2f343&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=boyne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n NRS: GD15/343]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 June 1484: Instrument of Resignation by Janet, Lady of Edmoundstoune in favour of Elizabeth and Margaret Edmoundstoune, her daughters, of lands of Tullealloun and the thanedom of Boyne. Witnesses:- Sir John Hog, Thomas Knolli
2 CONC s, David Gryndlaw, Gilbert Smyth and Alexander Hog. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD15%2f343&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=boyne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotla
2 CONC nd, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/343]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 February 1485: Charter by which Elizabeth Edmonstone of Tulliallan confirms that she has exchanged her half share of the thanedome of Boyne, together with her half share of an annualrent of six merks, for her sister Margaret
2 CONC  Edmonstone's half share of the lands of Tulliallan. Elizabeth is identified as one of the heirs of the deceased James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam. She made the exchange with the consent of her husband Patrick Blackadder, Her
2 CONC  charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 3 March 1485-86. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/345/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 1644]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 August 1485: Procuratory by Elizabeth Edmonstone, spouse of Patrick Blackadder, to receive grant of lands of Tulliallan, Perthshire (now Fife). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH
2 CONC 1%2f2%2f290&atst=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+edmonstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Transcripts and photocopies of Miscellaneous Charters and Papers, reference RH1/2/290]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 February 1487: REX concessit JOHANNI BLACADIR, filio Patricii Blacadir et Elizabetht Edmondstoun ejus sponse, et heredibus ejus, — terras de Tullalane, unacum donatione et patronatu ecclesie de Tullialane, in senesc. Straith
2 CONC erne, vic. Perth; — quas dicta Elizabeth resignavit : — Reservato libero tenemento dictis Pat. et Eliz. et eorum alteri diutius viventi. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/358/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: 1707]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 March 1488-89: Letters of confirmation under the privy seal of King James IV whereby notwithstanding the general revocation of all infeftments, remissions, gifts of lands etc passed since candlemas 1487-8 made by him on his c
2 CONC oronation at the Abbey of Scone, he ratifies, approves and confirms the resignation made by John Ramsay of Kylgoyr [Kilgour], procurator to Elizabeth Edmonston, spouse of Patrick Blacadyr [Blackadder] of the lands of Tulleallone [
2 CONC Tulliallan] with the donation and patronage of the kirk of the same in the sheriffdom of Peyrt [Perth] and stewartry of Strachteryne [Strathearn] into the hands of the King his father and the gift thereof thereupon made to John of
2 CONC  Blacadyr son to the said Patrick and Elizabeth and his heirs. At Tongland, 6 Mar 1488/1489. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f544&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+edmonston&ko
2 CONC =p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/544]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 August 1489: REX confirmavit cartam patris sui Jac. III regis, — [qua concessit JOHANNI BLAKADYR, et ELIZABETH EDMONDSTOUN . ejus spouse,— terras de Tuliallan etc., ut in carta 1707] : — Test. ut in carta 1884. xii. 133. [ht
2 CONC tps://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/396/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 1886]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 September 1494 and 12 October 1494: Instrument on proclamation of banns of marriage between Patrick Blacader of Tuliallan and Lady Elizabeth Edmundstone. Proclamations made by Mr. John Scot, vicar, and Sir Andrew Browstar, c
2 CONC haplain, in lower church of Glasgow, and instrument requested by Mr. Robert Blacader, canon of the cathedral church of Aberdeen, as procurator for said Patrick and Elizabeth, from John Thornton, notary. Witnesses: Robert Smyth, Th
2 CONC omas Hoige, John Hongofeld, Martin Rankyne, George Ramsae and William Cragane, burgesses of Glasgow. Dates are 28 Sep, 5 and 12 Oct 1494. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f393%2f1&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmundstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Graham of Gartur, Port of Menteith, Stirlingshire, reference GD1/393/1]'''
