2 CONT '''9 May 1429: Great seal charter of confirmation of charter, 12 June 1377, by George of Dunbar, earl of March, lord of Annandale and Man, to John of Sinclair of Hirdmanstoun of town of Polwarth, resigned by Patrick of Polwrth, kt
2 CONC . Witnesses to charter - John of Dunbar, earl of Moray, Sir Walter of Haliburtoun, laird of that ilk, Patrick of Hepburne, laird of Halis, JOHN OF EDMONDSTOUN, LAIRD OF THAT ILK, Alexander of Haliburtoun, John of Towers (de Turrib
2 CONC us), and John of Haliburtoun, kts., Nigel of Cynghame, laird of Beltoun, Alexander of Cokburne, laird of Langtoun, Alexander of Riclyntoun, Philip of Nesbit, laird of that ilk, Robert Leth. Witnesses to confirmation - John, bishop
2 CONC  of Glasgow, chancellor, John Forestar, chamberlain, Walter of Ogilbi, treasurer, kts., Mr. William Foulis, keeper of privy seal, provost of Bothuile, and Mr. Thomas of Myretoun, dean of Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD158%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Hume of Polwarth, Berwickshire, Earls of Marchmont, r
2 CONC eference GD158/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1458: REX concessit JOHANNI DE EDMONDSTOUNE filio Jac. de E. de eodem militis, — terras de Edname, vic. [Berwic] ; — quas idem Jac. resignavit : — Tenend. dicto Jac. et heredibus masculis de corpore ejus legitime procr
2 CONC eatis, quibus deficicntibus, legitimis et propinquioribus heredibus dicti Jac. (|uibuscunque: — Faciend. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/133/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of
2 CONC  the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 607]'''
2 CONT
