1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 4 Children: Andrew,Sir Robert,Elizabeth and John
2 CONT
2 CONT He [Robert Stewart] m. 2ndly (Papal dispensation 4 May 1380), Muriel, 1st daughter of Sir William Keith, Marischal of Scotland, by Margaret,daughter and heir of John Fraser of Zouch (sic . Touch?) Fraser, son and heir of Sir Alexa
2 CONC nder Fraser, High Chamberlain. He d. 3 Sep 1420, at Stirling Castle, aged above 80, and was buried in Donfermline Abbey. His widow d. shortly be fore Whitsunday (1 June) 1449. [Complete PeerageI:77-79, XIV:15]
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Stewart,_1st_Duke_of_Albany#Marriage_and_family Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Graham died in 1380 and Albany subsequently married Muriella de Keith, with whom he had four children, the elder of whom was:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Buchan (1381–1424); he fought in France against the English during the Hundred Years War, serving with distinction, but was killed at the Battle of Verneuil on 17 August 1424;
2 CONT
2 CONT the others being:
2 CONT * Robert Stewart, Earl of Ross, died without issue
2 CONT * Lady Marjorie Stewart (married to Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell)
2 CONT * Lady Elizabeth Stewart (married to Malcolm Fleming, ancestor of Malcolm Fleming, 3rd Lord Fleming)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/completepeerageo01coka#page/78/mode/2up  G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage] of England, Scotlan
2 CONC d, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 79. 
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/36/mode/2up page 36-37] of The Scots peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of th
2 CONC e nobility of that kingdom by Paul, James Balfour, Sir, 1846-1931 Published 1904 Volume 6.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=rlord335&id=I39355
