2 CONT
2 CONT (10) [ '''Sir Andrew Moray'''], died 1338, who was a strong supporter of King Robert Bruce. First Marriage -
2 CONT
2 CONT * 10 (a) '''Sir John''' (No. 11). 
2 CONT * 10 (b) '''Sir Thomas''' (No. 12). 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, second, Christian Bruce, sister of King Robert. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (11) '''Sir John Moray, Lord of Bothwell''', died s.p. before 5th September 1351. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN de Moray (-[20 Apr/5 Sep] 1351). Lord of Bothwell. "Thomas de Moravia panetarius Scotie" confirmed a donation by "bone memorie Johannis de Moravia fratris mei senioris" to Moray, for the soul of "bone memorie domini Andree de
2 CONC  Moravia patris mei", by charter dated 8 May 1353[534]. m (Papal dispensation 21 Nov 1348) as her first husband, MARGARET Graham Ctss of Menteith, widow of firstly of Sir JOHN Moray of Bothwell, divorced wife secondly of THOMAS Ea
2 CONC rl of Mar, and widow thirdly of Sir JOHN Drummond of Concraig, daughter of Sir JOHN Graham & his wife Mary Ctss of Menteith (-[21 Jul 1372/4 May 1380]). She married secondly (Papal dispensations 15 Aug 1352 and 29 May 1354, divorc
2 CONC ed before Feb 1359) as his first wife, Thomas Earl of Mar, thirdly (Papal dispensation 1360) John Drummond of Concraig, and fourthly (Papal dispensation 9 Sep 1361) as his first wife, Robert Stewart, who succeeded as Earl of Mente
2 CONC ith in 1361, de iure uxoris, and was appointed Duke of Albany in 1398.
