1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Thomas, Earl of Mar''' ''From Wikipedia''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas of Mar was a 14th century Mormaer (Earl) of Mar (1332–1374). He was a son of '''Domhnall II of Mar'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas became Earl of Mar whilst still a child living in the Kingdom of England, and it took several years for Thomas to return to the Kingdom of Scotland and take charge of his inheritance. He had a fairly successful career in Sc
2 CONC ottish politics, becoming '''Great Chamberlain of Scotland''', and several times acting as an ambassador to England.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice, firstly '''Margaret Graham of Menteith''', and secondly '''Margaret Stewart, Countess of Angus'''. He was succeeded by his sister Margaret, who was married to William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas. He died childle
2 CONC ss in 1374, bringing his line and the ancient Gaelic earldom of Mar through the male line to an end. The earldom passed into the Douglas family.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Name: Thomas Mar  Suffix: 9th Earl of Mar  Sex: M  Note: On 27 January 1356/7, David II granted Thomas, Earl of Mar, 2nd Lord of Garioch, securing his gfather's inheritable title by fee. In 1368 he was Great Chamberlain of Scotlan
2 CONC d. He had no children and was thus succeded by his only sister, Margaret, Countess of Mar.  Birth: BEF 1333  Death: 1373/74  _SDATE: 1 JUL 1373
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Donald Mar b: BEF 1305  Mother: Isabel Stewart b: BEF 1315
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Margaret Married: 
2 CONT
