2 CONC ell/6000000004157607493. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/341/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 341]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Isabella of Lennox is first referred to in her marriage-contract with Sir Murdach Stewart on 17 February 1391-92. In the contract hersisters Elizabeth and Margaret are referred to, and provision was made for their marriage
2 CONC , also at the disposal of the Earl of Fife. In August 1423 she confirmed a charter granted by her father, and did so under the title of Isabella Stewart, Duchess of Albany, Countess of Fife and Menteith, and heiress of the earldom
2 CONC  of Lennox. When her husband and father were arrested by King James I. she also was seized, while at Doune in Menteith, carried to Dunbar, and afterwards imprisoned in Tantallon Castle. How long she remained there is uncertain, bu
2 CONC t at a later date she was permitted to assume and to enjoy the honours and earldom of Lennox, which, as stated, were not forfeited. She resided chiefly at her castle of Inchmurrin in Loch Lomond, where she granted various charters
2 CONC  as Duchess of Albany and Countess of Lennox, but without the other titles of Fife and Menteith. One of these charters bound the grantee to provide stabling for her and her successors when they came to Drymen, and also lodging and
2 CONC  fire for poor people as had been required by former Lords of Lennox. Another writ provided for masses on behalf of King Robert Bruce and the Countess's own immediate kin, including her mother. Besides other pious gifts, the Count
2 CONC ess endowed, or proposed to endow, a collegiate church at Dumbarton. It was dedicated to the Virgin Mary, and to it the Countess granted land. The Countess died between 1456 and 1458, probably about the later date. [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/342/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 342-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 November 1392: Transumpt of great seal charter in favour of Duncan, earl of Levenax [Lennox], of earldom of Levenax [Lennox], and lordship thereof, previously resigned by him, to be held by said earl and his heirs male, whom 
2 CONC failing by Murdoch Stewart, King's relative and Isabella, daughter of said earl, and their heirs. Transumpt, 20 Feb. 1460/1, authenticated by Symon [Simon] of Dalgles [Dalgleish], licenciate in decreets, precentor and general offi
2 CONC cial of Glasgow, at instance of John, lord Dernele [Darnley]. Notaries John of Restoune [Reston], William Sympill [Semple], John Yrnnes [Innes], and John Hasty [Hastie], all priests, Glasgow diocese. Witnesses to transumpt: Willia
2 CONC m, prior of Whithorn, Mr. David of Cadzow, rector of University of Glasgow, Patrick Leth [Leith], chancellor, William of Glendunwyne, William of Elphynstoun [Elphinstone], William Sympyl [Semple], notary public, William Turnbull, 
2 CONC canon of church of Glasgow, Sir William Sterwylyne [Stirling] of Cadar [Cawdor], kt., Walter Stewart of Archwile, kt., Alexander of Hammyltoun [Hamilton], son and apparent heir of laird of Ennerwyk [Innerwick], George Stewart of R
2 CONC ass, John Stewart, provost of city of Glasgow, sir Edward of Calderwod [Calderwood], vicar of Cambuslang, John Restoun [Reston], vicar of Curmanok [Carmunnoch], John Hasty [Hastie], notary public, John of Akynhede [Aitkenhead] and
2 CONC  John Broune [Brown], priests, Glasgow diocese. Seal of official of Glasgow on tag. RMS i, 862. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f40&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isabella+lennox&k
2 CONC o=a&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/40]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 August 1430: Charter by King James I confirming a charter by Duncan, Earl of Lennox, with consent of Murdoch, Duke of Albany and Governor of Scotland and of Isabella, Duchess of Albany and daughter to the said Earl, and with
2 CONC  consent of Walter Stewart, son and heir to the said Duke of Albany, in favour of William, lord of Graham, of the lands of Arachybeg, Ryncastill, Ardule, Mukarycht, Easter Garthcaroun, Middle Garthcaroun, Killearn, Wester Ledlewan
2 CONC , the superiority of Middle Ledlewan, Kylmonogan, Strathblane, Mukdanachrois, Clochbarre, Dougalstoun, Caystoun, the two Chawnachies, Barloch, Achinross, Ballecleracht and Balgrochan lying within the earldom of Lennox; upon his ow
2 CONC n resignation in favour of himself and Patrick de Graham, son and heir to the deceased Alexander de Graham who was son and heir to the said William and heirs male, according to the tailzie [which cannot be read due to the charter 
2 CONC being damaged]. Earl Duncan's charter dated at Killearn, 10 Aug 1423. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f1%2f7%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isabella+lennox&ko=a&r=&ro=s
2 CONC &df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/A/1/7/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: See [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/35/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli II: 265]  for this confirmation. See [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/36/mode/1up Registrum Magni Si
2 CONC gilli II: 166] for a charter of confirmation by King James I, 28 Aug 1430, confirming a charter of confirmation granted by Isabella Stewart, Duchess of Albany, Countess of Fife and Menteith and heiress of the earldom of Lennox whe
2 CONC reby she confirms the foregoing charter by her father; her charter of confirmation is dated 25 Aug 1423.'''
