2 CONT '''20 January 1460: Instrument in favour of John Lord Darnley (in the hands of Steven de Heslyhope, nottar) proceeding on a charter by King Robert III in favour of Duncan, Earl of Levenax [Lennox] and his male heirs, which failing
2 CONC  to Murdo Stuart, the King's cousin and Isabel, daughter to the Earl of Lennox, the longest liver of the two of them and their heirs, which failing the nearest lawful heir of Duncan, proceeding on the Earl's resignation and dated 
2 CONC at Dunfermline, 8 Nov 1393. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f5%2f3%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isabel+lennox&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, 
