1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ALEXANDER STEWART of LENNOX ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, is misidentified as Sir Alasdair Stewart in a number of pedigrees published by [https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62741/?name=alasdair_Stewart&death=1425  Anc
2 CONC estry]. It is difficult to be certain of where the information published by Ancestry came from, but it is possible that it was first suggested in the profile published for Egidia Stewart, the wife of William Douglas of Nithsdale, 
2 CONC by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egidia_Stewart Wikipedia], which cites [https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Complete_Peerage_of_England_Scotland_Ire/JLAKAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=Egidia+Stewart&pg=PA134&printsec=frontcover Coc
2 CONC kayne's Complete Peerage: 134] as the source for the marriage of Alasdair Stewart and Egidia Douglas and then goes on to ignore the fact that Cockayne actually identified Egidia Douglas's husband as Alexander Stewart.'''</blockquo
2 CONC te>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, is the third son of https://www.geni.com/people/Murdoch-Stewart-Duke-Of-Albany/6000000000518137061?through=6000000003615436080. The name of his mother has not been satisfactorily i
2 CONC dentified but it seems quite likely, probable even, that he is the son of  https://www.geni.com/people/Isabella-of-Lennox-Duchess-of-Albany-and-Countess-of-Lennox/6000000000517621797?through=6000000225638263884. [https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/162/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 162] [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/n184/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV: clxxxi]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, is noticed in the witness list of a charter by which his father confirms that Alexander Lindsay, Earl of Crawford, has given certain lands and privileges to his eldest son, David L
2 CONC indsay. The date of the Duke's confirmation is not known, but the Earl of Crawford's charter was issued on 13 December 1421. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD121%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1390&dt=1430&di=n NRS: GD121/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 7 October 1423 Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox is noticed again, in the witness list of his father's charter of confirmation in favour of Walter Ogilvy of Luntrethin. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD16%2f3%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y NRS: GD16/3/8] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Knighthood ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 21 May 1424 Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, was knighted by James I, King of Scots. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/n90/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV: lxxxviii-lxxxviv where Extracta e v
2 CONC ariis Cronicis Scocie, p. 227 is cited.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, was was beheaded at Stirling on 25 May 1425. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/571/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 571] [https:
2 CONC //archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/162/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 150-1] [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir04grea/page/n95/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls IV: xcii]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Egidia-Douglas-Countess-of-Orkney/6000000001013085939. [https://archive.org/details/CalendarOfEntriesInThePapalRegisterV7/page/221/mode/1up Papa
2 CONC l Registers VII: 221]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 December 1421: Charter of confirmation by Murdach, duke of Albany, earl of Fife and of Menteth, governor of Scotland, of charter, 13 December 1421, by Alexander of Lindesai, earl of Craufurde, to David Lyndesay, his eldest s
2 CONC on, and specified heirs, of 100 merks of the great customs of burgh of Aberdeen, 40 merks of burgh fermes of said burgh, with office of sheriff thereof, annualrent of 13 merks from burgh of Banf with lands of Bauchlouch in sheriff
2 CONC dom of Banf, barony of Oures, lordship of Neudosk, in sheriffdom of Kincardyn, lordship of Glenesk, with advocation of church of Lethnot and chaplaincy of Dalbolge, 40 merks of the great customs of burgh of Montrosse, lordship of 
2 CONC Innerarite, with advocation of church thereof, barony of Douny, lordship of Guthry, lordship of Futhnevin and forest of Platarie, lordship of Clova, lordship of Ruthuen and advocation of four chaplaincies of altar of St George in 
2 CONC parish church of burgh of Dunde, with advocation of chaplaincy of altar of All Saints in said church, and a house in Dunde on north side of said church in vennel of the Friars, in sheriffdom of Forfare, lordship of Miggil, lordshi
2 CONC p of Melginche, lordship of Aberbothry, lordship of Lethnot, lordship of Carnbady, lordship of Baltrody, and tenement in burgh of Perth, in the Watirgate, on east side thereof, in sheriffdom of Perth, lordship of Carnbow and of Ne
2 CONC uhal in constabulary of Carale, 28 December 1421. Seal damaged on tag, in blue silk bag with a red ribbon. Witnesses: William, bishop of Glasgow, Chancellor of Scotland, Sir Alexander Stewart of Levenax, son of said Murdoch, [Note
2 CONC ] Sir Walter Stewart of Railstoun, Sir William Hay of Nachtane, kts., and Alan of Ottirburne, said Murdoch's secretary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD121%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn
2 CONC =n&tp=n&k=alexander+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1390&dt=1430&di=n National Records of Scotland, Fothringham of Powrie Muniments, reference GD121/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Duke Murdoch's charter of confirmation must be dated later than 21 May 1424, the date upon which his son Sir Alexander Stewart of Lennox was knighted by James I, King of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 October 1423: Charter of confirmation under the great seal by Murdach, Duke of Albany, Governor of Scotland, of charter, dated at Dundee 26 Aug 1423, by Alexander of Gardin of Boroufelde to Walter of Ogilvi of Luntrethin of t
2 CONC he lands and barony of Formale. Witnesses: Henry, bishop of St. Andrews, William, bishop of Glasgow, chancellor, Alexander Stewart, son of the granter and Robert of Conynghame of Kilmauris, esquires, Sir John of Wemis and Sir Alex
2 CONC ander of Forbes, knights and Alan of Ottirburne, secretary. Perth. [Fragment of seal appended; not registered in R.M.S.]. [84.7]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f3%2f8&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/3/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from Papal Registers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 Kal. May 1422: To the bishop of St. Andrews. Mandate to dispense Alexander Steuart, donsel, and Egidia de Duglas, relict of Henry Synclar, knight, of the dioceses of Glasgow and St. Andrews, to marry notwithstanding that Alex
2 CONC ander is distant in the third, and Egidia in the second degree of kindred from their common stock. Oblate nobis. [https://archive.org/details/CalendarOfEntriesInThePapalRegisterV7/page/221/mode/1up Papal Registers VII: 221]'''
