1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.swintonfamilysociety.org/
2 CONT
2 CONT * Living <1398
2 CONT * 1421: Wounded the Duke of Clarence in the face with a lance then the earl of Buchan killed him.
2 CONT * Married 1423 - Lady Marjory Dunbar, daughter of George Dunbar, the 11th and last Earl of March
2 CONT * 17 Aug 1424: Killed at the Battle of Vermeuil, France
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_John_Swinton,_15th_of_that_Ilk
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Swinton, 15th of that Ilk was a son of Sir John Swinton, 14th of that Ilk and Princess Margaret, daughter of Robert, Duke of Albany who served as Regent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Hundred Years' War he was a doughty warrior who fought and led the Clan Swinton at the Battle of Baugé against the English in France in 1421, where the French-Scottish forces were victorious. Although the credit for thi
2 CONC s is claimed by others, he is said to have been the knight who slew the Duke of Clarence, brother of King Henry V of England. The incident appears in Sir Walter Scott’s poem, ‘The Lay of the Last Minstrel’:
2 CONT
2 CONT  "And Swinton laid the lance in rest,
2 CONT
2 CONT  That amed of yore the sparkling crest
2 CONT
2 CONT  Of Clarence's Plantagenet".
2 CONT
2 CONT However Sir John Swinton was killed when the Clan Swinton fought at the Battle of Verneuil in France in 1424.
2 CONT
