1 OCCU 1st Lord Lorne and Inner Meath
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lord of Lorne is a title in the Peerage of Scotland. First it was created for Robert Stewart, son of John Stewart, ambassador to the English king, by a daughter of Eoghan de Ergadia, Laird of Latharna. Robert  was 
2 CONC succeeded by his oldest son John, member of the Scottish Parliament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Stewart, 1st Lord of Lorn, was a Commissioner to England for the release for King James, I in 1421  Between 1424 and 1429 he was one of the hostages for the payment of King James, I of Scotland's ransom. He was created 1st 
2 CONC Lord Lorn [Scotland] before 5 September 1439.1 He lived at Innermeath, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 1379 Lorn, Argyllshire, Scotland. Death: December 20, 1449 (70) Shrewsbury, Shropshire, England. ('''Possible alternate death date 20 Dec 1463''': http://www.thepeerage.com/p10798.htm). '''The same source lists one more pos
2 CONC sible child as Alan Stewart.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir John Stewart of Innermeath and Isobel MacDougall, of Argyll.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Janet MacDougall and Joan Stewart, of Albany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Sir David Stewart; John Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorn; Margaret Stewart of Lorn; Walter Stewart, 1st Lord Innermeath; David Stewart; daughter of Robert Stewart of Lorn; Robert Stewart; Agnes Stewart of Lorn and Mary Stewart of 
2 CONC Lorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Christian Dundas; Isabel Murray; James Stewart, the Black Knight of Lorn; Jean Bruce; Maud Stewart; Dau STEWART; Robert STEWART 1st Lord of Lorn; Alexander Stewart, 2nd of Grandtully and Archibald Stewart « less
2 CONT
