1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM ABERNETHY, LORD ABERNETHY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 January 1463-64: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James III, King of Scots, confirms possession of various lands to William, Lord Abernethy in Rothymay, who had previously resigned them in order to obtain a 
2 CONC new grant. The lands in question, which included Rothymay in the Sheriffdom of Aberdeen, were to be held by Lord Abernethy and his lawful male heirs; who failing by his brother James of Abernethy and his lawful heirs; whom failing
2 CONC  by his brother George Abernethy and his heirs; whom failing by his brother Archibald and his heirs; whom failing by his cousin John Abernethy and his heirs. John is identified as the son of Oswald Abernethy. In the event of the f
2 CONC ailure of all the heirs in remainder the lands in question were to pass to the nearest heirs of William, Lord Abernethy, bearing the Name and Arms of Abernethy. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/166/mode/1up
2 CONC  RMS 1424-1513: charter number 778]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1464: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James III, King of Scots, confirms possession of various lands to William, Lord Abernethy in Rothymay, who had previously resigned them in order to obtain a new g
2 CONC rant. The lands in question, which included Rothymay in the Sheriffdom of Aberdeen, were to be held by Lord Abernethy and his lawful male heirs; who failing by his brother James of Abernethy and his lawful heirs; whom failing by h
2 CONC is brother George Abernethy and his heirs; whom failing by his brother Archibald and his heirs; whom failing by his cousin John Abernethy and his heirs. John is identified as the son of Oswald Abernethy. In the event of the failur
2 CONC e of all the heirs in remainder the lands in question were to pass to the nearest heirs of William, Lord Abernethy, bearing the Name and Arms of Abernethy. One third of the lands in question were to be reserved to the unnamed spou
2 CONC se of Lord Abernethy. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/171/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 800]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 January 1482-83: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James III, King of Scots, confirms possession of various lands to William, Lord Abernethy in Rothymay, who had previously resigned them in order to obtain a 
2 CONC new grant. The lands in question, which included Rothymay in the Sheriffdom of Aberdeen, were incorporated by James III, King of Scots, as the barony of Abernethy. The barony was to be held by Lord Abernethy and his lawful male he
2 CONC irs; who failing by his brother James of Abernethy and his lawful male heirs; whom failing by his brother George Abernethy and his lawful male heirs; whom failing by the lawful male heirs of his deceased brother Archibald Aberneth
2 CONC y; whom failing by his cousin John Abernethy and his heirs. John is identified as the son of Oswald Abernethy. In the event of the failure of all the heirs in remainder the lands in question were to pass to the nearest heirs of Wi
2 CONC lliam, Lord Abernethy, bearing the Name and Arms of Abernethy. 
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/321/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 1534]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
