2 CONT '''25 January 1562-63: Charter by Alexander Bane of Tullich to Robert Munro of Foulis of half of the lands and fishings of Feirincosky in Braquhat, viz., half of the lands of Innerane and fishings thereof, Linset croy, Linset moyr
2 CONC , Altas beg, Altas moyr, Achynes, and half of the mill of Innerane, in the sheriffdom of Innernes, in excambion for infeftment to said Alexander Bane of the lands of Wester Logy, mill and brewhouse thereof, in the earldom of Ross 
2 CONC and sheriffdom foresaid, and of the arable lands in the burgh of Dingwall belonging to said Robert Munro, said half lands and fishings of Ferrincosky in Braquhat to be held of the Crown in fee and heritage for rights and services 
2 CONC used and wont; with clause of warrandice. Witnesses, Donald Munro, archdeacon of the Isles, Hugh Munro Hectorson, George Munro, brothergerman of said Robert Munro of Foulis, Donald Kemp, burgess of Dingwall, William Cumming, burge
2 CONC ss of Innernes, William Munro, vicar of Dingwall, and James Buchart, notary public. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD93%2f78&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bane&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=
2 CONC &dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Munro family of Foulis, reference GD93/78]'''
