2 CONT '''28 September 1571: Contract between Hugh, Lord Fraser of Lowet, and Alexander Bayne of Tulloch, whereby the said Hugh binds himself to infeft the said Alexander in the town and lands of Dunballach in lordship of Lowet and sheri
2 CONC ffdom of Innernes, in blenchfarm, and the said Alexander agrees to pay 1000 merks Scots and to grant letters of reversion containing the clause that when the said Hugh obtained sasine of the lands of the priory of Bewlie he would 
2 CONC infeft the said Alexander in the lands of Rowindoun and that if the said Hugh did not obtain sasine of the said lands he would pay the said Alexander the said sum of 1000 merks. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalog
