2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 September 1587: Charter of confirmation by King James VI in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tullich, his wife and his son, of the lands of Kilmuir. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D255%2f1%2f1%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous titles, including Fife, Sutherland and Midlothian, reference GD1/498/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    14
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 September 1590: Charter by which Alexander Bayne of Tulloch confirms that he has given the lands of Wester Logy to Alexander Bayne, his eldest son and heir, and his son's wife Agnes Fraser. The lands of Wester Logy, which ar
2 CONC e located within the earldom of Ross and sheriffdom of Inverness, were to be held by Alexander junior and his lawful male heirs by his wife Agnes Fraser, whom failing by the lawful heirs of his brother german John Bayne, whom fail
2 CONC ing by the heirs of his father Alexander Bayne of Tulloch. The charter was witnessed by Master Ronald Bayne, bastard son of Alexander Bayne of Tulloch: "M. Ronnaldo Bayne filio naturali dicti Alex. senioris" and others. Alexander 
2 CONC Bayne junior obtained a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland on 28 June 1600. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/355/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1045]
2 CONT
2 CONT                    15
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 October 1590: Letter of Reversion by David Clapen, indweller in Leyth, narrating that although Mr Hector Munro of Foulis has alienated to him the half davach of Lytill Clyne and the miln of Catoll, in the diocese of Ross and
2 CONC  sheriffdom of Innernes, nevertheless he binds himself to renounce the same on payment of 1,800 marks within 'Sanct Geillis Kirk of Edinburgh upon the dask foiranent the pulpet thereof'. Witnesses, Mr Andro Cramby, dean of Ross, M
2 CONC r James Robertsone, minister at Tayne, David Monypennye and John Hay, 'boweris' in the Channonrie of Ross, Adame Dunbar, notary public, and Mr Ronald Bayne, son of Alexander Bayne of Tullycht. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD93%2f127&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Munro family of Foulis, reference GD93/127]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    16
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1591: Charter of confirmation by King James VI in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tullich, of the town and lands of Sligo. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f2%2f3&st=
2 CONC 1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD255/1/2/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    17
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1591: Precept of sasine from chancery in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tullich, of the town and lands of Sligo. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f2%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD255/1/2/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    18
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 January 1592: Instrument of sasine in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tullich, his wife and his son, of the lands of Kilmuir. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f1%2f6&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD255/1/1/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    19
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 January 1596-97. Summons under the Quarter Seal to John Hay of Lochloy, David Brody of that Ilk, George Dunbar of Tarie, David Hay of Zett, William Douglas of Erlismylne, David Ross of Holme, John Ross, in Cantray, Alexander
2 CONC  Dolles of Burdett, John Hay of Urchuir, William Dolles, apparent of Burdett, John Ross, provost of Nairne, Donald Calder, in Litle Urchuire, Alexander Ross, in Leonach, Mungo Gollane, burgess of Rosmarkie, William Thomesoun, in t
2 CONC he Canonry of Ross, John Cuthbert of Auldcastlehill, John Ross, burgess of Nairne, William Tulloche, burgess there, Walter Ross, in Mekilgeddes, Robert Leslie, in Canonry of Ross, Alexander McKey, in the templelands in Urtissar, b
2 CONC lack John Ross, burgess of Innernes, and Thomas Fraser of Monack, who were upon the inquest of a chancery brieve at the instance of Elezebeth Ross, relict of Robert Monro of Foullis, for serving her to a reasonable terce of the la
2 CONC nds and others in which said deceased Robert died last vest and seased, as also requiring the compearance of said Elezebeth Ross and Gordoun, apparent of, now her spouse, and to all others having interest, to compear before the Ki
2 CONC ng and Lords of Council at Edinburgh on the day of the month of next, to answer at the instance of Thomas Hammiltoun of Drumcairnie and William Heart of Levelandis, advocates of the directors of chancery, and Hector Monro of Assin
2 CONC t, William Bailzie of Druneane, and Katherine Monro, his spouse, Ninian Lows, and Thomas Lows, lawful sons of deceased Ninian Lows, burgesses of Edinburgh, Alexander Bane of Tullich, William Monro, son of Ferquhard Monro of Kilter
2 CONC ne, Hugh Monro, son and heir of deceased Alexander Monro of Arduilzie, Ferquhard Monro, in Inverane, Robert Monro, vicar of Urquhart, and, heritable proprietors of the lands undermentioned, and also at the instance of Monro, now o
2 CONC f Fowlis, brother and heir of said deceased Robert Monro of Foulles, heritable possessor of said lands and others, asking for reduction of the service granted at the sheriff-court of Innernes on 07 Jul 1595 , to said Elezebeth of 
2 CONC the terce of the lands of Mekle Daane, the davach lands of Carbestill and Tayninver in Stratharron, and other lands, and for punishment according to law of said members of inquest, in respect that they erred in granting said servi
2 CONC ce to lands in which said deceased Robert Monro of Foullis did not die vest. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD93%2f140&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+Tulloche&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=
2 CONC 1600&di=n National Recprds of Scotland, Papers of the Munro family of Foulis, reference GD93/140]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    20
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1596: Instrument of sasine in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tullich, of the lands of Easter Sligo. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f2%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n
2 CONC &k=alexander+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD255/1/2/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    21
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 October 1596: Charter granted by Alexander Bayne of Tullich to John Bayne, his son, of the town and lands of Sligo. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f3%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD255/1/3/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    22
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 October 1596: Charter by which Alexander Bayne of Tulloch confirmed that he has given the eastern half of the town and lands of Sligo, which are located within the bishopric of Ross, lordship of Ardmananche, and sheriffdom o
2 CONC f Inverness, to his son John Bayne, burgess of Dingwall. This land was to be held by him in feu ferme. This charter, which was witnessed by Master Ronald Baynem burgess of Dingwall, and others, was confirmed under the Great Seal o
2 CONC f Scotland on 28 June 1600. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/355/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1046]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    23
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 June 1598: 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/355/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1045]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    24
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 July 1600: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms, for the good service given to his mother and grandfather by the deceased Alexander Bayne of Tulloch and by his son and heir Duncan Bayne, now of Tulloch, that he
2 CONC  has confirmed possession of the lands of Eister Drynie, in the earldom of Ross and sheriffdom of Inverness, to Duncan Bayne now of Tulloch. The lands of Eister Dyrnie had previously been resigned by Alexander Bayne lawful son of 
2 CONC the said deceased Alexander Bayne of Tulloch, the elder. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/362/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1066]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    25
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1600: (14) Jul. 31.1600 DUNCANUS BANE de Tullich, haeres Alexandri Bane de Tullich, patris, - in terris de Tullich: -E 3m. etc. - BallafreisL -E. 3m. 4s. etc. - Straithskey: -E. 3m. etc. - forresta de Strathbranoch: -E 
2 CONC 4 bollae ordei etc. - molendino de Oussie cum crofta et Airthouses - astrictis multuris et suken terrarum de Dunglust, quatuor Glakkis, Mekill, Kinnardie, Little Kinnardie, et Collie (vel Tollie), Wester Drynie, Dawachcarne, et Br
2 CONC awane ac allis multuris -E. 10l. 16s. etc. - et integro 18l. 4s. etc. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ah
