1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN BAYNE OF FEARLIN===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Burgess of Dingwall===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Tulloch made his last will and testament at Tulloch on 28 September 1596, in the presence of the Reverend Robert Logie, Minister of the Gospel at Urquart and Logie, Mr. Rannald Bayne, his son, and John Bayne,
2 CONC  his brother. He left his soul to God and appointed his body to be buried in the Kirk of Dingwall.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Tulloch nominated and constituted his four sons, Duncan Bayne, identified as his apparent heir, Alexander Bayne, John Bayne, and Mr. Alexander Bayne, to be his executors testamentary and intromitters with his
2 CONC  goods and gear. He left legacies to his brothers John Bayne and Lachlan Bayne, and his sisters Cristiane Bayne and Agnes Bayne. He also left legacies to his four sons, and his three surviving children by Agnes Fraser, John Bayne,
2 CONC  Jonet Bayne and Catherine Bayne. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of umqle Alexr Bane of Tulloch, within the Sheriffdom of Inverness, reference CC8/8/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118188605841& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118187259188& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118186998306& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118185998545& Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 June 1583: Charter, incorporating resignation and sasine, by Alexander Robertsoun [Robertson], burgess of Dyngwall [Dingwall], and Marion neyn Donnald vik Ane roy, his spouse, in favour of Alexander Bayne of Tulch and Agnes 
2 CONC Fraser, his spouse, and the survivor in conjunct infeftment, and John Bayne, their second son, of 1 1/2 acres of land at Gallowhyll [Gallowhill] in the burgh of Dyngwall, sheriffdom of Inverness. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f498%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous titles, including Fife, Sutherland and Midlothian, reference GD1/
2 CONC 498/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 October 1596: Charter by which Alexander Bayne of Tulloch confirmed that he has given the eastern half of the town and lands of Sligo, which are located within the bishopric of Ross, lordship of Ardmananche, and sheriffdom o
2 CONC f Inverness, to his son John Bayne, burgess of Dingwall. This land was to be held by him in feu ferme. This charter, which was witnessed by Master Ronald Baynem burgess of Dingwall, and others, was confirmed under the Great Seal o
2 CONC f Scotland on 28 June 1600. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/355/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1046]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
