1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER BAYNE OF WESTER LOGIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Alastair Mor Ban'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Wester Logie, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bayne-of-Tulloch/4162880419190037856?through=6000000100262364072 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Fraser/600000001
2 CONC 7601998007?through=6000000100262364072 In his father's last will and testament dated 28 September 1596 he is identified as the only surviving son of his father's marriage to Agnes Fraser. [NRS: CC8/8/35] [https://www.geni.com/docu
2 CONC ments/view?doc_id=6000000118185998545& Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Tulloch made his last will and testament at Tulloch on 28 September 1596, in the presence of the Reverend Robert Logie, Minister of the Gospel at Urquart and Logie, Mr. Rannald Bayne, his son, and John Bayne,
2 CONC  his brother. He left his soul to God and appointed his body to be buried in the Kirk of Dingwall.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Tulloch nominated and constituted his four sons, Duncan Bayne, identified as his apparent heir, Alexander Bayne, John Bayne, and Mr. Alexander Bayne, to be his executors testamentary and intromitters with his
2 CONC  goods and gear. He left legacies to his brothers John Bayne and Lachlan Bayne, and his sisters Cristiane Bayne and Agnes Bayne. He also left legacies to his four sons, and his three surviving children by Agnes Fraser, John Bayne,
2 CONC  Jonet Bayne and Catherine Bayne. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of umqle Alexr Bane of Tulloch, within the Sheriffdom of Inverness, reference CC8/8/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000127622355295& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118188605841& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118187259188& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000118185998545& Image of Testament] 	
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bayne of Wester Logie is reported to have died before 1624. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4ae/bayne3.php Stirnet: Bayne 3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 January 1582: Letters of procuratory by the Alexander Bane, lawful son to Alexander Bane of Tullich, with consent of his said father and of Agnes Fraser his mother, for their liferent interest appointing his procurators for 
2 CONC resigning into the hands of King James VI as superior, the half of the town and lands of Cultaloude and Glenskayth in favour and for new infeftment thereof to be given to Colin McKenzie of Kintail and his heirs and assignees: to b
2 CONC e held of the Crown as freely as the granter held the same. Dated at Carradell. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD305%2f1%2f20%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bane&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacKenzie Family, Earls of Cromartie (Cromartie Muniments), reference GD305/1/20/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 February 1581-82: Notarial instrument on the resignation by Alexander Bane of Tullich, Agnes Frayser his spouse and Alexander Bane their son. In favour of Colin McKennyth of Kintail and his heirs and assignees of the lands o
2 CONC f Culleleod, which were held by them in warrandice of the lands of Kilmure, and salmon fishings thereof called the Stell of the Ness, and in which latter lands and fishing the granters had now been infeft by the said Colin McKenny
2 CONC th in terms of a contract between them. Done in the castle of the Chanonry of Ross. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD305%2f1%2f20%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bane&ko=p&r
2 CONC =&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacKenzie Family, Earls of Cromartie (Cromartie Muniments), reference GD305/1/20/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 September 1590: Charter by which Alexander Bayne of Tulloch confirms that he has given the lands of Wester Logy to Alexander Bayne, his eldest son and heir, and his son's wife Agnes Fraser. The lands of Wester Logy, which ar
2 CONC e located within the earldom of Ross and sheriffdom of Inverness, were to be held by Alexander junior and his lawful male heirs by his wife Agnes Fraser, whom failing by the lawful heirs of his brother german John Bayne, whom fail
2 CONC ing by the heirs of his father Alexander Bayne of Tulloch. The charter was witnessed by Master Ronald Bayne, bastard son of Alexander Bayne of Tulloch: "M. Ronnaldo Bayne filio naturali dicti Alex. senioris" and others. Alexander 
2 CONC Bayne junior obtained a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland on 28 June 1600. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/355/mode/1up RMS, 1593-1608: 1045]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 September 1608: Instrument of renunciation of the lands of Kilmuir, granted by John Chisholm of Comer and Janet Bayne his spouse, in favour of Alexander Bayne of Logie Wester. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f4%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=janet+bayne&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal papers, reference GD
2 CONC 255/1/4/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1682: (6390) MAGISTER JOANNE BAYNE de Delnie, haeres Alexandri Bayne de Logie-Wester, filii primo geniti secundi matrimonu Alexandri Bayne de Tulloch, avi.  xxxvi. 212. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&p
2 CONC g=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=bayne&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc
2 CONC . II: Inquisitionis Generales]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1682: (6391) MAGISTER JOANNE BAYNE de Delnie, haeres masculus provisionis et conquestus secundi matrimonii Alexander Bayne de Tulloch, proavi.  xxxvi. 213. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR
2 CONC 17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=bayne&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II: Inquisi
2 CONC tionis Generales]'''
2 CONT
