2 CONT *''''''John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #72732, b. 1542, d. 6 April 1604
2 CONT *Father      James Hamilton, 2nd Earl Arran, Duc de Chatellerault, Regent of Scotland1 d. 22 Jan 1575
2 CONT *Mother     Margaret Douglas1 d. a 24 May 1579
2 CONT *''''''     John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton was born in 1542.1 A contract for the marriage of John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton and Margaret Lyon was signed on 30 December 1577 at Maybole, Scotland.2 John Hamilton, 1
2 CONC st Marquess of Hamilton died on 6 April 1604.1
2 CONT *''''''Family 1      Margaret Lyon d. 1626
2 CONT *''''''Family 2 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir John Hamilton, Member of Parliament for Lanarkshire+3 b. c 1590, d. c 1637
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11566] The Scots Peerage, Vol. IV, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 369-373.
2 CONT * 2.[S11566] The Scots Peerage, Vol. IV, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 372-373.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 405.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2420.htm#i72732
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT *''''''John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #109390, b. circa 1535, d. 6 April 1604
2 CONT *Last Edited=16 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.14%
2 CONT *''''''     John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton was born circa 1535.2 He was the son of James Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Arran and Lady Margaret Douglas.1 He married Margaret Lyon, daughter of John Lyon, 7th Lord Glamis and Janet K
2 CONC eith, between 30 December 1577 and 10 February 1578.3 He died on 6 April 1604.3 His will was probated on 30 June 1608.3
2 CONT *''''''     He was styled as Earl of Arran between 1575 and 1599.4 In 1579 he was forfault as a faithful adherent of Queen Mary.4 He fought in the siege of Stirling Castle on 3 November 1585, and the King.4 He held the office of G
2 CONC overnor of Dumbarton Castle in December 1585.4 On 10 December 1585 he was pardoned following the repeal (by Parliament) of the forfeiture against his family.4 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] on 10 December 
2 CONC 1585.4 He held the office of Lieutenant of the South of Scotland in 1589.4 He was created 1st Lord Aven [Scotland] on 17 April 1599, probably created at the same time as the Marquess of Hamilton, but possibly at the same time as t
2 CONC he Earl of Arran i.e. 11 Aug 1603. However this title doesn't appear to have been used after 1611.4 He was created 1st Marquess of Hamilton [Scotland] on 17 April 1599.5
2 CONT *''''''Children of John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton and Margaret Lyon
2 CONT ** 1.Lady Jean Hamilton+6
2 CONT ** 2.Lady Margaret Hamilton2 b. bt 1579 - 1585, d. a 10 Jun 1606
2 CONT ** 3.Hon. Edward Hamilton3 b. b 1589
2 CONT ** 4.James Hamilton, 2nd Marquess of Hamilton+5 b. 1589, d. 2 Mar 1624/25
2 CONT *''''''Child of John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton
2 CONT ** 1.Sir John Hamilton+7 b. b 1586, d. 1638
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 222. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 1283. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baroneta
2 CONC ge, 106th edition.
2 CONT * 3.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 258.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 257.
2 CONT * 5.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 223.
2 CONT * 6.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 860. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
