1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~tlosborne/Burnett/Burnetthistory/ourburnettkin.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. THOMAS BURNETT - born about 2 Sept. 1574 in St. Nicholas, Aberdeen, Scotland. He married MARGARET JOHNSTON, 8 Nov. 1608 in Aberdeen, Scotland.  She was born about 1575 in Scotland.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Some have the parents of  Thomas listed as John, born abt 1548, and Isabel Burnett, married in 1573 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland but I have not seen documentation on this as yet.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=collinsgensearch&id=I1557
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret JOHNSTON 8 NOV 1608 in St. Nicholas Church, Aberdeen, Scotland, daughter of John JOHNSTON. She was born 1584 in Scotland, and died 1672 in Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Thomas BURNETT and Margaret JOHNSTON are:
2 CONT *  i.	John BURNETT Sr was born 25 DEC 1610 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland, and died Feb 1685/1686 in Old Rappahannock County, Virginia.
2 CONT *  ii.	Isabel BURNETT was born 31 AUG 1609 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland, and died ABT 1612.
2 CONT *  iii.	Cristen BURNETT was born 28 DEC 1613 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT *   iv.	David BURNETT was born 28 DEC 1613 in Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT *   v.	Robert BURNETT was born 3 SEP 1615 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT *   vi.	Elspeth BURNETT was born 17 Feb 1616/17 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT *  vii.	Margaret BURNETT was born 11 MAY 1618 in St. Nicholas Parish, Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.callzia.com/Family_Friends/Burnett_Family/w/r/f/Thomas_Burnett.html THOMAS, OUR 9TH GREAT-GRANDFATHER was born in the St. Nicholas Parish in the city of Aberdeen. He died in Aberdeen. He was the 1st BARONET OF LEYS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Above provided by Maredia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Narrative At this point in history many of the Burnetts appear to have been merchants, Thomas among them. They were prominent people in Aberdeen and the records of St. Nicholas contains frequent references to Burnett names associa
2 CONC ted with donations in support of various aisles of the church. Church records indicate that the Burnetts were landowners within the developing Aberdeen and were building townhouses in the prime sites of the day such as Guestrow, S
2 CONC hiprow, and Schoolhill.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and his brother Andrew, Burgesses of Aberdeen, were killed during Montrose's Battle of Justicemills, or the subsequent rout of Aberdeen, on 13 September 1644. Over 150 burgesses and several members of the Council lost their
2 CONC  lives. In St. Mary's Aisle of St. Nichlas Church, Thomas' and Andrew's names are inscribed on a large stone which has, as a centerpiece, a shield with the Arms of Leys. Also inscribed on the stone is the name Alexander Burnett wh
2 CONC o died in 1685, son to Thomas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Provided by jboyle.  His Mother Elizabeth Lumsden's link http://www.lawrencefamhis.com/burnett-o/g0/p323.htm#i8073* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/121286806/thomas-burnett Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 10 2021, 7:24:17 UTC''
