2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The eldest son, '''John Johnston of that ilk''', also known as John Johnston of Caskieben, married, first, Janet, daughter of Turing of Foveran, by whom he had two sons, George and John, and two daughters; and, sec
2 CONC ondly, Catherine, daughter of Lundie of that ilk, in Fife, by whom he had, with one daughter, two sons, Thomas, in virtue of his mother’s contract, laird of Craig, from whom the present baronet is lineally descended, and Gilbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT Genealogical account of the family of Johnston of that Ilk, formerly of Caskieben, in the shire of Aberdeen, and of its principal branches.  by Johnston, Alexander, Writer to the Signet (Publication date 1832)  Page 9-10. [https:/
2 CONC /archive.org/details/genealogicalacco1832john/page/n23/mode/2up Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Johnston of that Ilk (John Johnston of Caskieben)  married  first to Janet, daughter of Turing of Foveran. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT #George, his successor, married to Elizabeth, daughter of William Forbes of Tolquohoun
2 CONT #John, no succession 
2 CONT #Elizabeth, married to Bannerman of Elsick
2 CONT #Jean, married to William Forbes of Knapernay
2 CONT
2 CONT John Johnston of that Ilk (John Johnston of Caskieben) married second to Katherine Lundin, (1573-1616), daughter of William Lundie of that Ilk, married 1597, by whom he has two sons and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Thomas of Craig 1598-1656, married Mary Irvine 
2 CONT #Gilbert 1600-1617, of whom we have obtained no account 
2 CONT #Margaret, married to Parson Cheyne
2 CONT # Christian, married to John Forbes of Pitnacadell, and has issue 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
