1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The brother of the poet was a man of some local celebrity; he was Dr William Johnston, professor of mathematics in the Marishcal college of Aberdeen. "He was," says Wodrow, "ane learned and experienced physitian. H
2 CONC e wrote on the mathematics. His skill in the Latin was truly Ciceronian." [Catalogues of Scottish Writers, published by Mr Maidment, Edinburgh, 1833, p. 114.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for William Johnston:
2 CONT * Medical Doctor 
2 CONT * Chaired humanities and philosophy at the Univ.of Sedan
2 CONT * First professor of Mathematics in Marischal College, Aberdeen, Scotland.
2 CONT
