1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-William-Kerr/6000000171498679005
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Kirkcaldy of Grange was the son of Sir Thomas Kerr of Ferniehirst and Janet Kirkcaldy.1 A contract for the marriage of William Kirkcaldy of Grange and Elizabeth Lyon was signed on 14 February 1586/87.2 He died circa 13 Jan
2 CONC uary 1598/99.1      He was given the name of William Kerr at birth.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of William Kirkcaldy of Grange and Elizabeth Lyon
2 CONT # Alexander Kerr, 2nd Lord Jedburgh+1 b. c 1590, d. c 1650
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L4TK-Y3S
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/191970466/william-kirkaldy_kerr
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://era.ed.ac.uk/handle/1842/6875 ''Lairds and gentlemen: A study of the landed families of the Eastern Anglo-Scottish Borders c.1540-1603''] Vol 2 pp 55-8 & 118-9
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT According to notes by David Carr, William became the 10th Baron of Ferniehurst, Scotland. However, he lived in London, England, and took his mother's maiden name to continue the Kirkcaldy line (Why? Possibly because she had no bro
2 CONC thers, and with a view to receiving the family inheritance.) However, when William failed to inherit family property in Grange, Scotland, his children reverted to the Carr or Kerr surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents:  son of Sir Thomas Kerr, 9th Baron of Fennerhurst and Janet Kirkaldy
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # on 14 February 1586/87 to Elizabeth Lyon was the daughter of John Lyon, 8th Lord Glamis and Elizabeth Abernethy.
2 CONT # in 1591 in London to Mary Ann Clifford b: ABT 1573 in England
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Elizabeth Lyon and William Kirkaldy of Grange
2 CONT # Alexander Kerr, 2nd Lord Jedburgh+3 b. c 1590, d. c 1650
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Direct line to the 9th Baron of Fennerhurst Scotland.... Andrew 1450-1543. The original Carr or Kerr was a follower of Norman Conquest-- WM the conqueror. His name is recorded ina charter in Battle Abbey "Karre". 
2 CONT
