1 OCCU Countess of Kinghorne
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Lyon,_Countess_of_Kinghorne
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Lyon, Countess of Kinghorne (1579 – 27 February 1618) was the daughter of John Murray, 1st Earl of Tullibardine and Catherine Drummond. Originally called Lady Anne Murray, she was the mistress of James VI of Scotland from 159
2 CONC 3 until her marriage to Patrick Lyon in 1595. Patrick Lyon, 1st Earl of Kinghorne, was the son of John Lyon, 8th Lord Glamis, and Elizabeth Abernethy. Upon marriage, Anne took the name of Lyon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne and Patrick Lyon, 1st Earl of Kinghorne were:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Lyon (d. August 1641)
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Lyon (d. 1660)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Lyon (d. 8 February 1637)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Lyon (d. 2 February 1618)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lyon, 2nd Earl of Kinghorne (13 August 1596 - 12 May 1646), a direct male-line ancestor to Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon (1900–2002), mother of Queen Elizabeth II.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 27 February 1618.
