1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Frederick Lyon</strong>, fifth son of John L. of Wester Ogil, and Catherine Ogilvie, and brother of preceding ; educated at Univ. of St Andrews ; M.A. (23rd July 1672); licen. by Presb. of Forfar in 1676 ; pres. by Patrick
2 CONC , first Earl of Strathmore, 29th Sept. 1681 ; was recommended 11th April for ordination, and adm. 12th May 1682; app. clerk to Presb. 1st May 1683; died of phthisis Sept. 1699, aged about 47. He marr. 1683, Isobel, daugh. of James
2 CONC  Cramond of Balnakeith, she survived him, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Patrick; 
2 CONT * John; 
2 CONT * James of Easterdeanhouses; 
2 CONT * William; 
2 CONT * Helen; 
2 CONT * Geilles; 
2 CONT * a daugh. (marr. George Lyon, min. of Yersdon).
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc05scot#page/246/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. V, page 247
