2 CONT
2 CONT John Guthrie, Bishop of Moray
2 CONT
2 CONT Diocese of Moray
2 CONT *In office	1623–1638
2 CONT *Predecessor	Alexander Douglas
2 CONT *Successor	Vacant (1638–1662); next bishop was Murdoch MacKenzie
2 CONT
2 CONT Orders
2 CONT *Consecration	October, 1623
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal details
2 CONT *Born	1580s - Scotland
2 CONT *Died	28 August 1649 - Guthrie, Angus
2 CONT
2 CONT Previous post	Minister of Kinnell, Arbirlot, Perth, then St Giles
2 CONT ___________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/The_arms_of_the_Scottish_bishoprics_%28IA_armsofscottishbi00lyonrich%29.pdf The Arms of the Scottish Bishoprics, Chapter X. Moray, pp.41-44]
2 CONT
2 CONT The arms of the diocese of Moray, like those of Aberdeen, are derived not from the dedication of the cathedral, as is common in Scotland, but from that of the parish church of the cathedral city. The diocesan arms of Moray are in 
2 CONC fact nothing more than an adaptation of the Common Seal of the Burgh of Elgin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The arms may be blazoned thus: --- "Azure, within a Church Porch St, Giles, vested and mired, holding in his dexter hand a Cross, and in the sinister a Book; fawning against him a Hind pierced in the back by an arrow, all proper."
2 CONT
