2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 February 1647: Ante-nuptial marriage contract between Donald Mcphersoune of Nuid and Bessie Mcphersoune, his sister, on the one part, and Malcolm Mcphersoune of Phoynes and Donald Mcphersoune, his eldest son on the other, wh
2 CONC ereby said Malcolm is to provide the sum of 800 merks, Bessie's tocher being 1200 merks, and whole sum of 2000 merks is to be invested in land. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f1
2 CONC 6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Phoynes&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/16]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1672: Discharge by William McIntoshe of Borlum to Donald and William Mcphersone, elder and younger of Nude, for 21/12 merks due by them to the deceased Lachlan Grant, minister at Kingusie, to which said William McInt
2 CONC oshe had right by assignation from Alexander Grant, son and executor dative of said Lachlan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f96&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lachlan+grant&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1675: Obligation by William M'Phersone [McPherson] of Nuid to fulfil the terms of his marriage-contract by obtaining a confirmation of the liferent right of Isobel M'Intoshe [McIntosh], his wife, in the two davochs of 
2 CONC Nuids. John M'Phersone [McPherson] of Bellichroane [Ballachroan] is cautioner. Dated at Nuide [Nuid], 30th August 1675; witnesses, John M'Pherson [McPherson] in Blarikie [Blaragie], and James and John, lawful sons of Donald M'Pher
2 CONC sone [McPherson] of Nuide. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f560&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of 
2 CONC Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/560]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
