1 NAME John John /Ogilvy/ 1st Baronet of Inverquarity
2 GIVN John John
2 SURN Ogilvy
2 NSFX 1st Baronet of Inverquarity
2 _MARNM Ogilvy
1 NAME Sir John Ogilvy, 1st Baronet of Inverquarity
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1587
2 PLAC Inverquharity, Aberdeenshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1660
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Oglivy of Inverquharity</strong>, in the parish of Kirriemuir, co Forfar, son and heir of Sir John Oglivy of the same (died about 1624), by Matilda, daughter of Thomas Fotheringham of Powrie, co Forfar, was born abou
2 CONC t 1587 and was created a Baronet [S] 29 September 1626, the patent being sealed 30 June 1627, but not recorded in the Great Seal register, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova S
2 CONC cotia, of which he had seizin in July 1627. He married, covenant 16 September 1622, Anne, daughter of Sir Alexander Irvine of Drum, co Aberdeen, by Marion, daughter of Robert (Douglas) Earl of Buchan [S]. He, who was a zealous roy
2 CONC alist, was living in 1647, when he had a remission on payment of a fine, but died before 1663."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n335/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 316
2 CONT
