1 OCCU Sheriff of Bute
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Stewart was born illegitimately between 1345 and 1390.2 He was the son of Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland and Moira Leitch.3 He married, firstly, Elizabeth Graham, daughter of Sir William Graham of Kin
2 CONC cardine and Mariot Oliphant, in 1407/8.1 He married, secondly, Janet Sympil.3 He died between 1445 and July 1449.3,4
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stewart also went by the nick-name of 'The Black Stewart'. Circa 1385 he had the islands of Arane (Arran), Bute and Cambrae erected into a county for him by his father.4 He held the office of Hereditary Sheriff of Bute.2 
2 CONC He was appointed Knight.3 He lived at Dundonald, Ayrshire, ScotlandG.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir John Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stewart of Fennock+4 d. c 1465
2 CONT James Stewart4 d. bt 1454 - 1464
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 3 1/2 brothers called John:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart, Lord of Burley (d. 1425)
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart of Cardney
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart ‘the Black’, sheriff of Bute (d. 1445/1449)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://www.thepeerage.com/p10210.htm#i102097
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT John had a another brother also named John. He was known as "The Black Stewart". Some sources confuse the two including their spouses.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Medlands [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_ftnref1433 Scotland, Kings] defers to a chapter in this source for John "the Black" Stewart:'''
2 CONT >Paul, J. B. (1905) “Stuart, Marquess of Bute,” in ''The Scots Peerage: Founded on Wood’s ed. of Sir Robert Douglas’s Peerage of Scotland; Containing an Historical and Genealogical Account of the Nobility of that Kingdom''. Edinbu
2 CONC rgh, Scotland, UK: David Douglas, pp. 285–311. '''Available at:''' [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/285/mode/1up?view=theater '''Archive.org'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two wives: Elizabeth Graham and Jean Simpill.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gilbert-bird&id=I63884
2 CONT
2 CONT This link shows his mother as Moira Leitch in the text but then states Elizabeth Mure is his mother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SP states his mother is Moira Leitch as listed below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The sudden rise in status of the Leitch family in Scotland, from this point in history (c. 1340), is clear evidence of the fact that Moira was the mother of John the "Black Steward".
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robertus dei gratia,* &c. sciatis nos dedisse, &c. dilecto fratri nostro, Johanni senescallo de Bute, officium vicecomitatus de Bute, Arran, &c. datum 11mo Novembris, anno 1400."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stewart was born between 1345 and 1390. He was the son of Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland and Moira Leitch.2  He married, firstly, Elizabeth Graham, daughter of Sir William Graham, in 1407/8.1 He married, secondly, Je
2 CONC an Simpill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 1445 and July 1449.2,3, Sherrif of Bute, Keeper of Rothesay Castle, and Baron of Ardmaleish and Grenan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stewart also went by the nick-name of 'The Black Stewart'. Circa 1385 he had the islands of Arane (Arran), Bute and Cambrae erected into a county for him by his father and was constituted Hereditary Sheriff of the new ent
2 CONC ity.  He was invested as a Knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Dundonald, Ayrshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/216/mode/2up The Scots peerage] founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility 
2 CONC of that kingdom. Published 1904 by D. Douglas in Edinburgh .  Vol Vl.  Page 217-218:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Elizabeth Graham married Sir John Stewart of Dundonald, natural son of Robert ll, between 1412 and 1414"
2 CONT
