1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 3 1/2 brothers called John:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart, Lord of Burley (d. 1425)
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart of Cardney
2 CONT * Sir John Stewart ‘the Black’, sheriff of Bute (d. 1445/1449)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://www.thepeerage.com/p10210.htm#i102097
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00276530&tree=LEO Geanologics.org]
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Steuart was an illegitimate son of Robert II, King of Scots, by Mariota Cardney, daughter of John Cardney and sister of Robert Cardney, Bishop of Dunkeld 1396-1436. In 1394 John was mentioned as being educated at the Univers
2 CONC ity of Paris. On 12 February 1399 he received the lands of Cardney from his half-brother Robert III, king of Scots. John was knighted on 21 May 1424. He died in 1466.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT * Walter Steuart, of Cluny and Cardney
2 CONT * Margaret Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From  [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I2809&tree=CC MacFarlane Families and Connected Clans Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir John Steuart, Kt., 21 May, 1424, at Scone, 7th natural son of King Robert II (1371 to 1390) by Mariota, dau. of de Cardney of that Ilk, and sister of Robert de Cardney, Bishop of Dunkeld."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Stewart, got charter of Cardneys 1399, and of Airntully 1383. He was alive 1425. He married Jean, daughter of Sir John Drummond of Stobhall and sister of Queen Annabella. He left issue a son, Walter Stewart of Cardneys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: The Landed Gentry of Great Britain, under "Steuart-Menzies of Culdares"
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Children_of_Robert_II_of_Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate children of Robert II and Mariota de Cardney
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons 	
2 CONT #  Alexander Stewart of Innerlunan 
2 CONT #  James Stewart of Abernethy & Kinfauna
2 CONT #  Sir John Stewart of Cardney  
2 CONT #  Walter Stewart 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Modern Athens! Displayed in a Series of Views: Or Edinburgh in the Nineteenth Century:: Exhibiting the Whole of the New Buildings, Modern Improvements, Antiquities, and Picturesque Scenery, of the Scottish Metropolis and Its
2 CONC  Environs," John Britton, Thomas Hosmer Shepherd Jones & Company, 1829 - Architecture.  Page 104 "JOHN STEUART, ESQ." [https://books.google.com/books?id=-TEOAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PT104&ots=qw5AVkysC-&dq=de%20Cardney%20of%20that%20Ilk&pg=PT
2 CONC 104#v=onepage&q=de%20Cardney%20of%20that%20Ilk&f=false link]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"The progenitor of the present family, possessing the barony of Dalguise, was Sir John Steuart, of Cardney, Lord of Dowallie, son of King Robert II., by Mariotta, daughter of John de Cardennie, or Cardney, of Ilk, in Perthshire. 
2 CONC  He married Jane, daughter of Sir John Drummond, of Stobhall, and sister of Annabella, queen of Robert III. His first charters appear to be dated in the year 1382, when he inherited, by his mother, the barony of Cardney, and other
2 CONC  lands."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT *[https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=RA2-PA563&dq=de%20cardeny%20genealogy&pg=RA2-PA563#v=onepage&q=de%20cardeny%20genealogy&f=false link] to Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval Families, 2nd Edi
2 CONC tion ....  " ... Marion de Cardney, daughter of John de Cardney, of Cardney and Foss, and sister of Robert de Cardney, Bishop of Dunkeld ..."
2 CONT *  [https://books.google.com/books?id=Ke4_AQAAMAAJ&lpg=PR169&ots=k6PritPWlP&dq=Sir%20John%20Stewart%20of%20Cardney&pg=PR169#v=onepage&q&f=false link] to Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum: The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, Volume 4 By
2 CONC  Scotland. Court of Exchequer. Appendix to Preface.
2 CONT ===Links
