2 CONT
2 CONT In 1425 when King James I (1406-1437) of Scots met hereof Scots met hat Dundonald Castle at Dundonald in Ayshire with John the 'Red' Stewart (an illegitimate son of Robert II to an unknown mistress), to mass a royal army and do ba
2 CONC ttle the Lennox rebels, led by James the 'Fat' Steward, a son of Murdoch Stewart, Duke of Albany who had been arrested along with the Earl of Lennox for treason by the King. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John the 'Red' was defeated and killed at Dumbarton castle by James the 'Fat'.
2 CONT
