1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ADAM MURE OF ROWALLAN (aka ADE MORE DE ROWALLANE militi)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan is the son of Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan. The Historie refers to him as: "Sr Adame Sone & successor to Sr Adam." [https://archive.org/stream/historieanddesc00muirgoog#page/n64/mode/1up Historie, p. 58]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan. According to Sir William Mure of Rowallan: "This Sr Adame deceased 1399." [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/68/mode/1up Hi
2 CONC storie, p. 68] However, he was still alive on  2 November 1404. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f27&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Rowallan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y NRS: GD2
2 CONC 5/1/27] Records show that he was succeeded by Robert Mure of Rowallan, in or before 1409, and it seems reasonable to suppose that he probably died before this date. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.as
2 CONC px?reference=GD8%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+muir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y NRS: GD8/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 November 1391: Charter by which Robert III, King of Scots, confirms possession of Rowallan to Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan: "Ade More de Rowalane, militi." [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846;view=1up;seq
2 CONC =359 Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 835 on pp. 330-1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 November 1391: Charter by Robert III in favour of Fergus de Foulertoun of Arane [Arran] of the lands of Erqwhonyne extending to a 2 merk land, lordship of Aranne and sheriffdom of Bute, to be held in blench ferm. Dated at Ar
2 CONC nele. Witnesses: Robert and Alexander, Earls of Fyf [Fife] and Buchan, the king's brothers, Thomas de Erskyne, [Erskine] R[obert] de Danyelstoun, Gilbert Kenedy, William de Conynghame, [Cunningham] the son, Adam Mure of Rowalayne 
2 CONC [Rowallan] and [blank, document torn] Foulerton, knights, John de Monte Gomeri, [Montgomery] John de Schaw [Shaw] and Reginald de Crau[furd]. [Seal wanting] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD1%2f19%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Rowallan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fullarton of Kilmichael, Arran, reference GD1/19/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1392: Carta Ade More de terris de Polmekle Gray Dumbwe, etc. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846;view=1up;seq=657 Appendix 2, Index A, charter number 1669]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1392: To Adam More of Rowallan and . . . . . Danielstoun his spouse, of the lands of Polmekill, Grey, Dumblay, Clunche, Clony Herber, Darlache, Balgram in the barony of Cunningham, vicecomitatu [de] Air, the lands of
2 CONC  Lyntslare, by resignation of Janet Danielstoun. Air. Lanark. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=njp.32101038096846;view=1up;seq=657 Appendix 2, Index B, charter number (5)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1393: Charter by which James II, King of Scots, confirms to Ade de Mure de Rowallane, and Jonete de Danyelstoune his wife, possession of the lands of Polnekel,  Grey, Drumbuy, Cliniche, Darclath and Bagraw in Cunning
2 CONC ham division of Ayrshire, and the lands of Lenflare in the sheriffdom of Lanark. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/58/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 253 on p. 
2 CONC 58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 November 1404: Charter by King Robert III. to Sir Gilbert Kennedy, Knight, and Agnes his wife in liferent, and after their demise James Kennedy son of the said Sir Gilbert and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Alexand
2 CONC er Kennedy, brother of the said James Kennedy, and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Hugh Kennedy, brother of the said James Kennedy, and the heirs male of his body, whom failling John Kennedy, brother of the said James Ke
2 CONC nnedy, and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Thomas Kennedy, brother of the said James Kennedy, and the heirs male of his body, whom failling David Kennedy also brother of the said James Kennedy and the heirs male of his b
2 CONC ody, whom all failling the said Sir Gilbert Kennedy his nearest heirs male whatsoever, of the lands of Cassillis and Gilletry and two Kilmories, lying in the Earldom of Carrick; proceeding on the resignation of the said Sir Gilber
2 CONC t Kennedy; To be holden of the King and his successors for services used and wont. Witnesses - Gilbert Bishop of Aberdeen Chancellor of Scotland, Sir Adam Mure of Rowallan, Sir Allan de Cathcart and Sir William Cunningham, Knights
2 CONC , James of Dalrymple and William Joyse, Chaplain. Dated at Dundonald. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f27&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Rowallan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/27] [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/87/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 
2 CONC 1424-1513, charter number 378 on p. 87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 July 1406: Charter in favour of Johanni de Crawfurde.The charter was witnessed by Adam Mure, militibus, and others. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/5/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A
2 CONC .D. 1424-1513, charter number 27 on pp. 5-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1409: Remission by Robert, Duke of Albany, Earl of Fife and Governor of Scotland, to Thomas Boyd of Kilmarnock, Robert Muir of Rowallan, John Keir, William of Nairn, Thomas Pontfray, James of Nesbit, Reginald Muir, Robert Muir,
2 CONC  Robert Boyd of Flatt, Thomas Boyd of Blair, John Lowriestoun, John Donaldson, Gilbert of Kelso, Thomas Ludy, Thomas Wilson, John Lowries, Allan Lowries, his brother and John Muir of Caldwell, for the slaughter of Mauris Neilson o
2 CONC f Dalrymple, Robert Black of Dalrymple and Donald Young at Dalmellington, for the burning of their houses and raiding of their goods and of the Castle, and Alexander Conynghame and the Lairds of Badlane and of Drumcross. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+muir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/1]'''
2 CONT
