2 CONT == [http://www.chuckspeed.com/balquhidder/history/Blackhall.htm Stewart History] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHN Stewart of Ardgowan and Blackhall. His father gave him charters for land at Auchingoun in 1390, Blackhall in 1395 and Ardgowan in 1403, all in Renfrewshire.  He was ancestor of the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaw-Stewar
2 CONC t_baronets SHAW-STEWART family, Baronetcy] created 27 Mar 1667[1262].  m ---.  The name of John’s wife is not known.  [http://www.chuckspeed.com/balquhidder/history/Blackhall.htm The Blackhall Connection]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc389122947 Stewart History] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ROBERT III (John), King of Scots, born circa 1337, died 4 April 1406 in Rothesay Castle on the Isle of Bute.  A papal dispensation of 13 March 1365/66 allowed him to marry Annabella Drummond, by whom he had three sons and four 
2 CONC daughters.  However, before his marriage he had two illegitimate sons by an unknown mistress (traditionally said to have been a daughter of Sir Archibald Campbell of Lochow, but that is problematic).  One of those illegitimate son
2 CONC s was: Sir John Stewart of Auchingoun, Blackhall, and Ardgowan, born perhaps as early as 1355, died circa 1412.  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc389122947 Medieval Lands]'''
