2 CONT [ '''Find A Grave Memorial# 8607676]'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabella Drummond'''
2 CONT * '''Birth:''' 	1350
2 CONT * '''Death:''' 	Oct., 1401
2 CONT * '''Burial:'''  Dunfermline Abbey, Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland
2 CONT * Scottish Monarch, queen consort of Robert III, King of Scots. 
2 CONT * The daughter of Sir John Drummond of Stobhall and Mary Montfichet, 
2 CONT * she married Prince John Stuart in 1367. 
2 CONT * They were crowned (John as Robert III) at Scone on August 14, 1390. The marriage produced 8 children. Annabella is known to have been very well-educated for her time. 
2 CONT * A letter survives which she wrote in 1394, in French, to King Richard II of England, informing him of the birth of her son, the future James I. 
2 CONT * She died at Scone at the age of approximately 51. (bio by: Kristen Conrad) 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family links:''' 
2 CONT * '''Spouse:'''   Robert Stewart, King of Scots (1337 - 1406)* 
2 CONT * '''Children:'''
2 CONT **  Margaret Stewart Douglas*
2 CONT ** Mary Stuart Edmonstone (1380 - 1458)*
2 CONT **James King of Scots (1394 - 1437)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  **************************
2 CONT
2 CONT Scottish Monarch, queen consort of Robert III, King of Scots. The daughter of Sir John Drummond of Stobhall and Mary Montfichet, she married Prince John Stuart in 1367. They were crowned (John as Robert III) at Scone on August 14,
2 CONC  1390. The marriage produced 8 children. Annabella is known to have been very well-educated for her time. A letter survives which she wrote in 1394, in French, to King Richard II of England, informing him of the birth of her son, 
2 CONC the future James I. She died at Scone at the age of approximately 51
