1 OCCU Princess of Scotland, Datter af Robert III Steward. Konge i Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} aka: ''Princess Margaret, Duchess of Touraine''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Douglas,_4th_Earl_of_Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1390 he married Lady Margaret (d.1451), eldest daughter of John Stewart, Earl of Carrick, who later became King Robert III
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.douglashistory.co.uk/history/monarchs/kingrobert3rd.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (Princess) Stewart b: ABT. 1370 = Archibald Tyneman 4th Earl of Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82433691/margaret-douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ""Margaret Stewart, Lady of Galloway''' was born after 1366 and before about 1375.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eldest daughter of King Robert the Third, and sister to King James the First.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland and Annabel Drummond. She married Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas, son of Archibald Douglas, 3rd Earl of Douglas and Joan Moray, before 1390.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died between 26 January 1450 and September 1456 at Thrieve Castle, Galloway, Scotland.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried at Collegiate Church of Lincluden, Dumfries, Dumfries-shire, Scotland.2
2 CONT
2 CONT She was styled as Lady of Galloway.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Stewart, Lady of Galloway and Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT # 1.Lady Elizabeth Douglas+3 b. bt 1385 - 1401, d. c 1451
2 CONT # 2.William Douglas2 b. bt 1385 - 1401
2 CONT # 3.James Douglas2 b. bt 1385 - 1401, d. 1424
2 CONT # 4.Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas+2 b. 1390, d. 26 Jun 1439
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 227. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT * 2.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 228.
2 CONT * 3.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family, page 219.
2 CONT
