2 CONT *Archibald [Douglas], 3rd Earl of Douglas
2 CONT *illegitimate son of Sir James Douglas "the Good", Lord of Douglas
2 CONT *born   c. 1325
2 CONT *mar.   after 23 Jul 1362 Lady Joan Moray (widow of Sir Thomas Moray, Lord of Bothwell; d. bef. Aug 1409), only child and hrss. of Maurice [Moray], 1st Earl of Strathearn, by his wife Joan Campbell, widow of Malise, 7th Earl of St
2 CONC rathearn, and of John [Campbell], 1st Earl of Atholl, and dau. of Sir John Menteith of Rusky
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **          1. Sir Archibald Douglas, later 4th Earl of Douglas later 1st Duke of Touraine
2 CONT **          2. Sir James Douglas, later 1st Earl of Avondale later 7th Earl of Douglas
2 CONT **'''          1. Lady Marjorie Douglas (d. bef. 11 May 1421), mar. (1) Feb 1399/1400 David, Prince of Scotland and Duke of Rothesay (b. 24 Oct 1378; dvp. and sp. 26 Mar 1402), 1st son and heir ap. of Robert III, King of Scotland,
2 CONC  by his wife Annabella Drummond, dau. of Sir John Drummond of Stobhall, and (2) 1403 Sir Walter Haliburton of Dirleton, Treasurer of Scotland
