2 CONT
2 CONT In 1395, David married Elizabeth Dunbar, the daughter of George Dunbar, Earl of March, but the Papal dispensation required because they were close relatives was never obtained, and in 1397 the couple separated.
2 CONT
2 CONT David later married (Marjorie) Mary Douglas, daughter of Archibald Douglas, 3rd Earl of Douglas, to form an alliance with the Douglases, which gravely offended George Dunbar. Dunbar accordingly switched his allegiance to Henry IV 
2 CONC of England, who then invaded Scotland, briefly capturing Edinburgh before returning to England.
2 CONT
