1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===PRINCESS MARY STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Princess Mary Stewart married Sir James Kennedy of Dunure. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f28&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1400&dt=1500&di=y NR
2 CONC S: GD25/1/28]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 January 1405: Charter by King Robert III. to James Kennedy and Mary Stewart his wife (daughter of the King) in liferent, and the heirs male procreate between them, whom failling Alexander, Hugh, John, Thomas and David Kenned
2 CONC ies, brothers of the said James Kennedy, and the heirs male of their bodies respectively, whom failling the nearest heirs whatsoever of Sir Gilbert Kennedy, Knight, of the Barony of Dalrymple lying in Kyle-regis; proceeding on the
2 CONC  resignation of the said Sir Gilbert Kennedy; To be holden of the King and his successors for services used and wont. Witnesses - Gilbert Bishop of Aberdeen Chancellor of Scotland, Sir John Montgomery of Ardrossan Knight, John Ste
2 CONC wart brother natural of the King, Hector Macgillane, John Kennedy of Lenzie [Lenzhe], Fergus Kennedy his son, Mr. Malcolm Macdowal [Macdoul] Dean of Kintyre, John Dean of Carrick, William [Joyse] chaplain, John of Dalrympil and Jo
2 CONC hn de Craufurd Chaplain to the King. Dated at Dundonald. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f28&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1400&dt=1500&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/28]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===NOTES===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc253996205
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady MARY Stewart''' (-after 1458, bur Strathblane).  
2 CONT * '''m firstly''' (contract 24 May 1397) GEORGE Douglas 1st Earl of Angus, 
2 CONT ** illegitimate son of WILLIAM Douglas 1st Earl of Douglas & his mistress Margaret Ctss of Angus ([1378 or before]-1402).  
2 CONT * '''m secondly''' (1404) Sir JAMES Kennedy of Dunure (-killed in battle before 8 Sep 1408).  
2 CONT * '''Betrothed''' (Papal dispensation Jul 1409) as his second wife, Sir WILLIAM Cunningham (-[7 Aug 1413/Dec 1415]).  
2 CONT ** There is no clear evidence that this marriage took place[1134]. 
2 CONT * '''m thirdly''' (13 Nov 1413) as his second wife, Sir WILLIAM Graham of Kincardine, 
2 CONT ** son of Sir PATRICK Graham & his first wife Maud --- (-1424).  
2 CONT ** He may have been created Lord Graham in [1419][1135].  
2 CONT * '''m fourthly''' (1425) Sir WILLIAM Edmonton of Duntreath (-1462, bur Strathblane).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1390 Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas, married Lady Margaret (d.1451), eldest daughter of John Stewart, Earl of Carrick, who later became King Robert III. Of their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas, and Wigton, &c., (1390–1439), who succeeded to the earldom.
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Elizabeth (d. c. 1451), who married first John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Buchan, secondly Thomas Mar, son of Alexander Stewart, Earl of Mar, and thirdly William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney (d. 1480).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * William Douglas (b. before 1401)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James Douglas (d. 17 August 1424)
2 CONT
2 CONT weblinks:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Douglas,_4th_Earl_of_Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT grand-daughter of King Robert III of scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Given lands of Duntreath castle as wedding gift in 1435
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Stewart was the daughter of Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland and Annabel Drummond.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married by contract, firstly, George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus, son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Countess of Angus, on 24 May 1397.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger, son of Sir Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, circa 1404.1 She and Sir William Cunningham were engaged in July 1409.1 S
2 CONT
2 CONT he married, thirdly, Sir William Graham on 13 November 1413.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, fourthly, Sir William Edmondstone of Culloden, son of Sir Archibald Edmonstone, in 1425.3 She died circa 1458.3 She was buried at Strathbane Church, Scotland.3
2 CONT
2 CONT      Lady Mary Stewart gained the title of Princess Mary of Scotland.4 As a result of her marriage, Lady Mary Stewart was styled as Countess of Angus after 24 May 1397. From after 24 May 1397, her married name became Douglas. From
2 CONC  circa 1404, her married name became Kennedy. From 13 November 1413, her married name became Graham. From 1425, her married name became Edmonstone.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=535803-16-5144&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-3110377944c892dbc420ef25e9aa9035&mrid=f5ae143337ba84ce6ba2c5a47e274618 MyHeri
2 CONC tage Family Trees] via son [http://www.geni.com/profile-34677600317 William Edmonston] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 3 2015, 5:28:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Stuart Edmonstone
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1380 Death: 	1458
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess of Scotland. Mary Stuart/Stewart was born in Of, Dunfermline, Fifeshire, Scotland, the daughter of King Robert III of Scotland and Annabella Drummond. She married 1st Sir George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus the son of Sir W
2 CONC illiam Douglas Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart Countess of Angus, at Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, on May 24, 1397 and had issue. She married 2nd Sir James Kennedy of Dunure in 1404. She married 3rd William, 1st Lord Graha
2 CONC m in 1413 and had issue. She married 4th in 1425 Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath and had issue.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
