1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''Medlands: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#RobertIIIdied1406B Scotland, Kings]:'''
2 CONT >Lady EGIDIA Stewart (-1417 or after). 
2 CONT >Accounts dated 1405 record payments “''per regem...de custuma...lane de crescentia terre Galwidie, vallium de Nith, Anandie, vel de Douglasdale''” to “''Egidie filie sue...per literas regis...et comitisse de Douglas de recepto''”
2 CONC  and dated 1406 from wool in the same lands “''per quondam regem Egidie filie sue''”[1493].  
2 CONT >Accounts dated 1409 and 1410 record payments “''pro apparamento suo''” to “''domine Egidie, filie domini quondam regis ultimo defuncti, ex concessione domini ducis, avunculi sui''”[1494].  
2 CONT >Accounts dated ''between 1410 and 1417'' record other payments to “lady Egidia Stewart by receipt of Earl of Athole”[1495]. Her uncle’s involvement suggests that Egidia was in some way incapacitated.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10533.htm#i105323 The Peerage] Egidia Stewart was the daughter of Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland and Annabel Drummond. She died, young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Egidia Stewart was also known as Jill.  Citations 1. [ S11 ] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 229. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
