2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''John''''', known as "the good John of Isla," owing to his benefactions to the Church. He married first Amy, daughter of Roderick, son of Allan MacRuari, his third cousin, for which union they are said to have obtained a papal
2 CONC  dispensation, and had:
2 CONT 1. ''John'', whose son Angus is mentioned as one of the hostages given to King David in pledge of the fidelity of the Lord of the Isles. John predeceased his father, and his son Angus does not appear to have left issue.
2 CONT 2. ''Reginald'' or Ranald, ancestor of the Clanranald.
2 CONT 3.'' Godfrey'', of whom the Siol Ghorraidh. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''John of Isla''''' is said to have repudiated Amy Macruari, his first wife, in favour of the Princess Margaret of Scotland, daughter of Robert II., whom he married as his second wife. By the Princess Margaret he had:
2 CONT 4. ''Donald'', his successor.
2 CONT 5.''''' John Mor Tanistear,''''' founder of the family of Dunnyveg.
2 CONT 6. ''Angus'', who left no issue.
2 CONT 7. ''Alexander,'' known as Alastair Carrach. of whom the family of Keppoch.
2 CONT 8.'' Hugh'', who got a Charter of the Thanage of Glentilt, and whose descendants, according to Skene, became Mclntoshes.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''John''''' had also a natural son, ''Donald'', who is mentioned as one of the hostages placed in the King's hands as pledge for his fidelity. He had a daughter ''Mary'', who married Lachlan Lubanach Maclean of Duart, and anoth
2 CONC er daughter ''Margaret'', who married Angus Dubh - Mackay of Strathnaver. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''John's''''' family by the first wife were cut off' from the succession to the lordship of the Isles.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 181.'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''THE MACDONALDS OF DUNNYVEG AND THE GLENS.'''
2 CONT This family, than which there was none more powerful or distinguished among the cadets of the Isles, derives its descent from ''John Mor Tanister'', second son of '''''John, Lord of the Isles''''', by his second wife, ''Princess M
2 CONC argaret Stewart'', daughter of King Robert II.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 374.'''''
