2 CONT From http://www.undiscoveredscotland.co.uk/usbiography/ghi/donaldofislay.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald inherited his father's titles in 1387 and spent the early years of his tenure suppressing a revolt by his younger brother John Mór who, with the support of the Macleans, was trying to expand on his small inheritance of land
2 CONC s. By 1395 Donald had driven John Mór into exile in Ireland and beaten off the challenge of the Macleans. 
2 CONT
