2 CONC 34155?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1603735077965&through=6000000002140596727 WILLIAM Earl of Ross], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-4th-Earl-of-Ross/6000000009677455510?through=6000000002140596727 HUGH Earl of Ross] & his fir
2 CONC st wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Matilda-Bruce/6000000002140596727 Matilda Bruce] (-Delny 9 Feb 1372).  http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#AngusIslesdied1330B From Wiki
2 CONT
2 CONT Domhnall spent some of his first years as Lord of the Isles suppressing a revolt by his brother John Mór. John was Domhnall's younger brother, and resented his meagre inheritance. Although he was recognized as heir-apparent (tànai
2 CONC ste), he only received patches of land in Kintyre and Islay. The rebellion started in 1387 and went on into the 1390s, and John obtained the support of the MacLean kindred. However, John and the MacLeans were eventually forced to 
2 CONC submit to Domhnall, and by 1395 John Mór had been forced into Ireland. There he entered the service of King Richard II of England and later established a MacDonald lordship in Antrim.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Assissinated in 1427
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://clandonaldusa.org/index.php/dna-after-somerled
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT This family, than which there was none more powerful or distinguished among the cadets of the Isles, derives its descent from '''''John Mor Tanister,''''' second son of ''John, Lord of the Isles,'' by his second wife, Princess Mar
2 CONC garet Stewart, daughter of King Robert II.
2 CONT '''''John Mor''''' married Margery Bisset, daughter of Sir Hugh Bisset, and heiress in her own right of the Seven Glens of Antrim. Besides their possessions in Isla and Kintyre, the family of Dunnyveg had thus extensive Irish terr
2 CONC itories, and played an important part in the stirring drama of Irish warfare.
2 CONT By his wife, Margery Bisset, John Mor had:
2 CONT 1''.''' Donald Balloch''''', his successor.
2 CONT 2. ''Ranald Bane'', from whom the family of Largie.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''John Mor''''' was assassinated in 1427.
2 CONT '''''
2 CONT Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 374.'''''
2 CONT ----
