2 CONT
2 CONT i. Neil Vass Mackay, by the first wife, and of whom an account follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert is mistaken in saying that the first wife of Angus Du was a daughter of '''Donald, Lord of the Isles. She was not his daughter, but his sister, Elizabeth''', as is clearly stated in the charter of 1415. As this marriage
2 CONC  did not take place till after the battle at Dingwall in 1411, and '''as John, Lord of the Isles (father of Elizabeth by his wife a daughter of King Robert II.),''' died in 1380, according to the Book of Clanranald, the lady must 
2 CONC have been somewhat advanced in years at the time of her marriage and incapable of bearing many children. It is more than probable that '''Neil Vass was the only child of the marriage, and that Lady Elizabeth''' died soon after the
2 CONC  charter of 1415 was granted pg. 61
