1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alistair_Carragh_Macdonald '''Wikipedia''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alastair Carragh MacDonald''' (Alexander the Strong) (d. c.1440) was a son of John of Islay, Lord of the Isles and Margaret Stewart, daughter of King Robert II of Scotland and Elizabeth Mure.[1] He is the eponymous ancestor of 
2 CONC Clan MacDonald of Keppoch.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought alongside his brother, Donald of the Isles, at the Battle of Harlaw in 1411, supporting Donald's claim to the Earldom of Ross. For his involvement in the 1431 insurrection of Donald Balloch and the Battle of Inverlochy, 
2 CONC Alistair had a large portion of his lands confiscated, with those lands transferred to the Malcolm Beg Mackintosh, Chief of Clan MacKintosh.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family=
2 CONT
2 CONT John, Lord of the Isles, married, secondly, Margaret, daughter of King Robert n.1 and had by her :—
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. '''Alexander''', known as ''Alastair Carrach'', from whom the
2 CONT Macdonalds of Keppoch. There were twenty succes- sive heads of this well-known family. Ohichester, the last of the line, died in 1848.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Mary, daughter of Malcolm, Earl of Lennox, they had:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Angus, d. c.1484, married a daughter of MacPhee of Glenpean.
2 CONT *and Alexander MacAlastair aka Lord Alexander MacAlistair b. 1420
2 CONT
