1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mairead inghean Eachann''' (English: ''Mariota, daughter of Eachann'') was the spouse of Alexander Stewart, 1st Earl of Buchan (also known as the "Wolf of Badenoch") and mother of Alexander Stewart, Earl of Mar.
2 CONC  She is mentioned in the Moray Registrum, which gives her name in Latin and informs us that she came from the lands within the sphere of the bishopric of Ross. She has been described as the Wolf's wife "by Gaelic secular marriage"
2 CONC , referring to the fact that the marriage was irregular in church custom and that the Wolf was already married to Euphemia I, Countess of Ross. In 1389, Countess Euphemia, complained to Pope Clement V that her marriage to Buchan w
2 CONC as meaningless as the Wolf was cohabiting with Mairead, and the pope subsequently annulled the marriage in late 1392. The Wolf continued his conhabitation with Mairead through the 1390s. The Wolf had seven "bastard" children, all 
2 CONC perhaps the children of Mairead. These were the aforementioned Alexander, Sir Andrew of Sandhauch, Donnchadh, James, Walter, Robert, and Margaret (who married the earl of Sutherland).
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mairead_inghean_Eachann Mairead inghean Eachann] 
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Boardman, Stephen, The Early Stewart Kings: Robert II and Robert III, 1371-1406, (Edinburgh, 1996)
2 CONT * Boardman, Steve, "Lordship in the North-East: The Badenoch Stewarts I: Alexander Stewart, Earl of Buchan, Lord of Badenoch", in Northern Scotland, vol. 16, 1996, pp. 1–29
2 CONT * Brown, Michael, "Regional Lordship in the North-East: The Badenoch Stewarts II: Alexander Stewart, Earl of Buchan, Lord of Badenoch", in Northern Scotland, vol. 16, 1996, pp. 31–53
2 CONT * Paul, James Balfour, The Scots Peerage, Vol. II, (Edinburgh, 1905)
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/registrumepisc5800morauoft/registrumepisc5800morauoft_djvu.txt page 353] of "The Moray Registrum" (Registrum Episcopatus Moraviensis; E Pluribus Codicibus Consarcinatum Circa A.D. Mcccc., Cum Continua
2 CONC tione Diplomatum Recentiorum Usque Ad A.D. Mdcxxiii by Moray, Scot. (Diocese); Innes, Cosmo Nelson, 1798-1874
2 CONT **"271. Sententia de Eufamia comitifla de Ros reftituenda marito, et''' Mariota filia Athyn''' amovenda. 1389. /. 101." 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
