2 CONT         Place: Inchetuthyll, Perthshire, Scotland[citation needed] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Thomas de la Haye, 7th of Erroll was the son of Sir David de la Haye, 6th of Erroll and unknown daughter Keith.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Stewart, daughter of Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland and Elizabeth Mure of Rowallan, circa 7 November 1372.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1354 he was a hostage in England for King David II's ransom.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Constable of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in July 1406.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Thomas de la Haye, 7th of Erroll and Elizabeth Stewart
