2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de la Haye, 1st Lord Hay [1]
2 CONT *M, #108041, 
2 CONT *d. 1437
2 CONT *Last Edited=31 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de la Haye, 1st Lord Hay was the son of Sir Thomas de la Haye, 7th of Erroll and Elizabeth Stewart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Gray, daughter of Sir Patrick Gray.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1437.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Commissioner to treat for the ransom of King James I in 1423.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Joint Lord Warden of the Marches in 1430.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Lord Hay [Scotland] before March 1429/30, following an Act of 1428 drawing a distinction between Lords of Parliament and the ordinary lairds in the Scots baronage.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir William de la Haye, 1st Lord Hay and Margaret Gray
2 CONT *1. Gilbert of the Haye+[2] d. 7 Sep 1436
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
