1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====The Peerage: [https://thepeerage.com/p991.htm#i9901 Alice de la Haye]
2 CONT Alice de la Haye is the daughter of Sir Thomas de la Haye, 7th of Erroll and Elizabeth Stewart.2 She married Sir William Hay of Lochorwart and Yester, son of Sir Thomas Haya of Lochorwart and Jean Gifford.1
2 CONT Children of Alice de la Haye and Sir William Hay of Lochorwart and Yester:
2 CONT # Janet Hay+
2 CONT # Margaret Hay+1 d. a 22 Apr 1484
2 CONT # Sir David Hay of Lochorwart and Yester+1 d. b 2 Sep 1478
2 CONT # Alice Hay+3
2 CONT # Sir Thomas Hay of Lochorwart and Yester3 d. Feb 1433/34
2 CONT # Edmund Hay of Tala3
2 CONT # Elizabeth Hay3
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] Peter W. Hammond, ed., ''The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times'', Vol. 14: "Addenda & Corrigenda" (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), p. 26.
2 CONT [2] Alison Weir, ''Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy'' (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), p. 222.
2 CONT [3] BP2003 volume 3, page 3960. ($ubscription)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Alicia Hay (daughter of Thomas Hay and Elizabeth Stewart) was born 1382 in ,,Perth, Scotland, and died 1451 in ,,,Scotland. She married William Hay on 1399 in Yester, Haddington, East Mid Loth, Scotland, son of Thomas Haya and Joh
2 CONC anna Gifford.
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Scots Peerage contradicts itself on this point. In Volume IV page 445 under "Home, Earl of Home" it says: "Sir Alexander married Jean or Janet Hay, daughter of Sir William Hay of Lochorwarth, by Joanna, daughter and heiress 
2 CONC of Hugh Gifford of Yester." [5, 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT * * Notes (Research):"It is doubtful whether this lady was a Hay at all. Her seal appended to her charter of mortification 23 February 1447-8 to the altar of the B.V.M. in the kirk of Bothans bears the arms of Hay of Yester impali
2 CONC ng three stars or cinquefoils." [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
2 CONT * 8. [S640] Scots Peerage, Vol. 9, Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King Of Arms (editor), (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1914), archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun09pauluoft., page 164 (Reliability: 4).
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://palmspringsbum.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I101653&tree=Legends
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/b/o/n/Lindon-N-Bontz/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0289.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice BORTHWICK [Parents] 1, 2, 3, 4 was born 1370 in Errol, Perth, Scotland. She died after 23 Feb 1448. Alice married Sir William HAY Knight on 1389 in Yester, East Lothian, Scotland.
