1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK AND EDNAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, writing in his 1851 account of the family, Sir John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, was the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that
2 CONC -Ilk-and-Boyne/6000000008010929285?through=6000000020816007489 The name of his mother is not known. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/24/mode/1up?view=theater Duntreath: 24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Edmonstone pf that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, probably died before 18 March 1414, the date upon which Eufemia, Countess Palatine of Stratherne, confirmed for her cousin, David Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, the gr
2 CONC ants of the land of Tullyallan formerly made to his father. [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa01bann/page/n69/mode/1up Inchaffrey Registrum: Appendix 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam married https://www.geni.com/people/Isabella-Stewart/6000000002174773680?through=6000000020816007489 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%
2 CONC 2f7%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmundiston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y NRS: GD237/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Edmonstone-of-Edmonstone-Kt/6000000008248653864?through=6000000020816007489
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone/6000000176846911888?through=6000000020816007489
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December 1389: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by Robert II, King of Scots, to said John [JOHN EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK] and Isabel [ISABEL STEWART, COUNTESS OF DOUGLAS] of said lands of Ednahame. Witnesses to charter:
2 CONC  Walter, archbishop of St Andrews, Matthew, bishop of Glasgow, John, earl of Carrick, the king's eldest son, steward of Scotland, Robert, earl of Fife and of Menteith, king's son, Archibald, earl of Douglas, James Douglas of Dalke
2 CONC ith, kt., the king's brother [in law], Thomas Erskyn, kt., and John Gray, clerk of rolls and register and keeper of the great seal. Notary: Nicholas of Bury, clerk, Glasgow diocese. Witnesses to sasine: Patrick, abbot of Kelso, Wi
2 CONC lliam and Richard, his co-monks, William Mautaland and William Del, vicars, and John Fordoun, and many other holders of husbandlands and tenants of town of Edynhame. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.a
2 CONC spx?reference=GD237%2f7%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmundiston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Don of Newton and Edmondstone, reference GD237/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 February 1389-90: Instrument reciting appointment under testimony of the great seal of Robert II, King of Scots, of William Mautaland, Thomas Turnbull and Adam Franche sheriffs specially assigned in cause to give sasine to J
2 CONC OHN EDMONDISTONE, kt., and ISABEL [STEWART], COUNTESS OF DOUGLAS, the king's daughter, [widow of James, 2nd earl of Douglas, and wife of said John,] in lands of Ednaham in sheriffdom of Roxburgh, formerly belonging to James, earl 
2 CONC of Douglas, and said Isabel, his spouse, and to appoint to her a reasonable terce of all lands and rents belonging to her by decease of said James, earl of Douglas; [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.as
2 CONC px?reference=GD237%2f7%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmundiston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Don of Newton and Edmondstone, reference GD237/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 July 1403: Charter by Archibald, Earl of Douglas, to SIR JOHN OF EDMONDSTOUN OF THAT ILK, knight, of lands of Tulyaloun lying in regality of Stratherne. Witnesses: John of Setoun, William of Abernethy, William of Haya, Willi
2 CONC am of Borthwyk, knights, Walter of Halyburtoun, John of Sanctoclaro, John of Lawdir, William of Crauforde, Robert of Oppryngyl, William of Cranstoun. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD
2 CONC 15%2f333&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/333]'''
