2 CONT '''2 August 1407: Tack by Archibald, Earl of Douglas, to Sir John of Edmondston of that Ilk, knight, of lands of Tulyaloun, for space of 19 years. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD15%
2 CONC 2f335&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/335]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1410: Charter by John de Crechtoun [Crichton], knt., of that ilk and Dryvisdale [Dryfesdale], to his brother Thomas de Crechtoun of Burnstoun [Burnston], of the lands of Daltonhuk [Daltonhook] and the island called Blabe
2 CONC ry Warde in the Water of Anand [Annan], in Dryvisdale; with common pasturage in the commonties of Bengal [Bengall] and Turnmure [Turnmuir] and specified multures; under penalty of £100 scots towards the fabric of St. Mungo's churc
2 CONC h, Glasgow. Witnesses: Sir William de Abernethy of Saultoun [Saltoun], SIR JOHN DE EDMONDSTOUN OF THAT ILK, Sir George de Prestoun of Gourtoun [Gorton], Sir William de Preston of Bynyn [Binning], knights, Andrew de Crechtoun, Robe
2 CONC rt de Crechtoun, Simon Derlyng [Darling], priest, and John Trypnay [Tripney] of le Wra [Wrae], notary. [Seal of granter appended in fair condition] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD78
2 CONC %2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hunter Family of Barjarg, Dumfriesshire, reference GD78/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1415: Discharge by Archibald, Earl of Douglas, to David of Edmondstoun of that Ilk, of 100 merks Scots paid for relief on the lands and lordship of Tulyaloun. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD15%2f338&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmondstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1450&di=y National Records of Scotland, Erskine family of Cardross, Perthshire, reference GD15/338]'''
