2 CONT ===Evidence from the Douglas Book===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 May 1400: Charter issued by Archibald Douglas, Earl of Douglas and Lord of Galloway. Witnessed by Sir John of Edmonstoun, lord of that ilk, and others. [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/400/mode/1up The Do
2 CONC uglas Book III: charter number 342]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 July 1401: Charter issued by Archibald Douglas, Earl of Douglas and Lord of Galloway. Witnessed by John of Edmondstone, lord of that Ilk, and others. [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/400/mode/1up The Dougl
2 CONC as Book III: charter number 344]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 May 1402: Charter by Archibald Earl of Douglas and Lord of Galloway, granting to his well-beloved and faithful Sir John of Edmondstone, knight, lord of that ilk, for faithful service, his fortalice with the pertinents, lying
2 CONC  in his lands of Tullyalone, in the sheriffdom of Perth ; to be held to the said John, his heirs and assignees, of the Earl and his heirs, in fee and heritage for ever, with all the buildings, walls, fosses, free ish and entry as 
2 CONC well by sea as by land, coney warrens, cruives, and sea- fishings, etc., for paying yearly one penny Scots at the feast of Whitsunday at the said fortalice, in name of blench farm, if asked only. At Edinburgh, at the feast of the 
2 CONC Holy Trinity (21 May) 1402. Witnesses, Sir John of Wyntone, Sir William Stewart, Sir William of Borthwyk, knights, William of Hay, John of Moray, the Earl's cousin, Mr. Alexander of Carnys, John of Saint Clair, Fergus of Halyburto
2 CONC ne, and William of Crawford. [Original charter in Cardross Charter-chest.] [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/401/mode/1up The Douglas Book III: charter number 346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1407: Charter issued by Archibald Douglas, Earl of Douglas and Lord of Galloway. Witnessed by Sir John of Edmondstoun, lord of that ilk, and others. [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/403/mode/1up 
2 CONC The Douglas Book III: charter number 351]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 March 1410: Obligation by Patrick Grame, Earl Palatine of Stratherne, bearing that, whereas he, with consent of Eufame, his spouse, had confirmed to Sir John of Edmundstoun, knight, lord of that ilk, and to his heirs, the gi
2 CONC ft and grant made to him and them by Sir Archibald Earl of Douglas, of the lands of Tulialoun and the " forslete of that ilk," he obliges him and his heirs that whenever Sir John or his heirs should procure the said Earl of Dougla
2 CONC s or his heirs to resign the lands in the hands of the Earl Palatine or his heirs, the latter shall receive the lands, and immediately infeft Sir John and his heirs in the same, with free charter and clause of warrandice, in the s
2 CONC ame form they were infeft by the Earl of Douglas, with charter of ward and relief. If before such resignation the Earl of Douglas or his heirs did not the service due and wont to the Earl Palatine or his heirs, or the heir to the 
2 CONC Earl of Douglas did not enter to the said lauds within a year after the Earl's decease, the Earl Palatine obliges himself and his heirs to receive the service from Sir John and his heirs, and allow him or them to enjoy the lands u
2 CONC ntil the Earl of Douglas would do the service ; or in the case of nonentry of the heir of the Earl of Douglas, to receive Sir John and his heirs to be full tenants of the lands to him and his heirs, within a year after the Earl of
2 CONC  Douglas's death, and let him or them enjoy the same till the heir of the Earl of Douglas entered thereto and performed the service due, which being done Sir John and his heirs should remain tenants of the Earl of Douglas and his 
2 CONC heirs as before • and binding him and his heirs during his own life and the life of Sir John, not to trouble the lands of Tulialoun, nor tenants dwelling there, but as the course of common law will; which obligation is also dated 
2 CONC at Perth, 1 April 1410. The said confirmation and obligation being read, Eufame Countess of Stratherne gave her bodily oath on the gospels to observe the same, on which Sir John of Edmundstoun craved instruments. Done in the paris
2 CONC h church of the burgh of Perth on St. Martin's altar, 3] March 1410. Witnesses, William Lord of Grahame, Sir William of Prestoun, knight, Mr. Thomas of Graham, archdeacon of Dunblane, etc., William of Kynarde, notary. [Original In
2 CONC strument at Floors.] [https://archive.org/details/douglasbookf03fras/page/405/mode/1up The Douglas Book III: charter number 358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from English Documents Relating to Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                      1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 August 1404: Commission, Robert K. of Scotland to Mathew bishop of Glasgow, James of Douglas lord of Dalketh, David Flemyng, John Steward of Innermeth, his cousins, JOHN OF EDMONDSTOUN, William of Borthwik, and Adam Forster 
2 CONC of Corstorfyne, knights, and Master John of Mertoun doctor of decrees, and Master Walter Forster his secretary, canons of Glasgow and Aberdeen, to meet the English commissioners at Haudenstank on 8th October following, and treat f
2 CONC or peace, etc. Linlithgow. By the K. in Council. [Chapter House (Scots Docs.), Box 95, No. 2, M.]  [https://archive.org/details/calendarofdocume04grea/page/138/mode/1up Calendar of Documents Relating to Scotland IV: document numbe
2 CONC r 664]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1407: The K. to his cousin the "Archbishop of Canterbury. Commands him after inspecting the safe conduct lately granted to Archibald of Douglas son and heir of the Earl of Douglas and the Earl's other hostages, on the ro
2 CONC lls, to issue general letters of same tenor in favour of said Archibald and the Earl's other hostages, viz., James of Douglas son of the Earl, William son of James of Douglas chivaler, son and heir of the ' Sire de Dalketh,' John 
2 CONC of Mongomery, ' Sire de Ardrossane chivaler/ John of Setone chivaler, son and heir of the ' Sire de Setone,' William of Douglas chivaler, ' Sire de Dunlangrig,' William Seynclare chivaler, ' Sire de Hyrdmaston,' Simon of Glendonwy
2 CONC ne chivaler, son and heir of Adam of Glendonwyne, John Heryce ' chivaler,' ' Sire de Trevereglys,' William Haye ' chivaler, Sire de Yhestre,' Harbarde of Maxvile ' chivaler,' son and heir of Robert of Maxvile chivaler, and William
2 CONC  of Abir- nethny ' chivaler. Sire de Saltone. ' Also similar conducts for John Steuart, William Grame, and JOHN OF EDMONDSTONE "chivalers" jointly and severally — all till Michaelmas following. Westminster. [Tower Miscellaneous Ro
2 CONC lls, No. 459.] [https://archive.org/details/calendarofdocume04grea/page/150/mode/1up Calendar of Documents Relating to Scotland IV: document number 736]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 April 1408: Safe conduct and protection for John of Montgomery lord of Ardrossane in Scotland, James of Douglas son of Archibald earl of Douglas, and SIR JOHN OF EDMONSTONE, knight of Scotland, with one attendant each, as ho
2 CONC stages for the return of Archibald earl of Douglas to Durham castle. [https://archive.org/details/calendarofdocume04grea/page/153/mode/1up Calendar of Documents Relating to Scotland IV: document number 752]'''
2 CONT
