2 CONT ===Research Note===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Edmonstone was most likely a comrade at arms under the leadership of  his commander James Douglas, 2nd Earl of Douglas, since they both fought together at the storied Battle of Otterburn (August 1388).  During the batt
2 CONC le which continued into the night, the Earl was killed.  Sir John was among the 300 Scots taken captive.  It was only after his release, he married James Douglas' widow, Isabel Stewart.  For details of the battle, see [https://en.
2 CONC wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Otterburn Otterburn]'''
