0 @I6000000002187899948@ INDI
1 NAME Walter /Stewart of Railston/
2 GIVN Walter
2 SURN Stewart of Railston
2 _MARNM Stewart of Railston
1 SEX M
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR WALTER STEWART OF RAILSTOUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Walter Stewart of Railston is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart-of-Railston/6000000003828038289?through=6000000002187899948 [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#Walter6Stewartdied1326B Foundation 
2 CONC for Medieval Genealogy: Scotland, Kings] Stirnet reports that his mother was https://www.geni.com/people/Alicia-Mure/6000000003828418175?through=6000000002187899948. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart01.php 
2 CONC Stirnet: Stewart 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Lands of Railston ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It should be noticed that the land called Railston is located in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire, formerly the barony of Cunningham, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f89&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=RAILSTOUN&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD150/89] and that the land called Ralston, now part of Paisley, is located in Renfrewshire, formerly the barony of Renfrew. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1115&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ralston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1501&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD26/3/1115] Sir Walter Stewart had no connection with Ralston in Renfrewshire.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 March 1392: Charter of wadset by Walter Stewart, lord of Rayliston, in favour of Patrick de Graham, lord of Kincardine, of all lands of Cultermeny and of Bodrey, for £66 13s 4d Scots money; to be held by Patrick and the male
2 CONC  heirs of Patrick and his wife, Euphemia, sister of Walter; paying the usual services and duties, until redeemed in full at the church of St John the Baptist in Perth; with clause as to redemption at the feast of Pentecost, 1392, 
2 CONC permitting Patrick to retain crops sown for next year. Dated at Perth. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f1%2f5%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Walter+Stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s
2 CONC &df=&dt=1430&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/A/1/5/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 July 1416: Resignation by Walter Stewart, lord of Railstoun, of his lands of Railstoune, in the barony of Conynghame and sheriffdom of Are, in the hands of Robert, duke of Albany, governor of Scotland. [http://catalogue.nrsco
2 CONC tland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f89&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=RAILSTOUN&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/89]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 July 1416: Procuratory of resignation by Walter Steuarte of Raylstoun, appointing John Steuarte of Dundonalde, James de Cunynghame of Grugare, John Tayte of Elynton and sir Thomas Walace, vicar of Inneroury, his procurators t
2 CONC o resign his lands of Barleth and Sesnok, in the barony of Kyle and Sheriffdom of Are, in the hands of William Walace, lord of Cragyne, the superior. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D150%2f90&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=raylstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/90]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 December 1421: Charter of confirmation by Murdach, duke of Albany, earl of Fife and of Menteth, governor of Scotland, of charter, 13 December 1421, by Alexander of Lindesai, earl of Craufurde, to David Lyndesay, his eldest s
2 CONC on, and specified heirs, of 100 merks of the great customs of burgh of Aberdeen, 40 merks of burgh fermes of said burgh, with office of sheriff thereof, annualrent of 13 merks from burgh of Banf with lands of Bauchlouch in sheriff
2 CONC dom of Banf, barony of Oures, lordship of Neudosk, in sheriffdom of Kincardyn, lordship of Glenesk, with advocation of church of Lethnot and chaplaincy of Dalbolge, 40 merks of the great customs of burgh of Montrosse, lordship of 
2 CONC Innerarite, with advocation of church thereof, barony of Douny, lordship of Guthry, lordship of Futhnevin and forest of Platarie, lordship of Clova, lordship of Ruthuen and advocation of four chaplaincies of altar of St George in 
2 CONC parish church of burgh of Dunde, with advocation of chaplaincy of altar of All Saints in said church, and a house in Dunde on north side of said church in vennel of the Friars, in sheriffdom of Forfare, lordship of Miggil, lordshi
2 CONC p of Melginche, lordship of Aberbothry, lordship of Lethnot, lordship of Carnbady, lordship of Baltrody, and tenement in burgh of Perth, in the Watirgate, on east side thereof, in sheriffdom of Perth, lordship of Carnbow and of Ne
2 CONC uhal in constabulary of Carale, 28 December 1421. Seal damaged on tag, in blue silk bag with a red ribbon. Witnesses: William, bishop of Glasgow, Chancellor of Scotland, Sir Alexander Stewart of Levenax, son of said Murdoch, Sir W
2 CONC alter Stewart of Railstoun, Sir William Hay of Nachtane, kts., and Alan of Ottirburne, said Murdoch's secretary. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD121%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&
2 CONC k=RAILSTOUN&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Fothringham of Powrie Muniments, reference GD121/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 February 1430-31: Charter by which Robert, Earl of Fife, confirms that he has given the lands of Achaland, Ketidy and Cragsumquhar in in sheriffdom of Fife to William Despensa, burgess of Perth, and his wife Isabelle Campbel
2 CONC l. Theese lands were given in exchange for the lands of Drumonde. With others, the charter was witnessed by Sir Walter Stewart of Railstoun: "D. Valt. Senescalli dom. de Railstoun". The earl of Fife's charter was confirmed under t
2 CONC he Great Seal of Scotland on 13 February 1430-31. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/41 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 187 on pp. 41-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
