2 CONT David Lindsay, 1st Earl of Crawford (c. 1360 – 1407) was a Scottish peer who was created Earl in 1398. Many historians believe that Lindsay was also the organiser for the Battle of the Clans at Perth in 1396. Additionally, Lindsay
2 CONC  was a noted jousting champion who fought the English champion Lord Welles in a remarkable duel on St. George's Day. In the duel, Lindsay unhorsed Welles so easily that the crowd began yelling that he had nailed himself to his sad
2 CONC dle. To prove he had not, Lindsay jumped off his horse and then back on, while still wearing his full suit of armor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Stewart, daughter of King Robert II and Euphemia de Ross. They had seven children:
2 CONT
