1 NOTE He succeeded his father in 1381 and his cousin as 9th Lord of Crawford in 1397. As and act of chivalry, he fought a "passage of arms" on St. George's Day, 1398 with Lord Welles on London Bridge. He was praised for unhorsing his op
2 CONC ponent. He was made Earl of Crawford on 21 Apr 1398 and Admiral of Scotland in 1398. He was appointed Ambassador to England in 1406. Through his wife, he acquired the Lordship of Strathcairn.
