1 NOTE William Douglas by 1448 was a powerful force in Scotland, as Earl of
2 CONT Douglas, Earl of wigtown, Lord of Galloway and Bothwell, and of the
2 CONT forests of Ettrick and Selkirk, possessor of great estates in the
2 CONT sheriffdoms of Edinburg, Haddington, Lanark, Roxburgh, Linlithgow, Peebles
2 CONT and Aberdeen; and his brothers in rule : Archibald, Earl of Moray; Hugh,
2 CONT Earl of Ormond; and John of Balveny - who all held vast areas in the north
2 CONT and northwest.  Called to make treaty with King James II, William Douglas
2 CONT was not inclined to relinquish his treaty, and gave the King a polite
2 CONT refusal..."then the King burst into a rage at his obstinancy, and stabbed
2 CONT the EArl with his dagger. The Sir Patrick Gray struck William Douglas on
2 CONT the head with a battle axe and others kept stabbing the dying man with
2 CONT knives and daggers.  He was covered with 26 wounds. He was not given a
2 CONT Christian burial.  Following the death of Douglas, his brothers led six
2 CONT hundred horsemen into Stirling to loot and burn, and the dishonoured safe
2 CONT conduct which had been give William Douglas was dragged through the
2 CONT streets at the tail of an old horse, and James Douglas, the brother,
2 CONT renounced his homage to King James II, and offered allegiance to the King
2 CONT of England.
