1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes was born before 1477.2 He was the son of William Forbes, 3rd Lord Forbes and Lady Christian Gordon.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, married '''Catherine Stewart,''' daughter of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl and his 1st wife, Margaret Douglas. Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth Forbes, who married John Grant of Freuchie (died 1585)
2 CONT # James Forbes (died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Christian Lundie, daughter of Sir John Lundie of that Ilk and Elizabeth Forrester, before 26 February 1509/10.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Brad Verity wrote:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She is called second daughter of the 1st wife in DP and CP sub Forbes (1926), 1st daughter of the 2nd wife by BEP, and listed as the 2nd daughter in SP Atholl (1904). 
2 CONT
2 CONT No marriage contract or settlement survives to verify the first name and marriage of this daughter of Atholl. We do have this, from a genealogy of the Forbes family written by one Matthew Lumsden, around the year 1580, when he die
2 CONC d:
2 CONT
2 CONT > "Next to him succeeded John Lord Forbes, the third brother, gray Willie's youngest son, who married Dame Katharine Stewart, daughter to Earle John of Atholl, who bear to him James Master of Forbes, who died unmarried, whilk was 
2 CONC a great pitie and dolor to them yt. knew him; and a daughter called Elspet, who was married on the Laird of Grant, and his Ladie departed but further succession: and after her death, the sd. Lord John married Dame Christian Lundie
2 CONC , daughter to Sr John Lundie of that ilk" 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/genealogyoffamil00lums#page/10/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT As Matthew Lumsden, the author of the above, was married to an illegitimate daughter of John, 6th Lord Forbes, presumably he was familiar enough with the family to correctly report the first name and parentage of the 6th Lord's St
2 CONC ewart wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Stewart died before 26 February 1510, when King James IV approved Forbes's settlement on his second wife Christine Lundy: 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/734/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Stewart's surviving child Elizabeth Forbes married James Grant, 3rd Laird of Freuchie, and three of their children were married in 1539, 1545, and 1553, pointing to births for them in the 1520s. Chronology then suggests 
2 CONC that Elizabeth Forbes was born around 1500, and that in turn her mother Katherine Stewart fits better as a daughter of the 1st Earl of Atholl and his second wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This is only guesswork. The 6th Lord Forbes doesn't have an entry in ODNB and only has a barebones account in CP, making it difficult to determine any links with the Stewarts of Atholl that could help to date his first marriage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart and Margaret Douglas had three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lady  Elizabeth Stewart, of Atholl, married Andrew Gray, 2nd Lord Gray.
2 CONT # Jean (or Janet) Stewart, married by contract dated 31 A |ugust 1507, James Arbuthnott of Arbuthnott. He had a crown charter of the feudal barony of Arbuthnott 29 January 1507. He left a testament dated 7 March 1521, and died bef
2 CONC ore 13 March 1521. [SIC:  daughter by 1st wife, Margaret Douglas]
2 CONT # Katherine Stewart, married Sir John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes. [SIC: daughter by 1st wife, Margaret Douglas]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart and Eleanor Sinclair had two sons and nine daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl, living 1520, and died before 1522, who married Janet Campbell (died about Candlemas 1545/6), daughter of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Arygll.
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, Bishop of Caithness.
2 CONT # Elizabeth | Isabel Stewart, married John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox
2 CONT #Lady Christian Stewart, married Niel Stewart, 3rd of Garth and Fothergill     d. 30 May 1538
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart, married Sir William Murray, of Castleton who was killed at Battle of Flodden Duke of Atholl
2 CONT # Elizabeth | Isabel Stewart, married Alexander Robertson, of Strowan.
2 CONT # Jean Stewart, married Robert Gordon, Knt., of Pitlurg.
2 CONT # Isabel | Margaret Stewart, married Robert Robertson younger, of Strowan.
2 CONT # Marjory [sic: MARIOTE] Stewart, married Sir Colin Campbell, of Glenorchy.  d. 26 Jul 1529, Lochtay
2 CONT #Elspeth Stewart, married Sir Robert Innes 2nd of Innermarky.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Atholl]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Stewart Born about 1473 in Of, Aberdeenshire, Scotland Daughter of John Stewart and Margaret (Douglas) Stewart Sister of Jean (Stewart) Arbuthnot [half], Elizabeth (Stewart) Gray, Joanna (Stewart) Gordon, Christian Stewa
2 CONC rt [half], Elspeth (Stewart) Innes [half], Isabel (Stewart) Robertson [half], Elizabeth (Stewart) Ross [half], John Stewart [half], Elizabeth (Stewart) Robertson [half], Jean Stewart [half], Andrew Stewart [half], Margaret Stewart
2 CONC  [half] and Mariote (Stewart) Campbell [half] Wife of John Forbes — married before 1508 in Scotland Mother of Elizabeth (Forbes) Grant and James Forbes Died about 1515 in Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT 1463 Traquair, Peebleshire, Scotland Death: February 26, 1510 (47) Scotland Immediate Family:
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl and Lady Margaret Douglas, Countess of Douglas Wife of John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes Mother of James Forbes and Hon. Elizabeth Forbes Sister of Isabella Stewart; Jean Stewart, Counte
2 CONC ss of Huntly; Elizabeth Stewart and Anne Stewart Half sister of Marjory Stewart; Margaret Stewart; Elspeth Stewart; John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl; Christian Stewart; Lady Elizabeth Stewart; Jean Stewart; Andrew Stewart, Bishop 
2 CONC of Caithness; Jean Stewart; Elizabeth Stewart; Henry Stewart; Malcolm Leslie, First Laird of Cults and Andrew Leslie of Pitscurry
