2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT #http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/2014-05/1400274049
2 CONT #Source: Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's Edition of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland. (Edinburgh: David Douglas, 1908-1919. 9 vols.), IV:54. (No entry in Vol. 9, corrections) 
2 CONT #Source: G E C et al, Complete Peerage (St Catharine press, London, 1910 on), V: 545 (Forbes). (No entry in Vol XIV, corrections) 
2 CONT #[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Atholl John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl] (c. 1437–1442 – 15 September 1512),[1] also known as Sir John Stewart of Balveny, was a Scottish nobleman and ambassador.  Sometime
2 CONC  before April 1475, he married as his second wife, Lady Eleanor Sinclair (died 21 March 1518), daughter of William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney and Marjory Sutherland. They had two sons and nine daughters: ... Lady Catherine Stewa
2 CONC rt, married John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes.
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Forbes,_6th_Lord_Forbes John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes] (died 1547) was a Scottish landowner.  He was the son of William Forbes, 3rd Lord Forbes and Christian Gordon, daughter of Alexander Gordo
2 CONC n, 1st Earl of Huntly. John Forbes married Catherine Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl and Eleanor Sinclair. Their children included:    Elizabeth Forbes, who married John Grant of Freuchie (died 1585).  John F
2 CONC orbes married secondly Christian Lundie or Lundin. 
2 CONT #'''en.Wikipedia: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Forbes%2C_6th_Lord_Forbes John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes]'''
2 CONT #'''Montgomery Rowntree Families and Genealogy:''' [http://www.montyhistnotes.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I3289&tree=MontyHistNotes_II 6th Lord Forbes John Forbes]
2 CONT # Matthew Lumsden, Genealogy of the Family of Forbes (Inverness, 1819), p. 12.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=sZdDAAAAYAAJ&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&pg=PA12#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT #James Balfour Paul,'' Scots Peerage,'' vol. 4 (Edinburgh, 1907), p. 53. < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/52/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT #"Red Book of Scotland, Volume 9" (Smi-You). Pages 580-582. < [https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62525/records/61048?_phcmd=u(%27https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62525/?name=john_stewart&birth=1440&death=1512&
2 CONC count=50&successSource=Search&queryId=5a027571-b213-4659-9f08-e627e26176d9%27,%27successSource%27) Ancestry.com] >; ([https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000216556017831&graph_node_id=profile-10029640&mode=tagged Docume
2 CONC nt attached]).  Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl, m. firstly, by 25 March 1460, to Margaret, daughter of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Douglas, by whom he was the father of: Janet, married Alexander Gordon; Catherine, married
2 CONC  John, 6th Lord Forbes; Elizabeth Stewart, married before 1483, to Andrew, 2nd Lord Gray, (he was widower of Janet, only daughter of Robert, Lord Keith, by whom he had issue. he d. in February of 1514), and had issue. He married s
2 CONC econdly, by 19 April 1475, to Eleanora, daughter of William Sinclair, Earl of Orkney and Caithness (she d. on 21 March 1518) .... and by whom he had further issue [2 sons and 9 daughters].  
2 CONT # https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00006030&tree=LEO cites
