1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM STEWART OF BRIERY HILL AND ROSYTH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart08.php StirnetL Stewart 08]'''
2 CONT # '''[http://www.s781.org/bonkyll-3B.html Armorial Ensigns: Stewart of Rosyth]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary by HRH Prince Kieren de Muire Von Drakenberg ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stewart of Briery-Hill, 5th Lord of Rosyth and Janet Moubray had the following children; 	
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir David Stewart, 6th of Rosyth. 2. Robert Stewart 3. Andrew Stewart,   d. By 11th March 1562 4. Adam Stewart, of Berriehill. 5. Margaret Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a charter from his nephew Sir David Stewart, of Rosyth, for the lands of Rosyth and Schanbothy on 21 November, 1490, and had an exemption and license to remain at home for the rest of his days from all parliaments and wars,
2 CONC  due to his weakness and disposition of his person "be gret infirmite and seiknes" from King James IV. on 24 May, 1505.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Comment ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Share some things about...........
2 CONT Sir William Stewart of Briery-Hill, 5th Lord of Rosyth is my/our third cousin 15 times removed.
2 CONT Janet Milburn 8/4/22
