1 NAME Margaret /Ogilvy/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN Ogilvy
2 _MARNM Ogilvy
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET OGILVY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''The Scots Peerage identifies Margaret Ogilvie, here treated, as the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Ogilvy-Laird-of-Lintrathen-Airlie/6000000002188045959?through=6000000002188101804 This is wrong. S
2 CONC ee below. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/124/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 124]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Ogilvie, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Ogilvy-1st-Lord-Ogilvy-of-Airlie/6000000002188101804 The name of her mother is not known. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD83%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family of Bamff, Perthshire, reference GD83/13] [https://archive.org/
2 CONC details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/31/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Ogilvy, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Gilbert-Ramsay-of-Bamff/6000000191446083880?through=6000000191456463838 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/124/mode/1up The Scots Peer
2 CONC age I: 124]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 April 1482: Contract of Marriage between Gilbert Ramsay, son of Alexander Ramsay of Woodwrae, and Margaret Ogilvy, daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?
2 CONC reference=GD83%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family of Bamff, Perthshire, reference GD83/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This document is printed in Sir James H Ramsay, bart., (ed.) 'Bamff Charters A.D. 1232-1703', (Oxford, 1915), pp. 31-33. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/31/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 
2 CONC 13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 April 1483: Precept by Finlay Ramsay of Bamff for infefting his grandson Gilbert Ramsay and his wife [Margaret] in the lands of Mawes and Petdrey (Pitdray). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD83%2f14&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=finlay+Ramsay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family of Bamff, Perthshire, reference GD83/14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This document is printed in Sir James H Ramsay, bart., (ed.) 'Bamff Charters A.D. 1232-1703', (Oxford, 1915), p. 33. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/33/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 14]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1483: Instrument of sasine which confirms possession of the lands of Mawis and Peddrey to Gilbert Ramsay and his wife Margaret Ogilvy. Gilbert Ramsay is identified as the son and apparent heir Alexander Ramsay, who is id
2 CONC entified as the son and heir of Finlay Ramsay. Margaret Ogilvy is identified as the daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie. Her brother Thomas Ogilvy acted as bailie and gave sasine to Gilbert and Margaret,  and her brothers Archi
2 CONC bald Ogilvy and John Ogilvy were the witnesses present. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/34/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
