0 @I6000000219736884857@ INDI
1 NAME Isabella /Ogilvy/
2 GIVN Isabella
2 SURN Ogilvy
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1477
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1497
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ogilvy-769
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella was born about 1479, daughter of James Ogilvy and Elene Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT While she was still a child a special dispensation by papal bull of Innocent VIII dated at Rome 5 June 1489 granted Isabella to marry her near relative Alexander, son of James Stewart, Earl of Buchan and Auchterhouse. A Notarial i
2 CONC nstrument narrating the papal dispensation for the marriage of Alexander Stewart, son and apparent heir of Sir James Stewart, lord of Buchan and Auchterhouse and Isobel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Lintrathen, they bein
2 CONC g related within the fourth degree was drawn up on 10 Jan 1491. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT At Bolshan on 21 Jan 1490/91James Earl of Buchan and Auchterhouse granted to his eldest son Alexander Stewart and Isbella Ogilvy his spouse lands in the barony of Kettins and the lands of ac terras de Leoch, in the barony of Aucht
2 CONC erhouse to be held by Alexander and Isoble and their heirs male. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Letters of reversion by James, Earl of Buchan, to Sir James Ogilvy of Lintrathen, of the lands of Carcary for redemption of the said lands of Broadland of Kettins and Kettins were formed at Arbroath on 24 April 1492.[3] This may h
2 CONC ave been associated the marriage of Isabel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel died without issue about 1497.
2 CONT
2 CONT Instrument of redemption of the lands of Carcary by James, Lord Ogilvy of Airlie, from James, Earl of Buchan was settled at the Parish church of Auchterhouse, on 26 June 1498. This may have come about by the death of Isabella with
2 CONC out issue. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ NRS GD16/44/3 see [1]
2 CONT ↑ RMS Vol.ii 2043 see [2]
2 CONT ↑ NRS GD16/22/6 see [3]
2 CONT ↑ NRS GD16/22/6 see [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
