1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the father of https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Fraser-1st-Lord-Lovat/6000000002225026281?through=6000000190039006836
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Sanctus Fraser, Lord of Lovat (C. 1417 – 1450)
2 CONT
2 CONT Fraser of Lovat (Baronage) describes Hugh Fraser, 5th feudal Lord of Lovat as the second son of Hugh Fraser, 4th Lord of Lovat, and his heir.  Sometimes referred to in the literature as ‘Sanctus,’ Latin for holy, Hugh was born in 
2 CONC C. 1417. He married Janet, daughter of Thomas Dunbar, 2d of Dunbar, Earl of Moray.  Hugh died at 33 years of age in about. 1450, leaving as his heir, Hugh, 6th feudal Lord of Lovat; Thomas Fraser; Isabel Fraser; and Alison Fraser.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From ''History of the Frasers of Lovat …'' page 56.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh, 2nd Lord Fraser, married when very young Lady Janet, daughter of Thomas Dunbar, Earl of Moray, with issue —
2 CONT 1. Thomas, who died young. He was Prior of Beauly ad commendum.
2 CONT 2. Hugh, who became his father's heir and successor.
2 CONT 3. Alison or Giles, who according to some authorities, died young, but 
2 CONT according to others married Farquhar Mackintosh XII. of Mackintosh, Captain of Clan Chattan, and secondly, her cousin, Walter Innes of Innes.
2 CONT 4. Isabel, who married David Gumming of Earnside, with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh, second Lord, died at Lovat in 1450, according to the MS. in the Advocates' Library, aged 33
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # ''History of the Frasers of Lovat, with genealogies of the principal families of the name: to which is added those of Dunballoch and Phopachy'' by Mackenzie, Alexander, 1838-1898. Publication date 1896.  Page 55-57.  <. [https:/
2 CONC /archive.org/details/historyoffrasers00mackuoft/page/54/mode/2up Archive.org] > 
2 CONT #  Paul, James Balfour (1908). "Fraser, Lord Fraser of Lovat". The Scots Peerage; Founded on Wood's Edition of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; Containing an Historical And Genealogical Account of The Nobility of That Kin
2 CONC gdom. Vol. V. Edinburgh: David Douglas. pp. 522-523. Retrieved 19 February 2022. < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/522/mode/2up Archive.Org] > this Hugh Fraser is not listed 
