2 CONT '''2 October 1494: Retour in favour of Thomas Ogilvy as heir of the deceased Thomas Ogilvy of Cloua, his grandfather, in the lands of Bradowne, Tulzemulye of Doyl, Ballinhard, Ballintyr, Kirktoun of Cloua, Clairteleycht and Arntib
2 CONC ir with the mill of the same, lying in barony of Cloua, three parts of the lands of Inchevin lying in barony of Kynzalte and the barony of Cortuquhy. Jury: William Maxwell of Telling, sheriff depute of Forfar, James Scrimgeour, Co
2 CONC nstable of Dunde, James Rind of Broxmoucht, John Dempstar of Caraldstoun, John Ouchterlowny of that Ilk, William Morres of Cullow, Alexander Stradraquhyn of Boigtoun, John Gardyn of Boroufeyld, Master Thomas Duram of Grange of Mon
2 CONC ifucht, John Mortoun of Fleimyntoun, John Ovilvy of Inuerquarady, John Haliburtoun of Gask, Alexander Ramsay of Newtibbir, Walter Boyd of Bonytoun, James Moncur of Balluny and John Thornton. Forfar. [One seal appended; others miss
2 CONC ing]. [20.11]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f2%2f16&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Thomas+Ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls o
2 CONC f Airlie, reference GD16/2/16]'''
2 CONT
