1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wemyss-100
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Wemyss of Kincaldrum, Reres and Wemyss, although his father is not known, he was the grandson of Sir John, the second son of Sir David Wemyss the ambassador.''' John was heir-male of the family. He was first named in 1
2 CONC 372, when he granted to Sir Andrew de Valoniis the half mill of Lochore which was his great-grandfather David Wemyss' property. In 1376, after Sir David's death, his son Duncan entered into an agreement with Sir John, and in 1389 
2 CONC the estates passed to John.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://olypen.com/zob/genealogy/Scot/Wemyss/Wemyss.html
2 CONT
2 CONT A1. Michael of Wemyss and Methil, lvd:1170/1210;
2 CONT B1. Sir John of Wemyss and Methil, lvd:1202/1260;
2 CONT C1. Sir Michael Wemyss of Wemyss, lvd:1231, m. N. Lochore;
2 CONT D1. Sir David Wemyss, m. Marjory Ramsay;
2 CONT E1. Sir John Wemyss;
2 CONT F1. N. Wemyss;
2 CONT G1. '''Sir John Wemyss of Leuchars, m1. Isabel Erskine,''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT - - -
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT of Fife, Scotland. Had lands in Leuchars, Kincaldrum, and Reres, inherited from his grandfather Sir John of Kincaldrum. In 1412-1413, he was among those engaged in negotiations in England for the release of King James I and in 142
2 CONC 4 was among the barons who received safe conduct to meet the King upon his return to Scotland. Sir John Wemyss married at least twice and had children. Married secondly Isabel Erskine (died c1424; daughter of Isabel Inchmartin and
2 CONC  Sir Alan Erskine; granddaughter of Margaret Wemyss and Sir John Inchmartin).
2 CONT //////////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT Sir John was a Knight of, Kincaldrum, Angusshire, Scotland 
2 CONT /////////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT Memorials of the family of Wemyss of Wemyss - https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/146/mode/2up/search/Elizabeth+Wemyss
2 CONT
2 CONT >"15. SIR JOHN DE WEMYSS. This Knight having only one daughter, as may be seen in the tree of the family, resigned his lands, holding of the earl of Fife, to John de Wemyss of Rivas, his cousin, and heir-male, A.D. 1376, and was s
2 CONC ucceeded by him. '''He married''' ISABELLA ERSKINE, co-heiress of Sir Allan Erskine of Inchmartine, heir-female, also of Wemyss; and A.D. 1403 obtained from King Robert the Third a charter of confirmation of all the lands disponed
2 CONC  to his grandfather by David. He left several children, and was succeeded by his eldest son.” 
2 CONT >SOURCE: Farnie, Henry Brougham. (1860). ''The Fife Coast from Queensferry to Fifeness: Handy-Book of Fifeness''@GoogleBooks: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Fife_coast_from_Queensferry_to_Fifen/Np8HAAAAQAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1
2 CONC &dq=%22Isabella+Erskine%22+Wemyss&pg=PA98&printsec=frontcover page 98].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Other Sources====
2 CONT * Balfour Paul, James. (1904), Vol. 8. Edinburgh: D. Douglas. @Archive.org: [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/480/mode/2up Vol. 8:480-483]. '''Note:''' This source spells her name ''Isabella''.
2 CONT * Blackwood, W. (Ed.). (1889).'' Blackwood’s Edinburgh Magazine'': “The Wemysses of Wemyss” (Vol. 145). William Blackwood & Sons. @GoogleBooks: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Blackwood_s_Edinburgh_Magazine/FsWJ8HZ0HksC?hl=e
2 CONC n&gbpv=1&dq=%22Isabel+Erskine%22+Wemyss&pg=PA691&printsec=frontcover May Issue, pages 691-92].
2 CONT * Boswell, J. J. (Ed.). (2019). ''The Boswell History and Arms of the Nobility''. @Babel.HathieTrust: [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=hvd.hncdk4&view=1up&seq=9 Pedigree Chart, page 9].
2 CONT * Easson, D. E. (Ed.). (1947). Charters of the Abbey of Coupar Angus, Vol. I: Charters I to CXVII 1166-1376. In ''Publications of the Scottish Historical Society'' @Digital.NLS.UK: [https://digital.nls.uk/scottish-history-society-
2 CONC publications/browse/archive/128319741#?c=0&m=0&s=0&cv=282&xywh=-439%2C-159%2C2612%2C3164 (Vol. 40, p. 206)]. University of Edinburgh for the Scottish History Society.
2 CONT * Fraser, Sir William. (1888). ''Memorials of the Family of Wemyss of Wemyss'', Vol. 1. @Google Books: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Memorials_of_the_Family_of_Wemyss_of_Wem/3Q6lWnM29hsC?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Isabel%20Erskin
2 CONC e%22%20Wemyss pp. VII, XIX, XXI, XXIII, XXVIII, XXIX, 40-41, 44, 46, 51, 55, 58-60, 67, 78, 85, 409]. '''Note:''' p. 83, fn. 1 refers to her as "Dame Isabel [Erskine]."
2 CONT * Gabaldon, D. (2015). ''The Outlandish Companion: Companion to Outlander, Dragonfly in Amber, Voyager, and Drums of Autumn'' (Revised and Updated). Random House. https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Outlandish_Companion_Revis
