2 CONT '''7 February 1503: James Ogibly of Ynchmartin. "In the accione and caus persewit be James Ogibly of Ynchmartin and Wilyeam Chawmer of Drumlochy, executouris til umquhile Thomas Blaere of Bathyok, aganis James Gray and Marjory Sco
2 CONC t, executouris til umquhile Thomas Gray of the Muretone, that incontinent eftit the deceiss of the sade Thomas Blaere, umquhile Thomas Gray come to the place and landis of Bawtrody pertenyng til the sade umquhile Thomas Blaere and
2 CONC  spulyeit and tuke away all his cornis that grew on the said landis of the quhilkis the sadis executouris of the sade Thomas Blaere suld have the disposicione, as of the laif of his gudis, be ressone of thair office of executory, 
2 CONC for the quhilkis cornis the executouris of the said Thomas Blaere rasir our soverane lordis letteris of summondis upon the sade umquhille Thomas Gray and als the sadis executouris of the sade Thomas Gray til bring with thaim our s
2 CONC overane lordis letteris gevin apone the sade Thomas Gray gift of bastardry, that thai may be sene and considerit gif thai war procedit of justice or nocht" , the parties being personally present, the lordis decern that the letters
2 CONC  given upon the bastardry of the said deceased Thomas Gray are legally correct as proceeding upon letters of gift produced under the privy seal, and they ordain letters. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&d
2 CONC q=Ogilvy+Balnagarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=Ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 228]'''
