2 CONT '''14 February 1503: "The prior of Perth. In the acc[i]one and caus persewit be the prior and freris predicatouris of Perrth aganis David Ogilby of Ynchmartin for the wrangus withhalding fra thaimof five bollis of quhete and ane h
2 CONC alf, aucht til furth of the landis of mannis of Ynchmartin," the said prior being personally present and the said David compearing by James Ogilby, his son and procurator, the lords, in presence of the king, and with consent of sa
2 CONC id James, as procurator, decern that David shall pay to the prior and convent a half chalder of wheat and a half chalder of bear, "of the great met that is now", that is now to be delivered immediately, as victuals owed to them of
2 CONC  the said lands of all times past. They also decern, with the same consent, that David shall pay to the prior and convent yearly in time to come a half chalder of wheat and a half chalder of bear, of King William's measure, for th
2 CONC is year to start as between this date and Whitsunday next, thereafter to be delivered between Martinmas and Pasche, and they [ordain] letters for distraint. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Baln
2 CONC agarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 268]'''
