2 CONC hts Templars] in lordship of Inchemartyn. '''Witnesses: David de Ogiluy [Ogilvie], eldest son of said Sir Andrew, Patrick de Ogiluy [Ogilvie], son of said David''', sir Thomas de Cruam [Cramb] and sir James Nefe [Neave], chaplains
2 CONC . [Seal appended.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f982&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=inchmartine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Lesl
2 CONC ie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/982]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Dates
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Ogilvy-of-Inchmartin-Kt/6000000011089191387 lives until at least 1503: https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKH
2 CONC WDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=Ynchmartin&f=false (Acts of the Lords of Council: 1501-1503 By Scotland, Scottish Record Office) when an action is brought against him and he is represented by his son James.
2 CONT But he's old enough to have an 'adult'? son https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Ogilvy/6000000184251283823?through=6000000011089191387 sign as a witness of a chartar with him in 1449 - which puts David's birth date at least 30 yea
2 CONC rs before 1449 (so he's born c 1410-1419?) and dies in his late 80s or 90s.
2 CONT And '''Patrick must be at least 15 when he signs as a witness above, so his birth must at least be c1430-34'''
