2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It has been claimed by at least one pedigree published by MyHeritage that Mariota Hay, here treated, is the daughter of William Hay, Earl of Erroll, and his wife Beatrice Douglas. However, verifiable evidence of rel
2 CONC ationship is not provided. [https://www.myheritage.com/names/mariota_hay MyHeritage] Moreover, this proposition is not supported by the Scots Peerage account of the family of the Earl of Erroll, which makes no mention of a daughte
2 CONC r named Mariota. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/564/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 564-5]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1492: Charter by which David Ogilvy of Inchmartine salutes the souls of his father and mother, "Andree  O. patris sui, Mariote O. matris sue" and, with the consent of his wife Mariote Hay, confirms that he has given an
2 CONC  annualrent of 12 merks from his lands of Petmedill and Inchmartyn to the Convent of the Friars Minor of Dundee. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/613/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2886]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 August 1500: Charter by which David Ogilvy of Inchmartine, with the consent of his wife Mariote Hay, confirms that he has given certain lands, including the lands of Westir-Inchmartyn and Estir-Inchmartyn, together with the 
2 CONC lands of Petmedil and Cragdaly, to his son James Ogilvy of Balgally. David Ogilvy of Inchmartine reserved a free tenement from these lands to himself, which liferent, after his death was to be enjoyed by his wife Mariote Hay. Excl
2 CONC uded from Mariote Hay's liferent interest was the tower of Inchmartine and a twenty merk land in the barony, which was to go to his son James in the period immediately after his decease. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagni
2 CONC si02scot/page/540/mode/1up  RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2547]''' 
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1500: Instrument of Sasine in favour of James Ogilve, son of David Ogilve of Inchmartin, of the lands of barony of Inchmartin following on charters by said David and Marion Hay, his spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotla
2 CONC nd.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1021&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+hay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference 
2 CONC GD26/3/1021]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 August 1500: Instrument of Sasine in favour of James Ogilvy of Balegave, son of David Ogilvy of Inchmartyn, of lands of Easter and Wester Inchmartyn, Petmedil and Cragdaly, in barony of Inchmartyn, superiority of lands of St
2 CONC rathardill in barony of Douny, and lands of Balgawe in barony of Inchstuyer, following on precept by said David and Marion Hay, his spouse, dated 17 August 1500. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx
2 CONC ?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1022&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+hay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1023]'''
2 CONT
