2 CONT == [https://www.myheritage.com/names/mariota_ogilvy Pedigrees Published by MyHeritage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mariota Ogilvy (born Hay of Leys) was born in 1460, at birth place , to William 1st Earl of Erroll Hay,1st Earl of Errol, 2nd Lord Hay, Constable of Scotland and Lady Beatrice Countess Of Erroll Hay Countess of Erroll in lieu o
2 CONC f a 2nd Earl of Erroll (born Douglas) . William was born in 1412, in Erroll, Perth, Scotland. Lady was born in 1429, in Douglas, South Lanarkshire, Scotland, United Kingdom. Mariota had 10 siblings: Willem 3rd Earl Van Erroll Hay 
2 CONC , Nicholas Erroll Hay 2nd Earl of Erroll and 8 other siblings . Mariota passed away in 1480, at age 20 at death place .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mariota Ogilvy (born Hay of Leys) was born in 1456, at birth place , to William de Hay and Beatrice Hay (born Douglas) . William was born in 1423, in Errol, Perth and Kinross, Scotland, United Kingdom. Beatrice was born circa 1
2 CONC 429, in Douglas, South Lanarkshire, Scotland, United Kingdom. Mariota had 10 siblings: Margaret Fraser (born Hay) , Nicholas Hay and 8 other siblings . Mariota married David (Sir) Ogilvy . David was born in 1455, in Perth, Perthsh
2 CONC ire, Scotland. His occupation was a knight. They had 3 children: James Ogilvy and 2 other children. Mariota passed away in 1480, at age 24 at death place .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hay-3773 Biographical Summary by Wikitree] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mariot was born about 1435 possibly a daughter of one of the Hay families in Errol. About 1455 she married David Ogilvy son and heir of Sir Andrew Ogilvy of Inchmartine and his wife Marjory Glen. David and Mariot had four child
2 CONC ren. 1. Alexander his only lawful son and heir apparent. He died without issue during the life of his father. 2. Marjory who married Thomas Blair of Balthayock. 3. Giles. On 9 Jun 1483 a contract was made regarding her marriage to
2 CONC  John Moncrieff son and heir apparent of John Moncrieff of that Ilk. 4. Christian who was contracted on 25 April 1478 to marry Patrick son of Lord Gray but this marriage did not take place.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At Inchmartine on 30 Apr 1492 David Ogilvy and his wife Mariot Hay for the salvation of the souls of his parents Andrew Ogilvy and Mariot Ogilvy (sic) donated to the Minor Friars of Dundee an annual rent of 12 merks from the la
2 CONC nds of Pitmiddle and Inchmartine.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In a charter made in Perth in the presence of Patrick Wells the provost of Perth on 13 August 1599 David Ogilvy and his wife Mariot Hay granted the lands of Balgay to his illegitimate son and heir, James Ogilvy, to be held of D
2 CONC avid and of the King reserving free tenement to David and after his decease to Mariot. '''
