2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Ogilvy, here treated, is the nephew of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Ogilvy-of-Inchmartin-Kt/6000000011089191387 The names of his father and mother are not known. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&
2 CONC pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Ogilvy, here treated, raised a legal action against his uncle David, presumably because he believed that he had the legal right to succeed to his lands and barony of Inchmartine, but his claim failed. [https://books.googl
2 CONC e.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarrow&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 July 1501: David Ogilby of Inchmartin. "Comperit, Andro, Lord Gray, and Maister James Henresone as procuratouris for David Ogilby of Ynchmartin, and protestit that becaus Thomas Berclay, son and executour till umquhile David 
2 CONC Berclay of Cullernye, and David Ogilby, nevo til the sade David Ogilby of Ynchmartin, gert summonf [him] for the wrangus postponyng and deferring til infeft the sade David Ogibly yongar, his nevo, heretably  be charter and saising
2 CONC  in dew forme in al and sindry his landis and baronry of Ynchmartin, with the pertinence, liand in the schirefdome of Perth, and certane utheris punctis contenit in the copy of the summondis, and wald nocht compere til folow him, 
2 CONC that thairfore thai suld refound the costis and expensis sustenit be him herethrow and that he suld nocht ansuere thairto quhill  he war new summond." [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=ENKQAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA389&dq=Ogilvy+Balnagarro
2 CONC w&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjd1L7f-M7qAhVOTcAKHWDhDJcQ6AEwBXoECAQQAg#v=onepage&q=ynchmartin&f=false Acts of the Lords of Council III: p. 35]'''
