2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 December 1462: Excambation between Silvester Rettra of that ilk and Thomas Lovell, whereby said Silvester exchanges lands of Ochtergaven for lands of Kynbachlaw, both in sheriffdom of Perth. Great seal charter confirming the 
2 CONC excambion was issued on 16 Dec. 1462. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f226&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettra&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1513&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Pap
2 CONC ers of the Rattray Family of Craighall, Perthshire, reference GD385/226]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 October 1474: Letters of reversion by John, Earl of Athole, Lord Balvany, to George, Earl of Huntle, Lord Gordon, over lands of Tullich and others in lordship of Obyne, sheriffdom of Aberdeen. Letters contain bond that notwi
2 CONC thstanding that the said George has sold the said John these lands, extending in all to 100 merks scots, as soon as the marriage between Alexander Gordon, son and apparent heir of said George, and failing of said George through de
2 CONC cease, Adam, his brother, 'and sa furth fra son to son lauchfully gottin or to be gottin apparand ayr to hym' with Jean, daughter of said John, or any other daughter, is solemnised, or if said marriage fails 'throw wilfulnes of ow
2 CONC r said douchter Jehan or ony of hir sisteris', then said John will resign to said George said lands. Redemption to take place on high altar of cathedral kirk of Dunkelde (3000 merks scots). Witnesses: James, Earl of Buchan, Lord O
2 CONC uchterhous, granter's brother, Andrew, Lord Gray, SILVESTER RETTRAY OF THAT ILK. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD181%2f174&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=silvester+rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&
2 CONC df=1450&dt=1542&di=n National Records of Scotland, Aboyne Muniments, reference GD181/174]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 March 1476: Bond of Renunciation by SILVESTER RETTRAY OF THAT ILK, and Margaret de Ogilwy [Ogilvie], sister of deceased Alexander de Ogilwy [Ogilvie] of Duntroon [Duntrune], to David Ogilwy [Ogilvie] of Inchmartyn [Inchmarti
2 CONC ne], heir of entail of said Alexander, of lands of Duntroon [Duntrune], sixth part of Inchmartyn, third part of Balmuto, third part of the quarter of the Dron, Kynnefe [Kinneff], and others, being the lands formerly belonging to s
2 CONC aid Alexander. Witnesses: William, bishop of Orkynnay [Orkney], James Scrymgour [Scrimgeour], constable of Dunde [Dundee], Mr. John of Schamyr [Chalmers], parson of Hay [Hoy], Thomas Thomsone [Thomson], burgess of Edinburgh, Gilbe
2 CONC rt Makkowlow [McCulloch], clerk of diocese of Galluay [Galloway]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1002&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National 
2 CONC Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1002]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 January 1480: Instrument of Transumpt of GD26/3/1002. Witnesses: John Rettre, son and apparent heir of said Silvester [SILVESTER RETTRAY OF THAT ILK]  John Rettre of Lichhil Thomas Fodringaym of Balleway Sir James Hudsone, c
2 CONC haplain John Murdowsone Andrew Balglaly Andrew Parkar of Balcasky Robert Ardlar [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1009&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettre&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&
2 CONC di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1009]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 July 1483: DECREET ARBITRAL by Alexander Blair of Balthiok [Balthayock], SILVESTER RETTRAY OF THAT ILK, Andrew Charteris of Cuthilgurdy, and Andrew Cramby [Crambie], burgess of Edinburgh, on a dispute between the abbot and c
2 CONC onvent of Scone and Thomas Wardropar [Wardrop] of Gothnys, over the peatmoss of Arnebothy. Dated at Turfhill [Turfhills], 30 July 1483. The abbot was accompanied by friars John Peblis [Peebles], Patrick Small, and John Boy (the ch
2 CONC amberlain, granitar and cellarer of the monastery), and by Henry Gulde [Guild, Gould] and John Quhiteheid [Whitehead], vicars of the parishes of Logyraitt [Logierait] and Rogortoun [Rogerton]. Witnesses: Thomas Blair, son and heir
2 CONC  apparent of said Alexander Blair; Patrick Haldane of Kelor [Keillor]; Mr. Henry Cramby [Crambie], vicar of Kilspindy [Kilspindie]; Thomas Peblis [Peebles], burgess of Perth; sir John Allanesone [Allanson], vicar of Kilbriny [?Kil
2 CONC birnie]; Alexander Habrahame [Abraham], chaplain; Andrew Bunche [Bunch]; Patrick Blair; David Blair in Banchory; John Tendell [Tindal]; William Peblis [Peebles]; George Small; Richard Grant; Bernard Allanesone [Allanson]; Thomas A
2 CONC llanesone [Allanson]; Thomas Robertsone [Robertson]; Gilbert Robertsone; Robert Eldar [Elder]; Patrick Roberstone; John Davidsone [Davidson]; Paul Patriksone [Patrickson]; Thomas Tod. Notary - John of Kynmonth [Kinmouth], diocese 
2 CONC of Dunkeld. Endorsed with a notarial instrument dated at Perth, [blank] 1540, narrating the supplication and grant. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD68%2f1%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=silvester+rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1542&di=n National Records of Scotland, Murray of Lintrose, reference GD68/1/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 September 1486: Bond by James Hering of Tuliboil to SILVESTER RETTRA OF THAT ILK granting warrandice on infeftment of Andrew Hering, his son and Janet of Rettra, spouse of said Andrew and daughter of said Silvester, in conjun
2 CONC ct fee, in the lands of the town of Clune whereby said James is to infeft said Andrew and Janet in £20 worth of land lying in the sheriffdom of Perth if the said lands of Clune be taken from by process of law, under penalty of 100
2 CONC 0 merks Scots. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f5%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=SILVESTER+RETTRA+OF+THAT+ILK&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of t
2 CONC he Earls of Airlie, GD16/5/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 January 1487-88: REX confirmavit cartam SILVESTRI RETHRAY DE EODEM, — [qua — pro filiali diloctione, etc., — concessit filio suo SILVESTRO RETTHRAY, heredibus ejus et assignatis,— terras de Balmakerd, vic. Perth : — Tenend. 
2 CONC a dicto Silv. seniore, de rege. Reddend. unum denarium argenti, nomine albe firme : — Test. Alex. Blair de Balthiok, And. Charteris do Cutilgurdy, Tho. Rottray, et Pat. Welles. Apud Perth 10 Dec. 1486. [https://archive.org/details
2 CONC /registrummagnisi02scot/page/358/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513, charter number 1699 on p. 358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 January 1487-88: Notarial copy by John Davidsone [Davidson], notary public, of charter of confirmation under the great seal of charter by SILVESTER RETTRAY OF THAT ILK to SILVESTER RETHRAY, his son, of the lands of Balnakerd
2 CONC , sheriffdom of Perth, dated 10 Dec. 1486. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD132%2f166&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers
2 CONC  of the Robertson Family of Lude, Perthshire, reference GD132/166]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 January 1490: Charter by Brother David Boyd Prior of the Convent of the above Blackfriars of Perth with consent of said Convent to SIR SYLVESTER RATTRAY OF RATTRAY knight of a South tenement on the North Side of the Road lead
2 CONC ing to the common lead. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD79%2f1%2f33&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sylvester+rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1542&di=n National Records of Scotland, Reco
2 CONC rds of King James VI Hospital, Perth, Blackfriars, reference GD79/1/33]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 February 1491-92: REX confirmavit cartam Margarete Ogilby sponse SILVESTRI RETTRA DE EODEM militis, — [qua, — amore filiali, etc., ac cum consensu sponsi sui, — concessit filio suo SILVESTRi RETTRA, et ALISONE HEPBURNE ejus s
2 CONC ponse, — terras de "Wemys, cum sale et carbonibus earundem, vic. Fiffe, — pro ejus servitiis : — Tenend. dictis Silvest. et Alis. et eorum alteri diutius viventi et heredibus eorum inter ipsos legitime procreatis, quibus deficient
2 CONC ibus, heredibus legitimis et propinquioribus ipsius Silvestri sponsi dicte Marg. quibuscunque, a dicta Marg. de rege : — Reservato libero tenemento dicte Marg. : — Test. Joh. Hering de Wormot, Wil. Hering de Fornocht, Geo. Spens, 
2 CONC Hen. Quhite, et D. Joh. de Kynmonth capellano ac notario publico : — Apud Perth, 31 Maii 1491. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/440/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513, charter number 2081 on p. 440]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1492: INDEX IN LIBROS RESPONSIONUM. LIBER I. 1492. . . . . . Perth. Sa. Johanni Rettrey, Kynbachlo, Downy. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir10grea/page/772/mode/1up RSRS X: 772]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1493: Charter by SYLVESTER RATTRAY knight to Elizabeth Buttergask of a tenement on the West Side of the road leading to the Convent of the Blackfriars of Perth. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD79%2f1%2f35&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sylvester+rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1542&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of King James VI Hospital, Perth, Blackfriars, reference GD79/1/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 October 1495: Instrument narrating that Andrew Gray, son of Andrew, lord Gray bailie of John Haliburtoun of Gask, held a court before which letters, 8 Oct 1495, by Walter Cargill of Lasinestone renouncing a sixth part of land
2 CONC s of Kynrossy in barony of Culace, in sheriffdom of Perth, to which he was found to be entitled by a retour. Notary: Thomas Andrew, priest, diocese of St. Andrews. Witnesses to renunciation: James Moncur of Balluny, sir Alexander 
2 CONC Barnard, 'sallerare' of Cowper, sir James Rettra, vicar of Culace, Walter Cargill, granter's eme, Patrick Bunche and sir Thomas Andersone, chaplain and notary. Witnesses to instrument: JOHN RETTRA OF THAT ILK, Silvester Rettra, Th
2 CONC omas Chawmer, George Blare of Bendachie, Patrick Haldane of Kelore, Silvester Haldane, his heir, Walter Haldane, John Bissate, James Moncur of Balluny, William Gray, Patrick Gray, Adam Gray, David Gray, Robert Small, David Pettill
2 CONC ok, David Archar, James Archar, Adam Talyour, Donald Mog, John Pullour, David Elder, sir David Cochrane, John Pettillok priest, and James Rettra, notary and vicar of Culace. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/
2 CONC details.aspx?reference=GD181%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rettra&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1490&dt=1517&di=n National Records of Scotland, Aboyne Muniments, reference GD181/11]'''
2 CONT
