2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Rattray, of that ilk, who was knighted by James IV. He m. Elizabeth, dau. of James, second Lord Kennedy, and had three sons and one dau., viz.,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. John, a military officer, who m. Margaret Abercrombie, but d. in Holland before his father, without issue. 
2 CONT 2. Patrick, 3. Sylvester (both these successively heirs.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Grisel, m. to John Steward, third Earl of Athol. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 2
2 CONT  By John Burke, p. 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Rattray son of Sir Silvester was, as you can see by referring to the notes above, killed at the Battle of Flodden in 1513, along with a very large proportion of the other nobility of Scotland. In the confusion after this 
2 CONC the Earl of Atholl (John Stewart, Grizel RattrayÙus husband) claimed the Rattray land.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://histfam.familysearch.org/getperson.php?personID=I16340&tree=Dodge
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Knighted by King James IV in 1488. Appointed Bailie of Regality at Scone 1506. Killed at the Battle of Flodden in 1513. Married Elizabeth d/o 2nd Lord Kennedy, and secondly, Matilda Johnstoun. 
2 CONT *Dawn Stapylton-Adkins. ''James Rattray & His Descendants in South Africa'' 1822-1992, self-published, Cape Town, 1992
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_History_of_Blairgowrie/l2YLAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=sir+john+rattray+1513&pg=PA216&printsec=frontcover
2 CONT
