1 DEAT
2 DATE 1562
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR WALTER OGILVIE OF BOYNE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 July 1526: Charter by which James V, king of Scots, confirms possession of the lands of Ardinboith, Bogtoun and Reidhicht, located in the Thanedome of Boyne and sheriffdom of Banff, to WALTERO OGILVY of Boyne, and CRISTINE K
2 CONC EITH his spouse. The lands in question had previously been resigned by Walter in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his wife. The land in question was to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and their la
2 CONC wful heirs, whom failing by Walter's nearest heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/74/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 327]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 January 1542-43: Charter by which Mary, Queen of Scots, confirms possession of the lands, barony and thaneage of Boyne, to WALTERO OGILVY of Boyne, and CRISTINE KEITH his wife. The lands in question had previously been resig
2 CONC ned by Walter in order to obtain a new grant to himself and his wife. The land in question was to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and by their lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest heirs of Walter Ogilvy of 
2 CONC Boyne.
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/670/mode/1up RMS1513-46: charter number 2857]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1545: Charter by which Mary, Queen of Scots, confirms possession of the lands of Baldavy, located in the sheriffdom of Banff, to SIR WALTERO OGILVY OF BOYNE and CRISTINE KEITH his wife. The land in question, which had 
2 CONC previously been resigned by John Ogilvy of Durny, was to be held by Walter and his wife in conjunct fee and liferent, and by their lawful male heirs, whom failing by Walter's nearest heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrumma
2 CONC gnisi03scot/page/725/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 3092]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1556: Charter by which Mary, Queen of Scots, confirms possession of the lands of Baldavy, located in the barony of Monbray (Moubray) and sheriffdom of Banff, to WALTERO OGYLVY, second son of Sir Walter Ogylvy of Boyne,
2 CONC  to be held by him and his lawful male heirs, who failing by the nearest heirs of Walter Ogiylvy, senior. The land in question had previously been resigned by Walter, senior, and his wife Cristina Keyth, who reserved their respect
2 CONC ive liferent interest. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/243/mode/1up RMS: 1546-80: charter number 1095]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 March 1575-76: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms possession of various lands in the thanedom of Boyne, including the manor of Craig of Boyne, to George Ogilwie of Dunl
2 CONC ugus, and his heirs and assignees. The King's charter of confirmation followed upon a judgement made against Alexander Ogilwie of Boyne in the sheriff court of Banff, in respect of debts incurred by him which amounted to 17,994 po
2 CONC unds,17 shillings and 8 pence. The lands conveyed were burdened with the liferent interests of Lady Christine Keith [Note], and it was the King's wish that the lands in question could be reclaimed by Alexander Ogilwie of Boyne and
2 CONC  his heirs and assigns, providing that the outstanding debts were paid within seven years. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/683/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 2535]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It would appear that Lady Christine Keith was still alive on 20 March 1575-76.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
