1 NAME Sir William Gordon of Schivas & of Gight
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1466
2 PLAC Huntly 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 SEP 1513
2 PLAC Battle of Flodden
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from the third son, Sir William, ancestor of the Gordons of Gight, the mother of Lord Byron was descended.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Gordon died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, killed in action.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly and Lady Annabella Stewart.1 He was ancestor of the Gordons of Gight.1 He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He had the lands of Aboyne and he exchanged these with his brother Adam for the lands of Gight.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # Janet Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy, of Boyne, b. est 1455 & Margaret Edmonstone 
2 CONT
2 CONT    Children 
2 CONT # Catherine Gordon.  Married James Innes, of Crommey 
2 CONT #  John Gordon.  Married Marjory Gordon.
2 CONT #  George Gordon, of Gight, b. Abt 1502.  Married Elizabeth Gordon, of Fetterletter 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
