1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CATHERINE GORDON (aka KATHARINE GORDOUN)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catherine Gordon, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Gordon/6000000097021743967
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1540: (Copy) feu charter by Patrick, bishop of Moray and commendator of Scone, to James Innes of Rothnakingye and Katharine Gordoun (Gordon), his spouse, in conjunct fee, of the lands of Fynrasie occupied by Elizabet
2 CONC h Troup, relict of the deceased Duncan Suthirland (Sutherland), in the barony and regality of Spynie and sheriffdom of Elgin, reserving the Bischope-moss or Laverokis-moss, for a yearly payment of 10 merks and certain victual. Dat
2 CONC ed at the cathedral of Elgin. Witnesses: Mr. John Douglas, vicar of Glastoun, Mr. Hugh Cragye (Craigie), chaplain of the cathedral of Elgin, and sir Thomas Hay, vicar of Duffous. The copy is certified by John Annand, notary public
2 CONC . [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD96%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=katharine+Gordoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Sinclair family of Me
2 CONC y, Caithness, reference GD96/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
