1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME ALISON HOME ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Alison Hume (1516) Alison Home (1517) Alison Hume (1535) Alison Hume (1538) Alison Home (1541) Alison Home (1541-42) Alisona Hume (1549) Alison Home (1550) Dame Alison Hume (1552) Alisone Hume (1556) dame Helen [Ali
2 CONC son] Home (1557) Alisona Hume (1557)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Alison Home, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Cuthbert-Home-of-Fastcastle/6000000000405427935?through=6000000007980701262 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Martin/60000000079809
2 CONC 70489?through=6000000007980701262. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f432&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alison+home&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD89/1/432]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 July 1516: Retour in favour of Alison Hume as heir to her father, Cuthbert Hume of Fastcastell, in the lands of Hutoun, Raufburn and Nesbitschelle in the earldom of March and Hornedane. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2743&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alison+hume&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2743]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''July 1517: (Extract) Submission by James, earl of Mortoun, on the one part, and Elizabeth Martyne, for herself and as tutrix to Elizabeth, Katherine and Alison Home, her daughters, as heirs to deceased Cuthbert H. of Fastcastel
2 CONC l, their father, and deceased Patrick H. thereof, their grandfather, on the other part, to Mr. Gavin Dunbar, archdeacon of St. Andrews, clerk register, Mr. Thomas Halkerstoun, provost of Creichtoun, and Mr. Patrick Covintre, [dean
2 CONC  of Restalrig], as arbiters on the claims by said Elizabeth and her daughters in a summons raised against said Earl regarding the spoliation of the maills and profits of said lands of Blyth during three years and one term and the 
2 CONC wrongous withholding of 40 merks and £20 due by deceased John, earl of Mortoun, father of said James. Dated 8 and recorded in the Books of Council, 17 July, 1517. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD89%2f1%2f432&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alison+home&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirling, reference GD89/1/432]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1535-36: Crown charter of confirmation of a charter, 3 Oct 1535, by John, Earl of Buchan, to Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, kt and to Alison Hume, his spouse, in conjunct fee of the lands of Fortry (Fortrie), with mills a
2 CONC nd multures, in the barony of Glendowachy, Banffshire. Witnesses: George Bard of Ardinhuffis; William Stewart in Todlaw; Robert Dun of Rate; Sir John Roberti, vicar of Fordyce and Master Alexander Currour (Curror), notary. Crown w
2 CONC itnesses: Gavin, Archbishop of Glasgow, Chancellor; George, Bishop of Dunkeld; Henry, Bishop of Whithorn and of the Chapel Royal, Stirling; Archibald, Earl of Argyll, Lord Campbell and Lorne, master of the king's household; Hugh, 
2 CONC Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery; Malcolm, Lord Fleming, Chamberlain; Patrick, Prior of St Andrews; David, Abbot of Arbroath, keeper of the Privy Seal; James Colville of East Wemyss, kt, comptroller and director of chancery; Mast
2 CONC er James Foulis of Colinton, clerk of the rolls, register and of council. Tag, no seal. [RMS, iii 1538] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f3617&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alison+
2 CONC hume&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/3617]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 April 1538: Letters of inspection under quarter seal of tack, 26 March 1537, by Margaret, queen of Scotland, to Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, her friend and servitor, and Alison Hume, his spouse, of lands, lordship and barony of
2 CONC  Cockburnspath, viz. the Bowscheill, Paddocleuch, Rauchanside, in sheriffdom of Berwick, for 19 years.
2 CONT Witnesses to tack: Mr Alexander Turing, provost of Methven, queen's secretary, Mr Thomas Kerre and sir Henry Adare, chaplain and notary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f8%2f7%
2 CONC 2f1-11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alison+hume&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/8/7/1-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 April 1541: Banffshire: Confirmation by the provosts of Methven and Seton, as papal judges delegate, of feu charter by the abbot and convent of Coupar to Sir Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugas and Alison Home, spouses, of the lands of
