1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 6. Lady Agnes Gordon, mar. James Ogilvy, Yr of Deskford and Findlater (dvp. 1 Feb 1505/6), 1st son and heir ap. of Sir James Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater by his first wife Margaret Innes, dau. of Sir Robert Inn
2 CONC es, 11th of that Ilk, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT # Alexander Ogilvy, of Deskford, Findlater and Ogilvy
2 CONT # James Ogilvy
2 CONT # John Ogilvy
2 CONT # Patrick Ogilvy
2 CONT # George Ogilvy
2 CONT # Elizabeth Ogilvy
2 CONT
2 CONT Also seen is daughter Margaret Ogilvy [Ogilvie], of Findlater family 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd married Agnes Gordon 5  td 15 2m. Gilbert Hay of Kilmallock [http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/british/gg/gordon02.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Douglas Hickling, 2003, as quoted in [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=maclaren&id=I03699 Rootsweb database]
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Probably the last and most authoritative word on Annabella's children as the Countess of Huntly belongs to Alison Weir in BRITAIN'S ROYAL FAMILIES, at 232. She regards Isabel as the only probable child of Annabella's marriage to
2 CONC  the earl. She says that "Annabella was also possibly, but improbably," the mother of Janet, Elizabeth, Margaret, and Agnes.  ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://kittybrewster.com/ancestry/gordon.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT George 2nd Earl of Huntly had illegitimate children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * L.	Alexander Gordon. Had letters of legitimation in Oct 1500.		
2 CONT * M.	Agnes Gordon. Married James Ogilvy of Findlater.		
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00116721&tree=LEO
2 CONT * http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/huntly1445.htm
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I29730&tree=CC												
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/528/mode/2up The Scots Peerage Vol IV] page 531.  "The second Earl also had a natural son, Alexander, who had letters of legitimation 8 October 1500.  Also a natural da
2 CONC ughter Agnes, married to James Ogilvy of Findlater.". Comment: Leo van de Pas has the name of the natural daughter as '''Margaret''' with a birth date about 1470, not 1480.
2 CONT # Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, London, 1938, Reference: Page 2203 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============================
2 CONT
2 CONT m. James Ogilvy; mother of Alexander who m. Janet Abernethy. [Richard Hodgson <ancestorsearch@talk21.com]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dau of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly; m. Sir Gilbert Hay. [Paul Moynagh <pmoynagh@argonet.co.uk, 19 May 2002]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dau of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly, and Lady Elizabeth Hay; m. James Ogilvy of Deskford. They are ancestors of Lady Diana Spencer and Sarah Ferguson. [Leo van de Pas <leovdpas@iinet.net.au, 7 Apr 2001]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.thepeerage.com/p32943.htm#i329430 thepeerage.com]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Agnes Gordon is the daughter of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly and Lady Elizabeth Hay.1 She married James Ogilvy, 3rd of Deskford and Findlater, son of Sir James Ogilvy, 2nd of Deskford and Findlater and Margaret Innes.1 H
2 CONC er married name became Ogilvy.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Agnes Gordon married James Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater, son of Sir James Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater and Margaret Innes.1
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the daughter of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly and Lady Elizabeth Hay.1 Her married name became Ogilvy.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Agnes Gordon and James Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater
2 CONT
