1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER OGILVY OF THAT ILK AND FINDLATER ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''In the charter creating the barony of Ogilvy Alexander Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater is designed of Deskford, but for the remainder of his life he is usually designed as Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk. [https://arc
2 CONC hive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/20/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 20]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 September 1519: Mutual bond of friendship between Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk and Walter Ogilvy, his eme, of Baddinspink. In the vernacular. Signed by Alexander Ogilvy. Trace of applied seal. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.go
2 CONC v.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f8%2f6%2f1-11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and
2 CONC  Birkenbog, reference GD185/8/6/1-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 Mat 1523: Instrument narrating that George Abircromby [Abercromby] of Petmathane [Pitmeddan] and George Bard [Baird] of Ordinhuff, with consent of their lords superior, agreed on boundaries between lands of Classindamer, bel
2 CONC onging to said George Abercromby, and lands of Ordinhuff, belonging to said George Baird, boundaries having been marked. Notary: Patrick Duncanson [Duncan]. Witnesses: Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, Walter Ogilvy of Baddinspink, Ge
2 CONC orge Crafurd [Crawford], heir apparent of William Crafurd [Crawford] of Fernat [?Fedderat], John Ogilvy, brother german of said Alexander, William Abircromby, William Bard [Baird], John Davidsoun, John Smyth [Smith]. Seal of Georg
2 CONC e Bard [Baird] of Ordihuff, on tag. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f1%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Record
2 CONC s of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/1/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 October 1525: Deputation by Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk, Sheriff of Aberdeen, to George Bisset, Mair, of fee of the said Sheriffdom to infeft Robert Forbes of Echt as heir to his grandfather in the lands of Tullyfoure, Tully
2 CONC boy, Tullyoicht, Auchtereicht, Vauchterdaill and Brimhill with the mill thereof, in terms of Crown Precept dated 14th September of 12th year of Reign. Dated at Aberdeen. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/deta
2 CONC ils.aspx?reference=GD42%2fA%2f60&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Viscount Cowdray (Dunecht papers), reference GD42/A/60]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 May 1528: Discharge by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk of all profits of court and jurisdiction of bailiery of Forest of Boyne within bounds belonging to Walter Ogilvy of Monycabok, notwithstanding his letter of bailiery of the
2 CONC  same made to granter. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f34%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotlan
2 CONC d, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/34/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 September 1532: harter by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk to Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, of various burgh lands in territory of royal burgh of Banff [specified]. Seal on tag. With sasine following. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.g
2 CONC ov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f8%2f7%2f1-11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen an
2 CONC d Birkenbog, reference GD185/8/7/1-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 September 1532: Letters of reversion by William Bard, son and apparent heir of George Bard of Ordinghufe, with consent of said George, to Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, granter's master, over lands of Sandlawche, with salmon 
2 CONC fishing on water of Doverne, in barony of Ogilvy, sheriffdom of Banff, under redemption of 600 merks scots paid on high altar of parish kirk of Banff, with letter of tack and bailiery of said lands for 19 years immediately followi
2 CONC ng, 'blud & thifte excepte'.Two tags; fragment of one seal. Witnesses: Mr Alexander Ogilvy in Glashalche, James Ogilvy of Cullard, Alexander Litilghone, David Ballie and sir Thomas Wallas, chaplain and notary. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f11%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forgl
2 CONC en and Birkenbog, reference GD185/11/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 October 1532: Letters of reversion by Alexander Ogilby in Balcrage and Christine Irwyne, his spouse, to Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, who has sold to them his lands of Bawchlaw and a barrel of salmon of fishing of the same, i
2 CONC n water of Duverne, in barony of Ogilvy, sheriffdom of Banff, on payment of 500 merks to be paid on high altar of parish church of Banff, with a tack thereof for one year immediately after redemption, on 40 days warning to be made
2 CONC  in parish kirk of Innerbondy on a solemn day in time of high mass, or personally. Witnesses: John Thomson, William Fenton, sir Andrew Scherwynd, sir William Hay, sir John Facher, chaplains, and sir Thomas Wallas, chaplain and not
2 CONC ary public. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f11%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/11/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1534: Charter of Sale by Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk, whereby, in consideration of certain sums of money paid to him by Patrick Chene of Essilmond, he grants to him his fishing of the Water of Ithane, with pertinents, be
2 CONC ginning at the Matharfurd and from thence ascending to the Sekfurd of Five, lying in the sheriffdom of Abirdene: To be held de me for payment of £30 Scots of feu-farm at Lammas; with clause of warrandice. At Edinburgh, 1 May 1534.
2 CONC  Witnesses, Mr. Alexander Ogilvy in Glashauch, William Bard, son and apparent heir of George Bard of Ardinhuif, Andrew Harvy and Mr. Laurence Chene, notary public. (Signed) Alexr. Ogyluy off that Ilk. Seal gone. [https://catalogue
2 CONC .nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f102&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD8
2 CONC 6/102]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1534: Precept of Sasine by Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk, addressed to Mr. William Chene, his bailie in that part, for infefting Patrick Chene of Essilmond in the fishing of the Water of Ithane in terms of the charter GD86
2 CONC /102. Same date, place and witnesses as the charter GD86/102. (Signed) Alexr. Ogyluy off that Ilk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f103&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogil
2 CONC vy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/103]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1536-37: Decreet arbitral pronounced by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, arbiter chosen between George Abercromby of Petmeddene, on one part, and Mr Alexander Ogilvy in Glasshaugh, on other part, dispute being over a '
2 CONC ward' [small piece of pasture ground] claimed to belong to lands of Cultane [Mr Alexander] or to lands of Deskford [George Abercromby]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f1%2f11-
2 CONC 14&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), reference GD185/1/11-14]'''
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 May 1536: Writs of Milntoun of Keith. Feu-charter by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk in favour of George Ogilvy and Janet Ogilvy, his spouse, 15 May 1536. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD248%2f3439%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), reference GD248/3439/3]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 July 1536: Deed of Submission by George Abercroomy of Petmedene and Mr. Alexander Ogilvy, in Glassaeht, of their dispute to the deliverance of Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD103%2f2%2f52&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y Papers of Society of Antiquaries of Scotland, reference GD103/2/52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 September 1539: Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk, in favour of Patrick Chene de Essilmond and Isobel Bad, his spouse, of fishing of Ithan from Machar ford to the Sek ford of Pyvie. Dated at: Fordyce. [https://catalogue.nrscotlan
2 CONC d.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH1%2f2%2f352&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous Transcripts Etc., Individual Docume
2 CONC nts, reference RH1/2/352]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    14
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 September 1539: Charter of Resignation by Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk granting to Patrick Chene of Essilmond and Isobel Bad, his spouse, and the longer liver of them in conjunct infeftment, and the heirs lawfully procreated
2 CONC  or to be procreated between them, whom failing to the heirs of the said Patrick whomsover, the fishing of the Water of Ithan, described in GD86/102, which he personally resigned into the hands of the granter at Fordyce: To be hel
2 CONC d de me, rendering therefor £30 Scots of feu-farm annually at Lammas: with clause of warrandice. At Fordyce 13th September 1539. Witnesses, Mr. Alexander Galloway, rector of Kinkill, Mr. James Wawane, rector of Oyne, John Ogilvy o
2 CONC f Durno, George Abircromy of Pettmedden, Mr. Alexander Ogilvy of Glassaucht, Sir John Robertsone, vicar of Fordyce, and Mr. Alexander Hay, notary public. (Signed) Alexr. Ogyluy off that Ilk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f120&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/120]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    15
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 September 1539: Precept of Sasine by Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk addressed to Robert Graye, his bailie in that part, for infefting Patrick Chene of Essilmond and Isobel Bad, his spouse, in the fishing of the Water of Ithane
2 CONC  in terms of the preceding charter. At Fordice 13th September 1539. (Signed) Alexr. Ogyluy off that Ilk. In dorso: "The second precept of the Watter of Ythan". [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?r
2 CONC eference=GD86%2f121&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sor William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/121]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    16
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1541-42: Writs of lands of Sandlaw, in sheriffdom of Banff, disponed by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk to Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, his grandson, and to Alison Home, his spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecata
2 CONC logue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f9%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), refer
2 CONC ence GD185/9/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    17
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1542: Privy seal letters in favour of Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk confirming licence to him to dispone lands of Brawchhill with fishings on water of Doverne in sheriffdom of Banff. Seal on tongue. [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f9%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilvy family, Earls of Seafi
2 CONC eld (Seafield Papers), reference GD185/9/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    18
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 March 1545-46: At Huntly. Contract between Sir Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, kt, and Thomas Baird of Burnesid, advised by George, earl of Huntly, Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk and of Fynletter, and George Gordon of Schewes, wher
2 CONC eby said Walter is to require Alexander Baird, son and heir of deceased William Baird of Sandlauche, and said Thomas, his tutor, to compear in parish kirk of Banff and receive 600 merks and a letter of tack and bailiery of said la
2 CONC nds of Sandlauch for 19 years, etc. Signed by both parties. Seal damaged on tag. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f9%2f7%2f1-22&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+th
2 CONC at+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/9/7/1-22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    19
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 November 1546: Copy agreement between George Abercromby, franktenementar of Galcors, and Mr Alexander Ogilvy, feuar of Glasshauche, whereby they are to abide by decreet arbitral to be given by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, R
2 CONC obert, bishop of Orkney, Walter Ogilvy of Dunlugus, kt, Mr William Gordon, parson of Duthell, and William Stewart of Todlaw, to recognosce upon alleged deliverance between the parties made by Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, 23 Febru
2 CONC ary 1536/7, and mediation made by him, last February 1541/2, concerning claims between lands of Galcors and Glasshauch. Witnesses: Alexander Ogilvy of that ilk, Mr Adam Gordon of Lethestoun, Mr James Dunbar, parson of Cumnock, Jam
2 CONC es Ogilvy in Cullan and Mr John Nicholls.
2 CONT Attested by Mr George Duncanson [Duncani], notary. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f1%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Alexander+Ogilvy+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1546&di=y
2 CONC  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of Forglen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/1/19]'''
2 CONT
