0 @I6000000007980630749@ INDI
1 NAME Patrick /Gordon of Methlick and Haddo/ second Laird of Haddo
2 GIVN Patrick
2 SURN Gordon of Methlick and Haddo
2 NSFX second Laird of Haddo
2 _MARNM Gordon of Methlick and Haddo
1 SEX M
1 OCCU Laird of Methlick and Haddo, ancestor of the Earls of Aberdeen
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage 1899
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ukga.org/browse.php?action=ViewRec&DB=33&bookID=224&page=bp189900148
2 CONT
2 CONT The House of Gordon, by J. M. Bulloch, 1903
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/houseofgordon01bulluoft/houseofgordon01bulluoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT The Genealogie of James Gordon of Methlick or Haddoe the third son of Jock begotten on the Knight of Gights daughter Maitland his Lawfull Wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The said James Gordon purchased [His wife was Canea Harper "half portioner of Methlick" of which her father "Johannes de Citharista " was the owner ; James G. or his son acquired the other half of the barony, and thus arose the Go
2 CONC rdons of Haddo 1 ] the Lands of Methlick and thereafter the Lands of Haddo being the first Laird thereof. He married Anna Harper (sic!) w l whom he begat four sons and four daughters, viz, his eldest son Patrick Gordon Laird of Ha
2 CONC ddo, Robert Gordon of Fetterletter, Mr Alexander Gordon first Chancellor of Murray and Chanery of Ross and thereafter Bishop of Aberdeen, and George Gordon of Achenniff in Buchan ; his eldest daughter married the Laird of Allardes
2 CONC , the Second married Eraser Laird of , the third married Andrew Prott Burgess in Aberdeen, the fourth married George Gray Burgess in Aberdeen. Their father dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His eldest son Patrick Gordon second Laird of Haddo married the Laird of Findlater's Daughter Ogilvy''' with whom he begat three sons and three daughters,viz, his eldest Son George Gordon third Laird of Haddo, Mr James Gordon P
2 CONC arson of Lonmey, and Alexander Gordon first Goodman of Bracoe ; his eldest Daughter married the Laird of Towie Forbes, another married the Laird of Altar Gumming, the third married the Goodman of Blairy or Kilravoch Dunbar. Their 
2 CONC father the said Patrick dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest son George Gordon third Laird of Haddoe married the Laird of Delgaties daughter Hay, with whom he begat his eldest son James Gordon fourth Laird of Haddo. His father the said George dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT His Son said James Gordon fourth Laird of Haddoe married Gilbert Menzies Provost of Aberdeens Daughter, with whom he begat five sons
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p12082.htm#i120819
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Gordon of Methlic and Haddo was the son of James Gordon of Methlic and Haddo.2 He married Marion Oglivie of Findlater.1 He died from 1531 to 2 March 1534.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also known as James Gordon of Methlic and Haddo.2 On 19 April 1475 he had seisin of Methlic as son and heir.1 In 1481 he obtained a charter under the Great Seal from King James III.2 In 1505 he obtained a charter under the 
2 CONC Great Seal from King James IV.2 In 1514 he obtained a charter under the Great Seal from King James V.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Patrick Gordon of Methlic and Haddo and Marion Oglivie of Findlater
2 CONT
2 CONT George Gordon+2 d. b 1531
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon of Braco+1
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Gordon3
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Gordon4
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149729635/patrick-gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Gordon BIRTH	unknown DEATH	1531 Scotland BURIAL	 Methlick Churchyard Methlick, Aberdeenshire, Scotland MEMORIAL ID	149729635 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Marion Ogilvy, daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Findlater.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Photo	 James Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Photo	 George Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT To the memory of the GORDONS of Methlic & Haddo & especially PATRICK GORDON of Methlick who fell fighting for King James the Second of Scotland at the Battle of Brechin 18 May 1452 & of his son JAMES GORDON of Methlick; also PATRI
2 CONC CK GORDON of Methlic & Archadlie (died 1531) son of aforesaid JAMES & of his son & heir GEORGE who predeceased his father, JAMES GORDON of Methlic, Archadlie & at Branchlaw & Haldane, son of the aforesaid GEORGE GORDON, a faithful
2 CONC  adherent of Mary Queen of Scots - of him it is recorded that he bigged a house called Kelly. He died 1582. Also of his wife MARJORY sister of Sir Thomas Menzies of Pitfodels, comptroller of Scotland & and of his son & heir PATRIC
2 CONC K GORDON who predeceased his father & of his wife AGNES FRASER dau of Andrew Fraser of Muchill. JAMES GORDON of Methlick, Haddo, Tarves EIC son of aforesaid Patrick Gordon d Nov 1642 & of his wife JEAN dau of William, Lord Keith, 
2 CONC Earl Marischal & of his son & heir GEORGE GORDON d 1610 & of his wife MARGARET dau of Sir Alexander Bannerman of Elsick.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Methlick branch is as folows, not to be  confused with Coclarachie branch
2 CONT
2 CONT * PATRICK GORDON of Methlick who fell fighting for King James the Second of Scotland at the Battle of Brechin 18 May 1452 
2 CONT ** 1 JAMES GORDON of Methlick 
2 CONT *** 11 PATRICK GORDON of Methlic & Archadlie (died 1531), m - Ogilvy 
2 CONT **** 111 GEORGE who predeceased his father (dvp), m - above mentioned daugher of Alexander Hay (NOT GEORGE of COCLARACHIE, who married!)
2 CONT ***** 1111 JAMES GORDON of Methlic, Archadlie & at Branchlaw & Haldane, son of the aforesaid GEORGE GORDON, a faithful adherent of Mary Queen of Scots - of him it is recorded that he bigged a house called Kelly. He died 1582, m - 
2 CONC MARJORY sister of Sir Thomas Menzies of Pitfodels, comptroller of Scotland 
2 CONT ******11111 PATRICK GORDON who predeceased his father & of his wife AGNES FRASER dau of Andrew Fraser of Muchill 
2 CONT ******* 111111 JAMES GORDON of Methlick, Haddo, Tarves EIC son of aforesaid Patrick Gordon d Nov 1642 & of his wife JEAN dau of William, Lord Keith, Earl Marischal 
2 CONT ******** 1111111 GEORGE GORDON d 1610 & of his wife MARGARET dau of Sir Alexander Bannerman of Elsick
