4 CONT To the memory of the GORDONS of Methlic & Haddo & especially PATRICK GORDON of Methlick who fell fighting for King James the Second of Scotland at the Battle of Brechin 18 May 1452 & of his son JAMES GORDON of Methlick; also PATRI
4 CONC CK GORDON of Methlic & Archadlie (died 1531) son of aforesaid JAMES & of his son & heir GEORGE who predeceased his father, JAMES GORDON of Methlic, Archadlie & at Branchlaw & Haldane, son of the aforesaid GEORGE GORDON, a faithful
4 CONC  adherent of Mary Queen of Scots - of him it is recorded that he bigged a house called Kelly. He died 1582. Also of his wife MARJORY sister of Sir Thomas Menzies of Pitfodels, comptroller of Scotland & and of his son & heir PATRIC
4 CONC K GORDON who predeceased his father & of his wife AGNES FRASER dau of Andrew Fraser of Muchill. JAMES GORDON of Methlick, Haddo, Tarves EIC son of aforesaid Patrick Gordon d Nov 1642 & of his wife JEAN dau of William, Lord Keith, 
4 CONC Earl Marischal & of his son & heir GEORGE GORDON d 1610 & of his wife MARGARET dau of Sir Alexander Bannerman of Elsick. Sir JOHN GORDON of Haddo son of the aforesaid George Gordon created Barton of Scotland in reward for his serv
4 CONC ices 1642. Second in Command of King Charles I forces in the North, was taken prisoner by the Covenanters under the Marquis of Argyll at his house of Kelly 6 May 1644 & was beheaded at the Market Cross at Edinburgh and was buried 
4 CONC in the Greyfriars Churchyard and of his wife MARY dau of Sir William Forbes of Tolquhoun.
4 CONT Gravesite Details Cenotaph - Inscription on top of the coping of the Gordon enclosure.
