2 CONT Grant of Freuchie, Laird Earl James Sheumas Nan Creach of the Forays The PEDIGREE of James (3rd of Freuchie) GRANT
2 CONT
2 CONT (1st of ROTHIEMURCHUS; 'of the Forays') Born: abt. 1483 Died: 1553 Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland AFN TK19-GR Name Sheumas Nan Creach (James Of The Forays) Died 26 Aug 1553 Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland Buried Duthil, I
2 CONC nverness-shire, Scotland IDENTITY: Called Sheumas nan Creach (James of the Forays). He was retoured heir to his father in Freuchie, with its castle and fortalice and other lands, in 1536 and 1539. On 27 July 1545 he purchased the 
2 CONC lands of Estir Urquhil (Easter Urquhart) and Cantradoun, within the barony of Clawach (Clava), in the sheriffdom of Nairn. On 23 April 1545, at Elgin, he excambed the lands of Easier Urquhart and others with Alexander Dolas of Can
2 CONC tray for the lands of Rothieimurchus. On 4 May 1548 Queen Mary granted him various lands in Lochalsh aud Lochcarron.  KINSHIP: 1st son. CHURCH: Made bailie of the Abbey of Kinloss before 20 Jun 1544. ASSIGNMENTS: One of those who 
2 CONC signed the Secret Bond by Cardinal Beaton and others, which was directed against the designs of our awid enymyis of Ingland against Queen Mary and the Queen-Regent. TITLES: Laird of Freuchie. PROPERTY: Retoured heir to his father 
2 CONC in Freuchie, with its castle and fortalice and other lands 1536, 1539. PROPERTY: He with his wife Christian Barclay were granted Knockando, Glencumrie and Brodland in the parish of Knockando by Alexander Douglas, Chaplain of St. A
2 CONC ndrews (Knockando) with consent of the dean and chapter of Moray 1545. PROPERTY: He purchased the lands of Estir Urquhil (Easter Urquhart) and Cantradoun, within the barony of Clawach (Clava), in the sheriffdom of Nairn 1545. PROP
2 CONC ERTY: He excambed the lands of Easter Urquhart for the lands of Rothiemurachus 1545. PROPERTY: Queen Mary granted him various lands in Lochalsh and Lochcarron 1548. BURIAL: Buried by his own testamentary direction in the Parish Ch
2 CONC urch of Duthil. PROBATE: Testament. Elizabeth Forbes Children 1. William Grant, b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland d. Bef 22 Dec 1560 Married: 1x 2. Duncan Grant, d. Oct 1580 + 3. Isabel Grant, b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, M
2 CONC oray, Scotland  Married: 1x 4. Margaret Grant,  + 5. Janet Grant Married: 3x3x , b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland d. 17-31 Oct 1600 Married: 1x 6. Agnes Grant, d. Yes, date unknown + 7. John Grant, 4th of Freuchie Marrie
2 CONC d: 3x3x , b. Abt 1522, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland  d. 3 Jun 1585, Ballachastel (Age ~ 63 years) Family ID F8813 Group Sheet
2 CONT
