1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER ABERCROMBIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 September 1472: Instrument of resignation by Agnes Johnstoun [Johnston], wife of Alexander Abircromy [Abercromby], laird of Ley, in hands of Thomas, bishop of Aberdeen, of lands of Ditouch and Braco, in lordship of Galcholis
2 CONC , sheriffdom of Banff, for new infeftment in favour of herself and her said spouse, and of Alexander Abircromy [Abercromby], their son, and Jonet Ogilvy, daughter of James Ogilvy of Deskfurde [Deskford], his [future] spouse. Notar
2 CONC y: Robert Leis [Lees], priest, Aberdeen diocese. Procurator: Walter Ogilvy of Auchlevin.
2 CONT Witnesses; Thomas [Spens]. bishop of Aberdeen, sirs and masters Duncan Lichtoun [Lichton], chancellor, Robert Stewart, archdeacon, Andrew Liel [Lyell], treasurer, Thomas Waus [Vaus] and John Myrtoun [Myrton], canons of Aberdeen. [
2 CONC https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD185%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1520&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Abercromby Family of For
2 CONC glen and Birkenbog, reference GD185/1/1]''''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT √ Burke's Peerage - page 7 Volume 1 107th edition
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Alexander Abercromby; m Marjorie Mowat and d by 2 May 1505,"
