2 CONT >>b1c2 https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=303610207620004050 x https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Bruce-Baroness-of-O-Lack/303610207620004050?through=6000000003435018681
2 CONT
2 CONT ====From the [https://archive.org/stream/collectionstowar1868clac/collectionstowar1868clac_djvu.txt2 Charters of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8th March, 1428'''— Charter of Confirmation of John Bruce of Rate and Clackmannan, ratifying and confirming the Charter  No. 9, granted by his grandfather, Robert de Bruys, to his son Thomas de Bruys, of the lands of Wester Ken
2 CONC net, &c. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22d Dec, 1447'''— Discharged by John de Bruce of Clackmannan to his eldest cousin, David, the Bruce of the Kennet, of the sum of 50 merks money of Scotland, addebted to the said John the Bruce, by Peter the Bruce, grandfather o
2 CONC f the above-mentioned David. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26th March 1473'''— Crown Charter of Resignation and Confirmation by King James III., to David Bruce, son, and apparent heir to John Bruce of Clackmannan, of the lands and Barony of Clackmannan and pertinents thereof, lying in 
2 CONC the county of Clackmannan, and the lands and Barony of Rait lying in the county of Perth, proceeding on the Procuratory of Resignation, granted by the said John Bruce. To be holden by the above mentioned David Bruce, his heirs of 
2 CONC the King, and his successors in fee and heritage for payment, and performance of services used and wont ; but reserving to the said John Bruce his liferent of the said Baronies, 
2 CONT and the third thereof to Elizabeth Stewart, his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20th March 1478'''— Charter by David Bruce of Clackmannan to Andrew Meffane and Margaret his spouse, of a tenement Yard and Croft with pasturage of a cow.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bruce of Clackmannan, for the purpose of insuring the recognition of his son David as the next proprietor, resigns his right to the King, who bestows it on David under reservation of John Bruce's liferent. The 1478 doc shows 
2 CONC that John Bruce died between 1473 and 1478, for David now exercises the full rights of a proprietor.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/collectionstowar1868clac/collectionstowar1868clac_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
2 CONT '''BRUCE,  EARLS  OF  ELGIN  AND AILESBURY''' [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/466/mode/1up?view=theater Balfour Paul, James, ed. (1906). The Scots Peerage, Vol. III. Edinburgh: David Douglas. pp. 467–468. 
2 CONC ISBN 0-9711966-2-1.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-Baron-of-Clackmannan/6000000001806579012?through=6000000168874433890 John  Bruce],  the  eldest  son,  succeeded  his  father,  before 23  May  1422,  when  he  appears  as  a  witness 3  to
2 CONC   a  notarial instrument  executed  at  Dunfermline ;  on  28  March  1428/  he ratified  and  confirmed  the  charter  of  2  May  1389  granted  by his  grandfather  Robert  De  Bruys  to  his  son  Thomas  de  Bruys of  the  la
2 CONC nds  of  Wester  Kennet,  and  on  24  September  1428 he  gave  sasine  to  Peter  de  Bruys  of  these  lands  to  which  he had  acquired  right  as  heir  to  his  father.  He  resigned  his estates  of  Clackmannan  and  Rait
2 CONC   in  favour  of  David  Bruis, his  son  and  heir,  reserving  his  own  liferent  and  a  reasonable terce  to  [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Stewart-of-Rossyth/6000000003435164456?through=6000000001806579012 Elizabeth
2 CONC   Stewart],  his  wife,  during  her  life- time, at  Edinburgh,  26  March  1473,  in  which  year  he died,  having  married  Elizabeth,  daughter  of  Sir  David Stewart  of  Rosyth,  by  whom  he  had  issue  two  sons,  viz. 
2 CONC : —
2 CONT 1.  Sir  David,  who  succeeded.
2 CONT 2.  Robert,  ancestor  of   the  Bruces  of   Cultmalundie  in Perthshire,  and  of  Muness  in  Zetland.
