1 NAME Elizabeth /Eglington/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Eglington
2 _MARNM Eglington
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1343
2 PLAC Eglinton Castle, Kilwinning, Ayrshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1398
2 PLAC Eglinton, Kilwinning, Ayr, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thepeerage.com/p26114.htm#i261137
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Eglinton1
2 CONT *F, #261137
2 CONT *Last Edited=13 Jan 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Eglinton is the daughter of Sir Hugh Eglinton of that Ilk and Egidia Stewart.1 She married John Montgomery.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Montgomery.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Eglinton and John Montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Montgomerie of Ardrossan+ d. fr 1426/27 - Nov 14291 
2 CONT
2 CONT unknown daughter Montgomery 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Montgomery 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Montgomery d. 5 Aug 13881 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1279. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peer
2 CONC age and Baronetage, 107th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Eglinton Castle was the home of the Eglinton family until it passed to John Alexander De Montgomery with his marriage to Elizabeth Eglinton abt 1350.  It then became the home of the Montgomery Clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=4KUHAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA10&ots=oWjZDUYsOS&dq=Fergus%20de%20Ardrossan&pg=PA10#v=onepage&q&f=true Page 10] of A genealogical account of the principal families in Ayrshire, more particulary [sic] in
2 CONC  Cunninghame By George Robertson.  1823.  “Ardrossan”
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Godfrey de Ardrossan, (son, it may be, of the preceding,) who is witness to an undated charter, in the reign of David II, to the Abbot of Kilwinning. To this charter, John Stewart of Periston also is witness; and this must ha
2 CONC ve been, after 1333, for James Stewart, the first of Periston, was that year killed at the battle of. Halidownhill; of course there could have been no John Stewart of Periston, till after that time. Should this Godfrey have been t
2 CONC he last male of the Ardrossans, it may be inferred that either his sister or his daughter carried this estate by marriage, (as Nisbet asserts, and as is otherwise known) to the Eglintons of Eglinton, from whence it came, not long 
2 CONC after, to the Montgomery family, by the marriage of Sir John Montgomery of Eagleshame, with Elisabeth, the heiress of Sir Hugh de Eglinton of 'that Ilk, about, or soon after 1360.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Eglinton-7
2 CONT
2 CONT  Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, Heiress of Eglington about 1343 in Eglinton Castle, Kilwinning, Ayrshire, Scotland. [1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was child of Sir Hugh by his first wife Agnes Mure, not daughter of Egidia [as originally published]. [Magna Charta Sureties] Note: This does not match the assigned parent.
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was married to John Montgomerie in 1361, Laird of Eaglesham. Renfrewshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT They have the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hugh Montgomerie[1][2]
2 CONT     John Montgomery[1][2]
2 CONT     Alexander Montgomery[1][2]
2 CONT     Hugh, this second Hugh was born after his older sibling of the same name was killed.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Other possible children:
2 CONT
2 CONT No sources have been found for these potential children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Joanna Demontgomerie
2 CONT     Anne Demontgomerie
2 CONT     Unknown daughter, who married a Maxwell[2]. While this person is in The Peerage and is the daughter of a John Montgomery of Eaglesham, it appears this is a different John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT     ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 Thomas Harrison Montgomery, A genealogical history of the family of Montgomery: including the Montgomery pedigree (Philadelphia: H. B. Ashmead, 1863), p. 47-51, digital images, https://archive.org/stream/
2 CONC genealogicalhist00mont#page/47/mode/1up/, The Internet Archive (https://archive.org : accessed 30 September 2019).
2 CONT     ↑ 2.0 2.1 2.2 2.3 2.4 "Elizabeth Eglinton", The Peerage, http://www.thepeerage.com/p26114.htm#i261137
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT     The Peerage: http://www.thepeerage.com/p26114.htm#i261137 
