1 NAME Isabella /Graham/
2 GIVN Isabella
2 SURN Graham
2 _MARNM Graham
2 NICK Lady Isabel Graham of Abercorn
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 ADDR
3 CITY Abercorn
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1325
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Seen as daughter of her brother https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Graham-of-Dalkeith-Abercorn-and-Eskdale/6000000026874295420?through=6000000006444108010 in some sources, which seems an error.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===ISABELLA GRAHAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/194/mode/2up The Scots Peerage etc. Volume VI]  p. 194, 195,197
2 CONT
2 CONT a. Sir '''Nicholas''' [Graham]  of Dalkeith, Abercorn, and Eskdale, who, in a charter to the monks of Melrose of their lands of Halsington, is styled ' primo genitus Domini Henrici de Graham.' 1 …. married, before 1269, Maria, you
2 CONC nger daughter of Malise, Earl of Strathearn, by his wife Marjory de Muschamp, co-heiress of the barony of Muschamp (including Wooler, Belford, and Lowick) in Northumberland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Sir Nicholas were : —
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a) Sir John of Dalkeith, Abercorn, and Eskdale. … married Isabella.
2 CONT * (b) '''Isabella''', married (as his second wife) to Walter, High Steward of Scotland, sometime husband of Marjory Bruce, daughter of Robert i., and by him, who died 1326, had a son, Sir John Stewart of Ralston, and other.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland was the son of James Stewart, 5th High Steward of Scotland and Gille de Burgh.1) Marjorie Bruce 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isabella Graham and Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir John Stewart of Ralston+1
2 CONT # Sir Andrew Stewart1
2 CONT # Egidia Stewart+1 d. b 1406
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT Cawley’s Medlands 
2 CONT SCOTLAND UNTITLED NOBILITY
2 CONT Graham 
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 06 May 2025
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#_Toc100910317
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella Graham (married Walter Stewart) is shown here as daughter of her brother.  We are however following The Scots Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT * HENRY [II] de Graham, son of HENRY [I] de Graham & his wife --- (-after 1233).  "Henricus de Graham filius Henrici de Graham" confirmed the donation of "terram de Balnebuth" to Newbattle abbey, made by "avus meus et pater meus P
2 CONC . et H. de Graham", by undated charter[735].  m ---.  The name of Henry’s wife is not known.  Henry [II] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT **1.  Henry [III] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT ***a)         NICHOLAS de Graham of Dalkeith (-after 20 Jan 1292).  "Nicholaus de Grham miles primogenitus dñi Henrici de Grham" confirmed the donation of "terra…  m MARY of Strathearn, daughter of MALISE Earl of Strathearn & his 
2 CONC first wife Marjory de Muschamp of Wooler ([1250/51]-after 1306).     Nicholas & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT ****i)          JOHN Graham of Abercorn (-25 Apr 1337).  "Johannes de Graham miles filius et heres Dñi Nicholai de Graham" donated "totam terram de Eskedal" to Melrose abbey by undated charter, dated to the early 14th century[744]
2 CONC .  "Johannes de Graham dñs de Abrecorn" confirmed "terram…in tenemento de Dalketh" to "Roberto de Lauuedre" by charter dated 4 Mar 1315 witnessed by "…dño Jacobo de Douglas…"[745].  m ISABELLA, daughter of --- (-after Apr 1337).  
2 CONC John & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT *****(a)       JOHN Graham (-after 6 Jan 1342).  Balfour Paul states that, as the last of the direct male line, he resigned Dalkeith in favour of William Douglas of Laudonia 6 Jan 1343[746]. 
2 CONT *****(b)       '''ISABEL de Graham''' .  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.   '''Balfour Paul records her parentage (as “sister of Sir John Graham of Abercorn”) and marriage (no s
2 CONC ource cited)'''[747].  Burnett says that the mother of John Stewart of Ralston “is said to have been Isabel, daughter of Sir John Graham of Abercorn”[748].  m as his second wife, WALTER Stewart, son of JAMES 5th High Steward of Sc
2 CONC otland & his [third] wife Egidia de Burgh ([1292]-9 Apr [1326/29]). 
2 CONT **** b)         HENRY de Graham .  "Henricus de Grahame" donated land by undated charter witnessed by "…Nich de Grahame Henrico de Grahame filio Radulpho de Corry"[749]. 
2 CONT ***2.         NICHOLAS de Graham .  According to Balfour Paul, he was ancestor of the Graham families of Tarbolton and Waiston in Ayrshire[750]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT Cawley’s Medlands 
2 CONT SCOTLAND, KINGS
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 26 March 2025
2 CONT A.         HIGH STEWARDS of SCOTLAND
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc100815218 
2 CONT
2 CONT WALTER Stewart, son of JAMES High Steward of Scotland & his [third] wife Egidia de Burgh ([1292]-9 Apr [1326/29]).  The Liber Pluscardensis names "dominus Alexander Stevart de Dundonald, pronepos primi Walteri Stewart" as "proavus
2 CONC …nobilis Walteri Stevart qui filiam Roberti de Broys desponsavit"[1288].  He succeeded his father as High Steward of Scotland.  Regent of Scotland.  … 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (1315) MARJORY Bruce, daughter of ROBERT I King of Scotland & his first wife Isabel of Mar ([1296/97]-Paisley, Renfrewshire 2 Mar 1316, bur Paisley Abbey).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) names "Marjoriam"
2 CONC  as the only daughter of "Robertus…rex, quuando fuit comes de Carric" and his wife "Isabellam sororem Garthenai comitis de Marr", adding that she married "Waltero senescallo Scotiæ"[1292].  The Liber Pluscardensis records that "no
2 CONC bilis Walteri Stevart" married "filiam Roberti de Broys"[1293].  She died in childbirth triggered by falling from her horse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ['''ISABEL de Graham''', daughter of JOHN Graham of Abercorn & his wife Isabella ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  Balfour Paul records her parentage ('''as
2 CONC  “sister of Sir John Graham of Abercorn”''') and marriage (no source cited)[1294].   Burnett says that the mother of John Stewart of Ralston “is said to have been Isabel, daughter of Sir John Graham of Abercorn”[1295].]  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Stewart & his first wife had one child:
2 CONT * 1.         ROBERT Stewart (Paisley, Renfrewshire 2 Mar 1316-Dundonald Castle, Ayrshire 19 Apr 1390, bur Scone Abbey, Perthshire).   … He succeeded his maternal uncle in 1371 as ROBERT II King of Scotland.  -        see below, Pa
2 CONC rt C. KINGS of SCOTLAND. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Stewart & his second wife had three children:
2 CONT * 2.         JOHN Stewart of Ralston (-1416).  … m ---.  The name of John's wife is not known.  John & his wife had five children: …
2 CONT * 3.         ANDREW Stewart (-before Jun 1413).  Burnett records an annuity paird between 1400 and 1413 to “Sir Andrew Stuart, Knight...of Raliston...brother of Sir John Stewart of Ralstoun”, noting that he was named as deceased i
2 CONC n the last payment dated Jun 1413 (full source citations)[1316].  Balfour Paul records his parentage, noting “of whose descendants, if any, there is no record” (no sources cited)[1317]. 
2 CONT * 4.         EGIDIA Stewart (-1396).  Balfour Paul records her parentage and three marriages (no sources cited)[1318].  The Papal dispensation for the marriage of "Jacobo nobili viro Jacobo de Lundesay" and "Egidie Steward", issue
2 CONC d by Pope Clement VI, is dated 11 Apr 1346[1319].  Burnett records payments to her “as widow of Sir James Lindsay...received from 1365 to 1375 by Sir Hugh Eglinton m firstly (Papal dispensation 11 Apr 1346, 21 Apr 1346) JAMES Lind
2 CONC say Lord of Crawford and Kirkmichael, son of DAVID Lindsay & his wife Maria Abernethy (-1358 before 11 Nov).  m secondly (1365 or before) HUGH Eglinton of Ardrossan, son of --- (-1376).  m thirdly (contract Oct 1378) as his [third
2 CONC ] wife, JAMES Douglas of Dalkeith and Arbroath, son of JOHN Douglas & his wife Agnes Graham (-1420). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
