1 NAME George /Stewart of Kilbride/
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Stewart of Kilbride
2 _MARNM Stewart of Kilbride
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == GEORGE STEWART OF KILBRIDE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Stewart of Kilbride is the son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stewart-of-Killbride/6000000026906171351?through=6000000005940228566. [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/383/mode/1up Mem
2 CONC oirs I: 383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1416: Indenture between James Stewart, Lord of Kilbride, and Sir Robert Maxwell of Calderwood, for the marriage of George Stewart, son and heir of the former, and Marion Maxwell, daughter of the latter, by his first mar
2 CONC riage ; whereby the said James binds himself to infeft George and Marion, and their heirs in his barony of Kilbride ; under entail, failing the heirs of the said parties, to the eldest of the said James's sons who should happen to
2 CONC  be heir, and a daughter of the said Robert, who should enter in the said barony as heirs of the said George and Marion, and be married in like manner ; and failing the sons of the said James, to his eldest daughter, and a son of 
2 CONC the said Robert, they to enter as heirs in the said barony by virtue of the said entail ; and so on, while the said James and Robert have sons and daughters. And the said Robert binds himself to pay to the said James £10 Scots yea
2 CONC rly, during his life, for Philpshill, for his part of Boysfield and Over Calderwood, and all the mail of all the lands falling in ward in the said barony, and all the reliefs and half escheats of courts thereof happening to be pai
2 CONC d to the said James ; and he binds himself likewise to pay the half of the said mails and reliefs, etc., to Isabel, wife of the said James, during her life, after her husband's death ; and to use his endeavours to recover the lord
2 CONC ship of Elamton, and in the event of succeeding, to cause the said James and Isabel to be jointly infeft in the franktenement thereof, and the children (George and Marion, etc.), in fee. And failing the recovery of the said lands 
2 CONC by Robert, the said children being espoused, he binds himself to pay to the said James and his heirs, for the said marriage, £100 at Whitsunday and Martinmas following the completion thereof. Sealed interchangeably at Lanark, 7th 
2 CONC April 1416.  [https://archive.org/details/memoirsofmaxwev100fras/page/383/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock I: 383]'''
1 FAMC @F6000000056429048942@
1 FAMS @F6000000005940358380@
1 RFN geni:6000000005940228566
1 SUBM @S6000000005939909082@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 27 OCT 2025
3 TIME 08:28:39
0 @I6000000011080081469@ INDI
1 NAME Margaret /Borthwick/ Lady Calderwood
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN Borthwick
2 NSFX Lady Calderwood
2 _MARNM Borthwick
1 SEX F
1 TITL Dame
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME MARGARET BORTHWICK Lady Calderwood == 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Borthwick, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Borthwick-Lord-Borthwick/6000000000172756659. The name of her mother has not been identified. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeera
2 CONC gefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/97/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 97]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Dame Margaret Borthwick, here treated. She was alive on 1 February 1463, [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/274/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: 1346] but she d
2 CONC ied before 7 January 1476-77, the date upon which her husband gave half the lands of Stanely to https://www.geni.com/people/George-Maxwell-of-Newark/6000000053082253094, his only son by his second wife https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Margaret-Rutherford-Lady-Calderwood/6000000056429563932. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/275/mode/1up Ibidem: 1352] It is quite possible that she actually died before 1 February 1463, upon which date she i
2 CONC s identified as the mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Maxwell/6000000055808086837.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/274/mode/1up Ibidem: 1346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Borthwick, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Maxwell-of-Calderwood/6000000019658638370?through=6000000011080081469 before 4 December 1450. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/p
2 CONC age/93/mode/1up RMS: 404]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 December 1450: Charter by which James II, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the barony of Fynlaustoun and the lands of Stanle in Renfrewshire to John Maxwell of Calderwood and his wife Margaret. [Note 1] [https://arch
2 CONC ive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/93/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA . Scot. (H.M. General Register
2 CONC  of House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 404]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It is not yet clear who Margaret was, although it seems quite likely, probable even, that she was Margaret Borthwick.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1463: Charter by which John Maxwell of Calderwood confirms that he has given the barony of Hiltoun in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and various other lands in the earldom of Lennox and sheriffdom of Dumbarton, to Elizab
2 CONC eth Maxwell, his daughter by Margaret Borthwick [Note]. John Maxwell of Calderwood's charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 19 January 1477-78. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/274/mode/1
2 CONC up Ibidem, charter number 1346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It is possible that Margaret Borthwick died before 1 February 1463.
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 August 1473: Charter by which he has given half the lands of Stanele in the barony of Renfrew to Patrick Maxwell. This land had previously been resigned by John Maxwell of Calderwood, who reserved his own liferent and that o
2 CONC f his wife Margaret. [Note 1] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/232/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number 1137]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 1: It is not yet clear who Margaret was.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1476: Charter by which Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood confirms that he has given the barony of Finlastoun in the sheriffdom of Renfrew to his son and heir George Maxwell. The barony is held in conjunct fee and liferen
2 CONC t by Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood and his wife Margaret [Note 2] , who reserved their liferent. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 22 January 1477-78. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02sco
2 CONC t/page/275/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number 1352]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 2: This appears to be https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Rutherford-Lady-Calderwood/6000000056429563932. '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/97/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 97]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/memoirsofmaxwev100fras#page/465/mode/1up Memoirs of the Maxwells of Pollock I:  p. 465]'''
2 CONT #  '''[https://thepeerage.com/p14542.htm#i145419 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]''' 
