2 CONC 80081469?through=6000000055808086837: '"Johannis Maxwell de Caldorwod qua concessit filie sua Elizabeth Maxwell procreate inter se et Margaretam Borthwic". On 1 February 1463 Sir John gave Elizabeth the barony of Hiltoun in Berwic
2 CONC kshire, together with certain other lands in the Earldom of Lennox. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/274/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: 1346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1463: Charter by which John Maxwell of Calderwood confirms that he has given the barony of Hiltoun in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and various other lands in the earldom of Lennox and sheriffdom of Dumbarton, to Elizab
2 CONC eth Maxwell, his daughter by Margaret Borthwick. John Maxwell of Calderwood's charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 19 January 1477-78. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/274/mode/1up RMS 
2 CONC 1424-1513: 1346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Re
2 CONC gister House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
