1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GEORGE MAXWELL OF NEWARK===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Maxwell of Newark is the son of Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/275/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 1352 on p. 275] His f
2 CONC ather gave him Newark (Finlastoun)  on 7 January 1476. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/275/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 1352 on p. 275]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Darryl Lundy's Peerage, his mother was Margaret Borthwick. [http://www.thepeerage.com/p43827.htm#i438267 Darryl Lundy's Peerage: George Maxwell] Clan MacFarlane is of the same opinion. [http://www.clanmacfarlanegen
2 CONC ealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3417&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy] MacFarlane cites Stirnet as the source of this information but Peter Barns-Graham is actually more cautious, and
2 CONC  does not go as far as to identify the mothers of any of Sir John Maxwell's children. [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mm4ae/maxwell04.php Stirnet: Maxwell 04]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notwithstang the before mentioned proposals, Sir William Fraser, the Maxwell family historian, writing in his 1863 account of the Maxwells of Pollock, tells us that George Maxwell of Newark's mother was in fact Margaret Rutherf
2 CONC ord, the second wife of Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood. George and his father and mother are noticed in a charter which was issued at Edinburgh on 7 January 1476. ''' [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/275/mod
2 CONC e/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 1352 on p. 275] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Barony of Fynlastoun afterwards the Barony of Newark===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This notice of the Maxwells of Newark is taken from Walter MacFarlane's geographical collection. The name of the author is not know: "Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood hath with ther Fynlastoun afterwards called the barony of Newa
2 CONC rk, and is lately sold by them. they were a race of brave gentlemen and in reputation inferior to none in this country." [https://archive.org/stream/geographicalcoll02macf#page/204/mode/1up Geographical Collections Relating to Sco
2 CONC tland made by Walter MacFarlane (Scottish Records Society, Edinburgh, 1907), ii, p. 204]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Maxwell of Newark died before 26 January 1484-85. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/339/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 1612 on pp. 339-40]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The name of George Maxwell of Newlands's wife is not known but he had at least three children. Their names follow:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Maxwell-3rd-of-Newark/6000000013416782068?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1489334328839&through=6000000053082253094
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Archibald-Maxwell-of-Stanely/6000000056429284858?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1490396405974&through=6000000053082253094
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Maxwell/6000000056302058830?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1490396618797&through=6000000053082253094
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1476: Charter by which Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood and his wife Margaret confirm that they have given the barony of Finlastoun in Renfrewshire to George of Maxwell, son and heir of Sir John Maxwell of Calderwood' A
2 CONC  charter of confirmation was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland on 22 January 1477-78. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/275/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 135
2 CONC 2 on p. 275]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1484-85: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland, following from a decreet of the Lords of Council, against Patrick Maxwell, son and heir of the deceased George Maxwell of Newark. [https://archive.org/stream/
2 CONC registrummagnisi02scot#page/339/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1424-1513, charter number 1612 on pp. 339-40]'''
2 CONT
