2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 October 1539: Charter. James Scrymgeour, Constable of Dundee of the lands of Ballegerno and others in favor of Elizabeth Scrymgeour his daughter and James Scrymgeour her spouse and longest liver of them in conjunct fee, and 
2 CONC the heirs-male procreate betwixt them; whom failing to return to the granter and his heirs male whatsoever for extinction of pleas and in full satisfaction of all rights, title or hereditary claim of the said Elizabeth and James S
2 CONC crymgeour for his interest to the unentailed lands of the Lordship of Duddop and Constabulary of Dundee, or to any other lands or competent to her by the decease of the said James, or any of his predecessors, and for the Renunciat
2 CONC ion of her half of the lands of Balrudry and specially for the Compliment keeping and observance of a Contract entered into and passed thereupon betwixt the said Constable and the said Elizabeth and James, registered in the books 
2 CONC of the Commissariot of St. Andrews 25 October 1539. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f786&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National 
2 CONC Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/786]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 October 1539: Obligation of warrandice of the said lands of Ballegerno by James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee to the said Elizabeth Scrymgeour and James her spouse. Dated the last day of October 1539. [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f789&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Fam
2 CONC ily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/789]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 March 1541: Certified copy of Charter. Dated the 2d March 1541, of the Lands and Barony of Duddop etc. in favor of James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee in liferent and John Scrymgeour of Glastre in fee, and the heirs-male of 
2 CONC his body; whom failing John Scrymgeour, Grandson to the said James, procreate betwixt James Scrymgeour formerly of Kirktoun and Elizabeth Scrymgeour, daughter of the said James the Constable, or any other heirs-male lawfully procr
2 CONC eated or to be procreated betwixt the said James and Elizabeth, Whom failing James Scrymgeour Fiar of Fardle, James Scrymgeour of Fordie, James Scrymgeour of Gond, and John Scrymgeour of Myres seriatim, and the heirs-male of their
2 CONC  bodies respective; whom failing the lawful and nearest heirs-male of the blood and name of Scrymgeour carrying its arms; whom all failing the lawful and nearest heirs whatsoever of the said James, with a reservation to the terce 
2 CONC of the Constable's present or any future wife, and a clause of return to the heirs-male of the Constable's body if any should be thereafter procreated for the safer preservation of the house of the said James. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f819&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn F
2 CONC amily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/819]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1547: Charter by Archibald Earl of Angus to John Scrimgeour of Glastre, constable of Dundee, his heirs and assignees, of all and sundry the lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradichty, and also three 8th parts and 25/ of a fourth
2 CONC  8th part of the lands of Ethybetoun, lying in the regality of Kerymure; which lands belonged to Elizabeth and Agnes Scrimgeours, daughters of the late James S. constable of Dundee, heritably and were by them, with consent of Jame
2 CONC s Scrimgeour husband of said Elizabeth, and of Peter Brus, heir apparent of Erlishall, husband of said Agnes, resigned in the hands of their superiors at Edinburgh: To be holden of the granter and his successors in fee and heritag
2 CONC e for the rights and services used and wont. Dated at Edinburgh 8 May 1547. Witnesses, James Scrimgeour of Roddgoddyn, Mr Hugh Rig of Carbery, James Ogilvy of Balfuir, David Grahame of Fentre, Knight, and William Rethe notary. Sea
2 CONC l broken.[https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f791&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=erlishall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn o
2 CONC f Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/791]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 May 1649: Receipt Janet Haliburton to James Scrymgeour of Ballegerno. Dated the 6 May 1549. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f824&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=scrymgeour+of+B
2 CONC allegerno&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/824]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1551: Precept of Sasine by John, Archbishop of St. Andrews, directed to the bailies of his regality of St. Andrews within his barony of Roscoby, for infefting John Scrymgeour son and apparent heir of an honourable man J
2 CONC ames Scrymgeour of Ballegarno and Elizabeth also Scrymgeour his spouse, the heirs and assignees of the said John, whatsoever, in all and whole the half parts of the half of the Kirktoun of Stradychty Martyne, and of Baldovane, in 
2 CONC the barony of Roscoby and shire of Forfar; which parts belong to the said Elizabeth Scrymgeour one of the daughters and elder of the heirs of the late James Scrymgeour of Dudop, constable of Dundee, and were resigned by her in fav
2 CONC our of the said John, reserving the life-rent and usufruct of the same to a noble lady, Isabella Gray, relict of James Scrymgeour of Dudop, Knight, and mother of the late James S. of Dudop, and now spouse of a noble man, John Camp
2 CONC bell of Lundy, Knight. Dated at the church of St. Andrews 9th April 1551. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f729&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&
2 CONC dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/729]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1555: Extract Contract betwixt John Scrymgeour of Duddop, Constable of Dundee, John Scrymgeour Son and heir of the deceased Elizabeth Scrymgeour, eldest daughter and heir of the deceased James Scrymgeour, Constable of 
2 CONC Dundee, procreated of the Marriage between her and the also deceased James Scrymgeour of Ballegerno. Dated the 28 March and registred in the books of Council and Session the penult day of the said month 1555. [https://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f863&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ballegerno&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earl
2 CONC s of Dundee, reference GD137/863]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 March 1555: Extracted Contract between John Scrymgeour of Dudop constable of Dundee, and John Scrymgeour son and heir of the deceased Elizabeth Scrymgeour eldest daughter and heir of the deceased James S. constable of Dundee
2 CONC , procreated between her and the also deceased James Scrymgeour of Ballegerno. Dated 28 March 1555. Regd in Books of Council and Session 30 March 1555. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD137%2f1457&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ballegerno&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/1457]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1565: Precept of Sasine by John Scrymgeour constable of Dundee, Lord of Dudop, and superior of the lands undernoted, directed to Patrick Gray of Ballegerno etc. for infefting John Scrymgeour, son and heir of the late Eli
2 CONC zabeth Scrymgeour, elder daughter and one of the heirs of line of the late James Scrymgeour, constable of Dundee, of the lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradichty, in excambion for the said John's part of the lands, mills and annualrent
2 CONC s of the barony of Stricmartyn, and of the lands of Ethibeton, and for resignation of the Mains of Ballegerno, Drumy and West Newton in the barony of Ballegerno, in favour of the granter: the said lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradich
2 CONC ty to hold to the said John Scrymgeour and the heirs male of his body, and to his brothers James, William, Thomas, and Alexander, and the heirs male of their bodies successively and respectively, in virtue of Contract between the 
2 CONC late James Scrymgeour constable of Dundee, and the late Elizabeth his daughter and James Scrymgeour her spouse, of date 21 October 1539; and of Contract between the late John Scrymgeour, constable of Dundee, father of the granter,
2 CONC  and John Scrymgeour aforesaid, son and heir of said Elizabeth, of date at Edinburgh 30th March 1555, recorded in the books of the Lords of Council, etc. Dated at Dundee 8 June 1565. Witnesses, Andrew Ventoun of Strikmertein, Patr
2 CONC ick Gray of Ballegerno, George Creichtoun of Cumpray, James Scrymgeour of Glaswell. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f733&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=
2 CONC &ro=s&df=1500&dt=1566&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/733]'''
2 CONT
