1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES SCRYMGEOUR of DUDHOPE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Constable of Dundee'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 May 1524: Charter. Robert Maule of Panmure of the lands of Balrudery in favor of Mariot Stewart formerly wife of James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee in liferent and Elizabeth and Agnes Scrymgeours their two daughters in fee
2 CONC , proceeding on the resignation of the said James Scrymgeour in favor of James Learthmonth of Dairsy Provost of St. Andrews as a mid person betwixt the said James Scrymgeour and an Honorable woman the said Mariot Stewart formerly 
2 CONC wife of the said James, before the pronunciation or promulgation of the sentence of Divorce betwixt them and upon the resignation of the said James Learmonth in favors of the said Mariot Stewart as is more fully contained in a Con
2 CONC tract betwixt the said James and Mariot. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f783&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/783]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1525: Sasine of an annuity by James Scrymgeour of Duddop in favor of Marion Stewart formerly (olim) his spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f782&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/782]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 August 1534: Copy of charter of resignation by Robert Mawle of Panmwyr to James Scrimgeor, constable of Dunde, and Marion Vadlaw, his wife, of two chalders of victual out of the lands of Banvye the said victual having been r
2 CONC esigned by the said James. Witnesses:- Thomas Strathaquhin, sir John Vyntown, Florence Rydy and David Lwyd, chaplains and notaries public. [Copied by David Lwyd.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD45%2f16%2f582&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=scrimgeor&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/582]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1547: Charter by Archibald Earl of Angus to John Scrimgeour of Glastre, constable of Dundee, his heirs and assignees, of all and sundry the lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradichty, and also three 8th parts and 25/ of a fourth
2 CONC  8th part of the lands of Ethybetoun, lying in the regality of Kerymure; which lands belonged to Elizabeth and Agnes Scrimgeours, daughters of the late James S. constable of Dundee, heritably and were by them, with consent of Jame
2 CONC s Scrimgeour husband of said Elizabeth, and of Peter Brus, heir apparent of Erlishall, husband of said Agnes, resigned in the hands of their superiors at Edinburgh: To be holden of the granter and his successors in fee and heritag
2 CONC e for the rights and services used and wont. Dated at Edinburgh 8 May 1547. Witnesses, James Scrimgeour of Roddgoddyn, Mr Hugh Rig of Carbery, James Ogilvy of Balfuir, David Grahame of Fentre, Knight, and William Rethe notary. Sea
2 CONC l broken.[https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f791&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=erlishall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn o
2 CONC f Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/791]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
