1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK AND EDNAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Edam, here treated, is the son of Sir James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam. On 5 August 1458 he had a charter under the Great Seal of Scotland which confirmed that his father had resigned the l
2 CONC ands of Ednam in the sheriffdom of Berwick in his favour. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/133/mode/1up RMS 1425-1513: 607]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, died before 16 January 1498. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%2f7%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmonstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df
2 CONC =&dt=1400&di=n NRS: GD237/7/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, married Isobell Hume. According to Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet: "In 1499 there is a solemn transaction whereby John Edmondstoune of that Ilk promises that 
2 CONC he will not sell nor put away any more of his lands from John, his son and heir, and the heirs of the said John's marriage with Isabel Home". [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/93/mode/1up Duntreath: 93]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1458: REX concessit JOHANNI DE EDMONDSTOUNE filio Jac. de E. de eodem militis, — terras de Edname, vic. [Berwic] ; — quas idem Jac. resignavit : — Tenend. dicto Jac. et heredibus masculis de corpore ejus legitime procr
2 CONC eatis, quibus deficicntibus, legitimis et propinquioribus heredibus dicti Jac. (|uibuscunque: — Faciend. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/133/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of
2 CONC  the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 607]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1465: Apud Civitatem S. Andree, 30 Apr. REX concessit familiari scutifero sue DAVID DE CREICHTOUNE et heredibus ejus, — terras de Walastoune, vie. Perth; — quas .Joh. de Edmondstoun de eodem resignavit : — Test, ut in 
2 CONC carta 830. vi. 30 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/176/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FS
2 CONC A. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 831]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1482-83: REX coniirmavit literam reversionis farailiaris sui Willelmi Routhen (Rothven) de eodem, — [qua se oligavit sursum reddere JOHANNI EDMONSTOUN de eodem, heredibus ejus et assignatis, — terras de Wallastoune, 
2 CONC in baronia de Methven, vic. Perth, —  quandocunque contigerit eundem Job. heredes suo.s, &c., persolvero dicto Wil., &c., .summam 300 merc, in le Scottis ridaris auri (quolibet ridar valente 24 sol. boni argenti prout dicti ridari
2 CONC s cursuni babuerunt in Scotia die confectionis presentium), in ecclesia parochiali Beati Jon. Bapt. de Perth super supremo altari : — Test. Pat. Cranstoun de Corsby, Gilb. Edmondstoun, Alex. Turing, Job. Berclay, Tho. do Cranstoun
2 CONC , et Jon. Rothven: — Apud Edinburgh, 20 Aug., 1482]: — Necnon aliam literam assignationis dicti Johannis Edmondstoun, sub hac forma, — [Be it kend, &c., . . . me John of Edmondstoun of that ilk constitutis and ordanis irrevocably 
2 CONC for me and my aris, JAMES OLIPHANT of Archeke, WALTER OLIPHANT, JOHN OLIPHANT, and JOHN OLIPHANT yonger, and LAURENS OLIPHANT, sones to the said James, LAURENS LORD OLI PHANT, ROBERT THE ROSS of Cragy, and JOHN THE ROSS his sone a
2 CONC nd apperand are, and ilk ane of thame, — my assignis to the redemyn of the lands of Wallastoun, fra Wlliame of Rothven of that ilk, his aris and assignis, the quhilkis landis the said Wlliame has under his reversioun to upgif quhe
2 CONC nsaever I pay to him 300 merkis in Scottis redaris of gold, &c., . . In witnes, &c., . . . — At Edinburgh, 20 Sep., 1482, befor thir witnes, Walt. Rothven of Forteviot, Job. Thane, And. Muncref of Estir-Muncreff, Gilb. Edmondstoun
2 CONC , Alex. Frasser, Job. Malcome] : — Test, ut in carta 1553. x. 64. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/325/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-
2 CONC 1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 1554]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 July 1496 Apud Edinburgh, 18 Jul. REX concessit armigero suo PATRICIO HUME de Polwort, et heredibus ejus, — dimedietatem terrarum de Hetschawe, in ballia de Lawderdaile, vic. Berwik ; — quam Joh. Edmonstoun de eodem resignav
2 CONC it : — Test. 30. 32. 42. 26. 84. 20. 37. 40.  xiii 231. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edit
2 CONC ed by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 2331]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 July 1496: Apud Edinburgh, 18 Jul. REX concessit GEORGEO HUME de Weddirburn, et MARIOTE SINCLARE ejus sponse, — dimedietatem terrarum de Hetschawe, in blallia de Laudirdale, vic. Berwik; — quam Joh. Edmonstounde eodem resigu
2 CONC avit : — Tenend. dictis Geo. et Mar. et eorum alteri diutius viventi in conjuncta infeodatione et heredibus inter ipsos legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, legitimis et jsropinquioribus heredibus dicti Geo. quibuscunque : —
2 CONC  Test, ut in carta 2321. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advoc
2 CONC ate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 2332]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1496: Apud Edinburgh, 31 Jul.  REX concessit JACOBO EDMONDSTOUN (filio Johannis E.) de eodem — terras et baroniam de Ednem, molendinum de E., unam tenandriam de E., unacum advocatione et donatione hospitalis de E., vic.
2 CONC  Roxburgh ; terras de Riselaw, vic. Berwic; tertiam partem terrarum de Hirdmanstoun, Gurre, et Nudremerschall, cum tenandria et molendino earundem, vic, Edinburgh ; — quequidem fuerunt dicti Johannis, et tertia pars de Nudremersch
2 CONC all cum molendino, &c., ejusdem fuit dicti Joh. et Margarete Mateland ejus sponse in conjuncta infeodatione, et quas terras et tertiam partem terrarum dicti Joh. et Merg. respective resignaverunt : — Tenend. dicto Jac. et heredibu
2 CONC s masculis ejus de corpora legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, David E. ejus fratri et heredibus, &c., (id supra), quibus def., "Willelmo E. fratri ejusdem, et heredibus, &c. (id supra), quibus def., lehitimis et propinquio
2 CONC ribus heredibus masculis dicti Jon. cognomen et arma do Edmonstoun gerentibus quibuscumiuo : — RESERVATIS. pro Ednem unum duiiarium argeiiti nomine albe firme ; pro ceteris terris, &c., wardns, &c., cum contigerint : — RESERVATIS 
2 CONC libero tenemento dicto Jon. ac rationabili tertia ejus spouse cuicunque cum contigerit :— Test. 30. 31. 32. 42. 26. 84. 20. 37. 40. xiii. 225. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up Registrum Magni S
2 CONC igilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 2333]'''
2 CONT
