1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alan II, Earl of Menteith (d. after 23 Aug 1315) was a Scottish Nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_II,_Earl_of_Menteith
2 CONT
2 CONT Menteith was the son of Alan, Earl of Menteith, and is first noted in an order dated at Carlisle in 1307 to provide foodstuffs ' to the two sons of the Earl of Menteith, and the son of the Earl of Stratherne'.[1] He evidently was 
2 CONC an English prisoner, but he either escaped to the Scottish camp or was exchanged for an English nobleman held by the Scots. 'Alan, son of Earl Alan of Menteith' was the beneficiary of the entail by his cousin Duncan of the Earldom
2 CONC  of Fife in the event of the failure of lawful heirs in an agreement dated at Crichton, 23 August 1315.[2] He died some time before 1 August 1323, on which date his uncle Muireadhach III witnessed a charter as Earl of Menteith.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan II, Earl of Menteith married an unknown lady, by whom he had a daughter Mary II, Countess of Menteith
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan,_Earl_of_Menteith
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan, Earl of Menteith married Marjory or Margery, who has been shown to have been a daughter of Colbán, Earl of Fife by his wife Anne Durward.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had two sons, one of whom,
2 CONT *Alan, succeeded his father as Earl when a minor.[4].  '''This 2nd Alan was the father of Mary, who married Sir John Graham.'''
2 CONT
