1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John "The Hero Of Sark" Wallace, 5th of Craigie, 10th of Riccarton ( b abt 1400 d about 1450)
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1448 clash was the first decisive victory for a Scottish force over the English since the Battle of Otterburn, 60 years earlier. It was the final pitched battle between the two countries in the period of the Hundred Years War.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Renewed border skirmishing saw Henry Percy, future 3rd earl of Northumberland, defeated by Hugh Douglas, earl of Ormond, on 23 October 1448. The encounter took place on the river Sark, near Gretna. Percy was taken prisoner and had
2 CONC  to be ransomed.
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n97/mode/2up/search/Hero+of+sark
2 CONT
2 CONT William Wallace of Craigie married Elizabeth, daughter of James, 7th Earl of Douglas, by his wife Beatrix, daughter of the Regent, Robert, Duke of Albany.  Of the union was born three sons, John, Hugh, and Adam; also a daughter Ma
2 CONC rgaret, who became the second wife of Robert, first Lord Lyle.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n101/mode/2up/search/Hero+of+sark
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Wallace hero of Sark left a widow and two sons, William and Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
