1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This Alexander Stewart, son of Walter, was the second person to hold the title of "1st Lord Avandale"; he inherited this from his uncle Andrew.  Upon Alexander's death the title of 2nd Lord Avandale went to another
2 CONC  Andrew, nephew of the original 1st Lord Avandale.
2 CONT *Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_1st_Lord_Avandale
2 CONT  _____________________________
2 CONT *''''''Alexander Stewart1
2 CONT *''''''M, #561426, b. before 1425, d. circa 1472
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Oct 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=7.15%
2 CONT *''''''     Alexander Stewart was born illegitimately before 1425.1 He was the son of Walter Stewart, Master of Fife and unknown daughter Campbell.1 He died circa 1472.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2768. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p56143.htm#i561426
2 CONT *__________________________
2 CONT *Sir Walter Stewart, Master of Fife, Lennox, & Menteith1,2,3,4
2 CONT *M, #37523, b. circa 1396, d. 24 May 1425
2 CONT *Father      Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke Albany5 b. c 1362, d. 25 May 1425
2 CONT *Mother     Isabel Lennox5 d. bt 1456 - 25 Jun 1460
2 CONT *     Sir Walter Stewart, Master of Fife, Lennox, & Menteith married (Miss) Campbell, daughter of Sir Arthur Campbell, 6th Laird of Strachur, Glenfalloch, & Glendochart, DID NOT MARRY; They had 6 illegitimate sons (Sir Andrew, 1st
2 CONC  Lord Avondale, Chancellor of Scotland; Sir Murdoch; Arthur; Robert; ''''''Alexander''''''; & Walter of Morphie) & 2 illegitimate daughters (Maud, wife of Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath; & Marion, wife of Sir Colin Campbell o
2 CONC f Glenorchy).6,3,4 Sir Walter Stewart, Master of Fife, Lennox, & Menteith was born circa 1396 at of Lennox, Scotland. He and Euphemia Stewart obtained a marriage license on 5 September 1415; Date of dispensation, but marriage neve
2 CONC r occurred.7,3,4 Sir Walter Stewart, Master of Fife, Lennox, & Menteith and Janet Erskine obtained a marriage license on 27 May 1421; Date of dispensation, being related in the 3rd degree of consanguinity. This marriage may not ha
2 CONC ve taken place.6,3,4 Sir Walter Stewart, Master of Fife, Lennox, & Menteith died on 24 May 1425 at Stirling, Stirlingshire, Scotland; Beheaded. Buried at Blackfriars church, Stirling.6,3,4
2 CONT *Family 1      (Miss) Campbell 
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avandale d. bt 11 Mar 1488 - 12 Jul 1488
2 CONT **Arthur Stewart
2 CONT *Family 2      Euphemia Stewart b. a 1378, d. Oct 1415
2 CONT *Family 3      Janet Erskine b. c 1396
