1 NAME Walter /Stewart of Morphie/
2 GIVN Walter
2 SURN Stewart of Morphie
2 _MARNM Stewart of Morphie
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1425
2 ADDR
3 CITY Morphy
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1488
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Walter Stewart Baron of Morphie{1} b. before 1425, d. before 1488
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Stewart of Morphie was born illegitimately, although he would be legitimate if truly a son of Janet Erskine, before 1425.  It is probably that if he was indeed the son of Janet, he was probably their only child.  ''(The oth
2 CONC er children of his father Walter were more likely from a daughter of Duncan Campell-1st Lord Cambell and Marjorie Stewart-daughter of Robert).''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Walter Stewart, Master of Fife and Lady Janet Erskine. He married Elizabeth Arnot. He died before 1488. On 17 April 1479 he was legitimised.{2}
2 CONT
2 CONT * {1.} [http://thepeerage.com/p10796.htm#i107959 The Peerage-p10796.htm-i107959]
2 CONT
2 CONT See also http://www.cwbn.ca/Walter_Stewart/Walter_Stewart.pdf
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT James Stewart "Black Knight of Lorn" did not have a son named Walter. No valid source documents found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Disconnected 7/21/2016
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofstewar00johnuoft/heraldryofstewar00johnuoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT 37) WALTER STEWART OF MORPHIE, son of Walter Stewart (No. 35), had four  sons : 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a) Alexander. 
2 CONT
2 CONT () Andrew. (See No. 38). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (c) John, ancestor of the Stewarts of Culbeg and Garchoile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (d) , ancestor of the Stuarts of Inchbrek and Johnston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ANDREW STEWART appears to have succeeded his elder brother in the Barony  of Avondale in 1489, but in any case he was created LORD A VON DALE  (S.) in that year. He fell at Flodden 1513, leaving three sons : 
2 CONT
2 CONT () Andrew (No. 39). 
2 CONT
2 CONT () Henry, Lord Methven (No. 45). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (f) Sir James of Beith (No. 48). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ANDREW, THIRD LORD AVONDALE (S.). In 1543 he obtained an Act of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parliament to exchange his title for that of LORD STEWART OF OCHIL-  TREE (S.), and died 1 548. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son : 
2 CONT
2 CONT (40) ANDREW, SECOND LORD OCHILTREE, had five sons : 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a) Andrew, Master of Ochiltree, who died in his father's life-  time, leaving : 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Andrew (No. 41). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Josias of Bonnytoun, who died without issue.  () James (No. 42). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (c) William of Monkton, killed 1588. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (d) Henry of Barbowie, Braidwood, Dunregan and Nether 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gogar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (e) Robert of Wester Braco.
2 CONT
2 CONT (41) ANDREW, THIRD LORD OCHILTREE, son of Andrew, Master of Ochiltree, 
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES STEWART OF BOTHWELLMUIR, second son of Andrew, second Lord 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ochiltree (No. 40), was created EARL OF ARRAN, Lord of Arane and  Hamilton (S.) in 1581, and was attainted 1585. He was killed 1596. 
2 CONT
2 CONT who died in his father's lifetime. He ruined himself and resigned his  Scotch estates and title to his cousin (see No. 43). He received grants of  land in Tyrone, Ireland, and was given a Peerage in Ireland, 1619 LORD  CASTLE STEW
2 CONC ART (I.) He died 1629, leaving three sons : 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a) Andrew, second Lord, father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Andrew, third Lord, died 1650. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Robert, died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) Josias, fourth Lord, died without issue 1662. 
2 CONT
2 CONT () John, fifth Lord. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (c) Robert, from whom descended the sixth, seventh, eighth and  ninth Lords. The last was created Viscount Castle Stewart in 1793, and EARL OF CASTLE STEWART (I.)  1800, and from him the present Earl descends. 
2 CONT
