1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''Sir James 'the Gross' Stewart, Master of Lennox1,2,3,4 
2 CONT *''''''M, #41395, d. 1451
2 CONT *Father      Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke Albany5,6 b. c 1362, d. 25 May 1425
2 CONT *Mother     Isabel Lennox1,5,6 d. bt 1456 - 25 Jun 1460
2 CONT *     Sir James 'the Gross' Stewart, Master of Lennox married (Miss) MacDonald, daughter of John Mor 'Iain Mhor Tanistair' MacDonald, 1st Chief of Dunnyveg and Margery Byset, DID NOT MARRY; He had 1 illegitimate son (James Beg).1,
2 CONC 3,4 Sir James 'the Gross' Stewart, Master of Lennox died in 1451 at Ireland.1,3,4
2 CONT *''''''Family      (Miss) MacDonald 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Matilda Stewart+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11563] The Scots Peerage, Vol. I, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 151.
2 CONT * 2.[S11649] Clan MacFarlane & Associated Clans Genealogy.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 545-546.
2 CONT * 4.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 622.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 543.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 619-620.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1378.htm#i41395
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *''''''Sir James Stewart, 1st of Baldorran1 
2 CONT *''''''M, #107963, b. between 1395 and 1426, d. before 18 May 1451
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Oct 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT *''''''     Sir James Stewart, 1st of Baldorran was born between 1395 and 1426. He was the son of Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany and Isabel of Lennox, Countess of Lennox.1 He died before 18 May 1451 at Ireland without legitim
2 CONC ate issue.2
2 CONT *''''''      Circa 1425 he fled to Ireland, after the execution of his father and brothers. He avenged his family byu burning Dumbarton at the head of a band of highlanders, killing its Keeper.3 Sir James Stewart, 1st of Baldorran
2 CONC  also went by the nick-name of Seumas Mor (or in English, Big James).3
2 CONT *''''''Children of Sir James Stewart, 1st of Baldorran and unknown Macdonald
2 CONT ** 1.Matilda Stewart+4
2 CONT ** 2.James Stewart, 2nd of Baldorran2 b. b 1451
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 218. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 78. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 3.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2768. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT * 4.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10797.htm#i107963
