1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1438
2 PLAC Orkney Islands, Orkney, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Countess of Orkney
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY EGIDIA DOUGLAS Countess of Orkney ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Fair Maid of Nithsdale===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/570/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 570]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/CalendarOfEntriesInThePapalRegisterV7/page/221/mode/1up Papal Registers VII: 221]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from Papal Registers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 Kal. May 1422: To the bishop of St. Andrews. Mandate to dispense Alexander Steuart, donsel, and Egidia de Duglas, relict of Henry Synclar, knight, of the dioceses of Glasgow and St. Andrews, to marry notwithstanding that Alex
2 CONC ander is distant in the third, and Egidia in the second degree of kindred from their common stock. Oblate nobis. [https://archive.org/details/CalendarOfEntriesInThePapalRegisterV7/page/221/mode/1up Papal Registers VII: 221]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/CalendarOfEntriesInThePapalRegisterV7/page/n5/mode/1up Calendar of Entries in the Papal Registers Relating to Great Britain and Ireland. Papal Letters. Vol. VII. A.D. 1417-1431. Prepared by J. A. Tr
2 CONC emlow, B.A. (HMSO., London, 1906) 724 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility
2 CONC  of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume VI. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), 601 pp.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT If her death date is abt  1438 as given then Orkney was a part of  Norway
2 CONT 3em>Orkney was colonised and later annexed by the Kingdom of Norway in 875 and settled by the Norsemen. '''In 1472, the Parliament of Scotland absorbed the Earldom of Orkney into the Kingdom of Scotland,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Maternal granddaughter of King Robert II of Scotland and great granddaughter of King Robert I the Bruce of Scotland. Was beautiful and known as the Fair Maiden of Nithsdale.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.scottish-places.info/features/featurehistory3649.html Nithsdale (Strathnith or Stranith)] A historical perspective, drawn from the Ordnance Gazetteer of Scotland: A Survey of Scottish Topography, Statistical, Biog
2 CONC raphical and Historical, edited by Francis H. Groome and originally published in parts by Thomas C. Jack, Grange Publishing Works, Edinburgh between 1882 and 1885. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Under Robert II. Nithsdale obtained new superiors. Sir William Douglas, natural son of Sir Archibald Douglas, Lord of Galloway, wedding Giles, the daughter of the king, received with her a grant of Nithsdale, and was constituted 
2 CONC sheriff of Dumfries.
2 CONT
2 CONT * >His only child, his daughter '''Giles''' - called ''the Fair Maid of Nithsdale'', who inherited her father's lordship and sheriffdom - married, 
2 CONT
2 CONT # first, in 1407, to Henry Sinclair, Earl of Orkney, and next, 
2 CONT # in 1418, Alexander Stewart, the son of James, who was the brother of Robert II., and had obtained from Robert Bruce the lands of Durisdeer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her children  by her first marriage were 
2 CONT # William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney, who inherited Nithsdale and the sheriffship of Dumfries.  
2 CONT # Beatrix Sinclair, who married James Douglas, 7th Earl of Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p128.htm#i3837
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Sinclair,_2nd_Earl_of_Orkney
