1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Lindsay:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10798.htm#i107976
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Lindsay [1]
2 CONT *F, #107976, 
2 CONT *d. 6 February 1482
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.07%
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Lindsay was the daughter of John Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of the Byres and Agnes Stewart.[2],[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Walter Stewart, 1st Lord Innermeath, son of Sir Robert Stewart, 1st Lord Lorn and Joan Stewart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henry Wardlow before December 1477.[2] She died on 6 February 1482.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT As a result of her marriage, Margaret Lindsay was styled as Lady Innermeath on 30 November 1469.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Lindsay and Walter Stewart, 1st Lord Innermeath
2 CONT *1. Thomas Stewart, 2nd Lord Innermeath+[2] b. b 1461, d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 218. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VIII, page 139. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VIII, page 7.
