1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Thomas Stewart, 2nd Lord Innermeath:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10927.htm#i109262
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Stewart, 2nd Lord Innermeath [1]
2 CONT *M, #109262, 
2 CONT *b. before 1461, 
2 CONT *d. 9 September 1513
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Mar 2009
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=12.58%
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Stewart, 2nd Lord Innermeath was born before 1461.[1] He was the son of Walter Stewart, 1st Lord Innermeath and Margaret Lindsay.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Janet Keith, daughter of William de Keith, 1st Earl Marischal and Marjorie Fraser, before 23 June 1481.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, killed in action.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Innermeath [S., 1469] circa 1488.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Coroner, County Perth in 1492.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Thomas Stewart, 2nd Lord Innermeath and Lady Janet Keith
2 CONT *1. Richard Stewart, 3rd Lord Innermeath+[2] b. b 1504, d. 1532
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VIII, page 139. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VIII, page 140.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://gw.geneanet.org/brynjulf?lang=no&pz=tor&nz=langballe&ocz=0&p=thomas&n=stewart&oc=4
2 CONT --------------------
