3 CITY Dunollych (Dunollie)
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1462
1 OCCU Tenth Chief of the Clan MacDougall. Married a daughter of Robert Stewart, the 2nd Stewart Lord of Lorn.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan MacDougall, 10th of Dunollie and of Lorn is the son of Dougall Macdougall, 9th of Dunollie and of Lorn and unknown MacDonnell.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married unknown daughter Stewart, daughter of Robert Stewart, 1st Lord Lorn.1 Is said to have m a dau of Robert Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorn (see MORAY, E.)1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alan MacDougall, 10th of Dunollie and of Lorn and unknown daughter Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir John Macdougall, 11th of Dunollie and of Lorn+2 d. 1480
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Burke's Peerage''' 107th edition Vol II page 2480
2 CONT
2 CONT >* Alan MacDougall of Dunollie and of Lorn; is said to have m a dau of Robert Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorn and had
2 CONT
2 CONT >>* Sir John MacDougall of Dungallie and of Lorn; m Gyllis or Egidia, dau of sir Colin Campbell 1sy=t of Glenorchy and d 1480, leaving ...
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>* 1a Alexander
2 CONT >>>* Anna Margaret; m Alexander MacKenzie 7th of Kinstall, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Alan of Dunollie: Tenth Chief of the clan and son of our Ninth Chief, Dougal of Dunollie. Married a daughter of Robert Stewart, the second Stewart Lord of Lorn.
2 CONT [ http://www.macdougall.org/chiefs.html ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.highlandstrathearn.com/content/maclarens
2 CONT
2 CONT This occurred when Sir John’s wife died in 1463 and sent word to his lady in Ardveich that she and her son join him at Dunstaffnage Castle for the wedding. No doubt it was a merry affair, and was only marred by the fact that the b
2 CONC ridegroom-to-be was stabbed to death as he walked across the chapel lawn to the ceremony. This called for some hasty action, and the ceremony was hurried through with Sir John’s last act being to slip the ring on to the bride’s fi
2 CONC nger, before expiring. His assailant was Alan MacDougall who coveted the Stewart lands of Lorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
