2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Byres Castle - ruins, thought to date back to the 16th century. During the Rough Wooing the English are said to have dismantled Byres in 1548, and it was probably rebuilt in its current form following the English departure from Ha
2 CONC ddington in 1549. The existence of an earlier castle is proved by the fact that the title of John, 1st Lord Lindsay of The Byres was created in 1445.
