1 NAME John Gordon, younger of Scardargue, 1st of Auchleuchries
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1409
2 ADDR
3 CITY Scudargue
3 STAE Aberdeenshire
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1496
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} a son Had John, of Auchlenchries who was slain at battle of Flodden, 1513, under the command of Alexander, 3rd Earl of Huntly. (Stirnet says he died about 1496).
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=ancestorsearch&id=I4064
2 CONT * http://www.patrickspeople.co.uk/ourfamily/3084.htm ____________________________________
2 CONT *'''John Gordon1
2 CONT *M, #44309
2 CONT *Father      John Gordon1
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth (Margaret) Maitland1
2 CONT *'''     John Gordon was born at of Auchlenchries, Aberdeenshire, Scotland.1 He married Elizabeth Abernethy, daughter of Laurence Abernethy, 1st Lord Abernethy of Saltoun and Margaret.2,1
2 CONT *'''Family      Elizabeth Abernethy 
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **James Gordon, 1st Laird of Cairnborrow+3
2 CONT **John Gordon+1 d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11580] A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, Vol. IV, by John Burke, Esq., p. 46.
2 CONT * 2.[S11586] The Scots Peerage, Vol. VII, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 407.
2 CONT * 3.[S11649] Clan MacFarlane & Associated Clans Genealogy.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1474.htm#i44309 _________________________
2 CONT *'''The thanage of Fermartyn including the district commonly called Formartine : its proprietors, with genealogical deductions; its parishes, ministers, churches, churchyards, antiquities &c. (1894)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/thanageoffermart00byutemp
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/3/mode/1up
2 CONT *   I. John Gordon of Essie or Scurdargue (as to whose genealogical status see article on Pitlurg) married Elizabeth Maitland, daughter of Robert Maitland, laird of Gight, by whom he had three sons. 
2 CONT **'''	I. John Gordon of Auchleuchries. 
2 CONT **	II. William Gordon of Tillytarmont. 
2 CONT **	III. James Gordon, ancestor of the Gordons of Haddo and Methlick. 
2 CONT *   II. — This James Gordon of Haddo and Methlick married Canea Harper, half-portioner of Methlick, of which her father, John Harper, called in the latin of the charters "Johannes de Citharista," was the owner. .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/308/mode/1up
2 CONT **	John Gordon of Essie. 
2 CONT *   He was called John of Scurdarg from his residence being at that place within the lands of Essie, which were granted to him by his father, Sir John Gordon. He had also Ardlaw in Aberdour, "noveritis me dedisse et vendidisse dil
2 CONC ecto et speciali meo Johanni de Gordon filio naturali quondam domini Johannis de Gordone militis omnes meas terras de Ardlach, &c." In the charter just quoted his wife's name is given as Elizabeth. The old MS. histories of the fam
2 CONC ily call the wife of whom the children were born Margaret. She was certainly daughter to Robert Matulant of Natyrdul (Maitland of Netherdale), who was grandson of Sir Robert Maitland of Thirlstane. Her brother was Sir Patrick Mait
2 CONC land of Netherdale, Gight, and Shivas. They had three sons and two daughters : — 
2 CONT **'''	I. John, ancestor of Pitlurg and other branches. 
2 CONT **	II. William, of Tillytarmont, ancestor of Craig, Lesmoir, and many others. 
2 CONT **	III. James, of Methlic, ancestor of the Gordons of Haddo, now Earls of Aberdeen. 
2 CONT **	1. Elizabeth, married, 1436, to James Baird of Ordinhivas. 
2 CONT **	2. Janet, married to Annand of Auchterellon. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/309/mode/1up
2 CONT *John Gordon, as has been already mentioned, left Essie to Alexander Gordon, his son by Henault Macleod, to whom he was hand-fasted. His eldest son, by his marriage with Elizabeth Maitland, became 
2 CONT *'''   II. John Grordon of Auchleuchry. 
2 CONT *'''   He got from his father the lands of Auchleuchry. He married Dame Elizabeth Abernethy, daughter of Lawrence, Lord Saltoun, of Rothiemay, and had issue two sons : 
2 CONT **	I. John, his successor. 
2 CONT **	II. James, of Cairnburrow, ancestor of Rothiemay, Glenbucket, Park, &c. 
2 CONT *'''John Gordon was succeeded by his son,
2 CONT *   III. John Gordon of Auchleuchry. 
2 CONT *   He obtained a portion of the Gordon territory by receiving the lands of Botarie from the Earl of Huntly ; had seisin of the lands of Kindrocht in 1487   In 1493, he purchased the lands of Longweir (Lungair or Lungar) and Hilto
2 CONC n in the county of Kincardine, forming the southern half of the barony of Dunnottar, and in the same year those of Cromy, Little Warthill, with the part of Harlaw and the Glack. In this deed he is designated John Gordon of Auchleu
2 CONC chry.  In 1506, he got a charter from Sir Alexander Seton of the lands of Kinmundy, Mylhill, Myllbrecks, and Petremarcus, and in the same year, he purchased the lands of Kyninmonde in Lonmay.  John Gordon married Barbara, daughter
2 CONC  of Alexander Forbes of Pitsligo, by his wife, Dame ___Hay, daughter of William, first Earl of Errol, by whom he had a son,  .... etc. ______________________
2 CONT *'''John Gordon1
2 CONT *M, #329391
2 CONT *Last Edited=4 Jan 2009
2 CONT *'''     John Gordon is the son of John Gordon of Scurdargue and Elizabeth Maitland.1
2 CONT *'''      He was ancestor of the Gordons of Pitlurg.1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2011. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p32940.htm#i329391 ___________________________________
2 CONT *	'Gordon01'
2 CONT *Because of similarities between their coats-of-arms, it is thought not unlikely that the Gordons were originally a cadet branch of the family of Swinton. There are many Gordons mentioned in early records. The following pulls toge
2 CONC ther the information shown in TSP (Huntly) but is not 'secure' until the Sir Adam of Gordon who was Justiciar of Lothian in 1305 and was one of the Ambassadors who carried the famous 'Declaration of Arbroath' to the Pope in 1320. 
2 CONC That Sir Adam was the first to be named in BP1934 (Huntly).
2 CONT *?? of Gordon 
2 CONT **	1. Richard of Gordon
2 CONT ***		A. Sir Thomas of Gordon (d c1233)
2 CONT ****			i. Sir Thomas of Gordon (dspm c1259)
2 CONT ****			  m. Marjorie
2 CONT *****				a. Alicia of Gordon (d 1280)
2 CONT *****				  m. Sir Adam of Huntly @@ just below
2 CONT **	2. Adam of Gordon (a 1190)
2 CONT ***		A. Alexander of Huntly 
2 CONT ****			i. William of Huntly (d Crusade)
2 CONT ****			ii. Adam of Huntly 
2 CONT *****				a. Sir Adam of Huntly
2 CONT *****				  m. Alicia of Gordon (d 1280, dau of Sir Thomas of Gordon) @@ just above
2 CONT ******					(1) Adam of Gordon (d by 1296)
2 CONT ******					  m. Marjorie
2 CONT *******						(A) Sir Adam of Gordon (d c1328, Justiciar of Lothian, Ambassador)
2 CONT *******						TSP names Sir Adam's wife but reports that her "family is unknown". A site visitor (CD, 16.09.08) has kindly drawn our attention to the fact that some web sites tentatively suggest that she was daughter of Sir David o
2 CONC f Strathbogie, Earl of Atholl, by Isabella Chilham some of whose lands eventually came to this family and formed the basis of the earldom of Huntly. We have not seen this supported by any reputable source.
2 CONT *******						  m. Amabilla
2 CONT ********							(i) Sir Adam Gordon of that ilk (d 1351)
2 CONT *********								(a) John Gordon of that ilk (d before 02.1360-1)
2 CONT *********								  m. Elizabeth
2 CONT **********									((1)) Sir John Gordon of that ilk (d unm before 11.10.1395)
2 CONT **********									  p. Elizabeth Cruickshanks (dau of the laird of Aswanley)
2 CONT ***********										((A)) John Gordon of Scurdargue 
2 CONT ***********										  m. Margaret Maitland (dau of Robert Maitland of Netherdale)
2 CONT ************'''											((i)) John Gordon, 1st of Auchleuchries
2 CONT ************'''											  m. Elizabeth Abernethy (dau of Laurence Abernethy, 1st Lord Saltoun)
2 CONT ************											((ii)) William Gordon of Tillytermont (b c1405, d c1480)
2 CONT ************											  m. dau of Sir John Rutherford
2 CONT ************											((iii)) James Gordon (of Methlic)
2 CONT ***********										  p. Henault (dau of McLeod of Harris)
2 CONT ************											((iv)) Alexander Gordon ancestor of Gordons of Buckie
2 CONT ************											  m. dau of Macleod of Harris
2 CONT ************											((v)) Adam Gordon
2 CONT ***********										((B))  .... etc.
2 CONT ********							(ii) William of Gordon of Stitchill (d c1370)
2 CONT ********							(iii) John Gordon
2 CONT ********							(iv) Thomas Gordon (b after 1300, a 1351)
2 CONT ********							(v) Mary Gordon
2 CONT ********							  m. Walter FitzGilbert de Hamilton, 1st of Cadzow (a 1296, 1323)
2 CONT *Main sources: TSP (Huntly), BP1934 (Huntly).
2 CONT *From: Stirnet.com
