1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AI Overview     5/10/26
2 CONT     William Abernethy, 2nd Lord Saltoun of Abernethy (c. 1430–1488), married Isabella Borthwick. She was the daughter of Laird William Borthwick of Borthwick and Beatrice Sinclair, and died on February 10, 1492. They had two known
2 CONC  daughters, Jane and Christian.Key Details regarding the 2nd Lord Saltoun:Wife: Isabella Borthwick (1428–1492).Children: Jane Abernathy (married Walter Ogston) and Christian Abernathy (married John Wemyss).Succession: As he lacked
2 CONC  a male heir, the title passed to his brother, James Abernethy, 3rd Lord Saltoun.Background: Son of Laurence Abernethy, 1st Lord Saltoun.Note: Some sources mistakenly identify the 2nd Lord as having a wife named Margaret, but hist
2 CONC orical accounts of the 2nd Lord's lack of a male heir in Scots Peerage confirm Isabella Borthwick as his wife.
