1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page for Alexander Irvine of Drum:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p44746.htm#i447458
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Irvine of Drum [1]
2 CONT *M, #447458, 
2 CONT *d. December 1493
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=25 Nov 2012 Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Irvine, 5th of Drum was the son of Alexander Irvine of Drum, younger and unknown daughter Abernethy.[2] He married, firstly, Elizabeth Forbes, daughter of Alexander Forbes, 1st Lord Forbes and Lady Elizabeth Douglas.[3] 
2 CONC He married, secondly, unknown daughter Lindsay.[4] He died in December 1493.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alexander Irvine of Drum
2 CONT *1. Sir Alexander Irvine of Drum+[1] d. b 4 Dec 1527
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1.   [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2063. Hereinafter cited as Burke'
2 CONC s Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2.    [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.    [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1451.
2 CONT *4.    [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2062.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sheriff of Aberdeen in 1471 he attacked the house of Sir Walter Lindsay of Beufort with a large force. The Lords of the Council fired him and sent him to prison. 
