2 CONT '''28 April 1625: Instrument of Sasine in favour of Ronald McRonald of Castelvorff, uncle of John Mackronnald of Moydort, Captain of Clanronnald, in liferent and after his death heritably to Ronald McRonnald, his eldest son by Mar
2 CONC garet McDonald, daughter of the late Angus McDonald of Downnyvack, of the 13 penny lands of Borrow in Beanbecula and others, within the sheriffdom of Inverness as principal, and the 7 penny lands of Borrowneishivichtterach and oth
2 CONC ers in warrandice thereof in case of eviction; following upon a feu charter by John McDonald of Moydort dated 12 April 1625. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f10&st=1&tc=y&t
2 CONC l=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201&ro=m&df=1620&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald (Clanranald Papers), reference GD201/1/10]'''   
