2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1637: Charter by Duncan Baine of Logie Wester to Thomas Ross, servitor to Adam Hebburne, clerk of taxation to His Majesty, and his heirs of the kirklands of Ulladill, with the crofts thereof called Rifleuch Ridorrach oth
2 CONC erwise called the Glen of Ulladill and the wood called Dunegold and in the earldom of Ross and shire of Inverness. To be held by the said Thomas Ross and his foresaids of the King and his successors in feu and heritage, for paymen
2 CONC t yearly of the sum of £6.13.4 in name of feu for the said lands of Ulladill and the said wood of Dunegold, and for the said crofts 12 pennies as the ancient feu and 6 pennies in augmentation of rental of the same. Dated at Ulladi
2 CONC ll. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD305%2f1%2f28%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=baine+of+logie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacKenzie Family,
2 CONC  Earls of Cromartie (Cromartie Muniments), reference GD305/1/28/6]'''
2 CONT
