1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR DUGALD CAMPBELL OF AUCHENBRECK Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1640: Charter by Donald McLauchlane, captain of Insedonnell, and Colin McLauchlane, his lawful first born son and heir apparent, in implement of their part in a contract of marriage made 3 March last between them and Si
2 CONC r Dugald Campbell of Auchinbreck, knight, bart., for himself and Moir Campbell, his natural daughter, giving said Moir Campbell in liferent the 20 shilling land of Couldconnell, the 16 shilling and 8 penny land of Dupenni alias Ba
2 CONC llegowne, the 3 merk land of Ereden, and 2½ merk land of Camismachgawine, in barony of Lochawe in sheriffdom of Argyll, in full satisfaction of all her third part as relict spouse of said Colin after his decease, with precept of s
2 CONC asine directed to John Campbell of Orgaig, baillie in that part to said Donald and Colin. Written by Donald Camerone, servitor to George Campbell, sheriff clerk of Argyll At Inversary Witnesses:- George Campbell and Donald Cameron
2 CONC e, Alexander Campbell and Patrick Denneistoune, also servitors to said George Campbell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD437%2f148&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=moir+campbell&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, MacNeill of Taynish and Campbell of Danna Titles, reference GD437/148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Dugald Campbell of Auchinbreck</strong>, son and heir of Duncan Campbell of Auchinbreck and Castlewene, by Mary (married 1567), daugher and heir of William Macleod of Dunvegan, was born of 1570; Knighted by James I, a
2 CONC nd was created a Baronet 12 or 24 January, sealed 23 December 1628, but not entered in the Great Seal Register [S], with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, of which he had 
2 CONC seizin in December 1628. He was a Royalist. He married firstly, Mary, sister of Thomas, 1st Viscount Fentoun [S], 3rd and youngest daughter of the Hon. Sir Alexander Erskine of Gogar, by his first wite Margaret, daughter of George
2 CONC  (Home), Lord Home [S]. He married secondly, Isabel Boyd. He died, at an advanced age, 1641."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n357/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 339
