2 CONT  THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT In the  HISTORY THE HOUSE AND CLAN MACKAY she is described as "the other married Gilbert Murray, laird of Pulrossie, who was slain at the battle of Pinkie in 1547."
2 CONT
2 CONT in the Scottish  peerage she is  described as "2. Margaret,  who was married to Walter Murray of Polrossie"
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT i. A daughter, who married Hugh Murray of Aberseross and to
2 CONT whom she bore Hugh, " son and heir of Hugh Moray of Aberseross and grandson, and one of the heirs, of John MacKay of Strathnaver," as is recorded in a charter by Wm. Sutherland of Duffus to the said Hugh Moray, dated 21st February
2 CONC , 1581. See Inventory of Dunrobin Papers in the Blk. JIS.pg. 85
2 CONT
2 CONT  THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============
2 CONT
2 CONT Scottish peerage lists her as "1. a daughter, who was married to Hugh Moray of Aberscross, and to whom she bore Hugh,  son and heir of Hugh Moray of  berscross, and grandson, and one of the heirs of, John Mackay of Strathnaver, as
2 CONT stated in a charter by Sutherland of Duffus."
2 CONT
2 CONT In the   HISTORY THE HOUSE AND CLAN MACKAY  she is described as "One of his  daughters married Hugh Murray, laird of Aberscors (Shiberscross)"
