1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JAMES CRICHTON OF RUTHVEN===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Laing Charters===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 August 1610: Charter by Sir James Creichtoun of Ruthvens, hereditary proprietor of the subjects named, with the consent of Dame Margaret Maxwell, Lady Ruthvenis, his wife, and others [not named], in terms of a contract dated 
2 CONC 29th June [1610], between them on one part, and Robert Erskine, royal tailor, and Agnes Sandilands, his spouse, on the other part, granting and alienating to them an annualrent of 600 merks Scots (representing a principal sum of 6
2 CONC 000 merks) from the lands of the mains of Ruthvend, the Coittown, Mylnetown, with mill, mill lands etc., in the barony of Ruthven and sheriffdom of Forfar. To be held to the grantees in fee and heritage of the granter and his heir
2 CONC s for one penny blench etc. At Kellie, 8th August 1610. Witnesses, Mr. George Dewar, Robert Quhytlaw, John Wylie, Mr. William Levingstoun, and Robert Scollay, notary. [https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaing00edin/page/383/mod
2 CONC e/1up Laing Charters: charter number 1579]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1622: Precept under the quarter seal by King James the Sixth for infefting in terms of a charter, John Inglis, servant of Sir George Erskine of of Invertiel, knight, in liferent, and his daughter Katherine Inglis, her 
2 CONC heirs, etc. in fee, the lands of Ruthvens, Balbirnie, and Brigton of Ruthvens, all lying in the sheriffdom of Forfar; which lands belonged to James Crichton, son of the late Sir James Crichton of Ruthvens, and were apprised from h
2 CONC im on 2nd April instant by a decree in favour of John Inglis and his daughter. Precept dated at Holyroodhouse, 24th April 1622. [https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaing00edin/page/458/mode/1up Laing Charters: charter number 19
2 CONC 04]'''
