1 NAME James /Stewart of Eday and Tullas/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Stewart of Eday and Tullas
2 _MARNM Stewart of Eday and Tullas
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 7 JUN 1653
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JAMES STEWART OF EDAY (aka SIR JAMES STEWART OF ETHAY) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Stewart of Eday, here treated, is the son of Robert Stewart, Earl of Orkney, and his wife Janet Kennedy. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/573/mode/1up The Scots Peerage] He died before 7 Jun
2 CONC e 1653. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f70&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+sir+james+stewart+of&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD31/70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Gentleman of the Bedchamber ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Stewart of Eday and Tullos was a gentleman of the bedchamber and received a pension from his father's lands in Holyrood, Edinburgh. He married Dame Margaret Lyon, daughter of Thomas, Master of Glamis. [https://archive
2 CONC .org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/573/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 573]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 June 1653: Disposition by Colonel John Stewart, second son of deceased Sir James Stewart of Ethay, knight, in favour of Captain Robert Stewart, his brother, eldest son of said deceased Sir James, of the 4½d. udal land in Howb
2 CONC uster, under his house of Corsquoy, in island of Sanday, disponed to him by Edward Cok, merchant in Kirkwall, and disponed to said Edward Cok by John Beg, eldest son and heir of deceased James Beg of Corsquoy, in the island of San
2 CONC day, and by Magnus Beg, only son and heir of deceased William Beg of Mussetter, in the island of Schapinscha. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f70&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+sir+
2 CONC james+stewart+of&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/573/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 572 -3]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart20.php Stirnet: Stewart 20]'''
