1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY MARGARET HAMILTON Countess of Crawford Lindsay ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Lady Margaret Hamilton, Countess of Crawford Lindsay, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Hamilton-Lady-Belhaven/6000000084228445871?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1568750771639&through=60000000
2 CONC 10120670637 who was her bastard sister'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Hamilton is the daughter of James, Marquess of Hamilton, and his wife Lady Anne Cunningham. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/134/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 134] [https://archive.org/detai
2 CONC ls/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/375/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 375]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Hamilton, Countess of Crawford Lindsay, is reported to have died in 1678. [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4aa/hamilton09.php Stirnet: Hamilton 09]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Margaret Hamilton married John, Earl of Crawfurd Lindsay, and they had issue.  [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog#page/n50/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, III, p. 36]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''May 30. Dated at Strother: Margaret Hamilton, wife of John, 17th earl of Crawford, to Anne, lady Findlater, her niece.The duchess [of Rothes, writer's daughter,] is safely brought to bed of a daughter; writer's daughter [Helen,
2 CONC  wife of Sir Robert Sinclair of] Stevenston of a boy, and writer's daughter [in law, wife of Patrick Lindsay of] Kilbirnie, of a daughter. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD248%2f567%2
2 CONC f89&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, Seafield Papers, reference GD248/567/89]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Oct. 8. Dated at Strother: Margaret Hamilton to Mary, lady Findlater, her niece.Thankful to learn that recipient has survived childbirth; suggests a plaster; Lady Newark says she has cured many by this means; further rather ill
2 CONC egible details. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD248%2f566%2f84&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, Seafield Paper
2 CONC s, reference GD248/567/84]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
