2 CONC antations in Virginia with goods from Scotland and England. John was a Cavalier: the term  •Note: applied to the followers of the royalist cause of King Charles I, of England. In her book, Bork states that she  •Note: believes tha
2 CONC t John became ill, perhaps even wounded by Indians, in the later part of 1685. By 3 March 1686, he had died  •Note: and his estate was ordered inventoried.  •Note:  •Note: On 28 December 1668, Thomas Gaines deeded 365 acres of lan
2 CONC d "for diverse good causes and valuable consideracons me  •Note: thereunto moveing" to John Burnett. The 365 acres was part of a patent of 730 acres.4 On 15 May 1691, this land was  •Note: surveyed at the request of Jno Burnett, S
2 CONC on to the within Jno. Burnett and described "beginning at the great leaning  •Note: Red Oake above ye land of Hold by ye Maine Pocoson of Piscattaway Creeke being the beginning of ye said Patent, and  •Note: runing thence North 11
