2 CONC  white Oakes by a Path; thence S. 21 d. 15 m. W. 268 poles to ye siad Pocoson to three Maples, and thence down alongst  •Note: ye said Pocoson its severall courses to ye place it began." It would appear that John Burnett did quite
2 CONC  well and could  •Note: be considered among the upper class of the Colony. The will of his wife, Lucretia, contained many luxury items that  •Note: would be used by a lady of the upper class. John sons, John II and Thomas Junr., a
