2 CONC was christened 1610 in St. Nicholas Parish Church,  •Note: Aberdeen, Scotland. He died Mar 1668 in Rappahannock Co., (later Essex), Virginia. John married Lucretia "Lues" JOHNSON  •Note: on 1657. crossed the Atlantic in 1635 on th
2 CONC e ship Abraham Lincoln First Burnett to immigrate to America Married  •Note: Lucrecia in 1657.  •Note:  •Note: His wife was his cousin.  •Note:  •Note: John Burnett is called "Of Aberdeen" in a warrant from King Charles dated: Mar
2 CONC ch 13, 1638, In a land Patent on May 23,  •Note: 1637 he called "Merchant of Edinborough". He supplied the colonies with tobacco  •Note:  •Note: John Burnett was christened at St. Nicholas Parish Church in 1610. He  •Note: married
2 CONC  his cousin Lucretia Johnston in 1657. Lucretia was the daughter of Andrew  •Note: Johnston and was christened at St., Nicholas Parish Church in 1629. At age 24 John and his wife Lucretia boarded the  •Note: Ship Abraham of London
2 CONC , Mr. John Baker, Master, bound for Virginia.  •Note:  •Note: John received the Warrant or Charter to trade in Virginia from King Charles in  •Note: 1638. John and Lucretia bought a Plantation and several hundred acres of land in 
2 CONC Old  •Note: Rappanhnnock County in Virginia. They started the family business of Merchant with ships, trading in the import and  •Note: export of tobacco. The Johnstons also owned acreage adjoining the Burnett Plantation. John and
2 CONC  Lucretia had five  •Note: children John II, Thomas, Charles, Phebe, and Sara all born on the Burnett Plantation. John died 1686 leaving the  •Note: Burnett Plantation and family business to his beloved wife Lucretia, John II and 
2 CONC Thomas. Lucretia died 1709 and was  •Note: buried beside John in the Burnett Plantation Cemetery.  •Note: Source: The Burnetts and Their Connections, June Baldwin Bork, Vol. 1, pg. 1  •Note:  •Note: "On July 2, 1638, King Charles 
