1 NAME George /Johnston/ of Caskieben, 1st Baronet
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Johnston
2 NSFX of Caskieben, 1st Baronet
2 _MARNM Johnston
1 NAME Sir George Johnston of Caskieben, 1st Baronet
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dyce
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1595
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Johnston of Caskieben</strong>, co Aberdeen, son and heir of John Johnston, of the same (who had sold the fee of Johnston in 1595, though retaining the superiority) by his 1st wife Janet, daughter of (--) Turing, o
2 CONC f Foveran, co Aberdeen, succeeded his father, 4 February 1613/4, and had special service to him in the Barony of Johnston, etc, 3 May 1614, and was created a Baronet [S] 31 March, sealed 23 May 1626, as 'of Caskieben', with rem. t
2 CONC o heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of , presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia entitled the Barony of Johnston, of which he had seizin in the said month of May, and again in November 1626, was Sheriff of co Aberdeen, 1630-
2 CONC 31. In 1641 he and his son were cited before Parliament as incendiaries. He married Elizabeth, daughter of William Forbes of Tolquhoun, co Aberdeen."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n325/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 307
