1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Johnston III of Crimond was one of the sureties on the marriage contract for his brother-in-law John Johnston which was signed on 26 October 1597 at Lundie, Scotland, prior to John's marriage to his second w
2 CONC ife Katherine Lundie (Lundy). Robert Johnston III of Crimond was a witness to the sale of the Johnston estate in Leslie Parish, Scotland, to John Leith, Friar of Mongerrie, by his brother-in-law John Johnston of Caskieben in 1595.
2 CONC  Robert Johnston III of Crimond was elected Provost of Aberdeen in the autumn of 1635 but was removed from office by the Lords of the Privy Council in January, 1636. Alexander Jaffray of Kingswell, who converted the Johnstons to Q
2 CONC uakerism, was appointed to replace him. At Michaelmas, 1637, Robert Johnston III of Crimond was re-elected as Provost of Aberdeen and continued in office until Michaelmas, 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sir Robert Johnston III sold Crimond to Robert Burnet and was dead by 1641 when Agnes Johnston was described as his relict.
2 CONT
