1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Arthur also married (2) (or 3) to Barbara GORDON, daughter of John GORDON and Margaret -daughter of the Laird of Widney's (Udny), on 4 Mar 1625. Barbara was born 1587 in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. She died4 Mar 1650 
2 CONC in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. In "Memoir of Arthur Johnston," it states: "After his first wife's decease, he is stated to have married Barbara Gordon, whose parentage is said to be unknown. In Dr. Temple's 'Thanage of Fermartyn,' pg
2 CONC  263, she is claimed as of the Gordon's of Newton. She was the mother of his son William who was born and baptized in 1636, and became in King's college a Regent Professor in 1657, and afterwards Civilist in 1669. Barbara Johnston
2 CONC  survived her husband and lived till 1650, when she was interred in Aberdeen."
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur and third wife, Barbara Gordon, had:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Barbara (b1631). Daughter Barbara Johnston married George Cullen on 14 AUG 1656 at St. Nicholas Chapel in Aberdeen.
2 CONT # Elizabeth (b1633) Daughter Elizabeth Johnston married Lt. Col. James Innes of Sandysyde.  Married 1st George Seaton and 2nd Lt. Col. James Innis.
2 CONT # Margaret (b1635) Margaret married George DALGARNO "son of the laird of Peithill".
2 CONT #William (b1636) William married Helen CULLEN (no children), daughter of George CULLEN and Margery FORBES, George's sister, in 1662. and possibly an 
2 CONT #Edward (b1638). There is no known primary record that identifies Edward Johnston/Johnson [of New Kent VA] as a son of Arthur Johnston and Barbara Gordon. All we know is that Edward was not a son by Arthur's earlier wives, and tha
2 CONC t he "appears" in New Kent Co. records beginning in 1680 for certain and "may" be the Edward Johnson who signed the Bacon's Rebellion grievance document in April, 1677. He may also be the Edward Johnston, cousin of Elizabeth Johns
2 CONC ton Keith, who reportedly accompanied Ann Keith to VA in 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT All except Edward's birth are recorded in the register of St. Nicholas Presbyterian Church in Aberdeen. Barbara Gordon married Arthur Johnston on 4 Mar 1625 (Aberdeen Register of Sasines). 
2 CONT
2 CONT The first child of Arthur and Barbara in the St. Nicholas records was born in 1631. Were their no children from March 1625 until 1631? More likely, the absence of records is due to the fact that this was the period when Arthur was
2 CONC  supposedly in London, serving as "physician ordinary" to Kings James I and Charles I. Any children born in London probably would not have made the St. Nicholas registry (although baptisms sometimes occur well after the fact). Per
2 CONC haps we should look in London records for signs of other children.
2 CONT
