2 CONC .geni.com/people/Margaret-Kerr/6000000006252789885?through=6000000012150705942 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Johnstone of Forresterhill is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Arthur-Johnstone/6000000002250516172?through=6000000033506680328 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Gordon/6000000002250351958?throug
2 CONC h=6000000033506680328 He was born before 15 December 1636, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Aberdeen in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. His baptismal record reads as follows: "Docr Arthor Jonstonne and [ blank space ] Go
2 CONC rdonn ane sone his name Wn bap be Docr James Sibbald Docr Robert Barronne Docr Wm yuile Docr Alexander Ross Docr Patk Dunne prinll of the college Docr Wm Jonstonne Thomas Tolmsonne Mr Patk Chalmers Godfathers." [National Records o
2 CONC f Scotland, Aberdeen Baptisms, reference OPR.168/A/3] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206380514830 Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Regent of King's College in Aberdeen ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1657. Mr. William Johnston. Entrants of 1657-58 (apparently succeeding Rule), 1661-62, 1665-66 ; graduates of 1668-69. Elected Civilist 8th June, 1669. "When Regent he marries Helen Cullen, daughter of Provost Cullen, 23rd Marc
2 CONC h, 1662." Gordon. Son of Arthur Johnston. Davidson's Garioch, p. 366. [https://archive.org/details/officersgraduate00univuoft/page/57/mode/1up Officers and Graduates: 57]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Johnstone of Forresterhill is reported to have died on 18 January 1673. [https://archive.org/details/officersgraduate00univuoft/page/32/mode/1up Officers and Graduates: 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Johnstone of Forresterhill married https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Cullen/6000000193132083919?through=6000000033506680328 [https://archive.org/details/officersgraduate00univuoft/page/57/mode/1up Officers and Graduates
2 CONC : 57] They were booked for proclamation on 23 March 1662, at Old Machar in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. The marriage booking reads as follows: "1662. 23 March. Mr Wm Jonstoune regent gave evidence of his booking in Abn wt Helen Cullen
2 CONC  daughter to provest Cullen they were thryse proclaimed here & married there." [National Records of Scotland, Old Machar Marriages, reference OPR.168/B/6] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206393341821 Image of Ma
2 CONC rriage Record] They were married on 29 April 1662, at Aberdeen in Aberdeenshire, Scotland. The marriage record reads as follows: "1662. Mr William Johnstoune and Helline Cullen mareid the 29 Apryll" [National Records of Scotland, 
2 CONC Aberdeen Marriages, reference OPR.168/A/12] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206393183889 Image of Marriage Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Johnstone/6000000206394038840?through=6000000033506680328 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Arthur-Johnstone/6000000206393536866?through=6000000033506680328 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/George-Johnstone/6000000206394335824?through=6000000033506680328 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/William-Johnstone/6000000206394346839?through=6000000033506680328 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/James-Johnstone/6000000206394726831?through=6000000033506680328 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 November 1663: William Johnstoun, regent of King's College, Old Aberdeen. Granter [Type of Deed] Bond [Office] Dur., volume 7, page 232] [National Records of Scotland, Index to the Register of Deeds for 1663][https://archive
2 CONC .org/details/indexes100scotuoft/indexes100scotuoft/page/249/mode/1up Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 July 1664: William Johnstoun. regent of King's College, Old Aberdeen. Granter [Type of Deed] Discharge [Office] Dur., volume 8, page 508 [National Records of Scotland, Index to the Register of Deeds for 1664] [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/details/indexes200scotuoft/indexes200scotuoft/page/245/mode/1up Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 June 1670: Extract registered heritable bond by Mr. William Johnston of Frosterhill [?Forresterhill] to Mr. Patrick Sandilandis, subprincipal of King's College. [Registered Commissary Court Books Aberdeen 7 November 1671] [h
2 CONC ttps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD74%2f317&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=forresterhill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Burnett of Powis, reference GD74/317]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Old Parochial Registers of Old Machar ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1662: The baptismal record of James Johnstone reads as follows: "Master Wm Johnston off Frosterhill ane son calld James Sr Jon Keith of Keithall Ja: Gordon of Seaton Gorton Ja: Lesly Ja: Sutherland mr off Duffus witness
2 CONC es." [National Records of Scotland, Old Machar Baptisms, reference OPR.168/B/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206417923823 Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1664: The baptismal record of Arthur Johnstone. reads as follows: "1664. i4 July. Mr Wm Johnstoune Regent in K colledge ane sone calld Arthur. Mr Arthur Gordon, [ ? ] Arthur fides. Mr Thomas Sandilands, Commsr Doctr And
2 CONC ru Muir Docr Ludovick Gordon. Mr Alexr Patton. Mr John forbes witness." [National Records of Scotland, Old Machar Baptisms, reference OPR.168/B/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206421981887 Image of Baptismal 
2 CONC Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 April 1669: The baptismal record of William Johnstone reads as follows: "1669. 13 Apryll. Mr William Jonstoune of Froster hill [ ane ] sone calld Wm [ ? ] Earle Marshall Pat : Lord Bp of Abn Mr Robert [ ?  ] and Wm forbes ba
2 CONC ilye witness." [National Records of Scotland, Old Machar Baptisms, reference OPR.168/B/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000206421779822 Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/officersgraduate00univuoft/page/n8/mode/1up Officers and Graduates of University & King's College, Aberdeen, MVD-MDCCCLX. Edited by Peter John Anderson, MA., LL.B. (New Spalding Club, Aberdeen, MDCC
2 CONC CXCIII), 399 pp. including index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Johnston (eldest lawful son in 1659) . . . . . This son William is the only one of Dr. Arthur's descendants, in a direct line, of whom we have been enabled to procure any certain account. He was designed "of Forrester-h
2 CONC ill," from the circumstance of his having been proprietor of a small property so called (and still known by the same name), in the neighborhood of Aberdeen. He was, in the year 1657, when he could scarcely have attained majority, 
2 CONC appointed one of the regents of King's College, Aberdeen. This office he held until 1669, when he was promoted to the Chair of Civil Law in the same University. He is believed to have died about 1673, as in that year he was succee
2 CONC ded, as Civilist, by Sir George Nicolson of Kemnay, also a native of Aberdeen.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In December 1659, Mr. William Johnston, "one of the Regents of King's College, eldest lawful son of the deceased Mr. Arthur Johnston, Doctor of Medicine," was, as appears form the Burgess Register of the City of Aberdeen, admit
2 CONC ted a burgess of guild "jure paternitatis." He married, in April 1662, Helen Cullen, third and youngest daughter of George Cullen, Provost of Aberdeen, by his first wife Marjorie Forbes. It does not appear that there was any survi
2 CONC ving issue of this marriage; and about 1673 the lands of Forrester-hill were adjudged for debt; the widow of the Professor having, however, within a year or two of the last mentioned date, made good her claim to a part of the rent
2 CONC s of the appraised lands.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[ Arthur ] Johnston's son William (b.1636) became a professor of civil law at Marischal College. In 1670, William Johnston was among the leaders of an insurrection at the College in which almost all the faculty and student body
2 CONC  declared themselves Quakers as a way to defeat unbearable political pressures on the College from Episcopalian and Covenant (Presbyterian) forces then battling for religious supremacy in Scotland. [http://oursoutherncousins.com/T
2 CONC HE%20SCOTTISH%20JOHNSTON'S.pdf Johnstone of Caskieben: 10-11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/funeralsermonsor00shanuoft/page/n4/mode/1up The Funeral Sermons, Orations, Epitaphs, and other pieces on the death of the Right Rev. Patrick Forbes, Bishop of Aberdeen. With Biographical Memoir an
2 CONC d Notes, by Charles Farqcuar Shand, Advocate (Spotiswode Society, Edinburgh, M.DCCC.XLV), 477 pp. including index, additions and corrections]'''
2 CONT # '''[http://oursoutherncousins.com/THE%20SCOTTISH%20JOHNSTON'S.pdf Johnstone of Caskieben]'''
