2 CONT >There is no known primary record that identifies Edward Johnston/Johnson [of New Kent VA] as a son of Arthur Johnston and Barbara Gordon. All we know is that Edward was not a son by Arthur's earlier wives, and that he "appears" i
2 CONC n New Kent Co. records beginning in 1680 for certain and "may" be the Edward Johnson who signed the Bacon's Rebellion grievance document in April, 1677. He may also be the Edward Johnston, cousin of Elizabeth Johnston Keith, who r
2 CONC eportedly accompanied Ann Keith to VA in 1676.
