1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Burke, Bernard, Sir. [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera00inburk#page/38/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic dictionary of the peerage and baronetage of the British Empire]. London : Harrison 1869. page 
2 CONC 38
2 CONT
2 CONT The entry in Burke's states that he was born in Fermanagh. One of the contributors to this profile gives his place of birth as Stonetown, Ulster. No Stonetown or Stonestown in Ulster can be identified, but Edmund settled at Stones
2 CONC town, King's County (now Offaly) according to 'Pedigree of Armstrong of Mangerton in Scotland' (National Library of Ireland GO Ms. 171). 
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the contributors to this profile gives his place of death as Boston. However, John Armstrong's 'The pedigree of the family of Armstrong' (National Library of Ireland Ms 5216) records that he was an officer in Charles I's ar
2 CONC my, was a Justice of the Peace, was sheriff for King's County, died at Stonestown which he had received for life from his wife's family the Hamiltons, and was buried at Tissaran in the Hamilton family vault.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-418748181-2-616495/matthew-edmund-armstrong-in-myheritage-family-trees MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 25 2022,
2 CONC  9:36:46 UTC''
