1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Alexander, second Earl of Linlithgow</strong>, had been appointed in his father's lifetime an Extraordinary Lord of Session, 13 January 1610, and was admitted a member of the Privy Council 17 February 1624...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, first (contract dated at Huntly and Callendar 29 April and 4 May 1611), Elizabeth Gordon, second daughter of George, Marquess of Huntly. This cost the minister of Slamannan, who married them, the penalty of depositi
2 CONC on. She died in childbed in July 1616...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, secondly (contract 16 and 17 October 1620), Mary Douglas, eldest daughter of William, tenth Earl of Angus."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/446/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. V, page 446
