4 CONT Name George Lindsay, 3rd Lord Spynie  [1, 2, 3]  
4 CONT Suffix 3rd Lord Spynie  
4 CONT Born of, Auchtermonzie, Fife, Scotland Find all individuals with events at this location  
4 CONT Gender Male  
4 CONT AFN 9FB2-ZH  
4 CONT Died Jan 1670/71  [2, 3]  
4 CONT Buried 21 Jan 1670/71  Holyroodhouse, Canongate, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland Find all individuals with events at this location  [2]  
4 CONT Notes  
4 CONT ◦IDENTITY: Served heir-male to his father in the family estates in Forfar and other counties
4 CONT  on 12 June 1646, and on the same date he also expede a general service as heir-male of his brother-german Alexander, Master of Spynie. On 8 November 1666 he was served as nearest and lawful heir-male of David, twelfth Earl of Cra
4 CONC wford. On the death of Ludovic, sixteenth Earl of
4 CONT  Crawford, Lord Spynie became the head of the family of Lindsay. [2]
4 CONT ◦KINSHIP: 2nd son and heir.
4 CONT  KINSHIP: Brother and heir of Alexander LINDSAY, "Master of Spynie".
4 CONT
4 CONT  MILITARY: Colonel for Angus, Scotland of the Scots Army 1648; commanded troop of 80 horse from the sheriffdom of Stirling and Clackmannan; Colonel of Foot for Angus, Scotland.
4 CONT
4 CONT  OFFICE: Sat in Parliament 1663, 1669 and 1670.
4 CONT  ASSIGNMENTS: Served on a committee for regulating the Army.
4 CONT
4 CONT  TITLES: Master of Spynie.
4 CONT  TITLES: Succeeded father, in 1646 as Lord Spynie, title created 1590.
4 CONT  TITLES: Forfeiture> By proclamation 1654.
4 CONT
4 CONT  PUNISHMENT: Imprisoned> Taken prisoner at Worcester; committed to the Tower; at liberty for the benefit of his health 1652.
4 CONT  PUNISHMENT: Forfeiture> Forfeited by proclamation 1654.
4 CONT
4 CONT  CONDITION: spm> Died without male issue.
4 CONT
