1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===PATRICK LYON OF BRIGTOUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lyon of Brigtoun is the eldest son of Frederick Lyon of Brigtoun. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2855&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lyon+of+brigtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&d
2 CONC f=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD45/16/2855]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1654: Bond by Frederick Lyon of Brigtoun and Patrick Lyon, fiar thereof, his eldest son, the said Frederick being tutor to Patrick, Earl of Kingorne, to appoint factors and chamberlains to manage the estate of the sa
2 CONC id Earl by the advice and consent of Patrick, Earl of Panmure, grandfather to the said Earl, and George, Lord Brechin, his son [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2855&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lyon+of+brigtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2855]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 February 1666: Charge to enter heir at the instance of James, Lord Ogilvie, against [David] Erskine of Dune, eldest son and apparent heir of Sir Alexander Erskine of Dun, and [Patrick] Lyon, eldest son and apparent heir of [
2 CONC blank] Lyon of Brigtoun. 22 February 1666. With relevant papers. (5 items). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/overview.aspx?st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD16%2f41%2f464&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Rec
2 CONC ords of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/41/464]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ll/lyon02.php Stirnet Lyon 02]
