2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1672: Ante-Nuptial Marriage Contract between Agnes Steuart and Robert Steuart of Lethindie, on the one part, and John Mcphersone in Noide beig with consent of William Mcphersone, apparent of Nuide, and Andrew Mcpherson
2 CONC e of Wester Reates, on the other, whereby the sum of 700 merks is to be added to Agnes' tocher of 500 merks and the whole secured in land. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f94&st=
2 CONC 1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/94]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1672: Discharge by William McIntoshe of Borlum to Donald and William Mcphersone, elder and younger of Nude, for 21/12 merks due by them to the deceased Lachlan Grant, minister at Kingusie, to which said William McInt
2 CONC oshe had right by assignation from Alexander Grant, son and executor dative of said Lachlan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f96&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lachlan+grant&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1675: Obligation by William M'Phersone [McPherson] of Nuid to fulfil the terms of his marriage-contract by obtaining a confirmation of the liferent right of Isobel M'Intoshe [McIntosh], his wife, in the two davochs of 
2 CONC Nuids. John M'Phersone [McPherson] of Bellichroane [Ballachroan] is cautioner. Dated at Nuide [Nuid], 30th August 1675; witnesses, John M'Pherson [McPherson] in Blarikie [Blaragie], and James and John, lawful sons of Donald M'Pher
2 CONC sone [McPherson] of Nuide. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f560&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of 
2 CONC Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/560]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December c. 1690: Contract of Friendship and Alliance, and copy thereof, between Alexander McDonell of Glengarrie and Duncan Mcpherson of Cluny. [The contract is not signed by the principals but by Sir Aeneas Mcpherson, advoc
2 CONC ate, and William Mcpherson of Nuide as witnesses and consenters to Cluny's signature] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f327&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=18
2 CONC 00&di=n National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/327]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1696: Bond by William Mcphersone of Nuide to Duncan Mcphersone of Cluny, to consent to the said Duncan taking the benefit of transactions with John Grant of Dell for assigning the adjudication by said John against the l
2 CONC ands of Cluny, on condition that said Duncan paid the expenses already incurred by said William. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f291&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/291]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 January 1703: Discharge by Donald Mcintosh, younger of Lynwilg, to William Mcphersone of Nuide, for 1000 merks as the tocher of Margaret Mcphersone, his daughter, contained in marriage contract dated 25 Dec., 1701. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f371&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/371]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 December 1705: Letter from P[aul] Mcphersone, Delliphour, to William Mcpherson of Nuide, "the tenants expects ye will use them kyndly for ye know that they have nothing". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD80%2f866&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nuide&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, MacPherson of Cluny Papers, reference GD80/866]'''
2 CONT
