1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Please see attached CPR (v. 11) document of pages RE known Wydevills.''' If anyone one has access to the expensive Douglas Richardson books, searching them may provide more documentation. ''The Complete Peerage'
2 CONC ' and FMG do not know Richard's ancestry. 
2 CONT Without further primary sources coming to light, '''all''' continuing lineal connections, starting with the fictive parents of Richard, represent guesswork,  not legitimate genealogy. '''The CPR states''': "Richard de Wydeville, b
2 CONC . about 1310, was the first member of the Wydevill family of Grafton (Regis), Northants, to achieve more than local prominence."[Footnote: "His parentage is unknown; but the family of Wydevill or Wodevill had long been seated at G
2 CONC rafton.]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm#_Toc196024007
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD de Wydeville of Grafton, Northamptonshire ([1310]-[after Jul 1378]). m firstly ---. The name of Richard´s family is not known. m secondly as her second husband, ELIZABETH Lyons, widow of Sir NICHOLAS Chetwode, daughter of 
2 CONC Sir JOHN Lyons of Warkworth & his wife ---. Richard & his first wife had one child: ...
2 CONT
2 CONT a)  JOHN de Wydeville ([1341/43]-[after 8 Sep 1403]).  m firstly KATHERINE Fermbrand, daughter of [JOHN Fermbrand of Biddenham, Bedfordshire & his wife ---].  m secondly (before 1379) as her second husband, ISABEL, widow of ROBERT
2 CONC  Passelaw of Drayton Parslow, daughter of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT High Sheriff of Northamptonshire
2 CONT
