2 DATE 27 JAN 1446
2 ADDR
3 CITY Arbroath
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Earl of Crawford, Hereditary Sheriff of Aberdeenshire, 2nd Earl of Crawford
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Lindsay, second Earl of Crawford, was conspicuous as a statesman and soldier. He married Mariota, daughter and heiress of Sir David Dunbar, of Cockburn, sixth son of George, tenth Earl of Dunbar and March
2 CONC . Sir David Dunbar was the grandson of Lady Agnes, the heroic daughter of Thomas Randolph, Earl of Moray. Of Lady Agnes, history tells us that her husband, the Earl of Dunbar, leaving his castle in her charge during the winter of 
2 CONC 1338, the Earl of Salisbury laid siege to it. The Countess performed all the duties of an able commander; animated the garrison by her exhortation, and braved every danger. The English, after a siege of nineteen weeks, retired. Al
2 CONC exander Lindsay, Lord Crawford, fell in the battle of Aberbrothwick January 13, 1446. His third son, by his wife Lady Mariota Dunbar, was  V. Sir Walter Lindsay, of Beufort and Panbride, who married secondly Isabel, daughter of Wi
2 CONC lliam, Lord Livingston, and by her had a son, David.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:The Descent Of General Robert Edward Lee From Robert The Bruce, Of Scotland. By Professor Wm. Winston Fontaine, of Louisville.  (From the Southern Historical Society Papers)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT 2nd Earl of Crawford
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Alexander "4th Lord Of The Mount" Lindsay
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Alexander Lindsay, second Earl of Crawford is a direct descendant of Charlemagne.'''
2 CONT This is his lineage:
2 CONT 1 Charlemagne
2 CONT 2 Louis I, The Pious
2 CONT 3 Charles II "the Bald", Western Emperor
2 CONT 4 Louis II the Stammerer, king of the West Franks
2 CONT 5 Ermentrude de France
2 CONT 6 Cunigunda, countess of Trèves & Ardennes
2 CONT 7 Siegfried I, count of Luxembourg
2 CONT 8 Frederick I, count of Moselgau
2 CONT 9 Gisèle de Luxemburg
2 CONT 10 Gislebert dit “Le Grand” de Gant (Gaunt), baron de Folkingham, seigneur de Hunmanby
2 CONT 11 Walter van Gent, lord of Folkingham (aka Walter de Lindsey)
2 CONT 12 Sir William de Lindsay
2 CONT 13 Sir Walter de Lindsay
2 CONT 14 Sir William de Lindsay, Lord of Luffness, Ercildoune and Crawford
2 CONT 15 Sir William de Lindsay
2 CONT 16 Sir David de Lindsay of Breneville
2 CONT 17 David Lindsay of the Byres
2 CONT 18 Sir Alexander Lindsay of Crawford
2 CONT 19 Sir David Lindsay of Crawford
2 CONT 20 Alexander Lindsay of Glenesk
2 CONT 21 David Lindsay, 9th Lord of Crawford, 1st Earl of Crawford
2 CONT 22 Alexander Lindsay, second Earl of Crawford
2 CONT ----
