2 CONT From the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy page on Kings of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#RobertIdied1329B
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT I 1306-1329, DAVID II 1329-1371
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT [VII] Bruce, son of ROBERT [VI] de Brus, Earl of Carrick, Lord of Annandale & his first wife Margaret Ctss of Carrick (Writtle, near Chelmsford, Essex 11 Jul 1274-Cardross Castle, Dumbartonshire 7 Jun 1329, bur Dunfermline 
2 CONC Abbey, Fife).  
2 CONT *The Liber Pluscardensis records the birth in 1274 of "Robertus de Broys tercius…rex Scociæ futurus"[1015].  The manuscript history of the Bruce family of Carleton records that “Robertus Brus quintus…rex Scotiæ” succeeded “Robertu
2 CONC s Brus quartus”[1016].  
2 CONT *He succeeded his father 27 Oct 1292 as Earl of Carrick.  
2 CONT *He succeeded his father in 1304 as Baron Bruce and Lord of Annandale.  Edward I King of England forfeited his English estates 20 Feb 1305/6.  
2 CONT *In defiance of Edward I King of England, he assumed the crown 25 or 27 Mar 1306 as ROBERT I King of Scotland, crowned 25 and 27 Mar 1306.  John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records the coronation "VI Kal Apr" in 1306 
2 CONC of "Robertus de Bruce comes tunc de Carrick" at Scone[1017].  
2 CONT *John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records the death "VII Id Jun…apud Cardros" in 1329 of "Robertus de Bruce rex Scotorum" in the twenty-fourth year of his reign[1018].  The Extracta ex Cronicis Scocie records the deat
2 CONC h "apud Cardross" of "Robertus de Broys rex Scotorum" and his burial "in medio chori de Dumfermling…VII Id Jun" in 1329[1019]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly ([1295]) ISABEL of Mar, daughter of DONALD 6th Earl of Mar & his wife Helen [of North Wales] (-before 1302).  
2 CONT *John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Robertus…rex, quuando fuit comes de Carric" married "Isabellam sororem Garthenai comitis de Marr"[1020]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly (1302) ELIZABETH de Burgh, daughter of RICHARD de Burgh 2nd Earl of Ulster and Connaught & his wife Margaret de Burgh of Lavanley (-Cullen Castle, Banffshire 26 Oct 1327, bur Dunfermline Abbey, Fife).  
2 CONT *John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Robertus, adhuc comes" married "Elizabeth filiam Haymeri de Burkis comitis de Hullister" after the death of his first wife[1021].  
2 CONT *The Chronicle of John of Fordun (Continuator - Annals) records that in 1306 "the queen" was captured by William Earl of Ross and "brought to the king of England and…kept a prisoner in close custody until the battle of Bannockburn
2 CONC "[1022].  Orders for the "farther…custody of the countesses of Carrick and Buchan, Marie and Christine the sisters, and Margerie the daughter, of Robert de Brus", specifying that "three of the ladies to be in kages", are dated 7 N
2 CONC ov 1306[1023].  
2 CONT *John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records the death "VII Kal Nov" in 1327 of "domina Elizabeth regina, mater regis David" and her burial "in choro de Dunfermeling juxta regem Robertum sponsum suum"[1024].  The Liber P
2 CONC luscardensis records the death in 1327 of "Elizabeth regina Scociæ mater David regis et uxor…Roberti de Broys" and her burial "apud Dunfermlyn"[1025].  The Extracta ex Cronicis Scocie records the death "VII Kal Nov" in 1327 of "Re
2 CONC gina Elizabeitht, mater regis David de Broys" and her burial "in choro de Dumfermling iuxta Robertem regem et suum sponsum"[1026]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT King Robert I & his first wife had one child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  MARJORY Bruce ([1296/97]-Paisley, Renfrewshire 2 Mar 1316, bur Paisley Abbey).  
2 CONT *John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) names "Marjoriam" as the only daughter of "Robertus…rex, quuando fuit comes de Carric" and his wife "Isabellam sororem Garthenai comitis de Marr", adding that she married "Waltero sen
2 CONC escallo Scotiæ"[1027].  Orders for the "farther…custody of the countesses of Carrick and Buchan, Marie and Christine the sisters, and Margerie the daughter, of Robert de Brus", specifying that "three of the ladies to be in kages",
2 CONC  are dated 7 Nov 1306[1028].  
2 CONT *The Liber Pluscardensis records that "nobilis Walteri Stevart" married "filiam Roberti de Broys"[1029].  
2 CONT *She died in childbirth triggered by falling from her horse.  
2 CONT *m (1315) [as his second wife,] WALTER 6th High Steward of Scotland, son of JAMES 5th High Steward of Scotland & his wife Cecilia de Dunbar (1292-9 Apr 1326).  
2 CONT *Marjory & her husband had one child: Robert Stewart (b. Paisley 2 March 1316, d. Dundonald Castle 19 April 1390, bur. Scone Abbey)
2 CONT
