1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gilles (or Egidia) de Burgh''', born about 1263, daughter of Walter de Burgh, 1st Earl of Ulster.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Egidia married James (Seumas) STEWART 5th High Steward of the Scots, son of Alexander LE STEWARD 4th High Steward of Scotland before 10 October 1296  (1) (date of charter) (James (Seumas) STEWART 5th High Steward of the Scots was 
2 CONC born say 1260 and died on 16 Jul 1309 in Dundonald Castle, Irvine, Ayrshire, Scotland 1970.)  His 3rd wife; his first wife was Cecilia, daughter of Patrick, Earl of Dunbar (died 1289) [is this proven?]. James' second wife appears 
2 CONC to have been Muriel (born 1244), daughter of Malise, Earl of Strathearn (died 1271). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT It appears all children of James Stewart were with his 3rd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James include:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Walter, 6th High Steward (1293–1326) who married King Robert I's daughter, Marjorie Bruce.[3]
2 CONT * Sir John, killed 14 October 1318 at the battle of Dundalk.[3]
2 CONT * Sir Andrew,[4] "younger son"[5][6]
2 CONT * Sir James Stewart of Durisdeer, Tutor to his nephew, the future King Robert II of Scotland, in 1327.[3]
2 CONT * Giles "Egidia" Stewart, who married Sir Alexander de Menzies, of Durisdeer.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===supporting data===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=PA356&ots=kvoLIVOOb2&dq=sir%20james%20stewart%20of%20preston%20giles%20stewart&pg=PA356#v=onepage&q&f=false page 356] of Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval 
2 CONC Families, 2nd Edition, 2011 by Douglas Richardson.  "Giles de Burgh, married (as his 3rd wife) James [Stewart] (or James fitz Alexander), Knt., 5th Stewart of Scotland, son and heir of Alexander Stewart, Knt., 4th Stewart of Scotl
2 CONC and, of Dundonlad.  They had four sons, Andrew, Walter, Knt. [6th Steward of Scotland], John, Knt., and James, Knt., [of Durrisdeer], and one daughter, '''Giles''' (wife of Alexander de Meyners or Menzies, Knt.). ...."
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/library/3976-the-wives-of-sir-james-the-steward-d-1309 "The Wives of Sir James the Steward (d.1309)"] Author: MacEwen, Andrew B W Publisher: Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Year published: 2011 Status: See notes
2 CONC  Description / Notes: "This paper rehabilitates the traditional year of Sir James the Steward’s birth, names his first two wives, explains the late date of his third marriage to Giles de Burgh, and provides information about their
2 CONC  four known children. It posits a double marriage alliance between the Stewarts and Comyns about 1240, clarifies the date of birth of Robert II, and establishes the circumstances of his mother’s death in 1317. It incidentally brin
2 CONC gs forward some overlooked information on the Muschamp family and shows when Sir William, earl of Mar, actually died. Lastly it draws together what little is known concerning Sir Nicholas Campbell (d.1305), whose representation pa
2 CONC ssed to the Lochawe branch."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.archive.org/stream/calendarofdocume02grea#page/222/mode/2up Cal.Doc Scot. vol ii, no 847. ] >1296. Oct. 10. 847. Inspeximus and confirmation by the K. [of a charter by Richard de Burgo earl of Ulster, lord of Connaug
2 CONC ht, in favor of James the Steward of Scotland and Egidia his wife (the earl's sister), in frank marriage, of his castle and burgh 'del Eoo' and rents of his English vassals in ' le Kenauthe ' pertaining to the castle, on the east 
2 CONC of the water of Roo, with the island in the water next said castle, and his whole land of Rennard, and farmers and vassals in and out of burgh, to be held as a free barony by them and the heirs begotten of their bodies, as a knigh
2 CONC t's fee. Witnesses to the charter : — Sir John earl of Warenne, Sir Richard fitz John, Sir John de Soules, Sir William fitz Warren, Sir Walter de Lindeseye, Sir Eustace le Pouere, and Sir Nicholas de Chambelle and others.] Northal
2 CONC lerton. [Patent, 2 Edw. I. m. 4-] 
2 CONT
