1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Marjory Douglas1,2
2 CONT *F, #4353
2 CONT *Father	Sir Archibald Douglas, 3rd Earl of Douglas, Earl of Wigtown, Lord of Galloway & Bothwell2 b. c 1325, d. 24 Dec 1400
2 CONT *Mother	Joanna Moray d. b Aug 1409
2 CONT *'''     Marjory Douglas married David Stewart, Duke Rothesay, Earl Carrick & Atholl, Steward of Scotland''', son of Sir Robert III Stewart, King of Scotland, Earl of Atholl & Carrick and Annabella Drummond, '''in February 1400 at
2 CONC  Bothwell, Lanarkshire, Scotland.3,2 Marjory Douglas married Sir Walter Haliburton''', son of Sir John Haliburton and Margaret Cameron, '''in 1403.
2 CONT *'''Family 1     Sir Walter Haliburton''' d. b 10 May 1447
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **John Halyburton, 1st Lord Haliburton+ d. a 5 Jul 1454
2 CONT **Margaret Halyburton+4
2 CONT **Walter Halyburton, Lord Halyburton+
2 CONT *'''Family 2     David Stewart, Duke Rothesay, Earl Carrick & Atholl, Steward of Scotland''' b. 24 Oct 1378, d. 26 Mar 1402
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S523] Unknown author, Burke's Guide to the Royal Family, p. 318.
2 CONT *[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 648.
2 CONT *[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 570.
2 CONT *[S11620] The Douglas Archives.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p145.htm#i4353 _______________
2 CONT *'''Name	Marjory (Mary) Douglas 
2 CONT *'''Born	Abt 1377 
2 CONT *Gender	Female 
2 CONT *'''Died	1421 
2 CONT *Father	Archibald The Grim (3rd Earl of Douglas) Douglas,   b. Abt 1346,   d. 24 Dec 1400  (Age ~ 54 years) 
2 CONT *Mother	Joan\Johana (of Strathearn) Moray,   b. Abt 1350,   d. Aug 1409, Threave Castle, Galloway   (Age ~ 59 years) 
2 CONT *'''Family 1	David (Duke of Rothesay) Stewart''',   b. 24 Oct 1378,   d. 27 Mar 1402, Falkland Palace, Starved To Death By His Uncle Duke Of Albany   (Age 23 years) 
2 CONT *'''Married	Feb 1399-1400 
2 CONT *'''Family 2	Sir Walter (of Dirleton Castle) Halyburton''',   b. Abt 1380,   d. Bef 5 Oct 1447  (Age ~ 67 years) 
2 CONT *'''Married	1403 
2 CONT *'''Children 	
2 CONT ** 	1. John (of Dirleton Castle) Halyburton,   d. Between 31 Oct 1452 and 5 Jul 1454
2 CONT ** 	2. Walter Halyburton
2 CONT ** 	3. Robert Halyburton
2 CONT ** 	4. William Halyburton
2 CONT ** 	5. Jean (of Dirleton Castle) Halyburton
2 CONT ** 	6. George (of Gogar) Halyburton
2 CONT ** 	7. Margaret Halyburton
2 CONT *Sources 	
2 CONT *[S883] Hamish Maclaren.
2 CONT *From: http://www.douglashistory.co.uk/famgen/getperson.php?personID=I47601&tree=tree1 ________________
2 CONT *Archibald Douglas, Earl of Douglas and Wigtown, Lord of Galloway, Douglas and Bothwell, called Archibald the Grim or Black Archibald, was a late medieval Scottish nobleman. Archibald was the bastard son of Sir James "the Black" D
2 CONC ouglas, Robert I's trusted lieutenant, and an unknown mother. .... etc.
2 CONT *Around 1362 Douglas married Joanna de Moravia, daughter of Maurice de Moravia, 1st Earl of Strathearn. They had four children.
2 CONT **Archibald Douglas, who succeeded as 4th earl
2 CONT **James Douglas, later the 7th earl
2 CONT **'''Marjory Douglas, married 1st David Stewart, Duke of Rothesay, 2nd Walter de Haliburton the Treasurer of Scotland
2 CONT **Helen, married Sir George de Lawedre of Haltoun,[14] Lord Provost of Edinburgh
2 CONT *Lord Douglas had an illegitimate son:
2 CONT *Sir William Douglas of Nithsdale (assassinated c. 1392), married Egidia Stewart daughter of Robert II
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Douglas,_3rd_Earl_of_Douglas ___________
2 CONT *'''David Stewart''' (24 October 1378 – 26 March 1402) was prince and heir to the throne of Scotland from 1390 and the first Duke of Rothesay from 1398. He was named after his great-great-uncle, David II of Scotland, and also held
2 CONC  the titles of Earl of Atholl (1398–1402) and Earl of Carrick (1390–1402). He shares with his uncle and arch-rival, Robert Stewart, first Duke of Albany, the distinction of being first Dukes to be created in the Scottish Peerage. 
2 CONC David never became King. '''His marriage to Marjorie Douglas''', daughter of Archibald the Grim, the third Earl of Douglas, '''was without issue.
2 CONT *'''David Stewart''', as eldest son of the King Robert III of Scotland and his Queen, Anabella Drummond, was heir to the throne of Scotland. In 1399, at the age of 21, he was appointed "Lieutenant" of the kingdom, partly due to th
2 CONC e infirmity of his father and at a time of civil unrest and conflict with England. Although this gave him an opportunity to flex political muscle, his room for manoeuvre was significantly constrained, however, by a combination of 
2 CONC youthful inexperience and the ultimately mortal rivalry of his uncle, Robert Stewart, who had been protector of the kingdom prior to David's lieutenancy. Albany was a ruthlessly effective politician with a well developed power bas
2 CONC e, and his designs on the throne were well understood. '''David's subsequent marriage to Marjorie, forming a Douglas alliance with the throne, also caused a serious rupture''' with George Dunbar the tenth Earl of March, whose daug
2 CONC hter Elizabeth had originally been betrothed to the Prince. David is known to have involved himself in the political life of the kingdom, playing a role for instance in peace negotiations with John of Gaunt in the Marches.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Stewart,_Duke_of_Rothesay ________________
2 CONT *'''Lady Marjorie Douglas1
2 CONT *'''F, #107987, d. before 11 May 1421
2 CONT *Last Edited=16 Jan 2016
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.39%
2 CONT *'''     Lady Marjorie Douglas was the daughter''' of Archibald Douglas, 3rd Earl of Douglas and Lady Joan Moray.1,2 '''She married, firstly, David Stewart, 1st and last Duke of Rothesay''', son of Robert III Stewart, King of Scot
2 CONC land and Annabel Drummond, '''in February 1399/0 at Bothwell Church, Scotland.2 She married, secondly, Sir Walter Haliburton''', son of Walter Haliburton and Lady Isabella Stewart, '''in 1403.2 She died before 11 May 1421.2 She di
2 CONC ed before 11 May 1421.3
2 CONT *'''     As a result of her marriage, Lady Marjorie Douglas was styled as Countess of Atholl in February 1399/0. From February 1399/0, her married name became Stewart. From 1403, her married name became Haliburton.2
2 CONT *'''Children of Lady Marjorie Douglas and Sir Walter Haliburton
