1 NAME 1st Earl of Angus George Douglas
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Saint Bride's Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Douglas
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY (now) United Kingdom
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 1378
2 PLAC Tantallon Castle, near
2 ADDR
3 CITY North Berwick
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 14 SEP 1402
2 ADDR
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU 1st Earl of Angus
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''George Douglas''', 1st Earl of Angus (born 1378 or before died after 14 September 1402)  - was a Scottish nobleman and peer.  He was born at Tantallon Castle, East Lothian, Scotland. He was the natural-illegitim
2 CONC ate son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Dowager Countess of Mar & Countess of Angus and Lady Abernethy in her own right.  He died after September 1402 at England from the Bubonic Plague.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#GeorgeDouglas1Angusdied1402B
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GEORGE Douglas''', illegitimate son of WILLIAM Douglas 1st Earl of Douglas & his mistress Margaret Stewart Ctss of Angus ([1378 or before]-1402).  He was created Earl of Angus.  <br/>
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 24 May 1397) as her first husband, Lady MARY Stewart, daughter of ROBERT III King of Scotland & his wife Annabel Drummond (-after 1458, bur Strathblane).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl George & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT #  WILLIAM Douglas (-Oct 1437).  He succeeded his father as 2nd Earl of Angus.  '''m''' (betrothed 12 Dec 1410, dispensation 1425) MARGARET Hay, daughter of Sir WILLIAM Hay of Yester & his first wife Jean Gifford of Yeser (-after 
2 CONC 22 Apr 1484).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Douglas,_1st_Earl_of_Angus
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife, Mary Stewart, a daughter of King Robert III, Angus had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus (1398–1437)
2 CONT *Lady Elizabeth Douglas, married firstly to Sir Alexander Forbes, later 1st Lord Forbes; married secondly to Sir David Hay of Yester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was to marry a further four times and bear seven more children by three of these husbands. The issue by her second husband, Sir James Kennedy the Younger of Dunure, were the ancestors of the Marquesses of Ailsa; The product o
2 CONC f her fourth marriage to William, 1st Lord Graham were the ancestors of the Viscounts of Dundee and the Dukes of Montrose.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Douglas,_1st_Earl_of_Angus
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born at Tantallon Castle, East Lothian, Scotland. He was the natural-illegitimate son of William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas and Margaret Stewart, Dowager Countess of Mar & Countess of Angus and Lady Abernethy in her own r
2 CONC ight.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father's wife Margaret had already produced an heir for her Lord in 1358, James, 2nd Earl of Douglas and Mar, who succeeded his father upon his death in 1384.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1389, Margaret of Angus relinquished her title in favour of her son, but George did not assume it until his betrothal in 1397 to Princess Mary Stewart, daughter of King Robert III of Scotland. The influence of George's mother m
2 CONC ust have been considerable - in addition to obtaining a royal bride for George, she persuaded King Robert III to confirm him in his style of Earl of Angus, and also to bestow upon him the lordships of Abernethy, (Perthshire) and B
2 CONC onkill, (Berwickshire); and "to endow him and his spouse with the justiciary fees of the County of Forfar, to ratify all gifts, entails, and leases made or to be made by his half-sister, Isabel, Countess of Mar, to the said Jorge 
2 CONC her brothir".[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James 2nd Earl of Douglas, was killed without issue in 1388, at the Battle of Otterburn, and the Earldom of Mar, and all non-entailed Douglas possessions passed to his sister Isabel. The earldom of Douglas passed to a cousin, the 
2 CONC aptly named Archibald the Grim, a natural (illegitimate) son of the Good Sir James Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT The descendants of Archibald the Grim formed the famed Black Douglas line, and those of George formed the equally famed and longer lived Red Line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus does not appear to have taken much interest in Public life, although his name appears on various minor charters. However, in 1402, he was dispatched under orders of the Duke of Albany, Regent of Scotland, to accompany Murdoc
2 CONC h, Earl of Fife and the Earl of Moray to assist Archibald Douglas, 4th Earl of Douglas during his invasion of Northumberland. That incursion ended at the disastrous field of Homildon Hill, where the Scots were routed and all of th
2 CONC e above taken prisoner. Both Moray and Angus died of the Plague whilst captive.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Douglas,_1st_Earl_of_Angus (1380-1403) cites
2 CONT ** Maxwell, Sir Herbert.A History of the House of Douglas. Freemantle, London 1902
2 CONT ** Godscroft, David Hume of. Ane Historie of the House and Race of Douglas and Angus. Edinburgh 1646
2 CONT **Brown, Michael. The Black Douglases. Tuckwell press, East Linton, East Lothian 1998
2 CONT ** From the Bloody Heart, Oliver Thomson. Sutton, Stroud, Gloucs. 2003
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LTHY-83T
2 CONT * https://it.findagrave.com/memorial/15201842/george-douglas (1378- 14sept.1402)
2 CONT
