2 NOTE The church﻿yard, which is now closed, can be found at the heart of the town. The church has recently been restored by Historic Scotland; dates back to the late 14th century, and houses the tomb of Douglas family. The clock is beli
3 CONC eved to be the oldest town﻿ clock in Scotland dating from 1565 and is said to have been gifted by Mary Queen of Scots. This is a must see facility. Records are available.
