2 CONT *''''''Sir William Edmonstone1 
2 CONT *M, #65494
2 CONT *Father      Sir William de Edmonstone, Captain of Threave Castle1 d. c 1460
2 CONT *Mother     Mary Stewart1 b. c 1378, d. a Feb 1462
2 CONT *''''''     Sir William Edmonstone was born at of Duntreath, Stirlingshire, Scotland.1 He married Matilda Stewart, daughter of Sir James 'the Gross' Stewart, Master of Lennox and (Miss) MacDonald.1
2 CONT *''''''Family      Matilda Stewart 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Sir Archibald Edmonstone, 3rd Laird Edmonstone+1
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 908.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2180.htm#i65494
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William, 2nd of Duntreath, 1460-1486.*
2 CONT
2 CONT m. Matilda, dau. of Lord James Stewart (surviving son of Murdoch, Duke of Albany.)
2 CONT
2 CONT By her he had 6 sons & 1 daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1  Sir Archibald who succeeded him.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2  James. 
2 CONT
2 CONT         m. 1stly Elizabeth, dau & heiress of Alexander Cunningham of Polmaise,
2 CONT
2 CONT         m. 2ndly Helen, dau of John Murray of Touchadam.
2 CONT
2 CONT     3  James, Became Prior of Collegiate church of Kirkheugh at St. Andrews.
2 CONT
2 CONT     4  John. m. dau. of Sir John Stewart of Ardgowan & Blackhall.
2 CONT
2 CONT     5  George.
2 CONT
2 CONT     6  William, deputy-master of household to James IV.
2 CONT
2 CONT and
2 CONT
2 CONT     1 daughter, m. Lawrence, 1st Lord Oliphant..
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William died in 1486 & was succeeded by his eldest son
2 CONT
