1 NOTE Joan Beaufort was born circa 1379 in Beaufort Castle. She married Robertde Ferrers, son of Robert Ferrers, before 30 September 1390. She latermarried Ralph de Neville, son of John Nevill and Maud de Percy, between 9June 1396 and 2
2 CONC 0 February 1397.1 She died on 13 November 1440 in Howden,County Yorkshire, England. She was buried in Lincoln Cathedral, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan (de Beaufort) Ferrers married 2nd Sir Ralph Neville, K.G. - 1st Earlof Westmoreland. She was his 2nd wife. He had been married first toMargaret Stafford. Joan died November 13, 1440 and was buried in LincolnCathedral.
1 NOTE Joan Beaufort Queen of Scotland
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=de900124-bac9-4943-89ea-53b447be0e47&tid=2456826&pid=232106897
1 NOTE Joan Beaufort and JamesI
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=image&guid=2828a72a-c1db-4a4d-819f-e051409d4dc2&tid=2456826&pid=232106897
1 NOTE Joan Beaufort (c. 1404 - 15 July 1445), was Queen Consort of the Kingdom of Scotland from 1424 to 1437, being married to James I of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of John Beaufort, 1st Earl of Somerset and Margaret Holland. Her paternal grandparents were John of Gaunt, Duke of Lancaster and his mistress and later third wife Katherine Swynford. Her maternal grandparents we
2 CONC re Thomas Holland, 2nd Earl of Kent and Alice Fitzalan. Alice was a daughter of Richard FitzAlan, 10th Earl of Arundel and Eleanor of Lancaster.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 2 February 1424 at Southwark Cathedral, Joan married James I, shortly before he was formally crowned. They were feasted at Winchester Palace that year by her uncle Henry Cardinal Beaufort. She is said to have been the inspirati
2 CONC on of James's famous long poem, The Kingis Quair. They had eight children, including the future James II, and Margaret of Scotland, wife of Louis XI of France. After James I was assassinated in 1437, she took over the regency for 
2 CONC her son.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Issue with James I of Scotland
2 CONT Margaret Stewart, Princess of Scotland (1424-1445) married Louis XI of France 
2 CONT Isabella Stewart, Princess of Scotland (1426-1494) married Francis I, Duke of Brittany 
2 CONT Mary of Scotland, Countess of Buchan died 1465 married Wolfart VI van Borsselen 
2 CONT Joan of Scotland, Countess of Morton (c. 1428-1486) married James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton 
2 CONT Alexander Stewart, Duke of Rothesay (born and died 1430); Twin of James 
2 CONT James II of Scotland (1430-1460) 
2 CONT Annabella Stewart, Princess of Scotland married and divorced 1. Louis of Savoy, and then married and divorced 2. George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly 
2 CONT Eleanor Stewart, Princess of Scotland (1433-1484) married Sigismund, Archduke of Austria. 
2 CONT Second Marriage and Issue
2 CONT In 1439 Joan married James Stewart, the Black Knight of Lorn (~1383 - >1451). They had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl (c. 1440 - September 12, 1512). 
2 CONT James Stewart, 1st Earl of Buchan (1442-1499), High Chamberlain of Scotland in 1471 and Scottish Ambassador to France in 1473. 
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, Bishop of Moray 
