2 CONT *'''Joanna (Jean) Stewart1,2,3,4,5,6
2 CONT *'''F, #2934, b. circa 1428, d. between 16 October 1486 and 1490
2 CONT *Father      James I Stewart, King of Scotland7,8 b. c 25 Jul 1394, d. 21 Feb 1437
2 CONT *Mother     Joan Beaufort7,8 b. 1398, d. 15 Jul 1445
2 CONT *'''     Joanna (Jean) Stewart was born circa 1428 at of Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.6 She married James Douglas, 1st Earl Morton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile, son of James Douglas, 2nd Lord Dalkeith and 
2 CONC Elizabeth Giffard, before 15 May 1459; They had 2 sons (Sir John, 2nd Earl of Morton; & James) and 2 daughters (Janet, wife of Patrick Hepburn, Earl of Bothwell; & Elizabeth).5,6 Joanna (Jean) Stewart and James Douglas, 1st Earl M
2 CONC orton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile obtained a marriage license on 7 January 1464; Date of Dispensation, being related in the 2nd and 3rd degrees. Joanna (Jean) Stewart died between 16 October 1486 and 1490.5,
2 CONC 6
2 CONT *'''Family      James Douglas, 1st Earl Morton, 3rd Lord Dalkeith, Ambassador to France & Castile b. c 1425, d. bt 22 Jun 1493 - 22 Oct 1493
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Janet Douglas+ d. b 21 Feb 1491
2 CONT **James Douglas3
2 CONT **Sir John Douglas, 2nd Earl Morton, 4th Lord Dalkeith+5,6 b. b 1466, d. bt 19 Jul 1511 - Sep 1515
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. IV, p. 40.
2 CONT * 2.[S11572] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, by Gerald Paget, Vol. II, p. 395.
2 CONT * 3.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 1788.
2 CONT * 4.[S11563] The Scots Peerage, Vol. I, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 19.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 579-580.
2 CONT * 6.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 658.
2 CONT * 7.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 577-578.
2 CONT * 8.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 655-656.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p98.htm#i2934 _________________________
2 CONT *'''Joan Stewart1
2 CONT *'''F, #105328, b. circa 1428, d. after 16 October 1486
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Apr 2013
2 CONT *'''     Joan Stewart was born circa 1428.2 She was the daughter of James I Stewart, King of Scotland and Lady Joan Beaufort.1,3 She and James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Angus were engaged on 18 October 1440.3 She married James Douglas,
2 CONC  1st Earl of Morton, son of James Douglas, 2nd Lord of Dalkeith and Elizabeth Gifford, before 15 May 1459.2 She died after 16 October 1486.2 She was buried at Dalkeith Church, Midlothian, Scotland.2
2 CONT *'''      Joan Stewart also went by the nick-name of 'The Dumb Lady'.3 From before 15 May 1459, her married name became Douglas. As a result of her marriage, Joan Stewart was styled as Countess of Morton before 15 May 1459.
2 CONT *'''Children of Joan Stewart and James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton
2 CONT ** 1.Lady Janet Douglas+1 d. b 1490
2 CONT ** 2.James Douglas2 d. a 1480
2 CONT ** 3.Lady Elizabeth Douglas2 d. a 1479
2 CONT ** 4.John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton+2 b. b 1466, d. bt 8 Nov 1511 - 26 Nov 1513
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 238. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 231. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 3.[S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 19. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p10533.htm#i105328 ____________________________
2 CONT * JAMES Stewart, son of ROBERT III King of Scotland & his wife Annabel Drummond (Dec 1394-murdered Perth 21 Feb 1437).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) names "Jacobum regem" as son of "Robertus tertius"[1264].  He be
2 CONC came Duke of Rothesay 10 Dec 1404 after receiving from his father all lands belonging to the office of Steward of Scotland[1265].  A prisoner in France 1406-1424.  He succeeded his father in 1406 as JAMES I King of Scotland.  
2 CONT *m (2 or 13 Feb 1424) as her first husband, JOAN Beaufort, daughter of JOHN Beaufort Earl of Somerset & his wife Margaret de Holand of the Earls of Kent (-15 Jul 1445).  A late 15th century/early 16th century manuscript names “Joh
2 CONC amem aliter Henricum comitem Somersecie qui cito moritur, Thomam qui moritur, Edmundum ducem Somersecie, Joh[anname reginam Scotorum et Margaretam comitissam Devoni]” as the children of “Johannes Bowfurth comes Somersecie”[1266]. 
2 CONC  The Julius B II Chronicle records the marriage in Feb 1424 of “Sir James Styward kyng of Scotland” and “dame Joan the duchesse douhter of Clarence goten by her ffirst hosbond the Erle of Somersete”[1267].  She married secondly Ja
2 CONC mes Stewart "the Black Knight of Lorn".  
2 CONT *King James I & his wife had eight children:
2 CONT **1.         Lady MARGARET Stewart (1424-Châlons-sur-Marne, Cathédrale Saint-Etienne 16 Aug 1445, bur Abbaye de Saint-Laon, Vienne).  m (contract Perth, Scotland 19 Jul 1428, contract Chinon, Indre-et-Loire 30 Oct 1428, Cathédrale
2 CONC  de Tours 24 Jun 1436) as his first wife, LOUIS de France Dauphin de Viennois, son of CHARLES VII King of France & his wife Marie d'Anjou (Bourges, Bishop's palace 3 Jul 1423-Château de Plessis-les-Tours, La Riche, Indre-et-Loire 
2 CONC 30 Aug 1483, bur Notre-Dame de Cléry, Loiret).  He succeeded his father in 1461 as LOUIS XI King of France. 
2 CONT **2.         Lady ISABEL Stewart (Autumn 1426-[13 Oct 1494/5 Mar 1499]).  Betrothed (contract 19 Jul 1441, ratified 29 Sep 1441) to JEAN VI Duke of Brittany, son of JEAN V "le Vaillant" Duke of Brittany & his third wife Infanta do
2 CONC ña Juana de Navarra (Château de l'Hermine, near Vannes, Morbihan 24 Dec 1389-manoir de La Touche, near Nantes 29 Aug 1442, bur Tréguier, Cathédrale Saint-Tugdual).  He died before the religious ceremony.  m (30 Oct 1442) as his se
2 CONC cond wife, FRANÇOIS I Duke of Brittany, son of JEAN VI Duke of Brittany & his wife Jeanne de France (Vannes 11 May 1414-Château de l'Hermine, Vannes 17 Jul 1450, bur Redon Abbaye de St Sauveur, Ille-et-Vilaine).  
2 CONT **'''3.         Lady JOAN Stewart ([1428]-after 16 Oct 1486).  She was deaf and dumb, known as "the dumb lady of Dalkeith".  She lived in France from Aug 1445 to Spring 1458[1268].  m (before 15 May 1459) JAMES Douglas Earl of Mor
2 CONC ton, son of JAMES Douglas of Dalkeith & his wife Elizabeth Gifford of Sheriffhall (-[22 Jun/22 Oct] 1493).  
2 CONT **4.         ALEXANDER Stewart (16 Oct 1430-young).  Duke of Rothesay. 
2 CONT **5.         JAMES Stewart (16 Oct 1430-Roxburgh 3 Aug 1460, bur Holyrood).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) names "Jacobum secundum regem qui nunc est" as son of "Jacobum secundum"[1269].  He succeeded his father in
2 CONC  1437 as JAMES II King of Scotland.    
2 CONT **-        see below. 
2 CONT **6.         Lady ELEANOR Stewart (Dunfermline 1433-Innsbruck 20 Nov 1480, bur Stams).  m (12 Feb 1449) as his first wife, SIGISMUND "der Münzreiche" Archduke of Austria, Graf von Tirol, son of FRIEDRICH IV "mit den leeren Tasche"
2 CONC  Duke of Austria, Graf von Tirol & his second wife Anna von Braunschweig-Lüneburg (Innsbruck 26 Oct 1427-Innsbruck 4 Mar 1496, bur Stams). 
2 CONT **7.         Lady MARY Stewart (-20 Mar 1465, bur Sandenburg, ter Veere, Zeeland).  She was granted the Earldom of Buchan, probably on her marriage, thereby becoming Ctss of Buchan[1270].  m (ter Veere, Zeeland 1444) as his first 
2 CONC wife, WOLFART van Borselen, son of HENDRIK van Borselen Comte de Grandpré & his second wife Jeanne van Halewijn (-Ghent 29 Apr 1487, bur Sandenburg, ter Veere, Zeeland).  Earl of Buchan, de iure uxoris.  He succeeded his father in
2 CONC  1474 as Comte de Grandpré.  Governor of Holland, Zeeland and Friesland 1477-1480[1271]. 
2 CONT **8.         Lady ANNABEL Stewart  .  The marriage contract between "Lodovico di Savoia figlio secundogenito del Duca Lodovico" and "Anabella figlia del Re Giacomo di Scozia" is dated 14 Dec 1444[1272].  m firstly (contract 14 Dec
2 CONC  1444[1273], 14 Dec 1447, divorced 1458) as his first wife, LOUIS de Savoie Comte de Genève, son of LOUIS Duke of Savoy & his wife Anne Pss of Cyprus (5 Jun 1436-château-monastère de Ripaille 16 Jul 1482).  m secondly (before 10 M
2 CONC ar 1460, divorced 24 Jul 1471) as his second wife, GEORGE Gordon, son of ALEXANDER Gordon [formerly Seton] Earl of Huntly & his second wife Elizabeth Crichton (-Stirling [8 Jun] 1501, bur Cambuskenneth).  He succeeded his father i
2 CONC n 1470 as Earl of Huntly.  
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#Joandiedafter16Oct1486 _______________________________
2 CONT *	Morton, Earl of (S, 1457/8)
2 CONT *			2b. James Douglas of Dalkeith, declared to be of unsound mind by Act of Parliament 1441 (d. betw. 8 Sep 1456 and 14 Mar 1457/8), mar. Elizabeth Giffard (d. after 8 Sep 1456), dau. of James Giffard of Sheriffhall, and had issue
2 CONC :
2 CONT **'''				1c. James Douglas of Dalkeith, later 1st Earl of Morton
2 CONT *			3b. Henry Douglas of Dalkeith  .... etc.
