2 CONT *'''James [Douglas], 1st Earl of Morton
2 CONT *born
2 CONT *'''mar.  bef. 15 May 1459 his first cousin once removed the Princess Jean (b. c. 1428; d. 16 Oct 1486), 3rd dau. of James I, King of Scotland, by his wife Lady Joan Beaufort, 1st dau. of John [Beaufort], 1st Earl of Somerset
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Sir John Douglas, later 2nd Earl of Morton
2 CONT **	2. James Douglas (d. after 1480)
2 CONT **	1. Lady Janet Douglas (dspm. bef. 21 Feb 1490/1), mar. bef. 1 Feb 1480/1 as his first wife Patrick [Hepburn], 1st Earl of Bothwell, and had issue
2 CONT **	2. Lady Elizabeth Douglas (d. after 1479)
2 CONT *'''died  bef. 22 Oct 1492
2 CONT *'''created  14 Mar 1457/8 Earl of Morton
2 CONT *'''suc. by  son
2 CONT *'''note  created Earl of Morton in contemplation of his marriage with the King's daughter; Ambassador to France and Castile 1491
2 CONT *
2 CONT *John [Douglas], 2nd Earl of Morton
2 CONT *born  bef. 1466
2 CONT *mar.  bef. Aug 1493 Janet Crichton, dau. of Patrick Crichton of Cranston-Riddel
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Hon James Douglas, later 3rd Earl of Morton
2 CONT **	2. Hon Richard Douglas (d. after 17 Oct 1564), mar., and had issue
2 CONT **	1. Lady Elizabeth (Beatrice?) Douglas, mar. bef. 8 Jan 1505/6 Hon Robert Keith, styled Lord Keith (dvp. bef. 22 Apr 1525), 1st son and heir ap. of William [Keith], 2nd Earl Marischal, by his wife Lady Elizabeth Gordon, 3rd dau.
2 CONC  by his third wife of George [Gordon], 2nd Earl of Huntly, and had issue
2 CONT **	2. Lady Agnes Douglas, mar. as his second wife Alexander [Livingston], 5th Lord Livingston, and had issue
2 CONT *died  betw. 8 Nov 1511 and 26 Nov 1513
2 CONT *suc. by  son
2 CONT *note  knighted c. 1469; Ambassador to England 1494; attended the Princess Margaret of England on her arrival in Scotland 1503
