1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Het graafschap „Bochane” in Schotland bracht zij als '''bruidsschat''' mede. Door dit huwelijk werd Veere bijzonder aantrekkelijk voor de Schotten, die in groot aantal daar heen kwamen om handel te drijven en speci
2 CONC aal om een belangrijken wolhandel daar te vestigen.
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00002912&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ====WIKITREE: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#MaryCtssBuchandied1465 Scotland, King]
2 CONT * 7.''' Lady MARY Stewart''' ([1435?]-20 Mar 1465, bur Veere, Zeeland). Her parentage is confirmed by her epitaph.  Balfour Paul records her mariage ”in 1444” (no source cited)[1519]. The primary source which confirms the date of 
2 CONC her marriage has not been identified. The family chronology suggests that Mary was little more than a child at the time, although her first known child was born in [1451] which in turn suggests that she could have been born in [14
2 CONC 35].  She was granted the earldom of Buchan, probably on her marriage, thereby becoming Ctss of Buchan[1520].  An epitaph at Ter Veere records the burial of “mevr. Marie van Schotland fa Jacob coninck van Inghelandt, Schotland, gr
2 CONC avinne van Bouchaue, d’eerste ghesellenede van mijnheere Wulfaert van Borsele ruddere...” who died 20 Mar 1465 (O.S.?)[1521]. 
2 CONT * '''m''' (Veere, Zeeland [1444]) as his first wife, '''WOLFARD van Borselen''', son of HENDRIK van Borselen Comte de Grandpré & his wife Jeanne de Halluin (-Gent 29 Apr 1487, bur Zandenburg).  Earl of Buchan, de iure uxoris.  He 
2 CONC succeeded his father as Comte de Grandpré.  Governor of Holland, Zeeland and Friesland 1477-1480[1522]
2 CONT * '''Wolfard [V] & his first wife had two children''' [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/DUTCH%20NOBILITY.htm#WolfardBorselendied1487 Dutch Nobility]:—
2 CONT ** (a) '''KAREL van Borselen''' ([1451]-Louvain [1463/64], bur Zandenburg castle).  Watson names “Charles and John, who both d. young” as Wolfard’s two sons by his first wife[1503].  Poswick records his year of birth and death “à 
2 CONC peine âgé de 13 ans à l’Université de Louvain” and place of burial[1504].  An epitaph at Zandenburg castle records the burial of “heere jonr Carolus van Borsele fs heer Wulfart ende van vrau Marie van Schotlant, fa coninc Jacobs” 
2 CONC who died at “Leuven, ter schole te zijne, 13 jaren 1454” [error?][1505]. 
2 CONT ** (b) ''' JAN van Borselen''' (-young).  Watson names “Charles and John, who both d. young” as Wolfard’s two sons by his first wife[1506]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====WIKITREE: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-7743 Mary (Stewart) Stewart Countess of Buchan]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====ThePeerage.com: [http://thepeerage.com/p10533.htm#i105329 Mary Stewart, Countess of Buchan]
