1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Domhnall Ballach From Wikipedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domhnall_Ballach
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Domhall Ballach MacDonald''' Title	2nd Clan Chief Predecessor	John Mór Tanister Successor	John Mor MacDonald, 3rd of Dunnyveg
2 CONT
2 CONT Domhnall Ballach, also known as Donald Balloch MacDonald (d. c. 1476) was a son of Iain Mòr Tànaiste MacDhòmhnaill and Margaret Bisset, daughter of MacEoin Bisset, Lord of The Glens. He was the second chief of Clan MacDonald of Du
2 CONC nnyveg.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the chieftainship of the clan after his father was murdered by James Campbell after a scheduled meeting at Ard-du, Islay in 1427. Donald took revenge and James Campbell was executed, protesting however, that it was
2 CONC  done under the King James I of Scotland's order.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known as a military leader he was chosen to lead Clan Donald and defeated the forces of King James I at the battle of Inverlochy in 1431.[1] Subsequently after a number of defeats against Royal forces Donald was forced to flee to 
2 CONC Ireland. A pickled head was presented by his friend, the Irish Chief Hugh Buy O'Neill, who presented it to the King James I, as that of the rebel Lord of Dunnyveg. After the death of King James I, Donald returned to Dunnyveg in 14
2 CONC 37.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on an islet upon Loch Gruinart, Islay in c. 1476.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT By his first wife Johanna, daughter of Conn O'Neill of Edenduffcarrick, they had;
2 CONT John Mor MacDonald, m. Sabina O'Neill, daughter of Felim 'Bacach' O'Neill Margaret, b. c. 1414 married Ruari MacDonald, 3rd of Clan Ranald. By his second wife Joan, daughter of O'Donnell, Lord of Tyrconnel, they had; Agnes, who ma
2 CONC rried Thomas Bannatyne of Knraes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Roberts (1999) p. 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References===
2 CONT
2 CONT Roberts, John Leonard (1999), Feuds, Forays and Rebellions: History of the Highland Clans, 1475-1625, Edinburgh University Press, ISBN 978-0-7486-6244-9
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Donald "Balloch"''''' married, first, Johanna, daughter of Conn O'Neill, by whom he had:
2 CONT 1.''' ''John''''', his successor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Joan, daughter of O'Donnell, Lord of Tyrconnel, and sister of Hugh Roe O'Donnell, by whom he had:
2 CONT 2. ''Agnes'', who married Thomas Bannatyne of Kames.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Donald Balloch''''' died on an islet on Lochgruinart, in Islay, in 1476.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 374.'''''
2 CONT ----
