1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/4/mode/2up Page 5 No. 20
2 CONT
2 CONT (20) John, seventh Earl of Sutherland, B-P died 1460. He married Margaret, daughter of Sir William Baillie of Lamington, and had four sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 20(a) Alexander, Master of Sutherland, died v.p. and s.p. before 1456.
2 CONT * 20(b) John (No. 21 below).
2 CONT * 20(c) Nicolas Sutherland.
2 CONT * 20(d) Thomas Beg Sutherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had also a natural son:
2 CONT
2 CONT 20(e) Thomas More, who had two sons, killed by the eighth Earl of Sutherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burke's Peerage entry -
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN SUTHERLAND, 7th Earl of Sutherland; born c 1390; knighted 1408; married by 1342 Margaret (died 1510), a famous beauty, daughter of Sir William Baillie of Lamington, and had:
2 CONT * 1a Alexander, Master of Sutherland; died in the lifetime of the father by 22 Feb 1455/6
2 CONT * 2a JOHN, 8th Earl
2 CONT * 3a Nicholas, living 1448
2 CONT * 4a Thomas Beg (‘The Little'); allegedly ancestor of the SUTHERLANDs OF STRATHALLIE
2 CONT * 5a Robert, living 1487
2 CONT * 1a Janet; married Alexander Dunbar, 3rd son of Sir Alexander Dunbar of Westfield (see DUNBAR OF MOCHRUM, Bt), and had issue
2 CONT * The 7th EARL died c 1460; his eldest surviving son,
