1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Caithness  is a historic county, registration county and lieutenancy area of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''There are two towns, being Wick, which was the county town, and Thurso''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dunbeath Castle is located on the east coast of Caithness''', 2 kilometres (1.2 mi) south of Dunbeath, in northern Scotland.  
2 CONT
2 CONT A castle is first recorded on the rocky peninsula at Dunbeath in 1428,[4] when the lands belonged to the Earl of Caithness. The first recorded laird was Alexander Sutherland.[4] It later became the property of the Clan Sinclair th
2 CONC rough the marriage of the daughter of Alexander Sutherland to William Sinclair (1410–1484), the first Sinclair Earl of Caithness.
2 CONT
2 CONT ============
2 CONT
2 CONT *http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p639.htm#i19186
2 CONT *Alexander Sutherland, Baron Dunbeath1,2
2 CONT *M, b. between 1395 and 1400, d. between 5 September 1454 and February 1456
2 CONT *Father Robert Sutherland, 6th Earl Sutherland2 b. c 1347, d. c 1427 
2 CONT *Mother Margaret Stewart2 d. 1442 
2 CONT *     Alexander Sutherland, Baron Dunbeath NOT Master of Sutherland. NOT son of John, 7th Lord Sutherland.3 He was born between 1395 and 1400 at of Dunbeath, Scotland. He married Catherine Chalmer circa 1422.4 Alexander Sutherland
2 CONC , Baron Dunbeath married Mariota of the Isles, daughter of Donald MacDonald, 8th Lord of the Isles and Mary Leslie, circa 1439.5 Alexander Sutherland, Baron Dunbeath died between 5 September 1454 and February 1456.6,7
2 CONT *Family 1 Catherine Chalmer d. a 1456 
