1 NAME Robert /Sutherland/
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Sutherland
2 _MARNM Sutherland
1 NAME Robert, Master of Sutherland
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/4/mode/2up Page 5 (No. 19-b)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0036
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, according to Sir Robert Gordon, married the younger daughter and co-heiress of James Dunbar of Frendraught, and had a son John, who died without issue. This statement has not been verified, and Sir Robert's pedigree of the
2 CONC  Dunbar family is erroneous. It may be noted, however, that Janet Dunbar, the eldest co-heiress, who married James Crichton, married as her second husband before 1458 a John Sutherland, who may have been the son of Robert, but the
2 CONC y had no issue. Robert Sutherland was, according to the family historian, still alive in 1487, when he is said to have led a company of Sutherland men against the Rosses at the battle of Aldycharrish; but if so, he must have been 
2 CONC a very old man, and it may be doubted if it were not another person of the same name.[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT [13] Genealogy, pp. 74, 78, 79. 
