1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Share some things about Malise, 7th Earl of Strathearn
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maol_%C3%8Dosa_IV,_Earl_of_Strathearn
2 CONT
2 CONT Maol Íosa IV of Strathearn, who ruled Strathearn (1317–1329), is the seventh known Mormaer of Strathearn, but of course this is simply a source problem and in no way means that he was the seventh in actuality.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maol Íosa was an ardent supporter of the cause of Robert de Brus during the Scottish Wars of Independence, even fighting against his father Maol Íosa III, whom he captured in 1313. Maol Íosa IV's with King Robert probably saved th
2 CONC e life of old Maol Íosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married a woman called Johanna, by whom he sired Mormaer Maol Íosa V, the last traditional Gaelic Mormaer of Strathearn.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ID: I26486 Name: Malise of Strathearn Sex: M Birth: BET 1275 AND 1280 in 7th Earl of Strathern Death: BEF 1329 Reference Number: 26486 Note: Malise, 7th Earl of Strathearn was born between 1275 and 1280.2 He married Agnes.3 He mar
2 CONC ried Joan Menteith, daughter of Sir John Menteith, circa 1323.1 He died before 1329.2 He died before 1320.3  Malise, 7th Earl of Strathearn gained the title of Earl of Strathearn.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 Agnes d. after 1311  Child Malise, 8th Earl of Strathearn+ b. c 1290, d. bt 1344 - 13572 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 Joan Menteith b. before 1315, d. after 1367 
