1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note:  There seem to be some generations missing.  The genealogy here does not match up with that contained in The Red Book of Menteith, which is available at archive.org.  There should be the William who is father
2 CONC  of the James who fell at Flodden in 1513, and this William was known as Sir William Menteith of Kerse and Alva, and he was married to Helen Bruce.  He had on May 24 1508 a charter from King James IV, to himself & spouse, on resig
2 CONC nation of his grandfather, of lands in Alva.  His mother was Ann (or Agnes) Erskine, and his father, was another William Menteith.  That William's father, who he predeceased, was yet another William Menteith of Kerse and Alva whos
2 CONC e wife is unnamed.    (This is where there could be an error in the book - possibly the William whose wife is unnamed is actually the William who was married to Ann Erskine?).  Anyway, next generation back, father to William is ag
2 CONC ain William Menteith of Kerse who was married to Helen Livingston.  Their children are listed as William, Archibald, Alexander, and John, and a daughter Elizabeth who married Sir John Bruce of Stanehouse in 1471.  It was this Will
2 CONC iam, the one married to Helen Livingstone, whose mother was Elizabeth Graham.  His father was Sir William Menteith of Kerse, who received on Oct 23 1382 a charter from King Robert II, to himself and Elizabeth his wife, of the land
2 CONC s of Carse, etc., on the resignation of Marjory Stirling his mother. Please have a look at the book and at the dates and also maybe check the subsequent review of the Red Book of Menteith (I haven't checked this) to see if there h
2 CONC as been some mistake here on Geni or if I am way off. However, the dates currently listed on Geni don't support the genealogy listed here. -  cheers, L Todd 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I3806&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Sir John of the Stanehous, married 1471, '''Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Menteith of Karse''', and by her had issue three sons and three daughters
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n44/mode/1up?view=theater
2 CONT ----
