2 CONT '''17 December 1400: Copy of Charter by David Earl of Carrick, eldest son of King Robert III., to Sir Gilbert Kennedy Knight and Agnes Maxwell his wife in liferent, and after their decease James Kennedy their son and the heirs mal
2 CONC e of his body, whom failling Alexander Kennedy and the heirs male of his body, whom failing Hugh Kennedy and the heirs male of his body, whom failing John Kennedy and the heirs male of his body, whom failing Thomas Kennedy and the
2 CONC  heirs male of his body, whom failing David Kennedy and the heirs male of his body, whom failing the nearest heirs whatsoever of the said Sir Gilbert Kennedy, of the lands of Dunure with the Castle thereof and lands of Girvan and 
2 CONC Glenop lying in the Earldom of Carrick, proceeding on the resignation of the said Sir Gilbert Kennedy; To be holden of the Earl and his successors, blanch for payment yearly in the Church of Ayr, on the Feast of St. John the Bapti
2 CONC st, of a pair of gilt spurs. Witnesses - David Lord Lindsay, Sir William Lindsay, Sir William Cunningham and Sir Robert Lauder, Knights, Patrick de Hepburn, and John de Ramorny. Dated at Ayr. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/n
2 CONC rsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f25&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), refe
2 CONC rence GD25/1/25]'''
