1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Egidia's husband Alexander was born Seton but changed his surname to Gordon (his mother's maiden name) before 1458.  See the entry on him for details.  That means that he was probably Seton during the time he and E
2 CONC gidia were married.  Yet several of their children are called Gordon.  I don't know the answer to this. -- Dominik Wujastyk, July 2012.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Egidia's husband Alexander was born Seton but changed his surname to Gordon (his mother's maiden name) before 1458.  See the entry on him for details.  That means that he was probably Seton during the time he and Egidia were marri
2 CONC ed.  Yet several of their children are called Gordon.  I don't know the answer to this. -- Dominik Wujastyk, July 2012.
