1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CATHERINE GRAHAM (aka KATHERINE GRAHAM)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The ancestry of Catherine Graham here treated is not certainly knowm. It has been suggested that she was the daughter of Alexander Graham and Elizabeth Wood [http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p5937.htm#i1
2 CONC 78268 Our Royal, Titled, Noble, and Commoner Ancestors] but this proposition finds no support in the Scots Peerage. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06paul#page/219/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, Volume VI, pp. 219-20] Thi
2 CONC s particular Alexander  Graham is known to have had a daughter named Catherine but she was married to Sir Humphrey Moray of Ogilvy and Abercairny [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06paul#page/220/mode/1up The Scots Peera
2 CONC ge, Volume VI, p. 220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Master Cuthberti Simonis===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: Instrument of resignation by George Wallace, in the hands of John Walles of Cragy, as superior, in favour of Patrick Walles, son and apparent heir of the said George, of all right, claim, property and possession 
2 CONC which he had in or to the lands of Ellersly, in the shire of Renfrew: reserving, however, to himself and to Katherine Graham, his spouse, the frank tenement of the foresaid lands during their respective lives. Whereup the said Pat
2 CONC rick asked instruments. Done at the castle of Cragy, on the 24th day of March 1499 [1500], at six o'clock in the afternoon, or thereby, in presence of Hugh Walles and William Walles, brothers german to the said John Walles of Crag
2 CONC y, Robert Walles, Gavin Ros, Charles Ros, Sir John Ledhous, chaplain, and John Douglas, witnesses to the premisses. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/266/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc
2 CONC . A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 2 on p. 266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:[https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/2/mode/1upThe original protocol was written in latin. It can be viewed at pp. 2-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: Instrument on the reservation by the said George Walles of Ellirsly, of the frank tenement of the lands above resigned, to himself and Katherine Graham, his spouse, during theor lives. Done at the same time and p
2 CONC lace,and before the same witnesses as above. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/267/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 3 on p. 267]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/3/mode/1up  The original protocol was wriiten in latin. It can be viewed at p. 3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1499-1500: Rex confirmavit cartam Johannis Wallace de Cragy, sub hac forma; - [To all men etc.,- Johnne Wallace of Cragy greting;-Wit ye me to have gevin and grantit to my dearest cousing PATRIK WALLACE, son and appe
2 CONC rand ayre to my derest eme George Wallace of Ellirsle, - for the homage and service of the said Patrick, etc., - my landis of Ellersle in the barony of Renfrew and schirefdome of the samyn; quilkis landis of before wer of the said
2 CONC  George heretably, and the quikis he of his free will and deliverir mynde, wilfully be staff and bastoun in my handis as oure lord resignit: To be HALDIN to the said Patrik and hys airis mail quatsumever, the quilkis failyeand tur
2 CONC nand to me the said Johne and my airis quatsumever: GEVAND tharfore yerly homage and service with dewities aucht and wonnt:- Reservand nevertheles the cheif chymmes to the said Johnne and to his airis, and half ane merkis worth of
2 CONC  land of aild extent liand nixt and togidder to the said chief chymmes; and alsa reservand the franktenement of the said landis of Ellersle to the said George Wallace and to Katherine Graham his spous and the langar levand of tham
2 CONC e:- In witnes etc., - At Cragy the third of Februare 1499, - befor thir witnes, Hew Wallace, William Wallace my broder germane, Robert Wallace, Johnne Lokarte, Charles Ros, Gawane Ros, and schir Donald Moffet, chaplain. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/536/mode/1up Great Seal of Scotland, II, charter number 2527 on pp. 536-37]'''
