2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith [1]
2 CONT *M, #20517, 
2 CONT *d. circa 1543/44
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Aug 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith was the son of Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Buchanan.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Moubray, daughter of John Moubray of Barnbougle, before 16 June 1521.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died circa 1543/44, allegedly killed in a clan feud with the Tutor of the Stewarts of Appin, whose retinue had eaten up a wedding breakfast at which the 3rd Earl of Menteith was a guest, constituting a casus belli.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Menteith [S., 1427] in 1537.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Moubray
2 CONT *1. John Graham, 4th Earl of Menteith+[1] d. Jan 1564/65
2 CONT *2. Lady Margaret Graham+[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2751. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 199. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
