2 CONT Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly [1]
2 CONT *M, #13398, 
2 CONT *d. 21 January 1523/24
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly married by contract, firstly, Lady Jean Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl and Margaret Douglas, on 14 October 1474.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Elizabeth Gray, daughter of Andrew Gray, 2nd Lord Gray and Janet Keith, after 27 July 1511.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 21 January 1523/24.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly and Lady Elizabeth Hay.[1],[2] 
2 CONT *He was granted Strathavon, Banffshire and the Brae of Lochaber.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Huntly [S., 1445] in June 1501.[1] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland].[1] 
2 CONT *He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513, where he commanded the Scots left wing.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Member of the Council Regency in 1517.[1]
2 CONT
