1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Mariot Home:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2042.htm#i20412
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariot Home [1]
2 CONT *F, #20412
2 CONT *Last Edited=22 Apr 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Mariot Home married John Lindsay, 6th Earl of Crawford, son of David Lindsay, 1st Duke of Montrose and Elizabeth Hamilton, between January 1493 and August 1493.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She is the daughter of Alexander Home, 2nd Lord Home and Nichole Ker.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From between January 1493 and August 1493, her married name became Lindsay.[1] As a result of her marriage, Mariot Home was styled as Countess of Crawford on 25 December 1495.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was living on 16 January 1533/34.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 513. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 221.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 514.
