2 CONT
2 CONT NameLady Jean KEITH Of Inverugie , F Birth Dateabt 1491 Birth PlaceInverugie, Banffshire, Scotland Death Dateabt 1522 Death PlacePitsligo, Aberdeenshire, Scotland FatherSir William KEITH 5th Of Inverugie , M (~1453-1521) MotherLad
2 CONC y Janet DUNBAR Of Cumnock , F (~1472-) Spouses 1Laird John FORBES 4th Of Pitsligo , M Birth Dateabt 1487 Birth PlacePitsligo, Aberdeenshire, Scotland Death Date16 Mar 1556 Death PlacePitsligo, Aberdeenshire, Scotland Death MemoIn 
2 CONC his 70th year. FatherSir Alexander FORBES 3rd Of Pitsligo , M (~1468-~1496) MotherLady Isabel / Elizabeth WEMYSS , F (~1470->1524) Marr Dateabt 1512 ChildrenChristian , F (~1512-1580)
2 CONT  Alexander “The Red Laird” , M (~1513-1562)
2 CONT  Arthur , M (~1514-1547)
2 CONT  Marjory , F (~1516-)
2 CONT  John , M (~1518-)
2 CONT  William , M (~1520-)
2 CONT  UNNAMED , F (~1522-) Notes for Lady Jean KEITH Of Inverugie He married, first, Jean, daughter of Sir William Keith of Inverugy;
2 CONT
2 CONT second, Isabel or Elizabeth, daughter of James Innes of that Ilk, and relict of George Meldrum of Fyvie; They had a charter in the lands of Meikle Wardis about 1523.
2 CONT
2 CONT John died 16 may 1556, in his seventieth year.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Alexander, his heir. 2. Arthur, killed at Pinkie 1547 3. John. 4. William 5. Christian, married to George Straton of Lauriston. 6. Marjory, married, first, to Henry Bannerman of Waterton; second, to Alexander Menzies. 7. _____,
2 CONC  married to [Alexander] Keith of Pittendrum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE SCOTS PEERAGE, ed. by Sir James Balfour Paul, Vol IV, Edinburgh, 1906, p.72. ------------------------------
