2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 October 1506: A letter made to JONET STEWART, spouse of the deceased Sir Alexander Bruce of Earlshall, and Edward Bruce of Kynnard, of the gift of the ward etc. of the deceased Sir Alexander Bruce of Earlshall, and the marri
2 CONC age of his heir, William Bruce, and, in the event that he dies without having married, the marriage of any other heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/192/mode/1up RSS 1488-1529: number 1347]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1517: Ane Lettre maid with consent of the govemour to JONET STEWART the relict of umquhile Alexander Bruce of Erlishall, knycht, and to hir assignais, ane or maa, — of the gift of the warde of all landis and heretage quh
2 CONC ilkis pertenit to umquhile Michell Balfour of Monquhanny . . . . . [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/455/mode/1up RSS 1488-1529: 2914]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n9/mode/1up Registrum Secreti Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The register of the Privy seal of Scotland. Vol I. A. D. 1488-1529. Edited by M. Livingstone, ISO., Late Deputy-K
2 CONC eeper of the Records of Scotland (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1908), 824 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
