2 CONT '''10 April 1482: Contract of Marriage between Gilbert Ramsay, son of Alexander Ramsay of Woodwrae, and Margaret Ogilvy, daughter of Sir James Ogilvy of Airlie. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?
2 CONC reference=GD83%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family of Bamff, Perthshire, reference GD83/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This document is printed in Sir James H Ramsay, bart., (ed.) 'Bamff Charters A.D. 1232-1703', (Oxford, 1915), pp. 31-33. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/31/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 
2 CONC 13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 April 1483: Precept by Finlay Ramsay of Bamff for infefting his grandson Gilbert Ramsay and his wife in the lands of Mawes and Petdrey (Pitdray). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD83%2f14&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=finlay+Ramsay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family of Bamff, Perthshire, reference GD83/14]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1483: Instrument of sasine which confirms possession of the lands of Mawis and Peddrey to Gilbert Ramsay and his wife Margaret Ogilvy. Gilbert Ramsay is identified as the son and apparent heir Alexander Ramsay, the son a
2 CONC nd heir of Finlay Ramsay. [https://archive.org/details/bamffchartersad100rams/page/34/mode/1up Bamff Charters: charter number 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 June 1495: Notarial instrument narrating that James, Lord Ogilwy, declared that Alexander Caldor of Futhas had bound himself to renounce in favour of the said Lord all writs relating to the lands of Campsy, Kynhard and Balnak
2 CONC elzhe; and the said Alexander swore on oath that he had not retained any such writs and revoked all grants made to him of the said lands. Witnesses: Oliver Ogilwy, Gilbert Ramsay, son and heir apparent of Alexander Ramsay of Banff
2 CONC , David Fothringam, David Irnys, David Ouchterlowny and Andrew Parrys. Symmerhyll, near the castle of Erly. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f3%2f25&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=al
2 CONC exander+Ramsay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1580&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/3/25]'''
2 CONT
