1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on James Ogilvy:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p1337.htm#i13361
2 CONT
2 CONT James Ogilvy, 3rd Lord Ogilvy of Airlie1
2 CONT *M, #13361, 
2 CONT *d. between 1513 and 29 November 1524
2 CONT *Last Edited=27 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT James Ogilvy, 3rd Lord Ogilvy of Airlie was the son of Sir John Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Ogilvy of Airlie and Jean Graham.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Lindsay, daughter of Alexander Lindsay of Auchtermonzie, 7th Earl of Crawford and Isobel Campbell.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between 1513 and 29 November 1524.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Ogilvy of Airlie [S., 1491] before 9 January 1505/6.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Ogilvy, 3rd Lord Ogilvy of Airlie and Margaret Lindsay
2 CONT *1. Margery Ogilvy+
2 CONT *2. John Ogilvy [3]
2 CONT *3. Archibald Ogilvy [3]
2 CONT *4. Margaret Ogilvy [3]
2 CONT *5. Isobel Ogilvy [3]
2 CONT *6. Beatrix Ogilvy [4]
2 CONT *7. James Ogilvy, 4th Lord Ogilvy of Airlie+ b. b 1505, d. bt 27 Nov 1547 - 13 Jul 1548
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 70. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 45. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage
2 CONC , 106th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 116. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage
2 CONC .
2 CONT *4. [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage, volume I, page 117.
