1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sources
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/272/mode/2up The Scots Peerage Vol 4] page 272. "Sir Andrew Gray of Broxmouth ... married secondly, daughter of Sir Walter Buchanan, knight ... she married secondly, Si
2 CONC r Thomas Oliphant of Dron, and was dead in 1471."
2 CONT # [http://books.google.com/books?id=ULhUAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA73&ots=ViVOpWqCOe&dq=Thomas%20Oliphant%20of%20Dron&pg=PA73#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20Oliphant%20of%20Dron&f=false The book of Perth] (Google eBook) John Parker Lawson.T. G. Stevens
2 CONC on, 1847 - Perth (Scotland) - 318 pages.  Page 73. "The Church of St. John the Baptist ... Thomas Oliphant of Dron is said to have been the second son of Sir John Oliphant of Aberdalgie, and younger brother of Laurence first Lord 
2 CONC Oliphant. He died on the 11th of December 1474, and left as an obit the sum of L.2, of which twenty-six shillings eight pennies were to be paid out of the lands of Wester Dron and Kintilloch, and thirteen shillings four pennies ou
2 CONC t of a tenement on the east side of the Kirkgate of Perth. Each officiating chorister was to receive twelve pennies, and each foundation chaplain who joined in the service eight pennies."
2 CONT
