1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 22. Sir James INNES , 12th of that Ilk was born about 1437 in Innes, MOR, SCT. He died about 1491. He is reference number 126. 12th Chief of Innes. Known as "James with the Beard". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Esquire to King James III. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James Innes had a precept of sasine from Alexander, Earl of Huntly, on 24 October 1464. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In November 1467 the Earl of Huntly added the lands of Blaremade from his own estates to that of Sir James Innes. This appears to have been a tocher given with his daughter. This is further evident by the precept of seasine said t
2 CONC hat failing heirs of her body, it was to be returned again to the Earl's own family. This proves that the estate of Blaremade was not previously part of the Innes estates. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1490 he entertained King James IV at Innes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James INNES , 12th of that Ilk and Lady Janet GORDON were married about 1460. Lady Janet GORDON (daughter of Alexander GORDON , 1st Earl of Huntly) died before 1473. She is reference number 127. Sir James INNES , 12th of that 
2 CONC Ilk and Lady Janet GORDON had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i.Janet INNES.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.Elizabeth INNES.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.Alexander INNES , 13th of that Ilk.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Robert INNES , of Rathmackenzie & Crommey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James INNES , 12th of that Ilk and Margaret CULANE were married before 26 Oct 1473. Margaret CULANE is reference number 191. Sir James INNES , 12th of that Ilk and Margaret CULANE had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i.William INNES , of Crommey6 is reference number 1459.
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.George INNES6 is reference number 194.
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. James INNES , of Rothiebrisbane6 is reference number 1465.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.Thomas INNES6 is reference number 1466.
