1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN GARBH MACLEAN OF COLL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Iain Garve MacLean, 1st of Coll, was a younger son of Lachlan 'Bronnach' MacLean, chief of the MacLeans, and Finola MacLeod. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel Fraser of Lovat. Iain Garve MacLean received from Macdonald, lord of the Isles, a charter of the twenty-pound lands of Coll, and the eighteen-merk lands of Cuinish in Mull. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ian Garve MacLean was a daring warrior of whose prowess the traditions of the western isles furnish many an interesting anecdote, even to the present day. He lived feared by his enemies, and respected by his friends. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son Iain Abrach.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
