1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Alexander Dundas of Fingask===
2 CONT * Son of:	 Alexander Dundas, son of James Dundas 11th of Dundas
2 CONT * and:	Elizabeth (Euffame) daughter of Sir Alexander Livingston of Callender 
2 CONT * born:
2 CONT * died:	 9th September 1513 at the battle of Flodden
2 CONT
2 CONT From www.dundasfamily.co.uk/record_61.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Dundas was served and retoured as heir to his father at Perth in 1460 although only in the lands of Fingask and not Dundas and from thenceforth designed himself from that estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was slain at the battle of Flodden along with four sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel, daughter of Laurence Lord Oliphant and Lady Isabel Hay
2 CONT
2 CONT The following children were born of this union: 1.	Alexander Dundas 2.	 Adam Dundas of Oxmure in Berwickshire. These lands were granted to him in 1513 and a further grant of land in Edinburgh was granted in 1525. (Register of the 
2 CONC great seal of Scotland) 3.	Margaret Dundas 4.	Archibald Dundas married Helen Arnot daughter and co-heiress of William Arnot of Balbarton in Fife . As a result of the marriage, Archibald Dundas obtained the lands of Knightspotty in
2 CONC  the barony of Abernethy and shire of Perth (sold 1584), also a tack of the lands of Bannachie near Kirkcaldy Fife . He left issue ...
2 CONT
