1 NOTE {geni:about_me} AI Overview      05/13/26
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on genealogical records and historical notes, the parents of Sir Richard de Glen (who married Margaret MacGilronan, often identified as Margaret nic Uilleam or Margaret de Mar) are identified as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John de Ness (sometimes referred to as John de Glen or John de le Glen).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Key Details Regarding Sir Richard de GlenHe is described as "Lord of the Glen" or "Richard de le Glen".He is often noted in records from around 1292, when he was deceased, and his lands in the Lennox were placed in wardship by Edw
2 CONC ard I of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Margaret MacGilronan (1253–1292/1337), was a lady of Mar/Erskine.His son and heir was John de Glen (born c. 1279), who was a beneficiary of a charter of lands (Gaytflat) in 1292.Some sources suggest the Glen family held 
2 CONC their lands under the Stewards, and the family name was assumed from the Lordship of Glen in Renfrewshire, with early connections to the de Ness line.
