1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert's only child by his first marriage was
2 CONT
2 CONT * Marjorie Bruce, married Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland (1293–1326). 
2 CONT
2 CONT By his second wife Elizabeth he had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * David II,
2 CONT * John (died in childhood),
2 CONT * Matilda (who married Thomas Isaac and died at Aberdeen 20 July 1353), and
2 CONT * Margaret (who married William de Moravia, 5th Earl of Sutherland in 1345).
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his legitimate offspring, Robert Bruce had several illegitimate children by unknown mothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir Robert (died 12 August 1332 at the Battle of Dupplin Moor);
2 CONT * Walter, of Odistoun on the Clyde, who predeceased his father; and
2 CONT * Niall, of Carrick, (died 17 October 1346 at the Battle of Neville's Cross).
2 CONT * Elizabeth (married Walter Oliphant of Gask);
2 CONT * Margaret (married Robert Glen), alive as of 29 February 1364; and
2 CONT * Christian of Carrick, who died after 1329, when she was in receipt of a pension
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>---------------------------------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter G. Ashworth 19th GGS
