1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MATILDA  de BRUCE (aka MATILDIS de BRUYS)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Matilda Bruce is the daughter of Robert I, King of Scots. and Elizabeth de Burgh, [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/7/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 8] and the sister of David II, King of Scots. [https
2 CONC ://archive.org/details/sutherlandbookv300fras/page/11/mode/1up The Sutherland Book III: charter number 12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to John of Fordun’s Chronicle, "Matildem…et Margaritam" were the two daughters of "Robertus, adhuc comes" and his wife "Elizabeth filiam Haymeri de Burkis comitis de Hullister" He added that Matilda "did nothing worth
2 CONC  recording" and in a later passage that Matilda married "Thomæ Isak" by whom she had two daughters, "Johannam" who married "Johanni domini de Lorn" and had "filios et filias", and "Catherinam" who died "apud Strivelyn".  The same 
2 CONC source in a later passage records the death "on the feast of the blessed virgin Margaret" in 1353 at Aberdeen of "Matilda of Bruce sister of the lord David king of Scotland" and her burial "at Dunfermline", adding that she married
2 CONC  "a certain squire named Thomas Isaac" and had two daughters Joan, who was the wife of John of Lorn, lord of that ilk, and Catherine who died "at Strivelyn".  Matilda married Thomas Isaac.  [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLA
2 CONC ND.htm#_Toc65391152 Medieval Lands]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 September 1345: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which David II, King of Scots, confirms possession of the thanedoms of Douny, Kincardine, and Aberluthnot, and half of Formartine and Kintore, to his sister Margare
2 CONC t and her husband William, Earl of Sutherland. His sister Matilda's possessions in the Thanage of Fermartyn ,and Kintore, were excluded from the King David's grant: "saluo jure quod Matildis de Bruys, soror nostra carissima, habet
2 CONC  ad eandem medietatem thaynagiorum de Fermartyne et de Kintor virtute concessionis nostre sibi per nos exinde facte, si ipsam prefatam Margaretam, sororem nostram, superuiuere contingat." [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=md
2 CONC p.35112105151130&view=image&seq=515 RMS, 1305-1424; Appendix I, charter number 120]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This charter is printed in full in volume three of The Sutherland Book. [https://archive.org/details/sutherlandbookv300fras/page/11/mode/1up The Sutherland Book III: charter number 12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112105151130&view=image&seq=7 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A.D. 1306-1424. New Edition, to which are added indexes and Remains 
2 CONC of the Lost Charter Rolls. Edited by James Maitland Thomson, LL.D. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1912), 780 pp. including indexes]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/sutherlandbookv300fras/page/n5/mode/1up The Sutherland Book. By Sir William Fraser. KCB., LL.D. Vol III - Charters (Edinburgh 1892), 357 pp. including index]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT #  [https://archive.org/details/sutherlandbookv300fras/page/11/mode/1up The Sutherland Book III: charter number 12]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/7/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 8]
2 CONT # [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc65391152 Medieval Lands]
2 CONT
2 CONT curators note
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1295, Robert the Brus married his first wife, Isabella of Mar (d. before 1302) the daughter of Domhnall (Donald), Earl of Mar (d. after July 1297)[13] by his wife Helen (1246 - after Feb 1295). They had one daughter, Marjorie, 
2 CONC who married Sir Walter FitzAlan, 6th High Steward of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married secondly, about September 19, 1295[14] Maud, daughter of John FitzAlan of Clun & Oswestry, and Arundel, Robert being her second husband: they had no issue, and a divorce was granted about 1301, presumably on grounds
2 CONC  of consanguinity.[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1302 Robert married his third wife, Elisabeth, daughter of Sir Richard de Burgh, 2nd Earl of Ulster, Knt.,[16] by his wife Margaret, daughter of John de Burgh, Baron of Lanvalley in Ireland. By Elizabeth, de Brus had four child
2 CONC ren: David, John (died in childhood), Matilda (who married Thomas Isaac and died at Aberdeen 20 July 1353), and Margaret (who married William de Moray, 5th Earl of Sutherland in 1345). http://en.metapedia.org/wiki/Robert_I_Bruce,_
2 CONC King_of_Scotland _______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Bruce1 
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #107865, d. before 22 September 1323
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Mary Bruce|d. b 22 Sep 1323|p10787.htm#i107865|Sir Robert le Brus, 1st Lord Brus|b. Jul 1243\nd. b 4 Apr 1304|p10776.htm#i107755|Margaret, Countess of Carrick|d. b 9 Nov 1292|p10248.htm#i102473|Sir Robert de Brus, Lord of Ann
2 CONC andale|b. 1210\nd. 31 Mar 1295|p10248.htm#i102474|Isabella de Clare|b. 2 Nov 1226\nd. a 10 Jul 1264|p10248.htm#i102475|Neil, 2nd Earl of Carrick|b. c 1202\nd. 1256|p10462.htm#i104611|Margaret Stewart|b. c 1206|p10785.htm#i107849|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=14 Apr 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT      Lady Mary Bruce was the daughter of Sir Robert le Brus, 1st Lord Brus and Margaret, Countess of Carrick.1 She married, firstly, Sir Neil Campbell of Lochow, son of Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow, circa 1312.1 She married, secon
2 CONC dly, Sir Alexander Fraser circa 1316.1 She died before 22 September 1323.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      From circa 1312, her married name became Campbell. From circa 1316, her married name became Fraser.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Mary Bruce and Sir Neil Campbell of Lochow
2 CONT
2 CONT Dougal Campbell+ d. a 13232 
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Campbell 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan Campbell Macdonnachie of Inverawe+ 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Campbell, 1st and last Earl of Atholl b. c 1313, d. 19 Jul 13331 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Mary Bruce and Sir Alexander Fraser
2 CONT
2 CONT John Fraser+ b. c 13171 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Fraser b. c 1318, d. 13461 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 208. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 103. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 1
2 CONC 06th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruce was a sister of King Robert I of Scotland (Robert the Bruce).
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with the king's other female relatives, she was captured and betrayed to the English by the Earl of Ross. By order of King Edward I of England, she was then held prisoner in a cage exposed to the public view in Roxburgh Cast
2 CONC le until 1310.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was eventually released, in exchange for English noblemen captured at the Battle of Bannockburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (1) Sir Neil Campbell, one of her brother's loyal supporters; (2) Alexander Fraser.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruce (b. c. 1282) was a younger sister of Robert the Bruce, King of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with the king's other female relatives, she was captured and betrayed to the English by the Earl of Ross. By order of King Edward I of England, she was then held prisoner in a cage exposed to the public view in Roxburgh Cast
2 CONC le until 1310. Isabella MacDuff was imprisoned in a similar cage at Berwick Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was eventually released, in exchange for English noblemen captured at the Battle of Bannockburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Sir Neil Campbell, one of her brother's loyal supporters; and secondly, Alexander Fraser of Touchfraser and Cowie. (from Wikipedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bruce was a sister of King Robert I of Scotland (Robert the Bruce).
2 CONT
2 CONT Along with the king's other female relatives, she was captured and betrayed to the English by the Earl of Ross. By order of King Edward I of England, she was then held prisoner in a cage exposed to the public view in Roxburgh Cast
2 CONC le until 1310.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was eventually released, in exchange for English noblemen captured at the Battle of Bannockburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (1) Sir Neil Campbell, one of her brother's loyal supporters; (2) Alexander Fraser.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Suggested birth years: 1303 and 1310.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10530.htm#i105299
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
