2 CONT
2 CONT Cawley [1] quotes 'John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) names "Matildem…et Margaritam" as the two daughters of "Robertus, adhuc comes" and his wife "Elizabeth filiam Haymeri de Burkis comitis de Hullister", adding that Ma
2 CONC tilda "did nothing worth recording" '
2 CONT
2 CONT She was sent to France "for her safety" in 1534 along with her sister and brother, King David. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married after June 1342 but before 1345.[2] She died at Aberdeen on July 20, 1353 and was buried at the church at Dumfermline. [2][3]
2 CONT
