1 OCCU Countess Of Carrick, Grevinna av Carrick, Countess of Carricik, Countess, Countess of Carrick. Married c.1271, 3rd Countess of Carrick, Countess of Carrick, III Countess of Carrick
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Marjorie of Carrick (also Margaret; c. 1253 or 1256 – soon bef. 9 November 1292) was Countess of Carrick, Scotland, from 1256 to 1292, and is notable as the mother of Robert the Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was the daughter and heiress of Niall, Earl of Carrick and Margaret Stewart, and Countess of Carrick in her own right. Her first husband was Adam of Kilconquhar, who died during the Eighth Crusade in 1271. Then, as the stor
2 CONC y goes, a handsome young man arrived one day to tell her of her husband's death in the Holy Land. He was Robert de Brus, (1243–soon bef. 4 March 1304), 6th Lord of Annandale, and he had been a companion-in-arms of Adam of Kilconqu
2 CONC har. Marjorie was so taken with him that she had him held captive until he agreed to marry her at Turnberry Castle in 1271. He became Earl of Carrick jure uxoris (in right of his wife). Their children were:
2 CONT * 1.Christina Bruce
2 CONT * 2.Robert the Bruce.
2 CONT * 3.Isabel Bruce (1275–1358), married King Eric II of Norway.
2 CONT * 4.Niall or Nigel Bruce, executed 1306 in Berwick-upon-Tweed, Northumberland, England.
2 CONT * 5.Edward Bruce.
2 CONT * 6.Sir Thomas Bruce, executed 1307.
2 CONT * 7.Alexander Bruce, executed 1307.
2 CONT * 8.Mary Bruce, married 1.Sir Niall Campbell  2.Sir Alexander Fraser of Touchfraser and Cowie.
2 CONT *9.Matilda Bruce, married Aodh, Earl of Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Bruce who married Sir William de Carlyle is thought by Barrow not to be their daughter. There is a traditional story that Thomas Randolph, 1st Earl of Moray was the son of '''Marjorie's daughter from her first marriage wi
2 CONC th Adam. However this is probably not true; it was probably put forward as an explanation of why Thomas Randolph was described as a nephew of Robert the Bruce. Any daughter of Adam of Kilconquhar would have inherited the Gaelic ti
2 CONC tle in the same way that Marjorie, eldest of four, or perhaps five, daughters did on her father's death. There is evidence that an "eldest daughter", unknown to history, married into the family of the earls of Mar, giving rise to 
2 CONC the now discounted first marriage of Christina to the son of the earl, Gratney.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marjorie died in before November 1292, at which time her husband transferred Carrick to their eldest son, Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marjorie,_Countess_of_Carrick ___________________
2 CONT *'''Margaret of Carrick1,2,3
2 CONT *'''F, #3117, b. circa 1252, d. before 27 October 1292
2 CONT *Father     Neil, 2nd Earl of Carrick2,4,3 d. b 1250
2 CONT *Mother     Isabel d. 1256
2 CONT *'''     Margaret of Carrick married Adam de Kilconquhar, 3rd Earl of Carrick, son of Donnchadh of Kilconquhar; Her 1st husband.5,2,4 Margaret of Carrick was born circa 1252.4 She married Sir Robert de Brus, Earl Carrick, Lord Ann
2 CONC andale, Sheriff of Cumberland, Governor of Carlisle Castle, son of Sir Robert de Brus, Lord Annandale, Sheriff of Cumberland, Governor of Carlisle Castle and Isabel de Clare, circa 1273 at Turnberry Castle, Ayrshire, Scotland; The
2 CONC y had 5 sons (Sir Robert, King of Scotland; Sir Edward, Lord of Galloway, Earl of Carrick, King of Ireland; Thomas; Alexander, Dean of Glasgow; & Sir Neil) and 5 daughters (Isabel, wife of Eric II Magnusson, King of Norway; Mary, 
2 CONC wife of Sir Neil Campbell, & of Sir Alexander Fraser, Chamberlain of Scotland; Christian, wife of Sir Christopher de Seton, & of Sir Andrew de Moray; Maud, wife of Hugh, 4th Earl of Ross; & Margaret, wife of Sir William de Carlyle
2 CONC ).2,4,3 Margaret of Carrick died before 27 October 1292.4
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Adam de Kilconquhar, 3rd Earl of Carrick d. 1271
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Isabel de Kilconquhar+
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Sir Robert de Brus, Earl Carrick, Lord Annandale, Sheriff of Cumberland, Governor of Carlisle Castle b. Jul 1243, d. 13 Jan 1304
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Mary de Brus+2,4 d. b 22 Sep 1323
2 CONT **Christian de Brus2,4 d. bt 1356 - 1357
2 CONT **Maud de Brus+2,4 d. bt Sep 1323 - 1329
2 CONT **Sir Edward de Brus, Earl of Carrick, King of Ireland, Lord of Galloway+2,4 d. 14 Oct 1318
2 CONT **Sir Thomas de Brus2,4 d. 17 Feb 1307
2 CONT **Alexander de Brus2,4 d. 17 Feb 1307
2 CONT **Sir Nigel de Brus2,4 d. Sep 1306
