2 CONT *'''Margaret, Countess of Carrick1
2 CONT *'''F, #102473, d. before 9 November 1292
2 CONT *Last Edited=11 May 2008
2 CONT *'''     Margaret, Countess of Carrick was the daughter of Neil, 2nd Earl of Carrick and Margaret Stewart.1 She married, firstly, Adam de Kilconquhar, Earl of Carrick before 4 October 1266.1 She married, secondly, Sir Robert le Br
2 CONC us, 1st Lord Brus, son of Sir Robert de Brus, Lord of Annandale and Isabella de Clare, in 1271 at Turnberry Castle, Turnberry, Ayrshire, Scotland, without Royal consent, and so she had to pay a heavy fine.2 She died before 9 Novem
2 CONC ber 1292.1
2 CONT *'''     She was also known as Marjorie. She succeeded to the title of 3rd Countess of Carrick [S., c. 1186] in 1256, suo jure.2 From 1271, her married name became le Brus.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Margaret, Countess of Carrick and Sir Robert le Brus, 1st Lord Brus
2 CONT ** 1.Edward de Bruce, 1st Earl and last of Carrick+ d. 14 Oct 1318
2 CONT ** 2.Sir Thomas Bruce d. 9 Feb 1307
2 CONT ** 3.Alexander Bruce d. 9 Feb 1307
2 CONT ** 4.Neil Bruce d. c Sep 1306
2 CONT ** 5.Lady Mary Bruce+3 d. b 22 Sep 1323
2 CONT ** 6.Lady Christina Bruce+3 d. 1356/57
2 CONT ** 7.Margaret Bruce+3
2 CONT ** 8.Matilda Bruce+3 d. bt 1323 - 1329
2 CONT ** 9.Robert I Bruce, King of Scotland+ b. 11 Jul 1274, d. 7 Jun 1329
2 CONT ** 10.Isabella Bruce+4 b. c 1275, d. 1358
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 206. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 2.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 55. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 3.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families, page 208.
2 CONT * 4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 56.
