2 CONT *'''     Lady Mary Bruce was the daughter of Sir Robert le Brus, 1st Lord Brus and Margaret, Countess of Carrick.1 She married, firstly, Sir Neil Campbell of Lochow, son of Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow, circa 1312.1 She married, s
2 CONC econdly, Alexander Fraser of Touchfraser and Cowie, son of Andrew Fraser and Beatrix (?), circa 1316.1 She died before 22 September 1323.1
2 CONT *'''      From circa 1312, her married name became Campbell. From circa 1316, her married name became Fraser. In 1332 and was killed at defeat of Scots by an invading host of English lords at Dupplin 12 August issue.2
