1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice de LINDSAY, daughter of Sir Alexander de LINDSAY Knight  and N.N. Stewart [1, 2, 3, 4, 5] was born 1298 in Crawford, Lanarkshire, Scotland. She died 1352 in Erskine, Renfrewshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice married Sir Archibald DOUGLAS Knight on 1314 in Douglas, Lanarkshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  		F	i	Eleanor DOUGLAS was born 1317.
2 CONT *  		M	ii	John DOUGLAS 1 was born 1319 in Douglas, Lanarkshire, Scotland. He died 1339 in Douglas, Lanarkshire, Scotland.
2 CONT *  		M	iii	Sir William DOUGLAS Earl of Douglas was born 1321 and died May 1384
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice married Sir Robert ERSKINE Knight on 1334 in Erskine, Renfrewshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT *  		M	i	Sir Thomas ERSKINE Knight was born 1338 and died May 1404.
2 CONT *  		M	ii	Sir Nicholas ERSKINE Knight was born 1341 and died Dec 1406.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#BeatriceLindsayM1ArchibaldDouglas
2 CONT
2 CONT BEATRICE Lindsay m firstly Sir ARCHIBALD Douglas, son of Sir WILLIAM Douglas of Douglas & his first wife Elizabeth Stewart (-killed in battle Halidon Hill 19 Jul 1333).  m secondly Sir ROBERT Erskine of Erskine, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''The Scots Peerage, Vol. 3.  “Lindsay, Earl of Crawford.” Page 9.  < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/9/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >''
2 CONT
2 CONT The five children of Alexander Lindsay and his wife were: 
2 CONT # Sir David de Lindsay, Lord Crawford, Custodian of Berwick & Edinburgh Castle+ d. 1355.  Married Maria Abernethy, widow of Andrew de Leschelyn (Leslie) and daughter (co-heiress with her sister Margaret, Countess of Angus) of Sir 
2 CONC Alexander de Abernethy.
2 CONT # Alexander,11 who was imprisoned at Carlisle, 1308-1314, became a knight banneret, and was ancestor, as alleged, of the Lindsays of Ormiston, afterwards represented by Cockburn of Langton.
2 CONT # Reginald, prisoner at Carlisle with his brother.
2 CONT # William, Rector of Ayr,1 and Chamberlain of Scotland in 1317, whose close connection with the house of Crawford2 suggests this affiliation.  He died before 5 Kal. January 1339.
2 CONT # Beatrix, d. b 1352,  married, first, to Sir Archibald Douglas, and was mother of the first Earl of Douglas ; 3 secondly, to Sir Robert Erskine of Erskine, Great Chamberlain of Scotland.4
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p114.htm#i3407
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/genealogy/aqwc1788.htm#54369C1 cites
2 CONT ##1Cokayne, George Edward, ''The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant'' (London: St. Catherine Press, 1910.), 4:430, Los Angeles Public Library, 929.721 
2 CONC C682.
2 CONT ##Johnston, George Harvey, ''The Heraldry of the Douglases: With Notes on All the Males of the Family, Descriptions of the Arms, Plates, and Pedigrees'' (Edinburgh: W. & A.K. Johnston, 1907.), p. 14, Family History Library, 929.24
2 CONC 1 D745j.
2 CONT ##Paul, James Balfour, ''The Scots Peerage'' (Edinburgh: D. Douglas, 1904-14.), 3:141, Los Angeles Public Library, 929.72 P324.
2 CONT ##Cokayne, G., ''CP'', 3:57.
2 CONT ##Linzee, John William, ''The Lindeseie and Limesi Families of Great Britain'' (Boston, Massachusetts: The Fort Hill Press, 1917.), pp. 293, 301, Family History Library, 929.242 L659L.
2 CONT # < [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ll/lindsay01.php#alexdau Stirnet - ‘Lindsay01’] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Erskine-of-that-Ilk/6000000220051411840 Sir Robert] married twice:
2 CONT
2 CONT x (1) '''Beatrice Lindsay''', daughter of Alexander Lindsay of Crawford and widow of Sir Archibald Douglas, Regent of Scotland, who died in 1333 at Halidon Hill. Children:
2 CONT *'''Thomas Erskine''' – his heir.
2 CONT *'''Nicholas of Kinnoull''' – uterine brother of Thomas. Received Kinnoull from his father in 1367. Present at King Robert II’s coronation in 1371. Died before December 1406. x (1) Jean Cameron, daughter and co-heiress of Sir John
2 CONC  Cameron of Balegarno. Son: William, succeeded at Kinnoull. Grandson: Sir John, died in 1445, leaving a daughter and heiress, who  was successively: contracted to James, son of James, 1st Lord Livingstone (unmarried); married to J
2 CONC ohn Crichton (details unknown), and later married Robert, 1st Lord Crichton of Sanquhar xx (2) Elizabeth Keith, widow of Sir Adam Gordon of that Ilk
2 CONT *'''Marion Erskine''' – married before 1362 to Maurice Drummond, 2nd of Concraig, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT xx (2) '''Christian Menteith (or Keith)''', widow of Sir Edward Keith of Sinton. This marriage was part of a reconciliation after Sir Robert had wounded her cousins during a feud. A dispensation was needed due to their kinship (Be
2 CONC atrice and Christian were related in the fourth degree). Due to clerical error, they married before the dispensation arrived. The marriage was later legitimised by the Pope. Although they had children, none appear to have survived
2 CONC . Christian survived Sir Robert and died around 1387.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References
2 CONT *[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/592/mode/2up James Balfour Paul, ed., ''The Scots Peerage'', vol. 5 (Edinburgh: D. Douglas, 1904), p592-96]
