1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN LIVINGSTON OF DRUMRY===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Livingston of Drumry succeeded Sir William Livingston of Drumry. It is not certain but quite likely, probable even, that they are father and son. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08paul#page/368/mode/1up The Scots 
2 CONC Peerage, viii, p.369]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Livingston of Drumry died in or before 1367 when his son Robert was still a minor child. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08paul#page/368/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, viii, p.369]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Livingston of Drumry married one of the three daughters and  co-heiresses of Sir Michael Wemyss of Wemyss. [https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/79/mode/1up Memorials of the Family of Wemyss of Wemyss, pp. 4
2 CONC 1-2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Child===
