1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Took a prominent part in public affairs and witnessed various charters. He was among those involved in decision making regarding selection of an heir to the throne of Scotland. He initially supported John Balliol a
2 CONC s King, but after King Edward I of England seized Scotland, he was among the Scottish nobles who did homage to him. King Edward I stayed at Wemyss Castle in March 1304.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Sources:'''
2 CONT >Memorials of the family of Wemyss of Wemyss - https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/44/mode/2up
2 CONT >[https://archive.org/details/memorialsoffamil01fras/page/61/mode/1up Chapter V] from the same source is devoted to this Michael from ca.1330–ca.1342.
2 CONT
