1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER STEWART OF AVANDALE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Stewart of Avondale was the son of Walter Stewart of Morphie and his wife Elizabeth Arnot. He died before 6 June 1489.  He held the office of Lord Auditor in January 1488-89
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Alexander Stewart
2 CONT # William Stewart
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 February 1481-82: Charter de me by Colin, earl of Ergile, to Duncan Campbell of Glenurcharde, of lands of Kilbride excepting the half merkland of Le Fery of Cragane, in earldom of Argyll, sheriffdom thereof, and that for ren
2 CONC unciation of all title and claim to a third part of lands of Dolare in sheriffdom of Clakmanan, and a third part of lands of Auchierneside in sheriffdom of Perth, 4 February 1481/2. Witnesses: Walter Stewart of Morffy, Alexander S
2 CONC tewart, his son, Mr Richard Lawsoun, David Kirkpatrik of Rokalehede, William Cumyn, macer to the King, and Gilbert of Galbraithe. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f2%2f94&st=1&tc
2 CONC =y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1450&dt=1490&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane, reference GD112/2/94]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1489: Tack under the privy seal by King James IV to John Lord Drummond of the lands of Drummond last possessed by the deceased Alexander Stuart [Stewart] of Avendeal [Avandale] with the power of bailiery within the said 
2 CONC lands and of outputting and inputting tenants for the space of five years after his entry which was the date for payment of the maills as the said Alexander paid; dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fC%2f5%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=avandale&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1490&di=n Nationa Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/C/5/1/1]'''
2 CONT
