1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN STEWART OF CULBEG===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Stewart of Culbeg may be the son of William Stewart of Morphie, although evidence for this is presently wanting. [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofstewar00johnuoft#page/32/mode/1up The Heraldry of the Stewarts, etc., p
2 CONC . 32] He held one half of the lands of Culbeg and Culmoir in right of his wife Agnes Ker. He is very probably the father of Arthur Stewart of Culbeg, since Agnes Ker was Arthur's mother. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnis
2 CONC i02scot#page/476/mode/1up RMS: charter 2250 on pp. 476-77]'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 May 1495: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms Arthur Stewart's possession of one half of the lands of Culbeg and Culmoir in the sheriffdom of Stirling. These lands were previously resigned in Arthur's favour by
2 CONC  his mother Agnes Ker, who reserved her own liferent and that of her husband John Stewart. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/476/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal
2 CONC  of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 2250 on pp. 476-77]'''. 
