2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Auchinleck of that Ilk, in King James the Fourth's time, disponed his estate of Auchinleck to his daughter, Marion Auchinleck, then the wife of William Cunninghame of Craigends, upon which the estate recognosced and fell 
2 CONC in the king's hands, who, upon that, disponed it to David Boswell [the ancestor of the late Sir Alexander Boswell, Baronet, of Auchinleck], son of Balmano's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA12&lpg=PA12&dq=marion+auchinleck+genealogy&sig=1adb0JJA-_3kqu2fUxAXGlwFjxo&ei=FiG8U5SUGtKtyATQxIDYBA&id=7CQIAAAAQAAJ&ots=wdgiZbOhTq&output=text
2 CONT
2 CONT Marion AUCHINLECK (b. 1444, d. date unknown) Marion AUCHINLECK was born 1444, and died date unknown. She married John Auchinleck on 1464.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Includes NotesNotes for Marion AUCHINLECK: Co heir of Sir John Auchinleck. Married William Cuninghame 31st Aug 1496 Widow of Sir George Campbell of Loudon
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Marion AUCHINLECK and John Auchinleck: Marriage: 1464
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Marion AUCHINLECK and John Auchinleck are:
2 CONT
2 CONT     +Marion Campbell, b. 1455, Auchinleck, Cumnock Ayreshire Scotland, United Kingdom, d. date unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/a/r/Brenda-Marquez-Minnesota/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0997.html
