1 OCCU 4th Earl of Rothes
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes</strong> (died 1558) was a Scottish nobleman and diplomat. George became Earl of Rothes after his father's death at the Battle of Flodden. The title had previously been possessed by his u
2 CONC ncle, William Leslie, the 2nd Earl. On 1 April 1517 he and his wife redeemed by purchase family lands which James IV of Scotland had sold to Andrew Barton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Sheriff of Fife from 1529 to 1540 and a Lord of Session from 1541 and a Lord of the Articles from 1544.
2 CONT
2 CONT George accompanied James V of Scotland on his wedding trip to France in 1536. He was tried for the murder of Cardinal Beaton and acquitted. He was ambassador to Denmark in 1550, and died at Dieppe, France in 1558.
2 CONT
2 CONT George died while returning from the solemnization of the marriage of Mary, Queen of Scots. Several of the other Scottish commissioners died, Lord Fleming at Paris, and the Bishop of Orkney and Earl of Cassillis at Dieppe on the s
2 CONC ame night as George, 24 November 1558. It was rumoured that they were murdered because of their stance of the issue of giving the Crown-Matrimonial of Scotland to the Dauphin.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Crichton, daughter of William Crichton, 3rd Lord Crichton and Princess Margaret Stewart. Their eldest son was Norman Leslie who was involved in the murder of Cardinal Beaton and the siege of St Andrews Castle. 
2 CONC Norman pre-deceased his father, and the next Earl was Andrew Leslie, a son of George's third marriage to Agnes Somerville.
2 CONT
2 CONT George divorced Margaret Crichton and married Elizabeth Gray, daughter of Andrew, 3rd Lord Gray. She was the widow of John Lyon, 4th Lord Glamis. They had no children. George subsequently married Agnes Somerville, a daughter of Jo
2 CONC hn Somerville of Cambusnethan, who was the widow of John, 2nd Lord Fleming. After Agnes's death, in 1542, George was re-united with Margaret Crichton. He then married Isobel Lundy widow of the 7th Earl of Crawford, they had no chi
2 CONC ldren."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 2 October 2012, 00:02 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=George_Leslie,_4th_Earl_of_Rothes&oldid=5155466
2 CONC 01> [accessed 1 December 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of birth has also been (erroneously?) reported to be circa 1476 and 1496.  It has also been erroneously reported to be 1517.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of death has also been erroneously reported to be November 28, 1559.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10831.htm#i108303
2 CONT *George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes1
2 CONT *M, #108303, d. 28 November 1558
2 CONT *Last Edited=15 Feb 2010
2 CONT *     George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes was the son of William Leslie, 3rd Earl of Rothes and Margaret Balfour. He married, firstly, Margaret Crichton, daughter of Robert Crichton, 3rd Lord Crichton of Sanquhar and Margaret Stewar
2 CONC t, circa 1517.2 He and Margaret Crichton were divorced on 27 December 1520. He married, secondly, Elizabeth Gray, daughter of Andrew Gray, 2nd Lord Gray and Janet Keith, before June 1525.3 He married, fourthly, Isobel Lundy, daugh
2 CONC ter of unknown Lundy of that Ilk, before 10 April 1543.4 He died on 28 November 1558.4
2 CONT *     George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes gained the title of 4th Earl of Rothes.
2 CONT *Children of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes and Margaret Crichton
2 CONT **1.Helen Leslie+ d. 28 Oct 1594
2 CONT **2.Lady Agnes Leslie+5
2 CONT **3.Norman Leslie, Master of Rothes d. 1554
2 CONT **4.Lady Margaret Leslie1
2 CONT *Child of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes and Agnes Somerville
2 CONT **1.Andrew Leslie, 5th Earl of Rothes+ d. 1611
2 CONT *Children of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes
2 CONT **1.Lady Janet Leslie6 d. 17 Dec 1591
2 CONT **2.Robert Leslie6
2 CONT **3.Katherine Leslie+7
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 158. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 601. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 1642.
2 CONT *4.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 514.
2 CONT *5.[S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 202.
2 CONT *6.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *7.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1220.
2 CONT
