2 CONT From Wikipedia:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sheriff of Fife from 1529 to 1540 and a Lord of Session from 1541 and a Lord of the Articles from 1544, he was tried for the murder of Cardinal Beaton and acquitted. He was ambassador to Denmark in 1550, and died at Dieppe, France
2 CONC  in 1558.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=lyENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA355#v=onepage&q=&f=false Page 355
2 CONT
2 CONT “THE FAMILY OF LESLIE, EARLS OF LEVEN
2 CONT
2 CONT “The family of Leslie, Earls of Leven, is descended from the Drummuir, Kininvie, and New Leslie branches of the family of Leslie, Barons of Balquhain.
2 CONT
2 CONT “George Leslie, second son of George Leslie, first Laird of Drummuir, acquired the lands of Balgonie.  He was captain of the castle in Blair of Athole in the reign of King James VI., and was held in great esteem as a brave soldier
2 CONC .  He married Sybil Stewart of Ballathan, and had issue -“
2 CONT
2 CONT “   I. John, who entered the French service, and was a captain in the Life Guards of the King of France.  He returned to Scotland, and lived with his sisters at Newtown in Fife. “   II. George, who went to Germany, entered the arm
2 CONC y, and attained the rank of Colonel.  He was killed at a siege, leaving a daughter, who was married in London to the Laird of Newhall. “   III. David, who died a student at Douai.
2 CONT
2 CONT “George Leslie had also several daughters, with whom their brother John lived at Newtown in Fife, after he retired from the French service.  Besides these, he had also a natural son, Alexander Leslie, afterwards created Earl of Le
2 CONC ven.  After the death of Sybil Stewart, George Leslie married Alexander’s mother to legitimatise him, who was then a general."
2 CONT
