1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://records.ancestry.com/Michael_Balfour_records.ashx?pid=43603214
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I29875&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT Name 	Agnes Forrester  [1]  Suffix 	Lady Burleigh  Gender 	Female  Died 	Aft 1569 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Sir Duncan Forrester, 6th of Torwood, 1st of Garden,   d. Yes, date unknown  Mother 	Margaret, dau. of Provost of Stirling,   d. Yes, date unknown  Married 	Y  [1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 	David Balfour, 3rd of Burleigh,   d. Bef 1530  Married 	Y  [1, 2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children  	
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1. Michael Balfour, 4th of Burleigh,   d. 29 Nov 1577
2 CONT
2 CONT  	2. Margaret Balfour,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	3. Walter Balfour,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	4. Robert Balfour,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	5. dau. Balfour,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	6. Janet Balfour,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 	James Hoppringle, of Tynnes and later of Buckholm,   d. Bef 26 Aug 1561  Married 	Y  [1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children   	
2 CONT  	1. James Hoppringle, of Tynnes,   d. Bef 1606
2 CONT
2 CONT  	2. John Hoppringle (Pringill), of Buckholm,   d. 1633
2 CONT
2 CONT  	3. Malcolm Hoppringle, of Cortleferry,   d. 1618
2 CONT
2 CONT  	4. Alexander Hoppringle, in Little Catpair,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	5. David Hoppringle,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	6. Margaret Hoppringle,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT  	7. Elizabeth Hoppringle,   d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes  	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Agnes Forester, by her first husband, David Balfour of Burleigh of the royal household, had issue before 1531:-
2 CONT     1.Michael Balfour of Burleigh, who was Commentator of Melrose Abbey for a few years before 1569, when he was succeeded by his grandnephew James, 2nd son of Sir William Douglas of Lochleven (nephew of the famous Regent Murray).
2 CONT     2. 3. Walter and Robert.
2 CONT     4. Margaret, who married Sir Robert Douglas, great grand- father of Sir William of Lochleven Castle, who was served heir in 1555, the Keeper of Queen Mary.
2 CONT     Agnes Forester, by her second husband, James Hoppringill of Buckholm and Tynnes, had issue:-
2 CONT     1 James, of Tynnes.
2 CONT     2. John of Buckholm.
2 CONT     3. Malcolm, of Cortleferry.
2 CONT     4, Alexander, in Little Catpair and partner with Sir James Hoppringill.
2 CONT     5. David, apothecary burgess of Edinburgh.
2 CONT     6. Margaret, marr. Ninian Crichton of Achintagart in 1575.
2 CONT     7. Elizabeth, marr. 1st, Alexander Stewart in Tynnes, 2nd, William Scott of Whithaugh (R. D.).
2 CONT     James 2 died before 26th August 1561. His spouse was alive in 1569.
2 CONT     [ http://salhun.100webcustomers.com/TheBook.htm ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  	
2 CONT
2 CONT     [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Forrester02.
2 CONT
