1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Michael Balfour:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p6725.htm#i67242
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Balfour, 4th of Burleigh [1],[2]
2 CONT *M, #67242, 
2 CONT *d. 29 November 1577
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Balfour, 4th of Burleigh was the son of David Balfour and Agnes Forester.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Christina Bethune, daughter of Sir John Bethune, 2nd of Creich and Janet Hay, before 27 April 1545.[3],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 29 November 1577.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Burleigh, Kinross-shire, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Michael Balfour, 4th of Burleigh and Christina Bethune
2 CONT *1. Margaret Balfour+[1] d. 1584
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 379. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S2226] Lawless Bethune, "re: Bethune Family," e-mail message to www.thepeerage.com, 27 March 2007. Hereinafter cited as "re: Bethune Family."
2 CONT *3. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 174. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetag
2 CONC e, 106th edition.
