1 NAME Isobel Oliphant
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isobel Oliphant, daughter of Walter Oliphant of Newton of Forgandenny. Isobel was a grand-daughter to Thomas Oliphant of Dron, brother of Laurence 1st Lord Oliphant, sons of Sir John of Aberdalgie who died at Arbro
2 CONC ath at 1446 and Margaret Ogilvie daughter of Patrick Ogilvie of Auchterhouse and Christian Keith his spouse who was a daughter of a cadet of the Keith family, Marischal of Scotland.
2 CONT Text in pdf below linked, written by Professor Richard Ogilvie:
2 CONT (See page 6 in URI:)
2 CONT https://atrium.lib.uoguelph.ca/xmlui/handle/10214/26962
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == ISOBEL OLIPHANT (aka ISABEL OLIPHANT) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Isobelle Oliphant, here treated, seems unlikely to be the same person as  https://www.geni.com/people/Isabel-Oliphant/6000000002116158763?through=6000000010462807267 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isobelle Oliphant, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/James-Ogilvy-of-Balgally-and-Inchmartin/6000000009523656204?through=6000000010515072326 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/830/mode/1up 
2 CONC RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3815]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1512-13: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given that lands and barony of Inchmartine to James Ogilvy of Inchmartine. He also confirms that he has given the western part of the land of P
2 CONC etmedle in the barony of Inchmartine to James and his wife, Isobelle Oliphant, which lands were in the king's hands, to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/830/mod
2 CONC e/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3815]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 October 1513: Transumpt of Charter under Great Seal, dated 24 February, 1512/1513, in favour of James Ogilvy of Inchmarten of lands of barony of Inchmarten, and to said James and Isobel Oliphant, his spouse, and survivor, of
2 CONC  lands of Easter Petmedle. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1029&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isobel+oliphant&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of
2 CONC  the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1029]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Re
2 CONC gister House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
