1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == PATRICK OGILVY OF INCHMARTINE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartine, here treated, is the son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Ogilvy-of-Balgally-and-Inchmartin/6000000009523656204?through=6000000010515081210 They had a charter for the lands of Balgall
2 CONC e and Petmydill on 14 January 1509. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1030&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1560&di=n NRS: GD26/3/1030]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartine married https://www.geni.com/people/Mariota-Stewart/6000000011088831828?through=6000000010515081210 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/741/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter numb
2 CONC er 3458]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartine married https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Kynnaird/6000000002116079549?through=6000000010515081210 They had a charter for one half of the lands of Balgalle, in the barony of Inchture and sherif
2 CONC fdom of Perth. on 10 March 1538. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/432/mode/1up RMS 1513-1546: charter number 1933]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 January 1509: Charter by which James Ogilvy of Inchmartine confirms that he has given part of the lands of Balgavy, extending to a twenty merk land, and the ten merk lands of Petmydill, both in the barony of Inchmartine, to 
2 CONC his son Patrick Ogilvy and his wife, Mariote Steuart, daughter of Thome, Lord of Innermethe. His charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 6 May 1510. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/741/mo
2 CONC de/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 3458]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 October 1513: Transumpt of Charter under Great Seal, dated 24 February, 1512/1513, in favour of James Ogilvy of Inchmarten of lands of barony of Inchmarten, and to said James and Isobel Oliphant, his spouse, and survivor, of
2 CONC  lands of Easter Petmedle. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1029&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isobel+oliphant&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of
2 CONC  the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1029]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1513: Libri Responsionem ImVcXIII. Perth. Vicecomes respondebit pro 40 li. de relevio terrarum baronie de Inchemertyne cum piscatura nuncupata le Kingis Inche super aquam de Taya, regi debito per sasinam datam Patricio Ogilvy d
2 CONC e eisdem die etc. [7 Novemb a r.l.] predictis. [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir14grea/page/524/mode/1up RSRS 1513-1523: 524]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1518: Instrument of sasine following on no. GD132/15. Witnesses: William Drummond in the Kirktoun of Abirnyt [Abernyte]; Peter Hay, son and heir apparent of Edmund Haye of Meginche [Megginch]; Andrew Ogilvy [Ogilvie] of 
2 CONC Duntrown; Andrew Ogilvy, brother german of Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmertyne [Inchmartine]; John Kynnard [Kinnaird]; John Terloicht; John Dogles [Douglas], and Gilbert Kynman [Kinman]. Notary: David Clerk [Clark], priest of the dioces
2 CONC e of St. Andrews. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD132%2f16&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=andrew+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Roberts
2 CONC on Family of Lude, Perthshire, reference GD132/16]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 October 1519: Instrument of Sasine in favour of Patrick Ogilvy, son and heir of deceased James Ogilvy of Inchmartyne, of lands of the West side of Petmyddyll, following on precept, dated 5 October, 1519, by John Steirling of
2 CONC  the Keir, kt., sheriff of Perth, which followed on Chancery precept. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1030&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt
2 CONC =1560&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1030]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 March 1538: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he has given one half of the lands of Balgalle, in the barony of Inchture and sheriffdom of Perth, to Patrick Ogilvie of Inchmartine and his wife Elizabeth K
2 CONC ynard. This land was to be held by Patrick and Elizabeth in conjunct fee and liferent, and thereafter by Patrick's heirs and assignees. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/432/mode/1up RMS 1513-1546: charter n
2 CONC umber 1933]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 March 1553-54: Precept of sasine in favour of Christian Ogilvy, daughter of Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmertine, of the lands of Unthank, Edieland, Rideland, Nine Rigs, Eleven Rigs, Fourteen Rigs and Thrislie Howme and mills of Kn
2 CONC ap. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f28%2f49&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1560&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family
2 CONC , Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/28/49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1555: Instrument of sasine in favour of William Ogilvy [Ogilvie] of the lands and barony of Lude, as heir to his father, deceased Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartyne [Inchmartine], following on precept from chancery, 27 April 
2 CONC 1555, and precept, 20 May 1555, by Patrick, Lord Ruthven, sheriff of Perth, to Alexander Borthuik [Borthwick] and Andrew Malcum [Malcolm], mairs of the said sheriffdom, said Alexander Borthuik giving sasine. Witnesses: John Tarloc
2 CONC hsoun [Tarlachson] younger; Patrick Raid [Reid]; William McRobbe [McRobb]; John McCarroquhair; Donald Johnnesoun [Johnson], and Donald McCarroquhair. Notary: Alan Justice, clerk of the diocese of St. Andrews; also signed by Robert
2 CONC  Rollok, clerk of the sheriff court of Perth. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD132%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1560&di=n National Records o
2 CONC f Scotland, Papers of the Robertson Family of Lude, Perthshire, reference GD132/17]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 April 1579: Kirk of Kynnoull Contract between Alexander Blair of Balthiok and Andro Blair, his son, on the one part, and John Ogilvy in Ballinscho, son of deceased Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartene, on the other part, for sale o
2 CONC f quarter part of the lands of Durdie Inglis alias Nethir Durdie, regality of Scone. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD190%2f3%2f58&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&r
2 CONC o=s&df=1550&dt=1560&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Smythe Family of Methven, Perthshire, reference GD190/3/58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccariir14grea/page/n8/mode/1up Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland. Vol. XIV. 1513-1522. Edited by A. J. G. Mackay, MA. Oxon., LL.D. Edin., Honorary Fellow of
2 CONC  King's College, London; Sheriff of Perth and Kinross. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1893), 836 pp. including index and corrigenda]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General 
2 CONC Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitl
2 CONC and Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/oo/ogilvy02.php Stirnet: Ogilvy 02]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/32/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/32/mode/1up Biographical Summary from the Scots Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick  Ogilvy had a charter from his father 14 January 1509, to himself and his wife, of the western part of  his lands of Balgally and others in the barony of Inchmartine. On 4 November 1513 Patrick was retoured heir to  his
2 CONC  father. Three days afterwards he received a Crown sasine of the barony of Inchmertyne, with the fishings of King's Insche on the water of Tay. On 5 September 1521 he acquired from Andrew Kynnaird of that Ilk the lower fourth part
2 CONC  of the lands of Kynnaird. On 10 March 1538-39 he had a Crown grant of one half of the lands of Ballgalle in the barony of Inchture to himself and his wife Elizabeth Kynnaird. On 29 April 1548 he acquired  from Patrick Kynnaird of
2 CONC  that Ilk the dominical lands of Drummye in the barony of Ballegarno and shire of  Perth.  He married, first, Mariota Stewart, daughter of Thomas, Lord Innermeath, and secondly, Elizabeth, daughter of  Andrew Kynnaird of that Ilk 
2 CONC and Inchture. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/32/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/274:107?page=root;print=1;size=100;view=text Biographical Summary] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''"Sir PATRICK OGILVIE of Inchmar∣tin, who succeeded him, and got a charter from King James V. of the lands of Balgillo, and many others, anno 1538.He got also a charter from queen Mary, terrarum dominicalium de Drimmy, etc. anno
2 CONC  1548.He married, 1st, Marian Stewart, daughter of Thomas lord Innermeath, by whom he had a son, William, his heir apparent. He married, 2dly, Janet, daughter of Pa∣trick, fourth lord Gray, by whom he had two daughters.1. Margaret
2 CONC , married to Patrick Hay of Megginch,Ibidem. ancestor of the earl of Kinnoul. 2. Janet, married to John Kinnaird of that ilk."'''
