2 CONT '''13 July 1623: Contract between Henry Rattrey as heir of progress of the deceased Andrew Rattrey of Westhall, his great grandfather, and of the deceased Andrew Rattray of Balnacaird, his grandfather, on the one part, and William
2 CONC  Stewart of Kinnaird and John Stewart, his eldest lawful son and apparent heir, on the other whereby for 300 merks Henry Rattrey dispones to the Stewarts that sixth part of the lands of Kinnaird lying in Athole on the west side of
2 CONC  the Water of Tay in the barony of Polmeis Cuningham by annexation and in the shire of Perth which sometime belonged to the deceased James Cuningham of Polmeis and his predecessors; also the said Henry's part of the lands of Over 
2 CONC Kynnarde lying within the marches of Athole and which formerly belonged to the deceased Roger Wood of Craig. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD38%2f1%2f125&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
