2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Kennedy, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000002116145618 On 16 April 1478, in completion of the marriage contract they had entered into, 
2 CONC her father-in-law gave Elizabeth and her husband the twenty pound lands of Kinbauloch, together with the lands of Haltoun, both in the barony of Kinbauloch and Sheriffdom of Perth. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02sc
2 CONC ot/page/294/mode/1up RMS: 1424-1513: 1427]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 April 1478: Charter by which SILVESTRI RETTRAY DE EODEM confirms that he has given the twenty pound lands of Kinbauloch and the lands of Haltoun, both in the barony of Kinbauloch and Sheriffdom of Perth, to his son and appar
2 CONC ent heir JOHANNI RETTRAY and his wife ELIZABETH KENNEDY, as agreed in their marriage contract. The lands in question were to be held by them in conjunct fee and liferent, and thereafter by the lawful heirs, whom failing by the nea
2 CONC rest lawful heirs of Silvestri Rettrat de eodem. A charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland was issued to Johanni and Elizabeth on 28 May 1479. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/294/mode/1up 
2 CONC RMS: 1424-1513: 1427]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 July 1479: Instrument of sasine following on precept, 20 April 1478, by Silvester Rattray of that ilk, in favour of John Rattray, his eldest son, and Elizabeth Kennedy, his spouse, of lands of Kinballach in barony thereof, s
2 CONC heriffdom of Perth, 23 July 1479. Notary: Partick Barry, clerk, St Andrews diocese. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f225&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=
2 CONC s&df=&dt=1540&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Rattray Family of Craighall, Perthshire, reference GD385/225]'''
2 CONT
