2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT i. John, a military officer, who m. Margaret Abercrombie, but d. in Holland before his father, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 2
2 CONT  By John Burke, p. 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT After the decease of Sir John, a calamitous and almost ruinous contest arose between his younger sons and their brother-in-law, the Earl of Athol. Tradition affirms that the Earl, having married Sir John's only daughter, deemed hi
2 CONC mself entitled to a portion, at least, of the Rattray estate, and being a person of great power and authority, came, with a considerable body of men, took possession of the castle of Rattray, and carried off the family writs; whil
2 CONC e Patrick Rattray, the second son, totally unable to resist so potent a nobleman, retired to the castle of Craighall, winch he gallantly defended, and succeeded in holding, together with the lands of Craighall and Klnballoch; the 
2 CONC Athol family continuing to possess the greater part of the lands of Rattray. until they were evicted from them by an appraising, at the instance of Sir Robert Crichton, of Clunie, about the beginning of the seventeenth century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT .....
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvester Rattray, who endeavoured to serve himself heir to his father and brothers at Perth, in which county his lands lay, but found it impossible, because (as the writ bears) the Earl of Athol and his friends are 
2 CONT
2 CONT " ''magnae potestatis et fortitudinis''" [Google translation: "of a great power, and of fortitude"] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...in that town. Rattray applied, in consequence, to King James V., and obtained from his majesty a commission under the great seal to have service done at Dundee. In this commission it is narrated that Patrick, his brother, had b
2 CONC een "''postpositus et impeditus''" for the space of twelve years by the said earl, from getting himself served in the lands that fell to him by the death of his father and brother John ; and that, 
2 CONT
2 CONT " ''post lites magnasque expensas per dictum Patricium in preefata materia, praefatus comes misit Walterum Leslie, Johannem Stewart, alias John of Lorn, Thomas Laing, David Stewart, suos servitores, et eorum complices, et dictum P
2 CONC atricium in sua capella ipsius loci de Kynballoch interficere causavit: et idem Silvester informatur, quod dictus comes, et sui complices, sibi similiter facere intendunt, si sua brevia de hujusmodi terris prosequi volet''." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Google Translation:  "the expenses of a large and powerful after the lawsuits by the said Patrick, in the matter of preefata began by saying that he sent the Earl Walter Leslie, John Stewart, John of Lorn other, Thomas Laing, Davi
2 CONC d Stewart, the servants of his, and of them, accomplices, and it was said Patrick, in his own chapel by the position of the Kynballoch caused to kill : Sylvester and the same is formed, that the said earl, and his own, accomplices
2 CONC , they intend to do to him in like manner, if his writs, of the like to pursue the lands he shall delight"
2 CONT
2 CONT This extraordinary commission Is dated at Edinburgh, 17 Oct. 1533, to which the great seal is appended, and, in consequence, Silvester Rattray was served heir to his father, Sir John, and to his brothers, John and Patrick, in the 
2 CONC barony of Craighall and Kynballoch, and infeft therein at Dundee, in 1534. He ''m''. Marjory, dau. of Andrew, third Lord Gray, (relict of Kennenmouth, of that ilk.) and had, with a dau., Elizabeth, ''m''. to John Blair, of Ardblai
2 CONC r, a son and successor, David Rattray...
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 2, By John Burke, p. 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------- John Rattray *1479  Married Margaret Abercrombie. Died soldiering in Holland, leaving 2 daughters who were forcibly surrendered to the Earl of Atholl for upbringing and marriage into his family.
2 CONT *Dawn Stapylton-Adkins. ''James Rattray & His Descendants in South Africa'' 1822-1992, self-published, Cape Town, 1992
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Using Neil's kindly supplied links: https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f225&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=bredwellis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n
2 CONT
2 CONT GB
2 CONT Repository code	234
2 CONT Repository	National Records of Scotland
2 CONT Reference	GD385/225
2 CONT Title	Miscellaneous writs
2 CONT Dates	1253-1572
2 CONT Access status	Open
2 CONT Location	Off site
2 CONT Description	Including:
2 CONT
2 CONT Copy agreement between abbot and convent of Aberbrothoc on one part, and Thomas Rattrie, kt., on the other, 1253. Taken from cartulary of Arbroath abbey in the Signet Library, Edinburgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT ..
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Instrument of sasine following on precept, 20 April 1478, by Silvester Rattray of that ilk, in favour of John Rattray, his eldest son, and Elizabeth Kennedy, his spouse, of lands of Kinballach in barony thereof, sheriffdom of P
2 CONC erth, 23 July 1479. Notary: Partick Barry, clerk, St Andrews diocese.''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/Silvester-Rattray-10th-of-that-Ilk/6000000011088749879?through=6000000003828323124; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-1
2 CONC 1th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000002116145618; https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Kennedy/6000000002116145618?through=6000000003828323124
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charter by John Rattray of that ilk, kt., to John Rattray, his son and apparent heir, and Margaret Abbircromme, his spouse, of lands of Bredwellis, Ottyrburne and Clayhillis and others in barony of Rattray, sheriffdom of Perth,
2 CONC  15 Jan. 1506/7. Seal damaged on tag. With precept and sasine following.''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000002116145618; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-you
2 CONC nger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090274612?through=6000000003828323124; https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Abercrombie/6000000011090514232?through=6000000011090274612
2 CONT
2 CONT ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Discharge by Donald Rollok of Polcak, son of deceased Robert Rollok in Polcak, to David Rattrie of Craighall, of 500 merks Scots, as assithment and amends for murder of said Robert and David Donald in the Grainge, and of 45 merks 
2 CONC from William Rattray, brother of said David, 8 Nov. 1572.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Letters by James, abbot of Scone, and convent thereof, appointing John Rattray of that ilk, kt., and Andrew Abbircromme of Innerpeffery, brother of said James, as bailies of regality of Scone, 18 May 1506. HMC 4th report p.536.
2 CONC ''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-younger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090274612?through=6000000011090514232; https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Abercrombie-of-Innerpeffray/6000000030380488216?through=6000000011090514232
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Copy special retour in favour of Silvester Rattray as heir of deceased John Rattray, kt., his father, at Dundee, 10 Nov. 1533.''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=60000000
2 CONC 11090274612; https://www.geni.com/people/Silvester-Rattray-of-Craighall-13th-Laird/6000000004109726768?through=6000000003828323124
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Instrument narrating that Michael Tullo of Hilcarny, sheriff of Perth in that part, compeared in tolbooth of Dundee at instance of procurator for Silvester Rattray, and produced a commission under quarter seal for service in fa
2 CONC vour of said Silvester as heir of deceased John Rattray, his father, and deceased John Rattray, his brother, which commission was read aloud and said procurator required the necessary breives for expeding the service, 22 Oct. 1533
2 CONC . HMC 4th report p.536.''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/Silvester-Rattray-of-Craighall-13th-Laird/6000000004109726768?through=6000000003828323124; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-younger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090274612?
2 CONC through=6000000004109726768; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000011090274612
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Precept of clare constat by Grizel Rattray of that ilk, wife of John, earl of Athol, in favour of Silvester Rattray as heir of deceased John Rattray, his brother, of lands of Bredwellis, Ottirburn and others in barony of Rattra
2 CONC y, sheriffdom of Perth, 20 Dec. 1533. HMC 4th report p.536.''' cf https://www.geni.com/people/Grizel-Rattray/6000000003828031793?through=6000000003828323124; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart-3rd-Earl-of-Atholl/600000000382
2 CONC 8031786?through=6000000003828031793; https://www.geni.com/people/Silvester-Rattray-of-Craighall-13th-Laird/6000000004109726768?through=6000000003828323124; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-younger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090
2 CONC 274612?through=6000000004109726768; https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000011090274612
