1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SILVESTER RATTRAY OF CRAIGHALL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Silvester Rattray of Craighall, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000004109726768 and the next younger brother of https://www.geni.com/people/J
2 CONC ohn-Rattray-younger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090274612?through=6000000004109726768 from whom he inherited the lands of Bredwellis in the barony of Rattray. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referenc
2 CONC e=GD385%2f225&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craighall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1513&di=n NRS: GD385/225]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Concerning the Lands of Bredwellis ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Silvester Rattray of Craighall, here treated, inherited the lands of Bredwellis, and others, from his elder brother https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-younger-of-that-Ilk/6000000011090274612?through=6000000004109726768 Th
2 CONC ese lands, which were an integral part of the barony of Rattray in the Sheriffdom of Perth, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f225&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s
2 CONC &df=&dt=1513&di=n NRS: GD385/225] were given to John by his father https://www.geni.com/people/John-Rattray-11th-of-that-Ilk/6000000003828323124?through=6000000004109726768 when John married https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Ab
2 CONC ercrombie/6000000011090514232 The charter in favour of John and Margaret, which is dated 15 January 1506-07, was evidently a feu charter, because the superiority of the lands remained with his father. It follows, therefore, that S
2 CONC ilvester Rattray of Craighall, here treated, held Bredwellis as the feudal tenant of the barony of Rattray. This is confirmed by the fact it was https://www.geni.com/people/Grizel-Rattray/6000000003828031793 , one of the heirs por
2 CONC tioners of the Barony of Rattray, who issued the precept of clare constat for the lands Bredwellis to Silvester Rattray on 20 December 1533. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f22
2 CONC 5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1513&di=n NRS: GD385/225]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Silvester Rattray of Craighall, here treated. He was alive on 20 December 1533, the date upon which he had a charter of confirmation (otherwise known as a precept of clare c
2 CONC onstat) for the lands of Bredwellis in the barony of Rattray, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f225&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1513&di=n NRS: GD385/2
2 CONC 25] but he died before 26 February 1533-34, the date upon which his son https://www.geni.com/people/David-Rattray-of-Craighall-14th-Laird/6000000004109768401?through=6000000004109726768 had a charter confirmation his possession of
2 CONC  the lands of Bredwellis. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f226&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craighall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1513&di=n NRS: GD385/226]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
