2 CONC logical Society of Utah, 1996), FHL film 1553977-1553985..
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Rattray was Knighted by King James IV in 1488. Appointed Bailie of Regality at Scone 1506. Killed at the Battle of Flodden in 1513. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.John Rattray *1479 Married Margaret Abercrombie. Died soldiering in Holland, leaving 2 daughters who were forcibly surrendered to the Earl of Atholl for upbringing and marriage into his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT >2.Grizel Rattray married John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Atholl, who murdered Patrick for the Rattray lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT >3.Patrick Rattray, 12th Laird of Kinballoch. Driven from Rattray Castle, he settled at KInballoch and began building Craighall. In 1553 he was murdered in his own chapel by his brother-in-law , the 3rd Earl of Atholl, who coveted
2 CONC  Rattray lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT >4.'''Sylvester Rattray of Craighall. 13th Laird. In spite of hindrances from the Atholls, he eventually was served heir to his father and brother to the barony of Craighall and Kinballoch. Married Marjorie d/o 3rd Lord Gray. Died
2 CONC  1554.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT *Dawn Stapylton-Adkins. James Rattray & His Descendants in South Africa 1822-1992, self-published, Cape Town, 1992
2 CONT
