1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER IRVINE OF DRUM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://clanirwin.org/index.php '''Clan Irwin Association'''] A Not For Profit Corporation
2 CONT
2 CONT Extract from "Short account of the family of Irvine of Drum in the county of Aberdeen", 1893, Page 7 (http://archive.org/details/shortaccountoffa00wimb)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, the 8th laird, grandson of the preceding, married Lady Elizabeth Keith, 2nd daughter of William, 4th Earl Marischal, and his wife Margaret, daughter and co-heiress of Sir William Keith of Inverugie, by whom he had five 
2 CONC sons and four daughters, viz.: 1. Alexander, younger of Drum. 2. Robert, of Fornett and Moncoffer, extinct. 3. James, of Brucklavv, predecessor of Saphock, extinct. 4. William, of Beltie, extinct. 5. John, of Artamford, whose desc
2 CONC endant, Irvine of Crimond, succeeded to Drum in 1737.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters— 1. married to Hay of Ury, the eldest cadet (failing heirs male of the 6th Earl), in 1541, of the Errol family. 2. married to Keith of Inverugie (or perhaps of Ludquhairn or of Ravenscraig). 3. Elizabeth, married to Jame
2 CONC s Ogilvy of Boyne. 4- Margaret,' married to Gilbert Menzies of Pitfodels.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was in this laird's favour, but before he succeeded to the estate, that a Charter - was granted, under the Great Seal of Scotland, on the resignation of his grandfather in favour of Alexander Irvine, grandson and heir apparent 
2 CONC of Alexander Irvine of Drum, and the heirs male of his body, to the nearest and lawful heirs male and assignees whatsomever, of the lands and barony of Drum, with the lands and baronies thereto annexed, Lonmay, Learney, Auchindoir
2 CONC , and particularly the lands of Tarland and Coul, dated at Edinburgh the of February in the I2th year of the Queen's reign (1554).
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
2 CONT *'''Alexander Irvine, 8th Laird of Drum1
2 CONT *'''M, #2753, d. 1603
2 CONT *Father	Alexander Irvine d. 9 Sep 1547
2 CONT *Mother	Elizabeth Ogilvy
2 CONT *'''     Alexander Irvine, 8th Laird of Drum married Elizabeth Keith''', daughter of William Keith, 4th Earl Marischal and Margaret Keith, '''in 1552. Alexander Irvine, 8th Laird of Drum died in 1603.
2 CONT *'''Family     Elizabeth Keith
2 CONT *'''Children	
2 CONT **Alexander Irvine, 9th Laird Drum+ d. 1629
2 CONT **Mary Irvine
2 CONT **Elizabeth Irvine
2 CONT **Janet Irvine
2 CONT **Margaret Irvine
2 CONT **Robert Irvine
2 CONT **James Irvine
2 CONT **William Irvine
2 CONT **John Irvine d. b 2 Mar 1636
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S145] Unknown author, Burke's Commoners, Vol. II, p. 681-682.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p92.htm#i2753 ______________________
2 CONT *'''Alexander Irvine, 8th of Drum1
2 CONT *'''M, #447447, d. 1603
2 CONT *Last Edited=2 Dec 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT *'''     Alexander Irvine, 8th of Drum was the son''' of Alexander Irvine of Lonmay and Elizabeth Ogilvy.1,2 '''He married Lady Elizabeth Keith''', daughter of George Keith, 4th Earl Marischal, '''in 1552.1 He died in 1603.1
2 CONT *'''      On 12 February 1553/54 he had charter under the Great Seal 12 of lands and barony of Drum, Learney and Auchindoch, to himself and the heirs-male of his body.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Alexander Irvine, 8th of Drum and Lady Elizabeth Keith
2 CONT **Alexander Irvine, 9th of Drum+1 d. c 1630
2 CONT **Robert Irvine, 1st of Moncoffer2
2 CONT **James Irvine+2
2 CONT **William Irvine2
2 CONT **John Irvine, 1st of Artamford+2 d. b 2 Mar 1636
2 CONT **unknown daughter Irvine+2
2 CONT **Elizabeth Irvine2
2 CONT **Margaret Irvine2
