1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == CRISTINA BARCLAY (aka CRISTINAM BARCLAY) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Cristina Barclay, here treated, was one of the mistresses of https://www.geni.com/people/James-V-King-of-Scots/6000000003233882803?through=6000000006727855355 [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm Medieval Lands] She i
2 CONC s noticed as the mother of his bastard son https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stewart-tertius/6000000010491982322?through=6000000006727855355 in a charter dated 28 October 1534, which was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland. [h
2 CONC ttps://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/315/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1425] and again on 31 August 1536, in a second charter that was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland. [https://archive.org/details/
2 CONC registrummagnisi03scot/page/360/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1620]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 October 1534: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Douglas to his eldest bastard son James Stewart. The king also gave him the la
2 CONC nds and barony of Dunsire, Craufurdmure and Bothwell, in the sheriffdom of Lanark; the lands and barony of Jedburgh Forrest in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh; the lands and barony of Bonkill in the sheriffdom of Berwick; the lands of 
2 CONC Temptalloune in the Constabulary of Haddington and sheriffdom of Edinburgh; and the superiority of the lands and lordship of Keremure in the sheriffdom of Forfar. These lands and baronies were to be held by James Stewart and his l
2 CONC awful male heirs; who failing by his brother James Stewart, the king's bastard son by Margaret Erskine and his lawful male heirs; whom failing by his brother James Stewart, the king's bastard son by Cristina Barclay, and his lawfu
2 CONC l male heirs; whom failing by his brother Robert Stewart, another of the king's bastard sons. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/315/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1425]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 August 1536: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that James Stewart, his bastard son by Elizabeth Schaw, has given the lands of Temptalloun, in the Constabulary of Haddin
2 CONC gton and sheriffdom of Edinburgh, and the lands and barony of Bonkill and Prestoun, in the sheriffdom of Berwick, to James Stewart, the king's bastard son by Margaret Erskine. These lands, which the king incorporated as the free b
2 CONC arony of Temptalloun, were to be held by the younger James Stewart and his lawful male heirs; whom failing by his brother Robert Stewart, the king's bastard son by Eufam Elphinstoun, and his lawful male heirs; whom failing by his 
2 CONC brother James Stewart, the king's bastard son by Cristinam Barclay, and his lawful male heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/360/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter number 1620]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitlan
2 CONC d Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
