1 OCCU Baronet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: Johnston, Alexander, Jr., ''Genealogical account of the family of Johnston of that ilk, formerly of Caskieben, in the Shire of Aberdeen, and of its principal branches.''  Edinburgh, 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Johnston - who married Clara, daughter of Barclay of Gartley, in Aberdeenshire and had 6th September 1521, a charter under the Great Seal from King James V "Jacobo Johnestoun de eodem, et Clarae Barclay ejus sponsae terrarum
2 CONC  dominicalium de Johnestoun, Inglistoune, etc, jacen. in baronia de Johnstoun, in vicecomitatu de Aberdeen." (Translation from Latin to English = James Johnestoun of the same, and Clare Barclay his spouse the lands of Johnestoun, 
2 CONC Inglistoune, etc., lying down. in the barony of Johnstoun in turn, in the county of Aberdeen) By this lady James had three sons and four daughters: 1) William the younger, predeceased his father leaving issue (2 Gilbert of Standin
2 CONC gstone married Margaret, daughter of William Forbes 3) George, bailie of Aberdeen married Katherine, duaghter of Thomas Menzies 4 Agnes 5) Isabel 6 Bessy 7)Janet.
2 CONT
2 CONT James died in the beginning of the year 1548, partly, it is believed, of greif, occasioned by the death of his son, and was succeeded by his grandson, George.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married September 6, 1521. Died year 1548, believed to have died of grief occasioned by death of his son William, succeeded by grandson.
2 CONT --------------------
