1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir James Foulis (died 1549), was a Scottish judge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Foulis was the son and heir of James de Foulis of Edinburgh (a skinner) and his wife Margaret, who was herself herself the daughter of Sir James Henderson of Fordell, Fifeshire, Lord Advocate to James IV of Scotland. In 1519 he ac
2 CONC quired from the Master of Glencairn the lands of Colinton. Thereafter his family would incorporate Colinton into their names.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Foulis_%28judge%29
