1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ELIZABETH GORDON ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Gordon, here treated, is the bastard daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Adam-Gordon-Dean-of-Caithness/6000000002188040017?through=6000000004149018496. Her paternal grandfather was https://www.geni.com/people/Alex
2 CONC ander-Gordon-1st-Earl-of-Huntly/6000000001644776831?through=6000000002188040017. The name of her mother has not been identified. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/22/mode/1up T
2 CONC he Scots Peerage IV: 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Elizabeth Gordon, here treated. She survived her second husband, who was executed at Aberdeen on 31 October 1562, and was still alive in 1566. [https://archive.org/details/s
2 CONC cotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/22/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Gordon, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Ogilvy-Laird-of-Findlater/6000000008630797292?through=6000000004149018496. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04
2 CONC pauluoft/page/22/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Gordon, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Gordon-of-Findlater/6000000221572023950?through=6000000004149018496 before 31 December 1535. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scots
2 CONC peeragefoun04pauluoft/page/22/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 April 1545: Charter by which Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk, with the consent of his wife Elizabeth Gordoun, confirms that he has given certain lands in the sheriffdom of Banff to Master Georgio Gordoun, constable of Ruthven i
2 CONC n Badenoch, and his wife Jonete Ros. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 10 December 1552. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/163/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 731]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 February 1546: Charter by which Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk and Findlater confirms that he has given certain lands in the sheriffdom of Aberdeen to John Ogilvy, now John Gordoun, third son of George Ogilvy, Earl of Gordon a
2 CONC nd Badenoch. Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk reserved his own liferent and that of his wife Elizabeth Gordoun. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 17 February 1546-47. [https://archive.org/details/registrum
2 CONC magnisi04scot/page/17/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 66]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 August 1547: Charter by which Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk confirms that he has given certain land in the sheriffdom of Banff to John Ogilvy, third son of George Ogilvy, Earl of Gordon. Alexander Ogilvy of that Ilk reserved 
2 CONC his own liferent and that of his wife Elizabeth Gordoun. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 24 August 1548. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/59/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter numb
2 CONC er 246]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility o
2 CONC f that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume IV. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1907), 597 pp.]'''
