1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Seen as the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Ogilvy-of-Findlater/6000000002116086269 Which looks unlikely.  William Mackintosh died 1550, and this Margaret was married to James Gordon of Lesmoir by 2 Ja
2 CONC nuary 1546.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Seen as daughter of Alexander Ogilvie of the Ilk, but perhaps his sister, - the daughter of James Ogilvy [Ogilvie], younger of Findlater, and his wife Agnes Gordon.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Other names for Margaret were OGILVIE, Margaret of Findlater 3 and OGILVY, Margaret Lady Gartly.
2 CONT
2 CONT She Married 1) Walter Barclay, 18th of Gartley 2) James Gordon, of Lesmoir, 1st of Crichie, his 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Walter Barclay, 18th of Gartley
2 CONT
2 CONT #BARCLAY, Margaret of Gartly+
2 CONT #BARCLAY, Walter of Bathnagoak+
2 CONT #BARCLAY, George 19th and last Laird of Gartly, Sir+
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The forsaid James Gordon first Laird of Lesmoir married two Ladies, his first was a daughter of Patrick Stuart of Lethers, Lady Eden, with whom he begat Six Sons and three daughters, viz, his eldest Son George Gordon 2d Laird of L
2 CONC esmoir, his second Son James Gordon of Crichie, 3 d Son Alexander Gordon of Birkenburn, fourth son Mr William Gordon of Terpersie, fifth son Patrick Gordon of Oxhill, and the Sixth Son John Gordon of Licheston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The said James married to his second Lady, the Laird of Findlater’s daughter Ogilvy, Lady Gartlie, whom he begat two Sons, 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Hary Gordon of Dilespro or Savach, and 
2 CONT *Thomas Gordon of Drumbuilg.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES ON A PEDIGREE OF THE GORDONS OF TERPERSIE [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9559/95590708.23.pdf PDF] page 17 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Gordons of Terpersie were descended from Jock of Scurdargue by his spouse, Elizabeth Maitland : Jock lived from say 1380-1460: their 2nd son, William in TiUytarmont, who lived say 1424-1484, married a sister of Sir John Ruthe
2 CONC rford : their eldest son was George in Tillytarmont, who lived say 1450-1500, married Isobel, daughter of Beroald limes of Meilliers : and their 2nd son was James Gordon, first of Lesmoir, who lived say 1475-1557 I he married, 1st
2 CONC , Margaret, daughter of Patrick Stewart of Laithers, relict of Meldrum of Eden : 2ndly, about 1546, Margaret, daughter of Alexander Ogilvy of Deskford, Finlater and Ogilvy, relict of Barclay of Gartly.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps32/ps32_409.html
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) The said James Gordon of Lesmoir, after the decease of Margaret Stuart, married Margaret Ogilbie, Lady Gartly, daughter of Sir Alexander Ogilvie of Findlater, knight, who bore him sundrie sons, of whom two came to position.
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. Thomas the eldest. “His father gave to him the lands of Seggieden, and he married a gentlewoman called _____ _____, who bare him sundrie sons and daughters. This Thomas was slain with his two sons, James and William, very brav
2 CONC e gentlemen, under the Earl of Huntly’s banner, on a field called Auchinachie, against George, Earle of Argyle.” From him, according to Douglas, the Gordons of Buthlaw and Newtyle are descended. They, however, claim descent from a
2 CONC nother branch, …
2 CONT *2. Henry, of Dilspro. He married a daughter of the laird of Muchalls called Fraser, who married first, Gordon of Haddoch. Thereafter he married one called Agnes Hapburne, who had children. This Henry Gordon made a fair conquest i
2 CONC n Buchan.
2 CONT *3. Catharine, married to _____ Blackhall of Barra.
2 CONT *4. Elizabeth, married to _____ Knowis of Ashintilly.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Gordon of Lesmoir and Margaret Ogilvie, the wife of his son, William, are mentioned in a charter of confirmation of date 1556
2 CONT
2 CONT James Gordon of Lesmoir died before 1559, 
2 CONT
2 CONT and was succeeded by his son, George.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE THANAGE OF FERMARTYN by William Temple, Aberdeen, 1894, pp.261-62
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/thanageoffermart00byutemp/page/260/mode/2up
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/houseofgordon01bulluoft/houseofgordon01bulluoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I29797&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT James (1st) of Lesmoir son of George Gordon of Tillytermount according to the books 'House of Gordon' and 'Thanage of Fermartyn' married twice, first to Margaret, daughter of Patrick Stuart of Laithers; second to Margaret Ogilvie,
2 CONC  Lady Gartly, daughter of the Laird of Findlater.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is the Records of Aboyne which the peerage takes its information from, but the source of that record is the Reg. Mag. Sig. which only notes James being married to a Margaret Ogilvy in 1546. There is no actual source to state Ma
2 CONC rgaret Ogilvy is the daughter of Alexander of Findlater in the Records of Aboyne only an assumption which the Peerage copied.
2 CONT
2 CONT The House of Gordon Balbithan M.S. book only states she was a daughter of the Laird of Findlater and that she was named Lady Gartlie. She was referenced as a widow when married to James, which matches the Margaret Ogilvy who in 15
2 CONC 17 is noted as the wife of Walter Barclay she must have been a daughter of James Ogilvy, younger of Findlater or his father Sir James Sr. Laird of Findlater and a sister or aunt of Alexander who only married in 1509.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Barclay was dead circa 1542, before James is first noted to have re-married to Margaret Ogilvy. If she was say 20 in 1517, then she was still within child-bearing age to have had James' two youngest. There is ample historic
2 CONC al evidence to suggest that women were able to bear children into their 40s back in those days. Considering there are no further children into the 1550s we assume Margaret has passed her child-bearing days.
2 CONT
2 CONT The House of Gordon book does not state that Walter and James' wife were the same person, but is is implied mistaking her for Alexander's daughter when she had to have been his sister. The History of the Barclay Family also states
2 CONC  that Margaret Ogilvy daughter of Alexander of Findlater married Walter Barclay, this again must be in error due to her age of at most 8 in 1517. It also makes reference to the marriage of Walter's widow to James Gordon.
2 CONT [E-mail from Jared Maddison rec: 19 Aug 2018]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Seems incorrect 
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p41320.htm#i413194
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Ogilvy is the daughter of''' Alexander Ogilvy of Deskford and Findlater and Janet Abernethy of Saltoun. [1] 
2 CONT * She''' married''' James Gordon, 2nd of Lesmoir, son of James Gordon, 1st of Lesmoir and Anne Stewart. [1]
2 CONT ** Her married name became Gordon. [1]
2 CONT ** '''Child of Margaret Ogilvy and James Gordon, 2nd of Lesmoir'''
2 CONT *** 1 George Gordon, 3rd of Lesmoir+ [1] b. 1516, d. 1590 '''Citations'''
2 CONT * 1.	[S4053] Christopher Davis, "re: Barton Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger LUNDY (101053), 30 October 2009. Hereinafter cited as "re: Barton Family."
2 CONT  ***************************
