1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www2.thesetonfamily.com/cadets/The_Setons_of_Meldrum_History.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Alexander Seton 4th of Meldrum''''' (p. 137), son of William, was, in 1512, served heir to his grandfather in the Lordship of Meldrum.  He was killed at Aberdeen in 1527.  He married – 1st Agnes, daughter of Patrick Gordon of
2 CONC  Haddo, ancestor of the Earls of Aberdeen, and had by her two sons, William of Meldrum and Alexander of Mounie.  By his second wife, Janet, daughter and co-heiress of George Leith of Barnes he had John Seton of Blair, who got a ch
2 CONC arter, in 1526, of the lands of Auchleven (whence he began the house later known as Licklyhead), Drumrossy, and others, inheriting also Blair from his mother.
