2 CONT
2 CONT I Vi Alexander Seton of.Meldrum (p. 137), son of William, was, in 1512, served heir to his grandfather in the Lordship of Meldrum. He was killed at Aberdeen in 1527. He married 1st, Agnes, daughter of Patrick Gordon of Haddo, ance
2 CONC stor of the Earls of Aberdeen, and had by her two sons, William of Meldrum and Alexander of Mounie. By his second wife, Janet, daughter and co-heiress of George Leith of Barnes he had John Seton of Blair, who got a charter, in 152
2 CONC 0, of half the lands of Auchleven, Drumrossy, and others, inheriting also Blair from his mother.
