2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/houseofgordon01bulluoft/houseofgordon01bulluoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT The Genealogie of James Gordon of Methlick or Haddoe the third son of Jock begotten on the Knight of Gights daughter Maitland his Lawfull Wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The said James Gordon purchased [His wife was Canea Harper "half portioner of Methlick" of which her father "Johannes de Citharista " was the owner ; James G. or his son acquired the other half of the barony, and thus arose the Go
2 CONC rdons of Haddo 1 ] the Lands of Methlick and thereafter the Lands of Haddo being the first Laird thereof. He married Anna Harper (sic!) w l whom he begat four sons and four daughters, viz, his eldest son Patrick Gordon Laird of Ha
2 CONC ddo, Robert Gordon of Fetterletter, Mr Alexander Gordon first Chancellor of Murray and Chanery of Ross and thereafter Bishop of Aberdeen, and George Gordon of Achenniff in Buchan ; his eldest daughter married the Laird of Allardes
2 CONC , the Second married Eraser Laird of , the third married Andrew Prott Burgess in Aberdeen, the fourth married George Gray Burgess in Aberdeen. Their father dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest son Patrick Gordon second Laird of Haddo married the Laird of Findlater's Daughter Ogilvy with whom he begat three sons and three daughters,viz, his eldest Son George Gordon third Laird of Haddo, Mr James Gordon Parson 
2 CONC of Lonmey, and Alexander Gordon first Goodman of Bracoe ; his eldest Daughter married the Laird of Towie Forbes, another married the Laird of Altar Gumming, the third married the Goodman of Blairy or Kilravoch Dunbar. Their father
2 CONC  the said Patrick dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT His eldest son George Gordon third Laird of Haddoe married the Laird of Delgaties daughter Hay, with whom he begat his eldest son '''James Gordon fourth Laird of Haddo'''. His father the said George dyed 
2 CONT
2 CONT His Son said '''James Gordon fourth Laird of Haddoe married Gilbert Menzies Provost of Aberdeens Daughter''', with whom he begat five sons
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149729917/james-gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT James Gordon BIRTH	unknown Aberdeenshire, Scotland DEATH	1581 Scotland BURIAL	 Methlick Churchyard Methlick, Aberdeenshire, Scotland PLOT	Gordon enclosure MEMORIAL ID	149729917 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 2 Jun 1582
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Photo	 George Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Photo	 Marjory Menzies Gordon 1523 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Photo	 Patrick Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription To the memory of the GORDONS of Methlic & Haddo & especially PATRICK GORDON of Methlick who fell fighting for King James the Second of Scotland at the Battle of Brechin 18 May 1452 & of his son JAMES GORDON of Methlick
2 CONC ; also PATRICK GORDON of Methlic & Archadlie (died 1531) son of aforesaid JAMES & of his son & heir GEORGE who predeceased his father, JAMES GORDON of Methlic, Archadlie & at Branchlaw & Haldane, son of the aforesaid GEORGE GORDON
2 CONC , a faithful adherent of Mary Queen of Scots - of him it is recorded that he bigged a house called Kelly. He died 1582. Also of his wife MARJORY sister of Sir Thomas Menzies of Pitfodels, comptroller of Scotland & and of his son &
2 CONC  heir PATRICK GORDON who predeceased his father & of his wife AGNES FRASER dau of Andrew Fraser of Muchill. JAMES GORDON of Methlick, Haddo, Tarves EIC son of aforesaid Patrick Gordon d Nov 1642 & of his wife JEAN dau of William, 
2 CONC Lord Keith, Earl Marischal & of his son & heir GEORGE GORDON d 1610 & of his wife MARGARET dau of Sir Alexander Bannerman of Elsick
