2 CONT >>I.-ARCHIBALD GRANT is Ballimtomb, in Parish of Knockando and County of Elgin. Archibald Grant was the youngest son of James Grant, third of Freuchie, by Christian Barclay his second spouse. He received, on 8th March 1580. a Crow
2 CONC n charter of the manse of the sub-deaconry of Moray, in which he is designated brother of John Grant of Freuchie. He married before 1599, Isobella Cumming, a daughter of the Laird or Erneside, as on 20th May in that year, the Lair
2 CONC d of Frenchie assigned to him and his spouse an annual rent of £100 in return for the loan of £1000. He died before 15th June 1619.He had issue two sons and three daughters.
