1 NAME John /Moray/ Minister of the Gospel at Dunfermline
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Moray
2 NSFX Minister of the Gospel at Dunfermline
2 _MARNM Moray
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE JAN 1632
1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Moray</strong>, fourth son of Robert M. of Abercairny, Foulis - Wester ; educated at Univ. of Edinburgh ; M.A. (10th Aug. 1595); pres. to Borthwick 15th Dec. and 6th Jan. 1598-9; trans, to Second Charge, South Leith,
2 CONC  1603 ; trans, to Second Charge here in 1614; trans, and adm. about 1620. He was summoned before the Court of High Commission 12th Dec. 1621 ; deprived 3rd Jan. 1622, for not conforming to the Five Articles of Perth, and he was or
2 CONC dered to confine himself within two miles of Foulis-Wester. Failing to comply, he was charged on pain of outlawry, 6th Feb. following, to appear before the Council within fifteen days. A further summons was sent on 24th June 1624,
2 CONC  but having fallen from his horse shortly before, he could not attend and his confinement was confirmed "more straitly than at first." During this confinement, he resided at Gorthie, which belonged to an elder brother, on whose de
2 CONC ath, in 1629, he removed a second time to Prestonpans, where he died Jan. 1632, aged about 57. He marr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Margaret Leslie (died 22nd June 1620), eldest daugh. of James, Master of Rothes, and had issue — 
2 CONT * David, born Dec. 1604, and another child, both of whom died while their father was confined in Newabbey
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Mary Melville (who survived him, and marr. John Hepburn of Nunraw), and had issue — 
2 CONT * Jean, served heir to her father 4th May 1633 (marr. Patrick, eldest son of John Hepburn of Nunraw)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc05scot#page/28/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. V, page 28
