1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Facts gathered from the Red Book of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Tosheoch-of-Monzievaird.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT *1577, Nov. 28: received an instrument of sasine (property transfer) for Monzievaird, Glenturret, and Meckven, succeeding his father instead of his older brother, Alexander.
2 CONT *1587: Prevented by King James VI from disposing property at the instigation of his two daughters, Janet and Marjory, and father-in-law John Campbell of Lawers. He was outlawed on many occasions.
2 CONT *married Marjory, daughter of John Campbell, 3rd of Lawers
2 CONT **she marries secondly by 1622 William Graham of Geddochie (RPC Vol. III, P. 758)
2 CONT *1619, December: died by this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of:
2 CONT *David Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 CONT *Janet Tosheoch
2 CONT *Marjory Tosheoch
