1 OCCU 10th Laird of Strowan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 10th Chief of Clan Donnachaidh, Strowan, Perth, Scotland, upon resignation of his uncle, William Robertson, in his favor on 06May1589.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, the tenth chief, was a reckless and improvident leader of his clan.  His estates were almost lost to him in 1597 and it was only through the generosity of an Edinburgh merchant and kinsman, John Robertson, that the estates
2 CONC  were saved.  This loyal Robertson purchased the estates and deeded them back to his chief in a crown charter of January, 1600.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Descent through 16 generations from Malcolm III who deposed MacBeth in 1093
