1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===NAME NOT KNOWN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A wife has not been identified for Sir Alexander de Lindsay. According to William A. Lindsay, KC., writing in the Scots Peerage account of the Lindsay family: "There is reason to believe that his wife was a sister of James, Ste
2 CONC ward of Scotland". [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/9/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 9] His suggestion is founded upon a Papal dispensation granted to his grandson, Sir James de Lindsay, Lord of Crawfo
2 CONC rd and Kirkmichael, but he does not identify the chain of reasoning which led him to make this speculative proposal. [https://archive.org/details/calendarentries00offigoog/page/n189/mode/1up  Papal Registers III: 225]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Scots Peerage account of the Stewart family makes no mention a marriage between a daughter of the fourth Steward and Sir Alexander de Lindsay. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/13/mode/1up The Sco
2 CONC ts Peerage I: 13] Nor does the account of the Stewart family publish by the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy. [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_Toc389122948 Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: High Stewards of Scotla
2 CONC nd], or the account of the Lindsay family. [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20UNTITLED.htm#_Toc389126085 Foundation for Medieval Genealogy: Lindsay]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Papal Registers===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 April 1346: To James de Lindesay, knight, and Egidia Stiward, of the diocese of Glasgow. Dispensation at the request of Philip, king of France, to intermarry, they being related in the third and fourth degrees of kindred. [h
2 CONC ttps://archive.org/details/calendarentries00offigoog/page/n189/mode/1up  Papal Registers III: 225]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Secondary Source Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/calendarentries00offigoog/page/n3/mode/1up Calendar of Entries in the Papal Registers Relating to Great Britain and Ireland. Papal Letters. Edited by W. H. Bliss and C. Johnston. (H.M.S.O., London, 189
2 CONC 7), 637 pp. plus index]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/n8/mode/1up The Scots Peerage. founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume I (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1904), 575 pp. For the Kings of Scotland see pp. 1-36]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage.  founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of
2 CONC  that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume III. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1906),  617 pp. plus Errata. For Lindsay Earl of Crawford see pp. 1-51]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes and Comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Stewart,_4th_High_Steward_of_Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Presumed legitimate, but possibly not.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT John Ravilious has postulated that the wife of Sir Alexander Lindsay was not a daughter of Alexander Stewart, but a granddaughter, either as daughter of Alexander's son John Stewart, or as daughter of Reginald Crawford by a daught
2 CONC er of Alexander Stewart. More info is needed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart01.php
2 CONT * http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/16/39907.HTM
2 CONT * 580 Jim Weber http://worldconnect.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=PED&db=jweber&id=I19404.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, Earl of Crawford married Margaret Dunbar, daughter of Sir David Dunbar of Cockburn, himself a son of George I, Earl of March, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lady Elizabeth Lindsay (d. 1509), married to John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond
2 CONT     David Lindsay, 1st Duke of Montrose (1440-1495)
2 CONT     Alexander Lindsay, 7th Earl of Crawford (d. 1517).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Crawford also had an illegitimate son, Alexander, who entered holy orders and became a canon of Aberdeen. - wikipedia
