1 OCCU LCVM-M5Q
1 TITL Governor of Dundee
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER ABERNETHY OF THAT ILK===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Governor of Dundee===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_de_Abernethy Biographical Summary by Wikipedia]===
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander de Abernethy (died c.1315) was a Scottish baron. He was a descendant of lay abbots of Abernethy; his grandfather Laurence, great-grandson of Gillemichael, Earl of Fife, was the first to style himself Lord (dominus). His 
2 CONC daughter Margaret married John Stewart of Bonkyll, the new Scottish earl of Angus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander swore fealty to Edward I in 1291, presumably on the death of his father, Hugh. Between 1301 and 1303 he was appointed warden of Scotland between the Forth and the Mounth. He lost the office in King Edward's ordinances of
2 CONC  1305 but supported Balliol's claims over Bruce's. He was ordered to join the expedition of John of Brittany to defend Galloway against Robert Bruce and was absent from King Robert's first parliament in 1309. In June 1308 he was a
2 CONC ppointed warden of Scotland between the Forth and Orkney in June 1308 together with Edward Hastings; and in July 1310 - warden between the Forth and the mountains. He was also contracted to serve from September in Berwick and Pert
2 CONC hshire under the command of Sir John de Segrave. He received Clackmannan in Stirlingshire from Edward II in 1310, was keeper of Dundee at least in mid-1311 and led the unsuccessful defence of the town against Edward Bruce in 1312.
2 CONC  In 1314 Abernethy was forfeited and attached to the earldom of Angus, so Alexander went to England and died by the end of 1315.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret de Menteith, daughter of Alexander, Earl of Menteith. 'lady Margaret de Abrenythy' was a lady of the court of Isabella of France, Queen of England, 1311/12. She resided in England as late as 30 Jan 1324/5, when
2 CONC  a record in the Patent Rolls dated at Langley stated, ' 860. The K. signifies that he has granted leave to Margaret de Abernethy to visit Scotland, to treat with her friends there as to recovery of her hereditary lands. Langley. 
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT They had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret, wife of John Stewart, Earl of Angus Margaret de Abernethy.
2 CONT * Mary, wife of (1) Sir Andrew de Leslie, and (2) Sir David de Lindsay Mary de Abernethy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bain (ed.) Calendar of documents relating to Scotland, volume 3;
2 CONT C. A. McGladdery, ‘Abernethy family (per. c.1260–c.1465)’, Oxford Dictionary of National Biography, OUP (2004); Cal. Patent Rolls, 18 Edw. II. p. 2, p. 87, m. 32. Bain, Cal. Docs. Scotland III:157, no. 860. J. Ravilious, The Earls
2 CONC  of Menteith: Alexander, Earl of Menteith and Sir Alexander de Abernethy, The Scottish Genealogist (September 2010), Vol. LVII, No. 3, pp. 130–139.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2116.htm#i21153 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Alexander Abernethy of that Ilk1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #21154
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=21 May 2007
2 CONT
