2 CONC ge and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2116.htm#i21153 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT # [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_de_Abernethy Wikipedia]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/aa/abernethy1.php Stirnet: Abernethy 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Abbots and lords of Abernethy
2 CONT The abbots of Abernethy were descendants of Gille Míchéil, Earl of Fife. The abbacy may have been held by Áed (called Hugo or Eggu and other Latinised forms), son of Gille Míchéil,[2] but the abbacy is first attested when Áed's so
2 CONC n Orm is confirmed in possession of it by King William of Scotland in the 1170s, in condition for making concessions favorable to the King's new monastic establishment at Arbroath Abbey.[3] The title of Abbot disappears in the sou
2 CONC rces during the abbacy of Laurence, with the title of dominus predominating:
2 CONT * Orm de Abernethy (fl. 1170s)
2 CONT * Laurence de Abernethy (fl. 1190s)
2 CONT * Hugh de Abernethy (d. 1291)
2 CONT * Alexander de Abernethy (d. c. 1315)
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of Alexander Abernethy, the title passed to his daughter Margaret who married John Stewart of Bonkyll, who assumed the title, as well as being granted the forfeited Earldom of Angus. https://en.wikipedia.org/wi
2 CONC ki/Lord_of_Abernethy
2 CONT
