2 CONT * '''Colonial and Revolutionary Families of Pennsylvania  By John W. Jordan. [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Colonial_And_Revolutionary_Families_Of_P/arAfWBsvO1gC?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=john+de+montgomery+1429+Maxwell&pg=PA1136&pri
2 CONC ntsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q=john%20de%20montgomery%201429%20Maxwell&f=false Google Books]
2 CONT * '''Pg.1136'''
2 CONT * Sir John De Montgomerie, second son of '''Sir John and Elizabeth Eglinton''', succeeded to the lands and titles of his father and mother in 1398, and is referred to as eldest male heir and chief of the French house of Montgomeri
2 CONC e. He was one of the chiefs of the Scottish army which invaded England in 1402, and was taken prisoner at the Battle of Halidon Hill. Five years later he was in Scotland and introduced the reputed Richard II, of England, to Robert
2 CONC  II, of Scotland. On the accession of James I, after his long imprisonment in England, Sir John de Montgomery (2) was among the nobles of high rank who were arrested on suspicion of having profited by their sovereign's imprisonmen
2 CONC t and brought before the Parliament held at Perth, March 12, 1425. He was, however, released immediately and restored to high favor, being on the the jury to try the Duke of Albany, and was commissioned to reduce the fortress of L
2 CONC ock Lamond, held by Albany's youngest son, James Stewart. He married Margaret, daughter of Sir Robert Maxwell, of Caerlaverock, the ancestor of the Earls of Nithsdale, and died prior to November, 1429, leaving three sons and four 
2 CONC daughters. His second son, Sir Robert de Montgomerie, became Knight of Giffen, a barony given by Robert II to Sir Hugh Eglinton, and brought into the Montgomerie family by Robert's grandmother, before mentioned. 
2 CONT * '''Pg. 1137'''
2 CONT * Hugh, the third son, is mentioned in a charter to his brother Alexander, Lord Montgomerie, in 1452. Of the daughters, Anne married, June 16, 1425, Sir Robert Cuninghame, father of the Earl of Glencairn; Janet became the second w
2 CONC ife of Sir Thomas Boyd, of Kilmarnock, whose daughter Margaret, by a former marriage, became the wife of Lord Montgomerie; and Isabel married Archibald Muir, of Rowallan.
2 CONT *.... etc. ______________________________
2 CONT * Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 38
2 CONT *Montgomerie, Alexander de		by Thomas Finlayson Henderson
2 CONT *MONTGOMERIE, Sir ALEXANDER de, of Ardrossan, first Lord Montgomerie (d. 1470?), was the eldest son of Sir John Montgomerie of Eaglesham, Eglinton, and Ardrossan, by his wife Agnes, daughter of Alexander, earl of Ross, lord of the
2 CONC  Isles. '''His grandfather, Sir John Montgomerie (d. 1398?), is separately noticed'''. The father was a hostage for the Earl of Douglas in 1408, a hostage for James I in 1423, and one of the jury on the trial of Murdac, duke of Al
2 CONC bany, in 1425. In 1425 the son was chosen a member of the privy council of James I. He succeeded his father some time before 22 Nov. 1429, and in August 1430 he was, jointly with his brother-in-law, Sir Robert Cunningham of Kilmau
2 CONC rs, appointed governor of Cantyre and Knapdale. .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Montgomerie,_Alexander_de_(DNB00) ______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=er1357&id=I6000000008517729892
2 CONT
2 CONT Spiceland and Choctaws Entries: 197805    Updated: 2017-01-12 20:35:30 UTC (Thu)    Contact: catherine Spiceland Index | Descendancy | Register | Pedigree | Ahnentafel | Public Profile | Add Post-em ID: I6000000008517729892 Name: 
2 CONC John Montgomerie of Eaglesham 1 2 3 Given Name: John Surname: Montgomerie 1 2 3 Suffix: of Eaglesham 1 3 Nickname: John Fourth de Montgomery 2 3 Sex: M Birth: 2 3 ABT 1338 Death: 1 2 3 DEC 1388 Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Montgomery, 10th Baron of Eaglesham was the distinguished warrior who captured Henry Percy, called Hotspur, at the Battle of Otterburn in 1388. With Percy's ransom he built the castle of Polnoon as well as acquiring the lands
2 CONC  of Eglinton and Ardrossan through his marriage to Elizabeth of Eglinton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====References
2 CONT * History from the Clan Montgomery Society
2 CONT * "Origin and History of the Montgomerys" by B.G. Montgomery of Sweden
2 CONT * Correspondence with Brent Friedrichs, Box 34, Charter Oak, IA 51439, 712-678-3720, email: blf@ia.frontiercomm.net, Dec. 1996.
2 CONT
