1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''This person is the first Montgomery for which Stirnet unconditionally vouches.'''
2 CONT '''His precise place''' in Montgomery ancestry '''and''' his exact ancestry are disputed. 
2 CONT '''His suffix''' "5th of Eagllesham" may not be adequately proven with extant sources.
2 CONT '''Please review''' the attached document in Sources titled "Stirnet - Montgomery Pedigree (2015)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >====From Stirnet Pedigree
2 CONT >'''GH does not mention''' John’s marriage to Agnes of the Isles, identifying Margaret Maxwell as mother of Alexander, Robert, Hugh, Anne, Janet & Isabel. 
2 CONT >'''TSP''' reports both marriages, identifying Agnes as mother of Alexander, Robert & Agnes and mentioning also Joanna & Isabella without being clear who their mother was. 
2 CONT >'''BP1934''' mentions both marriages without being clear who was mother of Alexander, Robert, Hugh, Anne & Joan. 
2 CONT >'''m1. Agnes MacDonald''' of the Isles (probably dau of John MacDonald, Lord of the Isles)
2 CONT >'''(a)''' Alexander Montgomery, 1st Lord (d 1470 or before 14.10.1465) '''m'''. Margaret Boyd (dau of Sir Thomas Boyd of Kilmarnock)
2 CONT >'''(b)''' Robert Montgomerie, 1st of Giffen (a 1413, d before 1452) '''m'''. Janet Murray (dau of Alexander Murray of Touch Adam and/or Polmais)
2 CONT >'''(c)''' Hugh Montgomery
2 CONT >'''(d)''' Agnes (Anne) Montgomery -- '''m'''. (mcrt 16.06.1425) Sir Robert Cunningham of Kilmaurs m2. Margaret Maxwell (dau of Sir Herbert Maxwell of Carlaverock)
2 CONT >'''(e)''' Joanna (Janet) Montgomery '''possibly of this marriage''' – ## Joanna is shown as wife of Sir Thomas Boyd of Kilmarnock. However, having regard to the marriage of Sir John's son Alexander, we accept the suggestion made 
2 CONC by a contributor (PK, 28.11.08) that his wife was more likely to have been sister rather than daughter of Sir John.
2 CONT >'''(f)''' Isabella Montgomery '''possibly of this marriage''' m. Archibald Muir of 8 Rowallan marriage not certain
2 CONT
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————————————
2 CONT
2 CONT ====From [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Colonial_And_Revolutionary_Families_Of_P/arAfWBsvO1gC?q=john+de+montgomery+1429+Maxwell&gbpv=1#f=false Colonial and Revolutionary Families of Pennsylvania], by John W. Jordan
2 CONT * '''Pg.1136'''
2 CONT * '''Sir John De Montgomerie, second son''' of Sir John and Elizabeth Eglinton, '''succeeded to the lands and titles of his father and mother in 1398, and is referred to as eldest male heir and chief of the French house of Montgom
2 CONC erie. He was one of the chiefs of the Scottish army which invaded England in 1402, and was taken prisoner at the Battle of Halidon Hill. Five years later he was in Scotland and introduced the reputed Richard II, of England, to Rob
2 CONC ert II, of Scotland. On the accession of James I, after his long imprisonment in England, Sir John de Montgomery (2) was among the nobles of high rank who were arrested on suspicion of having profited by their sovereign's imprison
2 CONC ment and brought before the Parliament held at Perth, March 12, 1425. He was, however, released immediately and restored to high favor, being on the the jury to try the Duke of Albany, and was commissioned to reduce the fortress o
2 CONC f Lock Lamond, held by Albany's youngest son, James Stewart. He married Margaret, daughter of''' Sir Robert Maxwell, of Caerlaverock, the ancestor of the Earls of Nithsdale, and '''died prior to November, 1429, leaving three sons 
2 CONC and four daughters. His second son''', Sir Robert de Montgomerie, became Knight of Giffen, a barony given by Robert II to Sir Hugh Eglinton, and brought into the Montgomerie family by Robert's grandmother, before mentioned
2 CONT * '''Pg. 1137'''
2 CONT * Hugh, '''the third son, is mentioned in a charter to his brother''' Alexander, Lord Montgomerie, in 1452. '''Of the daughters''', Anne married, June 16, 1425, Sir Robert Cuninghame, father of the Earl of Glencairn; Janet became 
2 CONC the second wife of Sir Thomas Boyd, of Kilmarnock, whose daughter Margaret, by a former marriage, became the wife of Lord Montgomerie; and Isabel married Archibald Muir, of Rowallan.
2 CONT ___________________________
2 CONT ====ThePeerage.com [http://www.thepeerage.com/p17248.htm#i172480 Sir John Montgomerie of Ardrossa]
2 CONT * '''Sir John Montgomerie of Ardrossan1 
