2 CONT *Alexander Montgomerie, 1st Lord Montgomerie (died 1470?) was a Scottish nobleman and diplomat.
2 CONT * He was the eldest son of '''Sir John Montgomerie of Ardrossan, by his wife Agnes, daughter of John of Islay, Lord of the Isles'''.[1] In 1425 he was chosen a member of the privy council of James I. He succeeded his father some t
2 CONC ime before 22 November 1429, and in August 1430 he was, jointly with his brother-in-law, Sir Robert Cunningham of Kilmaurs, appointed governor of Cantyre and Knapdale.[2] .... etc.
2 CONT * With his wife Margaret, Montgomerie had three or four sons and three daughters:[2]
2 CONT *  .... etc.
2 CONT * '''From''': http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Montgomerie,_1st_Lord_Montgomerie ________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 38
2 CONT * Montgomerie, Alexander de	– by Thomas Finlayson Henderson
2 CONT * MONTGOMERIE, Sir ALEXANDER de, of Ardrossan, first Lord Montgomerie (d. 1470?), was the eldest son of '''Sir John Montgomerie of Eaglesham, Eglinton, and Ardrossan, by his wife Agnes, daughter of Alexander, earl of Ross, lord of
2 CONC  the Isles'''. His grandfather, Sir John Montgomerie (d. 1398?), is separately noticed. '''The father was a hostage for the Earl of Douglas in 1408, a hostage for James I in 1423, and one of the jury on the trial of Murdac, duke o
2 CONC f Albany, in 1425'''. In 1425 the son was chosen a member of the privy council of James I. He '''succeeded his father some time before 22 Nov. 1429''', and in August 1430 he was, jointly with his brother-in-law, Sir Robert Cunning
2 CONC ham of Kilmaurs, appointed governor of Cantyre and Knapdale. .... etc.
2 CONT * From: http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Montgomerie,_Alexander_de_(DNB00) 
2 CONT ______________________________
