2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/194 The Scots Peerage etc. Volume VI, pp. 194-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas married Mary DE STRATHEARN, daughter of Sir Malise DE STRATHEARN 5th Earl of Strathearn and Marjory DE MUSCHAMP. (Mary DE STRATHEARN was born about 1248 in Strathearn, Perthshire, Scotland and died before 1318 in Dalkeith
2 CONC , Fife, Scotland.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of [https://www.geni.com/people/Nicholas-de-Graham-of-Dalkeith-Abercorn-and-Eskdale/6000000004533941060?through=6000000026874295420 '''Sir Nicholas'''] [d. 1306] and his wife [https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-of-Strat
2 CONC hearn/6000000004533941074?through=6000000004533941060 '''Mary of Strathearn'''] were : —
2 CONT
2 CONT *(a) [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Graham-of-Dalkeith-Abercorn-and-Eskdale/6000000026874295420 '''Sir John of Dalkeith, Abercorn, and Eskdale''']. In an inquest at Barnborough with regard to his mother's half of Muscham
2 CONC p, 19 May 1306, he is said to be twenty-eight years of age.10 … he died 25 April 1337, leaving a widow, Isabella, who had a terce of his lands in Crichton, apparently exempted from the forfeiture, and a lease of the other two-thir
2 CONC ds.6   
2 CONT *(b) [https://www.geni.com/people/Isabella-Graham/6000000002166220506?through=6000000026874295420 '''Isabella'''], married (as his second wife) to Walter, High Steward of Scotland, sometime husband of Marjory Bruce, daughter of Ro
2 CONC bert i., and by him, who died 1326, had a son, Sir John Stewart of Ralston, and other children.3
2 CONT
