2 CONT
2 CONT Born bef 20 Mar 1248/9.[1] Occupation: baroness of Muschamp. younger daughter and coheir (eventual sole heir) of her mother[10] ' Nicholas de Grame and Maria his wife ' held a market in Wooler, Northumberland in 1293, together wit
2 CONC h Walter de Huntercumb [her cousin and the other coheir], 'which they claimed from time out of mind ' (QW, p. 601).[13] as widow of Nicholas Graham, held Wooler by the service of 2 knights' fees, 1311 (Sanders p. 101)[10] Wooler p
2 CONC assed on her death to the Huntercomb heir, her cousin[10] (her husband Nicholas de Graham 'adhered to the Scots') cf. Chart. Inchaffray, lxiv[14] SP VI:195[1] SP VIII:247[1] Genealogics I00139257[8] 
