2 CONT Herbert Herries, 1st Lord Herries of Terregles
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Herbert Herries, 1st Lord Herries of Terregles (died c. 1505), was a Scottish peer.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Herries was summoned to the Scottish Parliament as Lord Herries of Terregles in 1490. He died about 1505 and was succeeded in the lordship of Parliament by his son Andrew.
2 CONT
2 CONT No mention of his wife or children
2 CONT Janet Milburn 10/9/22
2 CONT __________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT FamilySearch.Org Is this the same person as the one on this profile????
2 CONT
2 CONT The Life Summary of Herbert
2 CONT
2 CONT When Herbert Herries was born in 1460, in Terregles, Kirkcudbrightshire, Scotland, his father, Lord David Herries 5th Lord Of Terregles, was 24 and his mother, Margaretha Crichton, was 30. He married Marion Carlyle in January 0021
2 CONC , in Dumfries, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 3 daughters. He died on 12 June 1505, in Dumfriesshire, Scotland, at the age of 45, and was buried in Terregles, Kirkcudbrightshire, Scotland.
