1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER HAMILTON OF CAMBUSKEITH===
2 CONT
2 CONT is the son of John Hamilton of Cambuskeith. He was served heir to his father in 1489 [G. Harvey Johnston, FSA (Scot)., The Heraldry of the Hamiltons with Notes on all the Males of the Family, Descriptions of the Arms, Plates and P
2 CONC edigrees (W. & A. K. Johnston Limited, Edinburgh & London, MCMIX), pp. 120-21] https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/120/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Hamilton of Cambuskeith is mentioned in the Acta Auditorum on 24 January 1488 [John Anderson, Historical and Genealogical Memoirs of the House of Hamilton with Genealogical Memoirs of the several Branches of the Family (
2 CONC John Anderson, Jun., Limited, Edinburgh, MDCCCXXV), pp. 254-57] https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/254/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Hamilton of Cambuskeith married Marion Cunningham, the daughter of Sir Adam Cunningham of Caprington, and they are reported to have had three sons [G. Harvey Johnston, FSA (Scot)., The Heraldry of the Hamiltons with Note
2 CONC s on all the Males of the Family, Descriptions of the Arms, Plates and Pedigrees (W. & A. K. Johnston Limited, Edinburgh & London, MCMIX), pp. 120-21] https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/120/mode/1up The names o
2 CONC f their sons follow:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) John Hamilton of Cambuskeith
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) William Hamilton of Sorn and Sanquhar
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) Alexander Hamilton
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===ALEXANDER HAMILTON OF CAMBUSKEITH===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/254/mode/1up Memoirs, p. 254]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/382/mode/1up Memoirs, p. 382]
