2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 October 1505: Instrument of Procuratory upon David Colville, James Colville, Philip Colville, George Moran and Sir George Machelson, chaplain, as procurators for procuring the dispensation of the marriage contract between Ale
2 CONC xander Boyd of Kilmarnock and Janet Colville. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+boyd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=n National Records of Scotl
2 CONC and, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 October 1505: Instrument by Janet Colville, sister of Sir William Colville, of Ochiltree, Robert Colville of Hylton, Philip Colville, Mr John Wallis of Linlithgow and John Macadam, her procurators, for procuring confirmation
2 CONC  of the aforesaid dispensation. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f27&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Colville&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Boyd Pap
2 CONC ers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/27]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 November 1505: Instrument taken on sentence pronounced by James, Abbot of Dunfermline, dispensing (in terms of Letter of Pope Julius II dated at Rome 3 Jul 1504) with the impediments to the marriage, already contracted, betw
2 CONC een Alexander Boyd in Kilmarnock and Janet Colville, and legitimising the children already born of the marriage. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f25&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ale
2 CONC xander+boyd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/25]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 June 1508: Indenture: Margaret, Queen of Scotland, with the consent of King James IV, King of Scots, on the one part, and Alexander Boyd in Kilmarnock, on the other part, whereby she settles to him and his heirs, the lordshi
2 CONC p and lands of Kilmarnock, Dalry, Noddesdyle, Kilbride, Flatt, Narstone and the Annual of Martuam, for the space of 9 years, the said Alexander paying £100, at the terms therein specified. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrson
2 CONC linecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f29&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+boyd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1510&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1510: Discharge by Queen Margaret to Robert Boyd of 200 marks and the mails of the lands of Kilmarnock, which he had paid at her command to Mr Francis Bothwell, burgess of Edinbugh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonline
2 CONC catalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f35&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Boyd&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1508&dt=1560&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/150/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 150-2]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/boyd1.php Stirnet: Boyd 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://thepeerage.com/p3062.htm#i30617 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Boyd, 3rd Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock [Note] married Janet Colville, daughter of Sir Robert Colville and Eupheme Wallace, before 23 November 1505. He died after 26 June 1508. He was the son of Robert Boyd, 1st Lord Boyd o
2 CONC f Kilmarnock and Mariot Maxwell. He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock [S., c. 1454] in 1484. [Note] He was Chamberlain of Kilmarnock before 2 August 1488. Children of Alexander Boyd, 3rd Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock
2 CONC  [Note] and Janet Colville: (1) Margaret Boyd (2) Robert Boyd, 4th Lord Boyd of Kilmarnock d. bt 29 Jul 1557 - 10 May 1558. [http://thepeerage.com/p3062.htm#i30617 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This is wrong. Alexander Boyd did not succeed as the third Lord Boyd. See the evidence cited above.'''
