2 CONT <blockquote>'''Patrick Maxwell, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Maxwell-3rd-of-Newark/6000000013416782068?through=6000000210619181843 '''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Maxwell, here treated, is the uncle of https://www.geni.com/people/George-Maxwell-4th-of-Newark/6000000055569835893. He is noticed in the company of his nephew in the witness lists of three protocols dated 6 March 1556-
2 CONC 57. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc09robegoog#page/n27/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols V:  protocols numbered 1334-1336, on pp. 7-8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Abstracts from the Protocol Book of Henry Gibson ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 March 1556-57: George Maxuell of Nework bound himself to deliver to William Flemyng of Barruchan a sufficient letter of reversion, subscribed and sealed by him and Marion Conyghame, his spouse, for redemption of an annualrent
2 CONC  of 10 merks furth of the 40 s. land of Barlogan, lying in the parish of Killillan and shire of Renfrew on payment of 100 merks. Done in the chapter of the place of the Friars Minors, in the city of Glasgow. Witnesses : William Co
2 CONC nyghame of Carncurane, Mr. Robert Conyghame, brothers, Patrick Flemyng, brother of the said William, Patrick Maxuell, uncle of the said George, and Sir John Robeson, chaplain in Newerk. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc0
2 CONC 9robegoog#page/n27/mode/1up Abstracts of the Protocol of the Town Clerks of Glasgow, Volume V. Henry Gibson's Protocols, 1555-68, protocols numbered 1334-1336, on pp. 7-8]'''
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 March 1556-57: William Conyghame of Carncuran acknowledged an annualrent of 40 merks which he had furth of the 40 s. land of Barlogane, lying in the parish of Killillan and shire of Renfrew, to be lawfully redeemed by William
2 CONC  Flemyng of Barruchan: and he renounced the charter, sasine, and other evidents made to him. Done in the chapter of the place of the Friars Minors. Witnesses: George Maxuell of Newerk, Patrick Maxuell, his uncle, Patrick Fleming, 
2 CONC brother of the said William Flemyng, Mr. Robert Conygham, and Sir John Robeson, chaplain. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc09robegoog#page/n27/mode/1up Abstracts of the Protocol of the Town Clerks of Glasgow, Volume V. H
2 CONC enry Gibson's Protocols, 1555-68, protocols numbered 1334-1336, on pp. 7-8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 March 1556-57: Patrick Maxuell, uncle of George Maxuell of Newerk, acknowledged himself paid by William Conyghame of Carncurane of the sum of £100 in numerate money, contained in an act inserted in the books of the official o
2 CONC f Glasgow, in which the said William was enacted to Patrick; and he consented to the deletion of the act. Done in the chapter of the Friars Minora of Glasgow. Witnesses: George Maxuell of Newerk, William Flemyng of Barrochan, Patr
2 CONC ick Flemyng, his brother, Mr. Robert Conyghame, and Sir John Robeson. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsprotoc09robegoog#page/n27/mode/1up Abstracts of the Protocol of the Town Clerks of Glasgow, Volume V. Henry Gibson's Protoc
2 CONC ols, 1555-68, protocols numbered 1334-1336, on pp. 7-8]'''
