1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ELIZABETH SCRYMGEOR ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Scrymgeour, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Scrymgeour-of-Dudhope-Constable-of-Dundee/6000000009618105527?through=6000000009618037407 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Mariot-
2 CONC Stewart/6000000009618029483?through=6000000009618037407. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4as/scrymgeour01.php Stirnet: Scrymgeour 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/LKBG-B6G
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death have not been identified for Elizabeth Scrymgeour, here treated. However she is certainly known to have died before 8 June 1565. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD137%2f733&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1566&di=n NRS: GD137/733]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Scrymgeour, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/James-Scrymgeour-of-Kirkton/6000000199061286868?through=6000000009618037407 On 25 October 1539 she and her husband had a charter from her father for the un
2 CONC entailed lands of the lordship of Duddop and Constabulary of Dundee. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f786&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=16
2 CONC 00&di=y NRS: GD137/786]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/John-Scrymgeour-of-Kirkton/6000000009617990192?through=6000000009618037407 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/James-Scrymgeour/6000000207237173886?through=6000000009618037407 ''' 
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/William-Scrymgeour/6000000207237689836?through=6000000009618037407 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Scrymgeour/6000000207237816822?through=6000000009618037407 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Scrymgeour/6000000207237643845?through=6000000009618037407 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Scrymgeour Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 January 1525: Ane letter of regies grantit be Robert Mauld of Panmure in favouris of James Scrymgeour, constable of Dundie, upoun the alienatioun of the landis of Balrudrie in favouris of Marioun Stewart, Elizabeth and Agnes
2 CONC  Scrymgeours, douchteris gottin betuix him and the said Marioun, daitit the xxv day of Januar anno jmvc xxv zeiris. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso30scotuoft/page/2/mode/1up Scrymgeour Inventory: number 20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1533:  Precept of clare constat grantit be Robert Mauld of Panmure for infefting of Elizabeth Scrymgeour, ane of the douchteris and aris of Marie Stewart, in the landis of Balrudrie, daitit xxv Aprile 1533. [https://ar
2 CONC chive.org/details/scottishrecordso30scotuoft/page/1/mode/1up Scrymgeour Inventory: number 6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 June 1565: Charter gevin be Johnne Sciymgeour, sone and air of Elizabeth Scrymgeour ane of the airis of lyne of James Scrymgeour of Dudope, to Johnne Scrymgeour, constabill of Dundie, and his airis mail], of the Maynes of Bal
2 CONC legerno and Walkmylne, daitit 8 Junij anno jm vc lxv. Togidder with the seising following thairupoun. William Haitlie, notar. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso30scotuoft/page/9/mode/1up Scrymgeour Inventory: number 134
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 May 1533: Notarial Minutes of Sasine given to Elizabeth and Agnes Scrymgeours as heirs to their Mother, Margaret (also called Marion) Stewart, of the lands of Balrudrie in the Barony of Panmure and shire of Forfar. [https://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f864&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=balrudrie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Famil
2 CONC y, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/864]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 October 1539: Charter. James Scrymgeour, Constable of Dundee of the lands of Ballegerno and others in favor of Elizabeth Scrymgeour his daughter and James Scrymgeour her spouse and longest liver of them in conjunct fee, and 
2 CONC the heirs-male procreate betwixt them; whom failing to return to the granter and his heirs male whatsoever for extinction of pleas and in full satisfaction of all rights, title or hereditary claim of the said Elizabeth and James S
2 CONC crymgeour for his interest to the unentailed lands of the Lordship of Duddop and Constabulary of Dundee, or to any other lands or competent to her by the decease of the said James, or any of his predecessors, and for the Renunciat
2 CONC ion of her half of the lands of Balrudry and specially for the Compliment keeping and observance of a Contract entered into and passed thereupon betwixt the said Constable and the said Elizabeth and James, registered in the books 
2 CONC of the Commissariot of St. Andrews 25 October 1539. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f786&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National 
2 CONC Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/786]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 October 1539: Obligation of warrandice of the said lands of Ballegerno by James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee to the said Elizabeth Scrymgeour and James her spouse. Dated the last day of October 1539. [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f789&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Fam
2 CONC ily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/789]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 March 1541: Certified copy of Charter. Dated the 2d March 1541, of the Lands and Barony of Duddop etc. in favor of James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee in liferent and John Scrymgeour of Glastre in fee, and the heirs-male of 
2 CONC his body; whom failing John Scrymgeour, Grandson to the said James, procreate betwixt James Scrymgeour formerly of Kirktoun and Elizabeth Scrymgeour, daughter of the said James the Constable, or any other heirs-male lawfully procr
2 CONC eated or to be procreated betwixt the said James and Elizabeth, Whom failing James Scrymgeour Fiar of Fardle, James Scrymgeour of Fordie, James Scrymgeour of Gond, and John Scrymgeour of Myres seriatim, and the heirs-male of their
2 CONC  bodies respective; whom failing the lawful and nearest heirs-male of the blood and name of Scrymgeour carrying its arms; whom all failing the lawful and nearest heirs whatsoever of the said James, with a reservation to the terce 
2 CONC of the Constable's present or any future wife, and a clause of return to the heirs-male of the Constable's body if any should be thereafter procreated for the safer preservation of the house of the said James. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f819&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn F
2 CONC amily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/819]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1547: Charter by Archibald Earl of Angus to John Scrimgeour of Glastre, constable of Dundee, his heirs and assignees, of all and sundry the lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradichty, and also three 8th parts and 25/ of a fourth
2 CONC  8th part of the lands of Ethybetoun, lying in the regality of Kerymure; which lands belonged to Elizabeth and Agnes Scrimgeours, daughters of the late James S. constable of Dundee, heritably and were by them, with consent of Jame
2 CONC s Scrimgeour husband of said Elizabeth, and of Peter Brus, heir apparent of Erlishall, husband of said Agnes, resigned in the hands of their superiors at Edinburgh: To be holden of the granter and his successors in fee and heritag
2 CONC e for the rights and services used and wont. Dated at Edinburgh 8 May 1547. Witnesses, James Scrimgeour of Roddgoddyn, Mr Hugh Rig of Carbery, James Ogilvy of Balfuir, David Grahame of Fentre, Knight, and William Rethe notary. Sea
2 CONC l broken.[https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f791&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=erlishall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn o
2 CONC f Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/791]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 May 1547: Precept of seizin by Jonet Haliburtoun the elder of the daughters, and one of the heirs of the late Patrick lord Haliburtoun of Dirltoun, and lady superior of the lands, for Seizin to be given to Elizabeth Scrymgeo
2 CONC ur daughter and heir served and retoured to the late James Scrymgeour of Dudope, constable of Dundee, of the mains of Ballegarnoch, with tower and fortalice, etc. and half of the lands of Wester Newtoun of Ballegarnoch, in the bar
2 CONC ony thereof and shire of Perth: Dated at Edinburgh. William Lord Ruthven the husband of the granter consents, and signs the Deed with his lady; their seals are attached, that of Lord Ruthven wants about half. [https://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f2288&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn F
2 CONC amily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/2288]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 April 1551: Precept of Sasine by John, Archbishop of St. Andrews, directed to the bailies of his regality of St. Andrews within his barony of Roscoby, for infefting John Scrymgeour son and apparent heir of an honourable man J
2 CONC ames Scrymgeour of Ballegarno and Elizabeth also Scrymgeour his spouse, the heirs and assignees of the said John, whatsoever, in all and whole the half parts of the half of the Kirktoun of Stradychty Martyne, and of Baldovane, in 
2 CONC the barony of Roscoby and shire of Forfar; which parts belong to the said Elizabeth Scrymgeour one of the daughters and elder of the heirs of the late James Scrymgeour of Dudop, constable of Dundee, and were resigned by her in fav
2 CONC our of the said John, reserving the life-rent and usufruct of the same to a noble lady, Isabella Gray, relict of James Scrymgeour of Dudop, Knight, and mother of the late James S. of Dudop, and now spouse of a noble man, John Camp
2 CONC bell of Lundy, Knight. Dated at the church of St. Andrews 9th April 1551. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f729&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&
2 CONC dt=1600&di=y  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/729]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 October 1554: Judicial Instrument taken in the Sheriff Court of Perth by John Scrymgeour as heir to Elizabeth Scrymgeour his mother. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f828&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/828]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1555: Extract Contract betwixt John Scrymgeour of Duddop, Constable of Dundee, John Scrymgeour Son and heir of the deceased Elizabeth Scrymgeour, eldest daughter and heir of the deceased James Scrymgeour, Constable of 
2 CONC Dundee, procreated of the Marriage between her and the also deceased James Scrymgeour of Ballegerno. Dated the 28 March and registred in the books of Council and Session the penult day of the said month 1555. [https://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f863&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Fa
2 CONC mily, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/863]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 October 1556: Retour of the General Service of John Scrimgeour as heir of Elizabeth Scrimgeour his mother. Expede before a noble Lord Patrick master of Gray, sheriff principal of Forfar, Robert Maule of Panmure, Gilbert Monor
2 CONC guid of that Ilk, Ninian Guthre of Kingany, and James Fiffe in Drone, sheriffs deputes: On the inquest are John, Lord Invermeith, James Fenton of Ogill, William Blair of Balgillo, William Dempster of Carreldstone, George Semes of 
2 CONC Balzordy, Alexander Wellam of Woddanay Alexander Ogilvy of Clovay, David Gardin of Leys, Thomas Melving of Dysart, John Guthre of Balnabreich, Robert Dempster, George Falconar in Fyndory, Charles Fullerton, William Fullerton of Ar
2 CONC dy, and John Mortymer apparent of Flemyngton. In the Court House of the burgh of Forfar on 3rd October 1556. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f731&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=joh
2 CONC n+scrimgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1584&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/731]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1556: Reversion by Mr Thomas Scrimgeour chanter of Brechin, brother german and heir male of the late Andrew S. of Fordy, in favour of John Scrimgeour of Dudop constable of Dundee, and his heirs male and of taillie c
2 CONC ontained in his charter of new infeftment of Dudop, of the half lands of Balrudry in the barony of Panmure, which belonged before to Elizabeth Scrimgeour, daughter of the late James Scrimgeour constable of Dundee, which lands were
2 CONC  sold by the said James S. to the late James Scrimgeour of Fordy, father of the said Mr Thomas, in liferent, and to the said late Andrew S. and his heirs male in fee and heritage: which the granter becomes bound to renounce whenev
2 CONC er the said John S. shall pay him 1000 merks in gold and silver: and also along therewith a sufficient letter of Tack of the said half lands for 19 years for the yearly rent of 36 merks etc. Dated at Dundee 17 November 1556. [http
2 CONC s://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f794&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrimgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1584&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderb
2 CONC urn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/794]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
