2 CONT '''2 March 1541: Certified copy of Charter. Dated the 2d March 1541, of the Lands and Barony of Duddop etc. in favor of James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee in liferent and John Scrymgeour of Glastre in fee, and the heirs-male of 
2 CONC his body; whom failing John Scrymgeour, Grandson to the said James, procreate betwixt James Scrymgeour formerly of Kirktoun and Elizabeth Scrymgeour, daughter of the said James the Constable, or any other heirs-male lawfully procr
2 CONC eated or to be procreated betwixt the said James and Elizabeth, Whom failing James Scrymgeour Fiar of Fardle, James Scrymgeour of Fordie, James Scrymgeour of Gond, and John Scrymgeour of Myres seriatim, and the heirs-male of their
2 CONC  bodies respective; whom failing the lawful and nearest heirs-male of the blood and name of Scrymgeour carrying its arms; whom all failing the lawful and nearest heirs whatsoever of the said James, with a reservation to the terce 
2 CONC of the Constable's present or any future wife, and a clause of return to the heirs-male of the Constable's body if any should be thereafter procreated for the safer preservation of the house of the said James. [https://catalogue.n
