2 CONT
2 CONT                     26
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1590: The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Agnes Bruce, the "guid wyff of Kirktoun," who died on 2 July 1590. She made her last will and testament five days earlier, on 28 June 1590, at the Kirkton of Mains in the
2 CONC  Sheriffdom of Forfar. She nominated and appointed her eldest son, John Scrymgeour, to be her executor testamentar and the sole intromitter with her moveable estate. She left sixty-six pounds, thirteen shillings, and four pence, t
2 CONC o be divided equally between Gilbert Scrymgeour, George Scrymgeour, Margaret Scrymgeour, Issobell Scrymgeour, and Geills Scrymgeour, identified by her as her lawful bairnes. Confirmation was granted to John Scrymgeor on 23 Decembe
2 CONC r 1595. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Agnes Bruce, relict of John Scrymgeour of Kirktoun, Sheriffdom of Forfar, reference CC8/8/28]'''
