2 CONT '''8 June 1565: Precept of Sasine by John Scrymgeour constable of Dundee, Lord of Dudop, and superior of the lands undernoted, directed to Patrick Gray of Ballegerno etc. for infefting John Scrymgeour, son and heir of the late Eli
2 CONC zabeth Scrymgeour, elder daughter and one of the heirs of line of the late James Scrymgeour, constable of Dundee, of the lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradichty, in excambion for the said John's part of the lands, mills and annualrent
2 CONC s of the barony of Stricmartyn, and of the lands of Ethibeton, and for resignation of the Mains of Ballegerno, Drumy and West Newton in the barony of Ballegerno, in favour of the granter: the said lands of Kirktoun of Erlistradich
2 CONC ty to hold to the said John Scrymgeour and the heirs male of his body, and to his brothers James, William, Thomas, and Alexander, and the heirs male of their bodies successively and respectively, in virtue of Contract between the 
2 CONC late James Scrymgeour constable of Dundee, and the late Elizabeth his daughter and James Scrymgeour her spouse, of date 21 October 1539; and of Contract between the late John Scrymgeour, constable of Dundee, father of the granter,
2 CONC  and John Scrymgeour aforesaid, son and heir of said Elizabeth, of date at Edinburgh 30th March 1555, recorded in the books of the Lords of Council, etc. Dated at Dundee 8 June 1565. Witnesses, Andrew Ventoun of Strikmertein, Patr
2 CONC ick Gray of Ballegerno, George Creichtoun of Cumpray, James Scrymgeour of Glaswell. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f733&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=
2 CONC &ro=s&df=1500&dt=1566&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/733]'''
