1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARIOT STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mariot Stewart. here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/James-Scrymgeour-of-Dudhope-Constable-of-Dundee/6000000009618105527?through=6000000009618029483 They were divorced before 30 May 1524. [https://catalogue.nrscotl
2 CONC and.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f783&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n NRS: GD137/783]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1500: Copy instrument of sasine in favour of Marion Stewart lately spouse of James Scrymgeour, Constable of Dundee, of the lands of Balrudry in Forfar. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.
2 CONC aspx?reference=GD137%2f1A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/1A]''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 May 1524: Charter. Robert Maule of Panmure of the lands of Balrudery in favor of Mariot Stewart formerly wife of James Scrymgeour Constable of Dundee in liferent and Elizabeth and Agnes Scrymgeours their two daughters in fee
2 CONC , proceeding on the resignation of the said James Scrymgeour in favor of James Learthmonth of Dairsy Provost of St. Andrews as a mid person betwixt the said James Scrymgeour and an Honorable woman the said Mariot Stewart formerly 
2 CONC wife of the said James, before the pronunciation or promulgation of the sentence of Divorce betwixt them and upon the resignation of the said James Learmonth in favors of the said Mariot Stewart as is more fully contained in a Con
2 CONC tract betwixt the said James and Mariot. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f783&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/783]''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1525: Sasine of an annuity by James Scrymgeour of Duddop in favor of Marion Stewart formerly (olim) his spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f782&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+scrymgeour&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1500&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/782]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 January 1525: Instrument of Sasine following GD137/784 in favor of the said Mariot Stewart and Elizabeth and Agnes Scrymgeours. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f785&st=1&
2 CONC tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mariot+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/785]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1527-28: Notarial instrument on the appeal by Sir William Thomson, chaplain, and Marion Stewart, some time spouse of a noble man James Scrymgeour, constable of Dundee, as aggrieved by a venerable and distinguished ma
2 CONC n, Mr. Thomas Cowttis, canon of the Chapel Royal of Stirling, as official of St. Andrews within the archdeanery of of Lothian, by a sentence of excommunication pronounced by him against Janet Birkiston, spouse of John Lumbitter, b
2 CONC ecause of her unjustly detaining a gown which belonged to the said Marion Stewart; but which she had now confessed, and the appellants had moved for her absolution, which the said Mr Thomas would not grant, and therefore they appe
2 CONC al to the official of St. Andrews. Done in the collegiate Church of St. Giles, of Edinburgh, about the 10th hour before noon of 31st January 1527-8. Witnesses, James Stewart, John Bonar, and Mr. James Carmur. The notary is John Ca
2 CONC irns. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f728&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedder
2 CONC burn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/728]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1533: Precept of Clare Constat for infefting Agnes Scrymgeour in the lands of Balruthrie as heir to Mariot Stewart her mother. 25 April 1533. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referen
2 CONC ce=GD137%2f1475&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mariot+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/71475]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1533: Precept of clare constat by Robert Mawill of Panmur in favour of Agnes Scrimgeour, as one of the heirs of Marion Stewart, her mother, in one half of the lands of Balrudrye. Witnesses:- Hugh Liddall, John Murray, 
2 CONC Andrew Gray, John Dikestoun, Andrew Cwik, sir William Smyth and Mr. David Robertson, notaries public. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f577&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion
2 CONC +stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/577]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 May 1533: Notarial Minutes of Sasine given to Elizabeth and Agnes Scrymgeours as heirs to their Mother, Margaret (also called Marion) Stewart, of the lands of Balrudrie in the Barony of Panmure and shire of Forfar. [https://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f864&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderb
2 CONC urn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/7864]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
