2 CONT
2 CONT David Bruce, 7th of Clackmannan1
2 CONT M, #185119, d. after 1556
2 CONT Last Edited=25 Jan 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Bruce, 7th of Clackmannan was the son of Sir David Bruce, 6th of Clackmannan and Mariot Herries.2 He married Janet Blackadder, daughter of Sir Patrick Blackadder of Tulliallan.2 He died after 1556.3
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Clackmannan, Clackmannanshire, ScotlandG.4 In 1497 Clackmannan was settled on him by his father.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir David Bruce, 7th of Clackmannan and Janet Blackadder
2 CONT #Marion Bruce1
2 CONT #Alison Bruce+2
2 CONT #John Bruce, younger of Clackmannan+2 d. b 14 Feb 1550
2 CONT #Robert Bruce+2
2 CONT #David Bruce+2
2 CONT #Patrick Bruce2
2 CONT #Elizabeth Bruce+2
2 CONT #Agnes Bruce2
2 CONT #Sir Edward Bruce of Blairhall+2 b. 1505, d. 1565
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations [S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 547. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] [S37] BP2003. [S37] [S6286] Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy, online http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealog
2 CONC y.info. Hereinafter cited as Clan MacFarlane. [S8] BP1999 volume 1, page 174. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT
2 CONT * The Scots peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom Author Paul, James Balfour, Sir, 1846-1931 Page 471. [https
2 CONC ://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft#page/473/mode/1up/search/%22James+Shaw%22 Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==From the [https://archive.org/stream/collectionstowar1868clac/collectionstowar1868clac_djvu.txt2 Charters of Clackmannan]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28th August, 1485'''— Charter by David Bruce of Clackmannan to Robert Bruce, his son and apparent heir, and Elizabeth Lindsay, his wife, in liferent, and the heirs male, to be procreated between them, in fee of the six oxgates 
2 CONC of land pertaining to the said David Bruce of  his lands of Rate, on the east side of the burn, and lying in the Barony of Rate and county of Perth. To be holden by the said Robert Bruce and his heirs aforesaid, whom failing his h
2 CONC eirs, whatsoever of the King and his successors, for payment of a penny on the ground of the said lands, in manner of blench, if asked. Witnesses : Robert Bruce of Culmaluindie and Thomas Bruce, and others. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14rh Septr., 1497'''— Crown Charter 
2 CONT of Resignation by King James IV., to David Bruce, son of David Bruce of Clackmannan* of the lands and Barony of Clackmannan, lying in the County thereof, and lands of Rate, lying in the county of Perth, proceeding on the resignati
2 CONC on of the said David Bruce, elder. To be holden by the King and his successors, under the burden of the liferent of the said David Bruce, elder, and Margeret Harries, his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3d February, 1506'''— Crown Charter  by King James IV., to David Bruce, grandson and heir of the said deceased David Bruce of Clackmannan, to be holden by the said David Bruce, younger, of the King and his successors, in fee an
2 CONC d heritage, for rendering of services used and wont.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3d February, 1506'''— Charter under the Great Seal, to David Bruce, nepoti, and heir of David Bruce of Clackmannan, of the lands of Rate, &c. (Reg. of Great Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5th February, 1506'''— Crown Charter by King James IV. to David Bruce, knight, son of the deceased David Bruce of Clackmannan, of the lands of Ilallhill over and nether and Barony of Clackmannan, and others, now erected into a 
2 CONC Barony, to be called in all time coming the Barony of Clackmannan. To be holden by the said David Bruce and the heirs male, procreated between him and Janet Blackadder, his wife, whom failing, his nearest and lawful heirs whatsoev
2 CONC er, bearing the name and arms of Bruce, whom all failing, to revert to the King and his successors, according to the ancient Charters of Taillie of the said Barony in favour of the said ancestors of the said David Bruce for servic
2 CONC es used and wont.....
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest son of David of Clackmannan was, in 1485, Robert Bruce, to whom apparently, on his marriage, old David Bruce granted part of the Barony of Rate..
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Bruce, the eldest son of old David Bruce of Clackmannan (see No. 22), had died before his father, leaving this son David, who must have been at this time very young, and who, in 1506, was probably about twenty-one years of 
2 CONC age. In 1497 (see No. 26), this child's uncle, with the consent securingly of the child's grandfather, who was then in possession, got a Charter from King James IV., which was ratified in 1506. (See No. 28.)...
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas, in his history of the Bruces, says that David Bruce, son of Robert,, and grandson and heir-male of old David Bruce of Clackmannan, who was alive in 1497, resigned all his right to Clackmannan in favour of his uncle David,
2 CONC  brother of Robert Bruce, and younger son of old David Bruce. This statement is quite consistent with the Charters Nos. 26, 27, and 28, because David Bruce, the uncle, would not have any right to the estate as heir, so long as mal
2 CONC e-heirs of Robert existed, and the fact that the Charter No. 27 was granted to Robert's son David, as heir to his grandfather, on 3d February, 1506, shows that he was living when the King consented to grant this Charter, No. 28, t
2 CONC o his uncle, and that he must have acquiesced in his uncle's obtaining the grant. Douglas adds, that the male line is extinct, but he gives no authority for this, and it is clear that if any descendants of David Bruce, the son of 
2 CONC Robert, exist (probably in Perthshire), as suggested in the " History of the Bruces," (" History of Noble British Families, Part III.,") they are the representatives of the original Bruces of Clackmannan. The Barony of Rate, in Pe
2 CONC rthshire, does not appear to have been conveyed along with the Barony of Clackmannan, and David, the younger, may have settled there.  But Rate soon afterwards was possessed by the Bruces of Clackmannan.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------
