1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MASTER EDWARD BRUCE OF BALAIRHALL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master Edward Bruce of Blaihall, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=6000000003615931244 He is identified as: "magrm Edward Bruce filio Da
2 CONC vid Bruce de Clakman militis" in a charter in his favour which was issued by James V, King of Scots, on 20 July 1533. [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9494/94948513.23.pdf Collections towards a History of the County of Clackmannan, cha
2 CONC rter number 41 on page 15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Wife==
2 CONT Alison or Cristina Reid See [https://www.geni.com/discussions/271622?msg=1661551 Discussion]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Robert, succeeded his father in Blairhall, and was ancestor of the Bruces of Blairhall, and the Bruces, Baronets of Kinross and Balcaskie. Both these families are extinct in the male line.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Edward, first Lord Bruce of Kinloss, of whom presently .
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sir George, of Carnock, ancestor of the Earls of Elgin and Kincardine. (See next article.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. William, of Cothill and Collestoune, in Aberdeenshire. He is said to have been first a priest4 in Kinloss Abbey, but signs as a witness various documents connected with Kinloss as ' brother - german and factor to my Lord Abbot 
2 CONC of Kinloss.' He died s. p. before 24 May 1609, on which date his nephew Edward Bruce, afterwards second Lord Bruce of Kinloss,5 was served heir to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Bessie,1 married David Bar.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03paul/page/474/mode/1up?view=theater&q=blairhall p474
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
