2 CONT >>>>[https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=303629351820005598 Sir  David  Bruce],  eldest  son  of  the  second  marriage, succeeded  his  father  in  Clackmannan,  to  th
2 CONC e  exclusion  of his  elder  half-brother  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136940?through=303629351820005598 Robert]  and  his  son  [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-of-Rait/60000000031461369
2 CONC 55?through=6000000003146136940 David].  On  11 September  1497  he  had  a  Crown  charter of  Clackmannan, subject   to   his   father's  liferent  and   that   of   his   mother [https://www.geni.com/people/Mariot-Herries/600000
2 CONC 0001806317482?through=6000000003435018681 Mariota  Herries].  On  3  February  1506-7  he  had  a  Crown charter erecting  Clackmannan,  with  other  lands,  into  a barony,  when  he  is  styled  '  David  Bruis  de  Clackmannan 
2 CONC miles,  Alius  quondam  David  Bruce  de  Clackmannan,'  his nephew,  [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-of-Rait/6000000003146136955?through=6000000003146136940 David  Bruce  of  Rait],  having  resigned  any  interest he  m
2 CONC ight  have  in  it.  The  estate  must  have  been  a  very large  one,  from  the  enumeration  of  the  lands  incorporated in  the  barony.  He  had  a  licence  to  hold  a  fair  at  Clackmannan on  the  Feast  of  St.  Barth
2 CONC olomew  annually,  18  April 1517,  which  was  confirmed 18  September  1542.  Sir  David  was on  an  assize 1  December  1554,  On  21  January  1550-51  he gave  a  charter   to  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-8th-B
2 CONC ar-of-Clackmanan/6000000003146148174  Robert  Bruce],  his  grandson  and  apparent heir,  and  [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Livingston/6000000011335665999?through=6000000003146148174 Janet  Levingstone],  his  wife,  of  an
2 CONC   annualrent  of forty  merks,  and  was  alive  12  June  1556,  when  he  gave a  precept  of  sasine  for  infefting  Robert  Bruce,  brother- german  of  the  deceased  Mr.  John  Bruce,  in  the  lands  of Wester  Kennet.  [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-Bruce-7th-Baron-Of-Clackmannan/6000000003435018681?through=303610207620004050 Sir  David]  married  [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Bruce-Baroness-of-O-Lack/303610207620004050?through=600000
2 CONC 0003435018681 Jean],  daughter  of  [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Patrick-Blackadder-of-Tulliallan/303623670910007050?through=303610207620004050 Sir Patrick  Blacadder  of  Tulliallan],  by  whom  he  had  issue  five sons  and
2 CONC   four  daughters,  viz. : —
2 CONT >>>>>1.[https://www.geni.com/people/John-Bruce-of-Clackmannan/6000000003146136970?through=6000000003435018681 John],  died  vita  patris  before  14  February  1550-51,  but carried  on  the  line  of  the  Clackmannan  family,  w
2 CONC hich became  extinct  in  the  male  line  on  the  death,  8  July 1772,  of  Henry  Bruce,  fifteenth  and  last  Baron.
2 CONT >>>>>2.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Edward-Bruce-of-Blairhall-and-Easter-Kennet/6000000003615931244?through=6000000003435018681 Edward,  of  Blairhall]  born  1505,   had  a  charter  of  the  lands  of Easter  Kennet,  1537
2 CONC ,  on  the  resignation  of  Robert  Brady. This  charter  was  confirmed11  by  James  v.  24  April  1537. He  had  also  a  charter 12  from  the  Abbot  of  Culross  7  June 1540,  confirmed  15  February  1542-43,  of  the  l
2 CONC ands  of  Bergady and  two  parts  of  the  Shire  mills
2 CONT >>>>>3. [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Bruce-III/6000000003435071438?through=6000000003435018681 David,  of  Green].    He  was  ancestor  of  the  Bruces  of Kennet,  Lords  Balfour  of  Burleigh.  (See  vol.  i. p.  547.)
2 CONT >>>>>4.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Lynmiln/6000000180661927996?through=6000000003435018681 Robert,  of  Lynmylne.]    The  Swedish  Bruces  ennobled in  1668  were  probably  descended  from  him.
2 CONT >>>>>5.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Bruce-of-Valleyfield/6000000014194986036 Patrick,  of  Valleyfield].    He  had  a  charter  of  Valley-field  from  the  Commendator  of  Culross,  8  June  1540,  to himself  and  Ma
2 CONC rgaret  Falconer,  his  wife,  which  was confirmed7  15  February  1542-43.  In  this  confirmation charter  he  is  called  son  of  Sir  David  Bruce  of Clackmannan,  Knight.  He  is  said  to  have  resigned the  lands  and  
2 CONC barony  of  Valleyfield  to  James  Preston of   Craigmillar,  and  to  have  died   s.  p.,  leaving  the estate  of  Green  to  his  brother  David  ;  but,  on  the other  hand,  David  appears  as  a  witness  to  a  charter u
2 CONC nder  the  designation  'of  '  de  Greyne,'  30  January 1536-37.  He  is  also  a  witness   to  a  precept  of  sasine 6  November  1536,  and  in  an  ancient  MS.  pedigree, endorsed  1640,  Patrick  is  styled   of  Valleyfi
2 CONC eld,'  and David  is  called  '  of  Greyne.'  It  would,  on  the  whole, seem  that  Patrick  never  possessed  Green,  but  only Valleyfield.
2 CONT >>>>>6.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Bruce/6000000009380158593?through=6000000003146136970 Elizabeth],  married,  first,  to  Alexander  Dundas  of  Fingask ;   they  had  a  charter  of  Cottis, 8  August 1542.  She  w
2 CONC as  married,  secondly,  to  Robert  Oolless of  Bonneymoon.
2 CONT >>>>>7. ''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Marion-Bruce/6000000193466079848 Marion],  married Robert  Bruce  of  Airth  ; and    Magnus  Sinclair  of  Kynninmonth, second  son 7  of  William,  Lord  Sinclair.  She  died  July 1575; 
2 CONC  will  dated  at  Dysart  18  June  1575,  confirmed 11  August  1575.8'''
2 CONT >>>>>8.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Bruce/6000000003645966321?through=6000000009380158593 Agnes],  married  to  John  Elphinstone,  parson  of  Invernochty,  with  issue.
2 CONT >>>>>9.  [https://www.geni.com/people/Alison-Colville/303609872980008284?through=6000000003645966321  Alison],  married   to  Sir  James   Oolville  of   Ochiltree, circa  1530.  They  had  a  charter  of  East  Wemyss 20  August 
2 CONC  1533.
2 CONT
