2 CONT '''Margaret Maitland, here treated, is the daughter of William Maitland of Thirlestane. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/edmonstone1.php Stirnet 1: Edmonstone]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Maitland, here treated, married John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: 2333]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1496: Apud Edinburgh, 31 Jul.  REX concessit JACOBO EDMONDSTOUN (filio Johannis E.) de eodem — terras et baroniam de Ednem, molendinum de E., unam tenandriam de E., unacum advocatione et donatione hospitalis de E., vic.
2 CONC  Roxburgh ; terras de Riselaw, vic. Berwic; tertiam partem terrarum de Hirdmanstoun, Gurre, et Nudremerschall, cum tenandria et molendino earundem, vic, Edinburgh ; — quequidem fuerunt dicti Johannis, et tertia pars de Nudremersch
2 CONC all cum molendino, &c., ejusdem fuit dicti Joh. et MARGARETE MATELAND ejus sponse in conjuncta infeodatione, et quas terras et tertiam partem terrarum dicti Joh. et Merg. respective resignaverunt : — Tenend. dicto Jac. et heredibu
2 CONC s masculis ejus de corpora legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, David E. ejus fratri et heredibus, &c., (id supra), quibus def., "Willelmo E. fratri ejusdem, et heredibus, &c. (id supra), quibus def., legitimis et propinquio
2 CONC ribus heredibus masculis dicti Jon. cognomen et arma do Edmonstoun gerentibus quibuscumiuo : — RESERVATIS. pro Ednem unum duiiarium argeiiti nomine albe firme ; pro ceteris terris, &c., wardns, &c., cum contigerint : — RESERVATIS 
