2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam. is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000007980971015?through=6000000176833987821 [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/
2 CONC n261/mode/1up RPS 1488-1529: entry number 1626]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam died before 7 March 1508. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n261/mode/1up RPS 1488-1529: entry number 1626]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam. here treated, married Isobell Hume. According to Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet: "In 1499 there is a solemn transaction whereby John Edmondstoune of that Ilk promises that 
2 CONC he will not sell nor put away any more of his lands from John, his son and heir, and the heirs of the said John's marriage with Isabel Home". [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/93/mode/1up Duntreath: 93]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 March 1507-08: At Edinburgh, 7 Mar. A lettre made to PATRIK HUME of Fastcastel and his assignais, ane or maa, — of the gift of al malis, fermes, proffitis and dewiteis of al and hale the xl merkis worth of land, with the pert
2 CONC inentis, liand in the toun of Ednam within the schirefdome of Roxburgh, quhilkis war umquhile John Edmonstoun and Isobell Hume, his spous, in conjunct feftment, of al termes bigain that the said landis has bene in the kingis handi
2 CONC s sen thare decess, throw nonentre . . . and of al termes tocum quhil the richtwis ayrre or ayris thairof be lauchfully enterit thairto Per Signaturam subscriptam per Regem. Gratis. iii. 158. [https://archive.org/details/registrum
2 CONC secret00scotgoog/page/n261/mode/1up RPS 1488-1529: entry number 1626]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1513: Nonentre. Landis of Edine, etc. EDMONSTOUN. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n261/mode/1up RPS 1488-1529: entry number 2516]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
