1 NAME James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 11 JUN 1519
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES EDMONSTONE OF THAT ILK AND EDNAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176590641821?through=6000000041815356824 On 31 July 1496 he had a charter under the Gr
2 CONC eat Seal of Scotland which confirmed his possession of the lands of Ednam in the sheriffdom of Roxburgh, the lands of Riselaw in the sheriffdom of Berwick, and a third part of the lands of Hirdmanstoun, Gurre, et Nudremerschall, i
2 CONC n the sheriffdom of Edinburgh. His father https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176590641821?through=6000000041815356824 and his wife Margaret Maitland had previously held these lands in conjunct
2 CONC  fee and liferent, but each of them resigned their respective interests in favour of James. Thereafter, the land was to pass to James's lawful male heirs, whom failing to his brother David, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing 
2 CONC to his brother William, and his male heirs, whom failing by the nearest heirs whatsoever of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Edmonstone-of-that-Ilk-and-Ednam/6000000176590641821?through=6000000041815356824 bearing the name and arm
2 CONC s of Edmonstone. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: 2333]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, died before 11 June 1519, when the Exchequer Rolls of Scotland note that https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Home/6000000041815018396?through=6000000041815356824 , his wid
2 CONC ow, holds a ten merk land of Ryislaw in conjunct fee. [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/623/mode/1up Exchequer Rolls, 1513-22: p. 623]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, "It seems likely that Sir James fell with his superior, Alexander, Archbishop of St. Andrews (natural son of James the Fourth, a very young man), at the battle of Flo
2 CONC dden, for, as the battle occurred in September 1513, in February 1513 (which would now be 1514, as the year was then calculated as commencing in March), there is a precept of saisin, dated Dumferline, stating that John was the son
2 CONC  and heir of James, who had died in possession of the lands of Edmonstone." [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/93/mode/1up Duntreath: 93]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Edmonstone of that Ilk and Ednam, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Home/6000000041815018396?through=6000000041815356824 They are noticed as man and wife on 24 November 1496. [https://archive.org
2 CONC /details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/495/mode/1up RMS  1424-1513: 2334]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1496: Apud Edinburgh, 31 Jul.  REX concessit JACOBO EDMONDSTOUN (filio Johannis E.) de eodem — terras et baroniam de Ednem, molendinum de E., unam tenandriam de E., unacum advocatione et donatione hospitalis de E., vic.
2 CONC  Roxburgh ; terras de Riselaw, vic. Berwic; tertiam partem terrarum de Hirdmanstoun, Gurre, et Nudremerschall, cum tenandria et molendino earundem, vic, Edinburgh ; — quequidem fuerunt dicti Johannis, et tertia pars de Nudremersch
2 CONC all cum molendino, &c., ejusdem fuit dicti Joh. et Margarete Mateland ejus sponse in conjuncta infeodatione, et quas terras et tertiam partem terrarum dicti Joh. et Merg. respective resignaverunt : — Tenend. dicto Jac. et heredibu
2 CONC s masculis ejus de corpora legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, David E. ejus fratri et heredibus, &c., (id supra), quibus def., "Willelmo E. fratri ejusdem, et heredibus, &c. (id supra), quibus def., legitimis et propinquio
2 CONC ribus heredibus masculis dicti Jon. cognomen et arma do Edmonstoun gerentibus quibuscumiuo : — RESERVATIS. pro Ednem unum duiiarium argeiiti nomine albe firme ; pro ceteris terris, &c., wardns, &c., cum contigerint : — RESERVATIS 
2 CONC libero tenemento dicto Jon. ac rationabili tertia ejus spouse cuicunque cum contigerit :— Test. 30. 31. 32. 42. 26. 84. 20. 37. 40. xiii. 225. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/492/mode/1up Registrum Magni S
2 CONC igilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advocate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 2333]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 November 1496: REX concessit JACOBO EDMONSTOUN filio et heredi apparenti Johannis E. de eodem, et KATRINE HUME sponse dicti Jac, — terras 20 mere, terrarum de Edname, viz. 40 sol. terrarum per Joh. Leremonth tunc oecupatas, 
2 CONC 40 sol. terr. per Rob. Pilmuro commorantem apud le Kirkstile occupat., 5 mere. terr. per Rob. Pilmure in le Clayhole et Tho. Belwort occupat., 5 mere, terr. per Wil. Diksoun et Wil. Hiltstoun occupat., 20 sol. per Tho. Weddell occ
2 CONC upat., 20 sol. per Rob. Belwort occupat., et mercatam terr. per Wil. Trewnot occupat., in baronia de Edname, vic. Roxburgh ; necnon 20 mere, terrarum de Riselaw, viz. 6 mere, per Arch. Trotare tunc occupat., 5 mere, per Alex. Trot
2 CONC are occupat.,6 mere, per Jac. Hirdmonstoun occupat., et 3 merc, per Ricardum Tranent occupat, vic Beruic; -quarum feodum idem Jac, et liberum tenementum dictus Jon. personaliter resignaverunt : — Tenend. dictis Jac. et Kat. et eor
2 CONC um alteri diutius viventi in conjuncta infeodatione, et heredibus masculis inter ipsos legitime procreatis, quibus deficientibus, legitimis et propinquioribus heredibus masculis dicti Jac. quibuseunque :— Test. 30. 32. 42. 84. 20.
2 CONC  40. 38. 36, xiii. 612.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/495/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, Advoc
2 CONC ate, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), charter number 2334]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Exchequer Rolls of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 June 1519: Vicecomes respondebit pro 36 li. 13 s. 4 d. de firmis terrarum de Ryislaw cum tenen. etc. cum pertinen. jacentium infra balliam suam, exceptis Beruik - 40 marcatis dictarum terrarum alienatis Ade Hume, filio quond
2 CONC am Patricii Hume de Fastcastell, et 10 marcatis earundem terrarum quas Katherina Hume, sponsa quondam Jacobi Edmonstoun, habet in conjuncta infeodatione, existentium in manibus regis per spatium 5 annorum et 1 termini ult. elaps. 
2 CONC sasina non recuperata, et pro 6 ft. 13 s. 4 d. de relevio earundem, regi debitis per sasinam datam Johanni Edmonstoun de eisdem apud Edinburgh 11 Junii a.r.6 [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollsof14scot/page/623/mode/1up Ex
2 CONC chequer Rolls of Scotland, 1513-22: p. 623]'''
2 CONT
