2 TITL Internet Archive: The House of Argyll and the collateral branches of the clan Campbell, from the year 420 to the present time. 
1 NOTE Created First Earl of Argyle in 1457. Moved from Loch Awe and founded the
2 CONT burgh of Inverary by Loch Fyne in 1474. Was Master of the Royal Household
2 CONT in 1464 and eventually became Lord Chancellor of Scotland.
1 NOTE 1ST EARL OF ARGYLL
1 NOTE He was the 2nd Lord Campbell and created 1st Earl Argyll in 1457. He was appointed Master of the King's Household in 1464 and eventually made Lord High Chancellor of Scotland in 1483. He became Lord Lorne by charter on 17 Apr 1470
2 CONC . The galley of Lorne has ever since formed part of the family achievement. He was ancestor to the Campbells of Glenurchy, now Marquesses of Brendalbane.
