2 CONT John Fleming, 2nd Lord Fleming (c. 1465 – 1 November 1524) was a Scottish nobleman.
2 CONT He was the son of '''Malcolm Fleming, 1st Lord Fleming, and Euphame Livingstone''', a daughter of James Livingston, 1st Lord Livingston. He was assassinated by John Tweedie of Drumelzier, and his followers, while hawking.
2 CONT His son was Malcolm Fleming, 3rd Lord Fleming.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Fleming,_2nd_Lord_Fleming
2 CONT _______
2 CONT James Livingston, 1st Lord Livingston (c. 1410 – 1467) was a Scottish nobleman.
2 CONT Early life
2 CONT Livingston was born at Callendar House in Scotland around 1410. He was the son and heir of Sir Alexander Livingston of Callendar.[1] His sister, Janet Livingston, was married to James Hamilton of Cadzow. His father was Justiciar o
2 CONC f Scotland, and keeper of Stirling Castle who is known for conspiring with Lord William Crichton in the assassination of the 6th Earl of Douglas and his brother, David, at the "Black Dinner" at Edinburgh Castle.[2]
2 CONT His mother was a daughter of James Dundas of Dundas,[3] and his paternal grandparents were Sir John Livingston of Callendar and his wife, a daughter of Sir John Menteith of Kerse.[2] Through his sister, he was uncle to James Hamil
2 CONC ton, 1st Lord Hamilton, Alexander Hamilton (the ancestor of the Hamiltons of Silvertonhill), and Gavin Hamilton (ancestor of the Hamiltons of Dalzell).[2]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Livingston was married to Marian (née de Berwick) Oliphant (c. 1410–1478), the daughter of Thomas de Berwick and widow of Sir William Oliphant of Aberdalgie. Together, they were the parents of:[1]
2 CONT *James Livingston, 2nd Lord Livingston (1430–1497), who died unmarried.[1]
2 CONT *Alexander Livingston (d. 1472).[1]
2 CONT *Rev. David Livingston, who became rector of Ayr, Provost of Lincluden, and Keeper of the Privy Seal of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT *Elizabeth Livingston, who married John Macdonald, 11th Earl of Ross.[6]
2 CONT *'''Eupheme Livingston''' (c. 1445–1493), '''who married Malcolm Fleming, Master of Fleming (c. 1444–1477), eldest son and heir apparent''' of Robert Fleming, 1st Lord Fleming.[7]
2 CONT *Marion Livingston, who married William Crichton, 3rd Lord Crichton.[8]
2 CONT Livingston died sometime between 26 April and 7 November 1467.[1] His widow died sometime between 4 June and 19 October 1478.[3]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Livingston,_1st_Lord_Livingston
