1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan,_Earl_of_Menteith
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan, Earl of Menteith married Marjory or Margery, who has been shown to have been a daughter of Colbán, Earl of Fife by his wife Anne Durward.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had two sons, one of whom,
2 CONT *Alan, succeeded his father as Earl when a minor.[4].  This 2nd Alan was the father of Mary, who married Sir John Graham.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colb%C3%A1n,_Earl_of_Fife
2 CONT
2 CONT Colbán, Earl of Fife
2 CONT
2 CONT Mormaer Colbán of Fife ruled Fife, 1266 – 1270/2. He was probably the son of Maol Choluim II. (Malcolm II of Fife) Not much is known about his life and reign. Colbán's death is disputed, and depends on what evidence one interprets
2 CONC . G.W.S. Barrow gives 1272, but Bannerman gives 1270. He married Anna, the daughter of Alan Durward, with whom he fathered a son Donnchadh III of Fife and a daughter Margery, wife of Alan, Earl of Menteith.[1] The latter succeeded
2 CONC  him upon his death.
2 CONT
