1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander, Earl of Menteith, married a lady named Matilda, and had issue - 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan, Earl of Menteith (d. c. 1310) was, as his title suggests, Earl of Menteith.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan,_Earl_of_Menteith
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father and was succeeded by his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT He supported King Robert I of Scotland (Bruce) in his initial attempt to seize power. He was captured at the Battle of Methven and died in an English dungeon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Joined Robert Bruce in his claim to the throne of Scotland, and was captured by the English in 1306 and he died still in custody before 1330.
2 CONT
2 CONT The successful termination of the War of Independence at the battle of Bannockburn restored the earldom to the Stewarts, and it was reunited under the younger son of Alexander, Murdach, the eighth Earl, who enjoyed the title after
2 CONC  the death of his brother Alan, the seventh Earl.  
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT Alan, Earl of Menteith married Marjory or Margery, who has been shown to have been a daughter of Colbán, Earl of Fife by his wife Anne Durward.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had two sons, one of whom, 
2 CONT *Alan, succeeded his father as Earl when a minor.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY%20LATER.htm#_Toc359672170 
2 CONT
2 CONT (misses Alan ll, son of this Alan)
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Alexander & his wife had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         ALAN de Menteith (-before 13 Mar 1309).  Hostage, with his younger brother Piers, for his father's fidelity to Edward I King of England in 1296.  The Wardrobe Accounts of King Edward I for 1296/97 include payments to "A
2 CONC lano et Petro filiis comitis de Menetethe", dated 23 Jul[91].  He succeeded his father as Earl of Menteith.  He supported Robert Bruce as King of Scotland in 1306[92].  m MARJORY, daughter of ---.  Earl Alan & his wife had one chi
2 CONC ld: ...
2 CONT
