1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From  http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I5794&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt-Gen. Sir John Wallace, 5th of Craigie, 10th of Riccarton (Abt 1400 - abt 1450)  married Margaret Johnstone b. Abt 1400, who survived him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children 
2 CONT *1.  Sir William Wallace, 6th of Craigie, 11th of Riccarton b. Abt 1421 married Margaret de Dunbar, heiress of Cockburn b. Abt 1423, Cockburn, Berwickshire, Scotland  d. Abt 1498
2 CONT *2. Thomas Wallace wife unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT John "The Hero Of Sark" Wallace, 5th of Craigie, 10th of Riccarton ( b abt 1400 d about 1450)
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n97/mode/2up/search/Hero+of+sark
2 CONT
2 CONT William Wallace of Craigie married Elizabeth, daughter of James, 7th Earl of Douglas, by his wife Beatrix, daughter of the Regent, Robert, Duke of Albany.  Of the union was born three sons, John, Hugh, and Adam; also a daughter Ma
2 CONC rgaret, who became the second wife of Robert, first Lord Lyle.  
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n101/mode/2up/search/Hero+of+sark
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Wallace hero of Sark left a widow and two sons, William and Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.douglashistory.co.uk/famgen/getperson.php?personID=I48536&tree=tree1
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William WALLACE 9th of Riccarton & 4th of Craigie (b. abt 1375) Married, Lady Elizabeth DOUGLAS
2 CONT
2 CONT Son
2 CONT * Lieutenant-General Sir John WALLACE 10th of Riccarton & 5th of Craigie  b. abt 1400. d. 1450, Craigie, Ayrshire, Scotland '''Married, Margaret JOHNSTONE ?. b. abt 1400''' (http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~vfarch/Genealogy-data/wc1
2 CONC 5/wc15_360.htm) (died of his wounds at the battle of Sark)
2 CONT
2 CONT Son
2 CONT * Sir William WALLACE 11th of Riccarton & 6th of Craigie 14 b. abt 1421 m. abt 1453, Craufurd, Lanarkshire, Scotland, Margaret DUNBAR br. b. abt 1423, Cockburn, Berwickshire, d. ca 1498  daughter of SirDavid DUNBAR of Cockburn (Sh
2 CONC e also married Alexander LINDSAY 4th Earl of Crawford). (http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~vfarch/Genealogy-data/wc15/wc15_359.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Wallace03
2 CONT *The Book of Wallace by Rev. Charles Rogers pub.1889
