2 CONT Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to navigationJump to search Matthew Stewart 2nd Earl of Lennox Born	1460 Died	9 September 1513 Flodden Noble family	Stewart of Darnley Spouse(s)	Margar
2 CONC et Lyle Elizabeth Hamilton Father	John Stewart, 1st Earl of Lennox Mother	Margaret Montgomerie Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox (1460 – 9 September 1513, was a prominent Scottish nobleman. Stewart was the son of John Stewart, 1
2 CONC st Earl of Lennox, and Margaret Montgomerie, daughter of Alexander Montgomerie, 1st Lord Montgomerie. He died fighting in the Battle of Flodden Field.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married firstly, on 13 June 1490, Margaret Lyle, daughter of Robert Lyle, Lord Lyle. On 9 April 1494, he married Elizabeth Hamilton, daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Lord Hamilton, and Mary Stewart, Princess of Scotland, daughte
2 CONC r of King James II of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stewart and Elizabeth Hamilton had six children: Mungo Stewart, Agnes Stewart, John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox, Margaret Stewart, Elizabeth Stewart, and Catherine Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Lord Provost of Glasgow in 1497, and from 1509–1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestors Ancestors of Matthew Stewart, 2nd Earl of Lennox Sources G. E. Cokayne et al., eds. The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct, or Dormant. Reprint ed. (Glo
2 CONC ucester, UK: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000).
2 CONT
