1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Patrick Buchanan,[74][75] (Guthrie Smith identifies him as 7th Chief and Buchanan of Auchmar identifies him as 14th Chief) married Jonet Cunningham of Galbraith and by her a son (Walter his successor) and a '''dau
2 CONC ghter (Anabella)'''. He also had an illegitimate son (Patrick).
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clan_Buchanan _______________________
2 CONT *'''The Buchanan book. The life of Alexander Buchanan, Q.C., of Montreal, followed by an account of the family of Buchanan (1911)
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/details/buchananbooklife00buchuoft
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/169/mode/1up
2 CONT *   XI. Sir Walter Buchanan, who, according to Auchmar, . . . . He lived to a great age, and had only one son, John, who married the heiress of Lenny, and died before his father. This John had three sons, (1) Sir Alexander Buchana
2 CONC n, who slew the Duke of Clarence at the battle of Bauge in 1420, and was himself slain at the battle of Vemeuil in the year 1424, being never married. (2) Sir Walter Buchanan, who succeeded to the
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/170/mode/1up
2 CONT *Estate of Buchanan, and (3) John of Ballachondachy, ancestor of the Buchanans of Lenny.
2 CONT *http://www.archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/179/mode/1up
2 CONT *   XII. Sir Walter Buchanan, married Isobel Stewart, daughter of Murdoch, Duke of Albany, and Governor of Scotland. He had three sons : —
2 CONT **                    (1) Patrick, his successor;
2 CONT **                    (2) Maurice, who was Treasurer to Princess Margaret, daughter to King James I. of Scotland, and wife of the Dauphin of France, afterwards Louis XL, and who accompanied her to France, and was present at her de
2 CONC ath in the year 1430. This Maurice Buchanan is supposed by Mr. W. F. Skene to be the author of the Liber Pluscardensis.
2 CONT **                    http://www.archive.org/stream/buchananbooklife00buchuoft#page/182/mode/1up
2 CONT **                    (3) Thomas Buchanan, ancestor of Carbeth.
2 CONT *   XIII. Patrick Buchanan, who married one Galbraith, heiress of Killearn, Bamoir and Auchinreoch, had (1) Walter, his successor, and (2) Thomas Buchanan, ancestor of Drummikill, and '''a daughter Anabella married to James Stewar
2 CONC t of Baldorrans. _________________________
2 CONT * 'Buchanan02'
2 CONT *Patrick Buchanan of that ilk, 13th of Buchanan (d before 07.1477)
2 CONT *m. Jonet Cunynghame
2 CONT *Patrick's wife if identified by BLG1962 as the daughter and heiress of Galbraith of Killearn, Balmois, etc.
2 CONT **1. Walter Buchanan of that ilk, 14th of Buchanan (d 1526)
2 CONT **   m. (before 26.11.1463) Isabelle Graham (dau of William Graham, 2nd Lord)
2 CONT **'''2. Annabella Buchanan
2 CONT **'''   m. James Stewart of Baldorrans
2 CONT *partner unknown
2 CONT **3. Patrick Buchanan
2 CONT *Main sources:
2 CONT *(1) "Strathendrick and its Inhabitants from Early Times" by John Guthrie Smith, published in Glasgow in 1896
2 CONT *(2) BLG1952 (Murray-Buchanan of Leny).
