1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''William Stewart of Balquidder and Baldoran''' was born circa 1455 in Balindoran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-26151673 James Beag Stewart 1st of Baldorran] and [https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/profile-34646077772 Annabella Buchanan]. He was a Baillie of Balquhidder. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34658951098 Janet Buchanan] on May 1, 1484. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34670548366 Janet Stewart of Lettir]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34658951145 Agnes Stewart]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34840426728 Mariote Stewart].  
2 CONT
2 CONT William married [https://www.geni.com/profile-68251360 Mariote Campbell] before October 5, 1498.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-120420167 John Stewart, 1st of Glenbuckie]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34670504702 Walter Stewart, 3rd of Baldorran]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34840428161 Elen Stewart].  
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1528 in Balquhidder, Stirlingshire, Scotland. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT \
2 CONT Sir William Stewart, 2nd of Baldorran, 1st of Lettir, and Royal Bailie of Balquhidder
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William STEWART , 2nd of Baldorran, 1st of Lettir, 1st Royal Bailie of Balquhidder b: ABT 1440 in Balindoran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.  Sir William Stewart seems to be the one most responsible for restoring his family
2 CONC  to prosperity.  His grandfather fled the country as a fugitive of the Crown.  His father was born illegitimately but was able to return to Scotland where he was given the lands of Baldorran.  But it appears to be Sir William who 
2 CONC significantly expanded the family holdings to include parts of Upper Strathgartney and eventually most of Balquhidder.  We note that when William's brothers were established in their estates each was styled as "brother of William 
2 CONC Stewart of Baldorran" rather than "son of James Stewart of Baldorran", suggesting that James was already dead and that William was the head of the family and likely responsible for establishing his younger brothers in their proper
2 CONC ties.  We note, significantly, that it was Sir William's younger brothers and sons who established all of the major cadet branches of Balquhidder (later Ardvorlich), Glenbuckie, Gartnafuaran, and Garchell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William inherited Baldorran sometime prior to his marriage, ca. 1484, and acquired the property of Lettir in Strathgartney by his marriage to Janet BUCHANAN, daughter of Archibald Buchanan of Lettir of Strongartney.  Sir Willi
2 CONC am is mentioned in a charter dated 1 MAY 1484: "Charter by Archibald Buchannane, laird of lands of Lettir, to William Stewart and Janet Buchannane, his spouse, granter's daughter, and specified heirs of lands of Lettir in lordship
2 CONC  of Strongartnay, sheriffdom of Perth." (GD112/1/18) (Strongartney is on Loch Katrine in Strathgartney and is shown as "Strone" in the lower left corner of the map below.)  The charter is followed on 17 MAY 1484 by an instrument o
2 CONC f sasine: "Instrument of sasine propriis manibus given by Walter Buchquhanan of Tomboy ("Tombuie"), bailie in that part, for Archibald Buchquhanane, his brother, infefting William Stewart of Baldorane and Jonet Buchquhanane, his s
2 CONC pouse, in lands of Lettir, following on [the preceding] charter." (GD112/1/19)  And on 4 JUL 1493, "Charter by William Stewart of Baldorane and of Letter to Jonet Stewart, daughter of granter and Jonet Buchquhannane, his spouse, a
2 CONC nd specified heirs, of lands of Le Letter, in lordship of Strogarthnaa in sheriffdom of Perth." (GD112/1/27)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Stewart was appointed Royal Baillie of the Crown lands of Balquhidder sometime between 1484-1488. William held the townships listed in the Exchequer Rolls of 1488 (listed below).  In the Exchequer Rolls of 1502-1515 Si
2 CONC r William and his eldest son, Walter, are confirmed as Crown tenants in the Balquhidder lands and the lands of Estir and Westir Duchraa (these lands were also known as Innerquhawawane and Glenmaan) and Blarbaith.  The location of 
2 CONC these lands has not been accurately identified, but they are described as forming "part of Glenfinglas" (Ardvorlich MSS).  It is believed that Glenmaan is the same as Glean nam Meann, which lands encompass the sheiling lands north
2 CONC  of Glenfinglas and south of Glenbuckie.  In the portioning of Balquhidder which took place during the sixteenth century, the descendants of Sir William Stewart of Baldorran gained hereditary tacks of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William held the Crown rentals for the following lands in Balquhidder, Strathyre and Glenfinglas.  According to The Settlements of Western Perthshire, these lands were all small baile settlements or farm communities.  There wa
2 CONC s nothing in Balquhidder at the time that would be as large as what we would think of as even a village today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Stewart married firstly before 1 MAY 1484 to Janet BUCHANAN, daughter of Archibald Buchanan of Lettir of Strongartney.  They had the following daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Has No Children Janet STEWART , of Lettir b: ABT 1475 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.  She was cited in a charter by William Stewart of Balindoran of the lands of Lettir in favour of Janet Stewart his daughte
2 CONC r on 4 July, 1493 (presumably as a marriage dowry).  She married presumably about 1493 to John KINROSS , of Kippenross.
2 CONT #     Has No Children Agnes STEWART b: ABT 1477 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William married secondly before 1498 to Marion Helen CAMPBELL, daughter of Colin Campbell, 1st of Glenorchy.  They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Walter STEWART , 3rd of Baldorran, 2nd Bailie of Balquhidder, b: ABT 1480 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.  His information is presented below.
2 CONT #     John STEWART , 1st of Glenbuckie b: ABT 1485 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.  See Glenbuckie Page.
2 CONT #     Mariote STEWART b: ABT 1490 in Baldorran, Campsie, Stirlingshire, Scotland.  Mariote's birth date and mother are uncertain.  She could be the daughter of William's first marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
