2 CONT '''5 August 1505: Attested copy special retour in favour of John Haldene [Haldane] of Glenegas [Gleneagles], kt., as heir of deceased James Haldene [Haldane] of Glenegas [Gleneagles], kt., his father, in half lands of Thome, half 
2 CONC lands of three Lanerkynnis [Lanrick], half 4 merkland of land of old called Conlathe, now called Schaquhythome with fishing of water of Tethe [River Teith] and half mill of Lanerk and its aquaduct, with half of lands of Rusky [Rus
2 CONC kie] and lands of Auchinreg, in stewartry of Menteth [Menteith], sheriffdom of Perth. Sheriff of Perth: William Edmonstone [Edmiston] of Duntreth [Duntreath], stewart of Menteth. Members of inquest; Alexander, earl of Menteth, Dun
2 CONC can Forrest of Gardoun [Garden], JJAMES EDMONSTONE [EDMISTON] OF BUCHQUHADROK, Walter Forrest of Torwod [Torwood], Robert More [Muir] of Boquhoppil [Boquhapple], Patrick Menteth [Menteith] of Ratho, Robert Balfour of Boquhoppil [B
2 CONC oquhapple], William Menteth [Menteith] of Gallecat, James Stewart of Garthael, John Kinlouch [Kinloch] of Broklands [Brooklands], James Dog [Doig] of Domrobyne, James Menteth [Monteith], Walter Laur, Patrick Stewart, Patrick Bouch
2 CONC quhanane [Buchanan] of Lane [Leny], Alexander Balfour and George Stewart. Copy attested by Thomas Miller, substitute for James Dundas, depute of James St. Clair Erskine, earl of Rosslyn, director of chancery. [http://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f69&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+edmonstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1550&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, re
2 CONC ference GD198/69]'''
2 CONT
