1 NAME Archibald /Edmonstone/ 3rd Laird of Duntreath
2 GIVN Archibald
2 SURN Edmonstone
2 NSFX 3rd Laird of Duntreath
2 _MARNM Edmonstone
1 NAME Sir Archibald Edmonstone, 3rd Laird of Duntreath
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 6 MAR 1502 AND 31 DEC 1502
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ARCHIBALD EDMONSTONE OF DUNTREATH, BARONET===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, is the eldest son of Sir William Edmonstone of Duntreath. He was served heir to his deceased father on 20 April 1487 [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/33/
2 CONC mode/1up Edmonstone of Duntreath, p. 33]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath appears still to have been alive on 6 March 1502, when his son William is identified as his father's son and apparent heir, but he is reported to have died in the same year. [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/35/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 May 1497: REX concessit WILLELMO EDMONSTOUN, filio et heredi apparenti Archibaldi E. de Duntreth, et SIBELLE BAILYE sponse dicti Wil., — terras de Gartbaroune, cum molendino earundom, in baronia de Duntreth, vie. Striveling 
2 CONC ; — quas dictus Arch, personaliter resignavit : — Tenend. dictis Wil. et Sib. et eorum alteri diutius viventi in conjiincta infeodatione et heredibus inter ipsos legitime procreatis, quibus delicientibus, legitimis et propinquiori
2 CONC hus heredibus dicti Arch. quibuscunque. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/502/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1424-1513, charter number 2357]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 March 1501-2: REX confirmavit cartam Hugonis dom. Montgumry, — [qua, pro dilectione filiali, &c., concessit filio suo et heredi apparenti JOHANNI MONTGUMRY, et ELIZABETHE EDMONSTOUN ejus sponse,— terras de Bonyntouu et Piltou
2 CONC n, vie. Edinburgh : — Tenend. dictis Joh. et Eliz., et eorum alteri diutius viventi, in vitalem redditum, et post eorum decessus sibi et propinquioribus heredibus suis maseulis reversuras, de rege : — Test. Joh. Montgumry de Corsc
2 CONC rag milite, Joh. Kennedy de Culzeane, Joh. Montgumry filio et herede apparente Geo. M. de Skelmorle, M. Adam Culquhone, WIL. EDMONSTOUN FILIO ET HEREDE APPARENTE ARCH. E. DE DUNTREITH MILITIS, Jac. Stewart de Garthell, et Job. Dog
2 CONC  : — Apud Edinburgh, 5 Mar. 1501. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/558/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A. D. 1424-1513, charter number 2626]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ====BOOK
2 CONT * '''McGregor, G. (2022)''' ''The Red Books of Scotland''. 4th ed., pp. 173-75. Glasgow, Scotland: University of & Glasgow Press. Available at: [https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/62525/2016 Ancestry.com]:—
2 CONT ** Sir Archibald Edmonstone, 3rd of Duntreath, succeeded his father and was served heir to him on 20 April 1487, and infeft in the lands of Duntreath and others, as his heir on 1 June following [4GD97/1/22]. He m. firstly, to Jane
2 CONC t, daughter of Sir James Schaw of Sauchie, with whom, on his own resignation, he had a charter under the Great Seal for the lands of Cambuswallace on 14 February 1491[C2/12/261. Printed Vol. 1424-1513. No. 2008], and secondly, bef
2 CONC ore 27 April 1498, to Janet Melville[Acta Dom Conc. Vol. ii pp. 176-77. Her mother is then referred to as Christian Balfour, wife of Alexander Inglis of Tarvit], and d. before 31 May 1503. He was father of:
2 CONT *** Sir William Edmonstone, 4th of Duntreath, (see below).
2 CONT ***  James Edmonstone, was infeft in the lands of Ardbechlorn and Derry, in the Earldom of Strathearn, on 26 June 1506, and is then styled brother to William Edmonstone of Duntreath.7 He disponed those lands to James Reidheugh of 
2 CONC Tulliechettill on 25 February 1511,1 and was father of…etc.
2 CONT ***  Janet Edmonstone, m. William Graham, 1st Earl of Montrose, (he was widow of Annabella, daughter of John, 1st Lord Drummond, and after Janet’s death, he m. thirdly, to Christina, daughter of Thomas Wavan of Stevenson, he was k
2 CONC . at the battle of Flodden in September of 1513).
2 CONT ***  Catherine Edmonstone, m. John Montgomery, Master of Eglinton, eldest son and heir of Hugh, Lord Montgomery, (c/m 1 June 1498 [GD3/2/1/16]).
2 CONT ***  Christian Edmonstone, m. firstly, to John, 2nd Lord Ross of Halkheid, and had issue; and secondly, to Mr. George Knolls from whom she was divorced in 1514 on the grounds that she and Grisel Rattray, his first wife, were withi
2 CONC n the forbidden degrees of consanguinity [Liber Officialias Sancti Andreas. No. 3].
2 CONT ***  Margaret Edmonstone, m. by 2 January 1509, to George Buchannan of that Ilk, when they had a joint charter for the lands of Strathyre, (he survived her and m. secondly, by April of 1530, Janet Cunningham. He d. in 1561,
2 CONT ***  Beatrix Edmonstone, m. James Muschet of Burnbank, (he d. on 13 September 1546 [Dunblane Tests], and had issue.
2 CONT ***  He also had a natural son: James Edmonstone in Balewin, had letters of legitimation under the Great Seal on 2 September 1533, in which he is styled natural son to the late Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath [RMS 1546-1580. No.
2 CONC  838]. He had issue, (see Edmonstone of Broich & Spittal).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
