1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Leslie, Master of Rothes was the son of Andrew Leslie, Master of Rothes and Elizabeth Sinclair.  He gained the title of Master of Rothes. He lived at Balmain, Inverness-shire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT >1a. John Leslie of Balmain (dvp. and sp. bef. 23 Jun 1481), mar. bef. 16 Jan 1477/8 Lady Janet Keith (mar. (2) bef. 23 Jun 1481 Thomas [Stewart], 2nd Lord Innermeath; d. after 18 Jul 1509), 1st dau. of William [Keith], 1st Earl M
2 CONC arischal, by his wife Mariota Erskine, 4th dau. of Thomas [Erskine], 2nd Lord Erskine and de jure 13th Earl of Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/historicalrecord02lesluoft#page/30/mode/2up Historical records of the family of Leslie from 1067 to 1868-69.] Collected from public records and authentic private sources. by Colonel Leslie, K. H., of B
2 CONC alquhain. Published 1869 by Edmonston and Douglas in Edinburgh . Vol 2, pp 31-32
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/rothes1457.htm
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p2496.htm#i24957
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Janet KEITH, daughter of William KEITH Earl Marischal and Mariota ERSKINE, about 1476.1 (Janet KEITH was born about 1464.)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.patrickspeople.scot/ourfamily/16031.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT "I. John Leslie styled of Balmain, having got a part of the lands of Balmain as a provision. He married Lady Janet Keith, daughter of William, first Earl Marischal, about 1476. There is an agreement betwixt William, Earl Marischal
2 CONC , Lord Keith, and George, Earl of Rothes, Lord Leslie, whereby the Earl Marischal bound himself to pay the sum of 600 merks, and the Earl of Rothes bound himself to resign the barony of Ballinbreich, to be given in joint infeftmen
2 CONC t to John, son of Andrew, Master of Rothes, son of the said Earl of Rothes, and to Janet Keith, spouse to the said John, and also to infeft the said John, and Janet his spouse, in four merks of land in the barony of Leslie dated 1
2 CONC 6th January 1477. There is also an obligation whereby John Leslie, son's son and heir-apparent to George, Earl of Rothes, and Janet Keith his spouse, bound themselves to resign all right which they had in the lands of Pitkevey, an
2 CONC d four merks of annual rent in the barony of Leslie, whenever the said Earl of Rothes should let to them in free farm twenty-four merks of land in the barony of Balmain. The obligation is dated 20th May 1478, and has John Leslie's
2 CONC  seal appended ; and because Janet Keith had no proper seal of her own, she procured the seal of her dearest father, William, Earl Marischal, which is also appended."
2 CONT
2 CONT from Family of Leslie 1 3
