2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~rykbrown/stewart_of_invernahyle.htm#The%20Stewarts%20of%20Appin
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan STEWART 3rd Of Appin b: ABT 1478 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland.  "The major branches or "tacks" of Appin stem from the sons of Alan Stewart, 3rd of Appin. Originally they comprised John, 1st of Strathgarry, Dugald, 1st of Achna
2 CONC cone, James, 1st of Fasnacloich and Alexander, 1st of Invernahyle. Ardsheal, the branch our Chief hails from, was given to John, 1st of Ardsheal by his father, John Stewart, 5th of Appin." (Electric Scotland)  "Allan Stewart, 3rd 
2 CONC of Appin, divided his lands between his five sons: Duncan, 4th of Appin (sic), John of Strathgarry, Dugald of Achnacone, James of Fasnaloich, and Alexander of Invernahyle and thus established the branch clan." (Appin website)  All
2 CONC an married to Daughter CAMERON of Locheil b: ABT 1480 in Lochiel, Argyll, Scotland.  They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan STEWART b: ABT 1495 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland.  Duncan died during the lifetime of his father and thus did not inherit Appin.  Duncan married Janet GORDON of Huntly b: ABT 1500 in Scotland.  They had: Has Children John STE
2 CONC WART 4th of Appin b: ABT 1520 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland.  John married Catharine CAMPBELL of Lochnell b: ABT 1520 in Scotland.  They had: Has Children Duncan STEWART 5th of Appin b: ABT 1550 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland
2 CONT  Has Children Allan STEWART 6th of Appin b: ABT 1580 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland.  Allan is recorded as the third son of Duncan Stewart, 5th of Appin. He died without children. Has Children Daughter STEWART b: ABT 1595 in Appin, Ar
2 CONC gyll, Scotland.  She married to Alexander STEWART 4th of Invernahyle b: ABT 1590 in Invernahyle, Appin, Argyle, Scotland (see Invernahyle below). Has Children John STEWART 1st of Ardsheal b: ABT 1560 in Appin, Argyll, Scotland.  M
2 CONC ary MCDONALL of Keppoch b: ABT 1555 in Scotland.  See Ardsheal below
2 CONT
