1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CATHERINE CAMPBELL (aka KATERINAM CAMPBEL)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catherine Campbell, here treated, is the daughter of Colin Campbell, Earl of Argyll, and his wife Isabel Stewart. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/335/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 335] She is identified
2 CONC  as the sister of Archibald, Earl of Argyll, in a charter which was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland on 28 June 1498, presumably because her father was dead. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/515/mode
2 CONC /1up RMS, 1424-1513: 2424]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catherine Campbell, here treated,  is said by Macfarlane to have married Lachlan Oig Maclean. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/335/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 335]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Catherine Campbell, here treated, married Torquil Macleod of Lewis in 1498. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul/page/335/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 335] According to Alexander MacKenzie, they had no children.
2 CONC  [https://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/292/mode/1up History of the MacLeods: 292]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1498: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the office of Bailie of Trouternes, with the four merk lands of Teruga of Duntullyn and the four merk lands of Ardvetfullane, which office and l
2 CONC ands were to be held of the king by TORQUELLO MACLOID of LEWIS and his male heirs by KATERINAM CAMPBEL sister of ARCHIBALDI, EARL OF ARGYLL. This office and lands had been in the kings hands because of the forfeiture of JOHN, LORD
2 CONC  OF THE ISLES. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/515/mode/1up RMS, 1424-1513: 2424]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
