1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gillespie '''Archibald Campbell''', 2nd Earl of Argyll (c. 1465 – 9 September 1513) was a Scottish nobleman and politician who was killed at the Battle of Flodden.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Archibald was the eldest son of Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll and Isabel Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 2nd Lord Lorne.  He was   Master of the Royal Household of James IV of Scotland, March 24, 1495. Lord of Argyll, 2nd 
2 CONC Lord High Chancellor of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Killed in battle at Flodden Field, Branxton, Northumberland, Eng.  King James IV also killed in battle, which was an English victory, and a disaster for Scotland.  
2 CONT
2 CONT De Facto head of Government in Scotland during the War of 3 Kingdoms.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Scots Peerage:
2 CONT
2 CONT II. ARCHIBALD, second Earl of Argyll, had a grant of the lands of Auchintwerely (Auchintorlie) and others, co. Dumbarton, 3 July 1489,6 which were erected into a barony of that name. He succeeded his father 1493, and obtained a ch
2 CONC arter, 30 June 1494,7 confirming the purchase from Elisabeth Menteith, Lady of Rusky, with the consent of Archibald Napier of Merchiston her son, of half of the lands of Inchirnawrisky and others, co. Argyll. He had the office of 
2 CONC Master of the Household 1494, as appears from a charter which he witnessed on 24 March 1494-95 ; 8 and ob- tained a great number of charters under the great seal from 1494-1512. Argyll and his brother-in-law Lennox commanded the r
2 CONC ight wing of the royal army at the battle of Flodden, and were both killed on that field.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Elizabeth, a daughter of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Lennox, Argyll had issue:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Colin Campbell[1]
2 CONT # Archibald Campbell of Skipness (d 1537 escaping from Edinburgh Castle), second husband of Janet Douglas, Lady Glamis
2 CONT # Sir John Campbell of Calder (d.1546) ancestor of the Earls Cawdor
2 CONT # Donald Campbell the Abbot of Coupar Angus
2 CONT # Margaret Campbell, who married John Erskine, 5th Lord Erskine
2 CONT # Isabel Campbell, married Gilbert Kennedy, 2nd Earl of Cassilis
2 CONT # Janet Campbell, married John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl
2 CONT # Jean Campbell, married Sir John Lamont of that ilk, son Duncan Lamont
2 CONT # Catherine Campbell, married Lachlan Cattanach Maclean, 11th Chief of Duart, secondly to Archibald Campbell of Auchinbreck
2 CONT # Marion Campbell, married Sir Robert Menzies of that ilk
2 CONT # Elen Campbell, married Sir Gavin Kennedy of Blairquhan
2 CONT # Mary Campbell, married James Stewart, 4th Earl of Bute
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  James Balfour Paul, Scots Peerage, vol i, pp 335-337 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/358/mode/2up?view=theater Archive.Org] 
2 CONT
