2 CONT *'''Andrew Kerr of Auldtounburn and Cessford1
2 CONT *'''M, #14895, b. 1405, d. after 8 May 1481
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Apr 2014
2 CONT *'''     Andrew Kerr of Auldtounburn and Cessford was born in 1405 at Auldtounburn, Roxburghshire, Scotland.2 He was the son''' of Andrew Kerr of Auldtounburn.1 '''He married, secondly, Margaret Tweedie''', daughter of James Tweed
2 CONC ie of Drummelzier.1 '''He married, firstly, unknown daughter Douglas''', daughter of William Douglas, 2nd of Cavers.1 '''He died after 8 May 1481.1
2 CONT *'''      In 1451 he had a charter of the Corwn lands of the Barony of Old Roxburgh.1 He held the office of Warden of the Middle March in 1457.1 He lived at Auldtounburn, Scotland.1 He lived at Cessford, Scotland.1
2 CONT *'''Children of Andrew Kerr of Auldtounburn and Cessford and Margaret Tweedie
2 CONT **Thomas Kerr, 1st of Ferniehirst+1 d. 24 Jun 1484
2 CONT **Margaret Kerr+3
2 CONT **Robert Kerr3 d. b Jun 1505
2 CONT **William Kerr of Yair3
2 CONT **Ralph Kerr3
2 CONT *'''Children of Andrew Kerr of Auldtounburn and Cessford and unknown daughter Douglas
2 CONT **Walter Kerr of Cessford+ d. 25 Nov 1501
2 CONT **Andrew Kerr, younger of Aultounbrun and Cessford+1 d. c 27 Apr 1467
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2400. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT *[S6286] Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy, online http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info. Hereinafter cited as Clan MacFarlane.
2 CONT *[S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p1490.htm#i14895 ____________________
2 CONT *'''The Universal magazine, Volume 60 Pg. 264
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=bS42AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA265&lpg=PA265&dq=Robert+Ker+1500&source=bl&ots=iOETQfgphY&sig=7toW2p9s8EXYlUzLwFF4DgAst0E&hl=en&ei=CvQ8TOnyKIbmsQP8rcnaCg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=5&ved=0CCYQ6AEwBA#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Robert%20Ker%201500&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.264
2 CONT * .... According to the learned antiquary, Sir George McKenzie, the firft of this family, who fettled in the fouthern parts of Scotland, was Robert de Ker, who flourifhed in the beginning of the 14th century, and in the reigns of 
2 CONC King Robert and David Bruce. His fon John became proprietor of the whole barony of Auldtownburn, in the fhire of Roxburgh; and had a fon, who feems to have been a man of confiderable note; for he obtained letters of fafe conduct f
2 CONC rom King Edward III, for himfelf and twelve Knights in his retinue, to pafs through England in 1363.
2 CONT *   His grandfon, Andrew Ker, was armour-bearer to Archibald Duke of Turenne, Earl of Douglas, from whom he obtained a charter of the lands and barony of Prymfide, wherein he is ftyled 'Nobilis vir, Andreas Ker dominus the Auldtow
2 CONC nburn.' He died about the year 1450, in the reign of James II; and was fucceeded by his '''eldeft fon, Andrew Ker, who was a man of parts, highly efteemed by the King juft mentioned, and concerned in moft of the public trafactions
2 CONC  of the time. In 1459, he was appointed one of the Ambaffadores extraordinary to the count England. He died about the year 1486, leaving iffue four fons, of whom''' Walter, the eldeft, was named one of the Scotch Commiffioners to 
2 CONC treat with the Englifh, in 1484; and in 1491, and 1494, one of the Ambaffadors extraordinary to the court of England. he died in 1502, having had
2 CONT *Pg.265
2 CONT *iffue a daughter, Elifabeth, and a fon, Sir Robert Ker, who married Chriftain Rutherford, daughter of Philip Rutherford, and died in the beginning of the year 1500, leaving a fon, Sir Andrew Ker, who fucceeded his grandfather, an
2 CONC d, being a man of great parts, was often employed in negociations of importance, which he managed with dexterity and fuccefs. By his wife, daughter of William, third Lord Creichton, of Sanquhar, he had five fons and two daughters.
2 CONC  .... etc. _______________
2 CONT *'''Burke's landed gentry of Great Britain: together with members of the titled''' ... By Peter Beauclerk Dewar Pg.770
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=wEFuRPsYHwwC&pg=PA770&lpg=PA770&dq=Robert+Ker+1500&source=bl&ots=rZANSvtXbT&sig=nbTwSuuHQkJJpR4dN5KAOL4A3yM&hl=en&ei=uz4-TPelFIP6lwei0bX5BQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBUQ6AEwADgU
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Robert%20Ker%201500&f=false ___________________
