1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ======
2 CONT ===Margaret Stewart
2 CONT *(AKA Anne)
2 CONT *Born: About 1492
2 CONT *Marriage (1): GORDON, James 1st of Lesmoir 
2 CONT *Died: Between 1541 and 1546
2 CONT * Parents: Patrick Stewart, Laird of Laithers and an unknown woman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Stewart appears to have been the relict of (Thomas) Meldrum of Eden when she married James Gordon of Lesmois, married to him before 1521 and living in 1541.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret married James GORDON 1st of Lesmoir, son of George GORDON of Tillytarmont and Isabel INNES.1 (James GORDON 1st of Lesmoir was born about 1480 and died in 1558 1.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children  
2 CONT
2 CONT # GORDON, George 2nd of Lesmoir+
2 CONT # GORDON, James 1st of Crichie+
2 CONT # GORDON, Janet+
2 CONT # GORDON, Alexander 1st of Birkenburn+
2 CONT # GORDON, Marjorie+
2 CONT # GORDON, Margaret+
2 CONT # GORDON, Katharine
2 CONT # GORDON, William 1st of Terpersie+
2 CONT # GORDON, Patrick 1st of Oxhill+
2 CONT # GORDON, John 1st of Leitcheston (Lesmoir)+
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The forsaid James Gordon first Laird of Lesmoir married two Ladies, his first was a daughter of Patrick Stuart of Lethers:  Lady Eden, with whom he begat Six Sons and three daughters, viz, 
2 CONT *his eldest Son George Gordon 2d Laird of Lesmoir, 
2 CONT *his second Son James Gordon of Crichie, 
2 CONT *3 d Son Alexander Gordon of Birkenburn, 
2 CONT *fourth son Mr William Gordon of Terpersie, 
2 CONT *fifth son Patrick Gordon of Oxhill, and 
2 CONT *the Sixth Son John Gordon of Licheston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The said James married to his second Lady the Laird of Findlaters daughter Ogilvy Lady Gartlie, whom he begat two Sons, 
2 CONT *Hary Gordon of Dilespro or Savach, and 
2 CONT *Thomas Gordon of Drumbuilg.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/houseofgordon01bulluoft/houseofgordon01bulluoft_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Anne Stewart married James Gordon, 1st of Lesmoir, son of George Gordon and unknown Innes.1      Her married name became Gordon.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Anne Stewart and James Gordon, 1st of Lesmoir
2 CONT
2 CONT James Gordon, 2nd of Lesmoir+1 b. 1495, d. 1555
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES ON A PEDIGREE OF THE GORDONS OF TERPERSIE [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9559/95590708.23.pdf PDF] page 17 
2 CONT
2 CONT >The Gordons of Terpersie were descended from Jock of Scurdargue by his spouse, Elizabeth Maitland : Jock lived from say 1380-1460: their 2nd son, William in TiUytarmont, who lived say 1424-1484, married a sister of Sir John Ruthe
2 CONC rford : their eldest son was George in Tillytarmont, who lived say 1450-1500, married Isobel, daughter of Beroald limes of Meilliers : and their 2nd son was James Gordon, first of Lesmoir, who lived say 1475-1557 I he married, 1st
2 CONC , Margaret, daughter of Patrick Stewart of Laithers, relict of Meldrum of Eden : 2ndly, about 1546, Margaret, daughter of Alexander Ogilvy of Deskford, Finlater and Ogilvy, relict of Barclay of Gartly.
2 CONT
