2 CONT *'''Robert Cuninghame, 2nd Earl of Glencairn1
2 CONT *'''M, #21834, d. circa 1490
2 CONT *Last Edited=2 Jun 2014
2 CONT *'''     Robert Cuninghame, 2nd Earl of Glencairn was the son of Alexander Cuninghame, 1st Earl of Glencairn and Margaret Hepburn.2 He married Christian Lindsay, daughter of John Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of the Byres and Agnes St
2 CONC ewart, before 19 July 1476.1 He died circa 1490.2
2 CONT *'''     He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Kilmaurs [S., 1464] in June 1488.2 He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Glencairn [S., 1488] in June 1488.2 On 17 October 1488 he was stripped of the Earldom of Glencairn by Act o
2 CONC f Parliament (the rebel party was then in power).2
2 CONT *'''Child of Robert Cuninghame, 2nd Earl of Glencairn and Christian Lindsay
2 CONT ** 1.Cuthbert Cuninghame, 3rd Earl of Glencairn+2 d. fr 23 May 1540 - May 1541
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 1285. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S37] BP2003. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p2184.htm#i21834 __________________________
2 CONT *'''Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900, Volume 13
2 CONT *Cunningham, Alexander (d.1488) by Thomas Finlayson Henderson
2 CONT *CUNNINGHAM, ALEXANDER, first Earl of Glencairn (d. 1488), was descended from a family which obtained the manor of Cunningham, in the parish of Kilmaurs, Ayrshire, in the twelfth century. He was the eldest son of Sir Robert Cunnin
2 CONC gham (who received a charter of the lands of Kilmaurs from Robert, duke of Albany, and was knighted by James I) by his wife Ann, a daughter of Sir John de Montgomery of Eglinton and Ardrossan. He was created a lord of parliament b
2 CONC y the title Lord Kilmaurs about 1450. In January 1477–8 he received a charter of the lands of Drip in the parish of Kilbride, Lanarkshire (Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, vol. i. entry 1,342). He was created Earl of Glenca
2 CONC irn (a parish in the western part of Nithsdale, Dumfriesshire) by James III 28 May 1488, for the powerful assistance he had rendered against the rebel lords at Blackness. He was slain at the battle of Sauchieburn 11 June of the sa
2 CONC me year. By his wife Margaret, daughter of Adam Hepburn of Hailes, he had four sons. By the Rescissory Act passed by James IV 17 Oct. 1488, '''his eldest son Robert was deprived of the earldom and reduced to the rank of Lord Kilma
2 CONC urs'''. It was, however, revived in the person of Cuthbert, third earl, in 1505.
2 CONT *[Acts of Parliament of Scotland, vol. ii.; Reg. Magni Sig. Scotl. vol. i.; Douglas's Scotch Peerage (Wood), i. 633–4.]
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Cunningham,_Alexander_(d.1488)_(DNB00)
2 CONT *'''Dictionary of national biography (1885) Vol. XIII. Craik - Damer
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/dictionaryofnati13stepuoft
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/dictionaryofnati13stepuoft#page/303/mode/1up _____________________
2 CONT *	Glencairn, Earl of (S, 1488 - dormant 1796)
2 CONT *Alexander [Cunningham], 1st Lord Kilmaurs later 1st Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *son and heir of Sir Robert Cunningham of Kilmaurs, by his wife Anne Montgomerie, only dau. of Sir John Montgomerie of Ardrossan
2 CONT *born	after 1425
2 CONT *mar.	Margaret Hepburn, sister of Patrick [Hepburn], 1st Lord Hailes, and dau. of Sir Adam Hepburn of Hailes by his wife Janet Borthwick, dau. of Sir William Borthwick
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **'''	1. Sir Robert Cunningham, later 2nd Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT **	2. William Cunningham, 1st of Craigends (d. bef. 19 Jun 1520), mar. after 12 Mar 1497/8 Marion Auchinleek, dau. of Sir John Auchinleek of Auchinleek, and had issue [he was ancestor of the Cunninghams of Craigends and said to be
2 CONC  the ancestor of the Cunninghams of Robertland, Carncurin, Bedlaw, Auchinharvie, and Auchinyards)
2 CONT **	3. Alexander Cunningham (d. after 1483)
2 CONT **	4. Edward Cunningham (d. after 1483)
2 CONT *died	11 Jun 1488
2 CONT *created
2 CONT **betw. 8 Feb 1462/3 and 13 Jan 1463/4 Lord Kilmaurs
2 CONT **28 May 1488 Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *suc. by	son
2 CONT *note	defeated an uprising against King James III at the Battle of Blackness 1488; killed fighting for King James III against the latter's own son at the Battle of Sauchieburn
2 CONT *
2 CONT *'''Robert [Cunningham], 2nd Earl of Glencairn later known as 2nd Lord Kilmaurs
2 CONT *born
2 CONT *'''mar.	bef. 19 Jul 1476 Christian Seton (widow of John Seton, Master of Seton, 1st son and heir ap. by his first wife of George [Seton], 1st Lord Seton; d. betw. 1491/2 and 11 Mar 1495/6), 1st dau. of John [Lindsay], 1st Lord Li
2 CONC ndsay of the Byres, by his wife ..... Stewart, dau. of Robert [Stewart], 1st Lord Lorne, by his wife Lady Joan Stewart, dau. by his first wife of Robert [Stewart], 1st Duke of Albany
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Sir Cuthbert Cunningham, later 3rd Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *'''died	c. 1490
2 CONT *'''suc. by	son
2 CONT *'''note	the Earldom of Glencairn was annulled by Act of Parliament 17 Oct 1488 and he was thereafter known as Lord Kilmaurs
2 CONT *
2 CONT *Cuthbert [Cunningham], 3rd Lord Kilmaurs later 3rd Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *born
2 CONT *mar.	after 24 Jun 1492 Lady Mariot Douglas (d. after Jul 1511), 1st dau. of Archibald [Douglas], 5th Earl of Angus, by his first wife Elizabeth Boyd, 1st dau. of Robert [Boyd], 1st Lord Boyd
2 CONT *children
2 CONT **	1. Sir William Cunningham, later 4th Earl of Glencairn
2 CONT *died	betw. 23 May 1540 and May 1541
2 CONT *suc. by	son
2 CONT *note	restored to the Earldom of Glencairn c. 1503, confirmed by charter 1511; opposed the Douglas family in their control of King James V and was defeated by them at the Battle of Linlithgow 1526
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/glencairn1488.htm#GLENCAIRN_1488_3 ______________________________
2 CONT *'''Origins of the Clan Cunningham in Scotland
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *XII. Sir Robert Cuninghame of Kilmaurs. He married in 1425, Anne, the only daughter of Sir John de Montgomery of Ardrossan, by whom he had two sons. The second son, Archibald, was the first of the Cunninghames of Waterstoun, a fa
2 CONC mily now extinct. He was succeeded by his eldest son, Alexander Cunningham, the first Earl of Glencairn.
2 CONT *'''The Earls Of Glencairn: A Chronological Listing
2 CONT *The following is a brief summary of the part of the Cunningham clan history that covers the Earls of Glencairn. The Glencairn lineage can be traced as follows:
2 CONT **1st Earl (1488): Alexander Cunninghame
2 CONT *Alexander became the Earl of Glencairn in 1488. Took his title from the family’s estate/property located in Dumfrieshire. His title prior to being granted the earldom was Lord Kilmaurs. Receiving his title for battle services at 
2 CONC Blackness, Alexander was killed in the same year at the Battle of Sauchieburn.
2 CONT **'''2nd Earl (1488-1503): Robert Cunninghame
2 CONT *'''When the Earldom was rescinded by King James IV, Robert was left with only the title of the Lord of Kilmaurs
2 CONT **3rd Earl (1503-1540): Cuthbert Cunninghame
2 CONT *The title was restored to Cuthbert who created the Burgh of Barony of Kilmaurs in the year 1527. This was introduced in the form of a charter which granted 280 Scots acres to 40 “tennamenters”, each of whom would hold a fortieth 
2 CONC part of the total area.
2 CONT **4th Earl (1540-1547): William Cunninghame
2 CONT *The 4th Earl was active in the cause of the Reformation. At first, he was loyal to the Crown but when he witnessed the atrocities of the English, he joined the forces of the Reformation and played no small part in the cause.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *From: http://www.clancunninghamintl.org/history.htm ______________________
2 CONT *Alexander Cunningham, 1st Earl of Glencairn, 1st Lord Kilmaurs (1426 – 11 June 1488) was a Scottish nobleman.
2 CONT *He was firstly created a Lord of Parliament in 1450, with the title Lord Kilmaurs.
2 CONT *King James III of Scotland created Lord Kilmaurs Earl of Glencairn on 28 May 1488, by Letters Patent under the Great Seal.
2 CONT *Fighting on his king's side, he was slain at the Battle of Sauchieburn on 11 June 1488.
2 CONT *The Earl married Margaret, daughter of Sir Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes, and sister of Sir Patrick Hepburn, 1st Lord Hailes. They had four sons. The second son, William, was ancestor of the Cunninghams of Craigends, Robertland,
2 CONC Bedlan, Auchenharvey, and Auchenyards.
2 CONT *By the Act Rescissory, passed in the first parliament of James IV, 17 October 1488, all creations of new dignities granted by that monarch's father since the preceding 2 February were annulled, and, '''in consequence, Robert Cunn
2 CONC ingham, 2nd Lord Kilmaurs, eldest son of this Earl of Glencairn, was deprived of the title and dignity of Earl. This was, however, overturned by the 1503 Act Revocatory.
2 CONT *References
2 CONT *Anderson, William, The Scottish Nation, Edinburgh, 1867, vol.v, p. 310.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Cunningham,_1st_Earl_of_Glencairn ______________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Cunningham, Lord Kilmaurs, 2nd Earl of Glencairn; married before 19 Jul 1476 to Christian Lindsay (died between 1491/92 and 11 Mar 1495/96), eldest daughter of John, 1st Lord Lindsay of the Byres. Robert died about 1490.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert lost his earldom after a few months because his father had fought on the losing side at Sauchieburn, and sat in Parliament in 1489 as Lord Kilmaurs. Hugh Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Eglinton is said by some sources to have bee
2 CONC n involved in Robert's death.Robert lost his earldom after a few months because his father had fought on the losing side at Sauchieburn, and sat in Parliament in 1489 as Lord Kilmaurs. Hugh Montgomerie, 1st Earl of Eglinton is sai
2 CONC d by some sources to have been involved in Robert's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________
2 CONT *	'Cunningham02'
2 CONT *Alexander Cunningham, 1st Earl of Glencairn (d Sauchieburn 11.06.1488)
2 CONT *  m. Margaret Hepburn (dau of Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes)
2 CONT **'''	1. Robert Cunningham, 2nd Earl of Glencairn (d by 1492)
2 CONT **'''	TSP (Glencairn) reports that, because James IV revoked some of the appointments of his father, this Robert was "deprived the dignity of an earldom conferred on his father". James IV reinstated the earldom after Robert had di
2 CONC ed. Accordingly, TSP numbers subsequent Earls differently from (say) BE1883 (eg. Cuthbert identified by TSP as 2nd Earl). We follow the numbering used by BE1883 and BP1934 (Cuninghame of Caprington).
2 CONT **'''	  m. (before 19.07.1476) Christian Lindsay (dau of John Lindsay, 1st Lord of the Byres)
2 CONT ***		A. Cuthbert Cunningham, 3rd Earl of Glencairn (d 1540-1)
2 CONT ***		  m. (mcrt 24.06.1492) Marjory (or Mary or Marion) Douglas (a 1511, dau of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus)
2 CONT ****			i. William Cunningham, 4th Earl of Glencairn (b c1493, d 03.1547-8)
2 CONT ****			BE1883 reports that William left sundry children "by Margaret, or Elizabeth (Campbell), his 2nd wife". BPGS2001 reports that he m1. Margaret, m2. Elizabeth Campbell. We follow TSP which identifies his 1st wife as Katherine 
2 CONC Borthwick. It is thought that William had issue by both marriages but, other than to note that most of the children noted below appeared to be adult by the time of the second marriage, it is not clear who if any of these noted was
2 CONC  by the second marriage. We presume that none were (not least because Elizabeth must have been in her mid-40s by the time of the marriage) but note that some sources say otherwise.
