1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN LUNDY OF THAT ILK===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===EVIDENCE FROM THE NATIONAL RECORDS OF SCOTLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1490: Charter by John Lundy [Lundie] of that ilk knight, granting to his carnal son Robert Lundy [Lundie] half of the lands of Inchmedane [Inchmeddan]; on John Inchmedane's [Inchmeddan] resignation. To be held de me
2 CONC  blench. At Montrose. Seal entire. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f52&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1491-92: Charter by John Lundy [Lundie] of that ilk knight and Isabel his spouse, granting to Robert Lundy [Lundie] their son the lands and barony of Benhame [Benholm], viz. the Manis, Casteltoune [Castleton] and Tullo
2 CONC ch, with the mill. To be held of the King. Reserving the granters' liferent. At Lundy [Lundie], 24 March 1491/2. Sir John's seal is gone. Isabel Forrester's is entire. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=GD4%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 July 1495: Precept by Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benham [Benholm], son of John Lundy [Lundie] of that iIk knight and of Isabel Frostar [Forrester] his spouse, for giving sasine of the lands of the Tullowcht of Benhame [Tully o
2 CONC f Benholm] to Isabel Erskin [Erskine] daughter of John Erskin [Erskine] elder of Dun, conform to charter of sale thereof granted her. At Montrose. Robert Lundy's [Lundie] seal and his father's are entire. Two other seals lost. [ht
2 CONC tp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincard
2 CONC ineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:- Subsequent Writs show that the grant to Isabel (or Elizabeth) Erskine was made in contemplation of her marriage to Robert Lundy [Lundie]. '''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1498: Great Seal Charter by King James IV. granting the lands of Tullow of Benhame [Tully of Benholm] to Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benhame [Benholm] and Elizabeth Erskin [Erskine] his spouse, on said Elizabeth's resig
2 CONC nation. 14 Oct. 1498, an.reg.11. (Reg.Mag.Sig.ii.2460) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f21&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records o
2 CONC f Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 February 1502-03: Assignation by John Lundy [Lundie] of that ilk knight to Robert Lundy [Lundie] his natural son, of the right to redeem half of the Manelandis of Benehame [Benholm] and "chemys" thereof from the heirs and as
2 CONC signees of the deceased William Bonar of Rossy [Rossie]. At Cupar.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f42&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n Natio
2 CONC nal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/42]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:- This is a good instance of the use of the term "natural son" to denote a son who was undoubtedly legitimate; a matter which has come up for discussion in sundry peerage cases.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 August 1504: Sasine given by Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benhum [Benholm] to John Bonar of Rossy [Rossie], of half the Mains of Benhum, in which James Bonar his father had died vest and seized. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f43&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus,
2 CONC  reference GD4/43]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 October 1504: Instrument narrating that Robert Lundy [Lundie] son of Sir John Lundy [Lundie] of that ilk knight, and heir to him in the lands of Benhame [Benholm], and assignee to the Letters of Reversion granted by the dece
2 CONC ased William Bonar of Rossy [Rossie], delivered to John Bonur [Bonar] of Rossy [Rossie], son and heir of the deceased James Bonar of Rossy [Rossie], the sum of 250 merks Scots for redemption of the last half of the Mains of Benham
2 CONC e [Benholm]. Which lands the said John Bonar thereupon resigned and renounced. Done in the bishop's palace of Aberdeen. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f44&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=
2 CONC n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/44]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 October 1505: 	Sasine of said 40/- annual rent to David Inchmedan [Inchmeddan], given on behalf of Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benhum [Benholm] as superior. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?re
2 CONC ference=GD4%2f57&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/57]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 June 1523: Sasine to Andrew Lundy [Lundie], as heir of the deceased Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benhome [Benholm] his father, of the lands of Inchmedane [Inchmeddan], Tulloch of Benhome [Tully of Benholm] and Kyrktone of Benholm
2 CONC e [Kirkton of Benholm], with the mill thereof; which had been in nonentry for four years, and to which Andrew had the King's Dispensation to enter notwithstanding his minority. On Chancery Precept of Clare Constat, dated 25 June a
2 CONC n.reg. 10 (A.D.1523). Sasine dated 2 June 1523. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Andrew+Lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The Sasine bears to be dated earlier than the Precept, which shows that there must be some clerical error.'''
2 CONT
