1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester==
2 CONT '''John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester (c. 1450 – after October 1508) is the ancestor of the Marquesses of Tweeddale. He was created a Lord of Parliament on 29 January 1488 by James III of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He was born in Peebleshire, the son of Sir David Hay of Locherworth, Peebleshire, and later Yester in East Lothian (d. c. 1478) by his wife Elizabeth (b. c. 1400), daughter of George Douglas, 1st Earl of Angus (1370–1402) by Pr
2 CONC incess Mary (d. before 1458), daughter of Robert III, King of Scots.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Hay married (1) Mary (d. c. 1467), daughter of John Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of the Byres, and (2) by contract before 17 December 1468, Elizabeth (d. 1529), daughter of George Cunningham of Belton. There were children by 
2 CONC both marriages:
2 CONT * (1) Sir Thomas Hay, Master of Yester (d. 1491), who married Elizabeth (c. 1477–1544), daughter of Alexander Home, 2nd Lord Home, who later married James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran[1]
2 CONT * (1) Isabel, who married Sir Walter Ker of Cessford, & Caverton (d. 1501)
2 CONT * (2) Sir John Hay, 2nd Lord Hay of Yester (killed at the Battle of Flodden)
2 CONT * (2) George Hay of Menzion
2 CONT * (2) Isabella, who married Sir Robert Lauder of The Bass, Knt
2 CONT * (2) Margaret (d. c. 1525), married in 1491 to William Borthwick, 3rd Lord Borthwick (1460s – c. 1503)
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *1. ^ Greig, Elaine Finnie (2004). "Hamilton, James, first earl of Arran (1475?–1529)". Oxford Dictionary of National Biography. Oxford University Press. doi:10.1093/ref:odnb/12079. Retrieved 7 March 2009.
2 CONT * The Scots' Peerage, by Sir James Balfour Paul, Edinburgh, 1905, under 'Tweeddale'.
2 CONT * The New Extinct Peerage, 1884-1971, by L.G. Pine, London, 1972, p. 33.
2 CONT * Burke's Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage, edited by Peter Townend, 105th edition, London, 1970, p. 2697.
2 CONT * The Magna Charta Sureties 1215, by Frederick Lewis Weis, et al., 5th edition, Baltimore, 2002, p. 51.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Hay,_1st_Lord_Hay_of_Yester
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________
2 CONT *'''John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester1
2 CONT *'''M, #31411, b. circa 1450, d. September 1508
2 CONT *Father      Sir David Hay, Sheriff of Peebles, 1st Lord Yester d. bt 3 Apr 1478 - 2 Sep 1478
2 CONT *Mother     Elizabeth Douglas2
2 CONT *'''     John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester was born circa 1450 at of Yester, Haddingtonshire, Scotland. He married Mary Lindsay, daughter of Sir John Lindsay, 1st Lord of Byres and (Miss) Stewart, before 7 July 1462.3 A contract fo
2 CONC r the marriage of John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Cunningham was signed on 17 December 1468. John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester died in September 1508.
2 CONT *'''Family 1      Elizabeth Cunningham d. bt 16 Dec 1528 - 7 Dec 1529
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **John Hay, 2nd Lord Hay of Yester+ d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT **Margaret Hay+4,5
2 CONT **Isobell Hay+ b. c 1470 
2 CONT *'''Family 2      Mary Lindsay d. b 1468
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S9671] Unknown author, The Complete Peerage, by Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 421/2; The Magna Charta Barons, 1215, by F. L. Weis, 4th Ed., p. 44.
2 CONT * 2.[S147] Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage, Baronetage, and Knightage, 1938 ed., by Sir Bernard Burke, p., 2455.
2 CONT * 3.[S11584] The Scots Peerage, Vol. V, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 394.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. VI, p. 421.
2 CONT * 5.[S11564] The Scots Peerage, Vol. II, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 107-108.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1046.htm#i31411 _________________________
2 CONT *'''John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester1
2 CONT *'''M, #109387, d. between September 1508 and 23 October 1508
2 CONT *Last Edited=18 May 2011
2 CONT *'''     John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester was the son of Sir David Hay of Lochorwart and Yester and Lady Elizabeth Douglas.2 He married, firstly, Mariot Lindsay, daughter of John Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of the Byres and Agnes St
2 CONC ewart, before 7 July 1462.3 He married, secondly, Elizabeth Cunningham, daughter of George Cunningham of Belton, circa 1468.2 He died between September 1508 and 23 October 1508.1
2 CONT *'''     He held the office of Sheriff of Peebles.2 He was created 1st Lord Hay of Yester [Scotland] on 29 January 1487/88.2 He lived at Wester Hoprew, Peebles-shire, Scotland, which his father settled on him.2
2 CONT *'''Child of John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester
2 CONT ** 1.Isabel Hay3
2 CONT *'''Child of John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester and Mariot Lindsay
2 CONT ** 1.Sir Thomas Hay, Master of Yester+1 b. b 1470, d. bt 29 Sep 1502 - 8 Nov 1504
2 CONT *'''Children of John Hay, 1st Lord Hay of Yester and Elizabeth Cunningham
2 CONT ** 1.Margaret Hay+4
2 CONT ** 2.William Hay2 d. b 12 Jul 1512
2 CONT ** 3.Nicholas Hay2 d. 1498
2 CONT ** 4.Isobel Hay+2
2 CONT ** 5.John Hay, 2nd Lord Hay of Yester+2 b. c 1470, d. 9 Sep 1513
2 CONT ** 6.George Hay2 b. a 1471
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VI, page 422. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 2.[S37] BP2003 volume 3, page 3960. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
