1 NAME Walter Ogston of that Ilk
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1455
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ogston
3 CTRY Scotland
1 BURI
2 DATE 1489
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1489
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ogston
3 CTRY Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It has not been established that this Walter was knighted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ogston-26
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Ogston was the son of John Ogston, heir apparent of that Ilk and the Craigs. He may have been born at the Craigs of Glenisla. His father had died by December 1475, when Lord Gordon took measures to release the deceased John
2 CONC  Ogston of the mails of £140 due to the Lord Auditor, and Walter, his son and heir, was also released of the exact sums due to the king.[1] His grandfather, Alexander Ogston of that Ilk was still alive in 1475, and evidence sugges
2 CONC ts he lived beyond that date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter was designed of that Ilk when he appeared before the Lords of Council on 17 March 1482/3.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He has sasine of Ogston in Moray and Eglismaldy in Kincardineshire in 1483. Walter married Janet Scrymgeour, a daughter of John Scrymgeour of Dudhope, perhaps about 1475, and they had three daughters: Elizabeth, born about 1476; C
2 CONC hristian, who died young; and Janet, who was joint heiress with her elder sister Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter died about the close of the 1480's leaving his widow Janet and three daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT Other sources list his daughters as children of daughter Abernathy.
2 CONT
