2 NICK Thomas Wemyss of Winthank
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Second son of Sir John Wemyss of Wemyss. His first appearance in the sederunt of the Court is on the 5th November 1544. He was jointly with John Sinclair, Dean of Restalrig, Collector of "the Contribucione to the S
2 CONC ete," in 1549.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 82
2 CONT
2 CONT <strong>Note:</strong> As is noted in [http://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/198/mode/2up Memorials of the family of Wemyss of Wemyss, Volume I] (pages 101 and 153) the link between Sir John Wemyss and Thomas Wemys
2 CONC s of Unthank is disputed.
