1 NAME Henry /Wemyss/ Bishop of Galloway
2 GIVN Henry
2 SURN Wemyss
2 NSFX Bishop of Galloway
2 _MARNM Wemyss
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Bishop of Galloway is first mentioned in the Sederunt of the Court on 21st March 1533. The individual who then filled that see was Henry Wemyss who according to Douglas, was the son of John, fifth son of Sir Jo
2 CONC hn Wemyss of Wemyss, by a daughter of Sir John Arnot of Arnot. As he is, however designed in charters, <em>frater regis</em> and <em>frater natural is regis</em> it has been supposed he was a son of Sir John's daughter, by King Ja
2 CONC mes IV. He was a prelate of great piety, according to Lesly, who relates a supernatural interposition of heaven in his favour, during a remarkable storm of wind at Edinburgh, in 1524. He died shortly before 3d July 1541, and was s
2 CONC ucceeded by Andrew Durie, Abbot of Melrose.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 43
2 CONT
2 CONT <strong>Note:</strong> The father of the Bishop of Galloway is disputed.  In the above passage it is suggested it may be [http://www.geni.com/people/James-IV-of-Scotland/4229916861440069622 King James IV], and in [http://archive.o
2 CONC rg/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/198/mode/2up Memorials of the family of Wemyss of Wemyss, Volume I] (page 101) it is suggested to be Sir John Wemyss.
