1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MASTER JOHN BAYNE OF LOGIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master John Bayne of Logie, here treated, is the second son of Alexander Bayne of Logie-Wester, the grandson of Alexander Bayne of Tulloch, and the great-grandson of Alexander Bayne of Tulloch. [https://books.google.co.uk/books
2 CONC ?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=bayne&f=false Inquisitionum II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 June 1681: Instrument of sasine in favour of Anna Bayne, only daughter of John Bayne of Delnie and Anna Gray, his spouse, of the town and lands of Kilmuir and the town and lands of Easter Sligo. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.
2 CONC gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f9%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=delnie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1690&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds and other legal pa
2 CONC pers, reference GD255/1/9/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1682: (6390) MAGISTER JOANNE BAYNE de Delnie, haeres Alexandri Bayne de Logie-Wester, filii primo geniti secundi matrimonu Alexandri Bayne de Tulloch, avi.  xxxvi. 212. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&p
2 CONC g=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=bayne&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc
2 CONC . II: Inquisitionis Generales]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1682: (6391) MAGISTER JOANNE BAYNE de Delnie, haeres masculus provisionis et conquestus secundi matrimonii Alexander Bayne de Tulloch, proavi.  xxxvi. 213. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR
2 CONC 17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=bayne&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II: Inquisi
2 CONC tionis Generales]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 December 1683: Discharge and renunciation by Anna Bayne and John Gordon, her husband, to John Bayne of Delnie, in terms of the bond of provision made by John Bayne in favour of Anna Bayne, and dated 7 Jun 1681. [http://catal
2 CONC ogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD255%2f1%2f9%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=delnie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1690&di=n National Records of Scotland, Mackenzie of Kilmuir and Easter Sligo: title deeds an
2 CONC d other legal papers, reference GD255/1/9/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Bayne of Logie  is described in documents as "Mr John Bayne". He may be  the John Bayne from Ross-shire who graduated M.A.  in 1651 at King's College in Aberdeen. He married, about 1660, Anna, eldest daughter of Robert Gra
2 CONC y of Arboll, Sutherland, with issue an only daughter, also Anna, who married Sir John Gordon,3rd Baronet of Embo, Sutherland (marr. cont. dated 19 April 1683) with issue. By a bond, dated on 23 November 1694, at Fortrose, "Mr John
2 CONC  Bayne of Delnie binds himself to pay to his grandchildren John Robert, George, Anne, Elizabeth and Jean the sum of 1200 Merks with interest thereon ...". Mr John was dead by 1696 and on 28 May 1700 the fore-mentioned grandchildre
2 CONC n were infeft in the lands of Delny. [http://www.rossandcromartyheritage.org/Community/Dingwall/Heritage/History/The-Baynes-of-Tulloch.aspx Ross and Cromarty Heritage: The Baynes of Tulloch]'''
