1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Macleod:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p14694.htm#i146931
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Macleod [1]
2 CONT *F, #146931
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 May 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Macleod is the daughter of Torquil Macleod of the Lewes.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Sir Roderick Mackenzie of Castle Leod, son of Sir Colin Mackenzie of Kintail and Barbara Grant, circa 6 May 1605.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Thomas Fraser, 2nd of Strichen circa 17 February 1629.2
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 6 May 1605, her married name became Mackenzie.[2] From 17 February 1629, her married name became Fraser.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Margaret Macleod and Sir Roderick Mackenzie of Castle Leod
2 CONT *1. Sir John Mackenzie of Tarbat, 1st Bt.+[2] d. 10 Sep 1654
2 CONT *2. Margaret Mackenzie+[1]
2 CONT *3. Kenneth Mackenzie of Scatwell+[2] d. 3 Mar 1662
2 CONT *4. Colin Mackenzie [2] d. 1645
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume II, page 291. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 978. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
