1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kilravock Castle has been continuously tenanted by the House of Rose since 1293. The family is of Norman origin, arriving in Britain with William the Conqueror. Many Rose heirs have borne the Christian name of Hugh
2 CONC . They appear to be connected with two other Norman families; the de Bissets and the de Boscos.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p50050.htm#i500494
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh Rose, 12th of Kilravock was born in 1577. He was the son of William Rose, 11th of Kilvarock and Lilias Hay.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Magdalene Fraser, daughter of Thomas Fraser of Knockie, and 1st of Strichen and Isobel Forbes, in June 1603. He died on 10 June 1643. On 11 October 1611 he was infeft in the Barony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hugh Rose, 12th of Kilravock and Magdalene Fraser
2 CONT # Hugh Rose, 13th of Kilravock d. Mar 1649
2 CONT # Agnes Rose of Kilvarock+4
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
