1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "II. <strong>John Glassich Mackenzie</strong>, who appears to have been a minor at his father's death...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...John Glassich married Janet Agnes, daughter of James Fraser of Phoineas, brother of Hugh, sixth Lord Lovat (with whom he got the Barony of Inchlag, etc.), with issue — 
2 CONT * Hector, his heir and successor, 
2 CONT * Alexander, who succeeded his brother Hector. 
2 CONT * John, who succeeded Alexander. 
2 CONT * A daughter, who married John Mackenzie, II. of Loggie, with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Glassich's widow married, secondly, Thomas Chisholm, XV. of Chisholm, without issue male. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had also two natural sons before his marriage, Alexander Roy and Hector Caol...
2 CONT
2 CONT John Glassich, who was assassinated in 1550, as already stated, at Ellandonnan Castle, was buried in the Priory of Beauly, and succeeded by his eldest lawful son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/398/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 398
