1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "IV. <strong>John Roy Mackenzie</strong>, John Glassich's third son, who was at the time a minor, although his father had been dead for 15 or 16 years; and the estate was given in ward by Queen Mary in 1567...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...John Roy married, first, Elizabeth, daughter of Angus Macdonald, VII. of Glengarry, by his wife, Janet, daughter of Kenneth Mackenzie, X. of Kintail, by Lady Elizabeth, daughter of John, second Earl of Athole, with issue — 
2 CONT * John, who married, as already stated, Isabel, daughter of Alexander Mackenzie, II. of Fairburn, with issue — an only daughter, also named Isabel, who, as his second wife, married Colin Mackenzie of Kinnock, with issue — an only 
2 CONC son, who sold back his mother's jointure lands of Davochpollo and Pitlundie in 1666. John died before his father, in 1601, at Kinkell, and was buried at Beauly. 
2 CONT * Alexander, who succeeded to the estates. 
2 CONT * Murdoch, killed, unmarried, at Raasay in 1611. 
2 CONT * Kenneth, I. of Davochcairn, who married, first, Margaret, daughter of James Cuthbert of Alterlies and Drakies, Inverness, with issue, whose male representation is extinct. He married, secondly, a daughter of Hector Mackenzie, IV
2 CONC . of Fairburn, also with issue, of whose present representation nothing is known. Kenneth died at Davochcairn in 1643, and was buried at Beauly. 
2 CONT * Duncan of Sand, who married a daughter of Hugh Fraser of Belladrum, with issue
2 CONT * William Mackenzie of Shieldaig, who married a daughter of the Rev. Murdo Mackenzie, minister of Kintail, with issue
2 CONT * A daughter, who married Fraser of Foyers. 
2 CONT * Katherine, who married Hugh Fraser of Culbokie and Guisachan, 
2 CONT * Another Katherine, who married Fraser of Struy, 
2 CONT * Janet, who m.arried, first, George Cuthbert of Castlehill, Inverness (marriage contract 29th June, 1611); and secondly Neil Munro of Findon (marriage contract dated 5th of February, 1627).
2 CONT * A daughter, who married Alastair Mor, brother of Chisholm of Comar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Roy married, secondly, Isabel, daughter of Murdoch Mackenzie, I. of Fairburn, with issue — 
2 CONT * Captain Roderick of Pitglassie, who served in the army of the Prince of Orange, and died, unmarried, in Holland, in 1624. 
2 CONT * Hector of Mellan, who married, first, the widow of the Rev. John Mackenzie of Lochbroom, without issue ; and secondly, a daughter of Alexander Mackenzie, IV. of Achilty, with issue, five sons — Alexander, who married a daughter 
2 CONC of " Murdo Mc Cowil vie Ean Oig " ; Murdo, who married a daughter of Murdo Mackenzie of Sand ; and three others unmarried in 1669. 
2 CONT * John, a clergyman, who married a natural daughter of Alexander Mackenzie, I. of Kilcoy, with issue — four sons and two daughters. He died at Rhynduin in 1666, and is buried at Beauly. 
2 CONT * Katherine Og, who married Fraser of Belladrum, with issue — from whom the Frasers of Achnagairn and Seafield. 
2 CONT * Isabel, who married first, Alastair Og Macdonald of Cuidreach, brother-german to Sir Donald Macdonald of Sleat, and ancestor of the Macdonalds of Cuidreach and Kingsburgh, Isle of Skye. She married, secondly, Hugh Macdonald of S
2 CONC kirinish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John had also a natural son, Kenneth Buy Mackenzie, by a woman named Fraser, who married a daughter of Alexander Mackenzie, IV. of Achilty ; and two natural daughters, one of whom married Donald Bain, Seaforth's Chamberlain in the
2 CONC  Lewis, killed in the battle of Auldearn in 1645 ; the other, Margaret, in 1640, married Alexander, "second lawful son" of John Mackenzie, IV. of Hilton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Talladale in 1628, in the 80th year of his age ; was buried in the old churchyard of Gairloch, and succeeded by his eldest surviving son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/404/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 404
2 CONT --------------------
