2 CONT ===Evidence from the Laing Charters===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 April 1622: Precept under the quarter seal by King James the Sixth for infefting in terms of a charter, John Inglis, servant of Sir George Erskine of of Invertiel, knight, in liferent, and his daughter Katherine Inglis, her 
2 CONC heirs, etc. in fee, the lands of Ruthvens, Balbirnie, and Brigton of Ruthvens, all lying in the sheriffdom of Forfar; which lands belonged to James Crichton, son of the late Sir James Crichton of Ruthvens, and were apprised from h
2 CONC im on 2nd April instant by a decree in favour of John Inglis and his daughter. Precept dated at Holyroodhouse, 24th April 1622. [https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaing00edin/page/458/mode/1up Laing Charters: charter number 19
2 CONC 04]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 January 1659: Extract disposition by John, Earl of Loudoun, to James Creichtoun of Ruthven, of teinds of lands and barony of Ruthven in parish of Ruthven, teinds of lands of Kilry, Over Sand Easter Craig and other lands in p
2 CONC arish of Glenisla, lands of Brewhouse of Eassie, in parish of Eassie, and other lands in parish of Lintrathen, all in sheriffdom of Forfar. Registered in Books of Exchequer, 14 Jan 1659. Tag, seal gone. [http://catalogue.nrscotlan
2 CONC d.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD243%2f18%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=craigs&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Writs and legal papers relating mainly to families of Logie Wishart, K
2 CONC inloch of Kilry and Kinloch of Kinloch, reference GD243/18/1]'''
