1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John (Grant) Grant Vth of Glenmoriston is a member of Clan Grant.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, only child and heir, was born likely born in Glenmoriston, Inverness-shire, Scotland, to Patrick Grant, 4th Laird of Glenmoriston and his wife, Margaret Fraser, alleged daughter of Fraser of Culbockie.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married an unknown daughter of Fraser of Struie .[2][1] They had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John (d. 30 Nov 1736), 6th Laird of Glenmoriston, m. 1st a daughter of Baillie of Dunean, m. 2nd, in about 1698, Janet, a daughter of Sir Ewen Cameron of Lochiel.[1]
2 CONT # Alexander, in Blairy[1]
2 CONT # Patrick.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT n 1644, John is named "apparent of Glenmoriston" on the Valuation Roll of the county of Inverness. His lands were valued at £2482, 1s. 8d. Scots.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John likely died in Glenmoriston, Inverness-shire, Scotland, before 23 Jun 1703.[1] The location of his burial is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Peter Anderson in Major Alpin's Ancestors and Descendants (1904), Patrick IV (his father) also had two daughters:
2 CONT * Mary, married Colin Chisholm of Knockfin 24 June 1662.[3]
2 CONT * Janet (d. 6 March 1694), married Hugh Fraser, the second of Belladrum.[3]
2 CONT While sources used for Anderson's text are listed in the preface of his book, with numerous credible sources noted, he also relied on the work of Bernard Burke in The Landed Gentry of Great Britain and Ireland. Given that the info
2 CONC rmation provided in his book was not specifically cited, there is no way of knowing from which source Patrick's alleged daughters were retrieved. Moreover, this particular information could not be corroborated by other sources. Th
2 CONC ere is no credible evidence that John, 5th Laird of Glenmoriston, had any siblings. Further research is needed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
