1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAJOR GEORGE CRICHTON OF ABEKIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Major George Crichton of Abekie married Jean Stewart, the daughter of Sir James Stewart of Eday and his wife Margaret Lyon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/574/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 574]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1637: Signature of the lands of Ardbeikie granted to Capt George Crichton (Creighton) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f22%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=George+Cricht
2 CONC on&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/22/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 November 1665: INSTRUMENT of SASINE, dated 3rd November, 1665, on a disposition by Francis Duguid of Auchenhuiff to George Crichton, lawful son of George Crichtoune of Arbekie, of the lands of Cluny, Kennartie and Brownhill. 
2 CONC Witnesses, James Mortoune, miller of Clunie, James Huntar in Kenartie, Robert Burnet in Brownhill, James Hunre, servitor of Francis Duguid of Auchenhuf, Alexander Huntar, servitor of the said George Crichtoune, William Auchinleck,
2 CONC  clerk, of the diocese of Brechin, and notary public. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f30%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+crichton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Record
