1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John, seventeenth Earl of Crawford</strong>, who assumed the dignity after the forfeiture of Earl Ludovic, was retoured heir to his father Robert, Lord Lindsay of the Byres, 1 October 1616, and by letters patent dated 8 M
2 CONC ay 1613, he was created <strong>Earl of Lindsay</strong> and <strong>Lord Parbroath</strong>... He was also created in 1641 an Extraordinary Lord of Session and a Commissioner of the Treasury...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died in 1678 at Tynninghame, and was succeeded by his fourth but eldest surviving son. He married Margaret, daughter of James, second Marquess of Hamilton."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft#page/34/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. III, page 35-36
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 312
