1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lindsay of Kilbirnie is the fifth but second surviving so of John, first Earl of Lindsay, Lord Parbroath, who succeeded as the seventeenth Earl of Crawford, and his wife Lady Margaret Hamilton. He is said to have been b
2 CONC orn in September 1646. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefou02paulgoog/page/n50/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 36]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lindsay of Kilbirnie and his wife Margaret Crawford died intestate. The Scots Peerage account of the family reports that they died in October 1681, but this is wrong. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paulu
2 CONC oft/page/174/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 174] They actually died in October 1680. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Patrick Lindsay of Kilburnie, and Dame Margaret Craufurd, spouses, parish of Kilburnie, 
2 CONC reference CC9/7/44] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138907386947& Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and inventory of the deceased: "Mr Patrick Lindesay of Kilbirnie and Dame Margarit Craufurd spouses" was given up on 3 September 1681 by: "ane noble Earle Charles Earle of Haddingtoune tutor dative and upgi
2 CONC ver forsd in name & behalf of Johne Craufurd eldest lawfull sone to the defuncts in respect of his pupillaritie & lesse age". On 23 September 1681 Mr. Robert Mayne, fiar of Lochwood, acted himself as cautioner for the Earl of Hadd
2 CONC ington, and confirmation was granted to him on 20 October 1681. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Patrick Lindsay of Kilburnie, and Dame Margaret Craufurd, spouses, parish of Kilburnie, reference CC9/7/44]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138907386947& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138907135941& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138906815891& Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lindsay married Margaret Crawford, one of the daughters and heiresses of Sir John Crawford of Kilbirnie. He is said to have assumed the name and arms of Crawford of Kilbirnie, under the terms of a bond of tailzie execut
2 CONC ed by his father-in-law, but it is difficult to reconcile this statement with the evidence reviewed here. [Note] [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/174/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 174]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Lindsay and Margaret Crawford were married on 27 December 1664: "in the kirk of Halyroodhous" in the Canongate parish, near Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. Margaret may have been residing at Ceres in Fife in the peri
2 CONC od leading up to her marriage for she was booked for proclamation of marriage there, rather than at the Canongate. Her marriage record at the Canongate reads as follows: "Tuysday 27 December 1664. The same day Mr Patrick Lindsay s
2 CONC econd sone to the Earle of Craufurd and Mistris Margaret Craufurd heretrix of Kilburnie were lawfullie married in the kirk of Halyroodhous be Mr James Kid minister thrat and that on a testimonial of their proclamatioun from Sires 
2 CONC kirk subt be Mr William Row minister thr and Mr David Christison sessioun clerk daited the 25 December 1664". [National Records of Scotland, Canongate Marriages, 1645-93, reference OPR.685/3/13] [https://www.geni.com/documents/vie
2 CONC w?doc_id=6000000138924649892& Image of Canongate Marriage Record at Canongate] The marriage record at Ceres in Fife reads as follows: "[1664] Decr 18 Mr Patrick Lyndsay second son to the truly noble & honourable Lord Earle of Crau
2 CONC furd Lord Lyndsay and Mistris Margaret Craufurd heretrix of Kilbirne were proclaimed [ - ] and [ -] on the Lords day following they were married on 27 Decr in Edinburgh". [National Records of Scotland, Ceres Marriages, 1620-1700, 
2 CONC reference OPR.415/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138926690827& Image of Ceres Marriage Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Crawford-of-Kilbirnie-first-Viscount-Garnock/6000000014169740140?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591996135432&through=6000000014166503533
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Lindsay/6000000027376662307?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591996457610&through=6000000014166266587
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Magdalen-Lindsay/6000000027376706564?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591996542509&through=6000000014166503533
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Lindsay/6000000024024057356?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1591996728050&through=6000000014166503533
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 June 1663: Crown charter of confirmation and novodamus to Margaret Crawfurd, eldest daughter of Sir John Crawfurd of Kilbirnie, kt, of the barony of Kilbirnie. [RMS, 1660-1668, no 439]. [Tag]. (With precept under the Quarter
2 CONC  Seal. [Tongue and seal gone]). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f469&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+crawfurd&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1650&dt=1680&di=y  National Records of Scotl
2 CONC and, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/469]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1665: Charter of confirmation and novodamus granted by Margaret Crawford, Lady of Kilbirnie and PATRICK LINDSAY, youngest lawful son of John, Earl of Crawford and Lindsay, her husband for his interest in favour of Will
2 CONC iam Hamilton, his heirs and assignees whomsoever of certain lands, to hold of them, their heirs and successors in free blench farm for payment yearly of 2s Scots if asked. Dated at the Castle of Strathous, 31st July 1667 [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f3%2f27%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1650&dt=1675&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family,
2 CONC  Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/3/27/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1669: Extract decree at the instance of Margaret Crafoord of Kilburnie and PATRICK LINDSAY, second son of John, Earl of Crawfoord, her spouse, against the heirs of taillie of deceased Sir John Crafoord of Kilburnie, 
2 CONC declaring a disposition by the pursuers of the lands of Estergreenock in the barony of Renfrew and lands of Cartisburne in the barony of Greenock to be valid despite the terms of a bond of tallie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.
2 CONC uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f470&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1650&dt=1675&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD2
2 CONC 0/1/470]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 August 1669: Bond by PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNY to Thomas Crawford, merchant in Glasgow, to cause Margaret Crawford, spouse of said Patrick, to ratify a disposition to said Thomas of the lands of Carsburne and to deliver th
2 CONC e writs. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f471&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls o
2 CONC f Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/471]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 August 1671: Discharge of various debts by Thomas Crawfurd of Carsburne, merchant burgess of Glasgow, to Margaret Craufuird of Kilbirnie and PATRICK LINDSAY, her husband, in consideration of the sale to the said Thomas of th
2 CONC e lands of Carsburne. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f472&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/472]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1673: Charter of resignation and novodamus granted by Margaret Crawford and PATRICK LINDSAY, her spouse in favour of Captain William Hamilton and his foresaids of the foresaid lands; to hold of them as superiors in 
2 CONC free blench farm for payment yearly of the above blench duty of 2s Scots. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f3%2f27%2f15&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&
2 CONC df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/3/27/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1673: Extract process of adjudication at the instance of PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNIE against Richard Cunynghame of Glengarnock, son of deceased Richard Cunynghame thereof, in respect of the barony of Glengarnock in the
2 CONC  parish of Kilbirnie and the lands of Robertland and others in real warrandice. (Allowance endorsed, dated 27 August 1673). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f624&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/624]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 August 1673: Signature of the lands of Glengarnock granted to Patrick Lindsay (Lindesay). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f97%2f55&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay
2 CONC &ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1646&dt=1680&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/97/55]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 August 1673: Contract by which Richard Cuninghame of Glengarnock, with consent of his curators, renounces the reversion in terms of no 624 in favour of PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNIE and dispones the lands to the said Patrick. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f625&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow
2 CONC  (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/625]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''October 1675: Bond by PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNEY to Robert Faa, steward-depute of the regality of St Androis, and Janet Ninian, his spouse. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f
2 CONC 1%2f474&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/474]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 April 1677: Bond by PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNY to Matthew Miller, apothecary in Kilmarnock. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f475&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+lin
2 CONC dsay&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1660&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/475]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    12
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 September 1678: Signed inventory of writs of the forty shilling lands of Cartsburne (1628-1656) sold by Margaret Crawfurd, Lady Killbirney, and MR> PATRICK LYNDSAY, her husband, to Thomas Craufurd of Cartsburn. [http://catal
2 CONC ogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f476&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+crawfurd&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1650&dt=1680&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford 
2 CONC Priory), reference GD20/1/476]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    13
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 January 1691: Precept from Chancery in favour of John Crawfurd of Kilbirnie as heir to his mother, Margaret Crawfurd, relict of MR PATRICK LINDSAY OF KILBIRNIE, in the barony thereof in the bailiary of Cuninghame and sheriff
2 CONC dom of Ayr, the lands of Minnock and Gill in the parish of Dalry annexed thereto and the privilege of a burgh of barony. [Tongue]. (With extract instrument of sasine, dated 6 May and registered GRS 5 June 1691). [http://catalogue.
2 CONC nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f482&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+crawfurd&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1681&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Prior
2 CONC y), reference GD20/1/482]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: "The Garnock family assumed the surname and arms of Crawford of Kilburnie, in honour of their ancestress, and retained them until their succession to the Earldom." [https://archive.org/details/livesoflindsayso02crawuoft/p
2 CONC age/139/mode/1up Lives of the Lindsays II: 139]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
