2 CONT JOHNSTOUNE JOHN THOMAS JOHNSTOUNE/MARIE IRVING M 29/11/1649 190/ 10 5 Dyce
2 CONT
2 CONT "...who, as chronicled in the Krik Session Registers, was on 18th May, 1701, by the Heritors and Elders of Newhills, unanimously named "Paroch Baillie," - an office not now known in the parochial economy of North Britain..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Alexander married John Johnston, son of Thomas Johnston and Mary Irvine. [1] They were married 23 Nov 1672 at St Nicholas, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT *"His eldest son, Sir William Johnston of that Ilk, fifth Baronet of Caskieben, became, circa 1700, an Advocate in Aberdeen. Having, about the end of 1725, become insolvent, the last remnant of the old family estates was, a few ye
2 CONC ars thereafter, adjudge and sold."
2 CONT * "John, younger son of John of Bishoptown and Mrs. Margaret Alexander, his wife, was for several years in occupation of the farm of Bishopstown, or Bishops Clinterty, in Newhills parish; he as also joint tacksman, along with his 
2 CONC bachelor brother, Thomas Johnston, for the farm of Standingstones, in the parish of Dyce. The wife of John Johnston, now under notice, was Isobel Marnoch, "the Maiden of Balnagask, " i.e, the eldest unmarried daughter of the tenan
2 CONC t of the that farm, situated in the parish of Nigg, Kincardineshire."
2 CONT * bachelor brother, Thomas Johnston
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Johnston-8379
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile was initially connected to parents Arthur Johnston (1587-1641) and Barbara Gordon (abt.1600-1650). Since the father supposedly died in 1641, he can't be the father of this person with a 1649 birthdate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps birth of one is mixed with death of another? See: Find A Grave: Memorial #147834206 and [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/28528657:9289 Ancestry Record 9289 #28528657.] Name:	John Johnston/ alleged parent 
2 CONC of Penelope
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave: Memorial #147834206 is for John of Bishopstown Johnston, b 1649 Aberdeenshire, Scotland, died 1716 Scotland, son of Thomas Johnston 1598-1658 amd Mary D Irvine 1626-1659. [1]
