1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the  same as https://www.geni.com/people/James-Johnston-Sr/6000000007191834406?through=6000000174137060865 who married https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Alexander/6000000126032953873
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Irvine bore to the laird of Craig Johnston, besides daughters, four sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) James Johnston, litater of Aberdeen, born in the parish of Dyce, July 1656.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Jean Ogilvy married James Johnston, contract date 5 November 1690, and died 14 March 1716 as the wife of James Johnston, litster.  He was the son of Thomas “of Craig” Johnston and his wife, Mary Irvine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son was William Johnston, burgess, Pewterer in Aberdeen, who became proprietor of Badiefurrow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical account of the family of Johnston of that Ilk, formerly of Caskieben, in the shire of Aberdeen, and of its principal branches.” by Johnston, Alexander, Writer to the Signet. Page 40. [https://archive.org/details/genea
2 CONC logicalacco1832john/page/40/mode/1up Archive.Org]
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the Family of James Johnston, Litster in Aberdeen.  (XI.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT supra, page 17. I. — James Johnston, litster in Aberdeen (E E. App.), was  the fourth and youngest son of Thomas of Craig, by Mrs. Mary Irvine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT St. Nicholas Parish Record. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Miss Jean Ogilvie, by whom he had three sons,  viz. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1st. Alexander. 
2 CONT *2d. William. 
2 CONT *3d. John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And two daughters, 
2 CONT *1st. Mary. 
2 CONT *2d. Jean. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The after history of these children is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Jean Ogilvie or Johnston died in March 1716.  Extract Burgh The date of James' death is also unknown ; he was alive anno  1704.  Extract Burgh, Records of Aberdeen  1704. 
2 CONT
