2 CONT *litster (plural litsters) (archaic, Britain, Scotland) A dyer. quotations 1995, Richard H. Saunders, John Smibert: Colonial America's First Portrait Painter, Yale University Press (1995), →ISBN, pages 1-2: But it was the woolen i
2 CONC ndustry that provided the elder Smibert with a livelihood, for as a litster he spent his days dyeing wool, which was then woven into cloth
