2 CONT * Disputed Origins:  https://www.geni.com/people/James-Johnson-Sr/6000000007191834406 is seen as the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Johnston-of-Craig/6000000013134916306?through=6000000174137060865 & https://www.geni.co
2 CONC m/people/Mary-Irvine/6000000000114928331?through=6000000174137060865, who is seen in Scottish records and genealogies  as https://www.geni.com/people/James-Johnston-lister-in-Aberdeen/6000000174130939083?through=600000000719183440
2 CONC 6.  This James married  https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Ogilvy/6000000174136639029?through=6000000174137060865 in 1690, and was recorded as her  husband when she died in Aberdeen in 1716. The theory is that the James in Abderdeen
2 CONC  was the son of “that” James, the immigrant to Virginia, and therefore, “this” James was the grandson of Thomas of Craig and not his youngest son.  However, DNA testing has '''disproven''' Lorand Johnston's claim of Caskieben desc
2 CONC ent, and this is accepted by Clan Johnston USA.
