1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 February 1666: Isobel Maitland, daughter of Thomas M., minister at Garwald, and spouse of William Johnstone of Laverocklaw. [National Records of Scotland Register of Deeds for 1666. Grantee, [Nature of Deed] Renunciation. [Da
2 CONC te of Recording]  6 February 1666. [Office] Mack., volume 15, page 358] [https://archive.org/details/indexes500scotuoft/indexes500scotuoft/page/241/mode/1up Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Lifted from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Maitland-30 and then edited 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel (also spelled Issobell) was born on 24 November 1626 in Berwickshire, Scotland  to parents Rev. Thomas Maitland and Margaret (Durie) Maitland. [1] . She was Christened on 3 Dec 1626 in Haddington, Haddingtonshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. William Johnstone married Isabel Maitland,[1] daughter of Rev. Thomas Maitland.  Isabel Maitland,   b. 24 Nov 1626,   d. 1686  (Age 59 years)  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	3 sons and 3 daughters: "James, John, William, Margaret, Isabel, and a daughter unnamed." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Johnston, of Spotswood,   d. 22 Jun 1690, New Jersey. No known wife or children. I 
2 CONT # Marjorie Johnston  (–1682) d.  At Sea.  Married James Hume.
2 CONT # Dr. John Johnstone (1661–1732) b. Cal 1661, Scotland d. 6 Sep 1732, Perth Amboy, Middlesex, New Jersey.  Married Eupham Scot.
2 CONT #  Margaret Johnstone,   d. Aft 1700
2 CONT # Elizabeth or Isabel  Johnston (1663-?) [2] [3]
2 CONT # William Johnstone (1666–1692) [4] [5] Greyfriars Kirk, Edinburgh, Scotland.  No known wife or children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen Vertie (Johnstone) Wallace (1659–1701) Is seen without supporting evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away in 1687 in Haddington, Lothian, Scotland and is buried at the Saint Marys Parish Churchyard, Haddington, East Lothian, Scotland. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Rev. William Johnstone, A. M., graduated at St. Andrews, Edinburgh, June 5, 1638; was ordained minister at Lauder, 1652; translated to Coldstream, 1659; deprived by Parliament June 11, and by Privy Council, Oct. 1, 1662; died at 
2 CONC Hadington Abbey, 1670, or ’71. Will dated December 14, 1670; proved February 23, 1671. … His wife died in 1686. His children were: James, John, William, Margaret, Isabel, and a daughter unnamed.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized at Haddington on Dec. 3, 1626.
2 CONT
2 CONT “This source is to show that the the father of isabel Maitland Johnston is Rev. Thomas Maitland (1593-1637] a member of the clergy, who married Margaret Durie, and whose father is John Maitland but not the John Maitland, 1st Lord 
2 CONC of Thurlestane, husband of Jean Fleming, Countess of Cassilas, Lady Kennedy (a direct descendant of Robert the Bruce, King of Scotland).”….excerpted , Peerage of Scotland; https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:150
2 CONC ?rgn=div1;submit=Search;subview=detail;type=simple;view=fulltext;q1=thirlestane
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=118688318 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 28 2016, 2:28:03 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT # "Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae; the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation". Page 41.  < [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiaesc02scot/page/40/mode/1up Archive.Org] > Coldstream.  WILLIAM JOHNS
2 CONC TONE of Laverocklaw, M.A. (St Andrews, 5th June 1638); ord. to Lauder in 1652; trans, and adm. in 1659 ; deprived by Act of Parliament 11th June, and Decreet of Privy Council 1st Oct. 1662 ; died before 2nd April 1685. He marr. Is
2 CONC abel Maitland, probably of the Lauderdale family, and had issue— James, his heir ; Margaret, assisted by the Presb. in 1700 as " the daughter of an outed minister " ; William, buried in Greyfriars, Edinburgh, 17th March 1692. — [S
2 CONC i/n. (Kelso Presb.) Beg. ; Lothian Syn. Reg. ; Edin. Reg. Sas. ; Wodrow's Hist. ; Inq. Ret. Gen.., Berwick, 420, and Gen., 6634.]
2 CONT # http://hdhdata.org/docs/Eupham_Scot_and_Dr_John_Johnstone_by_Edith_Herbert_Mather.pdf page 7.  John Johnstone was the second son (James, of Spotswood being the eldest) of the Rev. William Johnstone of Laverlocklaw, in Berwickshi
2 CONC re, and his wife, Isabel Maitland.  
