2 CONT Eldest son of Edmund; died in mother's lifetime; Gentleman in 1st Troop of Horse Guards under Sir Thomas Armstrong (executed 1684), Cornet in Regiment of Horse under Earl of Plymouth 13 June 1685; promoted to Lieutenant 6 July 168
2 CONC 5 for saving Sarsfield's life at Marston Moor; attainted by the Irish Parliament in 1689; wounded 29 July 1693 at Landon; wounded at Battle of Hochstadt 1704 and made Major; later made Lieutenant-Colonel; died unmarried at Ghent a
2 CONC ged 77 - John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the Family of Armstrongs', continued by the Rev. W. A. Armstrong, 1813).
