1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Colonel, of Co. Kildare, wounded at the Battle of Hackstet, died in 1722 aged 80 - 'Pedigree of Armstrong of Mangerton in Scotland' (National Library of Ireland GO Ms. 171). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Stonestown; Lieutenant 13th Regiment of Foot 1685; Captain 1697; Major 1700; Lieutenant-Colonel; retired 1709/10 on being refused a regiment; bought Morristown Co. Kildare; Justice of the Peace; died 1722 aged 79 - John Armst
2 CONC rong, 'The Pedigree of the Family of Armstrongs' (National Library of Ireland Ms. 5216). "He married Lady Westhaw of the noble family of Sandilands in Scotland but by her who died many years before him he had no issue, so he left 
2 CONC his estate to Edmund the eldest son of his brother William" - John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the Family of Armstrongs', continued by the Rev. W. A. Armstrong, 1813), p. 10.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Twin with Hugh, served with credit under the Duke of Marlborough, and attained the rank of col. He m. Lady Westray, of the noble family of Sandilands, in Scotland, but had no issue. Colonel Armstrong d. in 1722, aged 80, leaving 
2 CONC his estate at Morristown, co. Kildare, to Edmund, the eldest son of his brother William" - http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera00inburk#page/38/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT A death date of 1721 was previously given: possibly this is Old Style.
