2 CONT * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Armstrong_%28British_Army_officer%29 John Armstrong (British Army officer)]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia.
2 CONT * [Minorca] A Correct Map of the Island of Minorca By John Armstrong Esqr. Engineer in Ordinary to his Majesty with many Additions and Improvements From the late surveys. . . . 1794 < [https://www.raremaps.com/gallery/detail/71522
2 CONC /minorca-a-correct-map-of-the-island-of-minorca-by-john-a-laurie-whittle link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT This John Armstrong, according to Wikipedia and Burke, had nothing to do with the island of Minorca. It was another [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Armstrong/6000000037541660306 John Armstrong from County Offaly, Ireland, b. 170
2 CONC 6,] who was governor of Minorca and who created a map of the island.
2 CONT
