1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Michael the third son of Robert was born the 28th April 1678, and in 1698 entered himself without his father's knowledge in a regiment of Dragoons in Ireland (Inniskillen)... Having served the Crown faithfully as 
2 CONC a brave Officer for the space of 49 years, when the last rebellion in Scotland was extinguished, he sold his Troop and retired from the Army" - John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the family of Armstrong', continued by the Rev. W. A.
2 CONC  Armstrong (no imprint, 1813), p. 26.
2 CONT
2 CONT An alternative birth date of 17 April 1678 is given in Registered Pedigrees (National Library of Ireland GO MS 171).
