1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Of Curraghstown, Co. Meath; Captain in Lord Brabazon's Regiment - 'Pedigree of Armstrong of Mangerton in Scotland' (National Library of Ireland GO Ms. 171).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Captain Wm. Charlton of Lord Barrymore's regiment of foot. He served in Spain all the war and selling his company a few years after the peace of Utrecht, retired to his estate at Curraghstown in the County of Meath, and building 
2 CONC a good house there called the place Mount Charlton. He died in 1735 aged 63 years" - John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the family of Armstrong', continued by the Rev. W. A. Armstrong (no imprint, 1813), p. 20.
