2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE For his survey work, the Proprietors gave him large grants of land including seven hundred acres in Monmouth County where he founded the town of Freehold (which broke off and became Marlboro). He established his home in a Quaker s
3 CONC ettlement near Topanemus where he helped to build a meeting house in which he preached to the people on the Quaker faith.
