1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Erskine,_Earl_of_Mar_(1585%E2%80%931654)_
2 CONT
2 CONT ===JOHN, EARL OF MAR===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/623/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, V, pp. 623-25]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John, Earl of Mar, married, as his second wife, Jean Mackenzie, daughter of George, Earl of Seaforth. The marriage contract is dated [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07paul#page/508/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, VII, p
2 CONC . 508] Following the death of her husband she married Andrew, Lord Fraser. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/118/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, IV,  p. 118]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John, Earl of Mar</strong>, who succeeded, was apparently the only child of his father's first marriage with Anna Drummond. He is first referred to in the will made by his father on 1 April 1608... On 2 June 1610 he was m
2 CONC ade a Knight of Bath, when Prince Henry was created Prince of Wales, and during the later years of his father's life he acted as his agent at Court...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...The date of the Earl's death is not certain, some authorities stating he died in 1654, others alleging 1653. There are indications which suggest he died between January and October 1653. The family genealogist of 1709 asserts t
2 CONC hat he became blind before his death...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...This Earl of Mar married, 6 February 1610, Jean Hay, second daughter of Francis, ninth Earl of Erroll. She survived him, made her will at Alloa on 6, and died on 14 May 1668."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/622/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. V, page 623-624
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
