2 CONT   Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT George Seton, styled as Lord Seton was born on 15 May 1613 the son of George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton and Lady Anne Hay. He was their second child, the first was also named George but died before this George was born. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of George Seton, Lord Seton and Lady Henrietta Gordon was signed on 19 October 1639. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 4 June 1648 at age 35. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Philiphaugh in 1645, where he was captured by the Parliamentarians.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sources 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. 
