1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Thomas Nicolson, Baronet [S 1637] of Carnock</strong>, son and heir; born 10 June 1628; succeeded to the Baronetcy, 8 January 1646. He married Margaret, daughter of Alexander (Livingstone), 2nd Earl of Linlithgow [S],
2 CONC  by his 2nd wife, Mary, daughter of William (Douglas), Earl of Angus [S]. He died 24 July 1664. His widow married in 1666, as his 4th wife, Sir George Stirling, of Keir, who died s.p. 1667. She married thirdly, in 1668, as his 1st
2 CONC  wife, Sir John Stirling, of Keir of Cawdor, who died 1684. She died 1674."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n443/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 424
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir John Houston, Baronet [S. 1668], of Houston, s. and h. ; was M.P. for Linlithgowshire (three Paris.), 1708-15 ; Commissary of Glasgow ; suc. to the Baronetcy in Dec. 1717. He m. Margaret, da. of Sir John Shaw, 2d Baronet [S. 
2 CONC 1687], of Greenock, by Margaret, da. of Sir Thomas Nicolson, 2d Baronet [S. 1637] of Carnock. He d. 11 Feb. 1722, " in the flower of his age," leaving his estate burdened with some 200,000 debt. His widow d. (a year before her son
2 CONC ) 29 Jan. 1750."
