2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1641: Contract between James, Lord Boyd, uncle and heir to the late Robert, Lord Boyd, his nephew, on the one part and Dame Anna Fleming, Lady Boyd, younger, relict of Robert, Lord Boyd, with consent of her curators.
2 CONC  Dated at Glasgow, 2 Dec 1641. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f695&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=anna+Fleming&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers
2 CONC , Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/695]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 December 1645: Discharge by Dame Anna Fleming, Lady Ramsay with consent of George, Lord Ramsay, now her spouse, to James, Lord Boyd, of 600 marks tack duty of the one half of Meddrois. Dated at Dalhousie, 8 Dec 1645. [http://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f727&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Meddrois&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/727]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1646: Discharge by Dame Anna Fleming, Lady Ramsay, with the consent of her husband to Sir William Cochrane of Cowden, knight, in name of James, Lord Boyd, of 1,200 marks tack duty of Meddrois. Dated at Edinburgh 17 
2 CONC Nov 1646. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f730A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Meddrois&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, r
2 CONC eference GD8/730A]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1647: Discharge by Dame Anna Fleming, Lady Ramsay, with the consent of her husband, to Sir William Cochrane of Cowden, and James, Lord Boyd, of 600 marks tack duty of Meddrois. Dated at Dalhousie, 24 Jun 1647. [http://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f743&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Meddrois&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/743]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 October 1647: Disposition by Dame Anna Fleming, sometime spouse to Robert, Lord Boyd, now spouse to George, Lord Ramsay, Master of Dalhousie, to James, Lord Boyd of her life-rent right to the lands and barony of Growgar. Dat
2 CONC ed at Edinburgh, 26 Oct 1647. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f746&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=anna+Fleming&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers,
2 CONC  Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/746]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1647: Discharge by Dame Anna Fleming, Lady Ramsay, with the consent of her husband, to James, Lord Boyd, of £423 10s 3d tack duty of the lands of Meddrois. Dated at Dalhousie, 6 Dec 1647. [http://catalogue.nrscotland
2 CONC .gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f745&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Meddrois&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/745]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 May 1648: Discharge by Dame Anna Fleming. Lady Ramsay, to James, Lord Boyd, of 600 marks of the tack duty of Meddrois. Dated at Cumbernauld, 29 May 1648. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?re
2 CONC ference=GD8%2f751&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Meddrois&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/751]'''
