1 OCCU Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland], office of Captain of the Yeomen of the Guard between 1632 and 1659, 2nd Earl of Kinnoull, 2nd Viscount of Dupplin, 2nd Lord Hay of Kinfauns
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p2214.htm#i22132
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of George Hay, 2nd Earl of Kinnoull and Lady Anne Douglas was signed on 7 September 1622. He died on 5 October 1644 at Whitehall, London, England. He was the son of George Hay, 1st Earl of Kinnoull and 
2 CONC Margaret Halyburton. He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland]. He held the office of Captain of the Yeomen of the Guard between 1632 and 1659. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Kinnoull [S., 1633] on 16 Decem
2 CONC ber 1634. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount of Dupplin [S., 1633] on 16 December 1634. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Hay of Kinfauns [S., 1633] on 16 December 1634.
