1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://thepeerage.com/p2596.htm#i25957
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born in Smithfield, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT George was a Lt. Colonel. in the Army, and a Minister of Parliament for the Isle of Orkney prior to his succesion to the Earldom in 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Earl of Morton.
2 CONT
2 CONT It's a fact George had 1 illagitimate child. William ( Domine Douglass )
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earls of Morton were keen Freemasons. James Douglas (1702-03-1768), fourteenth Earl Morton, president of the Royal Society, Freemason, was son of George Douglas, thirteenth earl, and second wife Frances Adderley, his spouses b
2 CONC eing firstly Agatha Halyburton and secondly Bridget Heathcote. Burke's Peerage and Baronetage for Radnor. Valentine, British Establishment, Vol. 1, pp. 94-95. This fourteenth Earl was Grand Master Mason of Scotland 1739-1740, Gran
2 CONC d Master of Lodge of England, March 1741-1742. GEC, Peerage, Morton, pp. 299-301, Aberdeen, p. 17; Abercorn, p. 8. The Freemason, Sholto Charles Douglas, fifteenth Earl Morton (1732-1774), was son of the fourteenth earl and Agatha
2 CONC  Halyburton, his first wife being Katherine Hamilton; he was Grand Master Mason of Scotland, 1755-1757, Grand Master of Grand Lodge of England, 1757-1761.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT (Research):George was a Lt. Colonel. in the Army, and a Minister of Parliament for the Isle of Orkney prior to his succesion to the Earldom in 1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Earl of Morton.
2 CONT
2 CONT It's a fact George had 1 illegitimate child. William ( Domine Douglass )
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earls of Morton were keen Freemasons. James Douglas (1702-03-1768), fourteenth Earl Morton, president of the Royal Society, Freemason, was son of George Douglas, thirteenth earl, and second wife Frances Adderley, his spouses b
2 CONC eing firstly Agatha Halyburton and secondly Bridget Heathcote. (Burke's Peerage and Baronetage for Radnor. Valentine, British Establishment, Vol. 1, pp. 94-95).&nbsp; This fourteenth Earl was Grand Master Mason of Scotland 1739-17
2 CONC 40, Grand Master of Lodge of England, March 1741-1742. (GEC, Peerage, Morton, pp. 299-301, Aberdeen, p. 17; Abercorn, p. 8.)&nbsp; The Freemason, Sholto Charles Douglas, fifteenth Earl Morton (1732-1774), was son of the fourteenth
2 CONC  earl and Agatha Halyburton, his first wife being Katherine Hamilton; he was Grand Master Mason of Scotland, 1755-1757, Grand Master of Grand Lodge of England, 1757-1761.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography:
2 CONT George Douglas, 13th Earl of Morton (1662-1738) was the son of James Douglas, 10th Earl of Morton and Anne Hay. He m.(1) the daughter of Alexander Muirhead and (2) Frances Adderly, daughter of William Adderly, bef. 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT MP Kirkall [Scotland] 1702-1707, (Whig) for Linlithgow 1708-1713, Orkney and Shetland 1713-1715 and 1722-1730. He succeeded his elder brother as 13th Earl of Morton on 22 January 1730. He served as a Representative Peer for Scotla
2 CONC nd between 1730 and 1738.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his 1st Wife, he had:-
2 CONT
2 CONT # A son, who died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Douglas, 13th Earl of Morton and his 2nd wife, Frances Adderly
2 CONT
2 CONT # Colonel Robert Douglas d. 30 Apr 1745
2 CONT # William Douglas, died young.
2 CONT # James Douglas, 14th Earl of Morton b. 1709, d. 12 Oct 1768
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
