1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles Seton, 2nd Earl of Dunfermline (November, 1615-May 11, 1672) was the son of Alexander Seton, 1st Earl of Dunfermline (1555-1622). Charles was a Royalist during the Civil War, and was forced to flee the coun
2 CONC try when Charles I was executed in 1649, only to return with Charles II the next year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Mary Douglas, daughter of William Douglas, 7th Earl of Morton. At his death in 1672, his two sons, Alexander Seton, 3rd Earl of Dunfermline (1642-1677) and James Seton, 4th Earl of Dunfermline (d. 1694) succeeded
2 CONC  him in turn. Both died without issue, and the title became extinct when James Seton was outlawed in 1690.
