1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES, MARQUESS OF MONTROSE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/259/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 259-61]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 June 1681: Articles of marriage between James, Marquess of Montrose, and Lady Christian Lesley, then his spouse, and John, Duke of Rothes, her father, whereby the Marquess is obliged to infeft Lady Christian in a free annuity
2 CONC  of 9000 merks yearly out of lands and barony of Mugdock, Dundaffmuir and Fintry and in the lodging in Glasgow for her dwelling house in satisfaction of all her terce except half of the insight plenishing which the Marquess dispon
2 CONC es to her; the Marquess obliges him to resign the whole Marquisdom of Montrose in favour of the male heirs of the said marriage, which failing to his other male heirs and assignees; if there are no male heirs of the marriage and o
2 CONC ther male heirs succeed, he obliges him to provide the daughters of the marriage as follows: to one daughter, 60 000 merks; if there be two daughters, 50 000 merks to the eldest and 30 000 merks to the younger; if there be three o
2 CONC r more, 40 000 merks to the eldest and 60 000 merks to be divided amongst the rest as their father see fit, payable upon their attaining the age of 16. The Duke of Rothes obliges him to pay the Marquess 50 000 merks in name of toc
2 CONC her, one half payable at Martinmas 1681 and the other half at Whitsunday thereafter, with penalty for each terms failure, accepted in place of all claim Lady Christian might have at her father's decease without prejudice to her of
2 CONC  any claim to benefit of the tailzie made by the Duke of his lands and estate, and the Marquess obliges him to cause his wife to ratify the articles of marriage and contract to be extended thereupon; dated at Holyroodhouse. [https
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fE%2f4%2f4%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marquess+of+montrose&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1670&dt=1684&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graha
2 CONC m Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/E/4/4/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 August 1703: Gift under Privy Seal in favour of Thomas Graham of Balgowan, of escheat of his estate by reason of being denounced rebel for payment of 10,000 merks Scots contained in contract of marriage between deceased Jonat
2 CONC han Urquhart, eldest son and apparent heir of Sir John Urquhart of Cromarty, and deceased Lady Jean Graham, sister of deceased James, Marquess of Montrose, for which sum said Thomas and others were cautioners. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD155%2f220&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+urquhart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1679&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maxtone Graham Family of Cultoquhey, Per
2 CONC thshire, reference GD155/220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
