1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LORD CHARLES GRAHAM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Charles Graham, here treated, is the second son of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Graham-2nd-Marquess-of-Montrose/6000000008640680982?through=6000000029965687343 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Isabel-Douglas/6
2 CONC 000000008640680965 According to William C. Bishop: "while on a tour, or series of visits, through the West of Scotland with his brother Lord Graham, contracted a painful illness, from which, after five months' suffering, he died a
2 CONC t Glasgow on 25 February 1674. He was buried  in Barony churchyard. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/258/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 258]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of birth has not been identified for Lord Charles Graham, here treated. However, he was probably born in the period between 20 October 1657 and February 1669, that is the date upon which his elder brother James
2 CONC  was born and the date of his father's death. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/258/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 258]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1662-64: Accounts mentioning Lord Robert and Lord Charles Graham. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f638&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Charles+Graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1656&dt=
2 CONC 1674&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/6/638]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1672: Extract bond of provision by James, Marquess of Montrose with consent of his curators in favour of his brother, Lord Charles Graham and his three sisters, stating that His Majesty had given Sir John Colquhoun o
2 CONC f Luss a gift of the Marquess' ward, relief and marriage, and that Sir John was bound by his backbond to dispose of the said gift in favour of whomever Isabel, Marchioness of Montrose, David Lord Madderty, Sir William Graham of Br
2 CONC aco, John Graham of Fintry, Patrick Graham of Inchbrakie, George Graham, fiar thereof, James Graham of Orchill, James Graham of Monorgane, deceased Mungo Graeme of Gorthie and George Graham of Pitcairns, or the majority of them st
2 CONC ill alive, should nominate; that there was no portion nor provision made for the Marquess' brother, Lord Charles nor his sisters, although the deceased Marquess had intended £20,000 for Lord Charles Graham, £12,000 to Lady Ann, an
2 CONC d £20,000 equally between Lady Jane and Lady Grizel; that the majority of those named, the Marquess with the consent of his curators, and with the consent of Sir John Colquhoun appoint the whole benefit of the gift to belong to th
2 CONC e Marquess himself with the burden of paying the above mentioned sums to Charles and his sisters when they reach the age of twenty-one (or when the girls marry) if His Majesty makes no provision for them out of his royal bounty. R
2 CONC egistered in the Burgh Court of Perth, 14 Sep 1682. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fH%2f5%2f3%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Charles+Graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1656&dt=1674&di
2 CONC =n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/H/5/3/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 March 1674:  Account of money paid during illness and burial of Lord Charles Graham at Glasgow. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f745&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Charle
2 CONC s+Graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1656&dt=1674&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/6/745]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1674: Account of things supplied for funeral of Lord Charles Graham by David Monteith. With related accounts. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f638&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=Charles+Graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1656&dt=1674&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/6/638]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 August 1674: Account due to David Sharpe, apothecary in Glasgow, for medicines furnished for Lord Charles Graham, ending in embalming the body. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD
2 CONC 220%2f6%2f638&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Charles+Graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1656&dt=1674&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/6/638]'''
2 CONT
