1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Robert-Douglas-Kt-of-Blackerstoun/6000000006717695088?through=4978308592920081650
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Legend has it that John Kimbrough arrived in the Colonies about 1666 with a wife, Mary, said to have been a Douglas, and children John, Jr., Marmaduke and Jane, in the company of a Robert Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I have just found records showing John and Mary (Douglas) Kimbrough as being married in 1660 in Kircaldy, Scotland. There are also the birth records for John, marmaduke and Jane. This ties in with previously known timing for their
2 CONC  immigration to Md. Mary Douglas was born in Kircaldy in Sep of 1645. Her father was Robert Douglas b. 21 Jul 1611 in Edinburgh. Her mother was Margaret Kirkaldie b. 1615 in Kinghorn, Fife. There is a pretty comprehensive record o
2 CONC f that branch of the Douglas,s. I live in southern England now but plan a trip soon to Edinburgh to view the microfiche. Hope this reaches you. Sid Kimbrough sidkimbrough@thebankhouse.net
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
