2 CONT Henry Ker, Lord Ker [1]
2 CONT *M, #24262, 
2 CONT *d. 1 February 1642/43
2 CONT *Last Edited=31 Dec 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Ker, Lord Ker was the son of Robert Ker, 1st Earl of Roxburghe and Jane Drummond.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Margaret Hay, daughter of William Hay, 10th Earl of Erroll and Lady Anne Lyon, on 3 February 1638.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 1 February 1642/43.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was styled as Master of Roxburgh.[1] He was styled as Lord Ker.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Henry Ker, Lord Ker and Lady Margaret Hay
2 CONT *1. Jean Ker+[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 77. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
