2 CONT XVIII. JOHN, fourth earl of Wigton, who got a charter under the great seal,*Johanni domino Fleming, et '''Annae Ker''' sponsae suae, of the earldom of Wigton, lordship of Baldouie, &c. 10th May 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT By the said Anne, a daughter of Henry lord Ker, he had only '''one daughter''',
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady ''Jean'', married to George third earl of Panmure.
2 CONT
2 CONT And dying without male-issue, anno 1668, his estate and honours devolved upon his next surviving brother,
