1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Glamis Castle is one of the most impressive, romantic and reputedly haunted castles in Scotland, home to the Bowes Lyon Earls of Strathmore and Kinghorne for hundreds of years and with a splendid interior, and set in beautiful gar
2 CONC dens and grounds near Forfar in Angus.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Glamis Castle - Historic Houses | Historic Houses
2 CONT By 1372 a castle had been built at Glamis, since in that year it was granted by Robert II to Sir John Lyon, Thane of Glamis, husband of the king's daughter. Glamis has remained in the Lyon (later Bowes-Lyon) family since this time
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lyon, 4th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT The Right Honourable
2 CONT The Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT 4th Earl of Strathmore.jpg
2 CONT John Lyon, 4th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT Born	1663
2 CONT Died	1712
2 CONT Nationality	Scottish
2 CONT Title	4th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT Spouse	Lady Elizabeth Stanhope
2 CONT Children	John Lyon, 5th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT Charles Lyon, 6th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT James Lyon, 7th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT Thomas Lyon, 8th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT 3 additional sons, 3 daughters
2 CONT Parent(s)	Patrick Lyon, 3rd Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne
2 CONT Helen Middleton
2 CONT John Lyon, 4th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne (1663 – 1712) was a Scottish nobleman and peer. He was the son of Patrick Lyon, 3rd Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne. He married Elizabeth Stanhope on 21 September 1691 and was succe
2 CONC eded as Earl by his son John Lyon, 5th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT On 21 September 1691, John married Elizabeth Stanhope, daughter of Lady Elizabeth Butler and possibly Philip Stanhope, 2nd Earl of Chesterfield. There are doubts whether he was indeed the father. In May 1695, almost four years aft
2 CONC er their marriage, he succeeded his father as the 4th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had 10 children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Lyon, Lord Glamis (1692 – September 1709)
2 CONT Philip Lyon, Lord Glamis (29 October 1693 – 18 March 1712), died of smallpox in London; he was unmarried.
2 CONT John Lyon, 5th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne (27 April 1696 – 13 November 1715), was killed at the Battle of Sheriffmuir while fighting for the Jacobite cause. Died unmarried.
2 CONT Charles Lyon, 6th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne (baptised 12 July 1699 – 11 May 1728), was killed in a brawl; he married Lady Susan Cochrane, but had no legitimate issue.
2 CONT Hendrie Lyon (born 1 July 1700), died young.
2 CONT James Lyon, 7th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne (baptised 24 December 1702 – 4 January 1735); a Freemason, he married Mary Oliphant, however, their marriage was childless.
2 CONT Thomas Lyon, 8th Earl of Strathmore and Kinghorne (baptised 6 July 1704 – 18 January 1753), married Jean Nicholson (died 13 May 1778), by whom he had issue. Elizabeth Bowes-Lyon, Queen consort of King George VI was one of his nume
2 CONC rous descendants.
2 CONT Lady Helen Lyon (baptised 8 January 1695 – 19 December 1723), married Robert Stuart, 7th Lord Blantyre; her only son died young
2 CONT Lady Mary Lyon (baptised 16 April 1697 – 26 May 1780), unmarried.
2 CONT Lady Catherine Lyon (baptised 24 April 1707), died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT
