1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1650
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1720
2 ADDR
3 CITY Jedburgh
3 CTRY Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - Thomas Rutherford (c.1650 - 1720) of Edgerston and Hunthill (He also acquired Bonjedward,) married Susanna, daughter and heiress of of Walter Riddell of Minto and Catherine Nisbet of Dirleton. He was succeeded by his eldest so
2 CONC n Sir John. His other children were: Barbara; Catherine; Jean, who secondly married William Douglas of Timpendean in 1718.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 - The third son Thomas RUTHERFURD of that ilk succeeded his father and brother Andrew who d. without lawful issue in 1718 He also acquired the lands of Bonjedward and together with the lands of Hunthill and from Robert Lord Ruth
2 CONC erfurd who likewise to Thomas with the estate the title of Lord Rutherfurd in like manner as it had been assigned to brothers and to him by the Earl of Teviot by virtue the patent which was the only right they had But Thomas estee
2 CONC ming a Scots peerage rather a loss than an advantage contented himself with assigning it in like manner to his son and successor who likewise declined claiming it It was however assumed by Captain John Rutherfurd collateral heir m
2 CONC ale descended from Richard Rutherfurd of Littlehaugh and since by others He m Susanna dau and heiress of Riddell of Minto of the ancient family of Riddell of that ilk by Catherine Nisbet sister to Sir John Nisbet of Dirleton lord 
2 CONC advocate and senator of the College of Justice and had one son and daus.
2 CONT * I John
2 CONT * I Barbara m to William Elliot of Swinside
2 CONT * II Jane m 1st to George Wilkie of Brigghaugh and 2ndly to William Douglas of Timpendean
2 CONT * III Susan m to Robert Alder of Pendrick
2 CONT * IV Agnes m to James Adams of Whitslade
2 CONT * V Violet m to Robert Scott of Falmash
2 CONT
2 CONT (Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Landed Gentry, Volume II M-Z 1847) [2]
2 CONT
