1 NOTE {geni:about_me} All that is currently known about John Clanton:
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1610. Emigrated to the Virginia Colony (James City) on the ship Abraham in October 1635 October. Info says he was 26 yrs old, so 1608/1609 might be more accurate.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Clanton arrived during the 'Dying Times' where disease and death ran rampant, killing 7 out of every 10 people in the colony at this time. John survived this and started a family. :)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source above: Stories from my gramps Richard Masterson and the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT COLDHAM, PETER WILSON. The Complete Book of Emigrants: A Comprehensive Listing Compiled from English Public Records of Those Who Took Ship to the Americas for Political, Religious, and Economic Reasons; of Those Who Were Deported 
2 CONC for Vagrancy, Roguery, or Non-Conformity; and of Those Who Were Sold to Labour in the New Colonies. Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co. 1607-1660. 1988. 600p.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gale Research. Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network, Inc., 2006. Original data: Filby, P. William, ed.. Passenger and Immigration Lists Index, 1500s-1900s. 
2 CONC Farmington Hills, MI, USA: Gale Research, 2006.
2 CONT
2 CONT additional scattered notes: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Bridenbaugh / Tobacco Coast
2 CONT
2 CONT copy of inventory 1624
2 CONT
