2 CONT
2 CONT source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.beginyouradventure.co.uk/forum/comments.php?DiscussionID=210
2 CONT
2 CONT Comment Author  Sharon Bennett-Roach       Comment Time  Jul 18th 2008 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Case ancestors of Thelma Richardson b. 1910, daughter of Forrest Richardson and Alverda Margaret Case.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unknown if in Jamestown; John Clanton b 1610 London, Clandon, England. His son Marmaduke Clanton was born 1637 James City, Virginia, married unknown Briggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the first settlers of the Case line settled in the 1600s in Connecticut, New York and Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT         *************
2 CONT
2 CONT I think this was posted by a distant relative, I'm not tracking it down right now but documenting it in this location for future use.  Anyone feel free to pursue this lead.
2 CONT
2 CONT For one, I'd like to see an explanation for the two conflicting birthplaces, Clandon or Somerlayton?  
2 CONT
2 CONT *************
2 CONT
2 CONT I do NOT "get" addresses in England!  Maybe Caroline could help...
2 CONT
2 CONT There are 9 "Clandon" place names in England, 
2 CONT
2 CONT the one below here is 13.9 mi from Somerlayton, which could reconsile the two reported birthplaces somehow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clandon, Halesworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Clandon, Hall Rd, Wenhaston, Halesworth, Suffolk IP19, UK
2 CONT
2 CONT The sole Somerlayton on Google maps is:
2 CONT
2 CONT Somerleyton
2 CONT
2 CONT Lowestoft, Suffolk, UK
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************************************
