1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===REVEREND MR. GEORGE LYON OF WESTER OGIL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Minister of the Gospel at Longforgan; Burgess and Guild Brother of Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Reverend Mr. George Lyon, Minister of the Gospel at Longforgan, was enrolled as a burgess and guild brother of Glasgow on 17 September 1744. He was admitted in right of his marriage to Margaret Rodger, daughter of the decea
2 CONC sed Hugh Rodger, merchant burgess and guild brother of Glasgow. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso43scotuoft/page/455 Glasgow Burgesses, 1573-1750, p. 455]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>George Lyon of Wester Ogil</strong>, born 26th Aug. 1711, son of William L., min. of Airlie ; educated at Univ. of St Andrews ; licen. by Presb. of Meigle 15th Dec. 1736 ; pres. by George II. ; called 31st May, and ord. 20
2 CONC th Sept. 1738; died 12th Feb. 1793. He is described as a man of " unimpeachable character. His charity, benevolence, and attention to the poor made him extremely useful and much beloved." He marr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) (cont. 23rd Aug. 1739) Catherine (died 1742), daugh. of James Hodge, min. of this parish, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) 15th June 1744, Margaret (died 9th April 1793, aged 76), daugh. of Hugh Rodger, merchant, and Provost of Glasgow, and had issue — 
2 CONT * William of Wester Ogil, born 10th May 1745, died 12th Aug. 1795
2 CONT * Margaret, born 20th April 1746
2 CONT * Hugh of Wester Ogil, captain H.E.I.C.S., born 29th Jan. 1748, died 12th Oct. 1797
2 CONT * Jean, born 12th Sept. 1749
2 CONT * Margaret, born 24th March 1751 (marr. James Playfair, Principal of St Andrews Univ. (q.v.)) ; 
2 CONT * George, born 20th Jan. 1755, died in London 7th Sept. 1812 ; 
2 CONT * Thomas, born 25th July 1756, died 7th Nov. 1763 ; 
2 CONT * James, D.D., min. of Glamis, born 29th March 1759; 
2 CONT * Janet, born 4th Jan. 1762 (marr. George Moncrieff, physician, Perth).
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc05scot#page/352/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. V, page 353
