1 OCCU Handelsman; Merchant, originally a lawyer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Omnämns första gången i Stockholm 1613 i samband med Älvsborgs lösen, då man gör en inventering av invånare i Stockholm. Då nämns Gilbert som besökare hos Tichert Patter(so)n. (källa: Stockholms tankeböcker)
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert was a young lawer when participating in a witch trial. After a controversial trial he was forced to move abroad. He ended up merchant in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert probably lived for a period of time in Tullibole Castle, Scotland, before moving abroad. His children were probably raised in Tulliebole. His son Hans Helleday, who was probably born in Tullibole, moved to Sweden with his 
2 CONC father. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert was the first Halliday (Helgdag, Helleday) of the Swedish branch. His name appears first time in Swedish written documents in 1613.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many prominent people descend from Gilbert Halliday/Helleday, ao. Alfred Nobel, the inventor of dynamite and the founder of the Nobel Price.
2 CONT
