1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 14 Oct 1713 Miln David merchant, Burgess and Guildbrother, by right of father David M., skinner, Burgess and Guildbrother - Collection Edinburgh Burgesses 1701-1760
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation is listed as a Merchant in his marriage registration 1712, Skinner & burgess of Edinburgh in the birth registration of his daughter Rachel in 1717 and a Brewer and Bailie of Portsburgh in the birth registration of his d
2 CONC aughter Dorothea in 1724 where his brother in-law Rev. Mathew Wood was a witness.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Portrait Gallery Exhibit Label Painted in London, this pair of portraits celebrates the success of the Milns. Mr. Miln, in a fashionable powdered wig and a brown velvet suit, is a man of power, whose profitable mercantile business
2 CONC  is indicated by the letter addressed to him and the world of shipping outside the window to which he gestures. Mrs. Miln sports asumptuous and costly blue velvet gown. An exotic African parrot beside her also references her husba
2 CONC nd's wide-ranging trade in luxury goods. Meanwhile, the cherries she holds suggest her future role as a mother.  
