1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard de Lyons born 1242 Warkworth Northhamptonshire England Son of Roger de Lyuns and Joanna de Napton married Emma born 1244 Warkworth Northhamptonshire England
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John de Lyons II(de Lyon), Baron of Warkworth was the son of Sir Richard de Lyons and Emma de Lyons and father of Sir Adam Lyons, Sir John de Lyons III and Sir Richard Lyons. This Noble Peerage was placed on the shoulders of e
2 CONC very Lyon male back to the birth of Sir John Lyon in 1187. First Knighted by King Henry II of England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard de Lyons was born in 1242 in of, Warkworth, Northhamptonshire, England. He married Emma.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma was born in 1244 in of, Warkworth, Northhamptonshire, England. She married Richard de Lyons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Richard de Lyons held lands in Oxford and Bucks 1276, and was father or grandfather of John de Lyons, who 1334 was summoned from Oxfordshire to attend the King with horses and arms at Roxburgh (Rot Scot. L 306). He in 1343 had
2 CONC  charters for lands in Perth and Aberdeen, and from David II and obtained the reversion of the thanage of Glamis. His son Sir John Lyon of Glamis, was Great Chamberlain of Scotland, and from him descended the Lords Glamis, Earls o
2 CONC f Strathmore and Kinghorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This Sir Richard resembles https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-de-Lyoun/6000000009515874245.  Are they supposed to be the same person?  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT In 1294, summoned for service against the Scots, when Edward I imprisoned King John Baliol.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT Date and place of marriage to Emma NN have also been (erroneously?) reported to be 1267 at Marston St. Lawrence, Northamptonshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of death have also been erroneously reported to be circa 1288 at Warkworth, Northamptonshire, England.
2 CONT
