1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET KINLOCH===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Kinloch, here treated, is the daughter of John Kinloch of Cruive. Her father was still alive on 3 July 1478, when he gave certain lands in Fife to his grandson John Sandilands. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeerage
2 CONC foun08pauluoft/page/383 The Scots Peerage VIII: p. 383] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/290 RMS: 1414]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Kinloch, here treated, died before 14 July 1498, before which date her widowed husband had already married his second wife Margaret Ker.  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/396 RMS: 1879]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Kinloch, here treated, married Sir James Sandilands of Calder. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/290 RMS: 1414] The dispensation for the marriage was dated 25 July 1463. [https://archive.org/deta
2 CONC ils/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/383 The Scots Peerage VIII: p. 383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Sandilands-6th-Laird-Of-Calder/6000000002116138070?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1545517607209&through=6000000002116138090
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Christiane-Hepburn/6000000029844968079?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1545517671667&through=6000000002116138090
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1478: Charter by which John Kinloch of Cruvie confirms that he has given certain lands if Fife to his grandson John Sandilands, who is identified as the son and apparent heir of Sir James Sandilands of Calder, who is ide
2 CONC ntified as the son and apparent heir of Sir John Sandilands of Calder.. He reserved his own liferent, and that of Sir James Sandilands, and Sir James's wife Margaret Kinloch. The charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotl
2 CONC and on 23 January 1478-79. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/290 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 1414 on pp. 290-91]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 July 1489: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland, by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms possession of certain lands in Stirlingshire to Sir James Sandilands of Calder, and his wife Margaret Ker. [https://archive.org/
2 CONC details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/396 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 1879 on p. 396]'''
2 CONT
