1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Muriel of Strathearn''', daughter of Malise, Earl of Strathearn and Marjory de Muschamp, was born about 1245 in Scotland and died shortly before 12 November 1291 in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1) William, 5th Earl of Mar (living 1270) 2) James Stewart, 5th Stewart of Scotland (d 1309); his 2nd wife. No issue by marriage with James.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===supporting data===
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malise_II,_Earl_of_Strathearn
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Malise married four times:
2 CONT
2 CONT Firstly, around 1245, to Marjory de Muschamp, daughter and coheiress of Sir Robert de Muschamp by his wife Isabel.[1] They had two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Muriel, born before 1245, married William, Earl of Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uilleam,_Earl_of_Mar
2 CONT
2 CONT When his wife Isabel (also called Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Comyn and Marjory Colham) died in 1267, Uilleam married''' Muriel, the daughter of Maol Íosa II, Mormaer of Strathea'''rn. Uilleam died in 1276, and was succeede
2 CONC d by his son Domhnall.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Stewart,_5th_High_Steward_of_Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT >James [James Stewart, 5th High Steward of Scotland] was married several times. His first wife was Cecilia, daughter of Patrick, Earl of Dunbar (died 1289). James' second wife appears to have been '''Muriel (born 1244), daughter o
2 CONC f Malise, Earl of Strathearn (died 1271)'''. His third wife was Giles, daughter of Walter de Burgh, Earl of Ulster (died 1271), and sister of Richard de Burgh, Earl of Ulster (died 1326).
2 CONT
2 CONT No issue of this marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=8JcbV309c5UC&lpg=PA356&ots=kvoLIVOOb2&dq=sir%20james%20stewart%20of%20preston%20giles%20stewart&pg=PA356#v=onepage&q&f=false page 356] of Magna Carta Ancestry: A Study in Colonial and Medieval 
2 CONC Families, 2nd Edition, 2011 by Douglas Richardson.  "Giles de Burgh, married (as his 3rd wife) James [Stewart] (or James fitz Alexander), Knt., 5th Stewart of Scotland, son and heir of Alexander Stewart, Knt., 4th Stewart of Scotl
2 CONC and, of Dundonlad.  They had four sons, Andrew, Walter, Knt. [6th Steward of Scotland], John, Knt., and James, Knt., [of Durrisdeer], and one daughter, '''Giles''' (wife of Alexander de Meyners or Menzies, Knt.). ...."
2 CONT * [http://fmg.ac/library/3976-the-wives-of-sir-james-the-steward-d-1309 "The Wives of Sir James the Steward (d.1309)"] Author: MacEwen, Andrew B W Publisher: Foundation for Medieval Genealogy Year published: 2011 Status: See notes
2 CONC  Description / Notes: "This paper rehabilitates the traditional year of Sir James the Steward’s birth, names his first two wives, explains the late date of his third marriage to Giles de Burgh, and provides information about their
2 CONC  four known children. It posits a double marriage alliance between the Stewarts and Comyns about 1240, clarifies the date of birth of Robert II, and establishes the circumstances of his mother’s death in 1317. It incidentally brin
2 CONC gs forward some overlooked information on the Muschamp family and shows when Sir William, earl of Mar, actually died. Lastly it draws together what little is known concerning Sir Nicholas Campbell (d.1305), whose representation pa
2 CONC ssed to the Lochawe branch."
