1 OCCU Heiress of Arran & Mac Rory of Bute
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''The identity of Alexander Stewart's wife is unknown. Traditionally she was [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-MacRory/6000000021718774080?through=6000000004831216872 Jean of Bute], the heir of Bute and Arran, but 
2 CONC Lord Lyon David Sellars has shown her parents are likely a later myth to justify the Stewart takeover.''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Jean MacRory of Rothesay & Bute''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “Jean” married Alexander Stewart 4th High Steward of Scotland, son of Walter Stewart 3rd High Steward of Scotland and Beatrix of Angus. No date for this marriage is given in Burke or by Thompsett, so have to assume that it occurre
2 CONC d before the birth of first child. He was  b. circa 1214, d. circa 1283.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children are variously given.
2 CONT
2 CONT Medlands as of June 2022 shows these six:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#JamesStewartPearstondied1333A
2 CONT
2 CONT # James, died young 
2 CONT # James Stewart 5th High Steward of Scotland+ b. 1243, d. 16 Jul 1309.  Married 1) Cecilia de Dunbar 2) Muriel of Strathearn 3) Egida de Burgh.
2 CONT #Elizabeth Stewart+ b. c 1250 4. Married Sir William "Le Hardi" Douglas of that Ilk.
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart (d after 1350) Married Beith.  (The chronology of this entry is extremely shaky and it is unlikely that Andrew was the son of Alexander.)
2 CONT #  Sir John Stewart of Jedworth + b. c 1240, d. 22 Jul 1298 2.  Married Margaret de Bonkyl.
2 CONT # daughter.  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a charter dated [Oct] [1299] under which "Robert de Feltone" reported to Edward I King of England damage caused by raids on castle Lochmaben whose constable was "Robert de C
2 CONC onigham…vallet of the Steward of Scotland, whose sister his uncle had married"[1285].  m --- Cunningham, son of ---. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Previously Geni showed also:
2 CONT * 1.	Hawise Stewart 2. Married John de Soulis.
2 CONT *  2.	Beatrix Stewart Countess of Crawford+ 2,6. also found as "daughter Stewart.". Married Sir Alexander Lindsay of Crawford and Luffness.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
