1 NOTE SLAIN AT THE BATTLE OF FALKIRK
1 NOTE He was one of the six Governors of the Kingdom during the controversy between Robert Bruce and John Balioll for the crown in 1292. He was a supporter of Robert Bruce. He fell at the Battle of Falkirk in 1298. His seal, attached to
2 CONC  a charter from 1296, shows: Fess checquy surmounted by bend (Laing.) He was the 2nd Baron of Garlies.
