1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Be sure to scroll to the bottom October 9, 2022.  
2 CONT
2 CONT More evidence needed to support as child of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Stewart-4th-High-Steward-of-Scotland/6000000000701216197?through=6000000006721156127.  Not listed at http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#_f
2 CONC tn1259
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise (pronounced Ha-wees-a) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise le Stewart b abt 1255. She md Sir John de Soulis abt 1270, son of Nicholas de Soulis and Anora de Normanville.  Heiress of the manor of Old Roxburgh, Roxburghshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # CP: Vol III[335], Vol V[391-392]; AR: Line 8 [31-32], Line 20[30-32], Line 21[30-32], Line 28[30-34], Line 60[31-33], Line 78[32-33], Line 149[27-29]; MCS: Line 134[2-8]; GL: English Origins of New England Families, Series 2, Vo
2 CONC lume 3, The Origin of the Stuarts and FitzAlans, pp 429-434, by George Washington, from an article originally appearing in NEHGR, republished by Genealogical Publishing Company; SGM: Chris Phillips.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.geneajourney.com/fzalan.html#hawise
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Source: Familysearch.org. [not a reliable source]
2 CONT
2 CONT October 9,2022
2 CONT
2 CONT The Life Summary of Hawise
2 CONT
2 CONT When Hawise Stewart was born in 1248, in Kyle, Ayrshire, Scotland, her father, Alexander Stewart 4th High Steward Of Scotland, was 34 and her mother, Jean Arran MacRory, was 38. She married Sir John de Soules Guardian of Scotland 
2 CONC after 1274, in Castle Cary, Somerset, England. They were the parents of at least 1 son and 2 daughters. She died on 18 February 1317, in Scotland, at the age of 69, and was buried in Scotland.
