1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ELIZABETH STEWART ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Stewart married Sir William Douglas of that Ilk, called ' Le Hardi,' and was the mother of the Good Sir James ' Douglas. The name of her mother has not been satisfactorily identified. [https://archive.org/details/scot
2 CONC speeragefoun01pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/13/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT We are assuming that Elizabeth Stewart  was born circa 1250. No birth date is given in Burke or in Thompsett's work.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: Alexander Stewart 4th High Steward of Scotland b. circa 1214, d. circa 1283 & Jean
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT # circa 1265	to William Douglas of Hermistoun, son of Andrew Douglas of Hermiston, b. circa 1245
2 CONT # Sir William Douglas the Hardy, Governor of Berwick-upon-Tweed.[7] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child 	
2 CONT # James Douglas of Lothian+ b. c 1265, d. c 1323
2 CONT # Good Sir James Douglas.[9][17]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # [S9603] Unknown author, Burke
2 CONT
