2 CONT
2 CONT '''[ANDREW Stewart (-after 1350).  The Visitation of Cambridge 1575 records "Andreas Stuard iunior filius" (of Alexander Stuart  secundo genitus Gualt, Senescalli Scotie), adding that he was decorated with a military swordbelt by 
2 CONC "Johanne Francor’ Rege" and naming "Alexander Styward unicus filius Andree" who was awarded military honours by "Carolus rex Francor" (together with eight generations of Alexander’s alleged descendants in East Anglia)[1350].  The 
2 CONC chronology of this entry is extremely shaky and it is unlikely that Andrew was the son of Alexander.  m --- Beith, daughter of JAMES Beith & his wife ---.  The Visitation of Cambridge 1575 records the marriage of "Andreas Stuard i
2 CONC unior filius" (of Alexander Stuart  secundo genitus Gualt, Senescalli Scotie) and "filiam Jacobi Bethe", adding that he was decorated with a military swordbelt by "Johanne Francor’ Rege" and naming "Alexander Styward unicus filius
2 CONC  Andree" who was awarded military honours by "Carolus rex Francor" (together with eight generations of Alexander’s alleged descendants in East Anglia)[1351].  The chronology of this entry is extremely shaky and it is unlikely that
2 CONC  Andrew was the son of Alexander.] [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#JamesStewartPearstondied1333A Medieval Lands]'''
