1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT MURE OF ROWALLAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Sir William Mure of Rowallan, Robert Mure of Rowallan is the son of Archibald Mure of Rowallan and his wife Euphame Kennedy. [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/69/mode/1up Historie, p. 69] Ac
2 CONC cording to the Historie and Descent of the House of Rowallane: "Robert succeided to his father Archibald, who [Robert] frequented court in the minoritie of king James the third. He was ane man black hared & of ane hudge large stat
2 CONC ure, Therefore commonlie called the Rud of Rowallan." [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/71/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 71]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Mure of Rowallan succeeded his father in or before 1460. [https://archive.org/stream/exchequerrollsof09scot#page/667/mode/1up The Exchequer Records of Scotland, Volume IX, A.D. 1480-1487. Addenda 1437-1487, page 667]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Mure of Rowallan was alive on 17 September 1496 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/495/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 2330 on p. 495] but he died befo
2 CONC re 23 June 1506. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/138/mode/1up pp. Liber Protocllorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, Notarii Publici et Scribae Capituli Glasguensis, A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 182 on pp. 138-39]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Historie and Descent of the House of Rowallane, Robert Mure of Rowallan married "Margerie Newtoune daughter to the laird of Michaell Hill in the Merse. ane druncken woman.....She bure to him Johne who succeided
2 CONC , Robert in the Well, James in Craig and Williame of Cocktries. And ane daughter married to Boyle of Hietrie." [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/72/mode/1up The Historie and Descent of the House of Rowallan
2 CONC e, pp. 72-3] A date and place of death has not been identified for Mariote Newton. She is mentioned in a precept of remission for John Mure of Rowallan dated 2 November 1507, but it is not clear from the text of this deed if she w
2 CONC as still alive on that date. All that can presently be said of her is that she was alive on 23 June 1506 and must have died anterior to this date. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/138/mode/1up pp. Liber Prot
2 CONC ocllorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, Notarii Publici et Scribae Capituli Glasguensis, A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 182 on pp. 138-39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Mure-of-Rowallan/6000000000437966724?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1509866314155&through=6000000000437966783
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Mure-in-the-Well/6000000032277507885
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Mure-in-Craig/6000000032277326210?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1509866764186&through=6000000069967807878
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Mure-of-Cocktries/6000000032277445998?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1509866846400&through=6000000000437966783
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N-Mure/6000000069967807878?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1509867167127&through=6000000000437966783
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1460: Sa. Roberti Mur t. Rowallan [https://archive.org/stream/exchequerrollsof09scot#page/667/mode/1up The Exchequer Records of Scotland, Volume IX, A.D. 1480-1487. Addenda 1437-1487, page 667]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 September 1495. Letter of Distraint by James IV, King of Scots, made in favour of Robert Mure of Rowallan and his son, the late John Mure.  [https://archive.org/stream/historiedescento1825mure#page/114/mode/1up Ibidem, Note D
2 CONC . on pp. 114-15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 September 1496: Rob. Mure de Rowallane is noticed in the witness list of a charter by which Johannis Spark in Berthanholme confirms that he has sold the lands of Bethanholme and Snodgers to Willelmo Cunynghame de Craganis an
2 CONC d his wife Mariote Achinlek. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/495/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 2330 on p. 495]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 November 1507: Precep of remission for John Mure of Rowallan and others for the opression committed against Elizabeth Stewart and Mariote Newtoun, with regard to their terce and conjunct fees.  [https://archive.org/stream/reg
2 CONC istrumsecret00scotgoog#page/n252/mode/1up The Register of the Privy Seal of Scotland, i, A.D. 1488-1529, warrant number 1569 on p. 228]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Master Cuthbert Simonis===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 June 1506: Agreement betweem Mariote Newtoun,widow of the deceased Robert Mure of Rowallan, and John Mure of Rowallan, concerning a contract between John and his wife Margaret Boyd. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocoll
2 CONC or02bain#page/138/mode/1up pp. Liber Protocllorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, Notarii Publici et Scribae Capituli Glasguensis, A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 182 on pp. 138-39]'''
2 CONT
