1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Duncan Campbell1
2 CONT *'''M, #24605, d. 1497
2 CONT *Father      Sir Duncan 'the Fortunate or Prosperous' Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell b. c 1364, d. c Dec 1453
2 CONT *Mother     Margaret Stewart
2 CONT *'''     Duncan Campbell was born at of Auchinbreck and Kilmichael in Glassary, Scotland. He and Anne MacDougall obtained a marriage license on 29 January 1457; Date of dispensation. Duncan Campbell died in 1497.
2 CONT *'''Family      Anne MacDougall 
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Dugald Campbell+ d. 1497
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S7809] Unknown author, Irvine of Drum, by D. A. McCormick, 1989, p. 13, 17; Burke's Peerage, 1938, p. 144; Burke's Landed Gentry, 1936, p. 335.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p819.htm#i24605 ________________________
2 CONT *'''Duncan Campbell of Kilmichael1
2 CONT *M, #19438
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.05%
2 CONT *'''     Duncan Campbell of Kilmichael was the son of Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell and Margaret Stewart.2
2 CONT *'''      On 19 June 1452 he had a large estate confirmed to him by charter.1 He lived at Kilmichael, Glassary, England.1
2 CONT *'''Child of Duncan Campbell of Kilmichael
2 CONT ** 1.Dugald Campbell of Auchinbreck and Kilmichael+3 b. 1460, d. 1497
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 1, page 666. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S8] Volume 1, page 104. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S8]
2 CONT * 3.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p1944.htm#i19438 __________________________
2 CONT *Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell (Classical Gaelic Donnchadh mac Cailein, and also called Donnchadh na-Adh (English: Duncan the fortunate) of Loch Awe, (died 1453), was an important figure in Scottish affairs in the first half 
2 CONC of the fifteenth century and Justiciar of Argyll. He was head of the Clan Campbell for 40 years. ....
2 CONT *He died between February 1453 and 21 May 1454, and was buried in a magnificent sculptured tomb in the collegiate church at Kilmun which he and Margaret Stewart had founded in 1442.
2 CONT *His second son by his wife Margaret, Colin, was the founder of the Campbell of Glenorchy and Breadalbane line. His other sons by his second marriage, Archibald, '''Duncan''', and Neil, created the Campbell septs of Otter, Kilmich
2 CONC ael and Ormidale, respectively.
2 CONT *His grandson Colin, son of his only child by his first wife, Gillespic (Archibald) (d. 1440), succeeded him as Chief of the Clan Campbell and continued Duncan's efforts to increase their power.
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncan_Campbell,_1st_Lord_Campbell ______________________________
