1 NAME James /Douglas/ 3rd Earl of Angus
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Douglas
2 NSFX 3rd Earl of Angus
2 _MARNM Douglas
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1428
2 PLAC Tantallon Castle
2 ADDR
3 CITY Near North Berwick
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 SEP 1446
2 ADDR
3 CITY Earldom of Mar
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU 3rd Earl of Angus, Earl 20 (3) of Angus
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Angus, Lord of Liddesdale and Jedburgh Forest (1426–1446) was a Scottish Nobleman. He was the son of William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus and Margaret Hay of Yester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus succeeded at the age of eleven years old, and was soon involved in strife with his Black Douglas cousins. He was forfeited of his estates by James II in 1445, under the influence of his near cousin William Douglas, 8th Earl 
2 CONC of Douglas. The Earl of Douglas was trying to consolidate the power vacuum created and partially filled by the murder of his cousins at the "Black Dinner" at Edinburgh Castle, sanctioned by the king and his own father James the Gr
2 CONC oss, 7th Earl of Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that the feud between the Black and Red Lines of the House of Douglas were fomented by Bishop Kennedy of St. Andrews as a method of controlling unruly magnates, and ensuring continued Stewart power.[1]. To co
2 CONC mpound the treachery, Kennedy was a first cousin through Angus' grandmother, Princess Mary of Scotland, a daughter of King Robert III.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his forfeiture, Angus was surprised at the reluctance of his tenantry to pay their Feus, he made a point of collecting them punctually in person.
2 CONT
2 CONT Angus died in 1446. He was betrothed briefly to Princess Joan, third daughter of King James I, she was twelve years old when he died and was with her sister the Dauphine of France. She later married James Douglas, 1st Earl of Mort
2 CONC on, the head of the Douglases of Dalkeith. Angus was succeeded by his brother, George Douglas, 4th Earl of Angus in 1446.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on James Douglas, Earl of Angus:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Angus1
2 CONT *M, #109553, 
2 CONT *b. before 1428, 
2 CONT *d. before 9 September 1446
2 CONT *Last Edited=12 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=1.6%
2 CONT
2 CONT James Douglas, 3rd Earl of Angus was born before 1428.[1] He was the son of William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus and Margaret Hay.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Joan Stewart were engaged on 18 October 1440.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died before 9 September 1446, without issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Angus [S., 1389] in October 1437.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 July 1445 he was attainted, but this was probably soon reveresed.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 155. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 19. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage.
