1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT XI. PATRICK CONYNGHAM of Glengarnock died before 1478.
2 CONT
2 CONT Umphra Conyngham of Glengarnock, on 12th October, 1478, as air of Patric, pursues for airschip of moveables; but is non-suited, because Patrick had no heritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lords assigns, 14th October, 1478, to Alexr. Conynggam and James Norie, cxecutouris to Patric of Conynggam, 11th Jan., to prufe that the twentie four yovvis and twentie thre lammis taken be William of Conynggam was the said um
2 CONC quhill Patrikis gudis, and byrnt with his Birn.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lords, 20th October, 1478, ordains that Patric Erskine deliver agane to James and AlexanderConynggam, cxecutouris to umqule. Patric Conynggam, the mails of the lands of Clothcrok, and the cornes that was prysit for said umqle 
2 CONC Patrikis herezeld gife he hcs takin the said corn or maills.
2 CONT
2 CONT ("History of the County of Ayr with a Genealogical Account of the families of Ayrshire' by James Paterson")
2 CONT
