2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT < [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Douglas,_7th_Earl_of_Douglas Wikipedia] > James Douglas, 7th Earl of Douglas, 1st Earl of Avondale (1371 – 24 March 1443), latterly known as James the Gross, and prior to his ennoblement as J
2 CONC ames of Balvenie, was a late mediaeval Scottish magnate.[1] He was the second son of Archibald Douglas, 3rd Earl of Douglas, and Joan Moray of Bothwell and Drumsargard (now Cambuslang), d. after 1408. … He married first Beatrice S
2 CONC tewart, daughter of Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany and Margaret Graham, Countess of Menteith. He married second Beatrice Sinclair, daughter of Henry Sinclair, 2nd Earl of Orkney, around 1425.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Douglas, married Henry Douglas of Borg (d. 1473)[2]
2 CONT
