1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Peerage and Baronetage'' (also known as ''Burke's Peerage'') and ''The Scots Peerage'' do not report a marriage to John Hay for this Janet.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Janet Douglas:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10827.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Douglas was the daughter of James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton and Joan Stewart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell, son of Adam Hepburn, Master of Hailes and Helen Home, before 1 February 1480/81.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died before 1490, without male issue.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Douglas was also known as Joanna.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1445, her married name became Erskine.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 1 February 1480/81, her married name became Hepburn.[1] As a result of her marriage, Lady Janet Douglas was styled as Countess of Bothwell on 17 October 1488.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Janet Douglas and Patrick Hepburn, 1st Earl of Bothwell
2 CONT *1. Lady Janet Hepburn+2
2 CONT *2. Lady Margaret Hepburn4 d. 1542
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 238. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 572. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume V, page 105.
2 CONT *4. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 157.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lady Janet Hepburn formerly Douglas Born 1461 in Morton, Dumfriesshire, Scotlandmap Daughter of James Douglas and Joan J. Stewart Sister of James Douglas, John (Gordon) Gordon, second of Lochinvar and	John Douglas Wife of Patrick 
2 CONC Hepburn — married 1480 in Burkes Peeragemap Mother of Janet Hepburn and	John Buchanan Died February 22, 1490 in Bothwell Castle, Uddington, Strathclydemap Profile managers: Katherine Patterson private message [send private message
