1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Elizabeth Douglas''', daughter of	James Douglas, 1st Earl of Morton and Joan of Scotland, Countess of Morton, was born between 1460 and 1466, of Dalkeith in Scotland, and died after 1479.  She is not known to ha
2 CONC ve married or had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was mentioned in a charter of 1479 by her father, after which nothing further is known of her.  She was not living at his death in 1504:
2 CONT
2 CONT According to [https://archive.org/stream/historyofhouseof01maxw#page/n308/mode/1up page 308] of 
2 CONT "The House of Douglas":
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Morton died about the year 1504, leaving two sons -- (1) John; who succeeded to the Earldom; (2) James; and one daughter, Janet, who married Patrick, Earl of Bothwell."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not merge with any other Elizabeth Douglas - add to this discussion instead: https://www.geni.com/discussions/161928
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations===
2 CONT # [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 231. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT
