1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR JOHN STEWART OF STICKS ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Scots Peerage, Sir John Stewart of Sticks, here treated, is the bastard son of https://www.geni.com/people/James-II-King-of-Scots/6000000001273909665?through=6000000023527575713 The name of his mother has not b
2 CONC een identified. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/20/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 20]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/n8/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility
2 CONC  of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume I. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1904), 575 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart02.php Stirnet: Stewart o2]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart07.php Stirnet: Stewart 07]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT A natural son, who purchased the lands of Sticks, and is called in a charter, dated 1486, frater bastardus supromi nostri Domini Regis, ancestor of the Stewarts of Ballechin in Perthshire. [6]
