1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on John Stewart:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p10212.htm#i102113
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, Earl of Mar and Garioch [1]
2 CONT *M, #102113, 
2 CONT *b. between 1456 and 1459, 
2 CONT *d. 9 July 1479
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.27%
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, Earl of Mar and Garioch was born between 1456 and 1459.1 He was the son of James II Stewart, King of Scotland and Marie von Geldern.2 He died on 9 July 1479 at Craigmillar Castle, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, pos
2 CONC sibly murdered on the orders of his brother, King James III, unmarried.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He gained the title of Earl of Garioch between 21 June 1458 and 25 June 1459.[1] 
2 CONT *He gained the title of Earl of Mar between 21 June 1458 and 25 June 1459.[1] 
2 CONT *Between 1479 and 1480 he forfeited all of his estates.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 236. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
2 CONT *2. [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume I, page 19. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the English Wikipedia page for Craigmillar Castle:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craigmillar_Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart, Earl of Mar, brother of King James III was held prisoner at Craigmillar, accused of practising witchcraft against the King.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT *4. Salter, Mike (1994). The Castles of Lothian and Borders. Folly Publications. ISBN 1-871731-20-8. pp.34-35
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
