1 NOTE {geni:about_me} George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly
2 CONT
2 CONT b. before 1425, d. circa 8 June 1501
2 CONT
2 CONT George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly|b. b 1425\\\\nd. c 8 Jun 1501|p335.htm#i11867|Alexander Seton Lord Gordon, Earl of Huntly|d. 15 Jul 1470|p683.htm#i11878|Elizabeth Crichton|d. 9 Jun 1479|p234.htm#i11880|Alexander Seton Sir, Lord Gord
2 CONC on|d. 1440|p683.htm#i11881|Elizabeth Gordon|d. bt 16 Mar 1438 - 1439|p334.htm#i11882|Lord William Crichton||p234.htm#i11879|Agnes Unknown (Crichton)||p775.htm#i23684|
2 CONT
2 CONT      Second son of Alexander. The Earldom was settled by charter, obtained by his father 8 Jan 1449/50. Among his acquisitions from the Crown were Schivas in co. Aberdeen, and Boyne, Enzie, and Netherdale in co. Banff.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Scottish Peerage states: George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly, his first marriage was rendered illegal canonically.
2 CONT
2 CONT > What puzzles me is the marriage contract of Alexander, 3rd Earl. Lets assume George, his father, married Elizabeth Hay in 1471 (after 18 August) Alexander, say born in 1472, would he contract to marry 20 October 1474? His brothe
2 CONC r Adam was already born and the contract stipulated that failing him, his brother Adam was to implement the contract and so forth, "from son to son lauchfully gotten." In 1485 Alexander (aged 13?) was sitting in Parliament.
2 CONT
2 CONT > CP Volume VI page 677. At first it seems CP is avoiding allotting Alexander a mother, but in a footnote gives the same details. "The identity of his mother is doubtful." To me, it seems Alexander should have been born well and t
2 CONC ruly before 1472 (to sit in Parliament) and Elizabeth Hay, as widow of Alexander's father, may well have been called his mother when she perhaps was his step-mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Could Alexander have been son of this first wife? Say born in 1458-9 he would have been about 25 when sitting in Parliament and about 15 when his marriage was contracted.
2 CONT
2 CONT "GEORGE, 2nd Earl of Huntly ... He m. 1stly, by contract 20 May 1445, Elizabeth Dunbar, widow of Archibald, Earl of Moray, and daughter. of James, Earl of Moray (...). He div. her and m. 2ndly, 10 Mar 1459, Lady Annabella Stuart, 
2 CONC daughter. of JAMES I, from whom he was div. 24 July 1471 (...) and by her had issue, with four daus.,
2 CONT
2 CONT "ALEXANDER, 3rd Earl.". George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly was born before 1425 at Scotland. He was the son of Alexander Seton Lord Gordon, Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Crichton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly married Elizabeth Dunbar, daughter of James Dunbar 4th Earl of Moray and Katherine or Janet Seton (of Gordon), circa 20 May 1455. She was married by forced contract dated 19 days after her husban
2 CONC d's death. They seem to have had no issue, and the marriage was dissolved before 10 March 1459/60. George was granted a divorce from Elizabeth Dunbar before 10 March 1459/60. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly married Lady Annabella Stewart, daughter of James I Stewart King of Scotland and Queen Joan or Jane Beaufort, on 10 March 1459/60. He married before 10 March 1459-60 Princess Annabella Stewart, d
2 CONC aughter of King James I. "The Princess appears to have had no male issue, and six years after the marriage George was again a-wooing." George was granted a divorce from Lady Annabella Stewart on 24 July 1471 at Aberdeen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly married Elizabeth Hay circa 18 August 1471 at Fyvie, Aberdeenshire, Scotland. On 4,11 and 18 August 1471 banns of marriage between George and Elizabeth Hay were published. "It is usually said the
2 CONC  marriage did not take place till after 12 May 1476, but this is founded on the erroneous date noted above (a footnote explains this), and the marriage probably followed closely on the final proclamation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly married Elizabeth Erroll (Gray) on 12 May 1476 at Scotland. George was Chancellor of Scotland between 1498 and 1501. 
2 CONT
2 CONT      George died circa 8 June 1501 at Stirling, Stirlingshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet or Agnes Gordon+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly and Lady Annabella Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Gordon (of Aboyne)+ d. 17 Mar 1537/38 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel or Elizabeth Gordon+ 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Gordon 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon 3rd Earl Huntly+ b. b 1464?, d. 16 Jan 1523/24 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Gordon 2nd Earl Huntly and Elizabeth Hay
2 CONT
2 CONT James Gordon Admiral, Sir 
2 CONT
