1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography: Iain "Garbh" MacLean, 2nd Laird of Coll ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Iain "Garbh" MacLean, 2nd Laird of Coll, was the son of Lachlan MacLean, 1st Laird of Coll, and his wife Anna, daughter of Alexander MacLeod of Dunvegan. He held the lordship of Coll during the mid-15th century, continuing the con
2 CONC solidation of the MacLean holdings in the Inner Hebrides.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriage and Issue ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Iain "Garbh" was married to an unidentified daughter of the Clan MacLean of Duart. He had two sons, both of whom served as Lairds of Coll:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John "Garve" MacLean, 3rd Laird of Coll (b. before 1499, d. after 1519); spouse: Jannet MacLean (daughter of Ewen MacLean of Urquhart); no issue.
2 CONT * Hector "Cainneach" MacLean, 4th Laird of Coll (b. before 1512, d. after 1558); spouse: Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Genealogical Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT The succession of the Coll lordship passed from Iain "Garbh" (2nd Laird) to his eldest son, John "Garve" (3rd Laird). Upon John's death without issue, the lordship reverted to his younger brother, Hector "Cainneach" (4th Laird). T
2 CONC his brother-to-brother succession is verified by the administrative records of the mid-16th century and the Register of the Great Seal of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Warning: Secondary Source Reliability ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Researchers are advised that digital platforms such as WikiTree and similar collaborative genealogical repositories frequently contain conflated data regarding this lineage. Specifically, these sources often erroneously collapse t
2 CONC he 4th and 5th Lairds, attribute incorrect spouses, and insert fabricated lineages such as the "Kingerloch" connection. Users must rely on primary administrative documentation—specifically the Register of the Great Seal—rather tha
2 CONC n automated Smart Matches derived from these platforms to maintain the integrity of the Master Profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Sources ===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Nicholas MacLean-Bristol, Warriors and Priests: The History of the Clan MacLean 1300-1570 (1995), Tuckwell Press Ltd.
2 CONT * Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum (Register of the Great Seal of Scotland).
2 CONT * The Clan Gillean, A. MacLean Sinclair (1899).
