1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marjory Sutherland
2 CONT * Born after 1424 in Dunbeath Castle, Caithness, Scotland
2 CONT * Died before 1480 in Dunbeath Castle, Caithness, Scotland
2 CONT * Father: 	Alexander Sutherland of Dunbeath 
2 CONT * Mother: 	Catherine Chalmers
2 CONT * Spouse: William Sinclair, Third Earl of Orkney, First Earl of Caithness (abt. 1404 - bef. 1480) - married  before 15 Nov 1456
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A castle is first recorded on the rocky peninsula at Dunbeath in 1428, when the lands belonged to the Earl of Caithness. The first recorded laird was Alexander Sutherland. It later became the property of the Clan Sinclair through 
2 CONC the marriage of '''the daughter of Alexander Sutherland''' to William Sinclair (1410–1484), the first Sinclair Earl of Caithness. The Sinclairs replaced the earlier structure with a four-storey tower house in 1620.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 	
2 CONT # bef 15 Nov 1456 to William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney, 1st Lord, Chancellor, b. Abt 1430 as 2nd wife  Children 	
2 CONT * >	1. Oliver Sinclair, of Roslin
2 CONT * >	2. William Sinclair, 2nd Earl of Caithness 
2 CONT * >	3. Marjory Sinclair 
2 CONT * >	4. Margaret Sinclair 
2 CONT * >	5. Elizabeth Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	6. Alexander Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	7. Susan Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	8. George Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	9. Robert Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	10. Arthur Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	11. Katherine Sinclair 
2 CONT *  	12. Mariot Sinclair 
2 CONT * >	13. Eleanor Sinclair, b. 1457, Ravenscraig, Fifeshire, Scotland 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sutherland-148
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Sutherland of Dunbeath’s family
2 CONT
2 CONT Historians have long debated this branch of the Sutherland and the parentage of his large family. It has become clear that Alexander Sutherland of Dunbeath and his wife Mariot MacDonald of the Isles only had one child who lived, t
2 CONC heir daughter Marion Sutherland who married William Calder 7th Thane of Calder. This is based on the fact that Alexander left his property to his legitimate heir, Marion.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his very detailed will, Alexander left items of property to his children by Katherine Chalmers also referred to as “Kateryn of Chaumer”. These children included''' his daughter Marjory Sutherland who married William Sinclair wh
2 CONC o went on to become the 1st Earl and Countess of Caithness.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/334/mode/2up Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots peerage] : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical ac
2 CONC count of the nobility of that kingdom. Edinburgh 1904. vol ii, p 334
2 CONT # Medieval, royalty, nobility family group sheets (filmed 1996), Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints. Family History Department. Medieval Family History Unit, (Manuscript. Salt Lake City, Utah : Filmed by the Genealogical 
2 CONC Society of Utah, 1996), FHL film 1553977-1553985..
2 CONT # Medieval Lands: A Prosopography of Medieval European Noble and Royal Families, Cawley, Charles, (http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands), SCOTLAND NOBILITY; http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm [Accessed Nov 2009].
2 CONT # Cahiers de Saint-Louis (1976), Louis IX, Roi de France, (Angers: J. Saillot, 1976), FHL book 944 D22ds., vol. 2 p. 93, vol. 11 p. 846, vol. 13 pt. 1 p. 89.
2 CONT #  The Wallop Family and Their Ancestry, Watney, Vernon James, (4 volumes. Oxford: John Johnson, 1928), FHL book Q 929.242 W159w; FHL microfilm 1696491 it., vol. 3 p. 728, 729.
2 CONT # The Genealogist (1980-), Association for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, (New York: Organization for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, 1980-), FHL book 929.105 G286n., Spring 1982, vol. 3 no. 1 p. 32:67.
2 CONT # [1883 edition] A Genealogical History of the Dormant, Abeyant, Forfeited, and Extinct Peerages of the British Empire (New edition, 1883, reprint 1962), Burke, Sir John Bernard, (New edition. 1883. Reprint, London: Harrison and S
2 CONC ons, 1962), FHL book 942 D22bug 1883., p. 509.
2 CONT # The Scots Peerage: Founded on Wood's Edition of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland, Containing an Historical and Genealogical Account of the Nobility of that Kingdom, with Armorial Illustrations (1904-1914), Paul , Sir Jam
2 CONC es Balfour, (9 volumes. Edinburgh: D. Douglas, 1904-1914), FHL book 941 D22p; FHL microfilms104,157-104,161., vol. 1 p. 442.
2 CONT # The Genealogist (1980-), Association for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, (New York: Organization for the Promotion of Scholarship in Genealogy, 1980-), FHL book 929.105 G286n., Spring 1982, vol. 3 no. 1 p. 32:66.
2 CONT #  Histoire de la maison royale de France anciens barons du royaume: et des grands officiers de la couronne (1726, reprint 1967-1968), Saint-Marie, Anselme de, (3rd edition. 9 volumes. 1726. Reprint Paris: Editions du Palais Royal
2 CONC , 1967-1968), FHL book 944 D5a; FHL microfilms 532,231-532,239., vol. 8 p. 807.
2 CONT # Arthur B. W. MacEwen, "Marjory Sutherland: Countess of Caithness and Orkney" in ''The Genealogist'', Volume 13 (1999).
2 CONT
