1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''THE  MACDONALDS  OF  SLEAT.'''    -
2 CONT The  Macdonalds  of  Sleat  are  descended  from
2 CONT 1.  HUGH,  son  of  Alexander,  Earl  of  Ross,  and Lord  of  the  Isles,  by  '''the  daughter  of  O'Beolan''',  lay Abbot  of  Applecross,  and  are  known  patronymically as  Clann  Uisdein. Hugh  married,  first,   Fynvola, 
2 CONC  daughter  of  Alexander Maclain  of  Ardnamurchan,  and  had  by  her — 
2 CONT >1.  John,  his  successor, d1502
2 CONT He  married,  secondly,  Elizabeth  Gunn,  daughter  of the  Crowner  of  Caithness,  and  had  by  her—
2 CONT >2.  Donald  Gallach.
2 CONT He   married,    thirdly,    a    daughter    of    Macleod   of Harris,  by  whom  he  had—
2 CONT >3.  Donald  Herrach,  from  whom  Clann  Domhnuill  Herraich. Hugh  had  also  several  sons,  whose  claims  to  legiti- macy do  not  seem  to  have  been  admitted  even  by the  social  canons  of  the  time,  viz. : —
2 CONT >4.  Archibald  Dubh,  by  a  daughter  of  Torquil  Macleod  of Lewis.
2 CONT >5.  Angus  Collach,  by  a  daughter  of  the  Laird  of  Coll.
2 CONT >6.  Angus   Dubh,   by   a   daughter  of  Maurice   Vicar  of  S.Uist,
2 CONT Hugh  Macdonald  of  Sleat  died  in    1498,   and  was succeeded  by  his  oldest  son,
2 CONT
2 CONT >II.  JOHN.  It  has  been  seen  how  he  surrendered his  whole  patrimony  to  the  King,  by  whom  it  was afterwards  bestowed  upon  Ranald  MacAllan  of  Clainranald  and  Angus  Reochson  MacKanald  of  Morar. This  grant
2 CONC ,  however,  never  took  effect.  John  died in  1502,  and  was  succeeded  by  his  brother,
2 CONT
2 CONT >III.  DONALD  GALLACH.  He  did  not  long  occupy the  position  of  Chief  of  Sleat,  as  he  was  murdered by  his  brother,  Archibald  Dubh,  in  1506.  He married  Agnes,  daughter  of  Sir  John  Cathanach Macdonald  of  
2 CONC Dunnyveg  and  the  Glens,  by  whom he  had—
2 CONT >>1.  Donald  Gruamach,  his  successor.
2 CONT >>2.  Alexander,  whose  sons  fought  in  Ireland  on  the  side  of their  kinsman,  Sorley  Buy.
2 CONT >>3.  Angus,  who  had  a  son,  John.
2 CONT >>4.  Ranald  Collach,  who  had  a  son,  Alexander.
2 CONT Donald  Gallach  of  Sleat  was  succeeded  by  his  oldest son,
2 CONT
2 CONT >>IV.  DONALD  GRUAMACH.  He  married,  first, Catherine,  daughter  of  Alexander  Macdonald  of Clanranald,  and  had  —
2 CONT >>>1.  Donald  Gorm,  his  successor.
2 CONT >>He   married,   secondly,    a   daughter  of  Macleod  of Lewis,  and  had  —
2 CONT >>>2;  John  Og,  who  married  a  daughter  of  Alastair  Crotach Macleod  of  Dunvegan,  without  issue.
2 CONT >>>3.  Archibald,  the  Clerk.     He  had  two  sons  —
2 CONT >>>>(A)  Hugh,    whose   career   and    fate   have   already   been described.     He  had  a  son,  Alexander,  who  appears on  record.
2 CONT >>>>(B)  Donald.
2 CONT >>>4.  James  of  Castle  Camus,  known  as  Seumas  a’  Chaisteil, progenitor  of  Kingsburgh  and  other  families.
2 CONT >>He  had  other  sons  said  to  have  been  natural,  viz.  :  —
2 CONT >>>5.  Alexander.
2 CONT >>>6.  John  Dubh.
2 CONT >>>7.  Angus.
2 CONT >>>8.  Alexander.     None  of  these  appear  to  have  left  traceable posterity.
2 CONT >>Donald  Gruamach  died  in  1534
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/clandonald03macduoft/page/n547/mode/2up?q=Camus&view=theater
