1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://gw0.geneanet.org/brynjulf?lang=en;pz=tor;nz=langballe;ocz=0;p=robert;n=lamont;oc=4
2 CONT
2 CONT Married before 30 October 1397, Rathesay, Bute, Scotland, to  Anna MacDonald, . of the Isles ?1380- (Parents :  Donald MacDonald, Lord of the Isles ?1351-1423 &   Margaret Leslie, grevinne av Ross ?1369-) (see note) with
2 CONT  Celestin Lamont, Chief of Lamonts 1402-1448 Christiana Lamont 1403- Mary Lamont 1404-
2 CONT  Duncan Lamont 1417-1488 Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Individual Note
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lamont Data Base 5th Chief of Lamonts 1396-1433 29 Nov1410 Notariall Copy of a Charter byt Robertus Duncanj Lagmane of Inneryne, in favours of Celestin Augustij M'Soirle and his heirs males of the lands of Auchachois and othe
2 CONC r proceeding upon the said Celestin's resignation, and dated the pennult day of November 1410 years. The bounding of the lands disponed is therin specified.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was known that Robert Lamont and Agnes ‘de insulis’ (or MacDonald as you may prefer) were closely related, as they eventually obtained a dispensation dated 30 October 1397. Based on Sir Norman Lamont’s previous work, Jean Munro
2 CONC  and R. W. Munro published details showing that ' Robert Duncani MacLagmayn and Ana Donaldi domini Insularum ' were dispensed to marry, as they were related in the 3rd degree of consanguinity [2]. The language of the dispensation 
2 CONC also makes it clear that Robert was the son of Duncan Lamont, and Agnes (or ‘Ana’) the daughter of Donald, Lord of the Isles (d. 1423).
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Note
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lamont Data Base Robert Lamont married Anne Macdonald before October 30 1397 in Toward. "Robert, son of Duncan Maclagmayn, married, by papal dispensation, of 30 Oct 1397, Anna Macdonald, daughter of Donald, eighth lord of the
2 CONC  Isles, by his wife Margaret Leslie"
2 CONT
