2 CONT Burke's Peerage - JOHN SUTHERLAND, 7th Earl of Sutherland; born c 1390; knighted 1408; married by 1342 Margaret (died 1510), a famous beauty, daughter of Sir William Baillie of Lamington, and had:
2 CONT * 1a Alexander, Master of Sutherland; died in the lifetime of the father by 22 Feb 1455/6
2 CONT * 2a JOHN, 8th Earl
2 CONT * 3a Nicholas, living 1448
2 CONT * 4a Thomas Beg (‘The Little'); allegedly ancestor of the SUTHERLANDs OF STRATHALLIE '''* 5a Robert, living 1487'''
2 CONT * 1a Janet; married Alexander Dunbar, 3rd son of Sir Alexander Dunbar of Westfield (see DUNBAR OF MOCHRUM, Bt), and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0037 
2 CONT
2 CONT >On 3 February 1444-45 a safe-conduct was issued to Margaret Sutherland, Alexander and Robert Sutherland, probably the Earl's wife and children, for a year, to pass between England and Scotland.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT [3] Cal. Doc. Scot., iv. No. 1175.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, named in the above safe-conduct of 3 February 1444-45, may have been a son, and not improbably he was the Robert Sutherland who, according to Sir Robert Gordon, took part in the battle of Aldycharrish. Sir Robert says he w
2 CONC as an uncle of the Earl, but if he were he must have been of great age in 1487, the alleged date of the conflict.
