2 CONT * “Historic Memorials of the Stewarts of Forthergill, Perthshire and Their Male ...” edited by Charles Poyntz Stewart.  Page 10.  <[https://books.google.com/books?id=IS0BAAAAQAAJ&lpg=RA1-PA10&ots=OZXt8xp6mX&dq=Elizabeth%20Gordon%2
2 CONC 0as%20wife%20of%20Niel%20Stewart&pg=RA1-PA10#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]> “John had a younger brother, Niel Stewart, who married Elizabeth Gordon, both being named in the deed by which John bequeaths money for prayers for him
2 CONC self and others.  This Elizabeth Gordon is believed to have been a sister of the [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Gordon-1st-Earl-of-Huntley/6000000001644776831?through=6000000003615927699 Earl of Huntly], with whose family 
2 CONC there was great intimacy for several generations. For example, we find George, Lord Huntly, surety for Niel, son of John Stewart of Forthergill, in the “ Band” with Duncan Campbell of Glenorchy in 1488; in 1477, by the bond of man
2 CONC rent between John, Earl of Athole, and said Niel, Niel reserves “his allegiance to the Earl of Huntlie,” besides several other instances, which will be found in the proofs printed in the Appendix.”
