1 NAME Alexander /Dunbar of Westfield/
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Dunbar of Westfield
2 _MARNM Dunbar of Westfield
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Elgin Cathedral/Elgin, Moray, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1425
2 ADDR
3 CITY Westfield
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 MAR 1497
2 ADDR
3 CITY Elgin
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Sheriff of Moray
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Alexander Dunbar was known as Alexander Dunbar of Westfield. He was born illegitimate circa 1425 at Scotland. He was the only son of James 4th Earl of Moray. He was the son of James Dunbar 4th Earl of Moray and
2 CONC  Isabel Innes (Dunbar). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His half-sister Elizabeth, wife of Archibald Douglas obtained the Earldom; but Alexander however, got from the crown a large estate, was knighted and created Heritable Sheriff of Moray. He had the lands of Conzie, Durrisk, Moyness
2 CONC , Tarrus, Carnausie, Clana, part of Fachabers and others and had several charters from James II. He obtained in 1450 from Archibald Douglas, Earl of Moray, a charter of the lands and barony of Westfield and other estates. He also 
2 CONC received lands from his sister Janet, Countess of Moray. Alexander was hereditary Sheriff of Moray. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The two eldest of Sir Alexander's 6 sons married Anne-Eupheme and Margaret, the two eldest daughters and co-heirs of Patrick Dunbar of Mochrum and founded the long lines of Westfield and Mochrum. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander died on 10 March 1497/98 at Moray, Scotland. He was killed by Alexander Sutherland. He was buried at the Dunbar aisle, Elgin Cathedral, Moray, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel, daughter of Alexander Sutherland, third Baron of Duffus, and had eight sons and one daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Alexander Dunbar and Isobel Sutherland:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Sir James Dunbar+ b. a 1451, d. 20 Apr 1504
2 CONT #     Sir John Dunbar (of Mochrum)+ b. c 1452, d. 1503
2 CONT #     Alexander Dunbar+ b. Oct 1455, d. c 31 Mar 1498
2 CONT #     Gavin Dunbar Bishop of Aberdeen b. c 1456, d. 9 Mar 1532
2 CONT #     Leonard Dunbar b. s 1459
2 CONT #     Isabella or Janet Dunbar (Keith) (of Innerugie)+
2 CONT #     Margaret Dunbar
2 CONT #     son Dunbar
2 CONT #     Patrick Dunbar+ b. b 1470?, d. 8 Sep 1525
2 CONT #     David Dunbar (of Durris)+ b. c 1470, d. 23 Feb 1521/22
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Knight, of Westfield, Sheriff of Moray.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunbar-668
