1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT THE CLAN LOGAN: 
2 CONT
2 CONT The early Lowland Logan's originated from Galloway. It is documented that two of them were killed in Spain in 1329 on their way to the Holy Land with the heart of King Robert I ( the Bruce). Sir Robert Logan of Restalrig ( died 16
2 CONC 06) had his bones exhumed and paraded in Parliament so that he could personally be convicted of treason. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * MOTTO: Hoc majorum vitus--" This is the valour of my ancestors"  
2 CONT * BADGE: A passion nail piercing a human heart, proper  
2 CONT * GAELIC NAME: Loganaich or Macgill'innein  
2 CONT * ORIGIN OF NAME: a place name  
2 CONT * WAR CRY: Druim-nan duer ( The ridge of tears) 
2 CONT
