2 DATE 1506
2 PLAC Lauchope, Lanarkshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT William, the oldest son of Willielmo and Jean de Muirhead, was born circa 1415. 
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1442, he married Mariota Hamilton, who was born circa 1418. They gave birth to two sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT #  John Muirhead of Lauchope and 
2 CONT # Richard Muirhead.(1.25) 
2 CONT
2 CONT It would be the descendants of William and Mariota Muirhead who would lay claim to the titles associated with the lands of and in the vicinity of Muirhead in Lanarkshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Muirhead was knighted by King James IV, taking the appellation: Sir William Muirhead (2nd) of Lauchope. He was appointed to the position of Lord Clerk Register, but resigned from that position. He then served his king as S
2 CONC ecretary of State and as one of the Lords of Council and Session.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Muirhead of Lauchope died circa 1506.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
