2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunglass_Collegiate_Church,_East_Lothian
2 CONT
2 CONT The date of building the Chapel, dedicated to St. Mary of Dunglass, is unclear but when Sir Alexander Home of that Ilk was granted a charter, in 1421, to the lands of Dunglass [1] the chapel was in existence. In 1423, Sir Alexande
2 CONC r of Dunglass employed priests (a college) to pray for the family's souls and the chapel was raised to collegiate status [2] which was confirmed by King James II of Scots in 1450 and confirmed by Pope Nicholas V. The college was c
2 CONC omposed of a provost, three chaplains and four boy choiristers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/239837461/alexander-home
2 CONT
2 CONT When Alexander Home was born in April 1407 in Wedderburn Castle, Berwickshire, Scotland, his father, Alexander, was 27 and his mother, Janet, was 15. He married Marion Lauder in 1434 in Scotland. They had one child during their ma
2 CONC rriage. He died in 1491 in Dunglass, East Lothian, Scotland, having lived a long life of 84 years.
