1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME ANNABELLA BOYD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Annabella Boyd, here treated, is said to have been a daughter of Robert, first Lord Boyd. According to the Marquess de Ruvigny, writing in his account of Hay, Marquess of Tweeddale, if she was Lord Boyd's daughter then she
2 CONC  married secondly: "as first wife, to Sir John Gordon of Lochinvar, who died after May 1517. She was certainly married to Edmund Hay before 9 December 1449, and a comparison between this date and those of the  ascertained daughter
2 CONC s and sisters of Lord Boyd will show that she is far more likely to have been his sister than his daughter.[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/425/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 425]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Annabella Boyd, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Edmund-Hay-of-Talla-and-Linplum/6000000182668151831?through=6000000182668789822 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/425/mode/1up Th
2 CONC e Scots Peerage VIII: 425]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Annabella Boyd, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Dunbar-of-Bele-younger/6000000182728169826?through=6000000056285393852 [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso42scotuoft/page/64/mode/1up Yest
2 CONC er Writs: number 134]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from Yester Writs ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 April 1467: Instrument of Assedation by Dame Annabella Boyd relict of Edmund of Hay of Thallow with consent of Patrick of Dunbar Lord of Bele then her spouse, to Sir Robert Morhame chaplain of the altar of St. Edmund, the Kin
2 CONC g and martyr, situated in the Collegiate Church of Bothanis, and his successors of the terce of a "terre cotarie templarie" lying in the town of Duncanelaw, and the third part of the mylnlands, lying in the territory of Duncanelaw
2 CONC , belonging to her terce by the decease of the said Edmund Hay her husband, Which lands etc., William Hay, Knight, her son, gave to the said altar in augmentation of the infeftment by the said late Edmund Hay ; in pure and perpetu
2 CONC al alms : Dated 2nd April 1467, in the Cloister of the Friars Minor of Haddington, 3 p.m. : Witnesses, Sir John of Swyntoun of that Ilk, Knight, Sir William Hay, Knight, Edmund of Hay his brother, William Home of Rauchburn, Robert
2 CONC  of Grenlaw, John Geddes and James Colylaw : Alexander Clerk is notary. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso42scotuoft/page/64/mode/1up Yester Writs: number 134]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 November 1468: Paper Letter of Warrandice by Sir Wm. Hay of Tallo knt. of his resignation to John the Hay son and heir of Sir D. Hay of Zestir of 2 and one half marks annualrent from Westir Hoprew, see No. 150, and in especi
2 CONC al that J. H. should not be vexit by Annabell Bold "my moder" now the spous of Patric Dunbar of Bele nor by the said Patrick for her third or terce of said annualrent the granter's lands of Tallo and Kingildurris becoming liable f
2 CONC or the amount: Edinburgh, 25 Nov. 1469: no witnesses. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso42scotuoft/page/68/mode/1up Yester Writs: number 151]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
