1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANNABELLA OF STRATHEARN===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Amabilie sorori [Malisius comes Strahern] (X 1289) Anable qe su la femme Patrik de Graham (1296) Annabella quae suit uxor Patricii de Graham (1296)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabella of Strathearn is reported to be the daughter of Robert, fourth Earl of Strathearn.  The name of her mother has not been identified. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/245/mode/1up The Scots P
2 CONC eerage VIII: 245] She was the sister of Malise, Earl of Strathearn, who gave her the lands of Kincardine. [https://archive.org/details/liberinsulemissa85inchuoft/page/xxxiii/mode/1up Inchaffrey Liber: pp. xxxii-iii]''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Annabella of Strathearn. She was alive on 28 August 1296, when her homage was received at Berwick on Tweed by King Edward I of England: "Anable qe su la femme Patrik de Grah
2 CONC am". [https://archive.org/stream/instrumentapublica00thomuoft#page/146/mode/1up Instrumenta Publica: p. 146] and she appears still to have been alive on 3 September 1296, when King Edward I of England seized her lands because her 
2 CONC husband had opposed him at Dunbar. [https://archive.org/details/cu31924091786024/page/n119/mode/1up Stevenson's Documents II: p. 92]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabella of Strathearn married Patrick Graham. [https://archive.org/stream/instrumentapublica00thomuoft#page/146/mode/1up Instrumenta Publica: p. 146] Her husband is reported to have been killed in action at the battle of Dunb
2 CONC ar on 27 April 1296. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/245/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 245]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Secondary Source Evidence===
2 CONT
