2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.electricscotland.com/history/nation/strathern.htm REPORT BY ELECTRIC SCOTLAND]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise, the younger son, got from King William the lands of Kincardine, to be held of his brother, Earl Robert, and through the marriage of his niece, '''Annabella''', elder daughter of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert,_Earl_o
2 CONC f_Strathearn Earl Robert], to Graham, ancestor of the duke of Montrose, they afterwards came into that family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Various sources indicate that his wife was Annabella, daughter of 4th Earl of Strathearn. TSP (Strathearn) specifically contradicts this and reports "the evidence is clear that she was the wife of his son Sir Patrick".
2 CONT * BP1934 Montrose and TSP Montrose disagree here as BP1934 inserts an additional generation of a Sir David of Dundaff (which we follow) and shows that David as husband of Annabella of Strathearn whom '''TSP shows as wife of SIr Pa
2 CONC trick of Kincardine'''. There is therefore some difference in allocation of children, the most 'important' one possibly being the John who became Earl of Menteith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # Neville, Cynthia J., Native Lordship in Medieval Scotland: The Earldoms of Strathearn and Lennox, c. 1140-1365, (Portland & Dublin, 2005)
2 CONT # Paul, James Balfour, Sir, "The Scots Peerage" (Edinburgh : D. Douglas 1904-1919)
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://www.multiwords.de/genealogy/graham01.htm Multiwords]
2 CONT # [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I4240&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clands genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Strathearn-7  REPORT BY WIKITREE]
2 CONT
2 CONT  Annabella Strathearn Born 1212 in Strathearn, Perthshire, Scotlandmap Daughter of Robert Strathearn and Matilda Strathearn Sister of Malise De Strathearn	 Wife of David Graham — married [date unknown] [location unknown] Mother of
2 CONC  David Graham	 Died 1263 in Strathearn, Perthshire, Scotlandmap 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Robert, 4th Earl of Strathearn '''Disputed'''
2 CONT
