1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Comyn-4th-Earl-of-Buchan/6000000002603656225?through=6000000006906839736 & https://www.geni.com/people/Joan-le-Latimer/6000000001745096693?through=6000000006906839736
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Strathearn-32
2 CONT
2 CONT This Malise was the 7th Earl of Strathearn.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise was born about 1278 son to Malise of Strathearn and his wife Agnes daughter to Alexander Comyn earl of Buchan.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1300 Malise married '''but the name of his wife is not discovered'''. He had issue from this first marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Malise his heir
2 CONT # Mary who about 1320 mar. Sir John Moray of Drumsagard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise died about 1327 and was succeeded in the title by his son Malise and survived by his daughter Mary who with her husband had been granted a very substantial portion of the Strathearn estate, His second wife Johanna Menteith 
2 CONC also survived him and remarried a further three times. Her second husband was John Campbell earl of Atholl who died 1333 and then she married Maurice Moray step- son of Mary Strathearn her step-daughter. Johanna retained the title
2 CONC  of Countess of Strathearn throughout her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Here, we follow MedLands:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#MaliseStrathearndied1271A
2 CONT
2 CONT MALISE ([1275/80]-before 1329). Andrew Wyntoun´s Cronykil records that "Jhon and Alysandyre" had five sisters, the second of which married "Off Stratherne the Erle Malys" by whom she had "a swne…Malys"[732]. He succeeded his fathe
2 CONC r in 1313 as Earl of Strathearn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly AGNES, daughter of --- (-after Aug 1320). John of Fordun´s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "dominus Willelmus de Sowlis et comitissa de Strathern" were convicted of high treason at a parliament in Scone in Aug 
2 CONC 1320 and sentenced to life imprisonment[733]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly ([1323]) as her first husband, JOAN Menteith, daughter of Sir JOHN Menteith of Rusky & his wife --- (-after 20 Mar 1367). She married secondly John Campbell Earl of Atholl, thirdly Maurice Moray Earl of Strathearn, and 
2 CONC fourthly (before 9 Nov 1347) as his second wife, William Sutherland 5th Earl of Sutherland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Malise & his first wife had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          MALISE (-killed in battle Neville’s Cross 17 Oct 1346).  He succeeded his father as Earl of Strathearn.  He succeeded his cousin Magnus as Earl of Caithness and Orkney in [1323/29].  He resigned the earldom of Strathea
2 CONC rn [24 Sep/16 Dec] 1332 into the hands of Edward Balliol, was tried for treason in 1344 for so doing, but found innocent[759].  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "Johannes Ranulphi comes Moraviæ ac etiam c
2 CONC omes de Strathern constabularius Scotiæ…David filius et heres David de Lindsay…Willelmus Fraser…" were killed at Durham 17 Oct 1346[760].  [761]m firstly MARY, daughter of ---.  m secondly ([1325/28]) MATILDA [Marjory] of Ross, da
2 CONC ughter of HUGH Earl of Ross & his first wife Matilda Bruce (-after 1350).  Earl Malise & his first wife had four children: …
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         MARY .  "Malisius comes Strathern" granted "terram de Abbercarny…que fuit Roberti filii Magni dicti de Strathern" to "Johanni de Moravia de Dromsygart…[et] heredibus suis de Maria filia nostra" by undated charter[763].
2 CONC   [764]m ([1319/22]) as his second wife, JOHN Moray of Drumsagard, co. Lanark, son of ---. 
