2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise III of Strathearn (Gaelic: Maol Íosa; c. 1257 – 1312) was a Scottish nobleman, the ruler of the region of Strathearn. The Earl married a lady named '''Agnes''', likely the second daughter of Alexander Comyn, Earl of Buchan.
2 CONC  The Countess Agnes would later be imprisoned for life for conspiring against King Robert with her nephew William Soules.
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise and Agnes had three sons and a daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise IV, succeeded as Earl
2 CONT Gilbert, went with King Edward to Flanders in 1297, and may have died or been killed there
2 CONT Robert, is recorded as having been imprisoned in the Tower of London with other Scottish youths in 1297. Nothing further is known of him
2 CONT Matilda, married Robert de Toeni, Lord Toeni of Flamsted (1276–1309), son of Ralph de Toeni.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#AgnesComynMMaliseStrathearn
2 CONT
2 CONT ALEXANDER Comyn, son of WILLIAM Comyn Earl of Buchan & his second wife Margaret Ctss of Buchan (-[1 Jan/5 Apr] 1290).  Andrew Wyntoun’s Cronykil names "Alysawndyr that Erle wes off Buchane" as "the thryd brothyr" of "Rychard and W
2 CONC altyre", sons of "Willame Cwmyn"[1050].  He succeeded his mother in [1244] as Earl of Buchan. He was one of the six Guardians on the death of Alexander III King of Scotland[1052]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ELIZABETH de Quincy, daughter of ROGER de Quincy Earl of Winchester & his first wife Helen of Galloway (-after Apr 1282). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Alexander & his wife had nine children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         AGNES Comyn (-after [28 Jan/25 Mar] 1313).  Andrew Wyntoun’s Cronykil records that "Jhon and Alysandyre" had five sisters, the second of which married "Off Stratherne the Erle Malys" by whom she had "a swne…Malys"[1072]
2 CONC .  m (1275 or before) MALISE Earl of Strathearn, son of MALISE Earl of Strathearn & his second wife Matilda of Caithness and Orkney ([1257]-[28 Jan/25 Mar] 1313, bur Inchaffray Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#MaliseStrathearndied1271A
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         MALISE ([1257]-[28 Jan/25 Mar] 1313, bur Inchaffray Abbey).  "Malisius comes de Strathernt" donated a serf to Inchaffray Abbey by charter dated 1258, witnessed by "Malisio filio comitis…Gilberto fratre comitis…[749].  H
2 CONC e succeeded his father in 1271 as Earl of Strathearn.  "Malisius filius quondam Malisii comitis de Stratherne" donated "advocacionem ecclesie de Struy" to Inchaffray Abbey by charter dated to [1282/83][750].  He swore fealty to Ed
2 CONC ward I King of England at Stirling 12 Jul 1291, and did homage to King Edward in 1296.  “Malisius comes de Strathern” confirmed the donation to Coupar-Angus made by “Gilbertus de Haya dominus de Erole” by charter dated to [1306], 
2 CONC witnessed by “...Roberto de Strathern fratre meo, Malisio filio meo et herede...”[751].  He was imprisoned in Rochester Castle in Nov 1306 for his alleged submission to Robert Bruce, but freed in Dec 1308 provided he lived in Engl
2 CONC and.  He is said to have been captured by his son, who fought for the Scots, at Perth 28 Jan 1313.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (1275 or before) AGNES Comyn, daughter of ALEXANDER Comyn Earl of Buchan & his wife Elizabeth de Quincy of Winchester (-after [28 Jan/25 Mar] 1313).  Andrew Wyntoun’s Cronykil records that "Jhon and Alysandyre" had five sisters,
2 CONC  the second of which married "Off Stratherne the Erle Malys" by whom she had "a swne…Malys"[752].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Malise & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         MALISE ([1275/80]-before 1329).  He succeeded his father in 1313 as Earl of Strathearn.  m firstly AGNES, daughter of --- (-after Aug 1320).  John of Fordun’s Scotichronicon (Continuator) records that "dominus Willelm
2 CONC us de Sowlis et comitissa de Strathern" were convicted of high treason at a parliament in Scone in Aug 1320 and sentenced to life imprisonment[755].  m secondly ([30 May 1323/7 Jun 1329]) as her first husband, JOAN Menteith, daugh
2 CONC ter of JOHN Menteith of Rusky & his wife --- (-after 20 Mar 1367).
2 CONT * b)         MATILDA (-[1340/48]).  A charter dated 2 May 1293 records the recognisance of "Radulpho de Tony…versus Malisium comitem de Stratherne" (respecting his marriage, although the document does not specify that this is the 
2 CONC case)[765].  m (contract 28 Apr 1293, after 2 May 1293) ROBERT de Tosny, son of RAOUL [VII] de Tosny & his wife Mary --- (Thornby, Scotland 4 Apr 1276-before 28 Nov 1309).  He was summoned to parliament in 1299, whereby he is held
2 CONC  to have become Lord Tosny/Tony. 
2 CONT * c)         GILBERT (-after 13 Aug 1296).  The Wardrobe Accounts of King Edward I for 1296/97 include payments to "Gilberto filio comitis de Straderne" for his expenses in coming to London in August, dated 13 Aug, and payments to
2 CONC  "Gilberto et Roberto filiis comitis de Straterne" dated 17 Jul[766]. 
2 CONT * d)         ROBERT (-after 17 Jul 1296).  The Wardrobe Accounts of King Edward I for 1296/97 include payments to "Gilberto et Roberto filiis comitis de Straterne" dated 17 Jul[767]
2 CONT . 
