1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/Caithness/Forse.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Sutherland married the daughter and heiress of Keith of Forse, and the family style then became "Sutherland of Forse". He was succeeded by his son, John.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/4/mode/2up Page 5 No.18-c and http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/6/mode/2up Page 6 - No. 24
2 CONT
2 CONT 18(c) Kenneth, ancestor of Sutherland of Forse 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Burke's Peerage entry''' - 3a Kenneth, of Drummoy, ancestor of the SUTHERLANDs OF FORSE
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0035
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Sutherland, (son of William, 5th Earl of Sutherland)  who received, in 1401, a charter from his brother Earl Robert of the lands of Drummoy, Backies and others, confirmed by the Duke of Albany, Regent, in 1408.[20] Lord Ha
2 CONC iles also quotes from the Forse charters a writ to Kenneth Sutherland, son of the late William, Earl of Sutherland. He was ancestor of the family of Sutherland of Forse, and his descendant in 1766, Mr. George Sutherland of Forse, 
2 CONC laid claim to the earldom of Sutherland as heir-male. This will be again referred to on a later page.[21]
2 CONT
2 CONT [20] Sutherland Book, iii. 22. [21] Sutherland Book, iii. 36, 37.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.google.com/site/fivegateways/alphabetical-index-s/sutherland/suth0001
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Sutherland of Forse (son of William, 5th Earl of Sutherland) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The descent of this family from that of William, Earl of Sutherland, who died in 1370, is unquestioned, althogh there are conflicting statements among genealogists as to the immediate descendants of that Earl. On 10th November 134
2 CONC 5 he obtained a charter from King David II., "Willelmo comiti de Sutherland et Margaretæ sponæ suæ sorori nostræ carissimæ." According to Douglas, who follows Sir Robert Gordon, he was the great-grandfather of Robert, Earl of Suth
2 CONC erland, and of his brother, Kenneth, ancestor of the Sutherlands of Forse. In the Sutherland Peerage case, 1771, Captain George Sutherland of Forse, a claimant to the dignity, averred his ancestor, Kenneth, to have been the son of
2 CONC  this Earl William, founding on a charter, in 1408, of the three davoch lands of Nottingham, granted by Mariot, daughter and co-heiress of Ranald, Lord Cheyne, with consent of Andrew of Keith, her son, "Kenatho de Sutherlandia fil
2 CONC io quondam Willelmi comitis Sutherlandiæ." It is certain that Kenneth Sutherland was brother of Earl Robert, and that he received from him, in 1400, Drummuy, Backies, and Torish, in Sutherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nottinghame, Nothingham, or Noddingham, as it is variously written, is mentioned as early as 1272, when there was a Canon of Caithness styled "Henry of Nothingham."
2 CONT
2 CONT Kenneth Sutherland married the daughter and heiress of Keith of Forse, and the family style then became "Sutherland of Forse." He was succeeded by his son, John Sutherland of Forse of whom nothing further is known. He had a son Ri
2 CONC chard, 3rd of Forse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Henderson, J. (1884) Caithness Family History. Edinburgh: David Douglas.
