1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Mentheith (1275-1323) married Helena, daughter of Gartnait, Earl of Mar,  by whom he had two sons, Sir John de Menteith the younger and Walter, and one daughter known by name, Johanna. He was said to have had 
2 CONC two other daughters.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_de_Menteith]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ====ThePeerage.com: [https://thepeerage.com/p10789.htm#i107882 Helen of Mar]
2 CONT "Helen of Mar was the daughter of Gartnait, 7th Earl of Mar and Lady Christina Bruce.1 She married Sir John Menteith, Lord of Arran, son of Sir John Menteith of Rusky.1 She married Sir James Garioch.1 She died after 1342.1 She was
2 CONC  also known as Ellen.2"...&c.
2 CONT # Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 208. 
2 CONT # BP2003 volume 2, page 2603.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: Scotland [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#GratneyMardied1305 Earls]
2 CONT '''GRATNEY of Mar,''' son of DONALD Earl of Mar & his wife Helen --- (-[24 Jul 1297/early 1302?])....'''m''' ([1295?]) as her first husband, '''CHRISTIANA Bruce''', daughter of ROBERT [VI] de Brus [Bruce] Earl of Carrick & his fir
2 CONC st wife Margaret Ctss of Carrick ([1280/83?]-[1356/27 Jan 1357], bur Dunfermline)....'''Gratney & his wife had three children:''' 
2 CONT # DONALD ([1298/1300?]-killed in battle Duplin 12 Aug 1332)....
2 CONT # DAVID of Mar (-after 1327)....
2 CONT # ELLEN of Mar. Her family origin and marriage are confirmed by the following document: King David II restored “terras de Strongartney...infra vicecomitatum de Perth, nunc autem infra vicecomitatum de Striuelyn”, which his father 
2 CONC had granted to “quondam Johanni de Meneteth militi patri predicti Johannis de Meneteth et Elene de Marr sponse eiusdem, nepti sue” to [her son] “Johanne de Meneteth milite, consanguineo nostro” by charter dated 5 Apr 1359[579]. De
2 CONC positions dated 6 Oct 1447 made by “Andreas de Keth de Inverwgy etatis octoginta annorum” state that “domini Roberti de Erskyne comitis de Marr” was descended from “domino comiti de Marr dicto Gartnay”, recording that “dictus come
2 CONC s Gartnay de Marr genuit Donaldum comitem de Marr et duas filias”, that the sisters of Earl Donald married “una cum Roberto de Broyss Rege [incorrect] que sine liberis decessit et alia soror...Domino Johanne de Menteth” by whom sh
2 CONC e had two daughters, of whom the older married “Dominus Edwardus de Keth qui genuit ex ea Jonetam” who married “Domino Thoma de Erskyn” who fathered “Dominum Robertum de Erskyn comitem de Marr sepedictum”[580].  he primary source 
2 CONC which confirms her name has not yet been identified. '''m JOHN de Menteith''' of Strathgartney and Arran, son of JOHN de Menteith of Rusky & his wife --- (-before 1344).
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Our Royal, Noble, Titled and Commoner Ancestors and Cousins [https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p122.htm#i3653 Ellen of Mar]
2 CONT "Ellen of Mar married Sir John Menteith, Lord Arran, son of Sir John Menteith, Sheriff of Dunbarton, Laird of Ruskie and Margery de Strivelyn, circa 1320. Ellen of Mar died after 1342."
2 CONT # Magna Charta Sureties, 1215, by F. L. Weis, 4th Ed., p. 45; Wallop Family, p. 541.
