1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John, the eldest son, was usually styled of " the Stanehous," which property seems to have been generally the residence of the heirs-apparent of the house of Airth. He was a knight, and was during his father's life
2 CONC time " slaughtered " by the Menteiths of Karse, his wife's brothers. In this feud, Sir John the Brois fell 1483 by the hand of his brother-in-law, William Menteith of Karse ;
2 CONT '''Sir John married 1471, Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Menteith of Karse, and by her had issue three sons and three daughters,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. Robert, succeeded his grandfather in Airth.
2 CONT
2 CONT >2. Thomas of Lethbertscheilles.
2 CONT
2 CONT >3. James  of Mungowallis.
2 CONT
2 CONT >4. Helen married Menteith of Karse.
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. Janet, married William Livingston, younger of Kilsyth, who was killed at Flodden, 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT >6. Elizabeth  married Muir of Skaithmure.
2 CONT
