1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT ''Last updated 17 July 2025''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isabella'''  was the widow of Sir John Graham, 'who had a terce of his lands in crichton... and a lease of the other two-thirds.' [SP VI:196[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her origins are not known.  Her husband, John de Graham, of Dalkeith, Abercorn and Eskdale (Nicholas2, Henry1) was born about 1278; died on 25 Apr 1337.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their three known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * A. [https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Graham-of-Dalkeith/6000000026876113073?through=6000000004533941022 '''Sir John de Graham''']  filius, last of Dalkeith, Abercorn, and Eskdale, who parted with those estates, finally resig
2 CONC ning Dalkeith in favour of Sir William Douglas de Laudonia 6 January '''1341-2''' [7].  On his death the direct male line of the elder branch of the family of Graham ended. [d.s.p.  No known wife or issue.]
2 CONT * B. [https://www.geni.com/people/Sybilla-Graham-of-Abercorn/6000000004533941022?through=6000000026874295420 '''Sybilla'''], (?), married to Sir '''William''' [Reginald?]  More, and, on the resignation of her father or brother, su
2 CONC cceeded to the barony of Abercorn.1 [Abercorn passed to the Mure family.]
2 CONT * C. [https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Graham/6000000083942139277?through=6000000010436556832 '''Margaret'''], said to have been married to Sir William Douglas de Laudonia, the ' Knight of Liddesdale, ' though his only known w
2 CONC ife was named Elizabeth. (See title Morton.) It may, however, have been a marriage with a Graham which carried to the family of Douglas Dalkeith, Kilbucho, and Newlands in Peeblesshire, and the lands of Eskdale.2 [As heir to her b
2 CONC rother John, Dalkeith passed to this Douglas family.]
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no recorded birth dates for these children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
