1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret Graham b: ABT 1302 in Abercorn, Linlithgow, Scotland was the younger daughter of Sir John de Graham of Dalkeith, Abercorn and Eskdale (d. 1337) and his wife Isabella. Her name is not certain and it’s also 
2 CONC seen as Elizabeth, but that could be a mixup with her husband’s second wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >From Stirnet (?): On the death of Sir John de Graham the estates at Dalkeith fell to Sir John's sister, '''''Marjory''''', who was married to William Douglas of Lugton, thus came into the possession of the House of Douglas.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first wife of Sir William Douglas of Liddesdale and mother of his daughter Mary Douglas (d. Bef 1367).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
