1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Wallace, 7th of Riccarton, 2nd of Craigie son of Sir John Wallace, 6th of Riccarton, 1st of Craigie and Margaret Lindsay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Abt 1399 in Lochleven, Kinross, Scotland to Margaret Douglas b. 25 Oct 1372 daughter of Sir Henry Douglas, of Lugton and Lochleven
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *1. Sir Hugh Wallace, 3rd of Craigie, 8th of Riccarton  b. d. Abt 1407 (Age ~ 37 years)
2 CONT *	2. Sir William Wallace, 4th of Craigie, 9th of Riccarton b.  d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT *	3. dau. Wallace d. Yes, date unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT To Sir John Wallace and Margaret Lindsay, spouses, was born a son, John. As "Sir John Wallace" he had a charter of the lands of Thuriston, in the barony of Innerwick; also of twenty merks of annual-rent out of the lands of Thornyl
2 CONC e, in the barony of Renfrew, and eight merks of annual-rent out of the lands of Ingliston, in the barony of Durisdeer and county of Dumfries; together with the lands of Retre (Rattray) in the earldom of Buchan. Prior to 1390 Sir J
2 CONC ohn Wallace witnessed a charter confirming grants of various lands in Kyle, executed by John Stewart, Earl of Carrick, afterwards Robert III. He married Lady Margaret Stewart, who, on the 6th April 1399, gave two merks to the Prea
2 CONC ching Friars of Glasgow. To Sir John Wallace and Lady Margaret Stewart were born two sons, Hugh and William.
2 CONT
2 CONT [The Book of Wallace by Rev. Charles Rogers pub.1889]
2 CONT
