2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Alexander Gordon,1st Earl of Huntly:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10957.htm#i109564
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly [1]
2 CONT *M, #109564, 
2 CONT *d. 15 July 1470
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly married, firstly, Egida Hay, daughter of Sir John Hay and Margaret Stewart, c 8 ajn 1426/7.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Elizabeth Crichton, daughter of William Crichton of that Ilk, 1st Lord Crichton, before 18 March 1439/40.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 15 July 1470 at Huntly, Aberdeenshire, Scotland.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir Alexander Seton and Elizabeth Gordon.[2] 
2 CONT *He was baptised with the name of Alexander Seton.[5] 
2 CONT *His marriage to Egida Hay was annulled before 1438.[2] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Earl of Huntly [Scotland] from 30 October 1444 to 3 July 1445.[1],[2] 
2 CONT *In 1451 he had Crown grants of the territorial Lordship of Badenoch.[2] 
2 CONT *He inherited from his grandmother, Elizabeth Keith, Aboyne, Cluny and Glenmuick, Aberdeenshire.2 On circa 1457 his name was legally changed to Alexander Gordon.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly
2 CONT *1. Catherine Seton [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Crichton
2 CONT *1. Lady Christian Gordon+
2 CONT *2. George Gordon, 2nd Earl of Huntly+[6] d. 8 Jun 1501
2 CONT *3. Lady Elizabeth Gordon+[1] d. 17 Apr 1500
2 CONT *4. Adam Gordon+[7] d. 1528
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and Egida Hay
2 CONT *1. Sir Alexander Gordon of Abergeldie+[8] d. b Jan 1504
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly and unknown Cumming
2 CONT *1. Janet Gordon+[2]
2 CONT *2. Margaret Gordon [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 156. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 2011. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VII, page 121. [S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family."
2 CONT *4. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume VI, page 675.
2 CONT *5. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 3, page 3397.
2 CONT *6. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2565.
2 CONT *7. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 23.
2 CONT
