1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GEORGE WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Paterson and Charles Rogers both agree that George Wallace of Elderslie here treated succeeded John Wallace of Elderslie, although neither man actually claims that John was his father. Charles Rogers says that George witn
2 CONC essed a charter in favour of Paisley Abbey dated 5 August 1466. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n74/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, p. 23] and Paterson, says that he was still  living in 1468. [https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/struntyay00pategoog#page/n231/mode/1up Ayrshire II, p. 220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for George Wallace of Elderslie. He was alive on 3 February 1499. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/536/mode/1up Great Seal of Scotland, II, charter number
2 CONC  2527 on pp. 536-37] and appears still to have been alive on 23 July 1502. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/56/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 74 on pp
2 CONC . 56-7]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Register of Paisley Abbey===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1466: Georgio Waless de Elyrisle [https://archive.org/stream/registrummonaste00mait#page/149/mode/1up Paisley Registrum, pp. 149-151. George Wallace is noticed on p. 151]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                   1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1495: Geo. Wallace de Ellerslee [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/529/mode/1up Great Seal of Scotland, II, charter number 2485 on p. 529]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 February 1499-1500: Rex confirmavit cartam Johannis Wallace de Cragy, sub hac forma; - [To all men etc.,- Johnne Wallace of Cragy greting;-Wit ye me to have gevin and grantit to my dearest cousing PATRIK WALLACE, son and appe
2 CONC rand ayre to my derest eme George Wallace of Ellirsle, - for the homage and service of the said Patrick, etc., - my landis of Ellersle in the barony of Renfrew and schirefdome of the samyn; quilkis landis of before wer of the said
2 CONC  George heretably, and the quikis he of his free will and deliverir mynde, wilfully be staff and bastoun in my handis as oure lord resignit: To bE HALDIN to the said Patrik and hys airis mail quatsumever, the quilkis failyeand tur
2 CONC nand to me the said Johne and my airis quatsumever: GEVAND tharfore yerly homage and service with dewities aucht and wonnt:- Reservand nevertheles the cheif chymmes to the said Johnne and to his airis, and half ane merkis worth of
2 CONC  land of aild extent liand nixt and togidder to the said chief chymmes; and alsa reservand the franktenement of the said landis of Ellersle to the said George Wallace and to Katherine Graham his spous and the langar levand of tham
2 CONC e:- In witnes etc., - At Cragy the third of Februare 1499, - befor thir witnes, Hew Wallace, William Wallace my broder germane, Robert Wallace, Johnne Lokarte, Charles Ros, Gawane Ros, and schir Donald Moffet, chaplain. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/536/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D.1424-1513, charter number 2527 on pp. 536-37]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Master Cuthberti Simonis===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/2/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 2 on pp. 2-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abstract in English'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: Instrument of resignation by George Wallace, in the hands of John Walles of Cragy, as superior, in favour of Patrick Walles, son and apparent heir of the said George, of all right, claim, property and possession 
2 CONC which he had in or to the lands of Ellersly, in the shire of Renfrew: reserving, however, to himself and to Katherine Graham, his spouse, the frank tenement of the foresaid lands during their respective lives. Whereup the said Pat
2 CONC rick asked instruments. Done at the castle of Cragy, on the 24th day of March 1499 [1500], at six o'clock in the afternoon, or thereby, in presence of Hugh Walles and William Walles, brothers german to the said John Walles of Crag
2 CONC y, Robert Walles, Gavin Ros, Charles Ros, Sir John Ledhous, chaplain, and John Douglas, witnesses to the premisses. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/266/mode/1up protocol number 2 on p. 266]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/3/mode/1up  Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 3 on p. 3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abstract in English'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/267/mode/1up protocol number 3 on p. 267]'''
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/3/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 4 on pp. 3-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abstract in English'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/267/mode/1up protocol number 4 on p. 267]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1499: "Patricio Walles, filio et apparenti herede Georgii Walles de Ellirsly" and "Johanne Walles, fratre germano eiusdem Patricio" are noticed in the witness list of a charter in favour of "Hugonis Walles, [fratre]
2 CONC  germani Johannis Walles de Cragy." [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/24/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 34 on pp.24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abstract in English'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1499: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/281/mode/1up protocol number 34 on pp. 281-82]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 July 1502: [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/56/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 74 on pp.56-7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abstract in English'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 July 1502: Instrument on the resignation by George Walles of Elllirsly into the hands of Andrew Graham of Knockdolian, his superior, of the 20s. lands of old extent of Penbraid, which were then in the lands of Patrick Walles
2 CONC , son and apparent heir of the said George, in the lordship of Knockdolian and earldom of Carrick; and on the obligation by the said Andrew, by formerly delivering to the said Patrick Walles, the staff and baton, to grant to the l
2 CONC atter a charter and precept of sasine of the said lands to him and to his heirs and assignees heritably. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor01bain#page/301/mode/1up protocol number 74 on 301]'''
