2 CONT Duke of Montrose
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Lords Graham (1445)
2 CONT Patrick Graham, 1st Lord Graham (d. c. 1466)
2 CONT '''William Graham, 2nd Lord Graham (d. 1472), eldest son of the 1st Lord'''
2 CONT William Graham, 3rd Lord Graham (1464–1513), became Earl of Montrose in 1503; a great-grandson of Robert III
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_of_Montrose
2 CONT _________
2 CONT William Graham, 1st Earl of Montrose (1464 – 9 September 1513) was a Scottish Lord of Parliament, who was raised to an earldom by James IV of Scotland and who died with his monarch at the Battle of Flodden.
2 CONT Origins
2 CONT Montrose was the '''eldest son and heir of William Graham, 2nd Lord Graham by Eleanor, or Elene''', the daughter of William Douglas, 2nd Earl of Angus. The Grahams were a long-established family of Norman origin, who first rose to
2 CONC  prominence in the reign of David I.[1]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Montrose married first (on 25 November 1479) Annabel Drummond, one of the five daughters of John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond, secondly Janet Edmonstone, daughter of Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath and thirdly Christian Wawan
2 CONC e of Seggie, in Fife, the widow of Patrick Haliburton, 5th Lord Haliburton.
2 CONT By his first wife, Montrose had:
2 CONT *William Graham, 2nd Earl of Montrose
2 CONT *Walter Graham, of Little Cairnie.
2 CONT By his third wife, Montrose had a further son, Patrick Graham of Inchbraikie (grandfather of Bishop George Graham), to which lands Patrick received a charter from his father on 20 June 1513.
2 CONT Montrose also had three daughters:
2 CONT *Helen Graham, who married (dispensation 13 July 1509) Humphrey Colquhoun, Younger of Luss
2 CONT *Nicolas Graham (a daughter of Graham's second marriage), who married (11 February 1504) John Moray, 6th of Abercairney
2 CONT *Elizabeth Graham (a daughter of Graham's second marriage), who married (February 1514) Walter Drummond, Master of Drummond, the grandson of John Drummond, 1st Lord Drummond
2 CONT *Margaret Graham (a daughter of Graham's second marriage), who married (contract 10 July 1510) Sir John Somerville of Cambusnethan
2 CONT *Jean Graham, who married David Graham, 3rd of Fintry.
2 CONT Other reputed (but doubtful) progeny include Andrew Graham, who was consecrated Bishop of Dunblane in 1575, and Jean Graham, who was said to have had a daughter by William Chisholm (I), who was consecrated Bishop of Dunblane in 15
2 CONC 26.[2][3]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Graham,_1st_Earl_of_Montrose
2 CONT ___
2 CONT William Graham, 2nd Lord Graham http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/s/a/n/Robert-Marion-Sanders-CA/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-1679.html
2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham (son of Patrick Graham) was born Abt. 1424, and died Abt. 1471. He married Helen Douglas, daughter of William 2nd Earl of Angus Douglas,  and Margaret Elizabeth Hay, .
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Graham and Helen Douglas are:
2 CONT
2 CONT     +William Graham, MCh41G.12, b. Abt. 1455, Montrose, Scotland, d. September 09, 1513, in battle of Flodden, Branxton, Northumberland, England.
