1 NOTE The following is copied from the "Clan Stirling Online" website athttp://www.clanstirling.org/Main/keirstory/2.FromLukastoThoraldus.html:
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. John de Striwelyne of Rathoran in Lorn was born about 1295 inScotland. He served in the military on July 19, 1333 in Halidon Hill,Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT John de Striwelyne is presumed to have been taken prisoner at HalidonHill on 19th of July 1333, where his cousin of the same name was slain.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Mary, the aunt of John of Argyll, Lord of Lorn the last ofthe male line of the ancient Lords of Lorn, who claimed descent fromDugal, the son of Somerled of Argyle and the Isles. John of Lorn grantedto Mary, his Aunt, 
2 CONC the lands of Rathoran, and others, in Lorn, to be heldof the granter of payment of a pair of spurs. This charter is dated atPerth on the (Activity of St. Mary 1338 (Haile's Annals, vol. iii. p. 92,1792 Edition); it was perhaps gra
2 CONC nted to the lady on the occasion of hermarriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the following year, 1339 John de Striwelyne and Alan Boyd, styled byFordun 'valentes armigeri' commanded the Archers, under the Steward ofScotland, at the siege of Perth, when they were both slain. (Fordoun,xiii. Page 45)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wyntoun in his Cronykil also records the death of John de Striwelyne atPerth -
2 CONT
2 CONT Qwhil thai ware lyand at that Toun
2 CONT Thai had oft tymys bykkoryng,
2 CONT Qwhare there wes far and nere schotyng
2 CONT Thaire deyd two Scottis Sqwyeris
2 CONT As thai war governand thaire archerys
2 CONT Alane Boyd and Jhone of Stryvelyne
2 CONT (Vol II, Page 233-234) He died in 1339 in Siege of Perth, Perth, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has reference number VI. - The Stirlings of Keir.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Mary of Lorn in 1338 in Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Mary of Lorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary is the Aunt of John of Argyll, Lord of Lorn, the last of the maleline of the ancient Lords of Lorn. John de Striwelyne of Rathoran in Lornand Mary of Lorn had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     i. William de Strivelyng of Rathoran.
