1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Livingston of Callendar, who fell at Homildon Hill, married to (first name unknown) Menteith, daughter of John Menteith of Kerse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Livingston and ? Menteith had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Alexander Livingston of Callendar  
2 CONT # Robert Livingston, Burgess of Stirling, reputed to have been the ancestor of the Livingstons of Westquarter.  
2 CONT # John Livingston, reputed to have been the progenitor of the Livingstons of Banton or Ballintoun in Stirlingshire.  
2 CONT # James Livingston who got into trouble with the officers of the Exchequer in 1417, in an attempt to evade the Linlithgow customs over the export of some wool. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT # The Livingstons of Callendar, etc by Edwin Brockholst Livingston 1920
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''(Miss) Menteith'''1
2 CONT Last Edited	4 Apr 2020
2 CONT F, #23424
2 CONT '''Father'''	John Menteith, 1st Laird of Kerse, Sheriff of Clackmannanshire b. c 1332, d. b Oct 1382
2 CONT Charts	Pedigree of James Irvine
2 CONT '''     (Miss) Menteith married Sir John Livingston''', son of Sir William Livingston, Sheriff of Haddington and Christian de Callendar. '''(Miss) Menteith was born at of Kerse, Scotland.'''
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Sir John Livingston''' d. 1402
2 CONT '''Children	'''
2 CONT *Christina Livingstone+2
2 CONT *Sir Alexander Livingston, Lord Callendar, Justiciary+ b. c 1382, d. 1451
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT 1.[S7363] Unknown author, Wallop Family, p. 494.
2 CONT 2.[S11649] Clan MacFarlane & Associated Clans Genealogy.
