1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Fergus Graham''' ''of Plomp'' married Sybil Bell, daughter of William Bell of Blackethouse and Elizabeth Bowmont. He lived at Plomp, Cumberland, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir Richard Graham of Esk, 1st Baronet. was the son of Fergus Graham of Plomp and Sybil Bell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=Cq8KAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA535&ots=fjDWmJXfED&dq=fergus%20graham%20of%20Plomp&pg=PA535#v=onepage&q=fergus%20graham%20of%20Plomp&f=true page 535] of A General and Heraldic Dictionary of the Peerage and 
2 CONC Baronetage of ..., Volume 1 By John Burke
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n87/mode/2up page 69] of George Edward Cokayne Complete Baronetage Volume 2 1900
2 CONT *Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, [http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/graham12.php Graham12] subscription required to view
2 CONT * [http://www.armigerousdescents.com/db/getperson.php?personID=I38609&tree=scratch#sthash.deFiRkUW.dpbs Ambigerous Descents] 
2 CONT ** Geschichte und Landesbeschreibung des Herzogthums Lauenburg, vol. II, von Kobbe, P. (1836), (Altona: Johann Friedrich Hammerich), p. 99.
2 CONT ***Fergus Graham, or Grahame, of Plomp, co. Cumberland, who by Sibill his wife, daughter of William Bell of Godsbrigg and Blacket House (or Bladethouse) in Scotland, had issue:-
2 CONT ***[In Nicholson and Burns' Westmoreland and Cumberland, ii. 466, and in Hutchinson's Cumberland, ii. 531, this Fergus is said to have been son of a Matthias Graham. It may be noted that in an agreement for arbitration entered int
2 CONC o 11 May 1573, between Sir John Johnstone, knight, and several of the Grahams, relating to the slaughter of Archibald Johnstone of Myrehead, occurs the name of 'Fargus Grahame son to vmquhile Mathew Grahame' (Annadale Family Book,
2 CONC  i. lxxiii); Fergus 'the Plumpe,' of 'of Plumpe,' is named in 1596 and 1597 (Border Papers, ii. 127, 308).]
2 CONT --------------------
