1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET MOUBRAY===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1545: Instrument of Sasine by John Buchquhanane [Buchanan] of Gartavirtane in favour of Margaret Mowbray [Moubray], Countess of Menteith and Walter Grahame [Graham], her son, of the lands of Gartavirtane, 22 May 1545. [h
2 CONC ttp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f452&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+mowbray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graha
2 CONC m Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/452]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1548: Instrument of Sasine following on the sale of the lands of Gartevertane by Andrew Buchquhanane, son and heir to the deceased John Buchquhanane of Gartavirtane in favour of Margaret Mowbray, Countess of Menteith an
2 CONC d Walter Grahame, her son, for the sum of £400 Scots, 26 July 1548. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f452&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+mowbray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1
2 CONC 670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/452]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://www.thepeerage.com/p1938.htm#i19376 Evidence from Darryl Lundy's Peerage]===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Moubray is the daughter of John Moubray.[1]  She married William Graham, 3rd Earl of Menteith, son of Alexander Graham, 2nd Earl of Menteith and Margaret Buchanan. Child of Margaret Moubray and William Graham, 3rd Earl
2 CONC  of Menteith 1. Lady Margaret Graham+[1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations: 1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom,
2 CONC  Extant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 199. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.'''
