2 CONT *Succeeded by George Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT Political offices
2 CONT *Lord Chancellor of Scotland (1546–1562)	
2 CONT *Preceded by Cardinal Beaton, Archbishop of St Andrews	
2 CONT *Succeeded by 4th Earl of Morton
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10922.htm#i109218
2 CONT
2 CONT George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly [1]
2 CONT *M, #109218, 
2 CONT *b. 1513, 
2 CONT *d. 22 October 1562
2 CONT *Last Edited=25 Apr 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.64%
2 CONT
2 CONT George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly was born in 1513.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Keith, daughter of Robert Keith, Master of Marischal and Lady Elizabeth Douglas, on 27 March 1530.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 22 October 1562, apparently from a seizure (not wounds).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of John Gordon, Lord Gordon and Margaret Stewart.[2] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Huntly [S., 1445] on 21 January 1523/24.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord Chancellor [Scotland] between 1546 and 1549.[3] 
2 CONT *He was decorated with the award of Knight, Order of St. Michael of France in 1548.[3] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Earl of Moray [Scotland] on 13 February 1548/49.[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lieutenant-General of the North.[3] 
2 CONT *He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland].[3] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord Chancellor [Scotland] from 1561 to 1562.[3] 
2 CONT *On 22 October 1562 at Corriche, Scotland, he was taken prisoner after rebelling.[3] On 28 May 1563 his titles were forfeited.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of George Gordon, 4th Earl of Huntly and Elizabeth Keith
2 CONT *1. Thomas Gordon [3]
2 CONT *2. George Gordon, 5th Earl of Huntly+[3] d. 19 Oct 1576
2 CONT *3. Lady Margaret Gordon+[4]
2 CONT *4. Lady Jean Gordon+[3] d. 14 May 1629
2 CONT *5. Lady Elizabeth Gordon+[1] d. b 1557
2 CONT *6. Alexander Gordon, Lord Gordon [3] d. bt 18 Sep 1552 - 11 Aug 1553
2 CONT *7. Sir John Gordon of Ogilvy [3] d. Oct 1562
2 CONT *8. Sir Adam Gordon [3] d. 1580
2 CONT
