1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "KYNNINMOND of That-Ilk, an ancient Family in the shire of Fife, Azure, a Cheveron Argent, between three Flower-de-lisses Or. Pont's Manuscript. Of this Family was Matthew Kynninmond Archdean of St. Andrews, who be
2 CONC came Bishop of Aberdeen, Anno 1172. The Family continued till of late that it came to an Heiress, Grissil Kynninmond, married to Sir William Murray of Melgum, descended of a younger Son of Philiphaugh." (Alexander Nisbet: A System
2 CONC  of Heraldry Speculative and Practical with the True Art of Blazon.... Edinburgh, MackEuen, 1722. Chap. VII, p. 387)
