1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAVID RATTRAY OF CRAIGHALL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1553-54: Precept by John, earl of Athole, lord of Balwany, for sasine in favour of David Rattray as heir of deceased Silvester Rattray of Kynballo, of lands of Bredwellis and others in barony of Rattray, sheriffdom 
2 CONC of Perth. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f226&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+rattray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Rattray Family
2 CONC  of Craighall, Perthshire, reference GD385/226]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 March 1554-55: Commissio justiciarie facta est Johanni, comiti Atholie, ad capiendum ac curias justiciario [tenendum] pro administratione justitie super Duncanum M*Kessane in Appin commorantem cum Leche More, delatum de crud
2 CONC eli interfectione quondam Dougalli Gow, commissa per dictum Duncanum snis propriis manibus in mense Septembri ultimo preterito in Oumry etc. [Edinburgh, 1 February.] . . . . . Vicecomes respondebit pro £26 18s. 4d. de relevio vigi
2 CONC nti librataram terrarum de Kinbachloch, viz., Ovir Kinbachloch, cum molendino et multuris ejusdem, ac tertie partis terrarum ville de Haltoun, jacentium in beronia de Kinbachloch et infra balliam suam, regine debitis per sasinam d
2 CONC atam David Rettray. [Edinburgh, 15 March.] [https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss02exchgoog/page/579/mode/1up RSRS XVIII: 579]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 August 1576: Antenuptial contract of marriage between George Rettray, son and apparent heir of David Rettray of Craighall, and Janet Drummond, daughter of George Drummond of Newtoun of Blair, 1 August 1576. [https://catalogue
2 CONC .nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD385%2f216&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=david+rettray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Rattray Family of Craighall, Perthshire, r
2 CONC eference GD385/216]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ‘’’[https://archive.org/details/exchequerrollss02exchgoog/page/n8/mode/1up Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland. Vol. XV. 1543-1556. Edited by George Powell McNeill, MA., LL.B., Advocate (H. M. General 
2 CONC Register House, Edinburgh, 1898), 777 pp. including index]’’’
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/qr/rattray01.php Stirnet: Rattray 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT David Rattray, of Craighall and Kynballoch, served heir to his father, ''anno'' 1554. He m. Isabel, dau. of Alexander Ramsay, of Banff, and had two sons, George, his heir; Silvester, minister at Auchtergevan, ancestor of Rattray O
2 CONC f Dalnoon. David Rattray d. in the commencement of the reign of James VI., and was s. by his eldest son, George Rattray, of Craighall...
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Burke's genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry, Volume 2, By John Burke, p. 1100
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Of Craighall, etc., 1554"
2 CONT
2 CONT This person and their pedigree are currently documented from "The Royal Lineage of Our Noble and Gentle Families together with Their Paternal Ancestry" Compiled by Joseph Foster, 1885
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: http://www.archive.org/details/royallineageofou02fost ]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------- David Rattray of Craighall. 14th Laird. Married Isobel d/o Alexander Ramsay of Bamff. Died 1586.
2 CONT *Dawn Stapylton-Adkins. ''James Rattray & His Descendants in South Africa'' 1822-1992, self-published, Cape Town, 1992
