1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don’t confuse her with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Janet_Douglas,_Lady_Glamis Janet Douglas, Lady Glamis] (executed by burning on 17 July 1537)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Janet Douglas
2 CONT * Father:	Sir William Douglas, 5th of Drumlanrig,   d. 10 Sep 1513, battle of Flodden Field, Kirknewton, Northumberland, England  
2 CONT * Mother: Elizabeth Gordon,   d. Yes, date unknown 
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Douglas was the daughter of Sir William Douglas, 6th of Drumlanrig and Elizabeth Gordon.2,1 She married Robert Maxwell, 4th Lord Maxwell, son of John Maxwell, 3rd Lord Maxwell and Agnes Stewart, after 4 July 1509
2 CONT
2 CONT Married  	
2 CONT # Robert Maxwell, 5th Lord Maxwell,   b. 1493-1494, Scotland, d. 9 Jul 1546  Married 	4 Jul 1509  [2, 3]  Type: Contract 
2 CONT
2 CONT from Scots Peerage:
2 CONT
2 CONT > "By agreement between his father and Sir William Douglas of Drumlanrig, he (''Robert Maxwell'') was to marry the latter's daughter Janet (with a tocher of 1000 pounds Scots) between 4 July 1509 and the following Candlemas."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 	
2 CONT *  	1. Robert Maxwell, 6th Lord Maxwell,   d. 13 Sep 1552, Dumfries, Dumfriesshire, Scotland 
2 CONT *  	2. Sir John Maxwell, Master of Maxwell, 4th Lord Herries,   b. 1512,   d. 20 Jan 1583, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland 
2 CONT *  	3. Margaret Maxwell,   b. Abt 1520,   d. 1593
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
