1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frasers_of_Philorth '''Frasers of Philorth''']
2 CONT
2 CONT The Frasers of Philorth are a Scottish lowland family, originally from the Anjou region of France. Their family seat is in Sauchen, Aberdeenshire, Scotland. Since the time of Alexander Fraser, 11th Lord Saltoun, the heads of the P
2 CONC hilorth family are the Lords Saltoun. The current head of the Frasers of Philorth is Flora Fraser, 21st Lady Saltoun who is Chief of the Name and Arms of Clan Fraser since 1 May 1984, by decree of the Court of the Lord Lyon. The f
2 CONC amily's arms are "azure, three cinquefoils argent"—three silver strawberry flowers on a field of blue. The heraldic cinquefoil is a stylized five-point leaf; the cinquefoils which appear the Fraser of Philorth coat-of-arms are spe
2 CONC cifically strawberry flowers. Only the Lady or Lord Saltoun is permitted to display these arms plain and undifferenced.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I32508&tree=CC
