1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME MARGARET KENNEDY Countess of Cassillis ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Kennedy is the daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany. Her date and place of birth are not known. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/471/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 471]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Kennedy made her last will and testament at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maybole Maybole,] probably at [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassillis_Castle Cassillis Castle] there, on 28 November 1580. She nominated 
2 CONC her son Thomas Kennedy "tutor of Cassillis" to be her only executor and intromitter with "all my guids & geir" and left a number of legacies. Confirmation was granted on 12 January 1597. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Co
2 CONC mmissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedie, relict of Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081030052877& Image of Testament A]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081030044838& Image of Testament B]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081028674309& Image of Testament C]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081029824836& Image of Testament D]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Date of Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''An exact date of death cannot be identified for Dame Margaret Kennedy. She made her last will and testament on 28 November 1580 and probably died very soon thereafter. According to the opening paragraph of her testamentary reco
2 CONC rd she died in 1580, and it seems safe to suppose, therefore, that she must have died after 28 November but before 31 December in that year. [Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedi
2 CONC e, relict of Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Place of Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''An exact place of death  cannot be identified for Dame Margaret Kennedy. However, she made her last will and testament at [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maybole Maybole] in the Carrick division of South Ayrshire, in Scotland, a
2 CONC nd it seems reasonable to suggest that she may have died at [https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassillis_Castle Cassillis Castle] there.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Kennedy was probably buried in the Collegiate Church of Maybole. This is certainly where she wished to be buried: "I dame mgaret kennedie countess of cassillis seik in body bot haill in mynd . . . . . In the first
2 CONC  I leif my saull to God Almytie my body to be bureit in the college kirk of Mayboill besyde my umqle sone erle of cassillis". [Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedie, relict of Gi
2 CONC lbert, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Kennedy married, as her first husband, William Wallace of Craigie. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/471/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 471] He died in 1538. [https://archive.org/stream/book
2 CONC ofwallace01roge#page/n116/mode/1up The Book of Wallace: 44]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Wallace/6000000003043322999
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Wallace/6000000002367962680?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1533717243190&through=6000000001745181424
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace/6000000033892559420
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Margaret Kennedy married, as her second husband, Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis. He died in 1558. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/471/mode/1up/search/quintin+kennedy The Scots Peerage II: 471]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children of Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Gilbert-Kennedy-4th-Earl-of-Cassilis/6000000008028072610?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1533710922846&through=6000000001745181424
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/David-Kennedy/6000000081020807726
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Thomas-Kennedy-1st-of-Culzean/6000000001213825537?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1533711264984&through=6000000001213825537
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Kennedy-Countess-of-Orkney/6000000003646057844
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Kennedy/6000000002166140373
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 February 1540-41: Precept from Chancery for infefting the Earl and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his lady in conjunct fee and liferent in the 10 merk land of Balgray the two Auchintibbers, Fulwood Gabrachhill Br
2 CONC ydilands, Struther and Peacockbank, with the mill thereof, the lands of Spittal, 20 shilling land of Whitelees, lands of Over and Nether Bordlands extending to a 40 merk land all lying in the Lordship of Stewarton and bailiary of 
2 CONC Cunningham. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f406&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy
2 CONC  Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/406] [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/518/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 151
2 CONC 3-1546, charter number 2270 on p. 518]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 August 1559: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his mother relict of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis his father, bearing that the Countess shall have the place of Cassillis w
2 CONC ith the garden and orchard thereof for her residence during all the days of her life, and the Earl assigns to her yearly during her life, 110 bolls of meal, 52 bolls bear, 115 merks money, 89 capons, 36 salmon and the 3d. part of 
2 CONC the Meadow of Blairboy, and that in contentation of all terce and conjunct fee lands falling to her, or to which she can anywise claim by and throw the decease of her husband, lying in the Counties of Ayr and Wigton, and which mea
2 CONC l, bear, silver, capons and salmon, to be uplifted and payable from the Mains of Cassillis, 4 merk land of Giltreehill, 2 merk land of Pinmyrie, 2 merk land of Carsonston, and lands of Holehouse, 20 shilling land of Lindsayston, h
2 CONC alf merk land of Dunurehill, Bernard thomsons merk land, 2 merk land of Milltoun of Cassillis, Archibald Hamiltons merk land, 20 shilling land of Drumboy, 20 shilling land of Barnshean, 20 shilling land of Over Craufurdston, 2 mer
2 CONC k land of Nether Craufurdston, 2 merk land of Middle Craufurdston, 2 merk land of Gunerston, half merk land of Makroriston, 10 shilling land of Burnmouth, Down-dunches half merk land, merk land of Garpin, 3 merk land of Burnford, 
2 CONC 21 merk land of Balquhirn and Balmuck, and Charles Kennedys merk land all lying in the barony of Cassillis - for which causes, the Countess discharges the Earl her son and his successors, of all right and title which she had to th
2 CONC e terce and conjunct fee lands falling to her by and through the decease of her husband as aforesaid, and of all tacks steadings and possessions pertaining to her husband, by virtue of the Act made at his going to France, dated at
2 CONC  Edinburgh ......... 1557, and renounces her office of executrice, to the Earl her son, which office was conferred on her by her husband, with power to the Earl to use the same as fully and freely as she could have done in virtue 
2 CONC of her husbands Latter Will - and also makes and constitutes the Earl and his successors her bailies (with service of men hosts, and raids or armies) of her terce lands, with power to his Lordship and his aforesaid, by themselves 
2 CONC or their deputes, to hold courts, and do every thing concerning the office of bailiary, which she could have done by her deputes; and also the Earl grants permission to her, during all the days of her life, to take wood to the pla
2 CONC ce of Cassillis from the woods of Cassillis and Dalrymple. Witnesses - David Kennedy of Culean, James Kennedy of Ochterlour, John Kennedy of Skeldon, John Blair of Middle-Auchindrain, and Dean John Mure Sub-Prior of Crossragwell. 
2 CONC Dated at Mayboll.This Contract ratified at Ayr 4th Novemb. 1559, by Quintin Abbot of Crossragwell, Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains, David Kennedy of Culean, and Mr Thomas Hay Parson of Spynie, four of the six curators of the Earl.
2 CONC  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f576&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Ea
2 CONC rls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/576]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 August 1559: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his mother, by which for the love and favor he bears to her, and for decorating her house, he gives her during all the d
2 CONC ays of her life, the yearly rent of the 2 and a half merk land of Craigmulloch, lying in the Earldom of Carrick as possessed by John Makquhilie herd, together with 101 milk ewes, 77 yeild ewes, 108 wedders, 40 gimmers, and 40 dinm
2 CONC ents, as also other 80 gimmers and dinments all to be received by her, from the said John Makquhilie, at the feast of Beltran then next 1560, together with 11 old goats and 2 kids - as also he gives to the Countess his mother 104 
2 CONC head of nolt pasturing upon the lands of Kericastle in the forest of Buchan viz. 16 nicol cows and as many calves, 17 ferow and 9 yeild cows, 5 three year old cows, 22 old oxen, 2 bulls, 6 three year old oxen and 2 bulls, 5 two ye
2 CONC ar old oxen, 3 two year old queys, 8 quey stirks and 9 oxen stirks, which sheep, goats, and cattle, the Countess obliges herself her heirs, and executors, to leave on the ground of the lands respectively above mentioned at her dec
2 CONC ease, or the like number, and of as great avail, for the use of the Earl and his successors - and also he gives to the Countess during all the days of her life, a silver basin and a laver, a double gilt cup of silver raised work, 
2 CONC with a cover, 2 cases of silver, the one gilt, and the other ungilt, a gilt macer, 2 silver trenchers (plates) with 2 little salt-fats in their nooks (corners), 12 silver spoons, a silver salt-fat, and cover thereof, ungilt, a bla
2 CONC ck velvet bed, with the curtains of black damask, and 4 pieces of tapestry in Edinburgh, and 4 feather beds and their bolsters - all which silver work, tapestry, and beding, the Countess obliges her and hers aforesaid, to leave to
2 CONC  the Earl and his successors, within the place of Cassillis at her decease, or as much, and of the same avail - and also for certain good causes, she assigns the Earl her son in and to all moveable goods which may belong to her at
2 CONC  the time of her decease, and the Earl being under age, he obliges himself to chuse curators between and Martinmas then next, and cause them ratify the Contract. Witnesses - David Kennedy of Culean, James Kennedy of Ochterlour, Jo
2 CONC hn Kennedy of Skeldon and John Blair of Middle-Auchindrain. Dated at Mayboll. The Contract ratified at Ayr 5th Novemb. 1559, by Quintin Abbot of Crossragwell Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains David Kennedy of Culean, and Mr Thomas H
2 CONC ay parson of Spynie the Earls curators. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f577&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Sco
2 CONC tland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/577]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''November 1573: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Hugh Earl of Eglinton, proceeding upon a narrative of the Earl of Cassillis having annalied under reversion to Robert Graham of Knockdolian, the greater half of the 
2 CONC barony of Stewarton, to be holden feu of the Earl for payment yearly of £120, and also the lesser half of the said barony, to be holden blanch of the Earl, together with the barony of Dunure in warrandice of the said barony of Ste
2 CONC warton, from the liferent of Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis Mother of the Earl and had discharged the said Robert Graham of the feu mails of the barony of Stewarton during the not redemption, as six several Letters of
2 CONC  Reversion granted by the said Robert Grahan containing 1000 merks each, did bear, and that the said Robert Graham had annalied to the Earl of Eglinton, the said baronies of Stewarton and Dunure to be holden of the Earl of Cassill
2 CONC is as said is, and had constitute the Earl of Eglinton and Dame Agnes Drummond his wife and their heirs his cessioners and assignees in and to the original Contract of Sale between the Earl of Cassillis and him, and Infeftment fol
2 CONC lowing thereupon, And subsuming that the Earl of Eglinton had paid to the said Robert Graham a greater sum than the 6000 merks contained in the Contract and Letters of Reversion above mentioned viz. 1100 merks, which computed alon
2 CONC g with the annualrent thereof extends to 1485 merks, so that the yearly rent which the Earl of Eglinton shall receive from the barony of Stewarton at the expiry of 3 years and a half from the date of the Contract extends to 748 me
2 CONC rks, 6 shillings, 8 pence, and therefore he shall possess the said barony and uplift the rents thereof during the not redemption, by seven several Letters of Reversion, the first six to contain 1000 merks each, every 1000 merks re
2 CONC deeming 100 merks of rent, and the last to contain 1485 merks, and shall ratify the first six Letters of Reversion granted by the said Robert Graham as said is, or renew the same conform to the Original Contract, and shall grant a
2 CONC  seventh Letter of Reversion as said is, containing 1485 merks upon redemption of the said sum of 748 merks 6 shillings 8 pence to be paid in the Church of Ayr, and at the expiry of the said 3 and a half years, the Earl of Cassill
2 CONC is to receive the said barony of Stewarton from the Earl of Eglinton and his wife for payment yearly of 748 merks 6 shillings 8 pence and find caution for payment thereof, according as the Earl of Eglinton shall desire. Witnesses 
2 CONC - Thomas Master of Cassillis, William Stewart of Dunduff, Andw. Nevin of Monkridding, and William Highgate burgess of Glasgow. Dated at Glasgow, and Irvin, 9th and 10th Novemb. 1573. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f806&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference G
2 CONC D25/1/806]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 December 1576: Gift by King James VI, to John Lord Glammis Chancellor of Scotland his heirs and assignees one or more of the ward and nonentry duties of the lands, lordships, baronies, mills, woods, fishings, and others, whi
2 CONC ch pertained to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who last deceased or others his predecessors, of all years and terms that the same has been in the Kings hands by the decease of the Earl in December then instant, and of all years and ter
2 CONC ms to come during the said ward, and specially when it shall happen the said lands and others to fall in nonentry, through the decease of Dame Margaret Kennedy relict of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis grandfather of John now Earl of Ca
2 CONC ssillis and of Dame Margaret Lyon relict of the said Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who last deceased, together with the marriage of the said John now of Earl of Cassillis son and apparent heir of the said Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who
2 CONC  last deceased. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f849&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ken
2 CONC nedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/849]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/471/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 471]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n116/mode/1up The Book of Wallace: 41]
2 CONT # [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2430.htm#i24291 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography and Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2430.htm#i24291 Account in Darryl Lundy's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Kennedy was the daughter of Alexander Kennedy. She married # firstly, William Wallace before 1540 William Wallace was born before 1525. He died before 1540 He lived at Craigie, Angus, Scotland. # secondly, Gilbert Kenn
2 CONC edy, 3rd Earl of Cassillis, son of Gilbert Kennedy, 2nd Earl of Cassillis and Lady Isabel Campbell, in 1540. She died circa 1596. Her will was proven (by probate) on 12 January 1596/97 at Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. Her marri
2 CONC ed name became Wallace. After her marriage, Margaret Kennedy was styled as Countess of Cassillis in 1540. Children of Margaret Kennedy and Gilbert Kennedy, 3rd Earl of Cassillis:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Lady Janet Kennedy d. 1598'''
2 CONT # '''Katherine Kennedy'''
2 CONT # '''Gilbert Kennedy, 4th Earl of Cassillis b. c 1541, d. 14 Dec 1576'''
2 CONT # '''Sir Thomas Kennedy, Master of Cassillis b. bt 1543 - 1558, d. 11 May 1602'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations  1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom,
2 CONC  Extant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 75. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 2. [S6] Cokayne, and others,
2 CONC  The Complete Peerage, volume III, page 79.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n116/mode/1up Account in The Book of Wallace]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On the death of his uncle "the good laird's" only child and heiress, William, son of the tutor of Craigie, became owner of Craigie: he died in 1538.  His wife Margaret, only daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargeny, subsequentl
2 CONC y married Gilbert, third Earl of Cassilis.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kennedy-912
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/247928813/margaret-kennedy
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany and Mariot Dunbar of Mochrum
2 CONT
2 CONT DAME MARGARET KENNEDY Countess of Cassillis
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy is the daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany. Her date and place of birth are not known. The Scots Peerage II: 471
2 CONT
2 CONT Her Last Will and Testament
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy made her last will and testament at Maybole, probably at Cassillis Castle there, on 28 November 1580. She nominated her son Thomas Kennedy "tutor of Cassillis" to be her only executor and intromitter with "al
2 CONC l my guids & geir" and left a number of legacies. Confirmation was granted on 12 January 1597. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedie, relict of Gil
2 CONC bert, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]
2 CONT
2 CONT Image of Testament A
2 CONT Image of Testament B
2 CONT Image of Testament C
2 CONT Image of Testament D
2 CONT Date of Death
2 CONT An exact date of death cannot be identified for Dame Margaret Kennedy. She made her last will and testament on 28 November 1580 and probably died very soon thereafter. According to the opening paragraph of her testamentary record 
2 CONC she died in 1580, and it seems safe to suppose, therefore, that she must have died after 28 November but before 31 December in that year. [Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedie, 
2 CONC relict of Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]
2 CONT
2 CONT Place of Death
2 CONT An exact place of death cannot be identified for Dame Margaret Kennedy. However, she made her last will and testament at Maybole in the Carrick division of South Ayrshire, in Scotland, and it seems reasonable to suggest that she m
2 CONC ay have died at Cassillis Castle there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy was probably buried in the Collegiate Church of Maybole. This is certainly where she wished to be buried: "I dame mgaret kennedie countess of cassillis seik in body bot haill in mynd . . . . . In the first I 
2 CONC leif my saull to God Almytie my body to be bureit in the college kirk of Mayboill besyde my umqle sone erle of cassillis". [Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Dame Margaret Kennedie, relict of Gilbe
2 CONC rt, Earl of Cassillis, sheriffdom of Ayr, reference CC8/8/29]
2 CONT
2 CONT First Marriage
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy married, as her first husband, William Wallace of Craigie. The Scots Peerage III: 471 He died in 1538. The Book of Wallace: 44
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of First Marriage
2 CONT Margaret Wallace
2 CONT Sir John Wallace, of Craigie
2 CONT William Wallace
2 CONT Second Marriage
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy married, as her second husband, Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis. He died in 1558. The Scots Peerage II: 471
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Second Marriage
2 CONT Gilbert Kennedy, 4th Earl of Cassilis
2 CONT David Kennedy
2 CONT Sir Thomas Kennedy, 1st of Culzean
2 CONT Janet Kennedy, Countess of Orkney
2 CONT Catherine Kennedy
2 CONT Evidence from the National Records of Scotland
2 CONT 1
2 CONT 6 February 1540-41: Precept from Chancery for infefting the Earl and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his lady in conjunct fee and liferent in the 10 merk land of Balgray the two Auchintibbers, Fulwood Gabrachhill Brydi
2 CONC lands, Struther and Peacockbank, with the mill thereof, the lands of Spittal, 20 shilling land of Whitelees, lands of Over and Nether Bordlands extending to a 40 merk land all lying in the Lordship of Stewarton and bailiary of Cun
2 CONC ningham. National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/406 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, ch
2 CONC arter number 2270 on p. 518
2 CONT
2 CONT 2
2 CONT 28 August 1559: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his mother relict of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis his father, bearing that the Countess shall have the place of Cassillis with
2 CONC  the garden and orchard thereof for her residence during all the days of her life, and the Earl assigns to her yearly during her life, 110 bolls of meal, 52 bolls bear, 115 merks money, 89 capons, 36 salmon and the 3d. part of the
2 CONC  Meadow of Blairboy, and that in contentation of all terce and conjunct fee lands falling to her, or to which she can anywise claim by and throw the decease of her husband, lying in the Counties of Ayr and Wigton, and which meal, 
2 CONC bear, silver, capons and salmon, to be uplifted and payable from the Mains of Cassillis, 4 merk land of Giltreehill, 2 merk land of Pinmyrie, 2 merk land of Carsonston, and lands of Holehouse, 20 shilling land of Lindsayston, half
2 CONC  merk land of Dunurehill, Bernard thomsons merk land, 2 merk land of Milltoun of Cassillis, Archibald Hamiltons merk land, 20 shilling land of Drumboy, 20 shilling land of Barnshean, 20 shilling land of Over Craufurdston, 2 merk l
2 CONC and of Nether Craufurdston, 2 merk land of Middle Craufurdston, 2 merk land of Gunerston, half merk land of Makroriston, 10 shilling land of Burnmouth, Down-dunches half merk land, merk land of Garpin, 3 merk land of Burnford, 21 
2 CONC merk land of Balquhirn and Balmuck, and Charles Kennedys merk land all lying in the barony of Cassillis - for which causes, the Countess discharges the Earl her son and his successors, of all right and title which she had to the t
2 CONC erce and conjunct fee lands falling to her by and through the decease of her husband as aforesaid, and of all tacks steadings and possessions pertaining to her husband, by virtue of the Act made at his going to France, dated at Ed
2 CONC inburgh ......... 1557, and renounces her office of executrice, to the Earl her son, which office was conferred on her by her husband, with power to the Earl to use the same as fully and freely as she could have done in virtue of 
2 CONC her husbands Latter Will - and also makes and constitutes the Earl and his successors her bailies (with service of men hosts, and raids or armies) of her terce lands, with power to his Lordship and his aforesaid, by themselves or 
2 CONC their deputes, to hold courts, and do every thing concerning the office of bailiary, which she could have done by her deputes; and also the Earl grants permission to her, during all the days of her life, to take wood to the place 
2 CONC of Cassillis from the woods of Cassillis and Dalrymple. Witnesses - David Kennedy of Culean, James Kennedy of Ochterlour, John Kennedy of Skeldon, John Blair of Middle-Auchindrain, and Dean John Mure Sub-Prior of Crossragwell. Dat
2 CONC ed at Mayboll.This Contract ratified at Ayr 4th Novemb. 1559, by Quintin Abbot of Crossragwell, Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains, David Kennedy of Culean, and Mr Thomas Hay Parson of Spynie, four of the six curators of the Earl. Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/576
2 CONT
2 CONT 3
2 CONT 29 August 1559: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis his mother, by which for the love and favor he bears to her, and for decorating her house, he gives her during all the days
2 CONC  of her life, the yearly rent of the 2 and a half merk land of Craigmulloch, lying in the Earldom of Carrick as possessed by John Makquhilie herd, together with 101 milk ewes, 77 yeild ewes, 108 wedders, 40 gimmers, and 40 dinment
2 CONC s, as also other 80 gimmers and dinments all to be received by her, from the said John Makquhilie, at the feast of Beltran then next 1560, together with 11 old goats and 2 kids - as also he gives to the Countess his mother 104 hea
2 CONC d of nolt pasturing upon the lands of Kericastle in the forest of Buchan viz. 16 nicol cows and as many calves, 17 ferow and 9 yeild cows, 5 three year old cows, 22 old oxen, 2 bulls, 6 three year old oxen and 2 bulls, 5 two year 
2 CONC old oxen, 3 two year old queys, 8 quey stirks and 9 oxen stirks, which sheep, goats, and cattle, the Countess obliges herself her heirs, and executors, to leave on the ground of the lands respectively above mentioned at her deceas
2 CONC e, or the like number, and of as great avail, for the use of the Earl and his successors - and also he gives to the Countess during all the days of her life, a silver basin and a laver, a double gilt cup of silver raised work, wit
2 CONC h a cover, 2 cases of silver, the one gilt, and the other ungilt, a gilt macer, 2 silver trenchers (plates) with 2 little salt-fats in their nooks (corners), 12 silver spoons, a silver salt-fat, and cover thereof, ungilt, a black 
2 CONC velvet bed, with the curtains of black damask, and 4 pieces of tapestry in Edinburgh, and 4 feather beds and their bolsters - all which silver work, tapestry, and beding, the Countess obliges her and hers aforesaid, to leave to th
2 CONC e Earl and his successors, within the place of Cassillis at her decease, or as much, and of the same avail - and also for certain good causes, she assigns the Earl her son in and to all moveable goods which may belong to her at th
2 CONC e time of her decease, and the Earl being under age, he obliges himself to chuse curators between and Martinmas then next, and cause them ratify the Contract. Witnesses - David Kennedy of Culean, James Kennedy of Ochterlour, John 
2 CONC Kennedy of Skeldon and John Blair of Middle-Auchindrain. Dated at Mayboll. The Contract ratified at Ayr 5th Novemb. 1559, by Quintin Abbot of Crossragwell Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains David Kennedy of Culean, and Mr Thomas Hay 
2 CONC parson of Spynie the Earls curators. National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/577
2 CONT
2 CONT 4
2 CONT November 1573: Contract between Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and Hugh Earl of Eglinton, proceeding upon a narrative of the Earl of Cassillis having annalied under reversion to Robert Graham of Knockdolian, the greater half of the bar
2 CONC ony of Stewarton, to be holden feu of the Earl for payment yearly of £120, and also the lesser half of the said barony, to be holden blanch of the Earl, together with the barony of Dunure in warrandice of the said barony of Stewar
2 CONC ton, from the liferent of Dame Margaret Kennedy Countess of Cassillis Mother of the Earl and had discharged the said Robert Graham of the feu mails of the barony of Stewarton during the not redemption, as six several Letters of Re
2 CONC version granted by the said Robert Grahan containing 1000 merks each, did bear, and that the said Robert Graham had annalied to the Earl of Eglinton, the said baronies of Stewarton and Dunure to be holden of the Earl of Cassillis 
2 CONC as said is, and had constitute the Earl of Eglinton and Dame Agnes Drummond his wife and their heirs his cessioners and assignees in and to the original Contract of Sale between the Earl of Cassillis and him, and Infeftment follow
2 CONC ing thereupon, And subsuming that the Earl of Eglinton had paid to the said Robert Graham a greater sum than the 6000 merks contained in the Contract and Letters of Reversion above mentioned viz. 1100 merks, which computed along w
2 CONC ith the annualrent thereof extends to 1485 merks, so that the yearly rent which the Earl of Eglinton shall receive from the barony of Stewarton at the expiry of 3 years and a half from the date of the Contract extends to 748 merks
2 CONC , 6 shillings, 8 pence, and therefore he shall possess the said barony and uplift the rents thereof during the not redemption, by seven several Letters of Reversion, the first six to contain 1000 merks each, every 1000 merks redee
2 CONC ming 100 merks of rent, and the last to contain 1485 merks, and shall ratify the first six Letters of Reversion granted by the said Robert Graham as said is, or renew the same conform to the Original Contract, and shall grant a se
2 CONC venth Letter of Reversion as said is, containing 1485 merks upon redemption of the said sum of 748 merks 6 shillings 8 pence to be paid in the Church of Ayr, and at the expiry of the said 3 and a half years, the Earl of Cassillis 
2 CONC to receive the said barony of Stewarton from the Earl of Eglinton and his wife for payment yearly of 748 merks 6 shillings 8 pence and find caution for payment thereof, according as the Earl of Eglinton shall desire. Witnesses - T
2 CONC homas Master of Cassillis, William Stewart of Dunduff, Andw. Nevin of Monkridding, and William Highgate burgess of Glasgow. Dated at Glasgow, and Irvin, 9th and 10th Novemb. 1573. National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kenned
2 CONC y Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/806
2 CONT
2 CONT 5
2 CONT 20 December 1576: Gift by King James VI, to John Lord Glammis Chancellor of Scotland his heirs and assignees one or more of the ward and nonentry duties of the lands, lordships, baronies, mills, woods, fishings, and others, which 
2 CONC pertained to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who last deceased or others his predecessors, of all years and terms that the same has been in the Kings hands by the decease of the Earl in December then instant, and of all years and terms 
2 CONC to come during the said ward, and especially when it shall happen the said lands and others to fall in nonentry, through the decease of Dame Margaret Kennedy relict of Gilbert Earl of Cassillis grandfather of John now Earl of Cass
2 CONC illis and of Dame Margaret Lyon relict of the said Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who last deceased, together with the marriage of the said John now of Earl of Cassillis son and apparent heir of the said Gilbert Earl of Cassillis who l
2 CONC ast deceased. National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/849
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy
2 CONT The Scots Peerage II: 471
2 CONT The Book of Wallace: 41
2 CONT Darryl Lundy's Peerage
2 CONT Biography and Genealogy
2 CONT 1
2 CONT Account in Darryl Lundy's Peerage
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Kennedy was the daughter of Alexander Kennedy. She married # firstly, William Wallace before 1540 William Wallace was born before 1525. He died before 1540 He lived at Craigie, Angus, Scotland. # Secondly, Gilbert Kennedy
2 CONC , 3rd Earl of Cassillis, son of Gilbert Kennedy, 2nd Earl of Cassillis and Lady Isabel Campbell, in 1540. She died circa 1596. Her will was proven (by probate) on 12 January 1596/97 at Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland. Her married 
2 CONC name became Wallace. After her marriage, Margaret Kennedy was styled as Countess of Cassillis in 1540. Children of Margaret Kennedy and Gilbert Kennedy, 3rd Earl of Cassillis:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Janet Kennedy d. 1598
2 CONT Katherine Kennedy
2 CONT Gilbert Kennedy, 4th Earl of Cassillis b. c 1541, d. 14 Dec 1576
2 CONT Sir Thomas Kennedy, Master of Cassillis b. bt 1543 - 1558, d. 11 May 1602
2 CONT Citations 1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Ext
2 CONC ant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 75. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 2. [S6] Cokayne, and others, The
2 CONC  Complete Peerage, volume III, page 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2
2 CONT Account in The Book of Wallace
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of his uncle "the good laird's" only child and heiress, William, son of the tutor of Craigie, became owner of Craigie: he died in 1538. His wife Margaret, only daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargeny, subsequently ma
2 CONC rried Gilbert, third Earl of Cassilis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dame Margaret Kennedy, Countess of Cassillis
2 CONT Birthdate: 1514
2 CONT Death: between November 28, 1580 and December 31, 1580 (65-66)
2 CONT probably at Cassillis Castle near Maybole, in the Carrick division of Ayrshire, Scotland (United Kingdom)
2 CONT Place of Burial: beside her son Gilbert, Earl of Cassillis
2 CONT Immediate Family:
2 CONT Daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany and Mariot Dunbar of Mochrum
2 CONT Wife of Sir William Wallace of Craigie, 12th of Craigie and Gilbert Kennedy, 3rd Earl of Cassilis
2 CONT Mother of Sir John Wallace, of Craigie; William Wallace; Sir Robert Wallace; Janet Kennedy, Countess of Orkney; Gilbert Kennedy, 4th Earl of Cassilis and 4 others
2 CONT Sister of Thomas Kennedy of Bargany
2 CONT Half-sister of Sir Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains, Knight
