1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ELIZABETH KENNEDY===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 October 1538: Charter by John Kennedy of Culean to Elizabeth Kennedy daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany, by which for a certain sum of money paid by the said Alex. Kennedy in name of his daughter, the said John Kennedy
2 CONC  dispones to her, her heirs and assignees, the 20 pound land of Culean, lying in the Earldom of Carrick - to be holden of the King and his successors, Princes and Stewarts of Scotland, for services used and wont. Witnesses - Adam 
2 CONC Boyd in Pinkil, William Kennedy brother of the Laird of Craigneil, Constantine Tait, James Park and Thomas Boyd. Dated at Bargany. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f351&st=1&t
2 CONC c=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/351]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 October 1538: Precept by the said John Kennedy of Culean for infefting Elizabeth Kennedy in the 20 pound land of Culean in consequence of the foregoing Charter. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.
2 CONC aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f352&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/352]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 November 1538: Charter by King James V, ratifying verbatim the Charter by John Kennedy of Culean (GD25/1/351) to Elizabeth Kennedy. Witnesses - Gavin Bishop of Glasgow Chancellor, Henry Bishop of Galloway, Archibald Earl of A
2 CONC rgyll Master of the Household, Malcom Lord Fleming Chamberlain, Sir Thomas Erskine of Brechin Knight Secretary, James Kirkcaldy of Grange Treasurer, Mr James Foulis of Colinton Keeper of the Rolls, and Mr Thomas Bellenden Director
2 CONC  of the Chancery. Dated at Falkland. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f353&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotl
2 CONC and, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/353]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 December 1538: Instrument of Seisin in favor of Elizabeth Kennedy daughter of Alexander Kennedy of Bargany, in the lands of Culean proceeding on Precept No. 352. Witnesses - Alexander Kennedy of Bargany, Thomas Davidson of Gr
2 CONC eenan, Adam Boyd in Pinkil, Sir Patrick Amurth Chaplain, Thomas Boyd and Constantin Tait. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f358&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+kennedy&ko
2 CONC =p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/358]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1541: Procuratory by Elizabeth Kennedy See GD25/1/351, GD25/1/352, et GD25/1/353 with consent of Hugh Kennedy her husband, to Oliver Sinclair and David Kennedy, to resign in the hands of King James V, the 20 pound la
2 CONC nd of Culean with the mill of Culean, for infeftment thereof to be granted by the King to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and his heirs. Witnesses - John and George Kennedys, Andrew Davidson and Andrew Philipson. Dated at Inch. The proc
2 CONC uratory bears that the Earl had paid Elizabeth Kennedy and her husband a certain sum of money. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f417&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy&ko
2 CONC =p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/417]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 February 1541: Instrument of Resignation by Oliver Sinclair as procurator for Elizabeth Kennedy and Hugh Kennedy her husband, in the hands of King James V, of the 20 pound land of Culean and mill of Culean, for infeftment th
2 CONC ereof to be granted by the King to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and his heirs. Witnesses - Robert Master of Erskine and John Ross of Craigy. Dated at Palace of Falkland. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.
2 CONC aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f418&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/418]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 February 1541: Charter by King James V, to Gilbert Earl of Cassillis and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Thomas, David, Quintin, Archibald and Hugh Kennedys brothers german of the Earl and the heirs male of their b
2 CONC odies respectively whom failling James Kennedy uncle of the Earl and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Thomas Kennedy of Goif, and the heirs male of his body, whom failling Hugh Kennedy of Girvanmains and the heirs male of
2 CONC  his body, whom all failling the nearest heirs male whatsoever of the Earl, bearing the name and arms of Kennedy - of the 20 pound land of Culean and mill of Culean - proceeding on the resignation of Elizabeth Kennedy and Hugh Ken
2 CONC nedy her husband and which lands were formerly alienated to the said Elizabeth Kennedy by John Kennedy of Culean and are thereby erected into a free barony to be called the barony of Culean, - to be holden of the King and his succ
2 CONC essors, Princes and Stewarts of Scotland and Earls of Carrick for services used and wont. Witnesses - Gavin Archbishop of Glasgow Chancellor, Malcom Lord Fleming Chamberlain, Sir Thomas Erskine of Brechin Knight Secretary, James K
2 CONC irkaldy of Grange Treasurer, David Wood of Craig Comptroller, Mr James Foulis of Colinton, clerk register and Thomas Bellenden of Auchnoul director of the Chancery. Dated at Falkland. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinec
2 CONC atalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f419&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n 
2 CONT [National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference 
2 CONT GD25/1/419]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It appears from Charter 6th Feb. 1540, (GD25/1/403) that the Earl had then six brothers in life - namely Thomas, David, Quintin, Archibald, Hugh, & James - in the Charter immediately above mentioned James's name is left o
2 CONC ut hence it is probable he had died without male issue before Feb. 1541.'''
