2 CONT *'''The thanage of Fermartyn including the district commonly called Formartine : its proprietors, with genealogical deductions; its parishes, ministers, churches, churchyards, antiquities &c. (1894)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/thanageoffermart00byutemp
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/309/mode/1up
2 CONT *   III. John Gordon of Auchleuchry. 
2 CONT *   He obtained a portion of the Gordon territory by receiving the lands of Botarie from the Earl of Huntly ; had seisin of the lands of Kindrocht in 1487   In 1493, he purchased the lands of Longweir (Lungair or Lungar) and Hilto
2 CONC n in the county of Kincardine, forming the southern half of the barony of Dunnottar, and in the same year those of Cromy, Little Warthill, with the part of Harlaw and the Glack. In this deed he is designated John Gordon of Auchleu
2 CONC chry.  In 1506, he got a charter from Sir Alexander Seton of the lands of Kinmundy, Mylhill, Myllbrecks, and Petremarcus, and in the same year, he purchased the lands of Kyninmonde in Lonmay.  John Gordon married Barbara, daughter
2 CONC  of Alexander Forbes of Pitsligo, by his wife, Dame ___Hay, daughter of William, first Earl of Errol, by whom he had a son,
2 CONT **	I. John, his successor. 
2 CONT **	II. Francis. 
2 CONT *John Gordon died 1506, and was succeeded by his son, 
2 CONT *'''   IV. John Gordon of Auchleuchry, Lungar, Kinmundie, &c. 
2 CONT *'''   In 1506, there is a deed of sasine in favour of John Gordon, son and heir of the late John Gordon of Lungar, on charter of William Gordon of Schivas, of the lands of Petnagoak, in the county of Aberdeen and barony of Schiva
2 CONC s, dated 24 November, 1506.  In 1531, there is a charter by King James V. confirming a charter of sale by Francis Gordon, portioner, Kindrocht and Sathlee to his brother, John Gordon of Lumgair, and eight years later, he got a feu
2 CONC  charter from the Bishop of Moray, to him and the lawful heirs male of his body, of the lands of Pitlurge, Ovir Auchquhorties, Nether Auchquhorties, in the barony of Keith. These lands adjoined to Botarie. He made an excambion in 
2 CONC 1541, with Sir Thomas Erskine of Brechin, receiving the lands of 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/310/mode/1up
2 CONT *'''Crevethin in Drumblade in exchange for Hilton, the harbour and fishings of the same; and in the same year also received a charter from John Forsyth de Dykis of the lands of Gilkenston. 
2 CONT *'''   He married Lady Jane Stuart, daughter of the first Earl of Athole of that family, by his second wife. Lady Eleanor St. Clair, daughter of William, Earl of Orkney and Caithness. The Earl of Athole was half-brother to King Ja
2 CONC mes II., being son of Queen Joan Beaufort, by her second husband. Sir James Stuart, the black knight of Lorne. Lady Jean predeceased her husband, having borne him two sons : — 
2 CONT **	I. John, his successor. 
2 CONT **	II. James, who received a grant of Auchleuchries from his brother in 1546. 
2 CONT **	I. A daughter, who married ___ Turing of Foveran. 
2 CONT *'''   John Gordon married secondly''', Margaret Drummond, of the family of Stobhall, without issue (she married after her husband's death George Baird of Auchmedden). 
2 CONT *'''   He died in 1546, and was succeeded by his eldest son,  .... etc. __________________________
2 CONT *Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl Atholl, Ambassador to England1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9
2 CONT *M, #2944, b. circa 1440, d. 15 September 1512
2 CONT *Father      Sir James Stewart, Black Knight of Lorn10,11 d. a 17 Aug 1451
2 CONT *Mother     Joan Beaufort10,11 b. 1398, d. 15 Jul 1445
2 CONT *     Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl Atholl, Ambassador to England was born circa 1440 at of Balveny, Fifeshire, Scotland.5,12 He married Margaret 'Fair Maid of Galloway' Douglas, daughter of Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl Douglas, Earl 
2 CONC of Wigtown, Duke of Touraine, Comte de Longueville and Euphemia Graham, between July 1459 and 25 March 1460; They had 3 daughters (Jean, wife of Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl Huntly; Elizabeth, wife of Andrew, 2nd Lord Gray; & Christ
2 CONC ian, wife of Neil Stewart of Forthergill & Garth).2,4,5,6,9,12 Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl Atholl, Ambassador to England married Eleanor Sinclair, daughter of Sir William Sinclair, 3rd Earl of Orkney, 1st Earl Caithness, Lord Sincl
2 CONC air and Marjory (Mary) Sutherland, before 19 April 1475; They had 2 sons (John, 2nd Earl of Atholl, Lord of Balveny; & Andrew, Bishop of Caithness, Bishop-elect of Dunkeld) and 9 daughters (Katherine, wife of John, 6th Lord Forbes
2 CONC ; Isabel, wife of John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox; Margaret, wife of William Murray of Castletown; '''Jean, wife of Sir Robert Gordon of Pitlurg'''; Elizabeth, wife of Alexander Robertson of Strowan; Margaret, wife of Robert Robe
2 CONC rtson, younger of Strowan; Marjory, wife of Sir Colin Campbell of Glenorchy; Elspeth, wife of Robert Innes of Innermarkie; & Jean (Janet), wife of James Arbuthnott).5,12 Sir John Stewart, 1st Earl Atholl, Ambassador to England die
2 CONC d on 15 September 1512 at Laighwood, Perthshire, Scotland; Buried at Dunkeld Cathedral, Perthshire.5,12
