2 CONT *3.         JAMES Stewart (-[1448]).  The Black Knight of Lorn.  m (1439) as her second husband, JOAN Beaufort, widow of JAMES I King of Scotland, daughter of JOHN Beaufort Earl of Somerset & his wife Margaret de Holand (-Dunbar C
2 CONC astle 15 Jul 1445, bur Monastery of the Charterhouse, Perth).  James & his wife had three children:  
2 CONT **a)         JOHN Stewart of Balveny ([1440]-the Laighwood 15 Sep 1512, bur Dunkeld Cathedral).  Earl of Atholl 1457.  
2 CONT **-        EARLS of ATHOLL.  
2 CONT **b)         JAMES Stewart (-[Jan 1497/Jan 1500]).  Earl of Buchan 1469.  
2 CONT **-        EARLS of BUCHAN.  
2 CONT **c)         ANDREW Stewart (1443-1501).  Bishop of Moray 1483. 
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#JohnBalveny1Atholldied1512
2 CONT * JOHN Stewart, son of JAMES Stewart, the Black Knight of Lorn & his wife Joan Beaufort ([1440]-the Laighwood 15 Sep 1512, bur Dunkeld Cathedral).  Earl of Atholl 1457.  
2 CONT *m firstly ([1459/60]) as her third husband, MARGARET Douglas "the Fair Maid of Galloway", widow of WILLIAM Douglas Earl of Douglas and divorced wife (secondly) of JAMES Douglas Earl of Douglas, daughter of ARCHIBALD Douglas Earl 
2 CONC of Douglas & his second wife Eupheme Graham of Strathearn (-[21 Jan 1473/early 1475]).  
2 CONT *m secondly (before 19 Apr 1475) ELEANOR Sinclair, daughter of WILLIAM Sinclair Earl of Caithness & his second wife Marjory Sutherland of Dunbeath (-21 Mar 1518, bur Dunkeld Cathedral).  
2 CONT *Earl John & his first wife had six children:
2 CONT **1.         JANET (-Strathbogie 27 Oct 1510).  m (contract 14 Oct 1474) as his first wife, ALEXANDER Gordon Master of Huntly, son of GEORGE Gordon Earl of Huntly & his first wife Elizabeth Douglas Dowager Ctss of Moray née Dunbar
2 CONC  of the Earls of Moray (-Perth 21 Jan 1524, bur Perth Dominican Friars).  He succeeded his father in 1501 as Earl of Huntly.  
2 CONT **2.         CATHERINE .  m as his first wife, JOHN Forbes, son of WILLIAM Forbes Lord Forbes & his wife Christian Gordon of the Earls of Huntly (-1547).
2 CONT **3.         three daughters .  
2 CONT **4.         ELIZABETH .  m (before 1483) as his second wife, ANDREW Gray Lord Gray, son of PATRICK Gray Master of Gray & his second wife Annabel Forbes (-Feb 1514). 
2 CONT *Earl John & his second wife had eleven children:
2 CONT **5.         JOHN (-1521).  Earl of Atholl.    
2 CONT **-        see below.  
2 CONT **6.         ANDREW (-1542).  Bishop of Caithness 1518. 
2 CONT **'''7.         JEAN .  m as his first wife, ROBERT Gordon of Pitlurgo, son of ---. 
2 CONT **8.         ELSPETH .  m ([1510]) ROBERT Innes of Innermarky, son of ---. 
2 CONT **9.         MARJORY (-1524).  m COLIN Campbell of Glenurchy, son of --- (-1523). 
2 CONT **10.      MARGARET .  m WILLIAM Murray of Tullibardine, son of --- (-killed in battle 1513). 
2 CONT **11.      ISABEL .  m as his second wife, ALEXANDER Robertson of Struan, son of ---.  
2 CONT **12.      ELISABETH .  m firstly JOHN Stuart Earl of Lennox, son of MATTHEW Stuart Earl of Lennox & his second wife Elizabeth Hamilton (-1526).  m secondly (1529) as his second wife, NINIAN Lord Ross, son of --- (-1556). 
2 CONT **13.      CHRISTIAN (-1538).  m as his first wife, NEIL Stuart of Garth, son of --- (-1554). 
2 CONT **14.      MARGARET [Isabel].  m ROBERT Robertson of Struan, son of ---.  
2 CONT *From: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTTISH%20NOBILITY.htm#JohnBalveny1Atholldied1512B ___________________________
2 CONT *'''The Scots peerage; founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom (1904)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01paul
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft#page/465/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.441
2 CONT *   I. Sir John Stewart of Balvany, first Earl of Atholl of this line, born about 1440, styled 'frater carnalis' of King James II. He was created EARL OF ATHOLL in or before 1457, and is so designed in a truce with the English tha
2 CONC t year. Styled Earl of Atholl in a charter under the Great Seal, 25 March 1460, of the lordship of Balvany. Another charter was granted to him by King James III., on account of near kinship and affection, of the earldom of Atholl 
2 CONC and the lands with remainder to the heirs-male of his body, whom failing to the King, with the reddendo of a red rose to be delivered at Blair, 18 March 1481-82. He was sent in the expedition against John, Lord of the Isles, in 14
2 CONC 75, and being victorious, adopted the motto 'Furth fortune and fill the fetters.' In 1484 he was one of the conservators of the peace with England, and in 1488 commanded in the army of James III. On that King's death the Earl was 
2 CONC imprisoned by King James IV., but was liberated before 1489, when he attended Parliament in Edinburgh. He died at the Laighwood, 15 September 1512, and was buried in Dunkeld Cathedral. He married, first, Margaret Douglas, the Fair
2 CONC  Maid of Galloway, only daughter and ultimate heiress of Archibald, fifth Earl of Douglas, Duke of Touraine. She married, first, in 1444, William, eighth Earl of Douglas, and on his death his brother James, ninth Earl. After the l
2 CONC atter's rebellion in 1455 she remained with him in England for a time, but about 1459 she is said to have repaired to 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft#page/466/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.442
2 CONT *King James II. entreating mercy, saying that she was forced to these ungodly nuptials against her will. The marriage being dissolved she was married to Atholl, as her third husband, before March 1460. He married, secondly, before
2 CONC  19 April 1475, Eleanor Sinclair, stated to be a daughter of William (Sinclair), Earl of Orkney and Caithness. He had issue by both wives : — 
2 CONT **	1. John, second Earl. 
2 CONT **	2. Andrew,  Bishop-elect of Dunkeld in 1515, but he never obtained possession of the see. He was made Bishop of Caithness in 1518, and died 1542. 
2 CONT **	3. Jean, married, before 1482, to Alexander, third Earl of Huntly.
2 CONT **	4. Katherine, married to John, sixth Lord Forbes.*
2 CONT **	5. Elisabeth, married, contract dated 19 January 1511-12, to John, third Earl of Lennox, by dispensation dated 29 January 1511-12, as they were related in the second and fourth degrees of consanguinity. 
2 CONT **	6. Christian, married to Neil Stewart of Garth, died 30 May 1538 and was buried in the Cathechal of Dunkeld. 
2 CONT **	7. Margaret, said to have been married to William Murray of Tullibardine, but more probably to his son, William Murray of Castletown, killed at Flodden 9 September 1513. {See Murray, Duke of Atholl.) 
2 CONT **	8. Elizabeth, married to Andrew, Lord Gray. {See that title.) 
2 CONT **'''	9. Jean, said to be married to Sir Robert Gordon of Pitlurg. 
2 CONT **	10. Elizabeth, married to Alexander Robertson of Strowan.
2 CONT **	11. Margaret, married to Robert Robertson, younger of Strowan. 
2 CONT **	12. Marjory, married to Sir Colin Campbell of Glenorchy, and died 26 July 1524. 
2 CONT **	13. Elspeth, married to Robert Innes of Innermarky.
2 CONT *___________________________________
