2 CONT
2 CONT =Balvenie Castle=
2 CONT
2 CONT From: [http://www.historic-scotland.gov.uk/index/places/propertyresults/propertyabout.htm?PropID=PL_027&PropName=Balvenie%20Castle Historic Scotland]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==One castle and three dynasties==
2 CONT
2 CONT For over 500 years, Balvenie Castle served as the formidable stronghold of the great lords who ruled over this part of north-east Scotland. The immensely powerful ‘Black’ Comyn earls of Buchan built it in the 13th century. When th
2 CONC ey were forfeited in the early 14th century, because of their alliance with the ill-fated John Balliol, the stronghold passed to the mighty ‘Black’ Douglases. And when the Douglases too were wiped out around 1455 by James II, the 
2 CONC victorious Stewart king entrusted it to a kinsman, John Stewart, Earl of Atholl. It remained with his descendants for the next 250 years. Today’s visitor will find important, and impressive, remains dating from all three dynastic 
2 CONC families.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==The castle of the Stewarts==
2 CONT
2 CONT James II granted Balvenie to his trusted kinsman, John Stewart, Earl of Atholl, and his lady, Margaret. Margaret had previously been the widow of the 8th Earl of Douglas and the divorced wife of the 9th Earl! The Stewarts held Bal
2 CONC venie for the next 250 years, in return for the princely sum of one red rose. During that time the Stewarts transformed the formidable medieval stronghold into a pleasing Renaissance residence. The noble Atholl Lodging at the SE c
2 CONC orner, to the right of the main entrance, was built by the 4th Earl of Atholl during Mary Queen of Scots’ reign in the mid-16th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stewart and Eleanor Sinclair had two sons and nine daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Atholl, living 1520, and died before 1522, who married Janet Campbell (died about Candlemas 1545/6), daughter of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Arygll.
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, Bishop of Caithness.
2 CONT # Jean (or Janet) Stewart, married by contract dated 31 August 1507, James Arbuthnott of Arbuthnott. He had a crown charter of the feudal barony of Arbuthnott 29 January 1507. He left a testament dated 7 March 1521, and died befor
2 CONC e 13 March 1521.
2 CONT # .Katherine Stewart, married Sir John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes.
2 CONT # Elizabeth/Elspeth Stewart, married Sir Robert Innes 2nd of Innermarky.
2 CONT # Marjory Stewart, married Sir Colin Campbell, of Glenorchy.
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart, married Sir William Murray, of Castleton who was killed at Battle of Flodden Duke of Atholl
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stewart, married Alexander Robertson, of Strowan.
2 CONT # Elizabeth (or Isabel) Stewart, married John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Lennox
2 CONT # Jean Stewart, married Robert Gordon, Knt., of Pitlurg.
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart, married Robert Robertson younger, of Strowan.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Stewart,_1st_Earl_of_Atholl]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
