1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR ALEXANDER BRUCE OF BIRGHAM AND EARLSHALL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce/6000000198682901835
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It is possible that Sir Alexander Bruce of Birgham and Earlshall, here treated, is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce/6000000198682901835 both of whom are know to have been sons of https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Stenhouse/6000000199019918833?through=6000000198682901835 but, presently, proof his wanting'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Bruce of Birgham and Earlshall, here treated, is the uncle of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce-of-Stenhouse/6000000198982307909 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/342/mode/1up RMS 142
2 CONC 4-1513: charter number 1628] who was the grandson and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Stenhouse/6000000199019918833  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f21&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1451&dt=1500&di=n NRS: GD11/21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Alexander Bruce of Birgham and Earlshall, here treated, is the brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Edward-Bruce/6000000198983612849?through=6000000198983916826 and https://www.geni.com/people/Luca-Bruce/60000001990196098
2 CONC 86?through=6000000198983916826 and https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Bruce/6000000199020031868?through=6000000198983916826 all three of whom are named as his heirs in remainder on 1 July 1495. [https://archive.org/details/registr
2 CONC ummagnisi02scot/page/478/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2258]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 February 1485-86: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James III, King of Scots, confirms that he has given 32 liberates of the land of Byrgehame, called Mekil Byrgehame, in the sheriffdom of Berwick, to Alexande
2 CONC r Bruse. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/345/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 1638]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 October 1485: Charter by which Robert Broys de Stanehouse confirms that he has made provision for priest to serve in his parish church of Erth, which had been constructed by the deceased Alex. Broys, his grandfather (avum su
2 CONC um).The charter was witnessed by his uncles (avunculis), viz. Alex. Brois, Luca Brois, Edwardo Brois and Robert Brois. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/342/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 1628]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 July 1495: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands and barony of Luchris-Monyponny in the sheriffdom of Perth to Alexander Brois of Brigheamo, The  baron
2 CONC y is to be held by Alexander Brois of Brigheamo and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother german Edward Bruce and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his nephew (filio fratris) Robert Brois of Stanehous, whom faili
2 CONC ng by his nephew  Luca Brois, brother's son of Alexander Brois of Brigheamo, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by Robert Brois, brother german of Luca Brois, whom failing by the nearest lawful heirs of Alexander Brois of Bri
2 CONC gheamo. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/478/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2258]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1497: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James IV, King of Scots, confirms possession of certain lands to Sir Alexander Bruse of Birgeame and his wife Jonete Stewarte, The lands in question were the land
2 CONC s of Erlishall, and the lands of the Prusk, both in the barony of Luchris and sheriffdom of Fife, and the lands of Maw in the sheriffdom of Fife. Sir Alexander Bruse of Birgeame had previously resigned these lands to the King in o
2 CONC rder to obtain a new grant in favour of him and his wife. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/499/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2346]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 June 1502: REX dedit literam ALEXANDEO BEUSE de Birgeame militi, sub magno sigillo, — super 40 libris in feodo, pro servitio regi impendendo, pro tempore ejus vite, de thecis regis per thesaurarium annuatim persolvendis, — i
2 CONC ntroitu incipiente ad festum S. Martini proximo sequens. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/563/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2653]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 November 1504: REX concessit WILLELMO BRUCE, filio et heredi quondam Alex. Bruce de Erlisball militis, et heredibus ejus,— cum consensu Jonete Stewart sponse dicti Alex., — terras de Drumlotho, vic. Fyfe ; — quas Alex. Lambe
2 CONC  civis S. Andree resignavit in favorem dictorum Alex. Bruce et Jonete Stewart 2 Mar. 1504 —et ante confectionem infeofamenti dictus Alex. Bruce diem clausit extremum. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/614/mo
2 CONC de/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2889]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 October 1506: Judgement made by James IV, King of Scots, in favour of the deceased Sir Alexander Bruce of Erlishaw, in the action raised by him for 400 merks that he was owed by George Lord Seton. The executors of Sir Alexan
2 CONC der Bruce of Erlishaw were the beneficiares, viz. Jonetam Stewart, his widow, and his daughters, Agnetem Brus, Elenam Bruse, Jonetam Bruse, and Margarete Bruse. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/637/mode/1up
2 CONC  RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2995]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 October 1506: A letter made to JONET STEWART, spouse of the deceased Sir Alexander Bruce of Earlshall, and Edward Bruce of Kynnard, of the gift of the ward etc. of the deceased Sir Alexander Bruce of Earlshall, and the marri
2 CONC age of his heir, William Bruce, and, in the event that he dies without having married, the marriage of any other heirs. [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/192/mode/1up RSS 1488-1529: number 1347]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1517: Ane Lettre maid with consent of the govemour to JONET STEWART the relict of umquhile Alexander Bruce of Erlishall, knycht, and to hir assignais, ane or maa, — of the gift of the warde of all landis and heretage quh
2 CONC ilkis pertenit to umquhile Michell Balfour of Monquhanny . . . . . [https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/455/mode/1up RSS 1488-1529: 2914]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General 
2 CONC Register House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrumsecret00scotgoog/page/n9/mode/1up Registrum Secreti Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The register of the Privy seal of Scotland. Vol I. A. D. 1488-1529. Edited by M. Livingstone, ISO., Late Deputy
2 CONC -Keeper of the Records of Scotland (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1908), 824 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n6/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth and their Cadets. By Major William Bruce Armstrong. (Printed for Private Circulation by T. & A. Constable,, Edinburgh, MDCCCXCII), 137 p
2 CONC p. plus drop-line pedigrees and Appendices]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bruce10.php Stirnet: Bruce 10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n29/mode/1up?q=janet+livingston&view=theater The Bruces of Airth and their cadets by Armstrong, William Bruce p 14-6]
2 CONT Alexander Bruce of the Stanehous and of Airth had numerous charters from the Abbots of Holyrood and from James ii. and iii. and others, from 1451 to 1468; the charter of James ii. to him and his wife Janet, was confirmed to his gr
2 CONC andson in 1489. Alexander died ante 1487. He is said to have married,' first, Jonet, daughter of the first Lord Livingston, by whom he had no issue ; that her name was Jonet, there is no question, but that she was a daughter of Lo
2 CONC rd Livingston's there is no proof except a memorandum  amongst the Blair Writs. He is also stated, on the authority of the same memorandum, to have married, secondly, Margaret, daughter of Sir Malcolm Forester of Torwoodhead, and 
2 CONC by her to have had issue six sons, viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. John, died during his father's lifetime.
2 CONT
2 CONT >2. '''Sir Alexander of Brigham and Earlshall.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >3. Edward of Kinnaird.
2 CONT
2 CONT >4. Lucas of Cultmalundie, who married Katherine Barbour,co-heiress of Cultmalundie ; they had one son,
2 CONT >>Henry Bruce of Cultmalundie, who was killed ' at the siege of Bray in France, 1510, when this family ended.
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. Robert of Auchenbowie and Bynning.
2 CONT
2 CONT >6. David, incorrectly called " of Kinnaird."
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n42/mode/1up?q=janet+livingston&view=theater
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == ALEXANDER BRUCE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''It is possible that Alexander Bruce, here treated, is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Birgham-and-Earlshall/6000000198983916826 both of whom are know to have been sons of https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Stenhouse/6000000199019918833?through=6000000198682901835 but, presently, proof his wanting'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Bruce, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-of-Stenhouse/6000000199019918833?through=6000000198682901835 The name of his mother is not known. [https://archive.org/details/calendarofl
2 CONC aingc00edin/page/37/mode/1up Laing Charters: charter number 143]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Laing Charters ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 December 1458: Charter by Malcolm of Kinbuk of that Ilk granting to Alexander Broyse [Bruce], son of Alexander Broyse of Stanehouse, the whole lands of Kinbuk, in the earldom of Strathern and shire of Perth, for the marriage 
2 CONC contracted and solemnised between the younger Alexander Bruce and Marjorie, daughter of the granter : To be held to them and their lawful heirs of the preceptor of Torphichen of the order of St. John of Jerusalem, in fee and herit
2 CONC age, rendering to the superior 20s. yearly. And if Alexander and Marjorie die without lawful heirs, the lands shall remain with Alexander and his heirs whomsoever, until the granter and his heirs repay to them, within the parish c
2 CONC hurch of Stirling, the sum of £173, 6s. 8d. Scots, which the elder Bruce paid to the said Malcolm for the contract of marriage. And if the lawful heirs of Alexander and Marjorie die without issue, the lands shall, upon payment of 
2 CONC said sum, revert to the granter, his heirs, or assignees. Dated at Dunblane, 1st December 1458, before William, James, John, and Maurice Drummond, squires ; Mr. John Cristinson, chancellor of the church of Dunblane, Malcolm Johnso
2 CONC n, dean of Lismore, Thomas Nicolson and John Spans, chaplains, and James of Redhuch, burgess of Stirling. Seal appended, in good condition ; a chevron, with a buck's head in base. Legend : ' Macolmus de Kynbuc' [https://archive.or
2 CONC g/details/calendaroflaingc00edin/page/37/mode/1up Laing Charters: charter number 143]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaingc00edin/page/n6/mode/1up Calendar of the Laing Charters, A.D. 854-1837, belonging to the University of Edinburgh. Edited by the Reverend John Anderson, Assistant Curator of the Histor
2 CONC ical Department H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh. (James Thin, Edinburgh, 1899), 1053 pp. including indices]'''
