1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Innerpeffray Chapel was a private chantry chapel built by John, 1st Lord Drummond, and associated with nearby Innerpeffray Castle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also known as St Mary's Chapel, stands on the east bank of the Rive Earn a little over three miles south-east of Crieff.
2 CONT
2 CONT Perth and Kinross  is one of the 32 council areas of Scotland, and a lieutenancy area. The area takes its name from the two historical shires of Perthshire and Kinross-shire
2 CONT
2 CONT Perthshire -   Burgh of Crieff (burgh of barony 1674, burgh of regality 1687, police burgh 1864)
