1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===William Halyburton===
2 CONT * Suffix: 	younger of Gask and Pitcur 
2 CONT * Birth:	1472 - Gask, Perth, Schottland
2 CONT *Death:	1523 - Gask, Perth, Schottland
2 CONT *Parents:	John Halyburton, Elizabeth Rattray
2 CONT *Wife:	Elizabeth Ogilvy Children:
2 CONT *	George Halyburton, 
2 CONT * Janet Halyburton, of Buttergask
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Haliburton, of Gask, had a charter from his father for the lands of Ingliston, Knoktoun, Kyngele, Crywe, Faynellan, Crulach, and others in the barony of Arde and Sheriffdom of Inverness on 22 June, 1496, and, as son and he
2 CONC ir to his father, granted a charter of the two oxgangs of the lands of Kinrossy to his cousin Alexander Rattray on 1 June, 1498.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I30983&tree=CC
2 CONT * 1. Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Ogilvy01 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p67740.htm#i677399
2 CONT
2 CONT William Halyburton, younger of Gask and Pitcur is the son of John Halyburton of Gask and Elizabeth Rattray.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Ogilvy, daughter of Alexander Ogilvy, younger of Clova.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Halyburton, younger of Gask and Pitcur and Elizabeth Ogilvy
2 CONT
2 CONT #George Halyburton of Pitcur+1 d. b 17 Jun 1538
2 CONT #James Halyburton of Gask1 d. b 4 May 1522
2 CONT
