1 NAME Eleanor
2 GIVN Eleanor
2 NICK Alianora
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 13 APR 1331 AND 8 SEP 1331
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''[https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-de-Bruce-6th-Lord-of-Annandale/6000000000523551913 ROBERT [VI] de Brus],''' son of ROBERT [V] de Brus Lord of Annandale & his first wife Isabel de Clare (Jul 1243-shortly befo
2 CONC re 4 Apr 1304, bur Abbey of Holm Cultram). 
2 CONT
2 CONT x m thirdly as her first husband, '''ELEANOR, daughter of --- (-[13 Apr/8 Sep] or [16 Mar/19 Oct] 1331).'''  A charter dated 2 Dec 1305 refers to "Alianora widow of Robert de Brus"[1115].  
2 CONT
2 CONT xx '''She married secondly ([2 Dec 1305/8 Feb 1306]) as his first wife, Richard le Waleys of Burgh Wallis, Yorkshire, Lord Waleys.  The primary source which confirms her second marriage has not yet been identified. ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SCOTLAND.htm#RobertBrusdied1304
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-235042
2 CONT
2 CONT Alianora was born about 1270. Alianora Unknown was the widow of Robert de Brus, 6th Lord Annandale and Earl of Carrick who died in 1304.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Robert's death, Eleanor married Sir Richard Waleys. It is unclear if she was the mother of any of his children. Given that her previous husband did not die until 1304, and [https://www.geni.com/people/Stephen-le-Waleys/60000
2 CONC 00000236157598?through=6000000005103827851 Stephen le Waleys] was a knight by 1294, [1]he could not have been the son of Eleanor. Likewise, his sister Alice, if she was the mother of Edmund Peverel, born by 1310, could not have be
2 CONC en the daughter of Eleanor. It is likely that all three of Richard's known children were the children of an earlier and unknown first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice is likely the Alice who married Sir Robert Peverel given that her son Edmund inherited the manor of Offord Daneys, which had been part of Eleanor's dower from Robert de Brus[2] as well as having been held by Alice's brother-
2 CONC in-law, Walter Langton, bishop of Coventry. [3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT The manor of Offord Daneys had come to the grandmother of Robert le Brus ca 1237.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alianora passed away about 1331. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  1.[S265] Colquoun_Cunningham.ged, Jamie Vans
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S289] Betty and Dick Field's Family History, Richard Field
