1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander de Bruce, 1st and last Earl of Carrick  [of the 3rd? creation] was born illegitimately before 1317.2 He was the son of Edward  de Bruce, 1st Earl and last of Carrick and Isabella  of Strathbogie.1  He mar
2 CONC ried Eleanor Douglas, daughter of Sir  Archibald Douglas and Beatrice  Lindsay. He died on 19 July 1333, killed in action, without male issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander de Bruce, 1st and last Earl of Carrick was created 1st Earl of Carrick [Scotland] circa 1330. He fought in the Battle of Halidon Hill on 19 July 1333.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://thepeerage.com/p10246.htm#i102460
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bruce-3933
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Numbering the Earls of Carrick is rather pointless, since by this time the title belonged to the Scottish royal family and was generally conferred within said family - usually, but not always, to the ruler's eldest son.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_de_Brus,_Earl_of_Carrick
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Bruce, Earl of Carrick (died 1333) was the Natural son of Edward Bruce and his mistress, Isabel, daughter of John de Strathbogie, 9th Earl of Atholl.
2 CONT
2 CONT He played an ambivalent role during Edward Balliol's first invasion of Scotland. For a time he fell in with Balliol, but then he rejoined the Bruce loyalist side.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was killed fighting on the Scottish side at the Battle of Halidon Hill. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Halidon_Hill
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander was the first husband of Eleanor Douglas, daughter of Sir Archibald Douglas, Guardian of Scotland, they had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleanor de Brus, who reputedly married Sir William de Cunynghame of Kilmaurs.
