4 CONT "Post hoc captum est castrum de Lochdown, in quo inventus est Christopherus Setonus sororius Roberti de Brus. Jussit rex deduci usque Dumfries, ibi∣que tractus, suspensusque, ac ultimo decolla∣tus. Johannes vero Setonus Christophe
4 CONC ri ger∣manus, apud Novum castrum super Tinam, tractus, suspensus, atque decollatus, horribiliter vitam terminavit, anno regni Edwardi I. 3410. 1306."
4 CONT
4 CONT
4 CONT King Robert afterwards, in memory of this brave sir Christopher, erected a chapel near Dumfries, where he was put to death; the ruins whereof are still to be seen, and it re∣tains the name of Christel's chapel to this day.
4 CONT
4 CONT By the said lady Christian Bruce, daughter of Robert earl of Carrick, and sister of king Robert, he left issue a son,
4 CONT
