2 CONT Notes  ◦It is not clear which Seton family Margaret came from. As reported in a footnote on 'Seton01 ', there are conflicting accounts of the early generations of that family. The dates make it possible that Margaret's father was 
2 CONC the Sir Christopher de Seton (d by 1307) who married Christian Bruce (d c1357), sister of King Robert. TSP suggests that this John's wife was Marjory Airth (heiress of Airth, who d c1340). It is noted that BP1999 shows a spouse of
2 CONC  that name for Alexander, shown below as grandson but by that article as son of this John. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  1.[S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, Elphinstone1 (Reliability: 3).
