2 CONT ?He is styled as brother to ?The Laird of Kellie? when he had was complained of for having fraudulently contrived to enter as tenant of the Crown lands of half of Balcarres for which a complaint was raised with the Lords of Counci
2 CONC l on 30 December, 1491, and appears to be identical with the person of the same name who obtained a quarter-part of the Crown lands of Murdocairney in 1492. 
