1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John de Yrskyn, Kt
2 CONT *John
2 CONT **'''John de Yrskyn [Erskine]''' 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''c1283 - c16 July 1309: Charter by James, Steward of Scotland, to John de Yrskyn [Erskine], son of John, son and heir of Sir John de Yrskyn, Kt, for his homage and service, of all land which the granter holds in tenement of the 
2 CONC (le) Larges, saving to granter 2 merks of land which Walter, son of Richard, held, and also right of patronage of the Larges, and saving to William, son of Sir John de Yrskyn, 2 merks of land in said tenement which said Sir John r
2 CONC esigned to granter by staff and baton, and in which he infefted said William; under provision that grantee shall perform forinsec service from said land, namely as much as pertains to 1/10 part of service of one Kt; with permissio
2 CONC n to grantee and his heirs to have 6 brewhouses in said land; and with clause of warrandice. Witnesses - Sir Robert, Bishop of Glasgow, Sir Reginald de Crauford [Crawford], Sir John de Yrskyn, Walter Logan, John Wyscard [Wishart],
2 CONC  Gilbert de Coningisburg. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f1%2f1112&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=erskine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1300&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the 
2 CONC Erskine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/1/1112]'''
