1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=canucktwo&id=I44386
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Margaret (Agnes) Erskine Surname: Erskine Given Name: Margaret (Agnes) Sex: F Birth: ABT 1280 in Erskine, Midlothian, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     The Scottish Peerage (Linthlighgow) shows William's wife merely as Margaret. Burke's Extinct Peerage 1883 shows her as a daughter of Sir John Erskine of Erskine. The Kilsyth web site referred to her as Margaret Comyn, daughter
2 CONC  of Sir Fergus Comyn of Gogyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT     William and Margaret (Erskine) Livingston had two children:
2 CONT     - William (c.1300 to 11-30-1364) married Christian de Callender.
2 CONT     - John (c.1310 to 8-22-1364) married the daughter of Michael Wemyss.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: John Erskine II b: ABT 1249 in Erskine, Midlothian, Scotland Mother: Miss Gilronan b: ABT 1254 in Renfrewshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 William Livingston (Laird of Drumry) b: ABT 1270 in Drumry, Dunbartonshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has Children William Livingston (Sheriff of Haddington, then Lanark) b: ABT 1300 in Carse, Forfarshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT     Has Children John Livingston of Drumry and East Wemyss b: ABT 1300 in Drumry, Dunbartonshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Repository:
2 CONT         Name: Internet
2 CONT     Title: Stirnet Genealogy - Section III - British Families - Medieval, Renaissance, Modern
2 CONT     Author: Peter Burns-Graham
2 CONT     Publication: http://www.stirnet.com/HTML/genie/genfam.htm
2 CONT     Page: Livingstone-01 
