2 CONT imprisonment in Engl and. From his activity in punishing the
2 CONT depredations of the Highlanders, w ho often committed great outrages
2 CONT in the low country of Dumbartonshir e, he rendered himself obnoxious
2 CONT to them, and a plot was formed for his de struction. He received a
2 CONT civil message from some of their chiefs, desiri ng a friendly
2 CONT conference, in order to accommodate all their differences. S uspecting
2 CONT no treachery, he went out to meet them but slightly attended, a nd was
2 CONT immediately attacked by a numerous body of Islanders, under two not ed
2 CONT robber-chiefs, Lachlan Maclean and Murdoch Gibson, and slain in
2 CONT Inchmur ren, on Loch Lommond, in 1439.
2 CONT Click here for <a href="http://ww
