2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE; Sheriff Perth, Keeper [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doune_Castle '''Doune Castle''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir DAVID MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE;  
2 CONT * acquired Polgour 1430, also Fendoch, half of Ardoch and half of Kintoches 1443; 
2 CONT * founded Collegiate Church of Tullibardine 1445; 
2 CONT * obtained Lethendy and Cultrannoch 1446; 
2 CONT * Auditor Exchequer 1448 and 1450, Bailie Earldom of Strathearn and Keeper Methven Castle; 
2 CONT * married 1430 Margaret, 2nd daughter of Sir John Colquhoun of Luss (see that Bt), 
2 CONT * died 1451/2, leaving, with other issue (including Patrick (see MURRAY OF OCHTERTYRE, Bt); Mariot, married Sir Malcolm Drummond; see PERTH, E), an eldest son:
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE;'''  Sheriff Perth, Keeper Doune Castle; married Margaret (married 2nd George Clephane of Carslogie), daughter of 1st Lord Gray (qv), and died c 1459, having had, with other issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT >>Sir WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Murray of Tullibardine1
2 CONT M, #24076, d. circa 1459
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Murray of Tullibardine|d. c 1459|p2408.htm#i24076|Sir David Murray of Tullibardine|d. bt 1451 - 1452|p2408.htm#i24080|Margaret Colquhoun||p2409.htm#i24081|Sir David Murray of Tullibardine||p4284.htm#i42838|Isabel Stewa
2 CONC rt||p4285.htm#i42848|Sir John Colquhoun of Luss|b. c 1390\nd. 1479|p2409.htm#i24082|unknown Boyd||p24569.htm#i245686|
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Murray of Tullibardine was the son of Sir David Murray of Tullibardine and Margaret Colquhoun.2 He married Margaret Gray, daughter of Andrew Gray, 1st Lord Gray and Elizabeth Wemyss.2 He died circa 1459.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Murray of Tullibardine held the office of Sheriff of Perthshire. He lived at Tullibardine, Perthshire, Scotland.2 He held the office of Keeper of Doune Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir William Murray of Tullibardine 1.Christian Murray+1 Child of Sir William Murray of Tullibardine and Margaret Gray 1.Sir William Murray of Tullibardine+2 b. c 1444, d. 10 Feb 1524/25 Citations 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, e
