1 NOTE {geni:about_me} {{icn_check.gif}} Burke's Peerage extract (full document attached)
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE;  Sheriff Perth, Keeper Doune Castle; married Margaret (married 2nd George Clephane of Carslogie), daughter of 1st Lord Gray (qv), and died c 1459, having had, with other issue:
2 CONT *'''Sir WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE''';  born c 1444; confirmed as Steward, Forester and Coroner of Strathearn by charter 1483 and Parl 1492; married Lady Mary Keith, daughter of 1st Earl Marischal (see KINTORE, E), and died 10
2 CONC  Feb 1524/5, having had, with other issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT >*Sir WILLIAM MURRAY OF CASTLETON
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/18/mode/2up Page 19 No 95
2 CONT
2 CONT (95) Sir William Murray of Tullibardine,  died 10th February 1524-25. He was served heir to his father, 6th October 1461, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 95(a) Sir John Murray of Polgour, died v.p., and probably s.p., before 16th January 1499-1500. He married Elizabeth Crichton. 
2 CONT * 95(b) Sir William Murray of Castleton, killed v.p. at Flodden, 9th September 1513. He married Margaret Stewart, daughter of John, Earl of Atholl
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2408.htm#i24073
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir William Murray of Tullibardine''' was born circa 1444. He was the son of Sir William Murray of Tullibardine and Margaret Gray. He married '''Lady Mary Keith''', daughter of William de Keith, 1st Earl Marischal and Margaret 
2 CONC Erskine. He died on 10 February 1524/25.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Tullibardine, Perthshire, Scotland.1 In 1483 he was confirmed as Steward, Forester and Coroner of Strathearn.
