1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ROBERT LIVINGSTON OF DRUMRY AND EAST WEMYSS===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Livingston of Drumry and East Wemyss died before 16 March 1504-05.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD172%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Livingstone+of+Drumry&ko=p&r=&r
2 CONC o=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Henderson Family of Fordell, reference GD172/123]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 March 1504-05 : Gift under Privy Seal in favour of Mr James Henryson of ward of £10 and 5 merk worth of lands of Balbeithy in barony of Lochorschire and sheriffdom of Fife (Fiffe), in ward since death of Robert Livingstone o
2 CONC f Drumry, kt.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD172%2f123&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Livingstone+of+Drumry&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hender
2 CONC son Family of Fordell, reference GD172/123]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08paul#page/368/mode/1up Sir James Balfour Paul, CVO., LL.D., The Scots Peerage; Containing an Historical and Genealogical Account of the Nobility of that Kingdom, VIII (David Douglas,
2 CONC  Edinburgh, 1911), pp.  368-77 for Livingston, Viscount Teviot]
