1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ROBERT LIVINGSTON OF DRUMRY AND EAST WEMYSS===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Livingston of Drumry and East Wemyss "grandson and heir of William Livingston of Drumry" had a charter under to Great Seal of Scotland dated 24 September 1511. Th charter charter confirmed his possession of the lands
2 CONC  of Hill of Auchenfure and others in the Renfrewshire parish of Inverkip which had been acquired by his grandfather. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/789/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, ii, 
2 CONC charter number 3651]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Livingston of Drumry and East Wemyss is reported to have been killed in action on 9 September 1513, fighting against the English at the Battle of Flodden. [http://www.venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps40/ps40_168.htm 
2 CONC Venitap: Genealogy Web Cards]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Robert Livingston of Drumry and his wife Jonete Betoun had a charter of confirmation for the lands of East and West Wemyss and others in Wenys-schire which was issued under the Great Seal of Scotland on 19 May 1508 [https:/
2 CONC /archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/690/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, ii, 1424-1523, charter number 3229]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Child===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Livingston/6000000002116167091?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1478464220397&through=6000000000437864655
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Isabella-Livingston/6000000005062574439
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 April 1805: Instrument of sasine in favour of '''Robert Levinstoun of Drumry''' in respect of the lands thereof, following on charter and precept by Matthew, Earl of Levinax. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalog
2 CONC ue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f627&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumry&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1471&dt=1570&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/627]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 July 1511: License of Quitclaim, '''Robert Levinstoun of Drumry. Kt''' to Sir Symon Prestoun. As Over Laird of twa parts of the barony of Craigmillar for 160 merks Sir John Ramsay, of Tervingzane, John Sinclair of Hirdmanstoun,
2 CONC  Thomas Sinclair of the Hiefield, Sir John Ker, Chaplain, Edward Hall, burgess of Edinburgh and John Litell, Signatures of Granter. Seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD122%2f1%2f17
2 CONC 3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumry&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1400&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, reference GD122/1/173]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note''' See Great Seal charter in favour of Simon Preston dated 10 August 1511. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/779/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotlan, ii, charter number 3614]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT 17 December 1524: Tack to Adam Lyndesay of Dowhill by '''Margaret Levinstoune of Eist Wemys with consent of James Hamilton of Fynnart, her husband''' of the lands of Petcarne. Witnesses: sir John Spittall, vicar of Hamiltoune and 
2 CONC Thomas Hamilton. Subscribed by '''James, earl of Arran and James Hamilton of Fynnart.'''(Faint traces and a few fragments of 3 applied seals.)[http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD254%2f21
2 CONC 5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1450&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Lindsay family of Dowhill. reference GD254/215]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note''' In 1508 King James the Fourth erected the lands of East Wemyss and part of Lochoreshire into the Barony of East Wemyss for Sir Robert Livingston pf Drumry and East Wemyss. Margaret Livingston, daughter and heiress of Si
2 CONC r Robert, married Sir James Hamilton of Finnart and in 1530 they exchanged East Wemyss with Sir James Colville of Ochiltree for his Barony of Ochiltree. [https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/n38/mode/1up/search/j
2 CONC ames+hamilton+of+finnart Wemyess Memorials, p. xix]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/memorialsoffamil01fras#page/n4/mode/1up Sir William Fraser, KCB., LL.B., Memorials of the Family of Wemyss of Wemyss (Edinburgh 1888), 426 pp.]
2 CONT
