1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Margaret Colville:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p17248.htm#i172477
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Colville [1]
2 CONT *F, #172477, 
2 CONT *d. after 21 April 1502
2 CONT *Last Edited=7 Oct 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Colville married John Sempill, 1st Lord Sempill, son of Sir Thomas Sempill and Elizabeth Ross, before 9 September 1501.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 21 April 1502.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Robert Colville of Hiltoun and Elizabeth Arnot.[2],[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was also known as Margaret Colvill.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From before 9 September 1501, her married name became Sempill.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Margaret Colville and John Sempill, 1st Lord Sempill
2 CONT *1. William Sempill, 2nd Lord Sempill+2 d. 3 Jun 1552
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 865. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 622. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
