1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord of Avondale
2 CONT * Birth - abt 1470
2 CONT * Death - 9 Sep 1513 Age: 43 Killed in action, Battle of Flodden
2 CONT * Parents: Alexander Stewart , M (<1465-1489), Mother	? Unknown , F
2 CONT * Married: Margaret Kennedy Also known as Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Avondale [1,2], Lord Avondale 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_1st_Lord_Avondale_(second_creation)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avondale (died 1513) was a Scottish nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander Stewart, from whom he inherited the lands of Avondale. Alexander had inherited them from his uncle Lord Avondale, who had in turn received them following their forfeiture by the last Earl of Douglas and
2 CONC  Avondale in 1455.
2 CONT
2 CONT The title Lord Avondale was revived for Andrew Stewart of Avondale in about 1499. He died in 1513 (killed at the Battle of Flodden) and was succeeded by his son Andrew, who exchanged Avondale for Ochiltree and thus became first Lo
2 CONC rd Ochiltree. Lord Avondale was also father of Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Methven and Sir James Stewart, father of James Stuart, 1st Lord Doune, whose son James became Earl of Moray.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # The Complete Peerage, 1936 , Doubleday, H.A. & Lord Howard de Walden, Reference: vol XII page 273 
2 CONT # A Genealogical History of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited and extinct peerages of the British Empire, London, 1866, Burke, Sir Bernard, Reference: page 509. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00006151&tree=LEO
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Flodden
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10928.htm#i109275
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avandale was born between January 1470 and 1488/89.1 He was the son of Alexander Stewart. He married Margaret Kennedy, daughter of John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy and Lady Elizabeth Gordon, before 4 Februar
2 CONC y 1499/0.2 He died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, killed in action.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avandale gained the title of 1st Lord Avandale.3 He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avandale and Margaret Kennedy
2 CONT
