1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ARTHUR STEWART OF CULBEG===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Arthur Stewart of Culbeg is the son of Agnes Ker. John Stewart, Agnes Ker's husband, is presumed to be his father. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/476/mode/1up RMS:  charter number 2250 on pp. 476-77]'''
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Arthur Stewart of Culbeg but he may have died in or before 1542, the date upon which the crown estates issued a precept of sasine for the lands of Culbeg and Culmoir to John
2 CONC  Stewart. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=umn.31951d00466524z;view=1up;seq=832 RSRS: 772]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 May 1495: Charter by which James IV, King of Scots,confirms Arthur Stewart's possession of one half of the lands of Culbeg and Culmoir in the sheriffdom of Stirling. These lands were previously resigned in Arthur's favour by 
2 CONC his mother Agnes Ker, who reserved her own liferent and that of her husband John Stewart. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/476/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal 
2 CONC of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513, charter number 2250 on pp. 476-77]'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 November 1509: Instrument of Sasine under the hand of David Menteth, Master of Arts, presbyter of the diocese of Dunblane, notary public, following upon a charter, (authenticated by the seal of the granter) granted by Andrew
2 CONC  Cunygahme of Drumchassile to Patrick Cunygahme, his lawful son (filio suo legittimo carnali), of one-sixth part of the lands of Cwlbeg in the sheriffdom of Steruilyng. Sasine given on 26th November 1509 by the granter to his son 
2 CONC upon the ground of said lands. Witnesses, Arthur Stewart of Culbeg, Sir Alexander Stewart, chaplain, his son, Malise McGilhoys and John Stewart. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f
2 CONC 60&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=culbeg&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/60]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1542: Libri Responsionum. Lib. 17. 1542. Striveling. Sa. Johanni Steuart t. Culbeg, Culmoir. 1. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=umn.31951d00466524z;view=1up;seq=832 Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls o
2 CONC f Scotland, Vol. XVII. A.D.1537-1542, page 772]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Register of Cambuskenneth Abbey===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 July 1510: Notorial instrument dealing with possession of the rectory of the parish church of Kippen. Among those present to witness the proceedings was Alexandro Forester de Culmore and Arthuro Steward de Culbeg. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/stream/registrummonast00camb#page/167/mode/1up Registrum Monasterii S. Marie de Cambuskenneth, A.D. 1147-1535 (Edinburgh 1872), pp. 167-68]'''
