2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 July 1476: Bond by tenants and feuars of earldom of Levenax [Lennox] to James, king of Scotland, to pay a year's maill to him within 30 days of his annexation of earldom to crown. Subscribed by Alexander of ?Conyham [Cunning
2 CONC holm] of ?Kylmaurese [Kilmaurs], Malcolm McClery [McCleary] of Garten [Garden]', James Nory [Norrie] of Terbart [Tarbert], James Balfour of Glendowlas and Andrew Cunyngam [Cunningham] of Drumquhas[il] [Drumquhassle]. [https://cata
2 CONC logue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f50&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassle&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1540&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshir
2 CONC e, reference GD198/50]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1482-83: The actioun and cause persewit and folowit be Andro Cuninggame of Drumquhassil . . . . . [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.30000047784453&view=1up&seq=111 The Acts of the Lords of Counvil in Civil Ca
2 CONC uses, 1496-1501: ciii]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 May 1490: Special retour in favour of James Haldane as heir of deceased Duncan, earl of Lennox, his great-great-grandfather, in a quarter of earldom of Lennox in sheriffdom of Dunbertan [Dumbarton], said lands having been in
2 CONC  king's hands for 66 years. Sheriff depute of Dunbertan [Dumbarton]: Robert Noble, younger. Members of inquests Alexander Ardincaple of that ilk, William Douglas of Ladcamberacht [Ledcameroch], Robert Noble of Ferme [Farme], Rober
2 CONC t Danzelstroun [Daniel] of Culgran, James Naper [Napier] of Kylmahew [Kilmahew], John Blar [Blair] of Fynwike [Finnich], Andrew Cuningham [Cunningham] of Drumquhastell [Drumquhassle], John Culquhoun [Colquhoun] of Camstrodan [Cams
2 CONC traddan], John Lyle of Ardardan, Nicol Buntyn [Bunting] of Ardoche [Ardoch], John Lyndesay [Lindsay] of Bonnull [Bonhill], John Ardincaple of Derlethe [Darleith], Thomas Galbraicht [Galbraith] and John Ardincaple. 6 tongues, seals
2 CONC  gone. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f53&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassle&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1540&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of G
2 CONC leneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/53]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 July 1493: Drimmen [Drymen]. Indenture between John, earl Lenax [Lennox], lord Dernle [Darnley], and Matthew, his son and apparent heir, fiar of said earldom, on one part, and John Haldane of Glennegas [Gleneagles] and James
2 CONC  Haldane, his son and apparent heir, one of personaris fiars of said earldom, on the other part . . . . . . . . . . Witnesses: James, lord Ogylvy [Ogilvie], James Hering [Herring] of Cluny, Thomas Blayr [Blair] of Bothyoke, John M
2 CONC axwell of Nethyr Polloke [Pollock], Andrew Cunynghame [Cunningham] of Drumquhassill [Drumquhassle], James Naper [Napier] of Kilmahew, Alexander Arngapill [Ardincaple] of that ilk, William Stewart of Baldorane [Baldorran], Andrew M
2 CONC acferland [McFarlane] of Arachare [Arrochar]. Subscribed by Jhone Steward [Stewart] and Mathew Steuard [Stewart]. Trace of applied seals. Other half of indenture printed in The Lennox, ii, 147-50. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov
2 CONC .uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f59&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/
2 CONC 59]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 July 1493: Charter by Mathew, earl of Lennax [Lennox], to Sir James Haudane [Haldane] of Glennegas [Gleneagles], kt. of lands as in GD198/59. Witnesses: James, lord Oggilby [Ogilvie], James Heryng [Herring] of Cluny, Thomas 
2 CONC Blar [Blair] of Bothick, John Maxwell of Neddyr Pollok [Pollock], Andrew Cunygam [Cunningham] of Drumquhassil [Drumquhassle], William Stewart of Baldorane [Baldorran] and Robert Boquhannen [Buchanan] of Lany [Leny]. Subscribed by 
2 CONC granter. Seal, damaged on tag. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f60&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD198%2f60&ro=m&df=&dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of t
2 CONC he Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/60]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 July 1493: Precept of sasine following on GD198/60. Bailies in that part: Robert Boquhuannan [Buchanan] of Lany [Leny], George Haudane [Haldane] of Kepparie [Kepdowrie], Thomas Boquhannen [Buchanan] of Drumnekill [Drumnakyle
2 CONC ] and Andrew Cunygam [Cunningham] of Drumquhassill [Drumquhassle]. Tag, seal gone. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f62&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=
2 CONC &dt=1500&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/62]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 April 1494: Instrument of Sasine under the hand of Walter Nory, presbyter of the diocese of Brechin, notary public, narrating that Robert Boquhannen, bailie and depute of Walter Boquhannen of that Ilk and bailie of John Knol
2 CONC lis, lord of Torfichyn, within the earldom of Lennax, passed to the ground of the lands of Fynvik-Tennand, lying in the earldon of Lennax and sheriffdom of Stirlyng and there gave sasine to Andrew Cunygam of Drumquhassil of the te
2 CONC mple lands of Fynvik-Danand with pertinents, and inducted and vested him in the lawful possession of the temple lands of Fynvik-Tennand with pertinents, in terms of the charter granted to him. Done on the ground of Fynvik Tenand o
2 CONC n 20 April 1494. Witnesses George Stewart, John Lennax, Alexander McNevin, James McGillern, Fynlaw McParkar, Maurice McGillern, James Makcaws and Patrick Morris (Moricii). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/de
2 CONC tails.aspx?reference=GD86%2f41&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassil&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/41]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 January 1501-02: Instrument of sasine following on letters by Mathew earl of Lenax [Lennox], [undated] in favour of James Haudane [Haldane] of Glennegas [Gleneagles], kt., of lands as in GD198/61. Notary: Walter Nory [Norrie]
2 CONC , priest, diocese of Brechin. Bailie in that part: Andrew Cunygam [Cunningham] of Drumquhassill [Drumquhassle]. Witnesses: George Haudane [Haldane], brother of said James, Alexander Cunygam [Cunningham], son of said Andrew, James 
2 CONC Menteth [Monteith], Alexander Haudane [Haldane], Archibald Lindsay, David Lindsay, John Haudane [Haldane], Patrick Davidson, William Huchonson [Hutchison] and Thomas Gillane [Gillan]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonline
2 CONC catalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD198%2f65&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Haldane Family of Gleneagles, Perthshire, reference GD198/65]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9       
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 May 1503: Charter by Andrew Cunyngame of Drumquhassill, to Walter Cunynghame, his son, of lands of Blairwoke, in earldom of Levenax, sheriffdom of Stirling. Tag, seal gone. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f1957&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1635&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference G
2 CONC D220/6/1957]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1504: Fragment of special retour in favour of William Lindesay, as heir of deceased John Lindesay, his father in lands of Bunhile in earldom of Levenax. Held before Matthew, earl of Levenax. Members of inquest include James Nap
2 CONC ar of Kilmahew, James Galbreith of Culcrugh, Alexander Ardincaple of that ilk, Andrew Cunnynghame of Drumcastile, Gilbert McKynny of Knokdore, James Blar of Fynwik and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogu
2 CONC e/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f6%2f1957&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1635&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD22
2 CONC 0/6/1957]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1566: Instrument of Sasine under the hand of John Buchquhannane, clerk of the diocese of Glasgow, notary public, following upon and narrating a precept of clare constat (dated at Ballindallycht 15th November 1565) by Joh
2 CONC n Cunynghame of Glengernok and Elizabeth Sinclar, his mother, addressed to Robert Cunynghame of Ros, their bailie in that part, for infefting John Cunynghame of Drumquhassill as heir of Andrew Cunynghame of Drumquhassill, his grea
2 CONC t-grandfather, in the lands of Blarvokke with pertinents lying in the sheriffdom of Striuling. Sasine given by the said Robert Cunynghame upon the ground of said lands on 1st June 1566. Witnesses to the precept, William Cunynghame
2 CONC , son of the said John Cunynghame [? of Glengernok] Malcolm Douglas, heir-apparent of Mathew Dowglas of Manis, and Paul Cunyngham. Witnesses to the Instrument, Nichol Cunynghame of Blairquhois, John Buchquhannan, son of the late W
2 CONC alter Buchquhannane of Spittell, Duncan McCawis McFrlane in Ardes, James Bullisland and John Maknoyer, alias Gilboye, servitor of George Buchquhannan of that Ilk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.asp
2 CONC x?reference=GD86%2f204&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/204]'''
2 CONT
