2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Cuthbert Simons ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 March 1509: Instrument on the obligation by Sir Dionysiiis Auchinlek, executor of the late Mr David Conigham, and Andrew Conigham of Drumquhassill, upon oath, to abide by the decree of James, archbishop of Glasgow, without a
2 CONC ppeal, respecting all sums due by the said Andrew to the deceased Mr David, and now to Sir Dionysius, by reason of executry, for which the said Andrew stood excommunicated by compulsory letters at the instance of the deceased Mr D
2 CONC avid and his said executor. Done in the chapter-house, Sabbath, 23d March 1509. 
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/liberprotocollor02bain/page/321/mode/1up Protocol Book of M. Cuthberti Simonis: Volume II, protocol number 407] [https://archive.org/details/liberprotocollor01glas/page/458/mode/1up Protocol Book of M.
2 CONC  Cuthberti Simonis: Volume I, protocol number 407]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 July 1510: Instrument on the resignation by the said Sir Martin Eede into the hands of John Schaw, one of the bailies of Glasgow for the time, of the said tenement belonging to his chaplaincy ; and on the sasine of the said 
2 CONC tenement thereafter given by the bailie, at the command of the said Sir Martin, to Mr James Neilson, vicar of ColmoneU. Done on the ground of the said tenement, lOth July 1510. Witnesses: dominis Gilberto Bynnyng, Richardo Ferguss
2 CONC on, notariis publicis, Andrea Care, vicario de Cumnok, presbiteris, Andrea Conigham de Druinquliassill, Willelmo Baxter, et Donaldo Chalmer, laicis. [https://archive.org/details/liberprotocollor01glas/page/458/mode/1up Protocol Bo
2 CONC ok of M. Cuthberti Simonis: Volume I, protocol number 472] [https://archive.org/details/liberprotocollor02bain/page/366/mode/1upProtocol Book of M. Cuthberti Simonis: Volume II, protocol number 472]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Gavin Ros ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1516: Instrument narrating that Walter Schaw, laird of . . . . . , the third part of the £5 lands of Cathcowrnan? (acknowledged?) that he had sealed a procuratory for resigning the third part into the hands of John,
2 CONC  Earl of Lennox, as superior, in favour of Alexander Conyghame, son and heir of Andrew Conyghame Drumquhassill. Done in the house (?) of Thomas Walker in Glasgow 26 February 1516. Witnesses, Sir George Ross, chaplain, Thomas Walke
2 CONC r and John Willison. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso29scotuoft/page/26 Protocol Book of Gavin Ros: 158]'''
