2 CONT '''20 May 1502: Apud Edinburgh, 20 Mali. REX, tanquam senescallus Scotie, concessit ALEXANDRO CRAUFURD, et heredibus ejus, — dimedietatem terrarum de Spango et molendini eanindem, in baronia de Renfrew, vic. ejusdem; — quas Eliz. 
2 CONC Park sponsa Geo. Striveling filii et heredis apparentis Job. S. de Cragbernard, et Margreta Park sponsa Alex. Cunyngbame filii et heredis apparentis And. C de Dramquhassill, cum consensu dictorum suorum maritorum, resignaverunt, —
2 CONC  in excambium pro terris de Kilwynnet, in comitatu de Levenax, vic. Strivehng, dictis Geo. Striveling et Eliz. ejus spouse concessis. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/563/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter num
2 CONC ber 2649]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1502: Charter by Mathew, Earl of Levenax, Lord Dernly, granting to Alexander Conynghame, son and heir apparent of Andrew Conynghame of Drumquhassile, and Margaret Park, his spouse and the longer liver of them in conjunct
2 CONC  infeftment, the one-half of the lands of Killermen with pertinents, lying in the earldom of Levenax and sheriffdom of Striveling, which pertained to the said Margaret and Elizabeth Park, her sister german, and which they resigned
2 CONC  into the hands of the granter at Edinburgh: To be held to the grantees and the heirs procreated or to be procreated between them, whom failing to the lawful and nearer heirs or assignees of the said Margaret whomsoever, de nobis 
2 CONC of the granter and his successors in fee and heritage: Rendering therefor annually one-half pound of pepper and one-half pound of cumin at Martinmas on the ground of said lands in name of blench-farm si petantur tantum. At Edinbur
2 CONC gh 27th May 1502. Witnesses, William Logane, John Mure of Hawtounburne, Robert Halyday, John Paris and Sir Walter Logane, notary public. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f46&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=conynghame&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, reference GD86/46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 May 1503: Instrument of Sasine under the hand of Robert Watsone, clerk of the diocese of Glasgow, notary public, narrating that Andrew Cwnygame of Drumquhassill passed to his lands of Croftinculloch, lying within the earldon
2 CONC  of Levenax and sheriffdom of Strivelyng, and there suis propriis manibus gave sasine thereof to Alexander Cwnygame, his son and apparent heir, in terms of a charter granted to him, under reservation of his own liferent and a reas
2 CONC onable terce to Issobel Stewart, his spouse. Done on the ground of said lands on 19th May 1503. Witnesses, Robert Schaw, Gilbert Gardner and John Dwn. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=
2 CONC GD86%2f49&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Drumquhassill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1550&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1506: REX confirmavit cartam Tho. Hume do Langschaw militis, — [qua, pro certa summa pecunie persoluta, vendidit et alienavit M. DAVID CUNYNGHAME, canonico Glasguensi gencrali, heredibus ejus et assignatis, — 6 mercatas
2 CONC  terrarum antiqui extentus de Cassiltoun, cum molcndino earundem, in parochia de Stewartoun, ballia de Cunynghamc, vic. Are : — Tenend. de rege tanquam senescallo Scotie in feodo : — Test. Wil. Cunynghame de Craganis, And. Cunyngh
2 CONC ame de Drumquliassill, Magistris et Dominis Job. Hugouis rectore de Kilbride, Jac. Nelesone, Dionisio Achinlek, et Wil. Smyth, capellanis : — Apud civitatem Glasguensem, manu dicti Tho. subscript., 13 Jul. 1506] [https://archive.o
2 CONC rg/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/632/mode/1up RMS 1424-1513: charter number 2976]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 May 1527: Gift by James V in favour of Andrew Cunningham, fiar of Drumquhassle, of ward of half lands and annual rents pertaining to Andrew Cunningham, elder, liferenter of Drumquhassle, said Andrew Cunningham, younger, and 
2 CONC to Margaret Park, his mother, in king's hands by decease of John, Earl of Lennox. The whole ward had belonged to James Hamilton of Finnart, kt, who assigned it to Cuthbert, Earl of Glencairn; and they resigned it to the king for g
2 CONC ift of a half to said Andrew Cunningham. Fragment of privy seal remains appended. RSS I: no 3794. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD430%2f178&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=drumquhassle&k
2 CONC o=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1540&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Napier Family, reference GD430/178]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Alexander Cunninghame of Drumquhassill, here treated, is not mentioned in this deed. It would appear to be the case, however, since his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Park/6000000062570389913?through=6000000062
2 CONC 570253946 is identified as the mother of Andrew Cunninghame, fiar of Drumquhassill, rather than as the widow  Alexander Cunninghame of Drumquhassill, here treated, that he died before 31 May 1527.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Gavin Ros ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1516: Instrument narrating that Walter Schaw, laird of . . . . . , the third part of the £5 lands of Cathcowrnan? (acknowledged?) that he had sealed a procuratory for resigning the third part into the hands of John,
2 CONC  Earl of Lennox, as superior, in favour of Alexander Conyghame, son and heir of Andrew Conyghame Drumquhassill. Done in the house (?) of Thomas Walker in Glasgow 26 February 1516. Witnesses, Sir George Ross, chaplain, Thomas Walke
2 CONC r and John Willison. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso29scotuoft/page/26 Protocol Book of Gavin Ros: 158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi02scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1424-1513. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot. (H. M. General Re
2 CONC gister House, Edinburgh, 1882), 1153 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
