1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM CUNNINGHAM OF CRAIGENDS ==
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 January 1514: Charter by which Agnes Langmure confirms, with the consent of her husband Nicholas Edyare, lord on Inglistoun, that she has sold her part of the lands of Auchinbotho-Langmure in the barony and sheriffdom of Ren
2 CONC frew to William Cunynghame, junior, and his wife Egidie Campbell. William Cunyghame, junior, is identified as the son and apparent heir of William Cunynghame of Craganis. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/33
2 CONC /mode/1up RMS: charter number 153]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: William Cunningham, junior, eventually succeeded his father at Craigends. Contrary to what is suggested elsewhere, his father was not killed at the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513. It would appear that he was still 
2 CONC alive on 20 January 1514.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitland T
2 CONC homson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indexes and Errata]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/cunningham03.php#top Stirnet: Cunningham 03]
2 CONT # [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart09.php Stirnet: Stewart 09]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Cuninghame, William 1st of Craigends [3394] 1 2
2 CONT
2 CONT     Born: Cir 1460 2
2 CONT     Marriage (1): Stewart, Elizabeth [3395] on 29 January 1484 1
2 CONT     Marriage (2): Auchinleck, Marion [2317] in 1496 2
2 CONT     Died: 9 September 1513, Flodden, Kirknewton, Northumberland, England at age 53 3
2 CONT
2 CONT   General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cuninghame, 1st Laird of Craigends; second son of Alexander de Cunynghame , Earl of Glencairn; married (1) on 29 January 1484 to Elizabeth Stewart (died before 31 August 1496), daughter of Sir Walter of Arthurlie and Janet
2 CONC  Cameron; married (2) by contract signed 31 August 1496 at Auchinleck to Marion Auchinleck, daughter of Sir John of Auchinleck. William was killed on 9 September 1513 at the Battle of Flodden Field, Northumberland, England. His fa
2 CONC ther granted William an annual rent of 15 merks from the lands of Walterston in Kilbarchany. On 4 February 1479 he was also granted a charter of the lands of Craiganys (Craigends) in the Lordship of Ranfurly. He married for a seco
2 CONC nd time in 1496, and the marriage contract laid out a number of conditions designed to provide for any children of that marriage: 'Craigends thereby obleishes him to infeft the son (if any be) of the marriage in six mks. worth of 
2 CONC land of auld extent called Bartanholm, and otherwise to pay the sowm of 1000 merks. If there be no son, but daughters, then to pay only the sowm of 300 mks.' William had a charter of Robertland on 10 July 1506, which was confirmed
2 CONC  by James IV in 1510. He was killed fighting for Scotland when king James IV broke his alliance with Henry VIII and invaded England; James IV and many of his noblemen were also killed ["Cunninghames of Craigends", handwritten note
2 CONC s by Robert D. Mackenzie, 1900]
2 CONT
2 CONT   Death Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT killed at battle of Flodden.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Alt. Death, After 1479. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Elizabeth Stewart [3395] [MRIN: 2157], daughter of Sir Walter Stewart of Arthurlie [3396] and Janet Cameron [19373], on 29 January 1484.1 (Elizabeth Stewart [3395] died before 31 August 1496.)
2 CONT
2 CONT William next married Marion Auchinleck [2317] [MRIN: 4346], daughter of Sir John Auchinleck of that ilk [2318], in 1496.2
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in their marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Marriage Contract, 31 August 1496.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses/Children: 1. Stewart, Elizabeth [3395]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Cuninghame, William 2nd of Craigends [2041]+
2 CONT     Cuninghame, Janet [8846]+
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Auchinleck, Marion [2317]
2 CONT
2 CONT     Cuningham, David of Bartinholm, 1st of Robertland [5154]+
2 CONT     Cuningham, James of Polquhairn [41574]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/cunningham02.php#top
2 CONT
