1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://thepeerage.com/p1489.htm#i14886 thepeerage...]  ;  
2 CONT * '''Helen Leslie''':  d. 28 October 1594
2 CONT *Helen Leslie, ''daughter'' of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes and Margaret Crichton.
2 CONT *She ''married'', 2. secondly, Mark Kerr, ''son'' of Sir Andrew Kerr of Cessford and Agnes Crichton
2 CONT *.She ''married'', 1 firstly, Gilbert Seton of Parbroath, 
2 CONT *She ''died'' on 28 October 1594.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Children of Helen Leslie and Mark Kerr
2 CONT >#    Andrew Kerr
2 CONT >#    George Kerr
2 CONT >#    William Kerr
2 CONT >#    Catherine Kerr + d. Mar 1600
2 CONT >#    Mark Kerr, 1st Earl of Lothian + b. c 1553, d. 8 Apr 1609
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lady Helen Kerr formerly Leslie aka Seton
2 CONT Born 1525 in Rothes, Morayshire, Scotland, United Kingdommap ANCESTORS ancestors Daughter of George Leslie and Agnes (Somerville) Leslie Sister of Katherine Leslie [half], Margaret Leslie [half], Margaret (Fleming) Cunningham [hal
2 CONC f], Peter Leslie, Euphemia (Leslie) Cunningham [half], James Leslie, Janet Leslie, Andrew (Leslie) Leslie Earl of Rothes 5th and Agnes (Leslie) Douglas [half] Wife of Gilbert Seton — married [date unknown] [location unknown] Wife 
2 CONC of Mark Kerr — married [date unknown] [location unknown] DESCENDANTS descendants Mother of George Seaton, Marion Mary Seton, David Seton, Catherine (Kerr) Maxwell and Mark Kerr Died 26 Oct 1594 in Abbey Newbottle, West Lothian, Sc
2 CONC otland map
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Helen Leslie was the daughter of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes and Margaret Crichton.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, Gilbert Seton of Parbroath, younger. Her married name became Seton then her married name became Kerr.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Mark Kerr, son of Sir Andrew Kerr of Cessford and Agnes Crichton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Helen Leslie and Mark Kerr:
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Kerr George Kerr William Kerr Catherine Kerr d. Mar 1600 Mark Kerr, 1st Earl of Lothian b. c 1553, d. 8 Apr 1609 Helen was born about 1520. She passed away about 1594.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Helen Lesley. [1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1526 Rothes, Morayshire, Schotland. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 26 October 1594. Abbey Newbottle, West Lothian, Scotland. [5][6]
