1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Wednesday, the twenty-second of February. 1569
2 CONT On this day, at the term appointed by the Superintendent for David Beaton of Creich and Beatrix Leslie his spouse, to submit in writing all their reasons and causes why either of them ought not to adhere to the other and continue 
2 CONC in the bond of marriage contracted and solemnized between them —
2 CONT both parties appeared in person.
2 CONT David declared that he had no reason or cause to present why he should not adhere and stated that he is willing to remain in the marriage.
2 CONT He requested reconciliation, with the advice of friends and especially of his brother-in-law, the Earl of Rothes, who is currently out of the country but whom he expects to return shortly.
2 CONT Therefore, he asked that the case be continued until the Earl’s return.
2 CONT The Superintendent, with the advice of the assembly and the consent of both parties, continued the case until the 15th of March next —
2 CONT with the warning that if Beatrix does not produce her reasons and causes on that day for refusing to adhere, the Superintendent will order her simply to return to her husband, under pain of excommunication.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On Wednesday, the fifteenth day of March, in the year of our Lord [15]69.
2 CONT On this day, at the term (appointed date) assigned to Beatrix Leslie to present in writing all her causes and reasons why she should not continue to live with David Beaton of Creich, her husband, in bed, board, and mutual cohabita
2 CONC tion (i.e., as man and wife), according to the last act in this case made on the 22nd of February last past — the assembly, in the absence of the Superintendent and with the consent of the parties, continued (postponed) the case i
2 CONC n the same state, form, and effect as it is now, to the 11th day of April next to come.
2 CONT The parties were cited in the record.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=uva.x001178872&seq=411&q1=Creich
2 CONT
2 CONT n the said day, regarding the summons raised at the Superintendent’s own initiative against David Beaton of Creich and his wife, Beatrix Leslie, concerning their marital adherence as Christian man and wife, or else to state cause 
2 CONC [why they should not],
2 CONT there appeared the said Beatrix, who alleged that she ought not to be compelled to adhere to David Beaton of Creich, because there was already pending before the Commissary Court of Edinburgh an action of divorce brought by her ag
2 CONC ainst him, on the grounds of adultery committed by him, as the full text of her legal complaint sets out in more detail.
2 CONT She offered to prove this adequately in writing, as allowed by law, and requested that a date be assigned to her to prove it.
2 CONT David Beaton also appeared, and requested a date be assigned to him to respond to the said allegations.
2 CONT Accordingly, the Superintendent assigned the 30th (penult) of August next for both parties.
2 CONT The parties were summoned and recorded in the official minutes (apud acta citatis).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015048380987&seq=418&q1=Beterage
2 CONT
2 CONT 30. august 1570 - On this day, at the term assigned to David Beaton of Creich to answer the allegations made by Beatrix (Beterage) Leslie on the 26th of July last past, both parties appeared in person; however, due to the absence 
2 CONC of the Superintendent, the case is suspended (sleeps).
2 CONT
2 CONT =====================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother is actually Agnes Somerville
