1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == AGNES SOMERVILLE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Leslie, fourth Earl of Rothes: "married, thirdly, before 29 January 1529-30,  Agnes Somerville, daughter of Sir John Somerville of Cambusnethan, and widow of John, second Lord Fleming. The date of her  death is not exact
2 CONC ly known, but she was alive on 18  August 1541, and she was dead some time  before 10 April  1543,  at which date the Earl and his fourth wife, Isobel Lundy, widow of David, eighth Earl of Crawford, who  had died on 27 or 28 Novem
2 CONC ber  1542, were infeft as husband and wife in the lands of Fynmonth". [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07paul/page/285/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 285]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Leslie, fourth Earl of Rothes: "married, thirdly, Agnes Somerville, daughter of Sir John Somerville of Cambusnethan, widow of John, second Lord Flemming, predecessor of the Earls of Wigton. Agnes Somerville, relict of th
2 CONC e deceased John, Lord Flemming, got a charter of the lands of Carsehaur, in Menteith, 7th December 1526 ; and George, Earl of Rothes, and Agnes Somerville his spouse, got a charter of the lands of Cairny, 29th January 1530, so tha
2 CONC t the marriage must have taken place between 1526 and 1530. [https://archive.org/details/historicalrecord02lesluoft/page/64/mode/1up Leslie: p. 64]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Fleming Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT John [Fleming], 2nd Lord Fleming married 3rd to '''Agnes''',  dau. of Sir '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan'''
2 CONT
2 CONT children by 1st husband 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.Margaret Fleming, mar. after 12 dec 1540 John Cunningham of Glengarnock
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Fleming (widow of John [Fleming], 2nd Lord Fleming; d. betw. 18 Aug 1541 and 10 Apr 1543), dau. of Sir John '''Somerville''' of Cambusnethan,  (mar. (2) betw. Dec 1526 and Jan 1528/9, as his 3rd wife, George [Leslie], 4th Ea
2 CONC rl of Rothes; d. betw. 18 Aug 1541 and 10 Apr 1543)
2 CONT
2 CONT children by 2nd husband 
2 CONT * 4. Hon Andrew Leslie of Kilmany, later 5th Earl of Rothes
2 CONT * 5. Hon Peter Leslie, Parson of Rothes (d. after 17 Jan 1558/9)
2 CONT * 6. Hon James Leslie (d. after 1574), mar., and had issue
2 CONT * 3. Lady Euphemia Leslie (d. Apr 1588), mar. (1) bef. 18 Aug 1548 George Learmouth of Balconie (d. Jun 1585), and (2) John Cunningham of West Barns
2 CONT * 4. Lady Agnes Leslie (d. after Feb 1593/4), mar. 19 Aug 1554 William [Douglas], 6th Earl of Morton, and had issue
2 CONT * 5. Lady Beatrix Leslie, mar. (1) after 14 Mar 1560/1 (div.) David Beaton of Creich, and (2) John Auchmoutie of that Ilk, and had issue by her first husband
2 CONT * 6. Lady Elizabeth Leslie, mar. after 1557 Patrick Crichton of Lugton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Leslie formerly Somerville aka Fleming. Born 1498 in Cambusnethan, Lanarkshire, Scotlandmap ANCESTORS ancestors Daughter of John Somerville and Elizabeth (Carmichael) Somerville Sister of Helen (Somerville) Boyd, John Somerv
2 CONC ille and	John Stewart I [half] Wife of John Fleming — married about 1518 [location unknown] Wife of George Leslie — married before 29 Jan 1530 (to before 10 Apr 1543) [location unknown] DESCENDANTS descendants Mother of Margaret (
2 CONC Fleming) Cunningham, Helen (Leslie) Kerr, Peter Leslie, James Leslie, Janet Leslie and Andrew (Leslie) Leslie Earl of Rothes 5th Died about 1543 in Rothesay, Elgin, Bute Island, Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT British Aristocracy Agnes (Somerville) Leslie was a member of aristocracy in the British Isles. Join: British Royals and Aristocrats Project Discuss: BRITISH_ARISTO Biography Agnes Somerville was a daughter of Sir John Somerville 
2 CONC of Cambusnethan.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, likely c. 1518, as his third wife, John Fleming, 3rd lord Fleming.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1524 and she had a charter under the Great Seal on 18 December 1526.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, before 29 January 1530, George, fourth Earl of Rothes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Balfour Paul notices that she gave birth to Margaret, the eldest daughter, and it could therefore be supposed she gave him the three girls.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
