1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Was a Scottish nobleman. He was the son of George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes, and his third wife Agnes Somerville, daughter of Sir John Somerville of Cambusnethan and Elizabeth Carmichael. He succeeded his father as 5th Earl in 15
2 CONC 58. His elder half-brothers Norman Leslie and William Leslie forfeited their rights by having been implicated in the murder of Cardinal Beaton in 1546.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Leslie married Grizel Hamilton, daughter of Sir James Hamilton of Finnart, and had issue. However, his eldest son James died before him. On Andrew Leslie's death in 1611 he was succeeded by his grandson John, James' only su
2 CONC rviving son.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=Zdyk2WG8ILQC&pg=PA120&lpg=PA120&dq=%22thomas+nairne%22+%22david+nairne%22&source=bl&ots=M5KYjo4QW7&sig=ShYEvYMLfh4zhGFa-sMlsh6jrK4&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjs5ve415jTAhVB9mMKHcq0C3oQ6AEIJzAE#v=one
2 CONC page&q=%22thomas%20nairne%22%20%22david%20nairne%22&f=false 635. Birth Brieve of Mr. David Nairne, 1687] in ''The Scottish Antiquary'', Vol. IX(1895), 119-24. 
