0 @N6000000001783427030@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT William Hay, 4th Earl of Erroll was the son of William Hay, 3rd Earl of Erroll and Lady Isabella Gordon.
1 CONT
1 CONT He succeeded to the title of 5th Lord Hay [S., 1430] on 14 January 1506/7. He succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Erroll [S., 1452] on 14 January 1506/7. He held the office of Hereditary Sheriff of Aberdeen on 10 February 1510/1
1 CONC 1. He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married, firstly, Christian Lyon, daughter of John Lyon, 3rd Lord Glamis and Elizabeth Scrymgeour, circa 24 April 1492. Children of William Hay, 4th Earl of Erroll and Christian Lyon were:
1 CONT William Hay, 5th Earl of Erroll d. 28 Jul 15221
1 CONT Lady Elizabeth Hay d. c 1576
1 CONT
1 CONT He married, secondly, Margaret Kerr, daughter of Andrew Kerr of Cessford, circa 17 May 1509.
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513 and was killed in action
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://thepeerage.com/p2630.htm>
1 CONT
1 CONT Other Source
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT ...In 1513 the Hays of Erroll (including Gilbert Hay of Delgatie Castle) and the Hays of Yester with 87 men of their same family name were all killed at the battle of Flodden Field along with King James IV of Scots. (Also falling 
1 CONC here was the Earl of Montrose, whose descendant, the Marquis of Montrose later was hanged with Hay's descendant, William Hay, for supporting Charles II during the English Civil War.)
1 CONT
1 CONT [There is another branch of the Hay family in Tweeddale. One of these Hays was created Baron Hay of Yester in 1488, Earl of Tweeddale in 1646, and Marquis of Tweeddale, Earl of Gifford, and Viscount of Walden, in 1694.  Their fami
1 CONC ly-seat is Yester-house, in Haddingtonshire.]
1 CONT
1 CONT Son, Thomas Hay was born abt 1479-81, d Sept 9, 1513, Flodden Field, Branxton, Northumberland, England. He was married to Margaret Logie in 1493.
1 CONT Son, William Hay (b abt 1480) married Christian Lyon.
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://mjgen.com/hay/hay.html>
