1 CONT
1 CONT Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy was born circa 1406. He was the son of Sir James Kennedy of Dunure, younger and Lady Mary Stewart
1 CONT .
1 CONT Gilbert Kennedy of Dunure, 1st Lord Kennedy held the office of Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun. He was created 1st Lord Kennedy [Scotland] from 27 March 1457 to 20 March 1457/58. In 1460 on the death of King James II, he was one 
1 CONC of the six Regents of Scotland.3 He held the office of Constable of Stirling Castle in 1466.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriages and Children
1 CONT
1 CONT He married, firstly, Catherine Maxwell, daughter of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell and an unknown Herries, circa 1440. Children of Gilbert and Catherine were:
1 CONT Catherine Kennedy
1 CONT John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy b. b 12 Oct 1454, d. bt 24 Jul 1508 - 13 May 15093
1 CONT
1 CONT He married, secondly, Isabel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Lintrathen and Isabel Glen, after 1460.
1 CONT
1 CONT Other Children
1 CONT
1 CONT Other children of Gilbert were:
1 CONT Elizabeth Kennedy
1 CONT Unknown Kennedy
1 CONT
1 CONT Death
1 CONT
1 CONT He died after 6 March 1478/79.
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://thepeerage.com/p2150.htm#i21499>
0 @N6000000002187931959@ NOTE Gilbert Kennedy, 1st Lord Kennedy
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gilbert Kennedy, 1st Lord Kennedy (b. c.1406, d. after 6 March 1478/79) was a Scottish lord, the son of Sir James Kennedy the younger, of Dunure, and Lady Mary Stewart, daughter of King Robert III of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had two children either out of wedlock or by an unnamed wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT Unnamed Kennedy 
1 CONT Elizabeth Kennedy (b. bef. 1425) 
1 CONT He married (1) Catherine Maxwell, daughter of Herbert Maxwell, 1st Lord Maxwell, circa 1440. They had two children.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children Catherine Kennedy (b. bef. 1444) 
1 CONT John Kennedy, 2nd Lord Kennedy (1454, d. bt 24 Jul 1508 - 13 May 1509) 
1 CONT He married (2) Isabel Ogilvy, daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy of Lintrathen, after 1460.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT He held the office of Keeper of the Castle of Lochdoun.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was created 1st Lord Kennedy between 27 March 1457 and 20 March 1458.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1460 on the death of King James II, he was one of the six Regents of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT He held the office of Constable of Stirling Castle in 1466.
1 CONT
1 CONT Peerage of Scotland 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT New Creation Lord Kennedy
1 CONT c.1457–c.1478 Succeeded by:
1 CONT John Kennedy 
