0 @N6000000001783346875@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT 1537 Lady Janet Douglas Lyon (Lady Glamis) died - Falsely accused witch
1 CONT
1 CONT Falsely accused witch. Janet was the widow of John Lyon, the 6th Lord Glamis (c.1491 - 1528) and then married Archibald Campbell of Skipnish. However, she was also grand-daughter of Archibald Douglas, the 5th Earl of Angus (c.1449
1 CONC  - 1513), a relationship which caused her terrible demise at the hands of King James V (1512-42). In his purge of the Douglases, Janet was accused of being a witch, arrested with her new husband and imprisoned in a dark dungeon in
1 CONC  Edinburgh Castle. He escaped, but was killed in the process, while she was burned on Castlehill in Edinburgh.
1 CONT
1 CONT (http://www.geo.ed.ac.uk/scotgaz/timeline1599.html)
0 @N6000000001877513169@ NOTE 7th Lord Glamis
0 @N6000000001783474475@ NOTE John Lyon, 7th Baron of Glamis. born between 1510-1515 in Ryslippe, Middlesex, England and died in 1558 or before Sept 18th, 1559. He was imprisoned and sentenced to be executed, but was respited until he
1 CONT should attain majority, in the interim, he was ordered to be closely confined and his estates declared forfeited. On the death of King James V, he was released and restored to his estates and honors by Parliament,
1 CONT 15 March 1542/3. He married Janet Keith Lyon between Feb 6th, 1543 - 1544. They had ( at least ) John Lyon, the 8th Baron of Glamis, Margaret and Sir Thomas Lyon.
1 CONT
1 CONT LeAnn
0 @N6000000001783474520@ NOTE John Lyon - Chamberlain of Scotland, born abt 1340 at Glamis, died Nov 4th, 1382 at Balhall, Scotland in a duel with Sir James Lindsay of Crawford. Married Princess Jean Stewart who was born abt 1350 in Dundonald, Ayrshire, Scotla
1 CONC nd. One of their sons was Sir John Lyon, Thane of Glamis.
1 CONT
1 CONT LeAnn
1 CONT
1 CONT Chamberlain of Scotland and ancestor of the Earls of Strathmore. Son of John de Lyon, feudal Baron of Forteviot, Lyon served as Chamberlain of Scotland between 1377 and his death. In 1372, King Robert II granted Lyon various lands
1 CONC , including those around Glamis. Established as the Thane of Glamis, he married Robert II's daughter, Princess Joanna (c.1376). The Princess was the widow of Sir John Keith and by this marriage Lyon also became Thane of Tannadyce.
1 CONC  Lyon was killed in a duel at Balhall (Angus) by Sir James Lindsay of Crawford. He was buried at Scone Abbey and was succeeded by his only son
1 CONT http://www.geo.ed.ac.uk/scotgaz/people/famousfirst1054.html
