0 @N6000000002187771052@ NOTE Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany (1362 – 24 May 1425) was a Scottish nobleman who inherited the Dukedom of Albany in 1420, but was convicted and executed for treason five years later. Together with the dukedom, he also inherite
1 CONC d the Earldom of Fife and the Earldom of Menteith. His father, Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany was a prominent Scottish nobleman who was regent in various capacities during the reigns of three kings (Robert II, Robert III, and 
1 CONC James I).
1 CONT
1 CONT Murdoch evidently served as Justiciar North of the Forth around 1389, then served in some military actions against the English in the early 15th century. He was captured in 1402 by the English, but was traded for Henry Percy, 2nd 
1 CONC Earl of Northumberland. Although Murdoch inherited his father's peerages and regency position in 1420, when James I returned to Scotland in 1424 he lost his position as regent.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1425 the king carried out a purge of the Albany Stewarts, and he was executed along with several members of his family and close associates; all of his peerage titles became attainted and were forfeited.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and children
1 CONT
1 CONT Murdoch was married to Isabella, daughter of Donnchadh, Earl of Lennox. They had four sons:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Robert Stewart (d. 1421)
1 CONT     * Walter Stewart (d. 1425). Fourth-generation ancestor of Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Methven.
1 CONT     * Alasdair Stewart (d. 1425)
1 CONT     * James/Seamas Mòr Stewart (d. 1451)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Robert Stewart Duke of Albany
1 CONT 1420 – 1425 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Forfeit, next held by Alexander Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Robert Stewart Earl of Fife
1 CONT 1420 – 1425 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Forfeit, next held by Alexander Duff, 1st Duke of Fife
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Margaret, Countess of Menteith Earl of Menteith
1 CONT 1420 – 1425 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Forfeit, next held by Malise Graham, 1st Earl of Menteith
