0 @N6000000002188101986@ NOTE Thomas, Earl of Mar
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas of Mar was a 14th century Mormaer (Earl) of Mar (1332 – 1374). He was a son of Domhnall II of Mar.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas became Earl of Mar whilst still a child living in the Kingdom of England, and it took several years for Thomas to return to the Kingdom of Scotland and take charge of his inheritance. He had a fairly successful career in Sc
1 CONC ottish politics, becoming Great Chamberlain of Scotland, and several times acting as an ambassador to England.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married twice, firstly to , Margaret Graham of Menteith, and secondly to Margaret Stewart, Countess of Angus. He was succeeded by his sister Margaret, who was married to William Douglas, 1st Earl of Douglas. He died childless i
1 CONC n 1374, bringing his line and the ancient Gaelic earldom of Mar through the male line to an end. The earldom passed into the Douglas family.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT
1 CONT     * A Genealogy Page
1 CONT     * Dated Link from Electric Scotland
1 CONT
