0 @N6000000002187962233@ NOTE Isabella, Countess of Lennox
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella of Lennox was the ruler of Lennox, 1437–1458. As the wife of Murdoch Stewart, she was Duchess of Albany (1420–1425) as well.
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella was the daughter of Duncan, Earl of Lennox and Helen, the daughter of Sir Archibald Campbell.
1 CONT
1 CONT Her father Duncan needed to create powerful links with the great Robert Stewart, who was the bastard son of King Robert II, and who ruled much of Scotland. In 1392, Duncan agreed to marry Isabella to Robert's son, Murdoch.
1 CONT
1 CONT Murdoch and Isabella had at least five children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Robert (d. 1421)
1 CONT     * Walter (d. 1425)
1 CONT     * Alasdair (d. 1425)
1 CONT     * James/Seamas Mòr (d. 1451)
1 CONT     * Isabel, who married Sir Walter Buchanan, 13th Laird Buchanan
1 CONT
1 CONT After her father and sons Walter and Alasdair were executed in 1425, Isabella was forced to spend eight years as a royal hostage. In 1437 she recovered her lands and title. In the next few years, although forced to govern her prov
1 CONC ince from Loch Lomond, she issued a large numbers of charters, was popular in the province, and was tolerated by James II.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, when she died in 1458, the oldest continuous Gaelic mormaerdom came to an end.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Bibliography
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Brown, Michael, "Earldom and Kindred: The Lennox and Its Earls, 1200-1458" in Steve Boardman and Alasdair Ross (eds.) The Exercise of Power in Medieval Scotland, c.1200-1500, (Dublin/Portland, 2003), pp. 201-224
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Donnchadh Mormaer of Lennox
1 CONT 1437-1458 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Extinct
