0 @N6000000000604979907@ NOTE Eupheme de Ross, Countess of Moray1 (F) b. before 1334, d. 1387, #105313d. 1387|p10532.htm#i105313|Hugh de Ross, 4th Earl of Ross|d. 19 Jul 1333|p10790.htm#i107897|Margaret Graham|b. b 1314|p10809.htm#i108086|William, 3rd Earl of 
1 CONC Ross|b. b 1274d. 28 Jan 1323|p467.htm#i4668|Euphemia (?)||p467.htm#i4669|Sir David Graham|b. b 1296d. c 1329|p468.htm#i4676||||');"Pedigree <JavaScript:pup('Eupheme de Ross, Countess of Moray|b. b 1334<BR> Last Edited=27 Nov 2003
1 CONT Eupheme de Ross, Countess of Moray was the daughter of Hugh de Ross, 4th Earl of Ross <p10790.htm> and Margaret Graham <p10809.htm>.1,2 She was born before 1334. She married Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland <p10210.htm>, son of
1 CONC  Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland <p10210.htm> and Margorie Bruce, Princess of Scotland <p10210.htm>, on 2 May 1355, by Papal dispensation.3 She married John Randolph, 3rd Earl of Moray <p10809.htm>.1 She died in 1387.
1 CONC 1,4  She was also known as Euphemia Leslie. She gained the title of Countess of Moray. Through her marriage, Eupheme de Ross, Countess of Moray gained the title of Countess of Atholl on 2 May 1355. Through her marriage, Eupheme de
1 CONC  Ross, Countess of Moray gained the title of Queen Consort Euphemia of Scotland in 1372.1
1 CONT Children of Eupheme de Ross, Countess of Moray and Robert II Stewart, King of Scotland <p10210.htm>:
1 CONT David Stewart, Earl of Caithness+ b. bt 1356 - 1360, d. b 5 Mar 1389 Elizabeth Stewart+ b. bt 1356 - 1370 Egidia Stewart+ b. bt 1356 - 1372, d. a 1388 Walter Stewart, 1st Earl of Atholl+ b. c 1360, d. 26 Mar 1437
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 223. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
1 CONT [S6 <s1.htm>] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant,
1 CONC  Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume XI, page 145. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
1 CONT [S6 <s1.htm>] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume I, page 311.
1 CONT [S2 <s1.htm>] Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998)
1 CONC , page 47. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
