0 @N6000000005597770985@ NOTE REFN: P2960
1 CONT EUPHEMIA ROSS, the 2nd wife and only queen of Robert II, was the d aughter
1 CONT of Hugh de Ross, 4th Earl of Ross. She was probably born between abou t
1 CONT 1325 and 1330, but this is very uncertain. Her mother was the earl's 2nd
1 CONT wife, Margaret, daughter of Sir David Graham of Montrose. Euphemia's
1 CONT parents were granted a dispensation to marry, and a legitimation of past
1 CONT and future c hildren born to them, 29 November 1329.
1 CONT She had married 1stly, John Randolph, 3rd Earl of Moray, who was killed
1 CONT at the disastrous battle of Neville's Cross , 17 October 1346, leaving her
1 CONT a childless and vulnerable widow of, at the mo st, 21 years of age, and
1 CONT probably rather younger.
1 CONT She married 2ndly (dispens ation granted by Pope Innocent VI at Avignon, 2
1 CONT May 1355), as his 2nd wife, R obert Stewart, Earl of Strathearn, who
1 CONT succeeded to the throne as Robert II, 22 February 1371. She gave him 2
1 CONT sons and 2 daughters. See: Genealogical Note s page. She was crowned at
1 CONT Scone by Alexander de Kyninmund II, bishop of Aber deen, in 1372.
1 CONT She died in 1387, predeceasing her husband by about 3 years, bu t the
1 CONT exact date and the place of her death and burial seem to have gone
1 CONT un recorded. She must have been a very good-natured and long-suffering
1 CONT lady, put ting up with the numerous and flagrant infidelities of her royal
1 CONT husband. Her personal charm and beauty may be inferred from the fact that
1 CONT both her daught ers possessed those qualities in a marked degree.
