0 @N6000000002187899150@ NOTE David Lindsay, 1st Earl of Crawford
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT David Lindsay, 1st Earl of Crawford (c. 1360–1407) was a Scottish peer, who was created Earl in 1398.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Elizabeth Stewart, daughter of King Robert II and they had seven children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Gerard Lindsay (d. 1421)
1 CONT     * Ingelram Lindsay, Bishop of Aberdeen (d. 1458)
1 CONT     * Marjorie Lindsay, married Sir William Douglas.
1 CONT     * Alexander Lindsay, 2nd Earl of Crawford (c. 1387–1438)
1 CONT     * David Lindsay , Lord of Newdosk (1407–?)
1 CONT     * Elizabeth Lindsay (1407–?), married Robert Erskine, 1st Lord Erskine and had issue.
1 CONT     * Isabella Lindsay (1407–?), married Sir John Maxwell.
1 CONT
1 CONT This biography of a peer or noble of the United Kingdom, or its constituent countries, is a stub. You can help Wikipedia by expanding it.
1 CONT
