1 CONT
1 CONT He [William Sinclair] married, 1stly, Elizabeth, widow of Sir Thomas STEWART [illegitimate son of Alexander [Stewart 11th Earl of Mar [SCT], and before that of John (STEWART), 3rd EARL OF BUCHAN [SCT], daughter of Archibald (DOUGL
1 CONC AS), 4th EARL OF DOUGLAS [SCT], by Lady Margaret STEWART, daughter of ROBERT III. She died about 1451.  [Complete Peerage II:477-78, XIV:133, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
0 @N6000000002187771006@ NOTE Archibald Campbell, Master of Campbell1 (M)
1 CONT b. before 1406, d. between August 1431 and March 1440, #108014
1 CONT Pedigree
1 CONT Last Edited=15 Sep 2003
1 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.1%
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Archibald Campbell, Master of Campbell was born before 1406. He was the son of Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell and Lady Marjorie Stewart.1 He married, firstly, Elizabeth Somerville, daughter of John Somerville, 2nd Lor
1 CONC d Somerville.1 He married, secondly, unknown Stewart, daughter of Murdoch Stewart, 2nd Duke of Albany, before 1440.2 He died between August 1431 and March 1440.1,3 
1 CONT      Archibald Campbell, Master of Campbell was also known as Gillespic.2 He was styled as Master of Campbell.4 He was also known as Celestine.1 He lived in Lochow, Argyllshire, Scotland.4 
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Archibald Campbell, Master of Campbell and Elizabeth Somerville
1 CONT Colin Campbell, 1st Earl of Argyll+ b. bt 1435 - 1440, d. 10 May 1493
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 220. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family. 
1 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 104. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 1
1 CONC 06th edition. 
1 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
1 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 198. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 
1 CONT [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 513. 
