0 @N6000000002188028402@ NOTE Colin Campbell, 3rd Earl of Argyll
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Colin Campbell, 3rd Earl of Argyll (c. 1486 – 09 October 1529) was a Scottish nobleman and soldier. He was the son of Archibald Campbell, 2nd Earl of Argyll and Elizabeth Stuart, daughter of John Stuart, 1st Earl of Lennox. In 150
1 CONC 6/07 he married Lady Jean Gordon, the eldest daughter of Alexander Gordon, 3rd Earl of Huntly. Campbell led an army against the insurrection of various Highland chieftains; a few years later, he joined the court of King James V. H
1 CONC e was given the position Lord Warden of the Marches and in 1528, Lord Justice General of Scotland.
1 CONT
1 CONT Judiciary Offices 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT ? Lord Justice General
1 CONT 1528–1529 Succeeded by:
1 CONT The Earl of Argyll 
1 CONT Peerage of Scotland 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Archibald Campbell Earl of Argyll
1 CONT 1513–1529 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Archibald Campbell 
