0 @N6000000003615874609@ NOTE Egidia (or Jill) Douglas, seen 1438; m. before 17 Nov 1407 Henry Sinclair, 2nd Earl of Orkney, b. c 1375, d. 1 Feb 1420/1, son of Henry Sinclair, Lord of Roslin, Earl of Orkney, and Jean, daughter of Sir Walter Haliburton of Dirle
1 CONC ton.  [Magna Charta Sureties]
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT He [Henry Sinclair] married, before 17 November 1407, Jill, daughter and heir of Sir William DOUGLAS, of Nithsdale, by Jill, daughter of ROBERT II, King of Scotland. He died probably 1 February 1420/1, of influenza. His widow marr
1 CONC ied, 2ndly, after 29 April 1422, Alexander STEWART, 3rd son of Murdoch, 2nd Duke of ALBANY [SCT], with whom he was beheaded at Stirling, 25 March 1425. She survived him, and was living in 1438. [Complete Peerage X:95-6, (transcrib
1 CONC ed by Dave Utzinger)]
