1 CONC p Iorwerth, Prince of North Wales|b. 1173d. 1240|p10791.htm#i107904||||');"Pedigree <JavaScript:pup('Isabella, Lady of Mar|d. b 1302|p10209.htm> Last Edited=9 Nov 2004
1 CONT Isabella, Lady of Mar was the daughter of Donald, 6th Earl of Mar <p10916.htm> and Helen (?) <p12728.htm>.1 She married Robert I Bruce, King of Scotland, son of Robert le Brus, Earl of Carrick <p10776.htm> and Margaret of Carrick,
1 CONC  Countess of Carrick <p10248.htm>, circa 1295.1 She died before 1302.1  She gained the title of Lady of Mar.
1 CONT Children of Isabella, Lady of Mar and Robert I Bruce, King of Scotland:
1 CONT Maud Bruce <p10926.htm>+ Margorie Bruce, Princess of Scotland <p10210.htm>+ b. c 1297, d. 2 Mar 1316
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S11 <s1.htm>] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 209. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family.
0 @N6000000003098284653@ NOTE Isabel of Mar was the wife of Robert the Bruce, King of Scotland. She was taken prisoner by the English in 1306 just before the Seige of Kildrummy Castle, along with Bruce's sister Mary.
1 CONT They were confined in timber and iron cages and hung from the walls of Berwick and Roxburgh castles, respectively. For months they were forbidden to communicate with anyone except the English who brought them food and water, expos
1 CONC ed to the weather and open mockery and allowed only the convenience of a privy.
1 CONT Somehow they survived the ordeal. Isabel was eventually released to join a nunnery as by that time Robert was himself dead.
0 @N6000000001783480273@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella of Mar (c. 1277 - December 1296; modern Scottish Gaelic: Iseabail) was the first wife of Robert Bruce. She was the daughter of Domhnall I, Earl of Mar and a woman named Helen (or Ellen) b. 1246 d. 1295, who had previously
1 CONC  been the wife of Maol Choluim II, Earl of Fife. Isabella was a wealthy young woman at the time of her arranged marriage to the Earl of Carrick, Robert Bruce. Her father was one of the seven guardians of Scotland who believed Robe
1 CONC rt Bruce to be the rightful King of Scotland. Despite the risks, he could see the advantage of the two families joining in marriage and bearing an heir to the throne. Mar was the first to sign over the estates of his family to the
1 CONC  Bruce.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Child
1 CONT
1 CONT Isabella was married to Robert at the age of 18 and legend has it that they were much in love. Shortly after their marriage Isabella became pregnant. She had a healthy pregnancy but she died soon after giving birth to a daughter, 
1 CONC Marjorie Bruce in 1296. Robert married his second wife, Elizabeth de Burgh, six years later. Isabella's daughter Princess Marjorie (d. 1316) married Walter Stewart, 6th High Steward of Scotland, and their son became Robert II of S
1 CONC cotland. From him descend the monarchs of the House of Stewart and the later royal families of the United Kingdom
1 CONT
1 CONT <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabella_of_Mar>
