0 @N6000000003615777628@ NOTE Margaret; married 2nd Earl of Angus.  [Burke's Peerage]
1 CONT
1 CONT -----------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret, seen 22 Apr 1484, daughter of Sir William Hay of Yester and Jean, daughter of Hew Gifford of Yester.  [Magna Charta Sureties]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: There is a big difference of opinion about where Jean Gifford fits in.  Burke's Peerage has Jean Gifford (daughter of Hugh/Hew Gifford of Yester) as grandmother of Margaret, married to Thomas de Hay, who is William's father.
1 CONC   I have gone along with Burke's Peerage.  Later Note: It looks like CP, as corrected by XIV:26, agrees with BP.  The fact that the original CP entry was wrong (It had Jean Gifford as mother of Margaret, rather than grandmother.) 
1 CONC explains the confusion.
1 CONT
1 CONT ----------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT He [William Douglas] m. (betrothal dated 12 Dec 1410) by dispensation date 3 Dec 1414, Margaret, 1st daughter of Sir William Hay of Locherworth and Yester by his wife Alice (bb).  He d. Oct 1437.  His widow was living as late as 2
1 CONC 2 Apr 1484.  [Complete Peerage I:155, XIV:26]
1 CONT
1 CONT (bb) [from XIV:26] 'Scots Peerage', Douglas gives as his wife Jean Giffard, she was, however his mother.
