1 CONT Sir David Hay of Yester, of which he acquired 1452 a further half in addition to the quarter share he already possessed, and Locherwort; married Elizabeth, only daughter of 1st Earl of Angus, and widow of 1st Lord Forbes, and died
1 CONC  by 2 Sep
1 CONT 1478. [Burke's Peerage]
1 CONT Note that Magna Charta Sureties has David marrying a Mary Douglas, sister of Elizabeth, who was not a widow; thus allowing the marriage to occur earlier. 
1 CONT The Hay family appears to have lost Lochorwart/Locherwort by 1430, as the Borthwick family had built a Castle on the site by that date. 
