0 @N6000000002116005764@ NOTE He was dispossessed by James II following an assize of error on the grounds of illegitimacy, and the earldom was found to have devolved on the crown following the decease of Alexander Stewart.  The title was then granted in 1459 t
1 CONC o Prince John, son of James II, and on his death in 1482 to Prince John's brother, Prince Alexander.  In 1486 it passed to Prince John, son of James III and in 1562 to James Stewart, natural brother of Mary Queen of Scots.  In 156
1 CONC 5 all these grants were declared inept, and Mary "restored the lawful heirs to their just inheritance".  At that time James Stewart was created Earl of Moray.
