0 @N6000000002188045689@ NOTE George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT George Leslie, 4th Earl of Rothes (d. 1558) was a Scottish nobleman and diplomat.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sheriff of Fife from 1529 to 1540 and a Lord of Session from 1541 and a Lord of the Articles from 1544, he was tried for the murder of Cardinal Beaton and acquitted. He was ambassador to Denmark in 1550, and died at Dieppe, France
1 CONC  in 1558.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT William Leslie Earl of Rothes
1 CONT 1513–1558 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Andrew Leslie 
