0 @N6000000003043429941@ NOTE Notes from Sally Walmsley <Geniedash@bigpond.com>:
1 CONT Lord Boyd - ALEXANDER BOYD, uncle and heir, and but for the attainder, LORD BOYD (though he does not appear to have been recognised as such), being 2nd son of the first Lord Boyd.   He is wronged stated, by old writers, to have be
1 CONC en beheaded at the time of his father's attainder in 1469.   Chamberlain of Kilmarnock before 2 August 1488.  Witness to the sasine to Queen Margaret to the Lordship of Kilmarnock, 19 April 1504.  he married (dispensation after ma
1 CONC rraige and birth of children, 23 November 1505) Janet, daughter of Sir Robert Colville, of Ochiltree.  He was living 26 June 1508 [CP: 2:260] - Gen-medieval
