1 CONT b. before 1390, d. 1453, #108013
1 CONT Pedigree
1 CONT Last Edited=12 Jul 2005
1 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.8%
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell was born before 1390.2 He was the son of Sir Colin Campbell of Lochow and Mariot Campbell.2 He married, firstly, Lady Marjorie Stewart, daughter of Robert Stewart, 1st Duke of Albany and
1 CONC  Margaret Graham, Countess of Menteith.2 He married, secondly, Margaret Stewart, daughter of Sir John Stewart, before 12 March 1439/40.3 He died in 1453.1 He was buried in Kilmun, Cowal.3 
1 CONT      In 1424 he was in the list of hostages for the redemption of King James I from captivity.2 He held the office of a Justiciar of Argyllshire.2 He was invested as a Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland].4 He was invested as a Knig
1 CONC ht before March 1440.2 On 4 August 1442 he founded the Collegiate Church of Kilmun, in Cowal.2 He was created 1st Lord Campbell [Scotland] in 1445.2 He lived in Lochow, Argyllshire, Scotland.4 
1 CONT
1 CONT Child of Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell and Lady Marjorie Stewart
1 CONT Archibald Campbell, Master of Campbell+ b. b 1406, d. bt Aug 1431 - Mar 1440
1 CONT
1 CONT Children of Sir Duncan Campbell, 1st Lord Campbell and Margaret Stewart
1 CONT Sir Colin Campbell, 1st of Glenorchy+ b. b 1432, d. c Sep 1475
1 CONT Neil Campbell b. b 1442
1 CONT Duncan Campbell b. b 1442
1 CONT Archibald Campbell b. b 1442
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT
1 CONT [S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Family: A Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 220. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Family. 
1 CONT [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct 
1 CONC or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume II, page 512. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage. 
1 CONT [S6] Cokayne, and others, The Complete Peerage, volume II, page 513. 
1 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 104. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 1
1 CONC 06th edition. 
