0 @N6000000002187761262@ NOTE Walter de Burgh, 1st Earl of Ulster
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Walter de Burgh, born about 1220 or after, died at his castle of Galway in 1271, buried at Athassel Abbey, County Tipperary. He was 2nd Lord of Connacht and 1st Earl of Ulster. Second son of Richard Mor de Burgh. Succeeded by his 
1 CONC eldest son, Richard Og de Burgh, 2nd Earl of Ulster (The Red Earl of Ulster).
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT New Creation Earl of Ulster Succeeded by:
1 CONT Richard Og de Burgh 
