0 @N6000000002322291693@ NOTE A member of an historic Anglo-Irish family, the Brughs, he became one of the
1 CONT most powerful Irish nobles of the late 13th and early 14th centuries. In
1 CONT 1286, he ravaged Connaught and reestablished his family's power there,
1 CONT deposing Brian O'Neil as chief native king of Connaught and substituting one
1 CONT of his own. He led his forces from Ireland to support England's King Edward I
1 CONT in his Scottish campaigns, and, on Edward de Bruces's invasion of Ulster,
1 CONT Richard marched against him, though his daughter married Robert de Bruce.
