0 @N6000000003403225221@ NOTE [huntingdonhenry_descendents10_fromrootsweb_bartont.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT 5th Earl of Annandale and Carrick, 1245-1304. (MCB, 1898, p. 433)
1 CONT BRUCE
1 CONT "The founder was Sir Robert de Brus, a Norman knight.  He came to England with William the Conqueror, who granted him vast lands in Yorkshire. His Son, Robert, went to Scotland and was made Lord of Annandale by David I, whose grea
1 CONC t-Grand-daughter Isabella married Robert Bruse, 5th Lord of Annandale,  Through this marriage their son Robert, 6th Lord of Annandale, Regent of Scotland, inherited a right to the Crown to which he was nominated by Alexander III b
1 CONC efore tghe birth of the "Maid of Norway."  Robert 7th Lord, m Celtic, Countess 9of Carrick; and their son became that Earl of Carrick who lwas to wear the Scottish Crown, complete the liberation of Scotland, and be familiarly know
1 CONC n as Robert the Bruce.  Bruce was born in 1274.  He died at Cardros, on the Clyde, in 1329. His body was buried in Dumfermline Abbey, and his heart in Melrose.
1 CONT The Earl of Elgin bears arms as chief fo teh Bruces.  A Baronercy of Stenhouse was created in 1629, and of Downhill in 1804."
1 CONT Chief: Earl of Elgin; Patronymic; The Bruce; Clan Seats: Clackmannan Tower, Alloa; Broomhall, Fife.; Tryst: Lochmabenstone, Annandale.; Plant: Rosemary.
